(13500,'enUS','Honor the Zul\'Drak flame.',0),
(13501,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(13502,'enUS','Well done! And here, please... keep the basket!$B$BRemember, you can always return with more Noblegarden Chocolates to trade for additional items.',0),
(13503,'enUS','Well done! And here, please... keep the basket!$B$BRemember, you can always return with more Noblegarden Chocolates to trade for additional items.',0),
(13503,'ruRU','Молодчина! Нет-нет, оставь корзину себе.',25549),
(13504,'enUS','Good work. Thank you, $C.',0),
(13505,'enUS','Perfect! Thank you so much. I would hate to lose more records of our culture to war - far too much has been sacrificed already.',0),
(13506,'enUS','\"Another?\" They have more than one. I will not leave any of my people to be tortured, we must act quickly.',0),
(13507,'enUS','Excellent work. One more threat we can worry a bit less about. We\'ll continue the offensive while they are still off-guard.',0),
(13508,'enUS','<Alanndarian looks very pale, though shallow breaths betray the life that remains in her.>$B$BYou\'re here... to save me? A bit later... than I hoped.',0),
(13509,'enUS','Excellent work. That should slow them down a bit.',0),
(13510,'enUS','Some sort of shield you say? We might have a way around that. Balthule had an idea for breaking whatever protective enchantments their shaman had, so it might work on this too. Thank you for saving Aynasha and bringing me this information - it may well make the difference in our battle.',0),
(13511,'enUS','Alanndarian is dead then. That saddens me greatly, but it is not entirely unexpected. I expect no mercy from these savages, and will show them none.',0),
(13512,'enUS','You\'ve shown a great deal of talent for one so young. Good work. It seems the final battle is before us.',0),
(13513,'enUS','These will do perfectly. I will prepare them for Sandrya - you are sure to be dispatched to meet with her shortly.',0),
(13514,'enUS','You performed excellently up there! We are fortunate to have you with us.$B$BI haven\'t yet received word regarding their leader. If you haven\'t spoken with Sandrya at the cave in the back of the vale, be sure to do so before you depart.',0),
(13515,'enUS','We owe a great debt to you for all that you\'ve done to see this battle through.$B$BNot often can we claim victories so decisively, but it seems there\'s far more to this plot than just the Shatterspear. If you haven\'t already checked his body for information, make sure to do so before you leave.',0),
(13518,'enUS','Thank you, $C. Some of them surely would not have made it without you.$B$BWe\'ll be taking the wounded to the main building once we have them all safely back in town. Perhaps you can meet us there later?',0),
(13519,'enUS','You\'ve done well, $n. The Twilight\'s Hammer is a dangerous cult. It would be foolish to underestimate the danger they represent.',0),
(13520,'enUS','This will do perfectly. Thank you so much!$B$BI suspect they will want to thank you personally should they recover, so perhaps you can stop by later on.',0),
(13521,'enUS','<The machine crackles loudly, and then Wizbang\'s static-ridden voice becomes audible.>$B$BLovely! I hope you didn\'t kill too many of them. We\'re not trying to wipe out the population, we just need to get to the source of this corruption quickly! I\'m proceeding with the analysis now.',0),
(13522,'enUS','Your efforts are very much appreciated. Since the Cataclysm, the elementals have been out of control. We have little hope of taking back Auberdine without extinguishing their presence first.',0),
(13523,'enUS','You\'ve succeeded... it hasn\'t all been in vain...$B$BMy time approaches. Go now, $n, and may Elune protect you.',0),
(13525,'enUS','Why have you come here, outsider?$B$B<You tell the elder that you were sent by Foriel Broadleaf at the Grove of the Ancients. He seems to relax slightly.>$B$BThe elf is right. The forces of Felwood have seeped into Darkshore and sickened my people.',0),
(13526,'enUS','These are poor, weak stalks, but they are all we have. The corruption spreads quickly, even among the plants of the forest.',0),
(13527,'enUS','This definitely looks like the stuff they were eating. Let me take a closer peek...',0),
(13528,'enUS','<Static precedes Wizbang\'s distorted voice.>$B$BThe results are coming in now. We should have some information on how the bears contracted this in just a moment.',0),
(13529,'enUS','It is done then. Thank you. I only hope that the wildlife here will see more peace with his passing.',0),
(13537,'enUS','It looks like fishing\'s your thing. My belly appreciates the gift.$B$BI\'m thinking you would get more use out of this pole than I would. Have at it.',0),
(13538,'enUS','I heard the explosion from here! Excellent job - we\'ve already begun rerouting the power into the Titan relic to super-charge our own forces.',0),
(13539,'enUS','Now in order to kill the enemy, our men must be roused to anger; that there may be advantage from defeating the enemy, they must have their rewards. I hope that these are sufficient for your service to the Horde.',0),
(13542,'enUS','I cannot thank you enough, $n. Now we\'ll have a fighting chance to retake the ruins as soon as we are in better health.',0),
(13543,'enUS','Without those three coaxing them, perhaps the flow of elementals into the Ruins of Auberdine will be stemmed.$B$BThank you, $n.',0),
(13544,'enUS','<Elder Brolg accepts the blessed bundle from you and looks over it.>$B$BThis is exactly what we needed. The bear\'s spirit favors us and there may be hope for my brothers after all.',0),
(13545,'enUS','You have done well. My people have begun to emerge from their madness, but they will fall back into it if we do not deal with the source of the corruption.',0),
(13546,'enUS','Thank you, $n. You are a hero to my people. Without you, we would be doomed to madness and death. May the bear spirit always watch over you.',0),
(13547,'enUS','So much death and pain. Can there be any doubt that there is more yet to come?$B$BAll I wish to do is move onward into the Goddess\'s embrace as do these others.$B$BBut first, let us see if we can keep even more misery and destruction from being spread.',0),
(13548,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(13549,'enUS','Very fine specimens indeed, $n! These are sure to provide many hours of curious speculation amongst my colleagues back home.',0),
(13554,'enUS','This should be plenty! Thanks so much! I\'ll get working on a cure for this nastiness immediately.',0),
(13556,'enUS','One, two, three,... hehe, that be a good number o\' them, mon! Now we be safe for quite some time!',0),
(13557,'enUS','I am pleased to hear that you were able to free some of the remaining wildlife. With a bit of good fortune, we will find the cure for the corruption that the others have faced before any more of them die.',0),
(13558,'enUS','Yalda? The spirits of others from the Ruins of Auberdine?$B$B<The druid ponders what you\'ve conveyed about your adventure in the ruins.>$B$BI remember them all. They will be dearly missed, but they have moved on into the Goddess\'s embrace and that is for the best.$B$BAnde\'thoras-ethil, may your troubles be diminished, $n!',0),
(13559,'enUS','The Sons of Hodir accept your tribute, small one. You continue to prove your worth as an ally in more ways than one.',0),
(13560,'enUS','The decoys worked then? Great to hear it! Don\'t you worry yourself one bit about the treasures. Me and Gary will take care of the rest this time around.$B$BTruth be told, if something went wrong again and I lost any more of you adventurer types, I\'m pretty sure they\'d kick me out of town.',0),
(13561,'enUS','You have my thanks. Though they may not be able to show it, you have the thanks of the Highborne spirits as well.$B$BFare safely, traveler.',0),
(13562,'enUS','You have our thanks. It is time that we leave the past behind us, and start looking to our future.',0),
(13563,'enUS','Thank you, $n. Perhaps it would have been better... if I had done it myself. But even after these thousands of years, I could not bear to raise my hand against my beloved.$B$BPlease, I would be alone with my grief...',0),
(13564,'enUS','Greetings, traveler. You seem to have an interest in my friend here. You\'re here on behalf of his friend Volcor then I imagine? If Volcor didn\'t come himself, he must be injured as well. I hope he recovers quickly.$B$BGimclaw is too injured to be moved far and he\'s going to need some immediate treatment. I\'m afraid I can\'t let you take him back just yet, but perhaps you can help me while I tend to him.',0),
(13565,'enUS','Thank you, ally. We shall keep a more vigilant eye should they return.',0),
(13566,'enUS','These will do perfectly. These are the final ingredients for an incense I\'ve been working on. I will explain in just a moment, let me mix these in first.',0),
(13567,'enUS','I am the caretaker for my kind, leading not through force, but through wisdom and swift action. Wisdom is what carries us into the deeper forest when danger beckons and swiftness is what leaves our enemies basking in our absence.$B$BIn this wisdom, I see through to your true intentions, and I know that you are deserving of my blessing, the blessing of my swiftness. It can be yours, but know that the other spirits will not welcome you once you proceed - consider this carefully before accepting my boon.',0),
(13568,'enUS','I share these forests willingly, accepting night elf kind into my home, and on occasion calling them friend. Though they have been tainted greatly in recent memory, I can see in you the same strength, honor, and spirit that first endeared them to me.$B$BIf you place value in the ferocity necessary to overcome all odds, then I am willing to call you my champion. Know now that if you side with my kind, the other spirits will not accept you, so consider your choice carefully.',0),
(13569,'enUS','So it is done. You have received the blessing of a great animal spirit, and I shall now complete the ritual for you. Please stand still.',0),
(13570,'enUS','I just want to offer my sincerest thanks for all that you\'ve done for us. In my grief, I\'m afraid that I didn\'t extend the gratitude that you truly deserve. We may not have made it here without you.$B$BKnow that you will always have friends here.$B$BAnd you needn\'t worry about my loneliness. Grimclaw has taken to keeping me company, and I have to say he\'s a more comforting companion than I would have expected.$B$BTake this, and go with all our blessings. Until we meet again, $n.',0),
(13571,'enUS','Above the stale, unwashed stench, you catch a whiff of a familiar smell! It appears as if this once-mighty adventurer has a real love for kungaloosh.$B$BPeeking through the bars, you can barely make out the recipe written on his arm....',0),
(13572,'enUS','Thank you, $n. With your efforts, we might be able to save the Blackwood who remain.',0),
(13573,'enUS','There is no time to waste, $C. It is taking every ounce of my power to keep Darkshore\'s entire landmass from being shattered and swept into the ocean... you must listen to me very carefully.',0),
(13575,'enUS','I have much respect for the great Malfurion Stormrage. I cannot, however, leave my people in their time of need. Maybe there is a way we can both help each other.',0),
(13576,'enUS','The element of fire is unique in that attacking it indiscriminately can often lead it to spreading further... succeeding only in agitating its flames.$B$BWe are wiser than that, $n. We are going to dispose of it properly.',0),
(13577,'enUS','A terrible sadness surrounds the creature. Its eyes stare beyond you as you approach it.',0),
(13578,'enUS','I thank you, $R. Soon my kin will rest.',0),
(13579,'enUS','If the great Malfurion requires my presence, it is my duty to heed his call. It is also my duty to protect these ruins, however.$B$BPerhaps you\'ll help me fulfill both my obligations, $n?',0),
(13580,'enUS','We are in your debt, $n. Perhaps now, with Malfurion\'s help, we can save the rest of Darkshore.',0),
(13581,'enUS','This is fortunate news, $n. The furbolg may seem little more than a savage race, but their ties to the land are ancient and their shamans are second to none.',0),
(13582,'enUS','<Aroom lets out a long low-pitched hoot.>$B$BFinally kin may rest.',0),
(13583,'enUS','The wildkin were once the guardians of the land. It is good to hear they haven\'t all forgotten their old ways.',0),
(13584,'enUS','It\'s become clear, $n. The elements won\'t be calm until Malfurion succeeds in returning balance to the land. Aiding him is, in a way, also fulfilling my task.',0),
(13585,'enUS','Excellent job, $n! Selenn\'s help in holding back the vortex will be invaluable.',0),
(13586,'enUS','Malfurion calls? Yes... I can hear his voice through the dream...',0),
(13587,'enUS','I thank you, $n. You\'ve given me my freedom. Let\'s see what we can do for your world now.',0),
(13588,'enUS','We are turning the tides, $n. We should be able to contain further damage.$B$BMuch work still remains to be done.',0),
(13589,'enUS','Glynda sent you to lend a hand, did she? I\'m glad she did - I could certainly use the help.$B$BI\'m working on our initial plans to start whittling away at their ranks. Please feel free to help Tysha and Balthule in the meantime.',0),
(13590,'enUS','It is good to meet you. Word has been sent to me of the efforts you have made to aid us against the trolls, and I must admit I am a bit impressed. The final fight is upon us now, I hope you are prepared.',0),
(13591,'enUS','Well, this news is disturbing indeed. I will start dispatching messengers to Ashenvale immediately and see if we can\'t get some reinforcements prepared for them.$B$BI cannot thank you enough for all the help you\'ve lent us in these trying times. Such heroic deeds deserve reward. I think I might have something that will serve you perfectly.',0),
(13592,'enUS','Welcome back from your exercises, $n. Even while we practice for the competition, it\'s good to remind ourselves that the Scourge is still out there.',0),
(13593,'enUS','We are proud that you have agreed to train with us and compete on our behalf.',0),
(13594,'enUS','<The sentinel eyes you appreciatively for a moment.>$B$BA job well done, $C. If you\'re any indication of the quality of the $R adventurers we\'re going to be seeing more of, we should have this war against the orcs and their Horde taken care of faster than expected.',0),
(13595,'enUS','You have helped me to return to the ground, $n.$B$BNow my hair will cease to sprout for these creatures. Better yet, I will be regrown all the sooner.',0),
(13596,'enUS','Excellent job, $n. Now give me a moment to examine the plans you\'ve brought me.',0),
(13597,'enUS','For countless ages I have walked these forests and lived in these mountains. Through snow and fire, I have watched civilizations crumble and nature press on. Now, the very earth turns against us, and it becomes very apparent that we must fight if our legacy is to continue.$B$BYour heart is true, and I would choose you as our champion. If you value the thick hide and resilience of my kind, then accept my boon. Know that the other spirits will not accept you once this choice is made, so choose wisely.',0),
(13598,'enUS','You have my thanks, young one. We should be able to speed Grimclaw\'s recovery dramatically with this salve.',0),
(13599,'enUS','You\'ve returned! It is good to see you again. I suppose we have you to thank for Grimclaw\'s return?$B$BI\'m afraid... I have some bad news. I\'ve been unable to purge the toxin... their conditions worsen. Gershalla died shortly after you left, and Volcor... Volcor passed just before you came back.$B$BHe lived long enough to see Grimclaw come back safely, so he died with a smile on his face. I\'m just sorry that I couldn\'t do more.$B$BFor now, I\'m doing everything I can to save Shaldyn, so please excuse me.',0),
(13600,'enUS','<The marshal accepts the Blade of Drak\'Mar from you.>$B$BA fine weapon, and perfectly balanced. It will serve me well in the next match.',0),
(13601,'enUS','I thank you for coming to our assistance. As you can see, the refugees\' situation is dire.',0),
(13602,'enUS','Very well done, $n. Your actions in the Zoram Strand against the naga are commendable.$B$BI know your feat was not easily accomplished, for the strength and guile of the naga is well known to the night elves. We know this, for we share a history with them.$B$BThe naga are cursed Highborne night elves. Ten thousand years ago, Queen Azshara made a pact of desperation with the Old Gods to save her surviving people from a watery grave.$B$BThe naga are the result of that pact.',0),
(13603,'enUS','So the tales were true? This is a fine blade and I have no doubt that it will serve me well in the tournament. You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(13604,'enUS','The platinum disc fits perfectly inside the console. It begins to spin as its contents are scanned by white beams of light.',0),
(13605,'enUS','Aye, you\'re the fine lad who saved my Hollee!$B$BWell, I\'ve got a fitting reward for you here, I\'m sure. We really can\'t thank you enough for bringing her to safety, $n.',0),
(13606,'enUS','Excellent job, $n. We\'re one step closer to saving Azeroth!',0),
(13607,'enUS','It\'s locked? Figures!$B$BLet\'s see what information this junk heap can give us...',0),
(13609,'enUS','Ye did it! I don\'t know how, but ye did!',0),
(13610,'enUS','Ye never cease to impress, $n.$B$BYe and me are having a pint together after all this is done, ye hear me?',0),
(13611,'enUS','I\'ve got to hand it to you, $n. Our odds might not be the best, but I feel a lot better with you lending a hand.',0),
(13612,'enUS','Good work, $C!$B$BYour efforts will help keep the enemy on their heels while our forces sweep across the land!',0),
(13613,'enUS','Thank you, $R. I shall include your service to the Horde in my report.$B$BI should have these troops fit to fight again in no time!',0),
(13614,'enUS','Stand by for verification.$B$BAccess to the Celestial Planetarium granted. Please retrieve your key.',0),
(13615,'enUS','Well done, $C.$B$BThis should help get us by until our shipment arrives.',0),
(13616,'enUS','The blade is as fine as the stories say. It would seem there\'s little reason to complete the repairs on my customary blade. Winter\'s Edge is far superior and I will continue to carry it. You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(13617,'enUS','Hello, $C.$B$BWhat\'s that? You say that Shyela sent you?$B$B$B$BVery well, let\'s get started.',0),
(13618,'enUS','Listen carefully, $R....',0),
(13619,'enUS','<Kadrak listens intently as you share Gorat\'s last words.>$B$BIt is as I feared, then. May his rest be peaceful - only not yet!',0),
(13620,'enUS','Let\'s have a look, $C.',0),
(13621,'enUS','Well done, $R.$B$BThe elf captain is dead and the soul of one of our beloved brethren can sleep in peace.$B$BI shall pass on word of your deeds to my superiors in Orgrimmar.',0),
(13622,'enUS','Analyzing fragments... please stand by.',0),
(13623,'enUS','So, Evenar was succesful. Actually, more to the point, YOU were successful.$B$BI cannot thank you enough, $C, but there is more that must be done to the leaves before they will serve as a curative for what ails the child, Relara.',0),
(13624,'enUS','I\'d received a report about you from some of my scouts out in the forest but I had no idea how capable you are!$B$BThank you, $n. With what you\'ve accomplished the tide is turned. I\'ve no doubt now that we\'ll route them by the end of the day!',0),
(13625,'enUS','Well done, $n. Mounted combat is often hard to pick up for those accustomed to fighting on foot. I have no doubt that you\'ll continue to improve with practice, which is more than I can say for some warriors.',0),
(13626,'enUS','I do not look forward to writing the letter to the Argent Dawn embassy in Darnassus. At least we\'ll be able to send their most prized possessions back for their loved ones.$B$BI cannot thank you enough for your courage, $n. Please accept this on behalf of the post.',0),
(13628,'enUS','Welcome, $C. It is good to see that the road to Mor\'shan Ramparts remains clear.',0),
(13629,'enUS','Object integrity confirmed. Please hold while solidified residue is removed.',0),
(13630,'enUS','Thank you, $n.$B$BWith the moonstones of Ordil\'Aran deactivated, we should not need to worry about any further incursions of furbolg here.$B$BHowever, my scouts have returned with disturbing news from the furbolg village. There is an imminent danger massing there.$B$BI wonder, might I entice you to carry a warning to Astranaar for me?',0),
(13631,'enUS','You\'re here. Let us hope this works. For all our sakes.',0),
(13632,'enUS','We are in your debt, $C. If I know anything about the furbolg, they do not like their noses bloodied.$B$BIt won\'t be long now before they tuck tail and return to their village.',0),
(13633,'enUS','So you\'re saying this knight\'s story is a sham? Most suspicious. Dishonorable at the least, and murderous at the worst. Still, we can\'t confront him until we know for certain whether he was involved in these murders.$B$BDo nothing to arouse his suspicions, $n. Discretion will serve us well as we continue to investigate.',0),
(13634,'enUS','So you\'re saying this knight\'s story is a sham? Most suspicious. Dishonorable at the least, and murderous at the worst. Still, we can\'t confront him until we know for certain whether he was involved in these murders.$B$BDo nothing to arouse his suspicions, $n. Discretion will serve us well as we continue to investigate.',0),
(13635,'enUS','The South Gate status report? Excellent. I\'ve been awaiting news from them for a while.$B$BWith the increasing number of troggs in the hills on all sides, I fear the outposts will be the first to feel any aggressive action.',0),
(13636,'enUS','Orders! Let\'s see what we have here... hah! He wants me to deal with the infestation of rat men. We\'re already in the middle of that, so no real deviation there.$B$BCare to lend a hand?',0),
(13639,'enUS','Hmph, it\'ll take more than a Dark Iron ambush to stop the deliveries!$B$BBut Saean... I would never have suspected him to be one of their sympathizers. We\'ve been working with him for almost a year now... maybe I missed the signs.$B$BWell, I\'ll consider that later.',0),
(13640,'enUS','It seems you\'ve solved one problem only to face another, $C.',0),
(13641,'enUS','This one will do nicely. All that remains is to imbue it with the power of the Light, giving it the ability to find truth amid deception.',0),
(13642,'enUS','With the concoction blessed by the Light of Elune, it should be ready for delivery to Astranaar.$B$BThere is no time to waste, $n!',0),
(13643,'enUS','So you say Lorien Sunblaze was done in by poison and Sir Wendell was burnt alive? Dreadful ways to die, both of them. Only Conall was killed by cold steel, and from your description, it was a coward\'s strike, not honorable combat that laid him in his grave.$B$BAll three sparred with and were scheduled to fight the Black Knight. This cannot be a coincidence. Now, we must find a way to prove it was the Black Knight\'s work.',0),
(13644,'enUS','With the death of the harbinger, I can begin to cleanse the lake.$B$BYou have my deepest thanks, $n. I mourn the loss of your friend, but know that his remains will fuel the reclamation of the forest hereabouts.',0),
(13645,'enUS','Teronis is dead?$B$B<The lady weeps softly for the loss of her friend and then composes herself after a moment.>$B$BWe must see to it that his sacrifice was not in vain. Are you willing to see this through, $C?$B$BVery well, allow me some time to think about how we should proceed. I will know shortly.',0),
(13646,'enUS','Avana is alive?! I feared that she might be dead when we heard about the attack on Maestra\'s Post!$B$BAs you can see, we have our hands full with the Horde here as well.$B$BYou have given me the greatest gift by letting me know she is well. Any time that you wish to ride one of my nightsabers back to Maestra\'s Post, it is yours.',0),
(13647,'enUS','Hello there, laddy! The mountaineers sent you over, eh? I do suspect we might have just the sort of work you\'re looking for. Welcome to the Farstrider Lodge!',0),
(13648,'enUS','You brought that damned spy to justice! This is good news. We can all rest a little bit easier, not worrying about that one.',0),
(13650,'enUS','Woo! I\'m relieved... I was worried they\'d all be destroyed by now. Thank you for checking in on them.',0),
(13651,'enUS','Thank you for the oil, $C. Now prepare yourself!$B$BMy runner has returned with some desperate news....$B$BSplintertree is surrounded!',0),
(13653,'enUS','Gorka...$B$BWe must always be prepared for losses. Her honorable service to the Horde will not be forgotten.$B$BAnd her sacrifice shall not be in vain!',0),
(13654,'enUS','<Crusader Rhydalla examines the bag\'s contents with a look of disgust on her face.>$B$BIt\'s all here, $n: the poison that killed Lorien, a collection of knives, torches, and oil. No man has cause to possess these things here and no squire would do so without orders from his knightly master. We\'ve found our murderer, $n, but who is he working for?',0),
(13655,'enUS','Well look at that. You found one of our stolen documents!$B$BWe\'re much obliged for it\'s return. Hopefully a bit of gold will suit your fancy for the finders fee?',0),
(13656,'enUS','Hello, sonny! You seem to have found one of our stolen documents, eh?$B$BThank you kindly for bringing it back to us. We\'ll gladly lend some coin as thanks for its return.',0),
(13657,'enUS','Our historical records! The thought of dark iron vermin delving into our past just made me sick to my stomach.$B$BWe appreciate you bringing this back to us. We\'d like to offer you some coin as a reward.',0),
(13658,'enUS','Ug, I can\'t believe they got their hands on our transport routes - that was just asking for trouble!!$B$BThank you for getting this back to us before they were able to do much with it! You probably saved us a lot of heartache. Please accept some coin as a reward for your efforts.',0),
(13659,'enUS','Hah! Think they got a kick out of seeing how low they were on our list of threat assessments! This document was admittedly a bit out of date, but none the less amusing.$B$BOf course, we\'ll offer you some money as a reward for returning this anyway - your efforts are appreciated!',0),
(13660,'enUS','Our artifact records! I was pretty well worried what the dark irons might try to steal with this information at their disposal.$B$BThank you for bringing this back to us. We\'ll gladly part with some coin to express our gratitude.',0),
(13661,'enUS','You located all of our documents! We can\'t thank you enough for the help... we\'d all but given up hope. It seemed sure that the dark irons would be able to act upon all of this information soon. It\'s good to know that they\'ll be left blind in their attacks for quite a while yet.$B$BTo thank you for all of your efforts on our behalf, we would like to offer you a gift. An artifact really... something we recovered from one of our digs. You have the appreciation of all of the Explorers\' League.',0),
(13662,'enUS','Keep the residue pouring in!',0),
(13663,'enUS','<Crusader Rhydalla\'s face pales as she reads the orders.>$B$BThis can only mean one thing, $n. The Black Knight is a member of the Cult of the Damned and has been sent by Arthas to disrupt the tournament!$B$BThe Black Knight has proven himself a fearsome combatant, and you will need to be every bit as good if you wish to face him. When you are a champion, return to me and we\'ll find a way to ensure his defeat.',0),
(13664,'enUS','With the death of the Black Knight, the tournament may once again serve its purpose. The champions of the Horde and Alliance may demonstrate their skill at arms and train for the day when Arthas and his minions will no longer threaten us.$B$BYou have the thanks of the Argent Crusade, $n, and that of all who have answered our call.',0),
(13665,'enUS','Well done. Training against the other valiants is one of the best ways to prepare yourself for tournament competition. I know you\'ll make Stormwind proud, $n.',0),
(13666,'enUS','So there is some truth to those old tales? It seems they did not lie about the quality of the blade. Well done, $n. The champion who wields it will be a lucky man, indeed.',0),
(13667,'enUS','I have entered your name in the rolls, $n. As an aspirant you will train with others who wish to compete in the tournament and hone your mounted combat skills. Once you have proven yourself, you will be allowed to enter the lowest rank of competition on behalf of your capital city.',0),
(13668,'enUS','I have entered your name in the rolls, $n. As an aspirant you will train with others who wish to compete in the tournament and hone your mounted combat skills. Once you have proven yourself, you will be allowed to enter the lowest rank of competition on behalf of your capital city.',0),
(13669,'enUS','There\'s no doubt that this is a blade of exquisite quality and balance. Now I understand why these weapons are so coveted among the champions of the Alliance.',0),
(13670,'enUS','The blade is as fine as the squire said it would be, but where did he find out about it? No matter; it will serve its new owner well. Perhaps it\'s only fair that Ironforge\'s grand champion be the one to wield it.',0),
(13671,'enUS','You have shown yourself a capable combatant, $n and you will serve as an example to the rest of the aspirants who clamor to compete on behalf of the Alliance.',0),
(13672,'enUS','Very well, I will make the arrangements.',0),
(13673,'enUS','So there is some truth to those old tales? It seems they did not lie about the quality of the blade. Well done, $n. The champion who wields it will be a lucky man, indeed.',0),
(13674,'enUS','There\'s no doubt that this is a blade of exquisite quality and balance. Now I understand why these weapons are so coveted among the champions of the Alliance.',0),
(13675,'enUS','The blade is as fine as the valiant said it would be, but where did he find out about it? No matter; it will serve its new owner well. Perhaps it\'s only fair that Orgrimmar\'s grand champion be the one to wield it.',0),
(13676,'enUS','You have shown yourself a capable combatant, $n and you will serve as an example to the rest of the aspirants who clamor to compete on behalf of the Horde.',0),
(13677,'enUS','Well done, $n. Mounted combat is often hard to pick up for those accustomed to fighting on foot. I have no doubt that you\'ll continue to improve with practice, which is more than I can say for some warriors.',0),
(13678,'enUS','Very well, I will make the arrangements.',0),
(13679,'enUS','Congratulations are in order, $n. You have bested your challenger and earned the right to advance to the rank of valiant.',0),
(13680,'enUS','Congratulations are in order, $n. You have bested your challenger and earned the right to advance to the rank of valiant.',0),
(13682,'enUS','$n, you and your allies have spared the tournament from a devastating attack. Though our skytalon riders are brave, they have their hands full keeping the peace on the tournament grounds and would be hard-pressed to defend the skies against the cult\'s attack. You have the thanks of the Argent Crusade and all who have gathered here to compete.',0),
(13683,'enUS','We are in your debt, $C.$B$BUnable to complete their nefarious rituals, the satyr are now fighting a losing battle where they are unable to replenish their numbers.',0),
(13684,'enUS','Welcome aboard then, Valiant $n. The Stormwind delegation is proud to count you among its members.',0),
(13685,'enUS','It\'s good to meet you, valiant. Ironforge needs competitors like you to prevail in the tournament.',0),
(13688,'enUS','Welcome aboard then, Valiant $n. The Gnomeregan delegation is proud to count you among its members.',0),
(13689,'enUS','Welcome to the Darnassus tournament delegation, $n. It will be a pleasure to train and compete alongside you.',0),
(13690,'enUS','Welcome aboard then, Valiant $n. The Exodar\'s delegation is proud to count you among its members.',0),
(13691,'enUS','So you want to compete for Orgrimmar? Just because you\'ve beaten up a few dummies doesn\'t mean you\'ll win, but you\'ll be training with the best from now on.',0),
(13693,'enUS','You think you have what it takes to compete for Sen\'jin? I think we\'ll be finding out.',0),
(13694,'enUS','On behalf of Thunder Bluff and its warriors, I welcome you, $n. Always fight honorably and bravely beneath our banner.',0),
(13695,'enUS','Welcome to the Undercity delegation. $n. As a valiant, you\'ll train with us to prepare you for the highest level of competition.',0),
(13696,'enUS','So you want to compete for Silvermoon? Very well. I\'ll add you to the rolls and you may begin working with the other valiants immediately.',0),
(13697,'enUS','Impressive, valiant. I will make the arrangements for your test immediately.',0),
(13698,'enUS','I saw those explosions all of the way from over here! Those filthy orcs and their goblin lackeys are going to have a hard time doing anything to despoil the forest now!$B$BWe can\'t thank you enough, $n. Will this do?',0),
(13699,'enUS','You have proven yourself worthy of the title of champion, $n. You will compete at the tournament\'s highest level on behalf of Stormwind, riding in the grand melee with your weapon at the ready and our mighty pennant at your back.',0),
(13702,'enUS','I welcome you as a champion of the tournament, $n. As a champion, you will be able to compete for the grand championship of the tournament. You may also choose to become a valiant with another Alliance city\'s delegation and in time, a champion for that city as well.$B$BAll champions must have the assistance of a squire, $n, and you are no exception. Allow me to appoint one of ours to accompany you in battle. He will proudly carry the banner of any city that has named you a champion.',0),
(13703,'enUS','We are proud that you have decided to join us and I know you will shine on the field.',0),
(13704,'enUS','We\'re proud to count you among us, $n, and we look forward to training with you.',0),
(13705,'enUS','It\'s good to have you on our team, $n. We will all benefit from training with you.',0),
(13706,'enUS','The warriors of Darnassus are honored to fight and train beside you.',0),
(13707,'enUS','Welcome, then, $n. I look forward to watching you train with my men.',0),
(13708,'enUS','I am glad that you have decided to join us and look forward to seeing you in action.',0),
(13709,'enUS','I am honored that you have chosen to join our delegation. I know you will make us proud, $n.',0),
(13710,'enUS','You have chosen wisely, $n. Both of us will benefit from this arrangement.',0),
(13711,'enUS','It will be an honor training and competing with you, $n.',0),
(13712,'enUS','Gorka\'s death was not in vain, $n.$B$BSplintertree would have certainly fallen if we hadn\'t come when we did.$B$BNow we must get to work shoring up her defenses.$B$BThis isn\'t over....',0),
(13713,'enUS','You have proven yourself worthy of the title of champion, $n. You will compete at the tournament\'s highest level on behalf of Ironforge, riding in the grand melee with your weapon at the ready and our mighty pennant at your back.',0),
(13714,'enUS','Impressive, valiant. I will make the arrangements for your test immediately.',0),
(13715,'enUS','Impressive, valiant. I will make the arrangements for your test immediately.',0),
(13716,'enUS','Impressive, valiant. I will make the arrangements for your test immediately.',0),
(13717,'enUS','Impressive, valiant. I will make the arrangements for your test immediately.',0),
(13718,'enUS','Impressive, valiant. I will make the arrangements for your test immediately.',0),
(13719,'enUS','Impressive, valiant. I will make the arrangements for your test immediately.',0),
(13720,'enUS','Impressive, valiant. I will make the arrangements for your test immediately.',0),
(13721,'enUS','Impressive, valiant. I will make the arrangements for your test immediately.',0),
(13722,'enUS','Impressive, valiant. I will make the arrangements for your test immediately.',0),
(13723,'enUS','You have proven yourself worthy of the title of champion, $n. You will compete at the tournament\'s highest level on behalf of Gnomeregan, riding in the grand melee with your weapon at the ready and our mighty pennant at your back.',0),
(13724,'enUS','You have proven yourself worthy of the title of champion, $n. You will compete at the tournament\'s highest level on behalf of the Exodar, riding in the grand melee with your weapon at the ready and our mighty pennant at your back.',0),
(13725,'enUS','You have proven yourself worthy of the title of champion, $n. You will compete at the tournament\'s highest level on behalf of Darnassus, riding in the grand melee with your weapon at the ready and our mighty pennant at your back.',0),
(13726,'enUS','You have proven yourself worthy of the title of champion, $n. You will compete at the tournament\'s highest level, riding in the grand melee and crushing the competition under the banner of Orgrimmar.',0),
(13727,'enUS','You have proven yourself worthy of the title of champion, $n. You will compete at the tournament\'s highest level, riding in the grand melee and crushing the competition under the banner of the Darkspears.',0),
(13728,'enUS','You have proven yourself worthy of the title of champion, $n. You will compete at the tournament\'s highest level, riding in the grand melee and crushing the competition under the banner of the Thunder Bluff.',0),
(13729,'enUS','You have proven yourself worthy of the title of champion, $n. You will compete at the tournament\'s highest level, riding in the grand melee and crushing the competition under the banner of the Undercity.',0),
(13730,'enUS','Oh, yes!$B$BThis will teach those elves, just you watch!',0),
(13731,'enUS','You have proven yourself worthy of the title of champion, $n. You will compete at the tournament\'s highest level, riding in the grand melee and crushing the competition under the banner of Silvermoon.',0),
(13732,'enUS','I welcome you as a champion of the tournament, $n. As a champion, you will be able to compete for the grand championship of the tournament. You may also choose to become a valiant with another Alliance city\'s delegation and in time, a champion for that city as well.$B$BAll champions must have the assistance of a squire, $n, and you are no exception. Allow me to appoint one of ours to accompany you in battle. He will proudly carry the banner of any city that has named you a champion.',0),
(13733,'enUS','I welcome you as a champion of the tournament, $n. As a champion, you will be able to compete for the grand championship of the tournament. You may also choose to become a valiant with another Alliance city\'s delegation and in time, a champion for that city as well.$B$BAll champions must have the assistance of a squire, $n, and you are no exception. Allow me to appoint one of ours to accompany you in battle. He will proudly carry the banner of any city that has named you a champion.',0),
(13734,'enUS','I welcome you as a champion of the tournament, $n. As a champion, you will be able to compete for the grand championship of the tournament. You may also choose to become a valiant with another Alliance city\'s delegation and in time, a champion for that city as well.$B$BAll champions must have the assistance of a squire, $n, and you are no exception. Allow me to appoint one of ours to accompany you in battle. He will proudly carry the banner of any city that has named you a champion.',0),
(13735,'enUS','I welcome you as a champion of the tournament, $n. As a champion, you will be able to compete for the grand championship of the tournament. You may also choose to become a valiant with another Alliance city\'s delegation and in time, a champion for that city as well.$B$BAll champions must have the assistance of a squire, $n, and you are no exception. Allow me to appoint one of ours to accompany you in battle. He will proudly carry the banner of any city that has named you a champion.',0),
(13736,'enUS','I welcome you as a champion of the tournament, $n. As a champion, you will be able to compete for the grand championship of the tournament. You may also choose to become a valiant with another Horde city\'s delegation and in time, a champion for that city as well.$B$BAll champions must have the assistance of a squire, $n, and you are no exception. Allow me to appoint one of ours to accompany you in battle. He will proudly carry the banner of any city that has named you a champion.',0),
(13737,'enUS','I welcome you as a champion of the tournament, $n. As a champion, you will be able to compete for the grand championship of the tournament. You may also choose to become a valiant with another Horde city\'s delegation and in time, a champion for that city as well.$B$BAll champions must have the assistance of a squire, $n, and you are no exception. Allow me to appoint one of ours to accompany you in battle. He will proudly carry the banner of any city that has named you a champion.',0),
(13738,'enUS','I welcome you as a champion of the tournament, $n. As a champion, you will be able to compete for the grand championship of the tournament. You may also choose to become a valiant with another Horde city\'s delegation and in time, a champion for that city as well.$B$BAll champions must have the assistance of a squire, $n, and you are no exception. Allow me to appoint one of ours to accompany you in battle. He will proudly carry the banner of any city that has named you a champion.',0),
(13739,'enUS','I welcome you as a champion of the tournament, $n. As a champion, you will be able to compete for the grand championship of the tournament. You may also choose to become a valiant with another Horde city\'s delegation and in time, a champion for that city as well.$B$BAll champions must have the assistance of a squire, $n, and you are no exception. Allow me to appoint one of ours to accompany you in battle. He will proudly carry the banner of any city that has named you a champion.',0),
(13740,'enUS','I welcome you as a champion of the tournament, $n. As a champion, you will be able to compete for the grand championship of the tournament. You may also choose to become a valiant with another Horde city\'s delegation and in time, a champion for that city as well.$B$BAll champions must have the assistance of a squire, $n, and you are no exception. Allow me to appoint one of ours to accompany you in battle. He will proudly carry the banner of any city that has named you a champion.',0),
(13741,'enUS','So the tales were true? This is a fine blade and I have no doubt that it will serve me well in the tournament. You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(13742,'enUS','<The grand champion accepts the Blade of Drak\'Mar from you.>$B$BA fine weapon, and perfectly balanced. It will serve me well in the next match.',0),
(13743,'enUS','The blade is as fine as the stories say. It would seem there\'s little reason to complete the repairs on my customary blade. Winter\'s Edge is far superior and I will continue to carry it. You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(13744,'enUS','Welcome back from your exercises, $n. Even while we practice for the competition, it\'s good to remind ourselves that the Scourge is still out there.',0),
(13745,'enUS','Well done. Training against the other valiants is one of the best ways to prepare yourself for tournament competition. I know you\'ll make Ironforge proud, $n.',0),
(13746,'enUS','So the tales were true? This is a fine blade and I have no doubt that it will serve me well in the tournament. You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(13747,'enUS','<Ambrose accepts the Blade of Drak\'Mar from you.>$B$BA fine weapon, and perfectly balanced. It will serve me well in the next match.',0),
(13748,'enUS','The blade is as fine as the stories say. It would seem there\'s little reason to complete the repairs on my customary blade. Winter\'s Edge is far superior and I will continue to carry it. You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(13749,'enUS','Welcome back from your exercises, $n. I\'m confident that you will make us proud when the competition starts.',0),
(13750,'enUS','Well done. Training against the other valiants is one of the best ways to prepare yourself for tournament competition. I know you\'ll make us proud, $n.',0),
(13751,'enUS','What\'s this? Who are you!?$B$B<Durak reads Draaka\'s note.>$B$BHrmphh...$B$BDraaka should know better than to be so brazen, but it looks like you\'re up to your eyes in this with as much to lose as anyone.$B$BVery well.',0),
(13752,'enUS','So the tales were true? This is a fine blade and I have no doubt that it will serve me well in the tournament. You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(13753,'enUS','<The grand champion accepts the Blade of Drak\'Mar from you.>$B$BA fine weapon, and perfectly balanced. It will serve me well in the next match.',0),
(13754,'enUS','The blade is as fine as the stories say. It would seem there\'s little reason to complete the repairs on my customary blade. Winter\'s Edge is far superior and I will continue to carry it. You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(13755,'enUS','Welcome back from your exercises, $n. Even while we practice for the competition, it\'s good to remind ourselves that the Scourge is still out there.',0),
(13756,'enUS','Well done. Training against the other valiants is one of the best ways to prepare yourself for tournament competition. I know you\'ll make us proud, $n.',0),
(13757,'enUS','So the tales were true? This is a fine blade and I have no doubt that it will serve me well in the tournament. You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(13758,'enUS','<Jaelyne accepts the Blade of Drak\'Mar from you.>$B$BA fine weapon, and perfectly balanced. It will serve me well in the next match.',0),
(13759,'enUS','The blade is as fine as the stories say. It would seem there\'s little reason to complete the repairs on my customary blade. Winter\'s Edge is far superior and I will continue to carry it. You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(13760,'enUS','Welcome back from your exercises, $n. Even while we practice for the competition, it\'s good to remind ourselves that the Scourge is still out there.',0),
(13761,'enUS','Well done. Training against the other valiants is one of the best ways to prepare yourself for tournament competition. I know you\'ll make Darnassus proud, $n.',0),
(13762,'enUS','So the tales were true? This blade should be enough to best anything those Alliance entrants can come up with.',0),
(13763,'enUS','This is a fine weapon that will help me crush the competition. Thank you, $n.',0),
(13764,'enUS','The blade is as fine as the stories say. It would seem there\'s little reason to complete the repairs on my customary blade. Winter\'s Edge is far superior and I will continue to carry it. You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(13765,'enUS','A good day of training will never hurt anyone. It\'s good to see you keeping up.',0),
(13766,'enUS','With their gates closed and no further reinforcements coming, it is only a matter of time now before the demons are no more.$B$BYou are a hero of the forest, $n. I give you thanks on behalf of all of Ashenvale\'s creatures!',0),
(13767,'enUS','Training against the other valiants will sharpen your claws and hone your battle instincts. When the competition begins, you will be ready.',0),
(13768,'enUS','So the tales were true? This blade should be enough to best anything those Alliance entrants can come up with.',0),
(13769,'enUS','This is a fine weapon that will help me crush the competition. Thank you, $n.',0),
(13770,'enUS','The blade is as fine as the stories say. It would seem there\'s little reason to complete the repairs on my customary blade. Winter\'s Edge is far superior and I will continue to carry it. You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(13771,'enUS','A good day of training will never hurt anyone. It\'s good to see you keeping up.',0),
(13772,'enUS','Training against other valiants will quickly teach you what you need to know to best them. Keep it up and you\'ll have no trouble defeating them in competition.',0),
(13773,'enUS','So the tales were true? This blade should be enough to best anything those Alliance entrants can come up with.',0),
(13774,'enUS','This is a fine weapon that will help me crush the competition. Thank you, $n.',0),
(13775,'enUS','The blade is as fine as the stories say. It would seem there\'s little reason to complete the repairs on my customary blade. Winter\'s Edge is far superior and I will continue to carry it. You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(13776,'enUS','A good day of training will never hurt anyone. It\'s good to see you keeping up.',0),
(13777,'enUS','Training against the other valiants will sharpen your claws and hone your battle instincts. When the competition begins, you will be ready.',0),
(13778,'enUS','So the tales were true? This blade should be enough to best anything those Alliance entrants can come up with.',0),
(13779,'enUS','This is a fine weapon that will help me crush the competition. Thank you, $n.',0),
(13780,'enUS','The blade is as fine as the stories say. It would seem there\'s little reason to complete the repairs on my customary blade. Winter\'s Edge is far superior and I will continue to carry it. You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(13781,'enUS','A good day of training will never hurt anyone. It\'s good to see you keeping up.',0),
(13782,'enUS','Training against the other valiants will sharpen your claws and hone your battle instincts. When the competition begins, you will be ready.',0),
(13783,'enUS','So the tales were true? This blade should be enough to best anything those Alliance entrants can come up with.',0),
(13784,'enUS','This is a fine weapon that will help me crush the competition. Thank you, $n.',0),
(13785,'enUS','The blade is as fine as the stories say. It would seem there\'s little reason to complete the repairs on my customary blade. Winter\'s Edge is far superior and I will continue to carry it. You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(13786,'enUS','A good day of training will never hurt anyone. It\'s good to see you keeping up.',0),
(13787,'enUS','Training against the other valiants will sharpen your claws and hone your battle instincts. When the competition begins, you will be ready.',0),
(13788,'enUS','$n, you have spared the tournament from a devastating attack. The Argent Crusade and all who gather here are in our debt and we\'ll make certain they remember it. For all their bluster about providing protection, the peacekeepers and skytalons spend more time breaking up drunken brawls than keeping us safe from the Scourge.$B$BIt\'s no matter. We always protect our own.',0),
(13789,'enUS','You are a true champion, $n, both inside the ring and on the field. We must all be vigilant against the Scourge and you are a great example to our brethren and your own people.',0),
(13790,'enUS','Well done. Training against the other champions is one of the best ways to prepare yourself for tournament competition. I know you\'ll make the Alliance proud, $n.',0),
(13791,'enUS','You have done well in demonstrating our commitment to fighting the Scourge, no matter where we are or what we are doing.',0),
(13792,'enUS','You are brave to come here, $C, but you may be too late. All of the druids are either dead or have been driven insane.$B$BStill, your tale is intriguing, and if what you say is true, then Gnarl must have the Forest Heart and soon, or Ashenvale will begin to wither!',0),
(13793,'enUS','You handle your mount well, $n. In time, your competitors will learn to fear you.',0),
(13794,'enUS','It\'s good to finally meet you, champion. The highlord has asked me to help coordinate the efforts of all champions to train together and bolster the defenses of the tournament grounds.',0),
(13795,'enUS','So you have become a champion, $n. I had no doubt that it would happen. We knights have been trained in the heat of battle, not in front of wooden dummies. Let\'s show the paladins and their guests what battle has made us.',0),
(13796,'enUS','The Forest Heart! It\'s corrupted!$B$B<The great ancient creaks as its immense limbs begin to perform a ritual.>$B$BStand back, $n, I will try to cleanse the heart before all is lost!',0),
(13797,'enUS','Well done! These should hold a curse long enough for our purposes....',0),
(13798,'enUS','Did you feel it, $n!?$B$BThe raw fel power seething through your being?$B$BThere is nothing else like it!',0),
(13801,'enUS','Woohooo!!$B$BYou\'ve silenced the voices! Thank you, thank you!',0),
(13803,'enUS','Tainting the Forest\'s Heart?$B$BHow ruthless - an utterly vicious blow....$B$BI adore the idea!',0),
(13805,'enUS','It is done?$B$BGood work, $n. That will gradually weaken their forces, as well as their spirit.',0),
(13806,'enUS','Good work, $R.$B$BOne less thing we have to worry about!',0),
(13808,'enUS','You have your work cut out for you here, friend.$B$BLet\'s hope that you\'re up to the task,,,,',0),
(13809,'enUS','$n, you and your allies have spared the tournament from a devastating attack. Though our skytalon riders are brave, they have their hands full keeping the peace on the tournament grounds and would be hard-pressed to defend the skies against the cult\'s attack. You have the thanks of the Argent Crusade and all who have gathered here to compete.',0),
(13810,'enUS','You are a true champion, $n, both inside the ring and on the field. We must all be vigilant against the Scourge and you are a great example to our brethren and your own people.',0),
(13811,'enUS','Well done. Training against the other champions is one of the best ways to prepare yourself for tournament competition. I know you\'ll make the Horde proud, $n.',0),
(13812,'enUS','$n, you have spared the tournament from a devastating attack. The Argent Crusade and all who gather here are in our debt and we\'ll make certain they remember it. For all their bluster about providing protection, the peacekeepers and skytalons spend more time breaking up drunken brawls than keeping us safe from the Scourge.$B$BIt\'s no matter. We always protect our own.',0),
(13813,'enUS','You have done well in demonstrating our commitment to fighting the Scourge, no matter where we are or what we are doing.',0),
(13814,'enUS','You handle your mount well, $n. In time, your competitors will learn to fear you.',0),
(13815,'enUS','Nice work, $n.$B$BYou\'ve demoralized the enemy and harvested resources for the Horde.$B$BLet\'s hope the rest of the mission goes as well.',0),
(13816,'enUS','It\'s locked? Figures!$B$BI\'ll let Brann know... maybe he can uncover something in the Archivum.',0),
(13817,'enUS','The platinum disc fits perfectly inside the console. It begins to spin as its contents are scanned by white beams of light.',0),
(13818,'enUS','Stand by for verification.$B$BAccess to the Celestial Planetarium granted. Please retrieve your key.',0),
(13819,'enUS','You\'re here. Let us hope this works. For all our sakes.',0),
(13821,'enUS','Excellent job, $n. We\'re one step closer to saving Azeroth!',0),
(13822,'enUS','Ye did it! I don\'t know how, but ye did!',0),
(13823,'enUS','Ye never cease to impress, $n.$B$BYe and me are having a pint together after all this is done, ye hear me?',0),
(13824,'enUS','I\'ve got to hand it to you, $n. Our odds might not be the best, but I feel a lot better with you lending a hand.',0),
(13825,'enUS','Hey, I remember you! Aren\'t you the $C that helped me make all that clamlette back in the day?$B$BTell you what, step on up and I\'ll show you my newest recipe - it\'s simple and delicious!',0),
(13826,'enUS','Well hello there, young $C. Either my memory is failing me, or I forgot to give you this last time we spoke...',0),
(13828,'enUS','Keep the words of the master in mind as you practice with the training dummies.',0),
(13829,'enUS','Keep the words of the master in mind as you practice with the training dummies.',0),
(13830,'enUS','So eating it makes you invisible... what a strange defense this clever fish has developed.$B$BI\'d like to digest this for a bit. Pun not intended, $n. Really. Why don\'t you come see me tomorrow?',0),
(13831,'enUS','<Tharnariun Treetender pages through the notes as you relate your story, the lines in his face deepening with concern.>$B$BSo the Forsaken have been studying Foulhoof\'s work? My gut crawls at the thought of what they might have done were they able to weaponize his corruption. You\'ve done well to destroy their work, but this raises deeper concerns. What brought the Forsaken to our doorstep? Are they working with the Shatterspear trolls to our north? Sorrows are heaping upon sorrows, $C. I\'m glad you\'re here.',0),
(13832,'enUS','Well now, that looks like it could be valuable. Difficult to know until it\'s cleaned up and appraised, but I\'m still willing to make the trade if you are.',0),
(13833,'enUS','You are a brave one, $n. I hope you didn\'t lose any extremities making your fishing spot. If you\'ve still got the fishing bug, come back tomorrow and we\'ll talk some more.',0),
(13834,'enUS','My, my, my! You\'ve caught yourself some Terrorfish. Why, that reminds me of the time...$B$B<Marcia regales you with stories of adventure and fishing for as long as you\'re willing to listen.>',0),
(13835,'enUS','Commit Valis\'s lesson to memory, $n. It will mean the difference between winning and losing your mounted combat matches.',0),
(13836,'enUS','Oh, hello there $n. Marcia said you\'d be coming by with that poor man\'s missing arm.$B$BShe also gave me this bag to give you as a reward. It smells horrible, and I\'m anxious to make the trade if you don\'t mind.',0),
(13837,'enUS','With a teacher like Rugan, you\'ll be an expert at mounted combat in no time.',0),
(13838,'enUS','Commit Valis\'s lesson to memory, $n. It will mean the difference between winning and losing your mounted combat matches.',0),
(13839,'enUS','With experience and practice, you will become deadly with the charge.',0),
(13841,'enUS','Fools!!$B$BThis Draaka woman has allowed herself to be manipulated by a demon!$B$B<Garrosh studies you for a moment.>$B$BAnd I smell its taint on you as well, $C....',0),
(13842,'enUS','Grah... very well.$B$BI\'ll remove the bounty I had placed upon your head. Though I am sorely tempted to end your life anyway, just on principle.$B$BBe sure that you never raise my ire again, $n. Now, get out of my sight...',0),
(13843,'enUS','You take note of the information displayed in the schematic and the materials required to construct the scrapbot kit.',0),
(13844,'enUS','Let\'s see what we\'ve got here.... By Elune, his notes are scrawled in a half dozen languages. What is this, blood? This archive makes my flesh seethe, but at least it\'s secure. It will take us some time to decipher these notes.$B$BOh - your reward? Yes, here. Nice work with those undead scavengers. Now get back to the fight.',0),
(13845,'enUS','You are brave to have carried this. If even one drop were to touch your skin, you\'d have died an agonizing death.$B$BAllow me to pay you for it... I can always use venom of exceptional potency.',0),
(13846,'enUS','Thank you. I just know the crusade will put it to good use!',0),
(13847,'enUS','Your bravery on the field has shown the crusaders what they already knew -- that our warriors are more than just parade ground decorations.',0),
(13848,'enUS','<Commander Grimfang\'s brow wrinkles as he reads the report.>$B$BThis is grim news, indeed.$B$BMay the spirits preserve them until we can fight our way to Splintertree....',0),
(13849,'enUS','Thank you!$B$BNow it\'s time to deal with the Horde!',0),
(13850,'enUS','You did it? You actually did it?!$B$BHo ho! Stubborn as my wife, you are.',0),
(13851,'enUS','Your bravery on the field has shown the crusaders that we are worthy allies.',0),
(13852,'enUS','Your bravery on the field has shown the that we are a match for the Argent Crusade\'s own.',0),
(13853,'enUS','We\'re saved! You\'ve shot down enough of them that we should be able to handle the rest.$B$BI cannot thank you enough, $n.',0),
(13854,'enUS','Your bravery on the field has shown the crusaders what they already knew -- that our warriors are more than just parade ground decorations.',0),
(13855,'enUS','Your bravery on the field has shown the crusaders that they can rely on us in the battle against the Lich King.',0),
(13856,'enUS','Your bravery on the field has shown the crusaders what they already knew -- that our warriors are the best in Azeroth.',0),
(13857,'enUS','Your bravery on the field has shown the crusaders that we are fearless in the face of the Lich King\'s minions.',0),
(13858,'enUS','Your bravery on the field has shown the crusaders that we are steadfast allies in the battle against the Lich King.',0),
(13859,'enUS','Your bravery on the field has shown the crusaders that we are ready to face any enemy.',0),
(13860,'enUS','The Argent Crusade has seen our resolve and they know that our warriors will see this through to the end.',0),
(13861,'enUS','The Argent Crusade is heartened to have paladins like you fighting alongside us in the battle against the Lich King.',0),
(13862,'enUS','The Argent Crusade is heartened to have paladins like you fighting alongside us in the battle against the Lich King.',0),
(13863,'enUS','Everywhere we have met the Scourge, we have made them fear us, and this campaign is no different.',0),
(13864,'enUS','Everywhere we have fought the Scourge, we have taught them to fear us and this campaign will be no different.',0),
(13865,'enUS','Well done, $C.$B$BThey\'re in complete disarray. Just look at them!',0),
(13866,'enUS','You are just in time, $C. Old Kulg has been slinking around those woods too long. He grows too cautious, jumping at shadows. We will fear this forest no longer - the time has come to subdue Ashenvale once and for all!',0),
(13867,'enUS','Well done, $n.$B$BWe are under constant threat from the furbolg. Hopefully this will keep them at bay for a bit longer.',0),
(13868,'enUS','A troll charm? What are the furbolg doing with such a thing?$B$BYou\'re right, it does have a feeling of corruption about it... even I can sense that.$B$BThere\'s someone here who might be able to help.',0),
(13869,'enUS','I have lived a very long time in peace with the forest, but what these orc-things are doing makes me want to feed them back to the ground!$B$BI will put this wood to rest now. Thank you for this kindness, $n. I will never forget.',0),
(13870,'enUS','<Gorthak sighs disappointedly.>$B$BIf only you\'d arrived an hour ago....$B$BThe diplomat suffered mortal wounds at the hands of an elf assassin.$B$BHow the enemy was able to infiltrate the camp undetected remains a mystery.',0),
(13871,'enUS','Well done, $C.$B$BOne last request - it would probably be best if none of my laborers knew this assassin ever existed.',0),
(13872,'enUS','<Looking down at the wooden carving in your extended hand, the worgen reaches out to take it.>',0),
(13873,'enUS','<Gurtar listens as you inform him of Sheelah\'s passing.>$B$BI\'ll deliver this to Hellscream personally, $R.$B$BIn the meantime, there\'s something I need you to do for me....',0),
(13874,'enUS','<Hephaestus nods slowly as he looks you straight in the eye.>$B$BYou\'ve likely saved the Thistlefur from themselves, at least in the short run. If they can keep from stealing objects of power that don\'t belong to them, that is.$B$BI understand that the night elves are having problems with the other furbolg tribe to the south. That\'s something that Raene is going to want to speak to you about.$B$BHowever, there are more immediate concerns that I would ask for your help with.',0),
(13875,'enUS','<Recognizing at once the nature of the gift, Draaka begins to weep.>$B$BOh, $n. Thank you for this gift! It means more than you could know.$B$BHe hasn\'t forgotten...',0),
(13876,'enUS','What was done had to be done. As our leader, Dal\'s sickness from the troll charms was destroying us.$B$BIt was better for the health and dignity of the tribe that it was you, outsider. This way there will be no civil war amongst us and we will easily find new leadership... hopefully one that does not have a tendency to so easily trust outsiders. Perhaps I am guilty of this as well?$B$BHere, allow me to repay the debt we owe you before we part ways forever.',0),
(13877,'enUS','My brother must have sent you. He wouldn\'t have done so unless you are capable of doing what must be done.$B$BFor all of our sakes I hope that he\'s right.$B$BThe elementals here are now my allies. You must do as they ask if we are to prevent the destruction of the rest of Ashenvale.',0),
(13878,'enUS','You save the wolves! So brave! Someday, maybe you get a wolf just like that to ride.$B$B<Dorak looks at the burning stables, then at the nearby river.>$B$BWhat should I do now?',0),
(13879,'enUS','<The goblin stares at you and blinks several times before speaking.>$B$BThe spirits whispered that help would soon arrive.$B$BPardon my surprise, but I was hoping the spirits would guide someone a little more... heroic.$B$BThese elementals are trusted allies. Listen to them and do their bidding. If we fail, there will remain nothing in Ashenvale worth fighting for.',0),
(13880,'enUS','Well done, $R. Lord Magmathar\'s fire is now trapped, restrained within the earth once more.',0),
(13881,'enUS','<Kathrena recoils at your description of the ravaged animals and the cruel device at the bottom of the lake>$B$B$n, this is terrible. What is that thing, and how did it get there? Something is devouring these animals, physically and spiritually. I had suspected the satyrs or some sort of disease was the culprit, but this is shaping up to be something ... unnatural.',0),
(13882,'enUS','Perfect, this is everything. Did you have fun collecting the wisp? I used to chase the wisps around Ashenvale when I was just a girl.$B$B<Lost in memories for a moment, Kathrena suddenly grows somber.>$B$BI\'m afraid I\'ve found out what we\'re dealing with.',0),
(13883,'enUS','Good work, $R.$B$BI\'ll show them how an armored ship should be built!',0),
(13884,'enUS','You acquitted yourself well in battle on the field. However, I\'m afraid that Lord Magmathar has taken notice of you and the destruction that you\'ve wreaked upon his minions.$B$BYou will have to deal with him or he is sure to burn you alive, $n.',0),
(13885,'enUS','So the animals are safe, then. Thank you, thank you!$B$BBut now it\'s time to turn our attention to the source.',0),
(13886,'enUS','It is done. The power of fire is subdued and the four elements are returned to harmony.$B$BYou have saved the rest of Ashenvale through your brave and selfless actions, $n. You have our eternal thanks.',0),
(13887,'enUS','Good work. Honestly, I\'m amazed you were able to find this many. With each clutch, they seem fewer in number.$B$BI\'ll let you raise one of the freshly-hatched venomhides. It shouldn\'t be shy about letting you know what it needs.',0),
(13888,'enUS','You\'ve done it! The spirits were right after all!$B$BThe power of fire is subdued and the four elements are returned to harmony.$B$BThe rest of Ashenvale is spared this fiery fate. You have the eternal thanks of the Earthen Ring.',0),
(13889,'enUS','The venomhide hatchling seems satisfied with the giant meal you\'ve provided, but there\'s no way of telling when it will be hungry again.',0),
(13890,'enUS','Nice work, $R!$B$BNo more ships will run aground, thanks to you.',0),
(13891,'enUS','Love of Elune, look at you. That must\'ve been some fight! You\'re covered in what looks like... chowder.$B$BIf a mere minion could cause so much agony here in Darkshore, I can\'t even imagine the suffering that a true Old One could bring about.$B$BWell, at least the animals are safe for now. I will plant the sapling you created to help rebuild this shattered land. Thank you, $n! I\'d give you a hug but, you know. Chowder.',0),
(13892,'enUS','This is dire news, $n. If you are correct, then we\'d best act swiftly and decisively.$B$BWe cannot allow this \"Soggoth\" to be brought back to life.',0),
(13893,'enUS','The dwarf\'s story is unsettling... yet informative. It seems we have few options left.',0),
(13895,'enUS','Aros\'s body appears to be lifeless yet still warm. Perhaps his killers are nearby.',0),
(13896,'enUS','Oh, we know a thing or two about this Soggoth. The question is... do you really want to know?',0),
(13897,'enUS','We can finally rest here now, $n. It appears Darkshore has been saved -- and we have you to thank for it.',0),
(13898,'enUS','Well done, $n. The naga seek the destruction and subjugation of all surface-dwellers -- do not hesitate to drive them out of our lands and back into the shadowy ocean depths where they belong.',0),
(13899,'enUS','The walord doesn\'t seem to have the horn on him. Perhaps he was telling the truth.',0),
(13900,'enUS','You\'ve done well, $n. Unfortunately the battle is far from over.',0),
(13901,'enUS','Excellent!$B$BLet the naga retreat back into the seas where they belong!',0),
(13902,'enUS','If Malfurion placed his trust on you, then so shall I. You\'ll find that our enemies greatly outnumber us this far south.$B$BWhere brute force and numbers fail us, strategy and guile will prove our biggest advantages.',0),
(13903,'enUS','Your venomhide hatchling flashes you a toothy smile and then settles in for a nap.',0),
(13904,'enUS','Your hatchling licks its lips after devouring the meal of silithid eggs. For a moment, you think it seems disappointed that feeding time has come to an end.',0),
(13905,'enUS','The venomhide hatchling accepts the feathers and begins looking them over, holding several up to its armbands.',0),
(13906,'enUS','It looks like both of you have managed to do some growing without killing one another.$B$BThere, everything\'s finished. I\'ve trained your venomhide ravasaur to respond when you blow this whistle.$B$BFew have the dedication to hand-feed and raise a venomhide, but they\'re well worth the effort.',0),
(13907,'enUS','Bravo, $n! Now let\'s take a look-see at our new situation.$B$BWhat? MORE murlocs? I swear on my stones, the more murlocs you kill, the more murlocs appear. Is it just me? We\'re going to need a new approach.',0),
(13909,'enUS','<Archaeologist Groff picks through the wreckage.>$B$BWell, not much here that don\'t look stepped on, sat on, or soaked in a toilet. But toss some thatch on top and it\'ll do.$B$BTell me, $n, do you consider yourself an architect?',0),
(13910,'enUS','Har har, that sounds like quite a heap you built there. Did they take to it? Good, good! Let\'s see if my plan comes to fruition.$B$B<Archaeologist Groff watches as scores of murlocs stream down the beach, pouring into the hovel from all corners of the compass. Gradually his brows knit together.>$B$BWhat have I done?',0),
(13911,'enUS','Ah, you\'ve helped the Prospector find his missing journal! To think it was here all along.$B$BSomeday you\'ll have to show me this other set of ruins he\'s always going on about.',0),
(13912,'enUS','Spectacular! Good work, $n. I\'m sure Remtravel would thank you himself if he could remember your name.$B$BLook at the surface of the disc - these microscopic etchings - this is amazing. I\'m certain this strange wheel holds information, if only we could read it...',0),
(13913,'enUS','Thank you, $n. Grim news you bring of the rest of the gnome team, but at least you managed to save a few. For that I am grateful.',0),
(13914,'enUS','The venomhide hatchling accepts the feathers and begins looking them over, holding several up to its armbands.',0),
(13915,'enUS','The venomhide hatchling seems satisfied with the giant meal you\'ve provided, but there\'s no way of telling when it will be hungry again.',0),
(13916,'enUS','Your hatchling licks its lips after devouring the meal of silithid eggs. For a moment, you think it seems disappointed that feeding time has come to an end.',0),
(13917,'enUS','Your venomhide hatchling flashes you a toothy smile and then settles in for a nap.',0),
(13918,'enUS','Why yes, yes, this is it! See here, the slot is the exact dimensions of the ancient disc, just as I\'d surmised. Here\'s your reward, $n - you\'ve earned it.$B$B$B$BAre you ready to meet history face to face? Let\'s see what the ancients have to say!',0),
(13920,'enUS','These venison should make our soldiers\' spirits rise for the coming battles. Here\'s something for your troubles.',0),
(13921,'enUS','<The satyr sneers, but when he realizes you are not here to chastise him, he changes his expression.>$B$BFinally, my redemption is at hand. I have waited long for this day and I think I know how to help you in turn.',0),
(13922,'enUS','You have all of the moonstones that are needed. And yet, it is said that a sacrifice of life is the only way to be ensure the saving of another.$B$BI will ensure that no matter what, the moonstones will cure Relara.',0),
(13923,'enUS','You come here as a child, $R.$B$BYou shall leave here a battle-hardened $C of the Horde!$B$BThat, or a corpse....',0),
(13924,'enUS','Oh, $n, you have saved my daughter! I know the power of the moonstones will give back my daughter her strength!$B$BI can never repay you fully for the aid you have given me, but... please, take this. Other than Relara, it is my most dear possession.',0),
(13925,'enUS','Interesting ... It sounds like our cure will keep the wildlife safe, but you say you saw something else? Some kind of angry presence?$B$BThis is a good sign, $n. Whatever is behind this isn\'t happy, and that means we\'re on to something.',0),
(13926,'enUS','You take us away from puppy-men hatchlings? Good. We like you already. Mean puppy-men hatchlings took all our favorite toys away.',0),
(13927,'enUS','You take Kekek hunting? Good to get away from mean old orphan lady who doesn\'t let Kekek hunt.',0),
(13928,'enUS','Thank you, $C. We have our hands full defending the retreat, but when I can catch my breath, I\'ll see to it that these sisters are returned to life, the goddess willing.$B$BYou\'ve demonstrated your prowess... we can use your help.',0),
(13929,'enUS','We never knew trees got that big! Nope. Maybe Great Ones had special plan for it?',0),
(13930,'enUS','This is Kekek\'s kind of city. Bear-men fight for home just like Frenzyheart do. Orphan lady tell Kekek not to fight with other pups, but Kekek fight anyway.',0),
(13933,'enUS','We very glad you brought us here, $n. We always worried what would happen to us when the orphan matron found us in Sholazar.',0),
(13934,'enUS','See? Kekek never get tired of saying, \"Kekek tell you so.\"$B$BMaybe now you believe other things Kekek tell you, like how sky is green.',0),
(13935,'enUS','A brutal display, but one fitting for the enemies of Ashenvale. The Horde dares to think that they can take our beloved forest away from us.$B$BThey are fatally mistaken!$B$BYou have saved Raynewood from destruction, $n. Surely we can find a reward suitable for our champion?',0),
(13936,'enUS','Let me tell ya somethin\' $C!$B$BThe bossman simply doesn\'t appreciate the art and craftsmanship that goes into making fine explosives.',0),
(13937,'enUS','That was fun! We like toy store. Maybe orphan matron take us sometimes. We ask. Maybe you tell her too?',0),
(13938,'enUS','Kekek like playing with paper zeppelin. Not as good as hunting, but give something to do when bored at orphanage.',0),
(13940,'enUS','You\'re just in time, $n. I don\'t know how much longer we can hold.',0),
(13942,'enUS','This is PERFECT!$B$BOh, just wait \'til you see what I can do with this....',0),
(13943,'enUS','Well done, $R. But there is much that remains to be done here.',0),
(13944,'enUS','So, Tweedle found a way to get those explosives working, eh?$B$BIt\'s about time...',0),
(13945,'enUS','Impressive. I hope my huntress carried her weight.$B$BIf we continue with this fervor, we may yet still free Teldrassil from the corruption that Alexstrasza herself could not burn out.',0),
(13946,'enUS','Good. I know this probably wasn\'t very pleasant work, but we greatly appreciate it.$B$BI fear for our dear Teldrassil... it seems it is becoming more corrupt by the day, and our ignorance to the cause is plaguing me greatly.',0),
(13947,'enUS','Your deeds today shall live long in the Horde\'s glorious history.$B$BYour efforts have dealt a devastating blow to the enemy!',0),
(13948,'enUS','This is dire news, $n. If you are correct, then we\'d best act swiftly and decisively.$B$BWe cannot allow this \"Soggoth\" to be brought back to life.',0),
(13949,'enUS','You\'re a sight, $R. That\'s the first caravan to make it through this week!',0),
(13950,'enUS','That was fun! We go again sometime? We can\'t wait to see our new friend again!',0),
(13951,'enUS','Kekek like new Snowfall friends, maybe come back and go hunting together sometime. Maybe we go tip over walrus-men when they sleeping.',0),
(13952,'enUS','Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),
(13953,'enUS','The naga are in league with the Twilight\'s Hammer? Just what we needed.',0),
(13954,'enUS','Do you think she ever saw an oracle before? We might be the first one ever to meet her! We thinks she liked us, but we\'re not sure. She doesn\'t talk a lot. Nope. But that was fun!',0),
(13955,'enUS','Queen not what Kekek expected, but Kekek understand why. Queen\'s visitors get crushed if she was always big dragon! Still want to see someday.',0),
(13956,'enUS','We got to meet a Great One! Too bad it was during his nap time, but we understand. We like naps, too! Maybe we learn naps from Great Ones like we learn about shrines and shinies!$B$BCan we come back and visit the Great One again when not sleeping?',0),
(13957,'enUS','You help Kekek learn him a book? Then, Kekek hunt with Hemet Nesingwary!',0),
(13958,'enUS','<Thagg listens intently as you recount your assault on Astranaar.>$B$BThis is good news indeed, $R. But right now, we need more than just good news here.$B$BThese triage kits will be put to good use!',0),
(13959,'enUS','It sounds like little Roo had a great time this week. I know he was getting awfully lonely in the orphanage and was eager to make some new friends. Thank you so much for agreeing to look after him.',0),
(13960,'enUS','Thank you for agreeing to care for Kekek this week. I know he can be a handful, but I think that with more individual attention and a few more friends, he\'ll do a lot better. No doubt he\'s going to be telling stories of his adventures with you for weeks.',0),
(13961,'enUS','Oh my. We want to question this Quilboar, not tenderize him!',0),
(13962,'enUS','Very well, $n.$B$BYou have succeeded where I could not. You have earned my respect.',0),
(13963,'enUS','Very interesting - our brute here seems both enthralled and terrified of the one they call \"Tortusk.\" A powerful leader can inspire his people to acts of greatness or atrocity... but we orcs would know that more than others.$B$BWe should turn our attention to this Tortusk problem.',0),
(13964,'enUS','Good to finally meet you, $n. I\'ve heard all about what you\'ve been up to and let me just say that I\'m impressed!$B$BThink you can lend us your expertise?',0),
(13965,'enUS','You say that Faldreas sent you? Good man.$B$BAs it happens, we could use your help.',0),
(13967,'enUS','Good work, $R.$B$BThis should keep them licking their wounds for a time.',0),
(13968,'enUS','Ah, so Tortusk behaved as I expected? Went right for your throat? It is good that he\'s dead.$B$BThe Razormane quilboar have been separated from their leadership in the southern Barrens, no doubt allowing an animal like him to come to power. Perhaps without his influence we can start a dialogue with the survivors... Although hotter heads may prevail.',0),
(13969,'enUS','This poor battered kodo looks to be on the verge of death, but is still breathing. The Razormane haven\'t even plundered its cargo yet. If it can be revived, you may be able to save the entire shipment.',0),
(13970,'enUS','The Kodo is voracious! You might as well be pouring those sacks of grain into a hole!$B$BAlready the animal is beginning to perk up.',0),
(13971,'enUS','So that was your handiwork, $R? Yes, the missing Kodo arrived just minutes ago. It will take many nights to nurse the poor beast\'s wounds, but thanks to you it\'s alive. And you saved a whole shipment!$B$BPlease, take your pick of the gear that the kodo was carrying.',0),
(13973,'enUS','I see you\'ve left a string of corpses in your wake, $R. I couldn\'t have done better. The livestock may be lost, but the land remains ours - thank you!',0),
(13974,'enUS','Well, look at this! Little Tweedle has really come through this time. This stuff blew up Astranaar, you say?$B$BAs you can see, we don\'t need any help taking over Silverwind Refuge, but Tweedle\'s ideas are as small as his hands.$B$BIf this stuff\'s really as good as you say, there\'s no limit to what we might do....',0),
(13975,'enUS','It\'s about time we got some supplies through here. It\'s bad enough to be severed from Mulgore, but this city would fall apart if we lost our trade with Orgrimmar.',0),
(13976,'enUS','$C, you must be wary! Kaliva, the foul demoness who has chained us is nearby!',0),
(13977,'enUS','<Jinx examines the powder carefully for a moment.>$B$BHmmm.$B$BIt\'ll take a little time. But yes, we can put this into a bomb....',0),
(13979,'enUS','That\'s better. Without him, their technicians are sure to fall back to their normal laziness, which should result in fewer bombs and more accidents.',0),
(13980,'enUS','Nice work, friend.$B$BYour skills have bought us the time we needed to prepare the bomb. It\'s almost complete!',0),
(13981,'enUS','They what? IT\'S HOW BIG?!!!$B$BI have a very bad feeling about this, $n.',0),
(13982,'enUS','Disgusting, I know, but if we three are to be free of Kaliva\'s chains, it is not enough that she is dead.$B$BWe must eat of her fel heart!',0),
(13983,'enUS','This looks right, $C.$B$BI should have your shredder put together in no time.',0),
(13985,'enUS','A fine job, my little $R friend. But as you can see, I am a little busy here.',0),
(13986,'enUS','Oh, my shield! I won\'t be using it anytime soon, but thank you. I hate that I\'m sitting here useless when I could be helping on the front, but fighting with my arm like this won\'t help anyone.$B$BTake care out there, won\'t you?',0),
(13987,'enUS','You\'ve saved us all, $n! I have the power to finish off these final few.$B$BNo longer will the forest have to fear the Burning Legion!',0),
(13988,'enUS','I am glad Tonga was able to witness the overgrowth firsthand - words can\'t convey the scope of the damage. Did you bring his totem? I will return it to him when I am finished here.',0),
(13989,'enUS','Good. Murgut sold his own tribe out to the Horde, allying with them when they took your precious Silverwind Refuge in order to \'save\' his people.$B$BHe sold them into slavery, or worse. And now he has gotten what he deserved!$B$BLet us speak now of a different traitor, one whom I believe has something that will make that rod of yours even more powerful.',0),
(13991,'enUS','I was hoping for a squad of grunts... but if you earned Sergra\'s respect, I suppose you\'ll be more than enough. Let me explain what\'s happening here.',0),
(13992,'enUS','Oh, ho! That was beautiful. I probably shouldn\'t have stayed to watch. Now that they\'re looking for you, I\'ll slip quietly away in the dust of their aimless gallopin\'.$B$BBe sure to look for my buds at the other pools. Boss has agents at every one.',0),
(13995,'enUS','Aw mon, why you have to go settin\' Gorgal off like that? Still, I can\'t argue with results. We\'ll need to watch these animals closely to see what they do with Kurak outta the way.$B$BMore watchin\' and waitin\'. Gorgal won\'t like that.',0),
(13998,'enUS','Explosive spore clouds? You don\'t say ... tell me more. Choking? Stinging? Burning of the eyes? Was there itching? Nausea? Mortification? Delightful, DELIGHTFUL! You\'ve certainly earned your commission, $n.$B$BThat skin rash of yours should pass in a day or two.',0),
(13999,'enUS','Quiet! Give me those notes. Were you followed here?',0),
(14001,'enUS','Oh, thank heavens that you survived, $n! I thought for sure that you\'d drowned when I saw you go over the side!$B$B$B$BLook at all of these folks you saved!',0),
(14003,'enUS','Sputtervalve scored us a Samophlange? Lemme see that thing!$B$BYeah, we can get this working again, no problem. Hand me that huge mallet...',0),
(14004,'enUS','Wenikee said what? Copperplug? BOSS Copperplug? Oh no, this might be tricky.',0),
(14005,'enUS','Elune be praised!$B$BEverything I had encountered suggested this corruption to be buried deep within Teldrassil itself... I had worried we might never be able to strike at the source without killing the world tree. I am thankful I was wrong!$B$BMalfurion was the start to this great turn of fortune. Perhaps I will seek him out before I depart to the wilds again.$B$BThank you, $n. Thank you for everything you have done. You are sure to be a great hero someday!',0),
(14006,'enUS','You found it! Wow, it\'s over 600 pages, only 30 of which are intentionally left blank.$B$BLet\'s see. Chapter three: Backsplicing the Reverse Crankshaft Flywheel Pulley? Interesting. Chapter seven: Valve Timing for the High-Pressure Expansion Condenser!? This stuff is great! And I still don\'t even know what this thing does.$B$BHere, have some of my old tools. Let\'s fire this thing up one last time!',0),
(14007,'enUS','There you go, boss!$B$BCome back anytime you want more training. I\'ll teach you what I know.',0),
(14008,'enUS','There you go, boss!$B$BCome back anytime you want more training. I\'ll teach you what I know.',0),
(14009,'enUS','There you go, boss!$B$BCome back anytime you want more training. I\'ll teach you what I know.',0),
(14010,'enUS','There you go, boss!$B$BCome back anytime you want more training. I\'ll teach you what I know.',0),
(14011,'enUS','There you go, boss!$B$BCome back anytime you want more training. I\'ll teach you what I know.',0),
(14012,'enUS','There you go, boss!$B$BCome back anytime you want more training. I\'ll teach you what I know.',0),
(14013,'enUS','$C-Matic NX-01 is programmed to serve.$B$BReturn anytime you seek more training. This unit will teach you what it knows.',0),
(14014,'enUS','<Sassy breathes a sigh of relief when she sees all of the tools and bombs that you recovered.>$B$BI thought we were doomed for sure. But now we can start working on a way to get off of this island!',0),
(14016,'enUS','<Crusader Rhydalla frowns.>$B$BDo you think they\'ve been planning this? I suppose it doesn\'t matter, but I don\'t like the implication that we\'ve been playing into their hands. Whatever is going on, we have to stop it.',0),
(14017,'enUS','The doctor will not have time to complete his work, but his plan is already in motion. From what you\'ve reported, the Lich King\'s servants have reanimated and empowered the Black Knight and there\'s no telling what the knight\'s master has in mind. You have done well in uncovering this plot. I will tell High Crusader Adelard of your findings and together, we will alert the tournament\'s participants.',0),
(14019,'enUS','They launched up into the air when they ate the bananas?! That is hilarious!$B$BI think I\'m going to take a bunch out there and feed them myself!',0),
(14021,'enUS','We\'ve hit the mother lode!!!$B$BNow, what\'s all this about a pygmy witchdoctor in charge of the monkeys? Is he dead? Because if he\'s dead, then legally I can stake my claim... not that I wasn\'t going to do that anyway. By $R law, all Kaja\'mite belongs to us!',0),
(14022,'enUS','If you\'d like to learn to cook Pilgrim\'s Bounty foods, I can help. If you\'re not already a cook, all you have to do is train and you\'ll be cooking in no time!',0),
(14023,'enUS','Excellent. This is just what we needed. It\'s going to be a chore keeping all the tables stocked with fresh food, but it\'s well worth it.',0),
(14024,'enUS','The pumpkin pie\'s been a big hit up here. I\'ve never seen a dwarf get so excited about anything made from a vegetable.',0),
(14028,'enUS','Finally, the cranberry chutney I was promised. You wouldn\'t believe how fast the celebrants go through the stuff here.',0),
(14030,'enUS','Thanks for bringing everything. I was starting to get worried.$B$BWhile you\'re here, you should try your hand at making some candied sweet potatoes.',0),
(14031,'enUS','What are these?$B$B<Sassy examines the pictures while listening to your tale from the Kaja\'mite cavern.>$B$BClearly that pygmy witchdoctor is from some new race never seen before. Maybe we should call them $n-ians?$B$BThey must be the ones that painted all of that stuff in the cavern. I\'m not sure that I like what you\'re describing.$B$BIt sounds to me like they\'re paintings of them and us on an island with an exploding volcano!',0),
(14033,'enUS','Ah, candied sweet potatoes! My favorite! Did Isaac tell you?',0),
(14034,'enUS','Ah, this is it - this is it right here! So his flagship is named \"The Bellipotent\" eh?$B$BLet\'s see what it\'ll take to send this nuisance to the bottom of the sea.',0),
(14035,'enUS','These are beautiful and just in time to feed hungry feasters. Thank you, $n. You\'ve truly mastered all the courses of a traditional Pilgrim\'s Bounty meal.',0),
(14036,'enUS','If you\'d like to learn to cook Pilgrim\'s Bounty foods, I can help. If you\'re not already a cook, all you have to do is train and you\'ll be cooking in no time.',0),
(14036,'ruRU','Если хочешь научиться готовить особые блюда Пиршества странников – я могу тебе помочь. Главное – знать основы кулинарии!',25549),
(14037,'enUS','It\'s a chore keeping all these tables stocked. If you stop and think about it, it\'s strange going to so much trouble when we needn\'t eat anymore.$B$B<William shrugs.>$B$BTradition is tradition.',0),
(14038,'enUS','Excellent! I wish I could\'ve seen the look on that Rear Admiral\'s face when his flagship went up like a candle. Let me use my telescope here to take a look at the damage.$B$BWhat - Whhhaaatt!? That thing is still floating? Hartley must\'ve moved the munitions ashore in case his ship was mined.$B$BI underestimated you, Hartley... but for the last time!',0),
(14039,'enUS','Ah, the blessed waters from our moonwells. You have borne witness to the Spirit of the Kaldorei, then?$B$BIn recent times, I\'ve come to find that the spirit offers more questions than it does answers, but such is the continuing nature of discovery that drives us in our darkest hours.$B$BI will offer you the simplest answers that I can. Malfurion has returned to me... to us... but harsh times are yet upon us. Staghelm is gone and the world is wracked with pain - Malfurion has much to mend, and he will need help.',0),
(14040,'enUS','The pie always goes first. I think people must be skipping the meal and going directly for the dessert. Have you given it a try yet?',0),
(14041,'enUS','Ah, more cranberry chutney! You wouldn\'t believe how fast the celebrants go through it.',0),
(14042,'enUS','Hah! Beautiful work, $n. Those Alliance cretins will never trace this back to me. Meanwhile, it\'s back to business as usual: smuggling, double-dealing, price-gouging... I\'ve got a lot of work to catch up on.$B$BHere, I\'ll let you in on a cut of my future profits. Enjoy!',0),
(14043,'enUS','So Dokin drafted you to help with the candied sweet potatoes?$B$B<Francis smiles.>$B$BIt\'s the only way he can keep up. Thanks for bringing these.',0),
(14044,'enUS','Thanks for bringing everything. Some of the tables were starting to look a little bereft of serving dishes.',0),
(14045,'enUS','Hah-har! So ol\' Gazzy ain\'t given up on his goods yet, has he? Well, looks like that ol\' floppy-eared goldgrubbler jes\' gave me somethin\' ta bargain with.',0),
(14046,'enUS','<The Baron rubs his sore wrists, his face widening into a malevolent grin.>$B$BOh I won\'t be runnin\' off just yet. I\'ll free me mates and murder my way out of here at a time of me choosin\'. As fer you - a deal\'s a deal. Let\'s talk about that treasure...',0),
(14047,'enUS','These look perfect. Thank you, $n. You\'ve truly mastered all the courses of a traditional Pilgrim\'s Bounty meal.',0),
(14048,'enUS','These are just what I need. Thanks, $n. You\'re a lifesaver.',0),
(14049,'enUS','What? What is this? I send you out to fetch my treasure and you bring me a big filthy head?',0),
(14050,'enUS','Nice work, $n!$B$BOh, the Baron tried to stop you, did he? Well, I hope you gave him a pounding.$B$BNow, I promised you a cut of the goods you recovered. Let\'s see... what\'s one percent of a half percent? Ah, here you go.',0),
(14051,'enUS','Thank goodness! I wouldn\'t be able to serve the feast without spice bread stuffing.',0),
(14052,'enUS','Hey hey mon, did Dizzywig send you? Good, good. Did you bring the money? No? ...what about the guns?',0),
(14053,'enUS','Thanks. This looks great, and you\'re a fair bit faster than Jasper, but don\'t tell him I said so.',0),
(14054,'enUS','These are perfect. Isaac, and everyone else, will love them!',0),
(14055,'enUS','These are perfect. Thanks for helping me with this, $n. The meal will get served on time and Ellen will be happy.',0),
(14056,'enUS','Look at that. We\'re loaded! In mutiny, you gotta make the money first. Then when you get the money, you get the power. Let\'s go get some power, $n...',0),
(14057,'enUS','<Tony unhinges one of the weapons and peers down the barrel.>$B$BOooh, very nice. Shiny. Loud. Now we\'re talkin\'.$B$BNot much left to do but close the deal...',0),
(14058,'enUS','Thanks, $n. Now, I can help the hostess out and still keep my word to Roberta.',0),
(14059,'enUS','Thanks for your help, and let me know if you ever get to the bottom of the case of the disappearing chutney.',0),
(14060,'enUS','These are great! Thank you for helping, $n.',0),
(14061,'enUS','These turkeys are exactly what I needed. Thanks for helping me out of a tough situation.',0),
(14062,'enUS','Perfect timing! I wouldn\'t be able to serve the feast without spice bread stuffing.',0),
(14063,'enUS','So Tony is running the show there now? Good! We need more pirates like him in these waters. He\'s a real businessman.$B$B<Dizzywig rubs his hands together greedily.>$B$BSpeaking of business, I suppose I owe you a cut. Would you be interested in insuring any of your new loot? You never know what can happen in a town like this...',0),
(14064,'enUS','What a feast, hmmm?$B$BI\'m so glad you could celebrate the spirit of Pilgrim\'s Bounty with us.',0),
(14065,'enUS','What a feast, hmmm?$B$BI\'m so glad you could celebrate the spirit of Pilgrim\'s Bounty with us.',0),
(14065,'ruRU','Ах, какой пир!$B$BСпасибо, что $gприсоединился:присоединилась; к празднованию Пиршества странников!',25549),
(14066,'enUS','This Horde caravan was not merely robbed. It was savagely brutalized. Crates of supplies have been ripped apart by sharp claws. The wagon has been demolished. The food has been eaten and the silver is gone, and yet useful supplies have been left behind...',0),
(14067,'enUS','<Gazrog opens the lockbox and begins counting up the silver while you relate your story.>$B$BWhat!? Raptors? Just the raptors? Assaulting our caravans and looting them? Perhaps they are as intelligent as the rumors say. As if we didn\'t have enough problems, now we\'ve got to deal with brainy lizards with a lust for coin.$B$BHere, $n - you\'ve earned a share of the rescued silver. Thank you.',0),
(14068,'enUS','Hooway! You twapped the waptors I was wooking for! Now we will twain them for twolls to wide to swaughter the Awwiance!',0),
(14069,'enUS','I couldn\'t have done better myself. In fact, I didn\'t.$B$BI\'m sure that in no time at all we\'ll all be talking about the great and powerful, and may I add extremely wealthy, Trade Prince $n!',0),
(14070,'enUS','A complete success if I do say so myself, sir! Your debtors will think twice now about not paying up!$B$B<Sassy taps her pencil against her lower lip for a moment, deep in thought.>$B$BPerhaps we should increase interest rates on loans across the board?',0),
(14071,'enUS','Well done, sir. You all look very good riding around in the hot rod. I\'m sure you made quite an impression on the citizenry.',0),
(14072,'enUS','Good work, $n. Did you look through these? They\'re barely legible - more like angry graffiti than war plans. Hatred, jealousy, rage, personal conflicts - it\'s a wonder Verog can keep these centaur from killing each other, much less form them into an army.$B$BWe can use this to our advantage.',0),
(14073,'enUS','Ah, I\'ve heard about your work, $C. Your timing is fortunate - I\'ve got a major offensive in the works.',0),
(14074,'enUS','These look a little worse for wear, but they\'re still edible. The crusaders will be glad to hear that we\'ve managed to recover some of the ship\'s cargo.',0),
(14075,'enUS','I say good riddance to those pests!',0),
(14076,'enUS','Well done, $n. I\'ll take these to the Argent Crusade\'s keepers right away. They\'ll have no choice but to acknowledge that we\'re doing far more than the Sunreavers to keep the coliseum running smoothly.',0),
(14077,'enUS','<Narasi accepts the prayer book from you.>$B$BThank you. The book was a gift from Confessor Paletress herself. She would be honored to know that you have used it to bring tranquility to the slain.',0),
(14078,'enUS','Deep claw marks run through the man\'s corpse.',0),
(14079,'enUS','So, shall we begin your Apprentice Riding training?',0),
(14080,'enUS','Your actions have shown that we stand as one with the Argent Crusade, while the Sunreavers are too busy preening to take up their blades.',0),
(14081,'enUS','So, shall we begin your Apprentice Riding training?',0),
(14081,'ruRU','Итак, начнем урок обучение верховой езды?',25549),
(14082,'enUS','So, shall we begin your Apprentice Riding training?',0),
(14083,'enUS','So, shall we begin your Apprentice Riding training?',0),
(14084,'enUS','So, shall we begin your Apprentice Riding training?',0),
(14085,'enUS','So, shall we begin your Apprentice Riding training?',0),
(14086,'enUS','So, shall we begin your Apprentice Riding training?',0),
(14087,'enUS','So, shall we begin your Apprentice Riding training?',0),
(14088,'enUS','So, shall we begin your Apprentice Riding training?',0),
(14089,'enUS','So, shall we begin your Apprentice Riding training?',0),
(14090,'enUS','The sooner we get these stinking things out of my sight and into their cage, the faster my mood will improve. I wish the Argent Crusade had given the Sunreavers the care of this creature. They\'re enough alike that they ought to be able to understand each other.',0),
(14091,'enUS','It\'s you again. Looks like you\'re not one to hide in the face of danger. Very well, then.',0),
(14092,'enUS','I\'ll let the crusaders know that you\'ve just returned with a fresh load of food while the Silver Covenant was sitting on its heels.',0),
(14093,'enUS','It\'s no use, $n! They\'re not letting up.',0),
(14094,'enUS','Excellent! I\'ll make sure these get taken to a safe place.',0),
(14095,'enUS','I knew that Kraken was not a match for the likes of you. Without that Kraken disrupting those boats, those Kvaldir will have no choice but to retreat. Great job, Champion!',0),
(14096,'enUS','Thanks to you, Kul and the aspirants will live to fight the Scourge again. That\'s far from the first time someone\'s had to save Kul from himself. My only hope is that the crusaders can find a better outlet for his enthusiasm than allowing him to impart all of his bad habits to impressionable young aspirants.',0),
(14098,'enUS','Good job, $n. Thanks to you, many Gilneans will live to see another day.',0),
(14099,'enUS','We\'re all fine here. A little shaken... but alive.',0),
(14100,'enUS','Ah, you\'ve mastered the four totems. You should be proud of your accomplishments so far, young $R, but this is only the beginning of your journey.$B$BHere, accept this gift from the Earthen Ring. Carry this relic with you and you will have the power of all four elements at your command.$B$BContinue your training, friend. Grave challenges are ahead for this world - I can hear it in the wind and feel it in the rumblings of the earth. We must be prepared for the worst.',0),
(14101,'enUS','The defeat of the drottinn will set the kvaldir to fighting amongst themselves, buying us time to use our advantage. The crusade and the tournament are in your debt, champion.',0),
(14102,'enUS','You have bought us valuable time to move against the Kvaldir and free the seas of these pests. Once again, the Argent Crusade is in your debt.',0),
(14103,'enUS','Wonderful! Another batch of powder!$B$BJust between us jewelcrafters, I\'ve been making hand over fist selling \"pure titanium\" jewelry to the local Dalaran mages. Even with their superior intellect, they aren\'t particularly savvy with their gold. If you get more, I\'ll be here.',0),
(14104,'enUS','Ornolf\'s crew will want to avenge their leader, but without him, they will be easier to defeat. We must live to carry out our mission, to see Icecrown rid of the Scourge and other evils.',0),
(14105,'enUS','You are truly an example to all who have gathered beneath our banner, $n. Together, we will show the Scourge that we will not be defeated.',0),
(14107,'enUS','You have done our fallen brethren a great service and spared us the need to face them again on the field of battle. As our campaign against the Scourge progresses, I find myself thinking about my own fate.$B$BShould I fall, $n, I would want someone like you to do for me what you have done for the spirits of the fallen this day. I could not bear the thought of forcing my own brothers to slay me again and again.',0),
(14108,'enUS','Crusader, you may have bought those sailors just enough time to escape, Maybe next time, those Silver Covenant and Sunreavers will listen before running head first at the enemy.',0),
(14109,'enUS','Oh, you are going to look so fine, but not as gorgeous as me! You\'re going to replace the Trade Prince any day now at the rate you\'re going!$B$BI can\'t wait to not have to work anymore! You\'re going to buy me everything that I want, right babe?$B$BLet me have all that stuff and I\'ll help you get into it right before the party.',0),
(14110,'enUS','Oh yeah, you\'re going to look hot! You\'re going to replace the Trade Prince any day now at the rate you\'re going!$B$BI can\'t wait to be a kept man!$B$BLet me have all that stuff and I\'ll help you get into it right before the party.',0),
(14112,'enUS','I\'m glad we\'ve gotten that done. It\'s not the most glorious task in the world, but when we partnered with the Argent Crusade, we promised to do all they asked of us without complaint. Of course, the same cannot be said of the Sunreavers.',0),
(14113,'enUS','Very nicely done, sir. The party appears to have been a smashing success!$B$BEr... what\'s that?',0),
(14115,'enUS','Phew, that was close, boss. Unfortunately, I\'m the bearer of more bad news.$B$BPlease don\'t shoot me....',0),
(14116,'enUS','Well, well, well, if it isn\'t my wayward protege, Mr. $n.$B$BI\'m hurt and disappointed. You didn\'t send me an invitation to your little party out there. Sorry about the crashers... you know how pirates can be.$B$BSo, shall we get down to business?',0),
(14117,'enUS','Excellent. As their scouts fail to report in, Talrendis will feel the terror they\'ve tried in vain to inflict on us.',0),
(14118,'enUS','Meat - and lots of it! Well done. This will keep bellies full as we build our arsenal.',0),
(14120,'enUS','A bazillion macaroons?!?! Where are we going to get that kind of moolah?$B$B<Sassy thinks a moment.>$B$BUm... did the Trade Prince say anything about letting me escape with you on his yacht?',0),
(14121,'enUS','Wow, you really did it?! Well, they had it coming, I guess.$B$BThat\'s an awful lot of loot. Do you think it\'s enough to get you a spot on the Trade Prince\'s yacht?$B$BAre you going to be able to bring anyone with you? I don\'t make too much working in marketing.',0),
(14122,'enUS','Hey, you have been saving! I\'m so proud of you!$B$B<Sassy counts all of your macaroons.>$B$BUm, boss... this isn\'t nearly enough.',0),
(14123,'enUS','Oh, wow! These are worth a fortune.$B$B<Slinky eyes everything with a practiced, greed-filled eye.>$B$BI just hope that the Trade Prince doesn\'t notice them when you hand them over with the rest of your wealth....',0),
(14124,'enUS','Nicely done, sir, nicely done! That\'s a fortune you have there in your bags.$B$BWith all of that, I bet the Trade Prince will let all of us come along on his yacht!',0),
(14125,'enUS','This is nothing. You should see Bilgewater Port... the whole thing is going up in flames!$B$BFine, fine, I don\'t have time to inspect this place. Here\'s the moolah from the Bilgewater Cartel\'s insurance policy.$B$BI\'ve got to find a way off the island! Good luck, $n!',0),
(14126,'enUS','Congratulations, you just made it. I see that you\'ve brought me all that I asked for, including your hot rod.$B$B<The Trade Prince flashes an evil grin.>$B$BA bazillion macaroons couldn\'t have been easy to come by. I\'m now the wealthiest, most powerful, $R on all of Azeroth!$B$BTOO BAD FOR YOU THAT I\'M CHANGING THE TERMS OF OUR DEAL!$B$BYou\'re now my slave. Get below deck and take a turn shoveling coal. Next stop, Azshara!$B$BMuahahahahahahahaha!',0),
(14127,'enUS','<Ag\'tor squints at the parchment, turning it in the light.>$B$BNo, I can\'t make sense of it either, but I don\'t like what I see. Are these arcane runes?$B$BI\'ll need you to deliver this to an expert.',0),
(14128,'enUS','What? Give that here, this instant! Ag\'tor is correct, these are arcane runes. They\'re scouting out magical sites? Experimenting with the arcane arts? This is a marked departure from thousands of years of night elven history.$B$BHmph! The idea that they will achieve any competence in this field - even those who once counted themselves among the highborne - is absurd.$B$B<Malynea puts aside the scroll dismissively, but her face is furrowed with concern.>',0),
(14129,'enUS','<Labor Captain Grabbit\'s voice crackles over the radio.>$B$BHey $n! Are you reading this?$B$BPiloting that sucker is easy. Push the pedals for your pedal controls and, ah, move the levers for your lever controls. Got it?',0),
(14130,'enUS','Hello there! A new friend! So glad to meet you. My name is Ergll. The g is silent.',0),
(14131,'enUS','Beautiful beans! They smell absolutely delicious, don\'t they?',0),
(14132,'enUS','Too mean? Naw, not too mean. They deserved it.$B$BI don\'t gum up their plants. Not ever.',0),
(14134,'enUS','Great! You\'ve loaded the shredder to capacity. You\'re getting pretty handy with that thing...',0),
(14135,'enUS','Great work, $n! That\'s how we took care of business back on Kezan.',0),
(14136,'enUS','Great job, Champion. The fight continues, but now the Kvaldir know that we do not tolerate such attacks.',0),
(14138,'enUS','A gift from Sassy? I hope it\'s a bonus!',0),
(14140,'enUS','Your actions have shown that we Sunreavers are far better allies to the Argent Crusade than the Silver Covenant and it is we who will be triumphant.',0),
(14141,'enUS','The sooner we get these stinking things out of my sight and into their cage, the faster my mood will improve. I wish the Argent Crusade had given the Silver Covenant the care of this creature. They\'re going to have to get their hands dirty when the battle for Icecrown Citadel starts and I have a feeling they\'ll prove fragile and fussy allies.',0),
(14142,'enUS','Kul will live to embarrass himself again. That\'s far from the first time someone\'s had to save Kul from himself. With examples like him, it\'s no wonder most of the aspirants are taking up the habits of the Silver Covenant.',0),
(14143,'enUS','These look a little worse for wear, but they\'re still edible. The crusaders will be glad to hear that we\'ve had some success. Maybe we can give the half-eaten ones to the Silver Covenant. That would make my day.',0),
(14144,'enUS','<Girana accepts the prayer book from you.>$B$BThank you. We don\'t always see eye-to-eye with the crusaders, but I\'ve learned a lot from Confessor Paletress in my time here.',0),
(14145,'enUS','I\'m glad we\'ve gotten that done. It\'s not the most glorious task in the world, but when we partnered with the Argent Crusade, we promised to do all they asked of us without complaint. Of course, the same cannot be said of the Silver Covenant.',0),
(14151,'enUS','Very good, $n.$B$BNow, the trick is to align the facets just right...',0),
(14152,'enUS','It seems things are worse than we initially thought. You still made a valiant effort and saved many of The Wavecrest\'s crew\'s lives.',0),
(14153,'enUS','Very nicely done, ma\'am. The party appears to have been a smashing success!$B$BEr... what\'s that?',0),
(14154,'enUS','We did it, $n. Thanks to you a good man has survived.',0),
(14155,'enUS','You did it, $n! The invaders have pulled back. And they told me I was crazy for installing a grenade launcher on a woodchipper...$B$BGreat work with the Shredder. With an impressive showing like that right here on the Warchief\'s doorstep, the Horde can\'t doubt what goblin technology can do for them. I owe you a big thanks!',0),
(14157,'enUS','Greymane wants to save Crowley? Has he gone mad?',0),
(14159,'enUS','Don\'t look at me! Leave me alone!',0),
(14161,'enUS','Good, good. One less nuisance to worry about.',0),
(14162,'enUS','You\'re here to help? Excellent! Here, sign this indemnity waiver. And here, this noncompete clause. Let\'s get you started!',0),
(14165,'enUS','Well well, let\'s take a look at what we got here...$B$B<Horzak examines the shattered remains of the poor petrified miner.>$B$BBah! Crumbly! Useless. Wouldn\'t even make a good countertop. My miners may be mediocre workers, but they make lousy bricks.$B$B<Sigh>. Well, I suppose we should re-fleshify these guys so I can get some return on my investment.',0),
(14166,'enUS','Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),
(14167,'enUS','Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),
(14168,'enUS','Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),
(14169,'enUS','Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),
(14170,'enUS','Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),
(14171,'enUS','Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),
(14171,'ruRU','Какой же все-таки вкусный этот поминальный хлеб!$B$BПрошу, прими вот это в знак моей благодарности... Веселого тебе праздника!',25549),
(14172,'enUS','Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),
(14173,'enUS','Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),
(14174,'enUS','Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),
(14175,'enUS','Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),
(14176,'enUS','Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),
(14177,'enUS','Ah, more delicious Bread of the Dead, thank you!$B$BPlease, take this in return... a little something fun for the holiday.',0),
(14184,'enUS','What!?$B$BFurien!! My brother is no more?$B$BThey must pay! All of them!',0),
(14188,'enUS','Furien\'s passing is... regrettable.$B$BI shall do all that I can to assist you in avenging his death.',0),
(14189,'enUS','Comparing the characters on the ancient tablet to those in Furien\'s journal, it is clear that there is a distinct correlation.',0),
(14190,'enUS','<Zignibble\'s voice squawks over the speakers.>$B$BIs that you, $n? Still alive? You aren\'t trashing my explosive stockpiles are you?$B$BHmmm... you say you found a clear crystal pendant. That makes sense. A perfect prism would refract the gaze of the basilisk. Maybe we can use this to our advantage. Time to drop some science!',0),
(14191,'enUS','It is clear to you now that these ruins are those that Furien recorded in his journal.$B$BAfter examining the engravings upon the ruins themselves, you feel that you are able to decipher more of Furien\'s writings.',0),
(14192,'enUS','<You pop out the lens assembly and slide the crystal into place. The weapon hums ominously.>',0),
(14193,'enUS','After filling it with liquid from the melons, you proceed to wash your eyes from the ancient font.$B$BUpon opening your eyes, you are able to see the spirits of ancient elves, still faithfully carrying out rituals to their goddess.',0),
(14194,'enUS','Ah, good. Now we can get these slackers back to work. You\'ve earned a cut of the profits though - minus the usual company fees. Take your pick!',0),
(14195,'enUS','It is clear to you now why you were guided here.$B$BYou recognize this ancient runestone from Furien\'s final journal entry:$B$B\"The ancients revered the gems created by this mystical object, claiming that they were gifts from the goddess herself. It was believed that they were weapons capable of delivering them from any enemy.\"',0),
(14196,'enUS','It is done! Furien\'s exhaustive research was not in vain.$B$BThe raging Vortex is ready to be unleashed upon your enemies at last!',0),
(14197,'enUS','Well done! When it comes to iron, always pick quantity over quality.',0),
(14198,'enUS','Very impressive, $C.$B$BYou completed Furien\'s work and rained vengeance down upon his killers.$B$BYou have brought peace to my brother\'s soul, and to my mind. Please accept this gift for your diligence.',0),
(14201,'enUS','<Malynea furrows her brow and begins sifting through the artifacts you brought her.>$B$BSo the spirits of the dead still haunt those old stones, hm? Well $n, as it happens, I\'m counting on their help. Let\'s see what the dead have to say...',0),
(14202,'enUS','Beautiful work! Now that we know the area better, we can tear this lake a new one.',0),
(14203,'enUS','This is quite a find, $n. I can\'t have you selling this to anyone else, so I\'m willing to offer generously.',0),
(14204,'enUS','Excellent. I\'ll start rounding up some help to get these cannons positioned.',0),
(14209,'enUS','Busted ball bearings! Look at this stuff - ugh, SMELL this stuff - my poor, poor dozer!$B$B$n, I consider myself a goop expert and this here goop ain\'t natural. It\'s supernatural. This is ghost goop. We\'re going to need more than a mechanic...',0),
(14212,'enUS','Brace yourself, $n.$B$BHere they come.',0),
(14213,'enUS','The divine brazier indiscriminately endows you with a blessing.',0),
(14214,'enUS','I knew Crowley would come through. His weapons will be more than useful to us.',0),
(14215,'enUS','You reel as the spirit\'s vision fades, relieved to once again feel the earth beneath your feet and the comforting rhythm of your own quickened heart.',0),
(14216,'enUS','A Sarcen stone? That\'s the stuff of legend - let me see that!$B$B$n, Sarcen stones are used to redirect the ley lines of magical energy. You realize what this means? The mages of Mennar weren\'t staying behind out of misguided loyalty. They sacrificed their lives in order to create this artifact in an attempt to draw energy away from the portal through which the demons were flooding Azeroth. They were buying time for the rest of the world to fight back! History never recorded their deeds. What a discovery!',0),
(14217,'enUS','The divine brazier indiscriminately endows you with a blessing.',0),
(14218,'enUS','You\'ve done well, $n. You\'ve done more than could be asked of any Gilnean.$B$BWe\'re running low on ammunition. It\'s time to regroup inside now.',0),
(14219,'enUS','With the ritual completed, you are awarded a divine gift.$B$BYou can\'t help but wonder what Elune would think of someone such as you receiving one of her boons.',0),
(14221,'enUS','We\'ve given them everything we have... yet still they come. Do not worry, $n. We\'ll slay many more before today is over.',0),
(14222,'enUS','They... they\'ve stopped coming.$B$BNo, $n. That\'s not a good thing.',0),
(14223,'enUS','It is done.$B$BSorrem should be able to sleep in peace now that Kohor\'s threats have been silenced.',0),
(14225,'enUS','It is most fortunate that you took the time to search for this.$B$BNo one would have expected the Burning Blade to be in possession of something so powerful!',0),
(14226,'enUS','<Archmage Xylem appears to be doing some kind of dance as he turns to you.>$B$BDo not fret, and better yet, do not forget, to do not let the bug juice set or you will regret... well, you\'ll regret the smell of your boots really! It won\'t smell good today and it won\'t smell good even more tomorrow!',0),
(14227,'enUS','You diverted what would have been a serious crisis, $C.$B$BIf that summoning was delayed just a bit longer, the demon would have become far too powerful for our small forces here to contend with.$B$BPlease accept this gift as our thanks for your service.',0),
(14230,'enUS','Peachy. Back to work then.$B$BThanks, snookums.',0),
(14232,'enUS','Ears of the Burning Blade?$B$B<Sorrem smiles.>$B$BWell done, $C. This is just a shadow of what will soon become of that vile cult!',0),
(14233,'enUS','Orcs?! They were sunk and stranded too? And now the Alliance are on the island? Do you think they\'re going to kill us?$B$B<Sassy looks thoughtful.>$B$BI think it\'s time for a little sitdown with these orcs.',0),
(14234,'enUS','<The orc makes a move to grab the field journal from you, but then stops herself, exhaling deeply.>$B$BI apologize. It has been a very rough couple of days for all of us.$B$BI am Aggra. All of us here are what remains of the crew of the Draka\'s Fury.$B$BPerhaps we can work together. We have a common enemy in the Alliance. Their SI:7 assassins are all over this island and they\'re not going to stop until we\'re all dead.',0),
(14235,'enUS','$R, can you fight?$B$BFor your sake, I hope so. Otherwise, there may be no breaking through this hell of killer plants.',0),
(14236,'enUS','I saw it with my own eyes, and still I do not believe it!$B$BYou have our thanks and the debt of our lives, little $R. I hope that soon we can repay you the honor.$B$BMay I ask a small favor of you while my scouts and I move on?',0),
(14237,'enUS','Throm-Ka, $n. We have a problem.',0),
(14238,'enUS','Well done, $n, well done. We\'ll make an orc of you yet!$B$BTime to move on. We\'d better hurry.',0),
(14239,'enUS','It\'s up to you now. Are you going to come back to life and be the hero that your fellow survivors need you to be, or are you going to rest for eternity here?$B$BOnly you can decide.$B$BDon\'t go into the Light, $n!',0),
(14240,'enUS','Hello, little $R. Bastia is fast, no?$B$BWe have something very important that needs doing. Can you help us?',0),
(14241,'enUS','Hmm, where the heck is the ignition?$B$BIt\'ll be a wonder if it flies without doing something weird, like turning into a chicken or shrinking down to the size of an ant.$B$BHey look, someone left their loose change in the ashtray! What else is in there?',0),
(14242,'enUS','If not for you, I would surely be on my way back to Stormwind to be paraded as a trophy and a slave.$B$BThe Alliance dogs found me unconscious on the shore and put me in this magical cage. It was keeping me from connecting with the elements.$B$BNo longer!',0),
(14243,'enUS','You have done what few others could have, $n. Our world owes you a debt larger than you can possibly understand.',0),
(14244,'enUS','$n, I sure am glad you survived the trip... not everyone did!',0),
(14245,'enUS','<cough, cough!>$B$BHey! Where\'s the dock?! Someone stole the dock and the oil refinery from our town-in-a-box!$B$BWho would do such a thing?$B$BWhere\'s the Trade Prince?',0),
(14246,'enUS','You have done well, $C.$B$BThis land is in your debt.',0),
(14247,'enUS','You look around, scanning the horizon for what might be responsible for placing this stone here....',0),
(14248,'enUS','Boss! Er, well, I guess you\'re not the boss anymore, but still, good to see you!$B$BCan you believe it? We\'ve got a cave full of intelligent killer monkeys mining Kaja\'mite!',0),
(14249,'enUS','Ha ha! Perfect! Let me toss this together really fast. The Archmage is sure to be taken in by my style!',0),
(14250,'enUS','Good work. This should keep us for another few hours before we have to go back for more.$B$BHe doesn\'t seem to be the brightest of giants. I expect we\'ll be able to keep doing this for a while before he catches on.',0),
(14251,'enUS','This is how I got my start, you know.$B$BSlingin\' poison to the rogues in Orgrimmar. Ahh, those were the days....',0),
(14252,'enUS','That\'ll do, $C.$B$BA few more friends like you and I\'ll be back on my feet in no time!',0),
(14253,'enUS','Well now, that\'s quite a load of feathers, $C.$B$BThey\'ll make for a good pillow \'til I get \'em to market!',0),
(14254,'enUS','What\'s this?$B$B<Bizby examines the ore.>$B$BWahoo! I know someone who will be most interested in acquiring these samples.$B$BMost generous in payment for them as well, I\'ll wager.$B$BHere, $C. Take this as your finder\'s fee.',0),
(14255,'enUS','It is good that you have come.$B$BThere is grave danger looming here.',0),
(14256,'enUS','So now you see. These are not a simple band of displaced naga, but a well organized army, capable of great devastation.$B$BDo you agree to assist me in my investigation?',0),
(14257,'enUS','You have done well, $C. But I\'m afraid that your work here is just beginning.',0),
(14258,'enUS','Sweet! Beautiful! Brilliant! Who loves you?$B$BWith my mortars re-supplied, I can help you as you assault the Naga east of here. Use these markers to call in an artillery strike anywhere on the cliffs, and I\'ll splatter the whole area with fiery hurt. Oh delicious, merciless, random destruction! I hope you\'re well-armored...',0),
(14260,'enUS','Don\'t just stand around, when there is so much to be done!$B$BMust I instruct everyone on each detail?',0),
(14261,'enUS','What? So you didn\'t bring any of the drake pieces back? Disappointing.$B$BI knew I should have made you sign a contract before I sent you out...',0),
(14262,'enUS','<Torg scans the horizon.> And still they come! They are like a plague, $n. But with strength like yours, we will crush them. Someday.',0),
(14263,'enUS','Perfect. It\'s quite interesting how useful the most random things end up being to incantations of this sort.$B$BSo much more to learn!',0),
(14264,'enUS','The enemy\'s ranks are thinning, little minnow.$B$BPerhaps you are worthy of assisting in our search....',0),
(14265,'enUS','$n! Where have you been?$B$BAnyway... it\'s great to see you in one piece.',0),
(14266,'enUS','Excellent work!',0),
(14267,'enUS','The stone in the center of this shrine emits a faint glow and roars with the power of the angry sea.',0),
(14268,'enUS','Yes! You\'ve found it!$B$BNeptulon\'s engravings... there can be no mistake!',0),
(14269,'enUS','Oh, hey! There you are!',0),
(14270,'enUS','The keystone shard slides into place and previously invisible runes suddenly erupt onto the surface of the stone, shimmering in blue and violet hues. Your knees buckle as powerful arcane currents suddenly race into your body...',0),
(14271,'enUS','An energy barrier, you say? This explains a great deal! I\'ve seen firsthand how Naga leaders have been able to turn aside the blades of some of my best warriors.$B$BNow we know the source of their power, $n. Let\'s finish this!',0),
(14272,'enUS','Don\'t get ahead of yourself now. Just remember who taught you everything you know.$B$BAnd now let\'s see if we can get out of this city with our skins attached.',0),
(14273,'enUS','A darkness has descended over our lands. And not our kind of darkness, if you know what I mean.',0),
(14274,'enUS','Yes! You can feel the power, can\'t you?',0),
(14275,'enUS','$n! I knew you had to be around here.',0),
(14276,'enUS','Excellent work, $n. These $R will regret ever setting foot in our lands.',0),
(14277,'enUS','A disciple of the arcane always finds a way forward. I\'m glad to see you, $n.',0),
(14278,'enUS','The Light is with you, $n. It\'s still quite a relief to see you.',0),
(14279,'enUS','You are blessed, $n. The Light shines upon you, even in these dark times.',0),
(14280,'enUS','We have been blessed today! You are alive and well!',0),
(14281,'enUS','You\'ve learned with such speed and ease. Soon you\'ll be the one doing the teaching.',0),
(14282,'enUS','The vision was true!$B$BYou have singlehandedly succeeded where others have failed.$B$BThe Circle will have no choice but to pay attention to these findings.',0),
(14283,'enUS','Not bad at all. Perhaps there is still hope for the old ways.',0),
(14284,'enUS','The priestess is no more...',0),
(14285,'enUS','You\'ve done well in coming here. If we Gilneans stick together we might yet defeat this terrible enemy.',0),
(14286,'enUS','You\'ve done well in coming here. If we Gilneans stick together we might yet defeat this terrible enemy.',0),
(14287,'enUS','You\'ve done well in coming here. If we Gilneans stick together we might yet defeat this terrible enemy.',0),
(14288,'enUS','You\'ve done well in coming here. If we Gilneans stick together we might yet defeat this terrible enemy.',0),
(14289,'enUS','You\'ve done well in coming here. If we Gilneans stick together we might yet defeat this terrible enemy.',0),
(14290,'enUS','You\'ve done well in coming here. If we Gilneans stick together we might yet defeat this terrible enemy.',0),
(14291,'enUS','You\'ve done well in coming here. If we Gilneans stick together we might yet defeat this terrible enemy.',0),
(14292,'enUS','I have witnessed your actions here, $R.$B$BYour presence here is both welcome and timely.',0),
(14293,'enUS','Well done, $n. We\'ll make sure Krennan makes it out of the city alive.',0),
(14294,'enUS','We\'re left with very few choices, $n. What we do next will be a critical decision.',0),
(14295,'enUS','Now THAT is how we used to handle serpents back in Durotar - we crushed them under our boots! You have done the Horde proud, $n. As soon as my reinforcements arrive we\'ll mop up the rest of those vermin and claim this peninsula once and for all.',0),
(14296,'enUS','It is in this moment that most of my apprentices wonder if there was a logical purpose to storing the energy for my portal in those conduits so that it has to be collected in such a fashion.$B$BOf course there\'s a purpose! I wish to study your behavior... your strategies, your mistakes, your frustrations, your triumphs. Those are the entire point of these trials.$B$BNow, more. More trials! Doesn\'t that sound exciting?! Of course it does.',0),
(14297,'enUS','Thanks there, pal. Here\'s your commission.$B$BIf you\'ll excuse me, I\'ve gotta get these slackers back to work.',0),
(14299,'enUS','Welcome! You seem to have survived the trials relatively unscathed. Good for you, love.$B$BYou look to have come with a purpose in mind as well. A question. Your thoughts are very loud, it\'s hard for me to not hear them.$B$BGo ahead then, hon. Ask away.',0),
(14300,'enUS','Woo! Good for you! That trial really put a fire under your bottom.',0),
(14301,'enUS','Please accept this reward for your heroic accomplishments, $n.$B$BYou have bought us precious time!',0),
(14302,'enUS','<Karnum opens and reads Korrah\'s Report.>$B$BThis is alarming news, indeeed, $R - something we have no shortage of here.$B$BI shall call a council regarding the issue. You will be summoned if you are needed.',0),
(14303,'enUS','<Aggra gives you the eye as if she doesn\'t quite believe what you are telling her.>$B$BI am not easily impressed, but if what you are telling me is true, then I have never before heard of such a thing.$B$BYou have my thanks, $n.',0),
(14304,'enUS','This should be enough.$B$BThank you, $C.',0),
(14305,'enUS','These are fine specimens, $R.$B$BI shall commence my studies immediately.',0),
(14306,'enUS','On behalf of Desolace herself, I thank you, $R.$B$BPlease accept our deepest gratitude.',0),
(14307,'enUS','You have done well, $C.$B$BWe will doubtlessly call upon you for assistance with more significant matters in the future.',0),
(14308,'enUS','Nice work, $n! Now, we need to decouple the reaction core matrix from the fuel sumps, or that whole place is gonna blow itself to Outland...',0),
(14309,'enUS','Wonderful! Karnum will be so pleased!$B$BPlease, accept this as my thanks.',0),
(14310,'enUS','Whew, the sample is secure. And it\'s still steaming! Thank you, $n.$B$BAzsharite is a complex mystery wrapped in a velvety enigma of danger. Grapplehammer insists that we learn more about this strange substance.',0),
(14311,'enUS','The rejuvenation is so invigorating! Don\'t you think?',0),
(14312,'enUS','Be not afraid, $R. I mean you no harm.',0),
(14313,'enUS','It worked! By the Light, it worked!',0),
(14313,'ruRU','Сработало! Хвала Свету, сработало!',26365),
(14314,'enUS','I thank you, $R.$B$BOur tribe may not have survived without your aid.',0),
(14316,'enUS','As we suspected, the Magram have been stealing our supplies.$B$BWe shall guard them more closely.',0),
(14318,'enUS','Why is it that you meddle in centaur affairs, $R?',0),
(14320,'enUS','The crate has been smashed and the vials inside of it appear to have been broken.',0),
(14320,'ruRU','Похоже, что ящик сильно пострадал, и все находящиеся в нем склянки разбились.',26365),
(14321,'enUS','Forsaken! Quick, $n! We must mount a defense.',0),
(14321,'ruRU','Отрекшиеся! У нас мало времени, $n! Мы должны организовать оборону.',26365),
(14322,'enUS','So the world is safe for science again? Excellent! Next time I\'ll try heated needles or something.',0),
(14323,'enUS','You\'ve collected all of the simmering water droplets that Ergll requested. Now it\'s just a matter of summoning the \"jumbo\" elemental.',0),
(14324,'enUS','Convenient, no? Who needs hot springs anyway. This is perfect.',0),
(14325,'enUS','Very good, $R.$B$BThis will sustain us for now.',0),
(14326,'enUS','My mission is too critical to let these meddlers continue to dog us. It\'s up to you and I to put an end to this once and for all!',0),
(14327,'enUS','You have done well, $C.$B$BNow we must convince the Gelkis...',0),
(14328,'enUS','My sons all slain... my clan in ruins....$B$BWere I in my youth, I would tear you limb from limb!$B$BGo now... kill me or leave me to mourn alone, $R.',0),
(14329,'enUS','As you slaughter their enemy, the Gelkis clan cannot help but to acknowledge your prowess.',0),
(14330,'enUS','Is it safe for me to leave, $R?',0),
(14332,'enUS','You have done well, $R.$B$BAnd not a moment too soon....',0),
(14333,'enUS','The destruction of those defiled relics will ease the minds of the Gelkis, and will strengthen their resolve.$B$BYou have done well.',0),
(14334,'enUS','Oy, mon! Ya did it!$B$BWe soon be havin\' fish to eat, thanks be to you.',0),
(14335,'enUS','On behalf of us all at Shadowprey Village, I thank you, $R.',0),
(14336,'enUS','$n!!! You ARE alive!$B$BI thought I was having dreams about the old days when I heard your voice...',0),
(14336,'ruRU','$n! Ты и правда $gвыжил:выжила;!!!$B$BЯ уж подумал, что твой голос мне померещился.',26365),
(14337,'enUS','Welcome to Shadowprey Village, $R.$B$BI was not sure the Cenarion Circle would send anyone.',0),
(14338,'enUS','Greetings, $C.$B$BIt is good that you have finally arrived....',0),
(14339,'enUS','Yes, yes.$B$BThese will do nicely....',0),
(14340,'enUS','Well look at you, aren\'t you just a marvel of modern Magery! Quite a fancy hat, I must say.$B$BApprentices. Apprentici? I do think that I might have quite a few already, but I suppose one can never have too many appren..tici.',0),
(14341,'enUS','Ahh, my harnesses!$B$BThanks, friend!',0),
(14342,'enUS','Well done, $R!$B$BThe danger persists, but you have bought us some time.',0),
(14343,'enUS','I hate to use such unnatural measures, but I fear we simply have no choice....',0),
(14344,'enUS','You should be proud of how you manipulated the enemy\'s power and used it against them.$B$BYou\'ve dealt the demons of Mannoroc a severe blow....',0),
(14345,'enUS','Look buddy, I was in your shoes not a week ago. Big powerful Archmage actually takes on apprentices! Who could pass up an opportunity like that?!$B$BSometimes, things really are just too good to be true.',0),
(14346,'enUS','Your deeds continue to impress me, $n.$B$BPlease accept this gift on behalf of the Cenarion Circle.',0),
(14347,'enUS','Yes, $n! Just like old times...$B$BI\'m going to have to work hard at not shooting you, but Krennan explained everything to us.',0),
(14348,'enUS','You and me, $n. We make a great team...$B$BIt\'s good to have you back.',0),
(14349,'enUS','The Grand Crusader sits safely in the Scarlet Bastion while his forces pour into our lands, desecrate our structures and monuments and murder our people.$B$BThe time has come to deal with this pest. You will become the instrument of our reckoning.',0),
(14350,'enUS','<Nathanos laughs.>$B$BExcellent! Finally! An opportunity to destroy the Scarlet Oracle!',0),
(14351,'enUS','So you\'re the $C who tore through the Alliance forces in the Hillsbrad Foothills? I\'ve heard your name already. Word travels fast.$B$BThe Horde can use someone like you if you keep this up, $n.$B$BWe need to keep our eyes on all threats around us, but with that king leading them, the humans will continue to be a problem. You\'ve confirmed that there\'s strength enough in the Horde to end that threat in time.',0),
(14352,'enUS','I\'ve seen the insignia on this scroll before during my time in Northrend. You say this was on that crone who leads the pigs in Razorfen Kraul?$B$BI\'ll be damned if I\'m going to let the Scourge get a foothold here. The one who wrote this - this Malcin - is one of the Lich King\'s servants, obviously, and that makes him a target. Your target.$B$BThey\'re not going to take Kalimdor.',0),
(14353,'enUS','Good work, $C!$B$BYou\'ve done the Horde proud by stopping the Scourge from setting down roots on our soil. An act like that deserves a reward, and the Forsaken have enough lying around that I\'m sure they can spare a few things.$B$BWe may not know everything they\'ve done in the Downs, but we\'ll find out. They can\'t slink around in the dark forever.',0),
(14354,'enUS','The relics are intact! Well, indeed, that is something.$B$BYou have put my mind at ease, $R. Please accept this as my gift to you.',0),
(14355,'enUS','I\'m sure Sylvanas will be glad to have that problem taken care of, $n. The task I gave you wasn\'t easy, but here you stand, victorious. That commands respect, and what you\'ve done won\'t be forgotten.',0),
(14356,'enUS','Good, $C. You\'ve done well. I\'ll keep these safe from prying eyes; the last thing we need is a strong Shadow Council rising up again.$B$BCheck back with me in the future; there\'s always something that needs doing around here, apparently, and I might need another able body.',0),
(14357,'enUS','With the ritual completed, you are awarded a divine gift.$B$BYou can\'t help but to feel a great sense of honor as you receive one of Elune\'s boons.',0),
(14358,'enUS','The divine brazier graciously endows you with a blessing.',0),
(14359,'enUS','The divine brazier graciously endows you with a blessing.',0),
(14360,'enUS','After filling it with liquid from the melons, you proceed to wash your eyes from the ancient font.$B$BUpon opening your eyes, you are able to see the spirits of ancient elves, still faithfully carrying out rituals to their goddess.$B$BYou ponder the significance of this revelation and determine to study Furien\'s research for more clues....',0),
(14361,'enUS','It is done.$B$BCaptain Pentigast should be able to sleep in peace now that Kohor\'s threats have been silenced.',0),
(14362,'enUS','Ears of the Burning Blade?$B$B<Captain Pentigast smiles.>$B$BWell done, $C. This is just a shadow of what will soon become of that vile cult!',0),
(14363,'enUS','It is most fortunate that you took the time to search for this.$B$BNo one would have expected the Burning Blade to be in possession of something so powerful!',0),
(14364,'enUS','You diverted what would have been a serious crisis, $C.$B$BIf that summoning was delayed just a bit longer, the demon would have become far too powerful for our small forces here to contend with.$B$BPlease accept this gift as our thanks for your service.',0),
(14365,'enUS','It is good that you have come.$B$BThere is grave danger looming here.',0),
(14366,'enUS','Great news, $n. I\'ve sent the remaining militia to the shore to meet the Forsaken force head on.',0),
(14367,'enUS','The Forsaken are here in full strength, $n. We barely have enough men to hold them back.',0),
(14367,'ruRU','Отрекшиеся обрушились на нас всей своей военной мощью, $n. У нас едва хватает людей, чтобы сдерживать их натиск.',26365),
(14368,'enUS','My children are safe! You\'ve done a wonderful thing, $n. I don\'t know how to thank you!',0),
(14369,'enUS','Not bad, $n. It\'s a good thing you\'re on our side.',0),
(14370,'enUS','Ah, excellent. Some of these samples look fresh. I\'m going to be up to my neck in this stuff trying to solve this mystery!',0),
(14371,'enUS','Phew! The stench! Well, hopefully that massive heap of carcasses smells more appetizing to a giant.',0),
(14372,'enUS','Demons?$B$BOh, there be lots I can tell yeh \'bout demons!',0),
(14373,'enUS','Well, lad!$B$BDon\'t hesitate to knock a few more down for good measure!',0),
(14374,'enUS','Aye, that\'ll buy us some time, $C.$B$BThank yeh.',0),
(14375,'enUS','I need you to pull through, $n. This dosage is strong enough to kill a horse.$B$BBut I know you. I know what you\'re made of. You will be fine.$B$BTrust me. I know what you\'re going through.$B$BNow drink up and close your eyes.',0),
(14375,'ruRU','Я тебя вытащу, $n. Я тебе приготовил такую дозу, что хватит свалить лошадь, но я знаю, что делаю. Я знаю, из какого теста ты $gсделан:сделана;. Ты выдержишь, и все будет хорошо.$B$BВерь мне, $n. Я понимаю, через что тебе придется пройти...$B$BА теперь выпей это и закрой глаза.',26365),
(14376,'enUS','You should be proud of how you manipulated the enemy\'s power and used it against them.$B$BYou\'ve dealt the demons of Mannoroc a severe blow....',0),
(14377,'enUS','Speak slower - what are you saying? Am I hearing you right? Those formations of azsharite are actually where the giants have - oh my. Groady!! Let\'s not tell Dr. Grapplehammer, he\'s made this stuff his life\'s work.$B$BWell, at least now we know where azsharite comes from, and why it\'s so rare. We\'ve got to figure out a way to speed up, uh, \"production!\"',0),
(14378,'enUS','Justice is done!$B$BNow let\'s have a peek at what\'s left of my goods....',0),
(14379,'enUS','Ohhh, these will do nicely!$B$BThargad will be so surprised!',0),
(14380,'enUS','<Karnum examines the concoction.>$B$BYes, $C. Not only do I know what this is, I know just how you should use it....',0),
(14381,'enUS','Your deeds continue to impress me, $n.$B$BPlease accept this gift on behalf of the Cenarion Circle.',0),
(14382,'enUS','Well done, $n. You might be a bloody beast, but you\'re our beast.',0),
(14383,'enUS','Oh - marvelous. Tell me more. And that precocious young Gadgetspring? Dead as well? Ah, wonderful. My work here is important but at times I do miss the carnage of demolishing my enemies on a more personal level. Here, perhaps you can make use of some of my discarded equipment.',0),
(14384,'enUS','Welcome to Nijel\'s Point, $R.$B$BNow, let\'s see about getting you briefed on our situation here.',0),
(14385,'enUS','So it was a no-go? Literally? Well, Grapplehammer won\'t take no for an answer. We\'ll have to try something else.$B$BMaybe I\'ll have my interns smuggle this laxative into the night elf encampment. That\'ll be good for a laugh, at least.',0),
(14386,'enUS','You did it, $n. That should take the wind out of their sails.',0),
(14387,'enUS','A pleasure to meet you, $C.',0),
(14388,'enUS','So scaring him didn\'t work, either? Double-nertz! I\'ll have to break the news to Grapplehammer: Azsharite\'s going to remain the rarest substance on the planet. We\'ll have to use it sparingly.',0),
(14389,'enUS','Azuregos! At last you\'ve found him!',0),
(14390,'enUS','Azuregos has agreed to rendezvous with Kalecgos. Success!',0),
(14391,'enUS','Great to see you again! Thank you for finding Azuregos and sending him to me.$B$BI do feel I owe you an apology - I may have undersold how difficult it would be to accomplish the task I gave you. You performed quite admirably, $n.',0),
(14392,'enUS','Hey there... again.$B$BLook, I gave you my hat. It was a gift. I thought you\'d make some use of it. More specifically though, I thought you\'d get it the heck away from me.$B$BCan you imagine my surprise when Xylem comes by himself to give it back to me? \"Want to be more like my other apprentices, Sorata? Give your hat another try.\" Not one of my proudest moments.$B$BSo what... you just tossed it aside for him to find? No. I don\'t think so. You\'re going to take this hat and you\'re going to like it. Really.',0),
(14393,'enUS','Well done, $n!$B$BLet us finish this!',0),
(14394,'enUS','Agogridon is no more.$B$BThe demons shall never again take hold in our lands!',0),
(14395,'enUS','You did what you could, $n. With any luck a few others will find their way to shore.',0),
(14396,'enUS','The ocean, $n. It swallowed everything... the land... the Forsaken... our men!',0),
(14397,'enUS','Liam is right. We must get everyone to higher ground.$B$BYou must help me spread the word while I manage the logistics of the evacuation.',0),
(14398,'enUS','A visitor! Are you staying for tea, sweetheart?',0),
(14399,'enUS','Why thank you, $n. I hope you didn\'t peek!$B$BWhere are your manners, dear?',0),
(14400,'enUS','You\'re a peach, $n. Thanks!',0),
(14401,'enUS','There he is! Grandma\'s special boy!$B$BThank you so much for finding him. I hope it wasn\'t too much trouble.$B$BMy... what manner of dirt found its way underneath my fingernails!',0),
(14402,'enUS','You did the impossible, $n. You convinced Grandma Wahl to leave her home.$B$BYou are something else, let me tell you.',0),
(14403,'enUS','You here to give us a hand?',0),
(14404,'enUS','This is great, $n. I should be able to finish the repairs in no time.',0),
(14405,'enUS','It\'s just as well, $n. Maybe the Haywards will fare better than us.',0),
(14406,'enUS','Stay back! Don\'t make me...$B$BIs it you? By the Light! It\'s you, $n!',0),
(14407,'enUS','Thank you for coming. I apologize for the discretion, but it\'s extremely important that I not be seen by certain individuals.$B$BI\'m in quite a bind and I\'ve taken notice of some of your recent deeds. Hear me out, help me, and I\'ll see to it that you\'re rewarded in kind.',0),
(14408,'enUS','<The raptor snatches the paperwork in her prehensile claws and holds the schematics up to her face, clucking her pointed teeth dismissively.>$B$BThese are like the scrawling of children. Common sense precludes the routing of control hydraulics so near to the secondary stage burners! Still, this is salvageable.$B$BDo you know how to refactor fuel matrixes for pressure variations at a fixed acceleration? No? Very well, perhaps you can do something else for me while I reconfigure the rocket...',0),
(14409,'enUS','Ah, the writings of Daros. He always was meticulous about tracking progress. His words may aid in explaining how far we\'ve come.$B$BYou have my thanks for bringing this to me, $R. Perhaps we will see more of each other once it is understood we mean no harm.',0),
(14410,'enUS','Welcome to Feralas, $C. I thank you for coming to assist us.',0),
(14412,'enUS','Excellent! I\'m almost done here.',0),
(14413,'enUS','Here so soon! Lovely trip I hope. Not too nauseous or anything?$B$BThere will be much running and much jumping, so a settled stomach is of great practicality.',0),
(14416,'enUS','We\'ve got the horses, I\'ll make sure Duskhaven gets them.',0),
(14422,'enUS','Wonderful! Exemplary work, $n! As you have no doubt surmised, my objective with regard to this rocket is to utilize it as a sort of astral cradle, an ark if you will, allowing my newly-forged race to slip the surly bonds of this ravaged planet and colonize a world to our own liking. You have been instrumental to our cause. Please accept this currency as I will be minting my own monetary units upon arrival. Farewell, $n!',0),
(14423,'enUS','What? ...What?$B$BMargene! Oh my sweet Margene!!',0),
(14424,'enUS','What is Clubnik talking about? Haunted construction equipment? Does it look like I have time for ghost stories?$B$BI\'ve got a laboratory in the middle of a meltdown, fires burning, animals mutated, and worst of all - projects falling behind schedule. Help!',0),
(14428,'enUS','Amberwind was making use of an Arcane Construct? Hah! How delightfully inexperienced. It\'s like watching children play with firearms.$B$BLet\'s take a look at that journal, $n. Hold it up to the scrying stone... keep it still ...',0),
(14429,'enUS','Good work getting those runestones. To be honest, I only needed one, but the thought of so many night elves slain for such useless baubles fills me with a dark, giddy joy.$B$BPlease hold one of those runes up to the scrying stone to let me see. Hmmm. As I suspected, an amateur effort at best.',0),
(14430,'enUS','Haha! Hah - HA! Night elf \"mages\" fleeing their own arcane creation. Your actions have made my month, $n. That\'s why we blood elves don\'t use arcane constructs anymore - they\'ve been outlawed for, oh, 1500 years. It\'s amusing to me to watch our foes repeat the mistakes of the past. \"Mages.\" Indeed.',0),
(14431,'enUS','I see... This definitely looks like a working draft of some sort of treaty. That\'s a worst-case scenario for us, $n: Night elves coordinating attacks with entrenched furbolg allies.$B$BMy initial instinct - a full-out frontal assault - would only drive them into the arms of the Alliance. We will have to take a different approach...',0),
(14432,'enUS','Ah good, that\'s plenty. We\'ll boil this stuff up and you can bask in the fumes for a while - you\'ll be speaking like a furbolg in no time. Our plan is beginning to take shape...',0),
(14433,'enUS','Excellent work! Let me see those documents. Hmm. Now we know exactly when and where the final negotiations will happen. Don\'t worry if those robes don\'t fit you - I\'ve got it all worked out.',0),
(14434,'enUS','Are you ready to set sail, $n? Your people have been granted shelter in the lands of the kaldorei.$B$BDo not worry, $R. Your people will get a chance to fight for Gilneas again. This time, with the full strength of the Alliance.',0),
(14435,'enUS','Victory! The Blackmaw won\'t know who to trust anymore.$B$BWith that delicate bit of business complete, I can orchestrate a full-on assault against those beasts without worrying about them siding with the Alliance.$B$BYou do good work, $n. Perhaps we should place you in the Horde diplomatic corps? Hah-har!',0),
(14438,'enUS','$n, it is good you\'ve taken the task seriously. Respect of the land and its creatures is important. Death and life are a circle... a necessity. One cannot exist without the other. Take time to ponder this and do well to never forget it.',0),
(14442,'enUS','Have you come to assist me with my work? My claws are quite dexterous, but I must reluctantly confess that my arms are debilitatingly short.',0),
(14443,'enUS','<Caladis takes the hilt from you and slowly turns it over in his hands.>$B$BThis seems somehow familiar, as though I should know its origins. You say you recovered this in the citadel? Most intriguing.$B$BThere are few who possess the ability to make such a blade. Perhaps they can tell us something about your find.',0),
(14444,'enUS','We can\'t let that book remain in Sunreaver hands. If we hope to identify the sword and use it to our advantage, we have to find a way to capture the book Krasus lent them.',0),
(14445,'enUS','Wow, oh wow! Is that who I think it is?$B$BYou rescued Thrall, Warchief of the Horde?!!!$B$B<Sassy gives you an appraising look.>$B$BWell, let\'s see about getting over to that larger island. I sure as heck don\'t want to swim the strait with all of those sharks down there.',0),
(14449,'enUS','Welcome to your first true test as a $R.',0),
(14452,'enUS','You\'ve fought well, $n. We may yet be saved.',0),
(14455,'enUS','With the corruptors slain, the Earth Mother will mend her own wounds in due time. The roots are not meant to thrive here, and will wither. Balance will return.',0),
(14456,'enUS','Well done, $n. Respect your prey, and the danger it carries, but never fear it. In fear, you become prey yourself.',0),
(14457,'enUS','<Arcanist Tybalin examines the captured orders.>$B$BThe agent you intercepted was supposed to transport the Wyrmrest Tome to Icecrown, after meeting with one Magister Hathorel in Sunreaver\'s Sanctuary. We have to get that book, $n, and this is our chance. It\'s not going to be easy, though.',0),
(14458,'enUS','More trials lay ahead, $n. I hope you\'re prepared.',0),
(14459,'enUS','Good work, $n. Those beasts could have been a greater threat than the quilboar themselves, if we had not taken action now.',0),
(14460,'enUS','<Chief Hawkwind holds the mane of Thornmantle over his head.>$B$BThe Chief of the Bristleback is slain. Greatmother Hawkwind\'s spirit has been avenged!',0),
(14461,'enUS','You\'ve not only wiped the boar pens clean, but put a stop to a horrible desecration. Well done.',0),
(14462,'enUS','You\'re just in time, $C. I\'m about to launch a lightning-strike precision assassination. Let\'s see...$B$BExplosives? Check.$BPneumatic grapplestabber? Check.$BPortable parachute? Check.$BCrippling nerve toxin?$B$B$B$BCheck. Let\'s do this thing.',0),
(14463,'enUS','Excellent work, $n. I think I speak for everyone when I say the sooner we get out of here, the better.',0),
(14464,'enUS','I\'m impressed by the cleverness of our new goblin allies, but I\'m even more impressed by you, $n. Look at the gaze of terror frozen onto the Captain\'s face! He never saw your attack coming. Imagine the fear this will cause in Northwatch when they see what happened to one of their precious officers in night elf lands.$B$BWell done, $C. Our assault proceeds...',0),
(14465,'enUS','$n. I\'ve heard much about you.$B$BI understand you were crucial in my family\'s survival during the outbreak in Gilneas City.',0),
(14466,'enUS','There you are, $n. I\'ve been expecting you.$B$BI got word of your recovery and... wait -- do you feel that?',0),
(14467,'enUS','Look, $n! Look at what\'s become of Duskhaven!$B$BLook at what\'s become of the last safe place in Gilneas!',0),
(14468,'enUS','Latest recruit, eh?$B$BI\'ll make this short and sweet. We\'re under contract to keep the naga in the ruins from reaching Gallywix or his property. You handle whatever we ask of you, and I\'ll see to it that you get paid when all of your rounds are complete.$B$BWelcome to the Bilgewater Battalion.',0),
(14469,'enUS','You\'re a light-footed bugger, aren\'t ya? Good work.$B$BHere are a few of the supplies to keep you lively.',0),
(14470,'enUS','Quick work there, recruit.$B$BShe\'s a beaut, isn\'t she? Assembled her myself. I\'ve got special plans for this baby.',0),
(14471,'enUS','Can you believe they PAY us to do this?',0),
(14472,'enUS','BAM! In the face! Nice shot, kid.',0),
(14473,'enUS','Let\'s just hope we don\'t have to deal with their mommy later. That would be very bad.',0),
(14474,'enUS','Oh, thank heavens that you survived, $n! I thought for sure that you\'d drowned when I saw you go over the side!$B$B$B$BLook at all of these folks you saved!',0),
(14475,'enUS','Reinforcements, at last!',0),
(14476,'enUS','Sweet. Let\'s torch this banana stand!',0),
(14477,'enUS','Yes, let them burn! Let them burn through the night, so that their flaming tower will light the battlefield beneath us as we rain terror upon their heads.$B$BThank you, $n. Stay close: the invasion is about to begin...',0),
(14478,'enUS','Welcome back to duty soldier. Good to have you back.',0),
(14479,'enUS','Bumpy ride?',0),
(14480,'enUS','Your name\'s getting around... nearly Gob Squad status some would say. You\'re a vicious one.',0),
(14482,'enUS','Not exactly the battle you had anticipated, I\'ll wager. But a battle nonetheless, as you shall soon see....',0),
(14483,'enUS','What\'ve you got there?$B$BOh hey, this is big. Real big. Most of the crazy details in one little package. Thanks - you really helped us reel this all in. Good working with ya.',0),
(14484,'enUS','Glad you\'re on our side, soldier.',0),
(14485,'enUS','The hope is that that cuts off a major source of their magic. The truth is, we don\'t really have a clue. Who can pass up an opportunity to blow some stuff up though.',0),
(14486,'enUS','Excellent. Here\'s your cut.$B$BGood doing business with you.',0),
(14487,'enUS','Hahah! It\'s HUGE!$B$BWe\'ll have you take it back to Uncle Bedlam as soon as everything\'s cleaned up here and you\'re ready to go.',0),
(14491,'enUS','The land is clearly still in great upheaval if it took such effort to calm.$B$BRemember this, $n. Do not forget seeing the fate of those who would scar the Earth Mother.',0),
(20438,'enUS','I knew Shandy would find a way to come through for us. Let me get this enchanted and ready for you to use. The sooner you get done with the tabard, the sooner we can get it back to Shandy and the better the chances that its owner will never have missed it.',0),
(20439,'enUS','Excellent work. Now that this is in our hands, we must get it to Caladis Brightspear as soon as possible. We can\'t risk the book falling back into Sunreaver hands.$B$BI\'ll ensure that Shandy Glossgleam gets his tabard back without incident, along with a healthy reward for his help.',0),
(20440,'enUS','You have done well, $n. I will take these and bind their power into a totem of cleansing.',0),
(20441,'enUS','Be not afraid, $n. You have successfully passed the Rite of Vision.',0),
(23733,'enUS','If you are prepared to leave Camp Narache behind, I will help call the spirits to guide you onwards.',0),
(24215,'enUS','Welcome to Bloodhoof Village, hero. I am glad the spirits have guided you safely here.',0),
(24428,'enUS','What? How did you get this? Isn\'t she... Never mind the details, I suppose. You\'ll be wanting one of these baubles as recompense, no doubt.',0),
(24429,'enUS','You\'ve brought me the head of someone who is... No, best not to think about it too hard. You\'ll be wanting recompense for your heroic deeds, no doubt.',0),
(24430,'enUS','Oh yeah! I love the smell of freshly-cratered dirt!$B$BWord around camp is that the elven front line is collapsing back toward the river. Talk to Chawg and see if there\'s anything you can do to help seal the deal.',0),
(24431,'enUS','This is quite a find, $n. I can\'t have you selling this to anyone else, so I\'m willing to offer generously.',0),
(24432,'enUS','Here you are, $C. With this you should find maneuvering in the sea to be nearly effortless. $B$BNow we must get to work. There is much to be done in little time.',0),
(24433,'enUS','Lok\'tar ogar, $n! As they discover the bodies of their comrades they will learn that no place is safe from the fury of the horde, and their will to fight will crumble.',0),
(24434,'enUS','Images of a great and distant tree flood your mind. Your stomach lurches as you reorient the stone, briefly filling your senses with visions of a fiery portal, a towering mountain, a frigid wasteland, and a terrible scar across the earth.$B$BAfter a moment, the magical energies of the stone calm, and you feel you are but a step away from Valormok. Andorel\'s invasion can begin...',0),
(24435,'enUS','Good clean fun.',0),
(24436,'enUS','Fine job there, bud. We\'ll have this beach cleaned up in no time.',0),
(24437,'enUS','Hah hah! Brilliant. Right fine job there, boy.',0),
(24438,'enUS','Thanks for stopping, $n. Our carriage got hit pretty bad.$B$BThe one in front of us got it worse.',0),
(24439,'enUS','...Then it is done!$B$B<Chawg surveys the battlefield.>$B$BThere are still pockets of resistance around our camp, but this rearguard action appears to be masking a full-fledged retreat to Ashenvale. Azshara is ours!$B$BThe Warchief will hear of this victory and your part in it. But we will surely need the help of a $C like you elsewhere. Be sure to speak with Kroum here in camp before you leave.',0),
(24440,'enUS','The Grimtotem...$B$B<Mull scowls.>$B$BI\'d hoped to see the end of my days before $R attacked other $R senselessly on the very plains of Mulgore. But be proud, $n. You have done a great thing for the land, and for our people.',0),
(24441,'enUS','Thank you, $n. The purity with which these beasts hunt is vital in the creation of the next cleansing totem.$B$BThe Thunderhorn Well is a symbol of my own tribe, and to know it is being desecrated by our own kind raises a fury in me I haven\'t felt for years.',0),
(24442,'enUS','<Mariel accepts the orders and the captured seeing crystal and examines both.>$B$BGood work, $n, and quick thinking. I\'m sure the theft of this trinket won\'t slow them down for long, but I think you\'ve bought us time to warn the leaders of the Horde and Alliance about the impending attacks.',0),
(24448,'enUS','$n! You made it in one piece, good.$B$BWe\'ve got a lot of work for you to handle for us inside the ruins, but we\'re sending you in with the best to take care of it. You\'re working with GAMA Force now, Goblin Army: Mergers and Acquisitions. Molotov says you can handle it - that\'s all I need to hear.',0),
(24449,'enUS','And you come with the artifact! The operation was a success then. Mergers and Acquisitions can definitely handle themselves. This thing will fetch quite a pretty penny.$B$BAnd you - I heard you did some impressive work down there. You may well have cut-down expenses by 10% single-handedly. That\'s the kind of smarty businessman I want in my army!$B$BHere are your wages, as promised. And a little something extra too - I hope you like it.',0),
(24451,'enUS','Excellent work. Now that this is in our hands, we must get it to Myralion Sunblaze as soon as possible. We can\'t risk the Silver Covenant taking the book from us again.$B$BI\'ll get that tabard back to Shandy and see that he\'s well compensated for his assistance. Once the book is in Myralion\'s hands, the Silver Covenant won\'t be a threat anymore.',0),
(24452,'enUS','Hahah! Sweet deal. I\'ll get the ball rolling on this. All I need now is to find a buyer and get the go-ahead from Uncle Bedlam.$B$BHere are your wages for your work here. Excellent work, soldier.',0),
(24453,'enUS','What?! I got left out of the action completely? Are you serious?$B$BAlright, alright... no shooting the messenger. Thanks for the news, bud. Maybe I\'ll see you back at town.',0),
(24454,'enUS','<Caladis accepts the heavy book and begins leafing through it.>$B$BI knew the symbols on the blade were familiar. The weapon was most certainly forged by the dragons and gifted to one of the mortal races, but which blade is this, and how did it come to rest in Icecrown?',0),
(24455,'enUS','Nice to meet you soldier. Commander Molotov speaks highly of you.',0),
(24456,'enUS','You\'ve done great honor for both me and my ancestors today. Please, take this with my gratitude.',0),
(24457,'enUS','I sensed you would be coming to me, $C. I can always recognize one who is trying to pass the Rites of the Earthmother.',0),
(24458,'enUS','Oh! This is it! It\'s the big one!$B$B<Fizzlefuse calls out to his workers.>$B$BWe\'re in business boys!',0),
(24459,'enUS','Well met. If Ahmo has already explained the minor quibbles of what kind of goblin we\'ll be driving from our lands, let\'s get to work.',0),
(24461,'enUS','You have remade the blade of Quel\'Delar, although Blood-Queen Lana\'thel proclaimed we could not! The blade must still be tempered, but she and her master will not stand in our way!',0),
(24463,'enUS','You say Talrendis Point has fallen? That\'s good news!$B$BIt also explains the exodus of elves I\'ve seen along this road.',0),
(24467,'enUS','You truly amaze me, mortal. It\'s rare to meet someone so dedicated and resourceful.$B$BAzuregos and I are likely to depart Azshara and remain discrete for a while. I do hope that we meet again someday though. Perhaps to put an end to Deathwing himself.$B$BFarewell, $n. Stay safe.',0),
(24468,'enUS','You\'ve done it again, $n. You have my thanks.',0),
(24469,'enUS','Impressive work, laddie. We can hold the perimeter from here on out.$B$BHere, take this for yer troubles. It might come in handy, as I\'ve got something more important to ask of ye...',0),
(24470,'enUS','Hmm... they blame us for destroying their home, ye say? Well, that wasn\'t us, that was the horrible earthquake we had earlier today. Are they that dense that they can\'t see we nearly lost our camp too?$B$BCan\'t blame a trogg for fightin\' for his home, though.',0),
(24471,'enUS','Many of those that y\'saved have already made it back to camp. The wounds\'re well-dressed! Ye might have a future in first aid, if ye\'re into that sorta thing.',0),
(24472,'enUS','You definitely got the ettin angry, $n.  I heard him myself.$B$BLet\'s hope this works.',0),
(24473,'enUS','Achh.. and what do YOU want? Can\'t ye see I\'m busy in here! Go an\' bother someone else, I haven\'t the time.$B$BWait, what\'s that ye say? Joren sent you to help? Well why didn\'t ye say so?',0),
(24474,'enUS','<Jona drinks deeply from the Gnomenbrau.>$B$BAhh... that hits the spot. Now we can get some work done around here.',0),
(24475,'enUS','This\'ll have to do for now. We\'ve a lot of people to feed here, but we\'ve got to make do with what we\'ve got. With any luck, King Bronzebeard in Ironforge will send us some help shortly.',0),
(24476,'enUS','I... I don\'t understand. Tempering the sword should\'ve restored the blade to its original condition. What has happened here?',0),
(24477,'enUS','Wonderful! Look at this one... it must be over 200 years old!$B$BNow, onto other matters...',0),
(24478,'enUS','Brilliant. You certainly don\'t let cold feet stop you. Or cold any part for that matter!$B$BNo? ...too soon?',0),
(24479,'enUS','I like the way you move, apprentice.$B$BDon\'t you worry about where I got all the souls from. They were obtained in a perfectly humane manner, I assure you.',0),
(24480,'enUS','I had not thought it possible for evil to take hold in such a sword, but I suppose it was naive of me. If the greatest of dragonkind\'s creations could be corrupted and turned against them, why not a mere sword?$B$BUther\'s advice is wise, $n, and I would urge you to heed it quickly.',0),
(24483,'enUS','It\'s good to see you made it, $n. It looks like most everybody did.$B$BWe\'re not doing too bad so far for an emergency evacuation.',0),
(24484,'enUS','You\'ve done well, $n. The spiders are everywhere, however, and I\'m afraid we\'ve barely put a dent in their numbers.',0),
(24486,'enUS','Well would you look at this! An axe blade, a couple of arrowheads, and what appears to be some sort of rudimentary spoon. This is indeed fascinating.$B$BThanks again for your help, $n. I\'ve much studying to keep myself occupied while Joren\'s got us under lockdown.',0),
(24487,'enUS','Welcome, $C. Are you ready to get to work?',0),
(24488,'enUS','That\'s my boy! Now to get one of these useless hunks of metal in working order and you into the game!',0),
(24489,'enUS','Hmm... interesting. From what you\'re saying, it sounds like a fire elemental might have snuck in from Searing Gorge. Or, the earthquake opened up a crack to the elemental plane...$B$B<Soren laughs uncomfortably.>$B$BEither way, this is bad news. You should probably report this information to Grelin.',0),
(24490,'enUS','To Ironforge? Well first, you\'ll need to go through Kharanos, and before that, you\'ll have to go through this tunnel.',0),
(24491,'enUS','Milo Geartwinge, reporting for duty. You sent up a distress signal?',0),
(24492,'enUS','Took you long enough. Hold on tight, and take a good hard look! Chances are you won\'t be coming back here for quite some time.',0),
(24493,'enUS','Coldridge Valley? I\'ve got my own problems here! What, they can\'t deal with a couple of troggs? And trolls? And incursions from the elemental plane?$B$BActually, on second thought, that\'s kind of a lot. I\'m surprised they\'re doing as well as they are. I\'ll see what I can do.',0),
(24494,'enUS','These are dark days, friend. Look around you... even here in remote Coldridge, the sprits are rebelling. The land is crying out for help. Yet still, even in times such as these, the spirits will always turn an ear to those who ask for their assistance.',0),
(24495,'enUS','Thank you, $n. It will take some time, but I\'ll try to make sense of what we have.',0),
(24496,'enUS','The power of the arcane is everywhere, $n. Only some of us have the ability to see it, and fewer still possess the ability to master it.$B$BYou are one of those few.',0),
(24497,'enUS','It\'s past time that these night elf scum be purged from Azshara. Glad to have an able body like you to sink the point home.$B$BReady to get to work?',0),
(24498,'enUS','You\'ve done well this day. With many of the slaves freed and now with access to the forges, it will not be long before I have a strong force to aid in delivering us from Scourgelord Tyrannus and this foul pit.',0),
(24499,'enUS','Just in time! Thank you, $n.$B$BThe Pit of Saron lies ahead, and if our scouts are correct, past that will be the Halls of Reflection. It is there that Arthas lets his guard down, and it is there that we hope to find a clue to his weakness... or maybe, just maybe, his redemption.',0),
(24500,'enUS','<Jaina is still catching her breath.>$B$BI can barely believe we\'re still alive. It was foolish of me to follow him. I\'ve made that mistake too many times. And you... it was reckless of you to come after me instead of escaping with the information!$B$BBut... well... thank you. You truly are a hero.$B$BWith Uther\'s guidance, we may stand a chance at defeating Arthas. All the lives lost today were not in vain.',0),
(24501,'enUS','Great job, $n. We\'ve heard rumors of survivors further in the mountains. Now we\'ll be able to send scouts there.',0),
(24503,'enUS','Uh... you did it, kid. You REALLY did it! We won the game and....$B$BDID YOU SEE THAT DRAGON?!!!',0),
(24504,'enUS','Patrolling the high road is grave business, but it must be done. These narrow mountain trails are, for the time being, one of our only lifelines into Stonetalon. They must be preserved.$B$BThank you.',0),
(24505,'enUS','So the Alliance is probing the twists and turns of the high road?$B$BEven if they were to map it out, they couldn\'t attack these hills in numbers. This is our land, $n. And they will pay dearly for presuming otherwise.',0),
(24506,'enUS','Good. $n, I know of you. You\'ll be perfect for these tasks.$B$BWe\'ve been afforded a rare chance to delve into Icecrown Citadel, but we must move quickly if we\'re to avoid Arthas\' notice.',0),
(24507,'enUS','You\'ve done well this day.$B$BWith many of the slaves freed and now with access to the forges, it will not be long before I have a strong force to aid in delivering us from Scourgelord Tyrannus and this foul pit.',0),
(24510,'enUS','$n! I\'m so glad you\'ve come.$B$BWe\'ve been afforded a rare chance to delve into Icecrown Citadel, but we must move quickly if we\'re to avoid Arthas\' notice.',0),
(24511,'enUS','The Pit of Saron lies ahead, and if our scouts are correct, past that will be the Halls of Reflection.$B$BIt is there that Arthas lets his guard down, and it is there that we hope to find a clue to his weakness... and a route to vengeance long overdue.',0),
(24512,'enUS','From up here I got the perfect view of the havoc you just caused, $n. Our lost brothers reclaimed some of their dignity, and the Alliance dogs were sent scrambling. Sharp work, my friend!$B$BIf the Alliance sleeps comfortably at night, we are not doing our job.$B$BWe will never let up.$B$BWe will never give in.',0),
(24513,'enUS','You have them? I\'ll take your word for it. Hearing Peake scream like one of his victims is reward enough for me.$B$BNow leave me be, $n. I do not wish to be a burden to my clan.',0),
(24514,'enUS','<Onatay looks over the fresh hides, nodding her head slowly.>$B$BYes $n, I can work with these. You work fast!$B$BThese hides will help us hold out for reinforcements longer. Thank you.',0),
(24515,'enUS','So my sister recognized the old signals? Her hunter\'s eyes are as sharp as ever.$B$B$n, when we first set up this camp we were at the edge of this jungle. Now look at it!$B$BSomething is amiss.',0),
(24517,'enUS','Excellent, $n. It will be some time before we can assault the hold proper, but until then, we must teach them to fear the Barrens.',0),
(24518,'enUS','<Kilrok pages through the plans you discovered.>$B$BThis explains much, $n. No wonder our foes are so hellbent on taking the southern Barrens. It\'s at the center of their plans for the continent!$B$BBut they didn\'t account for us, did they $C?',0),
(24519,'enUS','Good, good. We\'ve got to keep Honor\'s Stand isolated.$B$BAlone ... afraid ... $n, if we keep up the pressure, maybe someday they\'ll simply surrender the pass.',0),
(24520,'enUS','You\'re kidding, right?! DEATHWING?!!!$B$B<Sassy looks panicked for a moment.>$B$BOkay, this\'ll work out just fine. We\'ll throw your party and by the time it\'s over, I\'m sure that the dragon will be long gone and the ground will stop shaking.$B$BIf not, we can always charter a ship off of the island.',0),
(24522,'enUS','Admit you to the Sunwell? That\'s impossible! The Sunwell is the most sacred and important site of our people. We have only recently reclaimed it with the help of the Shattered Sun Offensive. It is not a place for tourists or travelers.',0),
(24523,'enUS','Very good, $n. I can feel the sacrifice of the land in this offering, and my spirit swells with sadness, and pride.',0),
(24524,'enUS','You\'ve done it. You have cleaned the wells, and healed our land. Bloodhoof village is grateful, $n.$B$BMay the wind whisper your deeds for a hundred seasons, and may the waters of Mulgore remain clean forever.',0),
(24525,'enUS','So it is done.$B$BNormally these scavengers are part of the Earthmother\'s cycle of life. But on the heels of the devastation wracked by both the Alliance and the cataclysm, their numbers grow overwhelming. It is good to thin them out.',0),
(24526,'enUS','There we go! One spell down, many many more to go. Come back to me after you\'ve had some experience casting this spell, and I\'ll show you some more tricks.',0),
(24527,'enUS','This has been but one of many footfalls on the long path of the $C. Come back to me after you\'ve had some experience in the field, and I will help guide you on your next step.',0),
(24528,'enUS','There, ya did it. The Light favors quick learners like you. Come back to me after you\'ve spent some time using what I\'ve taught ya, and I\'ll show ya something new.',0),
(24529,'enUS','It\'s bad enough to have one\'s village sacked... but to spend the following night in a quilboar cage? I\'m glad you were there to help, $n.',0),
(24530,'enUS','Now that ye\'ve got a new $C trick under yer belt, and now that I\'ve got some of yer money, go out there an\' track some beasts! Come back sometime in the future, an\' we\'ll talk again.',0),
(24531,'enUS','Now we\'re getting somewhere. You\'ve got quite a manly bellow, sir!$B$BCome back to me in a bit, and I\'ll teach you something else.',0),
(24532,'enUS','You\'ve got the hang of it. Go get some practice out there... maybe take out a few of those troggs or trolls. Or rabbits, I don\'t care.$B$BReturn after you\'ve gotten some practice, and I\'ll show you another trick of the trade.',0),
(24533,'enUS','Well done, $n. You\'ll make a fine $C in due time.$B$BReturn to me after you\'ve proven yourself a bit more, and I\'ll reward you by teaching you another spell or two.',0),
(24534,'enUS','What? He attacked you with a dozen boars? I guess quilboar have their own ideas of what \"single combat\" means.$B$BStill, the Bristleback will be left reeling after the blow you delivered. It will not be long before a new champion rises amongst them to stir up trouble... but at least this buys us some time to get these refugees relocated safely.$B$BThank you, $n. The survivors owe you a great debt.',0),
(24535,'enUS','I confess that I did not expect Thalorien\'s spirit to recognize you as the heir to Quel\'Delar, but I defer to his judgment. You may enter the Sunwell, but I remind you that you are a guest in our most sacred of precincts, and you should act accordingly.',0),
(24536,'enUS','Hey, thanks, kid. Give it over, let\'s take a look.$B$B<He takes the device from you and fiddles with it.>$B$BOh, that ain\'t good.',0),
(24539,'enUS','Thank you, $n. But now on to the larger question:$B$BWhere is this overgrowth coming from? And why is it raging out of control?',0),
(24540,'enUS','Welcome back, $n.$B$B$B$BWhat was done was not for revenge, or pride. It was simply to protect Thunder Bluff, and all our people, from torment and fear. Today, Mulgore is safe once more.$B$BThe Earth Mother thanks you for all your brave deeds, $n, as do I. You have earned your reward, hero. May you be welcome in Thunder Bluff always.',0),
(24541,'enUS','You got it, huh? Good job, kid. Top notch. Let\'s see what we got here.$B$B<He cracks open the crate and rummages around inside.>',0),
(24542,'enUS','Ah, samples from different parts of the overgrowth? These will be immensely helpful, yes. Thank you, $C.',0),
(24543,'enUS','<Kirge listens intently and then falls to one knee.>$B$BAlive! My boy still lives! Praise to the earthmother, I still have a son.$B$B<Kirge composes himself.>$B$B$C, my boy\'s mother didn\'t make it out of Taurajo alive. I will avenge her death, even if it means my son grows up without either of his parents.',0),
(24545,'enUS','A deep sense of dread washes over you as the flame devours the items.',0),
(24546,'enUS','So you held your ground! With tenacity like yours we may yet drive the Alliance from our lands.',0),
(24547,'enUS','<Highlord Mograine eyes you in silence for a moment.>$B$BYou seem to have endured this leg of your trial admirably, $R.$B$BPray that fate continues to smile upon you in your endeavor...',0),
(24548,'enUS','These should suffice, $C.$B$BSpeak to me when Shadow\'s Edge has been thoroughly empowered and I will attempt its completion.',0),
(24549,'enUS','Congratulations, $C.$B$BAgainst insurmountable odds, you have weathered the storm.$B$BI trust that you shall find your reward proportionate to your conviction...',0),
(24550,'enUS','Welcome to Thunder Bluff, $n. You\'ve done great things for our people.$B$BTell me of your journey.',0),
(24551,'enUS','<Bloodhilt looks at the badges, then allows them to spill from his hands onto the sands below. His lips curl open into a toothy grin.>$B$BNow THIS is what I like to see, $C! What is your name again?$B$BYou will go far here.',0),
(24552,'enUS','Ah yes... I see a cunning in your eyes that was not present before. Well done, $C.',0),
(24553,'enUS','This is unbelievable, $n. You\'ve really done it! All of the quel\'dorei have heard of Thalorien Dawnseeker and Quel\'Delar, but no one ever thought the sword would be restored.',0),
(24554,'enUS','<Myralion takes the hilt from you and scrutinizes the artifact.>$B$BThis came from the citadel? What was it doing there? This blade is certainly not of Scourge manufacture.$B$BWeapons of this quality can only be crafted by a few of Azeroth\'s creatures. We will have to consult them and see if they can help us identify it.',0),
(24555,'enUS','We must recover that book from the Silver Covenant. Without that book from Krasus, we stand little chance of solving the mystery of the sword in Icecrown or unlocking its power.',0),
(24556,'enUS','I knew Shandy would find a way to make it work. Let me get this enchanted and ready for you to use. With any luck, the tabard\'s owner won\'t even know it\'s missing and Shandy will cover the rest of our tracks.',0),
(24557,'enUS','<Magister Hathorel reads the captured orders.>$B$BThe agent you intercepted was supposed to deliver the Wyrmrest tome to Icecrown, after meeting with one Arcanist Tybalin inside the Silver Enclave. We have to reclaim that book, $n, and we only have one chance before it leaves the city. We have to work quickly.',0),
(24558,'enUS','<Myralion accepts the heavy book and begins leafing through it.>$B$BThose symbols on the blade seemed familiar and now there\'s little wonder why. This is certainly a dragon blade, gifted to one of the mortal races, but which blade is this, and how did it come to rest in Icecrown?',0),
(24559,'enUS','You have remade the blade of Quel\'Delar in defiance of that Blood-Queen Lana\'thel\'s pronouncement! Now, the blade must be tempered before we can show her the folly of her words.',0),
(24560,'enUS','Tempering the sword should\'ve restored the blade. Why hasn\'t it worked?',0),
(24561,'enUS','How can evil take root in such a sword? I would not have thought it possible if the evidence wasn\'t here before my eyes. If the greatest of dragonkind\'s creations could be corrupted and turned against them, why not a mere sword?$B$BI believe Uther is right. You must heed his advice quickly, $n.',0),
(24562,'enUS','I hope you understand that I can\'t just admit you to the Sunwell, $n. This is the most sacred place known to the sin\'dorei and we have only recently regained control over it.$B$BYou would raise the hopes of our people with tales of Quel\'Delar? Without proof of the truth of your claims, I see no reason to take you at your word.',0),
(24563,'enUS','You truly do carry Quel\'Delar. This is a great day for all of Quel\'Thalas and the sin\'dorei. You have my leave to enter the Sunwell and finish the sword\'s restoration. Keep your head high, $n. The children of Silvermoon have dreamt of this day for years.',0),
(24564,'enUS','Am I truly laying my eyes upon the weapon of Thalorien Dawnseeker? This is a wondrous day for the Sunreavers and for all sin\'dorei!',0),
(24565,'enUS','Thank you, $n. I\'m pleased to see you return intact; the viciousness I\'ve been seeing among these creatures is startling.',0),
(24566,'enUS','Oh dear. It seems the forces at work here are a bit difficult to control...$B$BPlease, don\'t bother Naralex with this. It will only upset him.',0),
(24567,'enUS','There you are, my boy! Quick, there\'s no time to waste! We need to get one of these shredders back in working order.$B$BI\'m bringing you off the bench... you\'re going to win the game and the title for us!',0),
(24569,'enUS','Very good. Now, should they storm the gates, they will have to do so with infantry.$B$BDo you think they have the stomach for that?',0),
(24570,'enUS','These will do perfectly. Bright colors like these don\'t occur naturally in the barrens, but they haven\'t developed any other mutations so far.',0),
(24571,'enUS','I\'m concerned by how...active these are. Nevertheless, it simply means we must continue to act quickly before the corruption here becomes worse.',0),
(24572,'enUS','Excellent. I\'ll have their bodies strung up along the gold road as a message to the Alliance.',0),
(24573,'enUS','<Winnoa bows her head.>$B$BThank you.',0),
(24574,'enUS','<Naralex slowly takes the squirming heart from you, visibly disturbed.>$B$BI\'ve been a fool. The one truth I did not want to accept has been staring me in the face this entire time...this foul thing is proof of that.$B$BYou and I have much work to do.',0),
(24575,'enUS','You\'ve done it again, $n. The freed villagers are eager to help us against the Forsaken in any way they can.',0),
(24576,'enUS','You got his ledger? Really? That\'s great, $n. There\'s probably loads of good information in here.',0),
(24577,'enUS','<Gar\'dul breaks into a sweat.>$B$BLook - ah - let\'s not discuss this here, in front of the men...',0),
(24578,'enUS','I\'ve been expecting you, $n. Do not be alarmed.$B$BMy name is Belrysa. I am a priestess of the moon... a night elf.$B$BYou might not know my people, but the destinies of our two races have been linked since the Curse befell you.',0),
(24579,'enUS','With Sartharion slain, surely Deathwing and Sinestra\'s plans are now stalled.',0),
(24580,'enUS','Word of your success precedes you, $C. Anub\'Rekhan is no more. You did him a great service, $n.',0),
(24581,'enUS','That\'s one less thorn in our side. With Noth destroyed, Scourge research into refining the means of creating the undead will grind to a halt.',0),
(24582,'enUS','Well done, $C. The Scourge military command out of Naxxramas has been thrown into disarray by Razuvious\'s demise.',0),
(24583,'enUS','Children everywhere will sleep easier knowing that Patchwerk is no more.',0),
(24584,'enUS','With Malygos defeated, the Nexus War should come to a swift conclusion. You have the gratitude of the Kirin Tor, $n.',0),
(24585,'enUS','I never cease to be amazed by the horrors that can be created through the use of technology.',0),
(24586,'enUS','Now Veranus can finally rest in peace.',0),
(24587,'enUS','I trust that you did not have to face too many of his iron construct assistants?',0),
(24588,'enUS','The greatest weakness of Ulduar is its masters\' blind faith in their inventions to protect it.',0),
(24589,'enUS','All of Azeroth is fortunate that Timear foresaw the Eredar lord\'s arrival and that you were there in time to slay him.',0),
(24590,'enUS','The Frozen Throne is without its chief guardian thanks to you. Our attacks upon the Lich King\'s forces will be all the more successful now.',0),
(24592,'enUS','I wish it could\'ve been avoided, $n. Let us ensure this is resolved without further bloodshed.',0),
(24593,'enUS','It is done then, $n. You are one of us now.',0),
(24594,'enUS','Am I truly laying my eyes upon the weapon of Thalorien Dawnseeker? This is a wondrous day for the Sunreavers and for all sin\'dorei!',0),
(24595,'enUS','This is unbelievable, $n. You\'ve really done it! All of the quel\'dorei have heard of Thalorien Dawnseeker and Quel\'Delar, but no one ever thought the sword would be restored.',0),
(24596,'enUS','Am I truly laying my eyes upon the weapon of Thalorien Dawnseeker? This is a wondrous day for the Sunreavers and for all sin\'dorei!',0),
(24597,'enUS','My thanks for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),
(24598,'enUS','Am I truly laying my eyes upon the weapon of Thalorien Dawnseeker? This is a wondrous day for the Sunreavers and for all sin\'dorei!',0),
(24601,'enUS','We\'ve done it! The nightmare\'s connection to this place has been severed. The rest of the land is safe from this intrusion now, and in time, the abberations here will be subsumed by the balance of nature.$B$BI cannot thank you enough, $n. By helping to restore order here, you\'ve let me make amends for my foolish actions.',0),
(24602,'enUS','Thank you, $n. Let us hope this works.',0),
(24603,'enUS','Good. Take your reward; this is only a prelude.',0),
(24604,'enUS','Mahka sent you?$B$B<Mankrik\'s fury quells for a moment.>$B$BIt is a small comfort. But nothing can console me until I am done here.',0),
(24606,'enUS','These are blood shards. They used to be found all over the Barrens.$B$BIt\'s said they were formed from the blood of Agamaggan, the great demigod that the quilboar sprang from. I knew the quilboar prized them, but nobody would think they\'d take the time and care to carve them like this one...$B$BThere may be more to learn here.',0),
(24607,'enUS','Anotha newblood, eh?$B$BYa actually look ta be in shape though. Steady hands. Fierce eyes. I may be able ta turn ya into a real $C.$B$BLets not waste anymore time \'den.',0),
(24608,'enUS','Good. Good! They will all die! Their chieftains, and their women, and their children, and their foul pets!',0),
(24609,'enUS','My thanks for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),
(24610,'enUS','My thanks for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),
(24611,'enUS','My thanks for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),
(24612,'enUS','My \"thanks\" for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),
(24613,'enUS','My thanks for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),
(24614,'enUS','My thanks for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),
(24615,'enUS','My thanks for this Lovely Charm Bracelet.',0),
(24616,'enUS','Well done, $n. The scout never had a chance.',0),
(24617,'enUS','You\'re all right, $n! I\'ve been waiting for this day for a long time, it truly is great to see you friend.$B$BI\'ve heard of what you\'ve done and I\'m thankful... especially for Lorna -- she\'s all I\'ve left. I will send for her right away.',0),
(24618,'enUS','Excellent! You\'re my kind of $C, $n.$B$BWith your help, we will throw these invaders back into the sea.',0),
(24619,'enUS','<Calder peers into the sack of extremities and licks his lips with a dry, black tongue.>$B$BOh my. This is exciting.$B$B Aren\'t you excited, $n?',0),
(24620,'enUS','<Calder grasps the gigantic heart in both hands, squeezing it and listening to the valves slurp and squish.>$B$B<His pale mask of a face splits open into an enormous, childlike grin.>$B$BIt is so very important to love one\'s work, wouldn\'t you agree, $n?',0),
(24621,'enUS','<Calder holds the brains in an outstretched hand while withdrawing a gore-caked multi-tool from his belt.>$B$BWonderful work! Now the secret here is to leave the reptilian nervous systems intact while removing the higher cognitive functions. We can\'t have our new friend developing a conscience or remembering he\'s Alliance...$B$B<Calder digs and snips at the brain, removing large chunks.>$B$BAnd... we\'re finished! How lovely.',0),
(24622,'enUS','Nice ta see new faces \'round here, mon. It\'s easy ta get ta feelin\' isolated since we left Orgrimmar.',0),
(24623,'enUS','Thank ya so much! They can be vicious when provoked, but most of da time dey don\'t know betta.',0),
(24624,'enUS','Thank you, $C.$B$BIt will be takin\' brave and determined people like you ta drive da Darkspear up again. I hope dere are more people even half as dedicated to come.',0),
(24625,'enUS','Well done, $n! Dis naga has set us back quite some time, but nothin\' will be holdin\' us down foreva.$B$BIt\'s good ta be havin\' ya wit us, $n. Ya have a fierce heart within ya.',0),
(24626,'enUS','Swiftclaw! Kijara was tellin\' me about him and he sounded like he\'d be a handful. I don\'t mind da challenge - it\'s da spirited ones like dat that be makin\' da bravest and truest companions when real times of need be comin\'.$B$BTank ya, hon. Ya\'ve been very helpful.',0),
(24627,'enUS','You are as good as I remember, $n. It is good to have you back.',0),
(24628,'enUS','These simple leaves grow by Elune\'s grace. They will help your mind understand the need for balance and your soul will permanently earn mastery over the beast.',0),
(24629,'enUS','Great work, $n! People will come running to buy Crown perfumes now that they\'ve had a chance to sample their wonders.$B$BHere\'s a little something for helping us out.',0),
(24631,'enUS','<Tomusa snorts as he takes back his hook.>$B$BVengeance feels hollow. Still. I could not allow them to go unpunished.',0),
(24632,'enUS','<Gann looks you up and down.>$B$BWe could use your help, $C. But this is not a skirmish. We fight here to strike a killing blow... or die trying.',0),
(24633,'enUS','Thank you, $n.',0),
(24634,'enUS','Hah! The fool didn\'t destroy these orders.$B$BLet\'s see what we can learn...',0),
(24635,'enUS','Nice work, $n! People will be buying Crown colognes by the crate-load now that they\'ve had a chance to try them.$B$BHere\'s a little something for helping us out.',0),
(24636,'enUS','Lovely work, $n! People will be tripping over one another to get Crown chocolates now that they\'ve had a chance to taste those sweet, romantic treats.$B$BHere\'s a little something for helping us out.',0),
(24637,'enUS','<Upon hearing the news, Bloodhilt snorts. His eyes gleam. He tips his head back and bellows a wet, cackling laugher that echoes between the blackened walls of Desolation hold and reverberates throughout the hills beyond.>$B$BSo it is done! The Butcher of Taurajo is felled at last. Cut down in the streets like a dog. Fitting.$B$BYou have done well, $n. You\'ve sowed fear into our enemies, and soon we will reap the harvest!',0),
(24638,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24639,'enUS','Not bad, mon. Ya have a natural flow to ya swings - you may have a talent for dis.$B$BSome rough edges ta be sure, but we\'ll get dose ironed out here and I\'ll teach ya a few new tings as we go.',0),
(24640,'enUS','Good work, mon! Dis stuff come easy to ya.',0),
(24641,'enUS','Dese are some fine pelts, boy. We could make some hefty cloaks outta dese.',0),
(24642,'enUS','Ya handle yerself quite well. Ya gonna be quite powerful some day.',0),
(24643,'enUS','Ya tha new recruit everyone\'s talkin\' about, eh? Welcome ta tha Darkspear.',0),
(24645,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24646,'enUS','I knew we could count on you. You\'ve done well, $n.',0),
(24647,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24648,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24649,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24650,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24651,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24652,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24653,'enUS','Yes, these are clearly symbols of Agamaggan. But if the quilboar are still devoted to their dead god, what is the source of their vicious agression? It is said Agamaggan was noble, and even gave his life fighting the Burning Legion...$B$BA moment, $n. We must confer with the spirits.',0),
(24654,'enUS','You\'re covered in hot tar and bug juice! Don\'t worry, friend. It\'ll come off.$B$BSomeday.',0),
(24655,'enUS','Hey, thanks, kid. Give it over, let\'s take a look.$B$B<He takes the device from you and fiddles with it.>$B$BOh, that ain\'t good.',0),
(24656,'enUS','You got it, huh? Good job, kid. Top notch. Let\'s see what we got here.$B$B<He cracks open the crate and rummages around inside.>',0),
(24657,'enUS','You got his ledger? Really? That\'s great, $n. There\'s probably loads of good information in here.',0),
(24658,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24659,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24660,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24662,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24663,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24664,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24665,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24666,'enUS','Good job, kid. You deserve a little somethin\'. And hey, come back tomorrow if you get the time; I might have a job for ya.',0),
(24667,'enUS','Is this from Crawgol? Wonderful! Despite all the turmoil in the world, we can\'t turn our back on the silithid threat. It is important to have people like Crawgol studying our enemy closely and learning its secrets for the fight ahead!$B$B<Tauna opens the book and glances over the first page. Her face falls.>$B$BOh. Well. I suppose it\'s something, at least.',0),
(24671,'enUS','Success! Was there ever any doubt?$B$BGreely, fire up the poultryizer!',0),
(24672,'enUS','$n!$B$BGenn... they\'ve taken Genn... they\'ve taken... our king!',0),
(24673,'enUS','King Greymane gave me a brief rundown of the plan before he set off for the Blackwald. Doesn\'t make it sound any less crazy.',0),
(24674,'enUS','I thank you, $n. Our people will no longer suffer under that monstrosity\'s yolk.',0),
(24675,'enUS','I thank you, $n. Our men and women will have a last good meal before they set off for battle.',0),
(24676,'enUS','We have the people of Emberstone on our side now thanks to you.',0),
(24677,'enUS','I am glad to have you here, $n. We\'re surrounded by Forsaken on all sides and can use all the help we can get.',0),
(24678,'enUS','You\'re here, $n. Most everyone made it through, but now we\'re stuck here... surrounded by our own... dead!',0),
(24679,'enUS','It\'s done, $n. The dead return to their slumber.',0),
(24680,'enUS','It\'s good to see you again, $n.',0),
(24681,'enUS','It\'s almost over, $n. Only one obstacle remains between us and survival.',0),
(24682,'enUS','Incapable fools.$B$BI begin to wonder if any of these louts from the tournament will be of any use at all. Perhaps you\'ll prove me wrong.',0),
(24683,'enUS','I underestimated this Scourgelord, and it\'s my men that paid for it. When I think that my guilt over Arthas\' betrayal cannot go any deeper, he proves me wrong yet again.$B$BWe have to press on. We cannot let their sacrifice be meaningless.',0),
(24684,'enUS','You do good work, $C. That riot you caused at the fortress entrance has these dwarves running around with their heads cut off.',0),
(24685,'enUS','Let\'s see, let\'s see.$B$BIt looks like the artillery shells are prepped here, then loaded into the secure magazine...$B$B<Weezil rubs his hands together.>$B$B$n, are you ready to blow some stuff up?',0),
(24686,'enUS','Hmm... yes, these seeds will do nicely. You have the gratitude of the Cenarion Circle, $n.',0),
(24687,'enUS','You return victorious. Good, good... perhaps the crater will now be a bit safer to those who travel through it.',0),
(24689,'enUS','Ahh... did Garl send you? How are his studies coming? I find that he can be a bit slow at times, but he\'s truly a force to be reckoned with when he takes the form of the bear.$B$BNow, we have more pressing matters to attend to.',0),
(24690,'enUS','At last, Blazerunner is dispatched. Thanks, $n... he was driving me batty.',0),
(24691,'enUS','Brilliant! We\'re on the cusp of something big here, $n. Here\'s your share of the inevitably huge profits.$B$BNow, on to other matters...',0),
(24692,'enUS','You\'ve completed a remarkable task, $n. You are truly worthy of commendation. Thank you, and congratulations!',0),
(24693,'enUS','Very well, if Quixxil recommended you, then I suppose you\'re alright. In all our years working together, Quixxil\'s never steered me wrong.',0),
(24694,'enUS','I have been watching you, $n. Your arrival was not unforeseen.$B$BIn fact, your arrival here has been predetermined for some time now.',0),
(24695,'enUS','You have proven to be both wise and agile, young $n. You have my blessing to take your newfound knowledge and spread it as you continue on your journey.',0),
(24697,'enUS','Excellent work, $n. Now we\'re a bit safer from dinosaur attacks... plus I\'ve got all this fresh meat to serve to my men.',0),
(24698,'enUS','Good ol\' Nolen. How is he doing? Hopefully better than I am...',0),
(24699,'enUS','Yes, this tar is just the stuff...$B$BHey, wait a minute, my hands... I can\'t seem to get them apart...$B$BMaybe this wasn\'t such a good idea. Oh, but wait! Super sticky tar remover! That\'s where the real money is!',0),
(24700,'enUS','Oh, there they are. Great work, handsome! Here\'s some gold. You\'ve earned it.',0),
(24701,'enUS','It\'s a bunch of junk, but it\'s a bunch of FREE junk, and that\'s all that matters to me.$B$BWell, mostly free. Here\'s your share. Thanks!',0),
(24702,'enUS','<You almost sense an air of gratitude as you place the Bloodpetal sprouts on the grave.>',0),
(24703,'enUS','You please me, $n. From this day forward, you are no longer a simple beggar, but a squire loyal to Maximillian of Northshire. Prepare yourself for our first sally, good squire, for together we shall plunge our fists elbow-deep into what they call adventure!',0),
(24704,'enUS','...and that makes 15 of them.$B$BJustice had a name today... and that name was Maximillian of Northshire. For Doloria!',0),
(24705,'enUS','Our duty is fulfilled. Even so, it troubles me that today\'s damsels were less than gracious... only the fair-haired one by the lake managed to show us any gratitude for our chivalry. Perhaps tomorrow\'s damsels will have thankfulness to match their beauty.$B$BNow we must ride. More adventures await!',0),
(24706,'enUS','Might I ask you a question? What act have you committed to make the spirits so angry at you? I\'m impressed that you had the patience to sit so still while they pummeled you so violently.$B$BNow we may proceed. The teeth and scales of Un\'Goro\'s greatest dragon await us.',0),
(24707,'enUS','The day is saved! Huzzah! Today we learned that while armor can be replaced, valor has no price.$B$BBecause of your key involvement in this task, I hereby graduate you from squire to fledgling knight. No longer do the chains of servitude bind you to me; you are free to serve other masters.$B$BGo with honor, young hero! For chivalry, the Light, and the beauty of Doloria!',0),
(24708,'enUS','What an interesting femur you\'ve brought here, but why\'s it all sharp and curvy?$B$B...$B$BWait a minute, that thing\'s a TALON? A dinosaur with a talon that size would\'ve been... well, really big, that\'s for sure. Is this the only fossil that you found there?',0),
(24709,'enUS','I knew it! Durrin HAS been digging around here. And he\'s been excavating what could be the archaeological find of the century! Now I just have to find out where he\'s stashing the bones...$B$BThanks $n. You\'ve been a great help.',0),
(24710,'enUS','Such a senseless waste! Arthas goes too far! I can only hope what we find in the Halls of Reflection makes this somehow worth it.$B$BIf what that vile gnome said is to be trusted, Frostmourne should be there, and with it, answers to confronting Arthas.',0),
(24711,'enUS','The Halls of Reflection. Finally.$B$BLet me know when you are ready. Arthas may not be here, but it would be naive to think that he would leave Frostmourne unguarded entirely.',0),
(24712,'enUS','The Halls of Reflection lie ahead.$B$BIf what that vile gnome said is to be trusted, Frostmourne should be there, and with it, answers to confronting Arthas.',0),
(24713,'enUS','The Halls of Reflection. Finally.$B$BLet me know when you are ready, $C. I will not be so naive as to think that Arthas left his precious sword entirely unguarded.',0),
(24714,'enUS','A-Me lies motionless before you. No power seems to be running through her components.',0),
(24715,'enUS','You pour the coconut milk into what appears to be A-Me 01\'s oil reservoir. You hear the sound of gears whirring and actuators firing.',0),
(24717,'enUS','Wow, 2 of each color! You\'re certainly an overachiever, $n. My companions and I could use a $R like you around here. Ever consider a career in profiteering?',0),
(24718,'enUS','Wow, look at this one! Not just the color, but the size of it... you could cover a tauren with this.$B$BHere you go, $n. You\'ve earned this. Stick around, I\'m sure we can find something else for you to do.',0),
(24719,'enUS','My mentor says that sometimes you have to take away from nature before you can give back. These raptors... I feel that they died for good cause.$B$BThank you, $n.',0),
(24720,'enUS','Now I will continue my experiments! Thank you, $n.',0),
(24721,'enUS','You were right to bring this pylon to my attention, $n. This is just the sort of thing I\'ve been studying.',0),
(24722,'enUS','You think this may be related to the attacks on Marshal\'s Refuge, $n?',0),
(24723,'enUS','A pylon in the west? And a relationship between titans and dinosaurs? This is a lot to take in, $n.',0),
(24724,'enUS','Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.$B$BThe resulting combination is now yours.',0),
(24725,'enUS','Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.$B$BThe resulting combination is now yours.',0),
(24726,'enUS','Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.$B$BThe resulting combination is now yours.',0),
(24727,'enUS','Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.$B$BThe resulting combination is now yours.',0),
(24728,'enUS','Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.$B$BThe resulting combination is now yours.',0),
(24729,'enUS','Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.$B$BThe resulting combination is now yours.',0),
(24730,'enUS','Excellent, these should do the trick. And now, if you\'ll permit me, in case anyone\'s listening...$B$BTHANKS FOR DIGGING ALL OF THESE BONES OUT OF THE GROUND FOR US AND NOT HURTING THE NATIVE BEASTS IN ANY WAY.$B$BWhether you really did or didn\'t, I don\'t want to know. Let\'s keep it that way, shall we? Here - maybe this will keep your lips shut on the whole thing. Anything to get out of here alive, I say!',0),
(24731,'enUS','This will do nicely, $n. It seems Lar\'korwi eats well these days. Although, I wonder where he found a threshadon in this area. Odd.$B$BRegardless, I will hold onto this until you are ready for your confrontation with the beast. Do not worry for my safety--I am sure you\'ve angered Lar\'korwi enough that he will not kill me until after he\'s tasted your flesh.',0),
(24732,'enUS','Ah, fine specimens, $n. The two pieces you\'ve found should be perfect for baiting Lar\'korwi into the open. I cannot wait to see the outcome of your fight with the monster. He is a massive thing with claws as sharp as the finest blades. You will look into his eyes and you will know death.',0),
(24733,'enUS','The Earth Mother be praised! You\'ve done it! Fair play to you, $n. You have proven to be a great hunter in your own right. Your spirit is strong. Your bravery unmatched. And your strength has been fortified. I bow down to your skills.$B$BOnly the greatest of my ancestors could have accomplished something so incredible. Congratulations.',0),
(24734,'enUS','You find what appears to be Ringo\'s belongings. If he left these here, he can\'t have gone far away. Maybe you should look for him.',0),
(24735,'enUS','Ringo\'s not in the best shape, $n, but I am glad to have him back in one piece!$B$BThank you for finding him.',0),
(24736,'enUS','Yes, these scales are perfect. I should be able to get this flyer off the ground with these scales for sure!$B$BThanks!',0),
(24737,'enUS','Yeah, this tar is pretty sticky, I guess. I mean, it\'s sticky, but it\'s not \"make fistfuls of money\" sticky. I guess I\'ll have to keep thinking.',0),
(24740,'enUS','I hope that did the trick. I\'ll take the ash... this may come in handy sometime down the line.',0),
(24741,'enUS','Nice! Look at the size of those things!$B$BThere\'s no way that Grapplehammer\'s going to be able to top those!',0),
(24742,'enUS','These results are astounding! My boss will be pleased. Thank you, kind $R!',0),
(24743,'enUS','Listen well, $C. In accepting this weapon your fate is sealed.$B$BOvercome or succumb.$B$BI have placed your feet upon this path. You are therefore my personal responsibility. Should you failter, I am duty-bound to deliver you from this life.$B$BRemember my words, $R, and do not fail.',0),
(24744,'enUS','Eureka! My genius saves the day yet again! Take that Bamm Megabomb!$B$BAnd now, to reap the benefits!',0),
(24745,'enUS','What\'ve you got there?$B$BOh hey, this is big. Real big. Most of the crazy details in one little package. Thanks - you really helped us reel this all in. Good working with ya.',0),
(24747,'enUS','Bael\'dun? Destroyed?$B$B<Wincing in pain, Gann twists his head to peer behind him, where plumes of smoke darken the skyline.>$B$B$n, my friend. You have avenged Taurajo and avenged the Tauren people. The invaders will not soon recover from that blow. Thank you.',0),
(24748,'enUS','So, at last it is done.$B$BMay the people of Azeroth remember our deeds here forevermore. May the sacrifices of so many burn in their hearts eternally. May they never fail to risk mortal peril in the face of great evil.',0),
(24749,'enUS','Well done, $C.$B$BThe completion of our work draws near.',0),
(24750,'enUS','Anotha newblood, eh?$B$BYa actually have an intense look about ya though. Fiery eyes. You might have the makings of a real $C.$B$BLets not waste anymore time \'den.',0),
(24751,'enUS','Not bad, mon. Ya have a natural flow to ya spells - you may have a talent for dis.$B$BSome rough edges ta be sure, but we\'ll get dose ironed out here and I\'ll teach ya a few new tings as we go.',0),
(24752,'enUS','Good work, mon! Dis stuff come easy to ya.',0),
(24753,'enUS','Dese are some fine pelts, boy. We could make some hefty cloaks outta dese.',0),
(24754,'enUS','Ya handle yerself quite well. Ya gonna be quite powerful some day.',0),
(24755,'enUS','Ya tha new recruit everyone\'s talkin\' about, eh? Welcome ta tha Darkspear.',0),
(24756,'enUS','Well done, $C.$B$BShadowmourne is nearly within reach.',0),
(24757,'enUS','The axe has drunk its fill, $R, and the forge is nearly ready for the creation of Shadowmourne...',0),
(24758,'enUS','Anotha newblood, eh?$B$BYa actually have a weathered look about ya though. Wise eyes. You might have the makings of a real $C.$B$BLets not waste anymore time \'den.',0),
(24758,'ruRU','Еще один новобранец?$B$BВид у тебя бывалый.И глаза мудрые. Может, ты и вправду $gнастоящий:настоящая:c; |3-6($c).$B$BНе будем терять время.',26365),
(24759,'enUS','Not bad, mon. Ya have a natural flow to ya spells - you may have a talent for dis.$B$BSome rough edges ta be sure, but we\'ll get dose ironed out here and I\'ll teach ya a few new tings as we go.',0),
(24759,'ruRU','Неплохо, $gдружище:подруга;. У тебя прирожденные способности к магии. Прямо-таки настоящий талант.$B$BКонечно, тебе предстоит потрудиться, чтобы овладеть магией по-настоящему. Но я тебя научу.',26365),
(24760,'enUS','Good work, mon! Dis stuff come easy to ya.',0),
(24761,'enUS','Dese are some fine pelts, boy. We could make some hefty cloaks outta dese.',0),
(24761,'ruRU','Хорошие шкуры, $gмалыш:малышка;. Из них можно справить отличные плащи.',26365),
(24762,'enUS','Ya handle yerself quite well. Ya gonna be quite powerful some day.',0),
(24762,'ruRU','А ты молодец. Когда-нибудь станешь очень $gсильным:сильной;.',26365),
(24763,'enUS','Ya tha new recruit everyone\'s talkin\' about, eh? Welcome ta tha Darkspear.',0),
(24763,'ruRU','Так ты и есть $gтот новенький:та новенькая;, о $gкотором:которой; все говорят? Добро пожаловать в Черное Копье.',26365),
(24764,'enUS','Anotha newblood, eh?$B$BYa actually have a wild look about ya though. Fierce eyes. You might have the makings of a real $C.$B$BLets not waste anymore time \'den.',0),
(24765,'enUS','Not bad, mon. Ya have a natural flow to ya casts - you may have a talent for dis.$B$BSome rough edges ta be sure, but we\'ll get dose ironed out here and I\'ll teach ya a few new tings as we go.',0),
