(31588,'enUS','Nice work, $n! You\'re better with those pets than I thought!',0),
(31589,'enUS','Now those look like some healthy pets, $n. Remember, you can heal and revive your entire collection of pets at any time by visiting a stable master.',0),
(31590,'enUS','I see... an excellent choice. You\'re on your way to building up a great team!$B$BRemember, any pet you can fight, you can catch, so go ahead and try to get as many as you can during your adventures.',0),
(31591,'enUS','Nice work, $n! You\'re better with those pets than I thought!',0),
(31592,'enUS','Now those look like some healthy pets, $n. Remember, you can heal and revive your entire collection of pets at any time by visiting a stable master.',0),
(31593,'enUS','I see... an excellent choice. You\'re on your way to building up a great team!$B$BRemember, any pet you can fight, you can catch, so go ahead and try to get as many as you can during your adventures.',0),
(31598,'enUS','Interesting. You were wise to spot the importance of this, Wakener. Organic kyparite is highly valuable to us.$B$BHere, a reward. In fair trade.',0),
(31599,'enUS','I recognize those mandibles. Karanosh ate my brother, you know.$B$BOf course, I have millions of brothers.$B$B<Zikk cackles.>',0),
(31603,'enUS','As long as these shards blanket the land, our home will be a place of fear and death.',0),
(31605,'enUS','<From the looks of it, this mantid was just recently broken out of his chamber. He lets out a hacking cough.>$B$B...Diss-ec...tor... has... returned...',0),
(31606,'enUS','Look at you! Many parts and pieces... yes... and all of them so good at killing. Fascinating.$B$BI must pick your brain some time. Muhahah.',0),
(31609,'enUS','The siege is broken, for now.',0),
(31611,'enUS','So I may have underestimated how safe it is to brew these days.',0),
(31612,'enUS','<Kil\'ruk gives you a strange glance.>$B$BThe Klaxxi\'va may never accept you fully. Their xenophobic minds are closed to the possibility of a useful $R.$B$BI, for one, have been proud to fight by your side, $C. Your presence, and your assistance, do us great honor.',0),
(31613,'enUS','I see you put my Volatile Greenstone Brew to good use. Well done, $C!',0),
(31656,'enUS','A volunteer for Dread Wastes duty? I think you might be the first.$B$BPleased to meet you.',0),
(31660,'enUS','Their eggs should have basked in the warmth of the sun and the song of a million wings for ten more years.$B$BThe Empress will pay for her crimes.',0),
(31661,'enUS','Do you have any idea what this is? It\'s amber!$B$BBut it is polluted with fear.$B$BI would not expect an outsider like you to understand the consequences of this.',0),
(31669,'enUS','Wait until they try these cabbages. Then they\'ll know I\'m the real deal.',0),
(31670,'enUS','I can\'t wait to get my paws on those carrots. Thank you, $n. See you again tomorrow?',0),
(31671,'enUS','I can already smell those scallions from over here. Can\'t wait to pick \'em and sell \'em tomorrow. Thanks!',0),
(31672,'enUS','And now, we play the waiting game...$B$BSorry, that sounded a little creepy. Forget I said that.',0),
(31673,'enUS','I\'d like to see any crocolisks attack my farm now!$B$BHa HA!',0),
(31674,'enUS','Hah! That\'ll show Hillpaw.',0),
(31675,'enUS','Look at that dirt. Practically sparkling.$B$BGrandpa would be proud.',0),
(31676,'enUS','We have a common enemy in the mogu. And perhaps others.$B$BWe shall see.',0),
(31677,'enUS','Gurthan was a coward who trained beasts to do the fighting for him and, in the face of death, chose to suspend his spirit in that urn.$B$BNow we can have the pleasure of killing him as many times as we like.$B$BWell done.',0),
(31680,'enUS','The Klaxxi are pleased with our work, outsider. You have proven to be more resourceful than we thought.',0),
(31681,'enUS','Even this raw amber will be of use. We can\'t afford to be picky in times like these.$B$BThe Klaxxi\'va will be glad I thought of this. I will tell them you helped!',0),
(31682,'enUS','What... what sort of creature are you?$B$BHow have you awoken me?',0),
(31685,'enUS','Welcome to Pandaria, $C. I have a selection of equipment that you may find useful on your journey.',0),
(31687,'enUS','The mantid are relentless. Fortunately for us, you have a dedication that surpasses even theirs.$B$BIt is good to have you walk these roads, $C.',0),
(31688,'enUS','Leng told me of your heroics. He is in your debt, as am I.',0),
(31689,'enUS','In disciplined hands, the spear is the perfect weapon. Only the weak would augment it with sorcery.$B$BAnd we have no need for the weak.',0),
(31690,'enUS','This is a weapon of great beauty and power. If you are certain you wish to part with it, I would be happy to take it from you.',0),
(31691,'enUS','This is a weapon of great beauty and power. If you are certain you wish to part with it, I would be happy to take it from you.',0),
(31692,'enUS','This is a weapon of great beauty and power. If you are certain you wish to part with it, I would be happy to take it from you.',0),
(31693,'enUS','Ouch, you really are a good pet trainer! I guess you\'re the exception.',0),
(31695,'enUS','Welcome to Townlong Steppes. If you insist on wandering in to the darkest places of Pandaria then far be it from me to not put you to good use.',0),
(31698,'enUS','You have carried out the task to the letter, $n.',0),
(31699,'enUS','You have put the sprites in their place, $n. They should cause no more trouble for a while.',0),
(31700,'enUS','I see you and Ningna have been up to some mischief. Unfortunately, this type of behavior is not condoned by the Order--$B$BWait, where did you find those shoes? I\'ve been looking for that pair of moleskin riding boots for ages!$B$BWell... I suppose I will let this slide... this time. Hmph.',0),
(31701,'enUS','Thank you, $n. You are proving to be quite a reliable student.',0),
(31702,'enUS','I see you have vanquished the beast. Quite a promising student, you are.',0),
(31703,'enUS','Good riddance. With everything that is worrying us these days, it is good to have one less problem to worry about.',0),
(31704,'enUS','The hatchling plays contentedly, oblivious to your efforts. Sigh... sometimes, the life of a serpent trainer is quite thankless.',0),
(31705,'enUS','The poisonous wasp is dead? Good. Where so many other students failed, you have succeeded, $n.',0),
(31706,'enUS','Instructor Skythorn updated me on the situation at The Widow\'s Wail. You have done well.',0),
(31707,'enUS','You have done a great deed today, $n. This is the duty of the Order of the Cloud Serpent - to protect the people of The Jade Forest.',0),
(31708,'enUS','<Your serpent sniffs the mushrooms and makes a horrible face. It tries to escape, but you hold it gently and coax it to eat the spongy morsels.>',0),
(31709,'enUS','Thank you for bringing me this report, $n. Big Bao is quite right to be concerned.$B$BThe sha is a subtle and deadly enemy. We must work to expel their dark energy from this land.',0),
(31710,'enUS','Your serpent nudges your hand affectionately, then proceeds to devour the treats!',0),
(31711,'enUS','Excellent work, $n. I \"doubt\" that this enemy is truly gone. Until we can be sure, we must stay vigilant.',0),
(31712,'enUS','The hozen presence is quite troubling. You did well to follow Instructor Skythorn\'s instructions.',0),
(31713,'enUS','Oh, thank the Stormstouts! You are my hero!',0),
(31714,'enUS','Ah yes, these hatchlings look quite tired. They have been through a great ordeal, but thanks to you, they are safe now.',0),
(31715,'enUS','The leader is dead, then? Good. Perhaps now the hozen will leave the villagers in peace.',0),
(31716,'enUS','The hatchling plays contentedly, oblivious to your efforts. Sigh... sometimes, the life of a serpent trainer is quite thankless.',0),
(31717,'enUS','Well done, $C. The sword that is hammered and folded produces a keen blade.',0),
(31718,'enUS','Both of you persevered to the end. Well done, my student.',0),
(31719,'enUS','A fight against Ningna will quickly reveal one\'s strengths and weaknesses. Well done.',0),
(31720,'enUS','Your focus was excellent, $n. Well done.',0),
(31721,'enUS','Your skills are remarkable, $n. When I see such promising students as yourself, I know that The Order will pass into good hands.',0),
(31724,'enUS','Well, I can\'t argue with results like those. You\'ve got a real gift, $n.',0),
(31725,'enUS','You\'re mean! Why didn\'t you let me win? Everyone always lets me win!',0),
(31726,'enUS','Not only do you not fear me or my home, you have defeated me honorably. I\'m impressed.',0),
(31727,'enUS','So the bugs have taken an interest in us have they? Well if they want somethin\' from us they\'ll have to come and earn it themselves!$B$BYou work for what you get here. That means you too!',0),
(31728,'enUS','I demand a do-over ...hic! That washn\'t fair! There was two of ye!',0),
(31729,'enUS','What a show! A most excellent skirmish indeed.',0),
(31730,'enUS','So they want us to leave do they? What a selfish request! We\'re only taking amber from one tree.$B$BWell, I\'m not going anywhere! I have brew to make.$B$BIf you help us maybe we can all come to a mutually beneficial agreement. I give them some brew, they stop trying to kill us.',0),
(31732,'enUS','A proper welcome for the Horde to this new land!',0),
(31733,'enUS','\'Bout time you showed up, laddy! Let\'s do some damage!',0),
(31734,'enUS','With those wagons out of commission, we can turn our attention to the commander.',0),
(31735,'enUS','We\'ll catch up with him again. I\'m sure of it.',0),
(31736,'enUS','When the mist fell, we knew it would only be a matter of time before visitors arrived.$B$BWe could not have predicted it would be like this.',0),
(31737,'enUS','I am glad you took responsibility for your actions. Left unchecked, negative emotions can quickly overwhelm an individual here, just as they started to overwhelm the one you call \"Rell.\"',0),
(31738,'enUS','Our orchard is one of our village\'s greatest treasures. For saving our harvest, we are truly grateful.',0),
(31739,'enUS','I see that you two have been busy. Thank you for recovering our kegs.',0),
(31740,'enUS','You did well to help the Brewers and bring this news to me.$B$BFrom what you have told me, it sounds as if Koukou was possessed by some dark energy. Could it be...?$B$BNo. That is impossible.',0),
(31741,'enUS','One heck of a bloody mess y\'made down there, kid.$B$BNice work.',0),
(31742,'enUS','That\'s some fine and fancy killin\', $C.$B$BNow, with those two all done \'n\' taken care of, all that\'s left is the big fella in the hall behind me.',0),
(31743,'enUS','Me lads up in the sky bring the heat, don\'t they? Ha ha ha!',0),
(31744,'enUS','Aye, I seen the wee ones, too. Busted a few out on m\'way up here.$B$BYe\'ve done good, lad. Those cubs might have some nasty nightmares, but they\'ll grow up some day, thanks to you.',0),
(31745,'enUS','Excellent work, $C. I can see why you came so highly recommended.',0),
(31752,'enUS','I am pleased to offer this gift to you, $R $C. According to my calibrations, it will invoke feelings of enjoyment and gratitude.$B$BHave a nice day.',0),
(31754,'enUS','It\'s a bit more quiet out now. My ringing ears appreciate your hard work.$B$BThanks!',0),
(31755,'enUS','My heart rests a little easier knowing what you\'ve done. Thank you, my dear.',0),
(31756,'enUS','It\'s a lot brighter out! And not just thanks to your sunny smile.$B$BWay to go!',0),
(31757,'enUS','The spirits still come, but our guards can hold them back. The Shao-Tien cannot keep this up for ever.$B$BThank you, $C.',0),
(31758,'enUS','You\'re a good man, helping that silly rogue out more than he deserves.',0),
(31760,'enUS','How went the diplomacy? I hope you didn\'t go easy on them.',0),
(31762,'enUS','Glorious. They will learn to fear us.',0),
(31765,'enUS','Superior Horde firepower at its finest!$B$B...and you did okay too I guess.',0),
(31766,'enUS','There you are!$B$BI was starting to worry we\'d have to charge in and have all the fun without you.',0),
(31767,'enUS','Good work, $C! We have them on their heels!',0),
(31768,'enUS','Haha! Good work, $n.$B$BLeave \'em nothing!',0),
(31769,'enUS','An air base - they had a hidden airbase here this entire time! Had I know I would\'ve kept more men on the guns, I would\'ve - Uaaghh -$B$B<The color drains from Nazgrim\'s face, and his body begins to exude a mysterious dark energy.>',0),
(31770,'enUS','Your fighting has brought about much destruction for our tiny village!$B$BWe have no interest in your war, but we will not turn your injured away.',0),
(31771,'enUS','I am glad you took responsibility for your actions. Left unchecked, negative emotions can quickly overwhelm an individual here, just as they started to overwhelm the one you call \"Nazgrim.\"',0),
(31772,'enUS','Well, it\'s not as much as I would have hoped, but it will have to do. I guess there is no sense in cryin\' over spilled brew.',0),
(31773,'enUS','Ah, so your conflict at the ruins is beginning to pollute the local wildlife? This is very troubling - I have never seen a reaction so intense.$B$BThank you for protecting the village, but it is a tragedy that those poor animals had to die.',0),
(31774,'enUS','<Zin\'Jun is grievously wounded, but senses that you\'re friendly.>$B$BMonkey-tings! Everywhere dere be dese monkey-tings!',0),
(31775,'enUS','The best thing about killing Alliance in Pandaria? It\'ll be months before they get any reinforcements.$B$BThis land will belong to the Horde, $C. We\'re nearly finished.',0),
(31776,'enUS','Blood and thunder, $n. Blood and thunder.',0),
(31777,'enUS','I hope those ding-dongs enjoyed the party you threw for them!',0),
(31778,'enUS','Although I can\'t understand why you chose to bring your war to our land, I can clearly see which side is more virtuous.$B$BThank you for your aid, $R.',0),
(31779,'enUS','The Alliance have been routed. You, Nazgrim, Kiryn, Gorrok, Shokia, and Rivett need a base of operations.$B$BThese flags will have to be changed.$B$BFor the Horde!',0),
(31780,'enUS','I guess I still have a lot to learn.',0),
(31781,'enUS','That wasn\'t fun at all!',0),
(31782,'enUS','We are... undone, wakener.$B$BYour efforts appear to have become imperative to our cause.$B$BOn behalf of the remaining council, I implore you to continue in your assistance.',0),
(31784,'enUS','You did well to bring this egg to me. We will take good care of it, $n.',0),
(31785,'enUS','Great job $n. Next up, catching your own pets!',0),
(31786,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31787,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31788,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31789,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31790,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31791,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31792,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31793,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31794,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31795,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31796,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31797,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31798,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31799,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31800,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31801,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31802,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31803,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31804,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31805,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(31808,'enUS','I was able to glimpse moments of the battle through your mind. It looked to be a massacre! Well done!',0),
(31809,'enUS','<As you present the Claw to Ban, his eyes grow wide with the realization of what you have done.>$B$BI see now what about you has changed.$B$BYou have done the impossible. The Shado-Pan shall record your name, and honor it as long as we stand watch over this land.',0),
(31810,'enUS','Today, we become brethren. Congratulations on joining the Order of the Cloud Serpent. Let us ride together!',0),
(31811,'enUS','Today, we become brethren. Congratulations on joining the Order of the Cloud Serpent. Let us ride together!',0),
(31812,'enUS','Ah, Varzok. Yes, I know him well. He be makin\' no mistake in sendin\' you here.',0),
(31813,'enUS','You fight with the determination of one who does not fear defeat, but does not tolerate it, either. You will go far.',0),
(31814,'enUS','You do not understand. I have not been defeated, merely set back.',0),
(31815,'enUS','Did you enjoy the taste of victory? It\'ll be your last, mon. Things do not get easier from here.',0),
(31817,'enUS','The resilience of Desolace cannot compare to your own desire to grow. I applaud your efforts.',0),
(31818,'enUS','Lay off, mon! Lay off! You win!',0),
(31819,'enUS','Impossible!',0),
(31820,'enUS','Thank you so much.',0),
(31821,'enUS','Great job $n. Next up, catching your own pets!',0),
(31822,'enUS','Great job $n. Next up, catching your own pets!',0),
(31823,'enUS','Great job $n. Next up, catching your own pets!',0),
(31824,'enUS','Great job $n. Next up, catching your own pets!',0),
(31824,'ruRU','Отлично, $n! Теперь поговорим о том, как ловить питомцев',25549),
(31825,'enUS','Great job $n. Next up, catching your own pets!',0),
(31826,'enUS','Great job $n. Next up, catching your own pets!',0),
(31827,'enUS','Great job $n. Next up, catching your own pets!',0),
(31828,'enUS','Great job $n. Next up, catching your own pets!',0),
(31830,'enUS','Great job $n. Next up, catching your own pets!',0),
(31831,'enUS','Great job $n. Next up, catching your own pets!',0),
(31832,'enUS','Great job $n. Next up, catching your own pets!',0),
(31833,'enUS','I hear from Master Woo that your training went well. Come back again in the future to continue your training.',0),
(31834,'enUS','I hear from Master Cheng that your training went well. Come back again in the future to continue your training.',0),
(31835,'enUS','I hear from Master Kistane that your training went well. Come back again in the future to continue your training.',0),
(31836,'enUS','I hear from Master Yoon that your training went well. Come back again in the future to continue your training.',0),
(31837,'enUS','I hear from Master Cheng that your training went well. Come back again in the future to continue your training.',0),
(31838,'enUS','I hear from Master Tsang that your training went well. Come back again in the future to continue your training.',0),
(31839,'enUS','I hear from Master Hsu that your training went well. Come back again in the future to continue your training.',0),
(31840,'enUS','I hear from Master Cheng that your training went well. Come back again in the future to continue your training.',0),
(31841,'enUS','I hear from Master Woo that your training went well. Come back again in the future to continue your training.',0),
(31842,'enUS','I hear from Master Kistane that your training went well. Come back again in the future to continue your training.',0),
(31843,'enUS','I hear from Master Yoon that your training went well. Come back again in the future to continue your training.',0),
(31844,'enUS','I hear from Master Cheng that your training went well. Come back again in the future to continue your training.',0),
(31845,'enUS','I hear from Master Tsang that your training went well. Come back again in the future to continue your training.',0),
(31846,'enUS','I hear from Master Hsu that your training went well. Come back again in the future to continue your training.',0),
(31847,'enUS','A volunteer for Dread Wastes duty? I think you might be the first.$B$BPleased to meet you.',0),
(31850,'enUS','Your risk has paid its reward.',0),
(31851,'enUS','You be the victor today, lad, but next time I won\'t be takin\' it so eashy on ye!',0),
(31852,'enUS','A thrilling match! Splendid! Well done indeed!',0),
(31853,'enUS','Welcome aboard Hellscream\'s Fist, $n!$B$BThis\'ll be her maiden voyage. Ain\'t she a beauty?',0),
(31854,'enUS','Your pets are ecstatic about their victory. I hope you are as well.',0),
(31855,'enUS','Welcome back, $n. It is time to continue your training.',0),
(31856,'enUS','Welcome, $n. It is time to begin your training.',0),
(31857,'enUS','Welcome back, $n. It is time to continue your training.',0),
(31858,'enUS','Welcome back, $n. It is time to continue your training.',0),
(31859,'enUS','Welcome back, $n. It is time to continue your training.',0),
(31860,'enUS','Welcome back, $n. It is time to continue your training.',0),
(31861,'enUS','Welcome back, $n. It is time to continue your training.',0),
(31862,'enUS','You think yourself victorious, but I be growin\' stronger with each defeat.',0),
(31870,'enUS','Woah! You really are somethin\'!',0),
(31871,'enUS','No! Gluk no lose! Rematch!',0),
(31872,'enUS','Your victory is well-deserved. Your skills are superior to my own.',0),
(31876,'enUS','Ah, a scribe of great skill. Some of us here could really use your help.',0),
(31886,'enUS','A volunteer for Dread Wastes duty? I think you might be the first.$B$BPleased to meet you.',0),
(31894,'enUS','<Orbiss groans at you in agony.>$B$BSo, the shado-pan have sent you to see what the yaungol are doing? Well, do you see?',0),
(31895,'enUS','A volunteer for Dread Wastes duty? I think you might be the first.$B$BPleased to meet you.',0),
(31897,'enUS','You really are some sort of hotshot, aren\'t ya? You won\'t be so lucky next time!',0),
(31904,'enUS','I must\'ve converted a line wrong somewhere...',0),
(31905,'enUS','It\'s like my pretties have lost their will to fight.',0),
(31906,'enUS','Mark my words, I will defeat you one day soon.',0),
(31907,'enUS','This world is doomed. Why do you continue to try so fervently?',0),
(31908,'enUS','My flight has come to an end. Victory is yours this day.',0),
(31909,'enUS','You\'re hot stuff!',0),
(31910,'enUS','Perhaps my research is not as complete as I thought.',0),
(31911,'enUS','Perhaps undeath is not the answer...',0),
(31912,'enUS','You\'re no better than Durin. In it for the glory. Pah!',0),
(31913,'enUS','I see you have secrets of your own.',0),
(31914,'enUS','I\'ll defeat ye if it\'s the last thing I ever do. I haven\'t come this far fer nothin\'!',0),
(31915,'enUS','I have an eternity to train. I will defeat you!',0),
(31916,'enUS','You continue to reveal your strategies to me. Eventually, your defeat will be certain.',0),
(31917,'enUS','I\'m so proud of you, $n. You\'re ready for the big time!',0),
(31918,'enUS','Well done, $n. You are finally prepared to truly come into your own as a tamer.',0),
(31920,'enUS','Impossible! I cannot lose!',0),
(31922,'enUS','I forgot to carry the 1!',0),
(31923,'enUS','Nice work!',0),
(31924,'enUS','It would seem that these younglings still have a lot of work to do before they are at full strength. Thank you.',0),
(31925,'enUS','Even I continue to learn from each passing day.',0),
(31926,'enUS','You are a fool for thinking yourself better than me. I will crush you, I swear it!',0),
(31928,'enUS','I was wrong about you, $n. You\'ve earned my respect as one of the finest adversaries I\'ve ever faced. Don\'t go and think that I\'ll let you defeat me again next time, though!',0),
(31931,'enUS','One day, when we\'re flying high above you, you\'ll be the loser!',0),
(31932,'enUS','Your risk has paid its due reward. Now begone!',0),
(31933,'enUS','I dare you to continue to fight the inevitable. Dragons will once again serve our purposes, and you will fall to my hand in a pet battle. I swear on the Warchief\'s mantle that it will be so!',0),
(31934,'enUS','Me like fighting you, even if me lose.',0),
(31935,'enUS','I applaud your tactics, but despise your victory. Well done, $n.',0),
(31936,'enUS','A sprinkler system? For the farm? Thank you, $n! We can use this instead of that old watering can.$B$BThe \"Jinyu Princess\" eh? What\'s up with that?$B$B$B$BAlright, I don\'t even want to know. I\'ll get this installed right away!',0),
(31937,'enUS','Pest repellers! You\'re a genius, $n! We can finally stop using that ancient bug sprayer.$B$B$B$BAw yeah, Thunder King! That\'s what I\'m talking about!$B$BI\'ll get this installed right away - those bugs won\'t know what hit \'em!',0),
(31938,'enUS','An Earth-Slasher master plow! I... I never thought I\'d get to use one of these. Do you have any idea how much time this will save us?!$B$BI heard if you push the Earth-Slasher through twenty yards of solid rock, you end up with a sandbox and a citation from the Shado-Pan for causing an earthquake scare!$B$BThis is going to be AWESOME.',0),
(31941,'enUS','Well planted, $n.$B$BNow we play the waiting game...',0),
(31942,'enUS','That was close. We almost missed melon time.',0),
(31943,'enUS','Alright, witchberries! I can\'t wait!$B$BBut I\'m gonna have to.',0),
(31944,'enUS','Well done, $n. Your training is now complete. Feel free to return in the future to spar with the masters here to practice what you have learned.',0),
(31945,'enUS','Well, I\'ll be! I\'ve certainly seen larger scallions, but this will do quite nicely. You\'ve just saved our hides, $n!',0),
(31946,'enUS','Whoa, these carrots look crunchy and juicy, $n! Mung-Mung did not know you had such a green thumb.',0),
(31947,'enUS','I was expecting cabbages, but not cabbages of this quality! Oh my!$B$BA perfectly round head, large waxy leaves, a perfect gradient of emerald color...$B$B<Farmer Fung takes a bite out of the cabbage.>$B$BMmm, and sweet, crisp flavor! These is a beautiful cabbage, $n. My yaks will certainly be spoiled by this tasty treat.',0),
(31948,'enUS','Found the falls, did you? Oh yes, I see you found the water. Wonderful!',0),
(31949,'enUS','<Nana Mudclaw scrutinizes a dark witchberry, then pops it into her mouth. Her face lights up.>$B$BLands alive! I haven\'t tasted such a sweet, juicy witchberry in years! Why, the only person who could grow berries like these was... Old Yoon, yer friend\'s grandpa.$B$B<Nana Mudclaw blushes.>$B$BOh that man was such a scamp! I still remember the summer days when we were young, eating these berries by the bushel without a care in the world.$B$BThank you for reminding me of an old friend, $n.',0),
(31951,'enUS','You have emerged victorious. Continue your training and find challenges in other trainers like yourself. The journey is never truly complete.',0),
(31953,'enUS','You are very strong. Will you lend your skills to my efforts?',0),
(31954,'enUS','Next time you lose. I\'m gonna beatcha!',0),
(31955,'enUS','Wow! I\'m not the only one that\'s been training!',0),
(31956,'enUS','Fine. Victory is yours once more. Begone, I have much preparation to do before we meet again.',0),
(31957,'enUS','In all my time as a grand master I\'ve never faced one as determined as you. The others were right about you. You are a force to be reckoned with.',0),
(31958,'enUS','You are stronger and your skills more refined. Your journey continues.',0),
(31970,'enUS','I have been proven wrong. You are prepared to face my greaters.',0),
(31971,'enUS','By defeating me, I grow stronger. I urge you to be wary during our next encounter.',0),
(31972,'enUS','Even in defeat I feel closer to my pets. Thank you for a worthy skirmish.',0),
(31973,'enUS','No, no, I just messed up. How about another go?',0),
(31974,'enUS','You fight with the wrath of my masters. Perhaps you and I aren\'t so different.',0),
(31975,'enUS','Let\'s see...where to send you next...',0),
(31976,'enUS','Let\'s see...where to send you next...',0),
(31977,'enUS','I\'ve been at work preparing your next set of challenges, $n. Let us see if you are prepared...',0),
(31978,'enUS','Well, it\'s not as much as I would have hoped, but it will have to do. I guess there is no sense in cryin\' over spilled brew.',0),
(31980,'enUS','I think I know just the right place to test you next.',0),
(31981,'enUS','You really beat Grand Master Antari? Wow! I\'m going to have to find you some really tough tamers to fight!',0),
(31982,'enUS','There is only one place to test you next.',0),
(31983,'enUS','I think I know the next step you ought to take.',0),
(31984,'enUS','Payne asked you to court me for him, didn\'t he? When is he ever going to learn?',0),
(31985,'enUS','I take it you met Obalis? He\'s a wonderful fellow, once you get past his rough exterior.',0),
(31986,'enUS','You are now prepared for a true test of your skill in battle. Are you up to it?',0),
(31989,'enUS','Welcome back, $n. It is time for the final step of your training.',0),
(31991,'enUS','You are indeed superior. If you would pardon me, I must consult the lake for guidance in my defeat.',0),
(31998,'enUS','You have my gratitude, $n. You\'ve displayed great valor today, and the speed at which you completed the challenge surely will impress your friends and intimidate your foes.',0),
(31999,'enUS','We may have won the battle against the Alliance, but we won\'t get any further with this many jabbering monkeys on our perimeter.$B$BThe hozen are our next target.',0),
(32000,'enUS','You have my sincerest thanks, $n. Without fine Stormstout brews to lighten the drudgery of the day, the world would be a dull place indeed.',0),
(32001,'enUS','Many blessings upon you, $n. Driving hatred from this world so quickly deserves rich reward.',0),
(32002,'enUS','Many thanks, $n. Your martial prowess is second to none, and your alacrity is sure to strike fear in the hearts of your enemies.',0),
(32003,'enUS','That was a blow well struck, $n. I\'ve never seen a $C fell a giant with such speed.',0),
(32004,'enUS','$n, that was amazing. Ner\'onok is a master tactician, and you schooled him handily.',0),
(32005,'enUS','$n, you\'re a stalwart $C. Your friends and guild mates will surely notice the speed and ferocity with which you conquered the Scarlet Monastery.',0),
(32006,'enUS','Excellent work, $n. Just the thought of him burning up that beautiful library makes me shudder. Your friends will appreciate the speed with which you dispatched him.',0),
(32007,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. May the skeletons of the dead remain peaceful now that Gandling no longer seeks to disturb their slumber.',0),
(32008,'enUS','Ah, you\'re $n. Splendid! Let\'s get to work then, shall we?',0),
(32009,'enUS','You must be $n. Well met. I am Varzok.$B$BI will serve as your contact from here on out.',0),
(32010,'enUS','The Vale is safer now, thanks to you. Now, you must help the Celestials.',0),
(32011,'enUS','The Vale is safer now, thanks to you. Now, you must help the Celestials.',0),
(32016,'enUS','May the stars smile upon you, $n.',0),
(32017,'enUS','May the stars smile upon you, $n.',0),
(32018,'enUS','Ha ha! You were sent by Bolo? The \"Keg Mender,\" right? From the Drunken Hozen?$B$BHow is his eye healing? Is his friend still hung over?$B$BAhh... that was an enjoyable evening.',0),
(32019,'enUS','You come from the Temple of the Jade Serpent? Rain-Zhu sends his thanks?$B$BAi yah... really, that was nothing. I could have defeated that saurok without spilling my beer.$B$BIn fact, I believe I did.',0),
(32020,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32021,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32022,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32023,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32024,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32026,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32027,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32028,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32029,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32030,'enUS','Your arrival is timely, wakener.$B$BOur ritual is underway.',0),
(32031,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32032,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32033,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32034,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32035,'enUS','Greetings, $C. Welcome to the Silken Fields.',0),
(32036,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32037,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32038,'enUS','I haven\'t seen stag hunting this good since Ashenvale.',0),
(32039,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32040,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32041,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32042,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32043,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32044,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32045,'enUS','Let this be a lesson to you: don\'t drink too much of the water.$B$BWhy do you think we have such a big brewery?',0),
(32046,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32047,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32048,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32049,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32050,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32051,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32052,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(32106,'enUS','A small tag on this present reads:$B$BHappy holidays, $n!',0),
(32108,'enUS','<This fire will signal the full might of the Horde invasion fleet to land on this beach, beginning Garrosh\'s campaign in Pandaria.>',0),
(32109,'enUS','<Blue sails are barely visible on the horizon - the full might of the Alliance fleet, awaiting one final signal.>',0),
(32115,'enUS','Ye\' did good work out there. It\'s not right seein\' the dead unable to rest like that.',0),
(32116,'enUS','Oi! We got a right nasty problem here. Kicked the hornet\'s nest. Except these are mogu ghost hornets with a mean streak a bloody mile wide!',0),
(32118,'enUS','Ah, yes. Good. Help from Belloc. He never does like to get his hands dirty.',0),
(32119,'enUS','Good work! Now maybe the workers can get through a day without fillin\' their britches!',0),
(32120,'enUS','Good, good. We\'ll begin our research post-haste.',0),
(32121,'enUS','Those things are nasty! Thanks for takin\' care of \'em for us.',0),
(32122,'enUS','You did it! Good work! Really saved our bacon!$B$BHere\'s to hoping those things don\'t come back...',0),
(32123,'enUS','Well done, $n. I see your time in this land has hardened your resolve and sharpened your skills.',0),
(32126,'enUS','Just remember, the weapon of choice is not always the weapon with the longest range or heaviest amount of damage. In the end, the best weapon is the weapon that works every time.',0),
(32127,'enUS','It is not enough to rob the Alliance of their leaders. We must warn those who would aspire to leadership the cost of such ambition.',0),
(32128,'enUS','Ah! Look at them burn. These new Alliance craft require more to destroy them permanently however. I am sure they will have those fires out in a day or two.',0),
(32130,'enUS','Good and waxy, just like they asked for. Here\'s your share.',0),
(32131,'enUS','Ha! YES! You got me some! I\'m gonna make the best bomb EVER!$B$BMan I love bombs! Love making them, love blowin\' em up...$B$B... and yeah, that IS how I got this eyepatch. What\'s it to ya?',0),
(32132,'enUS','Good work. That should slow them down by a few days, at least.$B$BYou don\'t win the war by playing the short game, friend. Trust me, this is the right strategy.',0),
(32133,'enUS','Good work, $n. I\'ve already been getting some useful information that should help make our next offensive even more devastating.',0),
(32134,'enUS','Oh heck yeah! That\'ll show \'em that NOBODY blows stuff up like goblins blow stuff up!$B$BOh, and you did good work too.',0),
(32135,'enUS','Cut off the head, and the body will fall.$B$B... Unless you\'re forsaken, I guess. I realize I should probably stop using that saying now that I am.',0),
(32136,'enUS','More fuel huh? Is her \"loveliness\" afraid she might have to do a little more than sit around lookin\' pretty?',0),
(32137,'enUS','Oh, yuck! Why are these barrels wet?! Oh nevermind! At least you got here before they made me work. I can\'t think of anything more horrible!',0),
(32138,'enUS','Good for nothin\' huh?! I\'m busting my rump down here!$B$BMaybe her \"uselessness\" would like to come down here and haul this lumber herself!',0),
(32139,'enUS','It\'s about time you showed up with this lumber order! I was just about to come down there and get it myself.',0),
(32140,'enUS','Is she still complaining about diamonds and rubies? We found something better than diamonds down here!$B$BThis ore is special. It has power!',0),
(32141,'enUS','Did they manage to find anything useful down there? Maybe an emerald or an opal? Is it too much to ask for a little bit of effort?!$B$BNevermind! I\'ll make sure this shipment gets where it\'s goin\'.',0),
(32142,'enUS','Well done, soldier. That should help keep the horde in check.',0),
(32144,'enUS','Thanks to your actions, the Horde knows it cannot feed its troops.$B$BThe timeframe they can withstand a siege is greatly reduced and their morale is going to start suffering soon.$B$BWe just need to keep applying pressure.',0),
(32145,'enUS','Great work! Sorry to put good soldiers in harms way but my Auto-Demolish-o-Tronic Mk 2 isn\'t functional yet.',0),
(32146,'enUS','Thank you soldier. That should teach the Horde that it will take more than a couple of mooks to scare us away.',0),
(32148,'enUS','Good work, soldier. Without those shamans, I don\'t think they\'ll have much luck breaking down our defenses.',0),
(32149,'enUS','Good work! With this, we\'ll be able to finish reinforcing the structure of the keep, which will help keep people safe. You\'ve saved lives today!',0),
(32150,'enUS','Without those supplies, they won\'t be able to support bringing more warriors in the fight. If they can\'t bring in more warriors, we have a great shot at holding out.$B$BFor today, at least.',0),
(32151,'enUS','Alright! We\'ll get that stone mortared into the cracks in our walls faster than a Dwarf downs a pint.',0),
(32152,'enUS','You really showed them who owns this beach, $n. Good work!',0),
(32153,'enUS','I know it wasn\'t easy, but you did it. Good work. You\'ve got my respect, soldier.',0),
(32154,'enUS','Wish I could\'ve been there to watch their fuel burn! Probably put on quite the show.$B$BYou\'ve done well, $n!',0),
(32156,'enUS','You have done these soldiers a great service, $n. The only thing left to do is make sure they did not die in vain.',0),
(32157,'enUS','Excellent work, $C! Eventually we will wipe the Horde from this continent.',0),
(32158,'enUS','Excellent work, $n! Now the forest can begin its regrowth process. From all death comes new life, and a new opportunity to protect it.',0),
(32161,'enUS','You place the feathers in the dirt, then look off in the direction of the temple...',0),
(32162,'enUS','You lay the meat out atop the trap, then turn your eyes toward the jungle...',0),
(32163,'enUS','You spread out the decaying fish, prepare the crate, then turn your eyes toward the beach...',0),
(32164,'enUS','You place the feathers in the dirt, then look off in the direction of the temple...',0),
(32165,'enUS','You lay the meat out atop the trap, then turn your eyes toward the jungle...',0),
(32166,'enUS','You spread out the decaying fish, prepare the crate, then turn your eyes toward the beach...',0),
(32169,'enUS','Well fought, $n.',0),
(32172,'enUS','Well fought, $n.',0),
(32175,'enUS','I must say, good show!',0),
(32181,'enUS','It only took one to capture the beast, but it will take many more to truly defeat it.$B$BSpeak to me again when you have gathered enough allies. We shall test the grace of the crane against the might of the Horde.',0),
(32182,'enUS','It only took one to capture the beast, but it will take many more to truly defeat it.$B$BSpeak to me again when you have gathered enough allies. We shall test the ferocity of the tiger against the might of the Horde.',0),
(32183,'enUS','It only took one to capture the beast, but it will take many more to truly defeat it.$B$BSpeak to me again when you have gathered enough allies. We shall test the resilience of the crab against the might of the Horde.',0),
(32184,'enUS','It might have taken just one $R to capture this beast, but it will take many more to put it down.$B$BGather up some friends, then come and speak with me again. We\'ll pit the grace of the crane against the glory of the Alliance!',0),
(32185,'enUS','It might have taken just one $R to capture this beast, but it will take many more to put it down.$B$BGather up some friends, then come and speak with me again. We\'ll pit the power of the tiger against the glory of the Alliance!',0),
(32186,'enUS','It might have taken just one $R to capture this beast, but it will take many more to put it down.$B$BGather up some friends, then come and speak with me again. We\'ll pit the stamina of the crab against the glory of the Alliance!',0),
(32189,'enUS','AUGHM... nomf... -slurp- mmmf...$B$B<Barnaby looks up from the table, revealing a tangled beard dotted with melon seeds. Juices rush down his chin as he greets you.>$B$BMmf... -cough- A customer! Hello! Name\'s Fletcher. Barnaby Fletcher - nice to meet you!$B$B<He wipes a hand on his robe before extending it, still visibly sticky and flecked with pulp.>',0),
(32190,'enUS','Well met, $C. We are an archaeological expedition, sent to excavate these ruins. We had no idea that this area was crawling with dangerous mogu.',0),
(32191,'enUS','Ah! Well done! With the guardians gone, we should be able to excavate these ruins safely.',0),
(32192,'enUS','We blood elves have served the Horde faithfully. Lately, I wonder what we have to gain from Garrosh\'s leadership.',0),
(32193,'enUS','These artifacts must be several thousand years old. Have ye ever seen the like?',0),
(32194,'enUS','Well done, $C. I knew that you could get the job done.',0),
(32197,'enUS','I have standards ya know! I\'m a chef, not a magician!$B$BThe only mystery here is how Duke thinks he\'ll pull this over on everyone else!',0),
(32198,'enUS','I knew you would be!$B$BHere\'s the catch - the shards, in their current state, are unstable. But the soil in this valley is renowned for its magical properties! I am sure if you were to \"plant\" the shard, a very interesting reaction would take place.$B$BIt could stabilize, leaving you with a functioning portal! Or... it might tear open a magical rift that spits out transdimensional horrors!$B$BMy gut tells me it will be a little of both, but there\'s only one way to know for sure.$B$BHere, take a sample!',0),
(32199,'enUS','This meat is disgusting! It\'s going to take every spice I have to cover that smell up.$B$BOnly the best for the Boss-Lady!$B$B<Sezik grins and winks at you.>',0),
(32200,'enUS','Much blood was spilled this day. It is on my hands, $n, not yours.',0),
(32201,'enUS','Excellent. You have dealt the mogu a blow that they shall not easily forget.',0),
(32204,'enUS','One day, this island will belong to the Horde. I can only hope that it will be free of saurok before then.$B$B<Aethas sneers.>$B$BAt least they attack the Alliance, too.',0),
(32206,'enUS','It\'s impressive how easily you were able to cut them down.$B$BPerhaps, it\'s you they should not underestimate. Thank you for your assistance, $C.',0),
(32207,'enUS','A trained Zandalari beastcaller with a mount unleashed on the battlefield can kill twenty times their number. Your preemptive attack has saved many lives. Thank you!',0),
(32212,'enUS','Yes! You have done it, champion!$B$BWe will be as a tide that sweeps over this island, bringing with it a new destiny for our people. And you, hero, are at its forefront.',0),
(32213,'enUS','So, Violet Rise runs red with the blood of our enemies? Well done, $n.$B$BThis will be an ongoing battle I fear. We must continue to show our strength here.',0),
(32214,'enUS','Very nice, $n! I knew it! I knew there were Alliance sneaking around down there!$B$BNo one messes with a Bilgewater rig and gets away with it!',0),
(32215,'enUS','I could feel the magic of their altars dissipating even here, $C.',0),
(32216,'enUS','It what?! It killed its master? Wonderful. These skyscreamers have more fight in them than I realized. Thank you for helping free the beast, $R - it is one less threat to the Horde, and one more for the Zandalari.',0),
(32217,'enUS','The tide of blood is slowed, at least for a time. Thank you for your efforts in stalling the sacrifices, $C.',0),
(32218,'enUS','Their dead shall rise no more, thanks to you, $n. Excellent work.',0),
(32219,'enUS','I am glad to hear that you left the quilen in a thousand tiny pieces. You have contributed much to our war effort.',0),
(32220,'enUS','Thank you, $n. You have lightened my heart of a heavy burden through your heroic actions.$B$BI will remember your efforts on this day.',0),
(32221,'enUS','Excellent work down there, $n! That should keep \'em outta our hair for awhile!',0),
(32222,'enUS','Excellent work, $C! This brings us one step closer to pushing them out of Pandaria!',0),
(32223,'enUS','It\'s a good day when another Lion\'s Landing leader falls, $C! Good work!',0),
(32224,'enUS','Wonderful work, $C. This will help our offensive a great deal.',0),
(32225,'enUS','You continue to exceed my expectations, $C. Well done.',0),
(32226,'enUS','Ah yes, you\'ve just confirmed my theory! Thank you, $C.',0),
(32227,'enUS','You have returned, $R. It is my hope that these young skyscreamers have the lives they deserve without dealing with the harsh treatment of the trolls.',0),
(32228,'enUS','You are not one to be trifled with. I am sure to have further use of your services.$B$BCome back to me in a day\'s time, $C.',0),
(32230,'enUS','When I give you a task, it gets handled.$B$BWell done, $C.',0),
(32232,'enUS','So I was correct to be concerned. It\'s a good thing you were there to stop them before that guardian was fully infused.$B$BGood work, $C.',0),
(32233,'enUS','Excellent work, $C!$B$BThese weapons are terrifying on their own, nevermind the magic they are infused with.',0),
(32234,'enUS','These will do nicely, $C. Excellent work.',0),
(32235,'enUS','Ha! Simple mechanical toys are no match for a well aimed bottle of grog.',0),
(32236,'enUS','Now that\'s what I like to hear! I bet those spiders will think twice before messing with a Bilgewater operation again!',0),
(32237,'enUS','So I was being followed! Those dirty rotten sneaks!$B$BI\'m going to have to start planting some real nice surprises for those cowards. Surprises that will really knock \'em out!',0),
(32238,'enUS','Good work, $n! I saw the fireworks from here!$B$BWho knew being a genius was this easy? I don\'t even have to try anymore.',0),
(32242,'enUS','The Warchief sent you? What does he say?',0),
(32243,'enUS','Oh my, look at this thing!',0),
(32244,'enUS','Yes, this is remarkable! This is just the kind of artifact that we came here to find!',0),
(32246,'enUS','You have impeccable timing, $C. King Wrynn is just about to land, and the full might of our fleet will follow soon after.',0),
(32247,'enUS','I\'m satisfied with this site, it\'s time to bring in our fleet.',0),
(32248,'enUS','Good to see you again, $n.$B$BWe have a delicate situation on our hands here. We need to plan our next moves carefully.',0),
(32249,'enUS','You are just in time. The Warchief is about to land. Once this site passes his inspection, the fleet will follow.',0),
(32250,'enUS','Well done. Our presence here will not be denied!',0),
(32251,'enUS','Good ta see ya, mon. I be needin\' true allies at my side for dis mission.',0),
(32252,'enUS','I can only imagine what horrors you witnessed, $n. Your bravery was put to the test this day, and you did not fail the Horde in your task.',0),
(32254,'enUS','<The archmage listens carefully to your report.>$B$BI understand. Thank you for your aid, $C.',0),
(32255,'enUS','That\'s more like it.$B$BThank you, $C.',0),
(32256,'enUS','What do you have to report?',0),
(32257,'enUS','Hmm... very interesting. This tablet will yield many secrets, indeed.',0),
(32262,'enUS','Those you have rescued today would no doubt thank you, if they had the strength.$B$BOur task here will be ongoing. I refuse to leave anyone behind!',0),
(32264,'enUS','I have desired this book for many years, $R. It\'s power is too immense to describe. You have done me a great service.',0),
(32265,'enUS','Well done, champion. This artifact will be put to better use in our hands than in the hands of the Kirin Tor.',0),
(32266,'enUS','This task will be ongoing, but you have done as a great service, $R.',0),
(32268,'enUS','I am sure the use of even these smaller mana bombs has Jaina squirming with rage. Serves her right.$B$BDalaran was my home before her grandparents were born. What right did she have to expel me from my home?',0),
(32269,'enUS','Good work, $C. With your help we were able to successfully sneak several spies behind enemy lines.',0),
(32274,'enUS','I know the true price of bloodshed. I know the cost of war.$B$BIt would be simpler to blindly massacre our attackers until they yield. But is it right?',0),
(32275,'enUS','I shall continue my unrest until the threat is subdued, but your aid brings us closer to that goal. I thank you, $n.',0),
(32276,'enUS','With your help, we\'re one giant step closer to our goal.',0),
(32277,'enUS','Incredible work. This presents us with a monumental opportunity.',0),
(32278,'enUS','Excellent work! With that blasted warship out of commission, the bombardments on our forces along the coast will cease.$B$BTaran Zhu has informed me that the Shado-Pan will keep vigil over Stormsea Landing, freeing up Sunreaver resources to press the siege elsewhere. Taoshi will be there. I am sure she will be glad to work with you again.$B$BWe are all grateful for your contributions, $n. Thank you.',0),
(32279,'enUS','Well done, $n. Shan Bu\'s fall will weaken the Mogu and your heroism will surely be remembered.',0),
(32282,'enUS','We lost three good soldiers when we first arrived on this island. Killed in their sleep by compies that had snuck into their tent. Some nights I still hear the screams.',0),
(32283,'enUS','Well done, champion. These beasts are strong enough. We don\'t need them infused with an angry spirit now do we?',0),
(32284,'enUS','Ah! You received my note. Very good. Vol\'jin is near death, and I will need your help healing his wounds.',0),
(32285,'enUS','Your efforts are appreciated.',0),
(32287,'enUS','Well done, $C. Thank you for the help.',0),
(32288,'enUS','Now that the wards have been fully armed, we can focus our attention elsewhere. Nothing will be slipping past us now!',0),
(32292,'enUS','Good work. What you did today brings us one step closer to our ultimate goal.',0),
(32293,'enUS','It\'s good to have a man I can trust close at hand.',0),
(32294,'enUS','You\'re a good $C to have around, that\'s for certain. Thank you.',0),
(32296,'enUS','Not entirely unsuccessful. Still, we\'ll do better next time.$B$BThanks for providing us with that key. The raid would not have gone off without you.',0),
(32297,'enUS','Few things in this world and beyond are more entertaining than watching a rampaging ancient beast tearing through an enemy\'s settlement.$B$BIf times were not so dire I would consider selling tickets to such an event.',0),
(32298,'enUS','Very interesting results. I am sure there is a mage somewhere that cares about the specifics. I, on the other hand, am just glad to hear the sound of trolls being assaulted by their own beasts.',0),
(32299,'enUS','Jobs like this make me glad that I left most of my nose in the tomb.',0),
(32300,'enUS','Good work. The real irony is had these been normal bombs we would have had a much harder time detecting them. Some gnomish devilry could have spelled the end of our operation here.',0),
(32301,'enUS','You have put a good dent in the Sunreaver forces here. Like vermin, there will always be more. We must be at the ready at all times.',0),
(32302,'enUS','So the constructs have fallen? Good!$B$BWe will remind Jaina and the Kirin Tor at every turn that the Sunreavers are not to be taken lightly.',0),
(32303,'enUS','I wish I could be there to see the look on Proudmoore\'s face as she mourns the loss of her death machine!$B$BWe can be certain she will build another, but we have at least set her back.',0),
(32304,'enUS','Your presence on the battlefield cannot be ignored. I would like to give you something extra for your efforts, $C.',0),
(32305,'enUS','Excellent work, $C! It will take them days to rebuild those foci.',0),
(32307,'enUS','What... where in the great dark did you find this?',0),
(32309,'enUS','You are ready to learn more...',0),
(32310,'enUS','You are now ready to learn more...',0),
(32315,'enUS','Well met, $C. We have much work to do here.',0),
(32316,'enUS','I see that you and my son have been hard at work. Thank you for taking the initiative to aid our cause here in the Vale.',0),
(32318,'enUS','Very good. These should work nicely.',0),
(32319,'enUS','<Thrall stares at the stone you have handed him.>$B$BVol\'jin\'s hearthstone? My friend, has it come to this?',0),
(32320,'enUS','Vol\'jin has saved my life many times in the past. To see my own Kor\'kron used against his people cuts deeper than I can put into words.',0),
(32321,'enUS','You come asking for the Monkey King?$B$BLet us see how well you ookin\' sing.$B$BWho are you, so tiny and boring?$B$BYour cause is silly! You leave me snoring.$B$BThree riddles I will ask,$B$BThese riddles are a task,$B$BFinish each without pause,$B$BAnd we shall see if I help your cause.',0),
(32325,'enUS','You have done more for this world than you can know, $C. It is... something of a shame Kanrethad met this end. A shame, but inevitable.',0),
(32326,'enUS','$n! So glad Nazgrim selected you.$B$BIt\'s taken a great deal of the Horde\'s effort to get you here through Jaina\'s traps. Maintaining our illusion this close to Darnassus is considerably expensive.$B$BFurthermore, the Sunreavers of Dalaran are risking their neutrality by assisting the Horde with this operation.$B$BIn other words, we expect only the best from you.',0),
(32327,'enUS','Well executed, $R! I knew we could count on you.$B$BNow to get off this wretched tree.',0),
(32328,'enUS','You found the bell! And Fanlyr teleported it to Silvermoon for study, as instructed? The Horde will put this to good use.$B$BYou have done the Horde a great service today. Lok\'tar, friend!',0),
(32329,'enUS','The Warchief \"demands\" progress? His impatience is growing more destructive with each command.$B$BAs it stands, we could use your expertise.',0),
(32330,'enUS','This reckless use of my people by Garrosh is becoming intolerable. If you had not been here to assist I dread to think what might have happened.',0),
(32331,'enUS','I am glad to see you friend. While I have learned much about diplomacy I think Jaina is too familiar with my tactics.$B$BI could use a friendly hand in resolving this conflict.',0),
(32332,'enUS','Ah! Amber! Fresh and untamed. Did you kill to get it? But of course.$B$BThough free, the untamed amber is a dangerous thing, and many might die because of it.$B$BMercy comes in many forms, like spikes and mantid and really ookin\' spooky storms.',0),
(32333,'enUS','The Metal Brew is strong and lasting, a brew to be shared with friends after a battle.$B$BEmperor Shaohao and his Monkey King had many a round in our day. Many battles, and many good friends.',0),
(32334,'enUS','Why engage in duelery? Why engage in foolery?$B$BYou ask the Monkey King for an artifact of power, I have to make sure when the time comes you will not cower. One tough dooker you think you might ookin be, but against mogu, many will turn and flee.',0),
(32335,'enUS','It looks like it is going to take us a few days to track all of these \"minions\" down.$B$BThank you for your help, $n. Meet me in Lion\'s Landing in a few days and we will embark to track down these objects.',0),
(32336,'enUS','Artifacts not make people great. Artifacts allow people to be more of themselves. Good becomes gooder. Bad becomes badder. And Chief Ingoo Ingoo became worser.',0),
(32337,'enUS','What virmen do not understand, they worship, fight or flee.$B$BI should send them a few statues of me.',0),
(32338,'enUS','Woot woot!',0),
(32340,'enUS','You\'ve looted everything you could grab on your way up. Time to tally up your plunder and hide it before Akama catches up...',0),
(32342,'enUS','Ahh, yes. Hmm. Hand that over. Carefully.',0),
(32343,'enUS','What treasures! With any luck, the spirits will return and we will be able to sample their essence further.',0),
(32344,'enUS','Ahh, yes. I received word from one of our researchers that they are no longer troubled by that anomaly. Well done.',0),
(32345,'enUS','Ah, good work. As much as it may seem trivial in comparison to our larger research goals, it is important that we maintain appearances, $n.',0),
(32346,'enUS','Alright! We\'ll be back up and runnin\' in no time!',0),
(32347,'enUS','Ha! That should send \'em runnin\' back to Silvermoon with their tail \'tween their legs!',0),
(32348,'enUS','Oh, what a fine day. Alliance fools defeated, and our research is moving ahead quite nicely.',0),
(32351,'enUS','Well met, $C. You were sent from Domination Point? Very well. We have much to discuss.',0),
(32352,'enUS','You bested my defenders? Finally, one who can control his hatred and violence!$B$BI need more men like you.',0),
(32355,'enUS','I am glad you made it, my friend. I could really use your help with what is to come. My father would prefer I remain in the safe custody of his legion.$B$BBut if there is one thing Pandaria has taught me, it is a few people in the right place at the right time can make a bigger difference than the greatest of armies.',0),
(32362,'enUS','Thank you for your help, hero. I hear the wisdom in Jaina\'s words.$B$BLet\'s hope her faith in the Sunreavers is justified.',0),
(32363,'enUS','Thank you for coming, $n.',0),
(32368,'enUS','What did you see, $C?',0),
(32370,'enUS','<You do a doubletake when the Pandaren suddenly speaks with Connelly\'s voice.>$B$B\'Bout time, laddie! I\'ve been waitin\' fer ya to show up.$B$BThese Pandaren are good people but can\'t mix a martini fer nothin\'.',0),
(32371,'enUS','Back so fast, rookie? So what did ye learn?',0),
(32372,'enUS','The orcs have changed. My Horde has changed. Do I kill my fellow orcs until it is once again \"my\" Horde? Do I have any right to try force the Horde to be what it once was?$B$BThese are troubling times. But for now, I must see to Vol\'jin\'s people.',0),
(32373,'enUS','I am curious to see how King Wrynn rises to the occasion.$B$BI am even more curious to see what YOU are capable of. Let\'s find out...',0),
(32374,'enUS','Marvelous! Even in the midst of the chaos of battle you\'ve proven that an individual can have an impact. The Horde has learned that their actions in Pandaria will not be unopposed.$B$BI believe it is time for a more substantial challenge...',0),
(32376,'enUS','Ah, good. You have come. $B$BAgain, I apologize for the cryptic note - but Garrosh is increasingly distrustful of us. I do not want this operation disturbed by hasty action on his part.',0),
(32377,'enUS','<Agent Connelly\'s voice comes over the radio.>$B$BEy, you\'re good! I knew those Kor\'kron wouldn\'t be a problem fer ya. Couldn\'t\'ve done much better meself.',0),
(32378,'enUS','Good. We should be ready to make our move.',0),
(32379,'enUS','Good. There\'s quite a bit to pore through here... $B$BI will have the Reliquary investigate these. Surely we can use them to discern more of the secrets of these Korune mogu.',0),
(32380,'enUS','Following Connelly has been interesting to say the least. The man is a master of disguise!$B$BTalking him into joining you won\'t be the hard part, $C. Figuring out which of these lively individuals is him will be next to impossble.',0),
(32381,'enUS','You have a keen eye, $C! I think you are ready to meet Connelly.',0),
(32382,'enUS','You\'ve arrived just in time. From the intel I\'ve gathered, Garrosh is hot on the trail of some sort of ancient mogu artifact of power.$B$BIf we can figure out what he\'s after, we can stop him from getting it!$B$BWe have to act fast to gather as much information as possible.',0),
(32383,'enUS','Well done! Everyone always underestimates the little guys and it is always a grave mistake!',0),
(32384,'enUS','We managed to capture our quarry. $B$BIn truth, though, I am not sure what our next move should be. I will contact the leaders of our allies and see if they have ideas - I don\'t know that our arcane talents are going to pry the secrets of our mogu captive.',0),
(32388,'enUS','<Wrathion grins.>$B$BYou were being tested, $C. I knew you were capable of great things by yourself.$B$BBut you have proven to me that you have the makings of a leader, cobbling together support among a group of strangers in the midst of a battlefield.$B$BThe Alliance is fortunate to have you.',0),
(32389,'enUS','<Wrathion hungrily listens to tales of your exploits on the battlefield, his eyes gleaming bright red.>$B$BOhh... oh! Incredible! In the very eye of battle, one\'s true heart is revealed.$B$BYou do not disappoint, $n.$B$BNeither does your Alliance.',0),
(32390,'enUS','<A strange device sits within an ornate silk-lined chest. It appears as though it can be fastened to your sha-touched weapon as an additional upgrade. The empty socket is disconcerting; you feel as though it is staring back at you. A single, hollow, judgmental eye...>',0),
(32391,'enUS','The Alliance beat us here. How could this happen?',0),
(32392,'enUS','Darnassus, is it?$B$BThe Alliance believes they have won the day. Now, when their arrogance is at its greatest, is our opportunity to pluck the prize from their fingers.',0),
(32393,'enUS','We blasted the doors open moments ago, $C. You arrived just in time to join us for the excavation.',0),
(32394,'enUS','Fantastic work, $n. I could not even imagine the atrocity that Garrosh would commit if this bell were to fall into his hands.$B$BToday, we have secured a safe future for the Alliance. I will see to it that the bell makes it safely to Darnassus.$B$BI will extoll your deeds to the King.',0),
(32397,'enUS','Phew! That was a close one! I never doubted you for a minute though.$B$BNow let me take a look at that journal...',0),
(32398,'enUS','I was wondering when you would arrive, $n.',0),
(32399,'enUS','They may have destroyed the Divine Bell, but I have taken the life of the Alliance\'s prodigal son!$B$BIt is nothing less than my own father would have expected of me.$B$BThis victory may have come at a high cost, but it is of little consequence.$B$BI will find other ways to destroy my enemies, and bring glory to the Horde!',0),
(32400,'enUS','$n! Just the $C I was hoping to see. You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time.',0),
(32401,'enUS','<Anduin looks like a crumpled doll. He lays as still as a stone, and the only movement comes from the frigid air ruffling his fair, golden hair.>$B$B<You sit quietly for a while, until the cold settles into your bones. The bell is destroyed, but the silence is deafening.>$B$B<Out of the corner of your eye, you see the slightest flicker from the boy\'s hand. You lean in close. He breathes - but just barely! Anduin is alive!>',0),
(32402,'enUS','Good... you\'ve arrived. It\'s not a good day to be Horde in Dalaran.$B$BJaina\'s called for the exile of all the Sunreavers. You and I are going to save as many as we can - including Archmage Aethas Sunreaver himself - and then get out of here as fast as possible.',0),
(32403,'enUS','Let\'s press on.',0),
(32404,'enUS','So much bloodshed! In a place of peace!$B$BJaina has gone too far this time.',0),
(32405,'enUS','The first stage of our mission is complete. That was the easy part.$B$B<Rommath takes a deep, measured breath, then continues...>',0),
(32406,'enUS','Now, let\'s move quickly.',0),
(32408,'enUS','We will continue saving Sunreavers for a while longer. Aethas\' location may become clearer as we press on.',0),
(32409,'enUS','Thank you for that, $n.$B$BIt unsettles me to have to fight directly with the high elves of the Silver Covenant... but I never tire of slaying Alliance.',0),
(32410,'enUS','Well done, $n. Well done.',0),
(32411,'enUS','Excellent. They should be waiting for us in Silvermoon when we return.',0),
(32412,'enUS','Is this... $n? What\'s going on here?',0),
(32413,'enUS','<Nazgrim listens as you recount the day\'s events.>$B$BWe take the bell... and the Alliance takes Dalaran. That escalated quickly.$B$BWar is coming, $n. Be on your toes.',0),
(32414,'enUS','The Bell is gone...$B$BAt the scene of the crime, we found traces of arcane magic... I may be able to use my skills to track the thieves.',0),
(32416,'enUS','I will instruct you from here on out.$B$BJaina will be going down into the city to enforce our new rules.',0),
(32417,'enUS','It\'s nice to have those rats out of here for good. Well done, hero.',0),
(32418,'enUS','While I can\'t say I agree completely with Jaina\'s methods, I do understand her motives.$B$BSometimes, you have to fight back.',0),
(32419,'enUS','This is a bloody day, $n, and this is bloody work.$B$BBut do not forget what the Sunreavers did to bring this on: They used neutral Kirin Tor resources to aid the Horde in their fight against the Alliance.$B$BDo not hesitate to believe that they would do the same to us, given the chance.',0),
(32420,'enUS','I suppose it wasn\'t enough for him to be a coward and a backstabber... he had to be a greedy thief as well.$B$BHmph. The Horde and the Sunreavers aren\'t all that different. They deserve one another.',0),
(32421,'enUS','Now, the Sunreavers have to answer to us. Jail or death - their fate is in their own hands.',0),
(32423,'enUS','I can\'t fault you for following orders. In fact, I can\'t really fault Jaina for acting on her own behalf, for once.$B$BBut still... we aren\'t playing a game here. We are dealing with war, with people\'s lives, with the future of the Alliance itself.$B$BAt the very least, we now have the Kirin Tor on our side. Today will be remembered by all as a victory for the Alliance.',0),
(32426,'enUS','So the SI: 7 needs a reminder in what the word retirement means?$B$BI suppose they wouldn\'t be comin\' to me if the situation weren\'t dire.$B$BI\'ll help, but I\'ll need a few days to gather some intel.',0),
(32427,'enUS','Like all great leaders, Garrosh has greatly extended himself. Just what is he ultimately capable of?$B$BMore importantly, what YOU are capable of? Fresh bloodshed along the coast gives us an opportunity to find out...',0),
(32428,'enUS','I can\'t belive you took out those spirits!',0),
(32429,'enUS','Marvelous! Even in the midst of the chaos of battle you\'ve proven that an individual can have an impact. The Alliance buckles under Horde might, although their King refuses to break.$B$BI believe it is time for a more substantial challenge...',0),
(32430,'enUS','<Wrathion grins.>$B$BYou were being tested, $C. I knew you were capable of great things by yourself.$B$BBut you have proven to me that you have the makings of a leader, cobbling together support among a group of strangers in the midst of a battlefield.$B$BThe Horde is fortunate to have you.',0),
(32431,'enUS','<Wrathion hungrily listens to tales of your exploits on the battlefield, his eyes gleaming bright red.>$B$BOhh... oh! Incredible! In the very eye of battle, one\'s true heart is revealed.$B$BYou do not disappoint, $n.$B$BNeither does this Horde of yours.',0),
(32432,'enUS','<A strange device sits within an ornate silk-lined chest. It appears as though it can be fastened to your sha-touched weapon as an additional upgrade. The empty socket is disconcerting; you feel as though it is staring back at you. A single, hollow, judgmental eye...>',0),
(32434,'enUS','I will get you next time!',0),
(32435,'enUS','Hurry up and turn those in if you want to get second place! I have been standing around here for HOURS with nothing to eat!  Hand those suckers over!',0),
(32436,'enUS','Hurry up and turn those in if you want to be awarded the third and final prize! I have been standing around here for HOURS with nothing to eat!  Hand those suckers over!',0),
(32439,'enUS','I will get you next time!',0),
(32440,'enUS','I will get you next time!',0),
(32441,'enUS','I will get you next time!',0),
(32442,'enUS','Our champions defeated the first wave of attackers, but the command ship is nearly upon us!',0),
(32446,'enUS','Goblin construction leaves somethin\' to be desired, but it\'ll have to do. Good work, $n!',0),
(32448,'enUS','Ah, very good. This is the last thing we needed.',0),
(32449,'enUS','We have a lot of work to do, $C. Who knows what has already been uncovered in Ogudei!',0),
(32450,'enUS','Now things can get interesting! I have a few plans for Lion\'s Landing...',0),
(32451,'enUS','The battle is already underway, $C. Let\'s get you out there!',0),
(32452,'enUS','It\'s about time we dealt with this nuisance. Those Bilgewater runts need to be taught a lesson!',0),
(32455,'enUS','I hesitate to guess what would have happened if you had not been there with the young Prince, $n.$B$BToday, you put an end to Garrosh\'s plans.$B$BYou have undoubtedly saved thousands of lives, and most importantly, you brought Anduin back to us.$B$BWe are doing everything we can for the boy, but we can only wait and see.$B$BI believe he has the fight in him. I must believe it...',0),
(32457,'enUS','The Sunreavers and the Kirin-Tor are mounting an assault on the Thunder King\'s base of operations! My new friend here and I were just discussing the ramifications of their attack.$B$BYou and I can stand to benefit from the situation, $n. I have a few ideas...',0),
(32460,'enUS','I\'ve decided.$B$BCertain members of the Kirin-Tor have put their allegiance to the Horde above the order, and I will NOT tolerate it. This is nothing short of a betrayal.$B$B<Jaina\'s eyes flare with rage.>$B$BCome with me, $n. We\'re going to clean up Dalaran.',0),
(32461,'enUS','Ah, have you come to join the Order?',0),
(32468,'enUS','Count me surprised to hear from you again, you must be tougher than I thought. You\'ve earned my respect, kid, here\'s your lens upgrade kit. Now get out there and take some S.E.L.F.I.E.S!',0),
(32469,'enUS','I knew from the moment we met that you were an adventurer, just like me! Here\'s your lens upgrade kit, now get out there and take some S.E.L.F.I.E.S!',0),
(32470,'enUS','Great! I\'ve just gotta put this box here, and jam this part in here... and done!$B$BHere\'s your new S.E.L.F.I.E. cam, enjoy!',0),
(32471,'enUS','You\'re all set, kid. You\'ve got a face the camera will love, now get out there and get shooting!',0),
(32474,'enUS','<Wrathion nods slowly.>$B$BYes, $n. I saw your deeds, and I was most impressed.$B$BYou are truly an instrument of change.',0),
(32476,'enUS','<Wrathion nods slowly.>$B$BYes, $n. I saw your deeds, and I was most impressed.$B$BYou are truly an instrument of change.',0),
(32485,'enUS','Excellent work, $n. Those perimeter wards should keep out all manner of filth.$B$BWith Violet Rise protected we can focus on more pressing matters.',0),
(32489,'enUS','Every little bit helps.',0),
(32491,'enUS','Left standing, those piles of discarded food are the perfect breeding ground for disease.$B$BWere I still in the disease-spreading business, I\'d consider using them myself.',0),
(32493,'enUS','Excellent work, $C! This will aid my studies greatly, as well as advance our cause here.',0),
(32494,'enUS','Getting these masks was no easy task, $C. I am grateful for your service.',0),
(32495,'enUS','I am glad to hear that this piece of filth is slain. You have done us all a great favor, $n.',0),
(32496,'enUS','Desecrate the Horde\'s Vale of Eternal Blossoms bonfire!',0),
(32497,'enUS','Honor the Dread Wastes flame.',0),
(32498,'enUS','Honor the Jade Forest flame.',0),
(32499,'enUS','Honor the Krasarang Wilds flame.',0),
(32500,'enUS','Honor the Kun-Lai Summit flame.',0),
(32501,'enUS','Honor the Townlong Steppes flame.',0),
(32502,'enUS','Honor the Valley of the Four Winds flame.',0),
(32503,'enUS','Desecrate the Alliance\'s Vale of Eternal Blossoms bonfire!',0),
(32505,'enUS','Ah! To feel whole again! You have my gratitude, servant. Take this stone and use it wisely. Should you encounter his majesty the Thunder King in your travels, do not tell him where you received it, or you will be standing in a statue next to me for the remainder of eternity.',0),
(32506,'enUS','Wonderful! I\'ll pass him off to our caretaker. Thank you.',0),
(32509,'enUS','Honor the Vale of Eternal Blossoms flame.',0),
(32510,'enUS','Honor the Vale of Eternal Blossoms flame.',0),
(32517,'enUS','A good defense is just as effective as a strong offense. One less enemy to worry about.$B$BWell done.',0),
(32520,'enUS','Your skills are impressive indeed. Thank you for doing this for me, $n.',0),
(32521,'enUS','You have our gratitude, $n.',0),
(32522,'enUS','One less threat at our doorstep. Thank you, $n.',0),
(32523,'enUS','I\'m glad you were the one Lor\'themar sent. These beasts are more than we can handle on our own. Time to spook the livestock.',0),
(32524,'enUS','These Zandalari are even more dangerous than we anticipated.$B$BDo not make the mistake of underestimating them, for that may be the last mistake you make.',0),
(32525,'enUS','Their dead shall rise no more, thanks to you, $n. Excellent work.',0),
(32526,'enUS','Thank you, $n. You have lightened my heart of a heavy burden through your heroic actions.$B$BI will remember your efforts on this day.',0),
(32527,'enUS','Excellent. You have dealt the mogu a blow that they shall not easily forget.',0),
(32528,'enUS','Ah yes, you\'ve just confirmed my theory! Thank you, $C.',0),
(32529,'enUS','You continue to exceed my expectations, $C. Well done.',0),
(32530,'enUS','I am glad to hear that this piece of filth is slain. You have done us all a great favor, $n.',0),
(32531,'enUS','A good defense is just as effective as a strong offense. One less enemy to worry about.$B$BWell done.',0),
(32532,'enUS','Wonderful work, $C. This will help our offensive a great deal.',0),
(32533,'enUS','I am glad to hear that you left the quilen in a thousand tiny pieces. They are little more than a nuisance to my work here on the island.',0),
(32535,'enUS','One day, this island will belong to the Alliance. I can only hope that it will be free of saurok before then.$B$B<Modera sneers.>$B$BAt least they attack the Horde, too.',0),
(32536,'enUS','<The archmage listens carefully to your report.>$B$BI understand. Thank you for your aid, $C.',0),
(32537,'enUS','That\'s more like it.$B$BThank you, $C.',0),
(32538,'enUS','$C, the destruction of those altars will force the trolls to halt their most heinous of sacrifices. You have the thanks of everyone here.',0),
(32539,'enUS','Without the offerings, they will need to collect more before their sacrifices can proceed. Thank you, $C.',0),
(32540,'enUS','Most who witness such rituals never return, and those that do tend to be shaken. You, $n, seem little moved by your incredible deeds. I am impressed.',0),
(32541,'enUS','Welcome back, $R. The hatchlings you frightened will live a better life without their captors.',0),
(32542,'enUS','With a few of their more threatening kin slain, perhaps the Zandalari will show reluctance next time they decide to trifle with us.',0),
(32543,'enUS','$n, your help against the Zandalari is appreciated. I realize it seems we cannot stem the tide, but your efforts make a difference.',0),
(32544,'enUS','I hope that creature has the intelligence necessary to know who saved it. It seems to me that it would be a dangerous foe if provoked.',0),
(32545,'enUS','I know the true price of bloodshed. I know the cost of war.$B$BIt would be simpler to blindly massacre our attackers until they yield. But is it right?',0),
(32546,'enUS','Well done, $n. Looking at you, I\'m suddenly quite proud of Dalaran\'s state-of-the-art plumbing system.',0),
(32547,'enUS','Every little bit helps.',0),
(32548,'enUS','Left standing, those piles of discarded food are the perfect breeding ground for disease.$B$BWere I still in the disease-spreading business, I\'d consider using them myself.',0),
(32550,'enUS','These trolls have been using dark magics to achieve their goals. No patience, no honor. You have done the world a good service in reducing their numbers today.',0),
(32551,'enUS','We lost three good soldiers when we first arrived on this island. Killed in their sleep by compies that had snuck into their tent. Some nights I still hear the screams.',0),
(32552,'enUS','Well done, champion. These beasts are strong enough. We don\'t need them infused with an angry spirit now do we?',0),
(32553,'enUS','Few things in this world and beyond are more entertaining than watching a rampaging ancient beast tearing through an enemy\'s settlement.$B$BIf times were not so dire I would consider selling tickets to such an event.',0),
(32554,'enUS','Very interesting results. I am sure there is a mage somewhere that cares about the specifics. I, on the other hand, am just glad to hear the sound of trolls being assaulted by their own beasts.',0),
(32555,'enUS','This is very interesting, $C. The crystal hums with the rage of its captive inhabitants. Even after the passage of time their devotion has not decreased.$B$BI will need to study this further.',0),
(32556,'enUS','These are excellent finds! Studying them will take time, but there is much to be gained in understanding the Zandalari.',0),
(32557,'enUS','Excellent work, $C! These weapons are impressive. Now we have a few less things to worry about in the field of battle.',0),
(32558,'enUS','It\'s a shame really that these masks must be destroyed. I would have liked to study this ancient magic, but it is better that they be destroyed than become the tools of the Horde.$B$BGood work, $C.',0),
(32559,'enUS','It\'s fortunate that you were able to intervene, $C. Who knows what damage that golem would have caused had he not been stopped.',0),
(32560,'enUS','Well done, $C. The more Zandalari we destroy, the less chance their magic will fall into Horde hands.',0),
(32561,'enUS','You\'re dependable, $n. I like that.',0),
(32562,'enUS','I appreciate what you\'ve done for us this day, $n.',0),
(32563,'enUS','Thank you, $n. That\'s a worry off my mind.',0),
(32564,'enUS','Yet again you prove yourself. We would be fortunate if all amongst us could aspire to your talents.',0),
(32565,'enUS','Your skills are impressive. You have our gratitude.',0),
(32567,'enUS','Today, we hunt the hunters!',0),
(32568,'enUS','The Zandalari here are not to be under-estimated, $C. Powerful magic overwhelms this space.$B$BWe must be diligent in our efforts.',0),
(32571,'enUS','Wonderful! I\'ll pass him off to our caretaker. Thank you.',0),
(32572,'enUS','Your efforts are appreciated, $C.',0),
(32573,'enUS','Well done, $C. Thank you for the help.',0),
(32574,'enUS','You are not one to be trifled with. I am sure to have further use of your services.$B$BCome back to me in a day\'s time, $C.',0),
(32575,'enUS','When I give you a task, it gets handled.$B$BWell done, $C.',0),
(32576,'enUS','You\'re dependable, $n. I like that.',0),
(32577,'enUS','I appreciate what you\'ve done for us this day, $n.',0),
(32578,'enUS','It\'s good to have a man I can trust close at hand.',0),
(32579,'enUS','Your skills are impressive indeed. Thank you for doing this for me, $n.',0),
(32580,'enUS','You have our gratitude, $n.',0),
(32581,'enUS','One less threat at our doorstep. Thank you, $n.',0),
(32582,'enUS','You\'re a good $C to have around, that\'s for certain. Thank you.',0),
(32583,'enUS','Yet again you prove yourself. We would be fortunate if all amongst us could aspire to your talents.',0),
(32584,'enUS','Thank you, $n. That\'s a worry off my mind.',0),
(32585,'enUS','Your skills are impressive. You have our gratitude.',0),
(32587,'enUS','Good work. What you did today brings us one step closer to our ultimate goal.',0),
(32589,'enUS','Excellent work, $C. This is a dark magic indeed. We have much to learn here if we are to succeed.$B$BNow, we have only to hope that we can reanimate this creature.',0),
(32590,'enUS','<Wrathion introduces you both.>$B$BPrince Anduin, this is $n, possibly the most powerful $C in Pandaria.$B$BOh - do you already know of each other? Interesting.',0),
(32591,'enUS','<Wrathion inspects the treasures you brought him.>$B$BWell done. The trillium will need additional refinement, of course, but these samples are pure.$B$BI will need to study these artifacts for a time but I believe I can use the knowledge contained here to craft something of great value to us both.',0),
(32592,'enUS','My Shado-Pan associates have spoken highly of your deeds. You have earned quite the name for yourself here in Pandaria!$B$BIt is settled. When the materials are ready, you will be my champion. You will be my instrument, my standard-bearer, my voice of change across this world.$B$BWe will do marvelous things together.',0),
(32593,'enUS','Behold! The Lightning Lance! A conduit that can channel and control the very same power that the Thunder King used to found an empire.$B$BIt is dormant... but you\'re about to change that. If you\'re worthy.',0),
(32594,'enUS','You\'ve done it! The lance seethes with power and potential!$B$BOh my friend, you have earned a great reward...',0),
(32595,'enUS','The Crown of Heaven! Use this to augment any piece of headgear.$B$BIt will also act as a third eye - I will be able to follow your progress as we embark on the next stage of our journey.',0),
(32596,'enUS','Thanks to your work, $n, we\'ve reconstructed an ancient narrative. The mogu were once creatures of stone, enacting the will of the Titans. But then their master fell silent, and they succumbed to the curse of the flesh. Eventually Lei Shen came along, imprisoned the keeper Ra, and took his power. Ah, what an empire he built!$B$BArmed with this knowledge, it\'s time to act...',0),
(32597,'enUS','<Wrathion squeezes the black heart in his hand, his eyes burning brightly.>$B$BYou did it... you did it! The black heart of the Thunder King!',0),
(32599,'enUS','You have just secured our advantage, $n. Your work here will be remembered.$B$BGarrosh will be made to pay for his actions!',0),
(32600,'enUS','No wonder the Zandalari have come. They are in need of a new home, and I am sure their mogu allies have promised them much.$B$BWe will add this knowledge to your collection. If you wish me to narrate this for you, simply point at the correct volume in your Private Collection.',0),
(32601,'enUS','What we know of Lei Shen are dark legends that have been remembered over the vast span of time. I often wondered if these legends had exaggerated the power of Lei Shen. But your research would suggest they may have greatly underestimated the Thunder King. These are dark days indeed.$B$BWe will add this knowledge to your collection. If you wish me to narrate this for you, simply point at the correct volume in your Private Collection.',0),
(32602,'enUS','Your research is most distressing. But it sheds light on a truth we have long sought: \"Where did the mogu come from? And why were they such tyrants?\"$B$BWe will add this knowledge to your collection. If you wish me to narrate this for you, simply point at the correct volume in your Private Collection.',0),
(32603,'enUS','You found them all? Amazing! So the stories ARE true! Perhaps you will write the next great Pandaren fable based on your own incredible journey!',0),
(32604,'enUS','I bow to you who continues to walk in the footfalls of the great Pandaren fables.',0),
(32605,'enUS','Masterfully done, $C.',0),
(32606,'enUS','Masterfully done, $C.',0),
(32607,'enUS','Casualties are down significantly with that warship out of commission, and we continue to press the siege on Lei Shen.$B$BFantastic work out there today, hero.$B$BPlease, take this - you have earned it.',0),
(32608,'enUS','What\'s this? A necklace? What are you trying to- ahh, I see... A relic from the Thunder King\'s vault! Fascinating... Powerful, too.$B$BThe Kirin Tor will keep it safe. In return, please accept this.',0),
(32613,'enUS','<Ku\'ma shrugs.>',0),
(32614,'enUS','Bones bones bones bones bones...',0),
(32615,'enUS','Too many, not enough, no no...give them to Ku\'ma...',0),
(32616,'enUS','Do you fear death? Hehe...',0),
(32617,'enUS','<Ku\'ma\'s jaw falls off at the sight of so many bones.>',0),
(32618,'enUS','Don\'t forget to buy your mount while you are here! Katie Hunter can be found here in camp.',0),
(32621,'enUS','While the language is incomprehensible, the diagrams in this book yield their knowledge to your skilled blacksmith\'s eye. It is clear that, by manipulating the properties of ghost iron, you can create a material of great power, perhaps powerful enough to recreate and increase the power of weapons long lost to the mists of time.',0),
(32627,'enUS','Well done, champion. This artifact will be put to better use in our hands than in the hands of the Sunreavers.',0),
(32628,'enUS','It pains me to resort to such weaponry, but the Sunreavers must be taught the price of their actions.',0),
(32631,'enUS','Your presence on the battlefield cannot be ignored. I would like to give you something extra for your efforts, $C.',0),
(32632,'enUS','Excellent work, $R. The problem with constructs is they can always be rebuilt.$B$BI imagine it will not take the Sunreavers long to build a new death machine.',0),
(32633,'enUS','Ah yes! This is it. You\'ve done well, $R.',0),
(32634,'enUS','Excellent work, $R! I was able to get a few of my scouts behind their lines before the perimeter wards were repaired.',0),
(32635,'enUS','I\'m grateful for your efforts here, $n. We would have lost so much had you not disarmed those bombs in time.',0),
(32636,'enUS','You have saved many today, $n. I cannot imagine the horror of being frozen and helpless among so many enemies.',0),
(32637,'enUS','So they\'ve constructed objects that infuse their forces with additional power? This will have to be watched closely.$B$BThank you for your efforts today.',0),
(32638,'enUS','You\'ve made excellent progress today, $C. Rest assured however, our work here is nowhere close to done.',0),
(32639,'enUS','Good work, $C. As long as we keep the construct numbers in check, we will ensure our success here.',0),
(32640,'enUS','Yours skills as a $C are unquestionable. You\'ve aided the cause greatly this day. You have my thanks.$B$BAnd now for that reward I promised you...',0),
(32641,'enUS','Yours skills as a $C are unquestionable. You\'ve aided the cause greatly this day. You have my thanks.$B$BAnd now for that reward I promised you...',0),
(32643,'enUS','Throw the Red Blossom Leeks into the crate! A Dominance Offensive representative will be along shortly for pick-up.',0),
(32644,'enUS','Yes! You have done it, champion!$B$BNow, the Thunder King will taste the full force of the Kirin Tor!',0),
(32646,'enUS','Throw the Witchberries into the crate! An Operation: Shieldwall representative will be along shortly for pick-up.',0),
(32648,'enUS','Throw the White Turnips into the crate! A Golden Lotus representative will be along shortly for pick-up.',0),
(32650,'enUS','Gently place the Green Cabbages into the crate! A Shado-Pan representative will be along shortly for pick-up.',0),
(32652,'enUS','Incredible work. This presents us with a monumental opportunity.',0),
(32654,'enUS','With your help, we\'re one giant step closer to our goal.',0),
(32655,'enUS','Well done. That warship won\'t be raining fire on us again any time soon.$B$BTaran Zhu has informed me that the Shado-Pan will keep vigil over Stormsea Landing, freeing up Kirin Tor resources to press the siege elsewhere. Taoshi will be there. I am sure she will be glad to work with you again.$B$BWe are all grateful for your contributions, $n. Thank you.',0),
(32656,'enUS','You\'ve done it, $C! Shan Bu is dead once and for all, and we\'ve learned that Lor\'themar may not be all that he seems.',0),
(32657,'enUS','Throw the Striped Melons into the crate! Now the August Celestials\' order is ready to go!',0),
(32659,'enUS','Throw the Mogu Pumpkins into the crate! A Klaxxi representative will be along shortly for pick-up.',0),
(32661,'enUS','Don\'t forget to buy your mount while you are here! Torallius is right over there.',0),
(32662,'enUS','Don\'t forget to buy your mount while you are here! Veron Amberstill is standing just outside the gates to the Ranch.',0),
(32663,'enUS','Don\'t forget to buy your mount while you are here! Milli\'s right over there!',0),
(32664,'enUS','Don\'t forget to buy your mount while you are here! You can buy one from Lelanai right here.',0),
(32665,'enUS','Don\'t forget to buy your mount while you are here! You can buy one from Old Whitenose here.',0),
(32667,'enUS','Don\'t forget to buy your mount while you are here! You can buy one from Turtlemaster Odai here.',0),
(32668,'enUS','Don\'t forget to buy your mount while you are here! You can buy one from Winaestra just outside.',0),
(32668,'ruRU','Не забудь купить скакуна, пока ты здесь. С этим тебе поможет Винестра, ее можно найти сразу за городскими воротами.',25549),
(32669,'enUS','Don\'t forget to buy your mount while you are here! You can buy one from Ogunaro over there.',0),
(32670,'enUS','Don\'t forget to buy your mount while you are here! You can buy one from Harb Clawhoof over there.',0),
(32671,'enUS','Don\'t forget to buy your mount while you are here! You can buy one from Zjolnir over there.',0),
(32672,'enUS','Don\'t forget to buy your mount while you are here! You can buy one from Zachariah Post here.',0),
(32673,'enUS','Don\'t forget to buy your mount while you are here! You can buy one from Kall Worthaton over there.',0),
(32674,'enUS','Ah, good to see you. You look like you are ready to take to the skies!$B$BRemember, you can buy a flying mount from Drakma, just behind me.',0),
(32675,'enUS','Ah, good to see you. You look like you are ready to take to the skies!$B$BRemember, you can buy a flying mount from Tannec Stonebeak over there.',0),
(32676,'enUS','This so-called \"Thunder King\" is surrounded and cut off from his allies. No tyrant is strong enough to stand alone.$B$BYour efforts have not gone unnoticed. Take this, with my thanks.',0),
(32677,'enUS','Ah, I know a powerful artifact when I see one. You were wise to bring this here. I will see that Aethas examines it right away - perhaps we can put it to work in our favor.$B$BIn the meantime, take this in trade.',0),
(32678,'enUS','We must move quickly, $n! The others have gone ahead of us, but I will brief you in the flight over.',0),
(32679,'enUS','We must move quickly, $n! The others have gone ahead of us, but I will brief you in the flight over.',0),
(32680,'enUS','You have arrived just in time, $R. It is crucial we gain control of these shores before the Kirin Tor.$B$BThere is much to explain.',0),
(32681,'enUS','You have arrived just in time, $n. This land needs to be controlled by the Kirin Tor for everyone\'s safety. This will not be an easy task.',0),
(32682,'enUS','Why I just knew you could convince him, $n. You\'ve set my heart at ease, knowing the Tillers will be in good hands.',0),
(32683,'enUS','Well done. You are ready to become a zen master blacksmith.',0),
(32684,'enUS','Ah! Have you come to learn how to fish? You\'re talking to the right person. First, here - have some fish!',0),
(32685,'enUS','Let me see... Yes, these are nice. Good job! Here, have some more.',0),
(32686,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(32687,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(32688,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(32689,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(32690,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(32691,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(32692,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(32693,'enUS','This will aid lorewalkers and archaeologists in understanding the history of Pandaria.',0),
(32706,'enUS','Welcome, $n.',0),
(32707,'enUS','Perfect. I will show you how to use these stones, and then you can spring the ambush.',0),
(32708,'enUS','Very impressive.$B$BShould you find more stones, you should continue this ruse. It is sure to be quite some time before they catch on to our ploy.',0),
(32709,'enUS','Welcome, $n.',0),
(32718,'enUS','May the stars smile upon you, $n.',0),
(32719,'enUS','May the stars smile upon you, $n.',0),
(32722,'enUS','Good work. What you did today brings us one step closer to our ultimate goal.',0),
(32724,'enUS','Good work. What you did today brings us one step closer to our ultimate goal.',0),
(32726,'enUS','Well done. You are ready to become a zen master blacksmith.',0),
(32728,'enUS','Yes, good, come... there is work to be done.',0),
(32729,'enUS','One more to join the Zandalari hunt? Good. Very good.',0),
(32730,'enUS','You have good timing. I am quite in need of your assistance.',0),
(32731,'enUS','Yes, good, come... there is work to be done.',0),
(32732,'enUS','You have good timing. I am quite in need of your assistance.',0),
(32733,'enUS','One more to join the Zandalari hunt? Good. Very good.',0),
(32783,'enUS','So my brother would not dare come himself?',0),
(32791,'enUS','The Thunderlord think their numbers will save them.$B$BWe will show them that their numbers count for nothing when hunted by a pack of Frostwolves.',0),
(32792,'enUS','Hrmph. The burning smell of Thunderlord. This pleases me, $C.',0),
(32794,'enUS','For many years I hunted all sorts of prey alongside my father. This hunt shall honor his memory as well as avenge his death at the hands of these traitorous, honorless Thunderlords.',0),
(32795,'enUS','Today is a good day.',0),
(32796,'enUS','Ga\'nar is coming. Good. We need his forces if we are to press the advantage.$B$BI can only hope his bloodlust has quelled enough for him to listen to reason.',0),
(32804,'enUS','You have shown honor to our clan. This act shall be remembered.',0),
(32805,'enUS','We have the four blessings of the celestials, and you have proven yourself by completing one of their challenges! I knew I saw great potential in you.',0),
(32806,'enUS','So, King Wrynn and the Dark Iron dwarves saved the city, and the bitterly divided Council of Three Hammers gained a new unity under the Alliance banner. How interesting!$B$BBut what is happening within the Horde?',0),
(32807,'enUS','Whaaaat? The remains of an Old God are buried beneath Pandaria? No wonder the land is so haunted!$B$BThe warchief\'s pursuit of those dormant powers are fraying apart the very Horde he leads. His vision is narrow, but very, very dangerous. I must inform the Shado-Pan immediately.',0),
(32808,'enUS','$n! I cannot tell you how relieved I am to have some backup!$B$BKing Wrynn himself sent us to gather intel on Garrosh\'s activities and Orgrimmar\'s defenses, but... things are looking grim.$B$BWe need your help.',0),
(32809,'enUS','Let\'s see... the warchief is moving tons of supplies through the Barrens... And what\'s this about the Darkspear? The trolls are in open rebellion?! Garrosh certainly has his hands full.$B$BI think I know how we can use this intel. It\'s a crazy idea, but it just might work...',0),
(32810,'enUS','<Zen\'tabra narrows her eyes at you.>$B$BWhy de Alliance seek de Darkspear? We fightin\' de \"Warchief,\" sure, but dat don\'t mean we friends. I never trust de Alliance, an\' I ain\'t \'bout ta start now.$B$BStill, dat funny mechanical cat ya have saved me life... so I give you dis. I let ya speak wit\' Vol\'jin.$B$BLet him decide if ya words be venom or honey.$B$BDon\'t be tryin\' nothin\', $C. Ya lift a finger against Vol\'jin, ya life be forfeit.',0),
(32811,'enUS','<Vol\'jin motions to his guards to allow you to come forward and speak.>$B$BDe Barrens be splattered wit\' blood, $R. Ya done right by me.$B$BTell de Alliance ta rally its fleet. When de time comes, de Darkspear an\' de other rebels will try ta hold de harbor for ya. Hellscream made too many enemies ta fight \'em all off at once, hah!$B$B$B$BYa have me thanks, $R. Dis rebellion only gonna get so far wit\'out ya.',0),
(32812,'enUS','<Ki\'ta Arrowtusk beckons you over.>$B$BI been waiting for ya, hero. Dis be a time of reckoning.',0),
(32813,'enUS','De \"Warchief\" thought we\'d scatter once he sent in de Kor\'kron. Hah. He shoulda sent ev\'ryting he got.$B$BTime ta make \'im pay!',0),
(32814,'enUS','Razor Hill. We did it, $n! Look to de north - you can almost see Orgrimmar from here.$B$BHellscream gonna figure out who did dis. Hah hah. He gonna be one angry orc.$B$BNext stop is de capital. We gonna need a lot more help. An\' more supplies...',0),
(32815,'enUS','<Huff> Oh, hello- <puff> hello there, young man.$B$BQuite the squall we\'re having up here today, isn\'t it?',0),
(32816,'enUS','We made it, $C! Thank you so much. Please, help yourself to some of my old knick-knacks.$B$BBut... I am afraid I have not been completely honest with you...',0),
(32819,'enUS','<Sen\'jin is buzzing with activity. Vol\'jin motions for you to approach, a dark sadistic grin spreading across his tired face.>$B$BYa done good, $n. Blood in de Barrens. Hellscream got to be feelin\' that.$B$BNo doubt he gonna come for us, but we gonna be ready...',0),
(32836,'enUS','Ah, you\'ve found one of my treasures. Well done, adventurer.$B$BIn return, I will allow you to purchase one of my rare challenge cards.',0),
(32837,'enUS','Great fighting out there! Even if he was just a little guy.$B$BYou\'ve earned every bit of this.',0),
(32838,'enUS','Ah, you\'ve found one of my treasures. Well done, adventurer.$B$BIn return, I will allow you to purchase one of my rare challenge cards.',0),
(32839,'enUS','You sailed through the air so... so... majestically! Well done!',0),
(32840,'enUS','Ah, you\'ve found one of my treasures. Well done, adventurer.$B$BIn return, I will allow you to purchase one of my rare challenge cards.',0),
(32841,'enUS','I\'m not sure how to feel. I wanted you to win, but then again... I also kinda wanted to see you explode.$B$BNo hard feelings! I just like seeing explosions.',0),
(32842,'enUS','Ah, you\'ve found one of my treasures. Well done, adventurer.$B$BIn return, I will allow you to purchase one of my rare challenge cards.',0),
(32843,'enUS','Congratulations!$B$BAlso, how embarrassing would it have been if you got eaten by a beached shark?',0),
(32844,'enUS','Ah, you\'ve found one of my treasures. Well done, adventurer.$B$BIn return, I will allow you to purchase one of my rare challenge cards.',0),
(32845,'enUS','You left quite a mess behind you, but you did it. Well done, $R!',0),
(32846,'enUS','Ah, you\'ve found one of my treasures. Well done, adventurer.$B$BIn return, I will allow you to purchase one of my rare challenge cards.',0),
(32847,'enUS','Aww... poor Mecha-Bruce.$B$BI\'ll give you your reward. But I don\'t have to be happy about it.',0),
(32848,'enUS','Ah, you\'ve found one of my treasures. Well done, adventurer.$B$BIn return, I will allow you to purchase one of my rare challenge cards.',0),
(32849,'enUS','I never thought I\'d say this, but successfully beating up a couple penguins is the sign of a true, tried-and-tested brawler. You\'ve earned your reward.',0),
(32850,'enUS','Ah, you\'ve found one of my treasures. Well done, adventurer.$B$BIn return, I will allow you to purchase one of my rare challenge cards.',0),
(32851,'enUS','You\'ve got a real knack for beating up robots, $n.',0),
(32852,'enUS','Ah, you\'ve found one of my treasures. Well done, adventurer.$B$BIn return, I will allow you to purchase one of my rare challenge cards.',0),
(32853,'enUS','You ran around that arena so quickly, I got dizzy for a moment.$B$BWell done!',0),
(32854,'enUS','Ah, you\'ve found one of my treasures. Well done, adventurer.$B$BIn return, I will allow you to purchase one of my rare challenge cards.',0),
(32855,'enUS','I would normally shame someone for fighting a blind person, but in this case, I have to commend you.$B$BBrilliant brawling, $n!',0),
(32856,'enUS','Ah, you\'ve found one of my treasures. Well done, adventurer.$B$BIn return, I will allow you to purchase one of my rare challenge cards.',0),
(32857,'enUS','You did well! Even if you did get a little lucky...',0),
(32858,'enUS','Ah, you\'ve found one of my treasures. Well done, adventurer.$B$BIn return, I will allow you to purchase one of my rare challenge cards.',0),
(32859,'enUS','Look at you! You went into that arena and beat Ty\'thar at his own game.$B$BHere. You deserve this.',0),
(32861,'enUS','I can custom-tailor the cloak to your preferred abilities. Choose wisely!$B$BThe cloak contains only a fraction of its potential power. I\'m already hatching a plan to augment it...',0),
(32862,'enUS','<Ki\'ta Arrowtusk chuckles to himself.> I see you made a whole lotta Kor\'kron heads roll for dese supplies.$B$BWell mon, Vol\'jin was right to commend you. Dese supplies will be lastin\' us an entire week.',0),
(32863,'enUS','I\'ve heard stories about some of your matches circulating around, apparently they were quite a sight to behold! I think you\'ve earned this reward. Congratulations, trainer, and keep up the good work.',0),
(32867,'enUS','<Vol\'jin nods at you.>$B$B$C. Looks like ya just chose a side.$B$BI hope ya ready ta fight.',0),
(32868,'enUS','I bow to you who continues to walk in the footfalls of the great Pandaren fables.',0),
(32869,'enUS','I bow to you who continues to walk in the footfalls of the great Pandaren fables.',0),
(32870,'enUS','Are you ready for your next adventure, $C?$B$BOur campaign is nearing its conclusion...',0),
(32871,'enUS','<The troll does not have a strong grasp of the common tongue, and his throat is still bandaged from a knife wound. But the meaning of his words is clear.>$B$BWhat de Alliance want wit\' ol\' Vol\'jin, hmm? Zen\'tabra says we got a common enemy. That don\'t make us friends.$B$BBut... Maybe we can work together dis once. You want to strangle de Warchief, hm? Shut \'im out?$B$B<Vol\'jin smiles disarmingly, his grin slow and savage.>',0),
(32872,'enUS','<Ki\'ta Arrowtusk chuckles to himself.> I see you made a whole lotta Kor\'kron heads roll for dese supplies.$B$BWell mon, Vol\'jin was right to commend you. Dese supplies will be lastin\' us an entire week.',0),
(32892,'enUS','Ah! Welcome my friend. I am very glad that I was able to get your attention. Great deeds are at work that require a hero such as yourself.',0),
(32895,'enUS','It be good to see dat some Alliance have a sense of loyalty.',0),
(32896,'enUS','Ah, it be good to see your face again, $n.',0),
(32900,'enUS','Congratulations, $n, you did it! Before I forget, here\'s the special surprise I promised -- I hope you like it.$B$BNow tell me all about the adventure. Did you face certain death? Meet any friends? I wish I had more friends like you.',0),
(32901,'enUS','Congratulations, $n, you did it! Before I forget, here\'s the special surprise I promised -- I hope you like it.$B$BNow tell me all about the adventure. Did you face certain death? Meet any friends? I wish I had more friends like you.',0),
(32929,'enUS','A fine headcount, commander.',0),
(32943,'enUS','Throw the scallions into the crate! A Sunreaver Onslaught representative will be along shortly for pick-up.',0),
(32945,'enUS','Throw the juicycrunch carrots into the crate! A Kirin Tor Offensive representative will be along shortly for pick-up.',0),
(32974,'enUS','<The dirt here looks overturned. Perhaps something is buried beneath.>',0),
(32975,'enUS','<Another pile of dirt! Could there be something buried here?>',0),
(32976,'enUS','<The ancient chest has not been disturbed for a long time.>',0),
(32979,'enUS','You again? Not eaten by ogres or killed by Thunderlords yet? Ha!',0),
(32980,'enUS','I came seeking aid from the elements. I see now that we are the ones who must aid them.$B$BCome, $n, witness what I have witnessed.',0),
(32981,'enUS','Strag was the puppet of the Iron Wolf. She would do nothing unless ordered to by him.$B$BThis made us weak, changing us from a force to be feared to a target.$B$BIf this is what the Thunderlord have become then I will have no part of them.',0),
(32983,'enUS','You have done well, $C.$B$BWe will need the aid of these children when the time comes to rescue Exurotus.',0),
(32984,'enUS','This is ancient magic, from a time before the orcs. It will not be easy to undo.',0),
(32985,'enUS','With Kron defeated I can finish breaching the magic that holds Exurotus, but I may be too late. So much of the fury has already been expended and drained by the magnaron and goren.$B$BI fear we may have only bought this spirit a peaceful death.',0),
(32989,'enUS','$n! They told me you\'d be heading this way. You are late to the party! We are just cleaning up now.',0),
(32990,'enUS','You\'re back! But where is Karg?',0),
(32991,'enUS','Thank you for finding the others. Karg and his captor are one step ahead of us, but they\'re limping.',0),
(32992,'enUS','<Lokra\'s gaze remains fixed on her dying frost wolf.>$B$BWe had them... We had them, Asha. You were so fast. So beautiful.$B$BI failed you, Asha. I am sorry.',0),
(32993,'enUS','Help me out of these chains. We have work to do.',0),
(32994,'enUS','See how their machines fail them! There is no better weapon than pure orc muscle!',0),
(33010,'enUS','Thank you for protecting my family, $n.',0),
(33018,'enUS','Well, hello there. I am Lin Chao-Wei.$B$BHave you come here to try my family\'s famous noodle soup?',0),
(33020,'enUS','You recognize the name, Lin, on the scroll. A few characters down you see the character for \"Recipe.\"$B$BThis must be it!$B$BYour only worry is that the sha energies that manifested themselves in the tales of the pandaren may have corrupted the scroll as well.$B$BThere is only one way to find out....',0),
(33021,'enUS','Hello, $n. What is it you have there?',0),
(33022,'enUS','Excellent work, $n! With all this grain I think we\'re ready to start.$B$BFor now I think you should try making noodle soup. Try using this recipe I\'ve written down for you. It\'ll make for excellent practice.',0),
(33024,'enUS','Well done, $n. With this we can make a truly unique soup broth.$B$BI\'ve managed to get some updated schematics for your noodle cart. With this broth, you\'re definitely going to want to upgrade your operation.$B$BNext up: finding the secret ingredient of the Lin secret ingredient noodle soup!',0),
(33026,'enUS','Ooh, these will do nicely, $n.$B$BNow for the final step: the Lin secret ingredient soup\'s secret ingredient.$B$BThat\'s a mouthful!',0),
(33027,'enUS','Well done, $n. All those people came by to taste your noodle soup and YOU made them so happy!$B$BDon\'t you see? The secret ingredient is in you!$B$BNow go out there and make the world happy with this latest noodle cart!',0),
(33059,'enUS','I have seen enough. Ner\'zhul must be stopped.',0),
(33062,'enUS','As soon as we have enough blessed water from the priestess\'s moonwell, we\'ll break the demon\'s will and use it as a proxy to see into Gul\'var.$B$BThat way, they won\'t know it\'s us scrying upon them.$B$BBut first, we need to weaken their shrouding magic.',0),
(33066,'enUS','Now all that\'s left to do is to fashion them together into something strong enough to ensnare Gul\'dan.$B$BLuckily, we can do that right here.',0),
(33070,'enUS','I am glad to hear that the children are safe. They will remember your heroic deeds for their entire lives.',0),
(33072,'enUS','Thank you for coming, $n. There is much to be done.',0),
(33075,'enUS','Thank you, stranger! The Prophet spoke of new allies arriving on our shores.$B$BI hear it is thanks to you that my sister is safe.$B$BI owe you a great debt, friend.',0),
(33076,'enUS','My trust in you is well placed, young $C.$B$BThis task would have been troublesome for many of my students, and yet you finished it with ease.',0),
(33077,'enUS','Oh thank you child, thank you, thank you.$B$BThe nights in the swamp are cold. It means a lot to this old woman to have some comfort from her aching bones.',0),
(33078,'enUS','Oh my, I see, I see! These writings will give me much insight into the Shadowmoon clan\'s culture.$B$BThank you, $n.',0),
(33080,'enUS','You made it, $n! Boy, am I glad to see you.',0),
(33081,'enUS','I could never have done it without you, $n. Your words unlocked something within me which I have not felt before.$B$BCall it what you wish - resolve, conviction, faith. I will not soon forget this, $C.',0),
(33082,'enUS','We will find new traditions. My people will become something... new.',0),
(33083,'enUS','The Shadowmoon are not simple opponents. Your fighting skill is truly comparable to none.',0),
(33084,'enUS','Brilliant, just brilliant! Ay\'ve never seen such a haul in my entire life!$B$BGet tha wagons ready. We\'re eatin\' well tonight!',0),
(33087,'enUS','Are you ready for your next adventure?',0),
(33088,'enUS','You\'re here! How long have I been waiting for you?$B$B<Wrathion appears momentarily confused.>$B$BI feel like I just arrived... but maybe I\'ve been here for weeks... This island plays with one\'s head.$B$BKairoz has been trying to explain it to me, but sometimes I think bronze dragons speak in riddles.',0),
(33098,'enUS','Wonderful, these are exactly what I need.$B$B<Wrathion holds one of the coins up, admiring it in the glow of the unmoving sun.>$B$BI will deconstruct their mysterious power, and use their timelessness to enhance your cloak. You will be most pleased with the result.',0),
(33100,'enUS','An impressive display of martial skill, $C! You have truly walked the path of the emperor, and demonstrated the very traits pandaren value most.',0),
(33104,'enUS','Step forward, my champion.$B$BThis is your hour.',0),
(33105,'enUS','<Wrathion is FURIOUS. News of Hellscream\'s defeat and King Wrynn\'s gesture of peace must\'ve already reached the black dragon\'s ears.>',0),
(33111,'enUS','Unfortunate that the ancient guardians of the woods fell to such corruption.$B$BAt least now, its long nightmare has ended. Not to mention its sacrifice is our gain.',0),
(33112,'enUS','Gul\'dan is there! We must move quickly to capture him.',0),
(33113,'enUS','Thank you, $n. The White Lady will be pleased.$B$BNow, I shall go about the business of preparing the moonwell water for use in the archmage\'s plan.$B$BBut first, I wonder if you\'d be willing to help me again. The warden brought back very disturbing stories about the creatures in the woods.',0),
(33114,'enUS','You\'ve forged the soul trap. There\'s no time to waste, $n.$B$BWe must capture Gul\'dan.',0),
(33115,'enUS','Now that the veil has been lifted from the woods, we can make use of the demon.$B$BWe will convince it to turn its eye upon Gul\'var and show us what the Shadow Council is planning.',0),
(33116,'enUS','Unfortunate, but not surprising. At least we were able to defeat one of the inner council members.$B$BAll is not lost, $n. We know what the Shadow Council is up to and where they\'re heading.$B$BWe\'ll regroup in Talador. Together, we\'ll put an end to Teron\'gor and his plans for Auchindoun.$B$BDid you hear that?',0),
(33119,'enUS','Who are you, outsider? I saw you freeing some of my kin...',0),
(33120,'enUS','Grim business. I wish that it could have gone differently.$B$BThank you for your dedication, $n. Be comforted in the fact that Elune understands.',0),
(33125,'enUS','You bring honor to the clan by giving my family a proper burial, $n.',0),
(33132,'enUS','Wolfchew is defeated? *cough* Glorious.',0),
(33133,'enUS','May the stars smile upon you, $n.',0),
(33134,'enUS','May the stars smile upon you, $n.',0),
(33135,'enUS','Every world is better off without those demon-loving scum.',0),
(33136,'enUS','$n, I can see the look in your eyes. I have heard of your deeds in the tournament. You are ready to choose a companion!$B$BThis one time I will gift you these two additional coins. Use them wisely, as you will only be able to earn one coin each week from this point forward.',0),
(33137,'enUS','A true leader stands before me. It is my honor to grant you this coin, $n.',0),
(33138,'enUS','Our precious Vale of Eternal Blossoms. So much destruction and violence. But... I sense a glimmer of hope.',0),
(33146,'enUS','Great work $n! Everyone always loves it when they hear that you\'ll be making noodle soup. People come from all over Pandaria just to try a taste.',0),
(33147,'enUS','Do you see? Even now it fades from being.',0),
(33156,'enUS','Ah! Well met, $n!$B$BI was told you would be coming, but had not expected you so soon.$B$B...or has it been a long while? It is difficult to tell, here.$B$BSo! Shall we begin?',0),
(33160,'enUS','Ah! Well met, $n!$B$BI was told you would be coming, but had not expected you so soon.$B$B...or has it been a long while? It is difficult to tell, here.$B$BSo! Shall we begin?',0),
(33161,'enUS','Bizarre place, is it not?$B$BI do hope you found some adventure along the way.',0),
(33168,'enUS','Quickly, place the heart in the forge. We\'ll use its infernal heat to forge the trap.',0),
(33211,'enUS','This is the great burden of the Historian - should Azeroth\'s timeways come under attack, we must reconstruct history exactly as it happened, or the consequences could be dire. As we spread our stories and knowledge, so do we create a stronger future for us all.',0),
(33222,'enUS','You cheated! I know it!',0),
(33228,'enUS','I believe you are getting the feel for this place! Yes, opportunities abound to gather up timeless treasures. Strange events happen all the time here - always keep your eyes open.$B$BSpeak to the mistweavers you met to spend your hard-earned currency. Meanwhile, I will continue my research.$B$BHere is a taste of some of the treasures you can find here. More powerful items are available. You\'ll find that hidden caches in the more dangerous parts of the island can be... extremely rewarding. Good luck.',0),
(33229,'enUS','<The tiny gnome\'s eyes reflect the light with a copper sheen. She is not what she seems.>$B$B$n! I have been waiting for you. The bronze dragonflight has need of your services.',0),
(33230,'enUS','<The tiny gnome\'s eyes reflect the light with a copper sheen. She is not what she seems.>$B$B$n! I have been waiting for you. The bronze dragonflight has need of your services.',0),
(33231,'enUS','I see Chronormu has made good on her promise! You are right on time.',0),
(33232,'enUS','I see Chronormu has made good on her promise! You are right on time.',0),
(33234,'enUS','Oh wow, that thing is really meaty! Think of the soup I could make with it! Here, I will give you some timeless coins for it.',0),
(33235,'enUS','It is so... spongy! Hmm, yes, perhaps a little soy sauce and some oil... Here, take these coins as payment!',0),
(33236,'enUS','Thanks for the flanks! Ha ha, just a little food humor for you. Here are some coins for not groaning!',0),
(33238,'enUS','The stripes on this haunch are so interesting, I wonder how they will cook? First I am going to have to tenderize it a bit, though. Time to beat some meat! Here is a little something for your troubles!',0),
(33239,'enUS','I have never seen one of those before, where in the world did you get it? It is so beautiful, I am not sure I can bear to break it open. Just kidding, this is going to make the best omelet! Here is a bunch of coins!',0),
(33248,'enUS','Welcome to the Proving Grounds, $C. I am Trial Master Rotun.$B$BHere, you may test your skill at performing several different combat roles: dealing damage, absorbing damage, and healing. I shall administer and judge these trials.$B$B$B$BAre you ready to begin?',0),
(33249,'enUS','Welcome to the Proving Grounds, $C. I am Trial Master Rotun.$B$BHere, you may test your skill at performing several different combat roles: dealing damage, absorbing damage, and healing. I shall administer and judge these trials.$B$B$B$BAre you ready to begin?',0),
(33250,'enUS','This is astounding, an egg like this hasn\'t been seen on Pandaria for thousands of years. I believe some of our more ancient scrolls will detail how best to handle it, though many are written in Mogu. I had best get to translating, then!',0),
(33252,'enUS','A small tag on this present reads:$B$BHappy holidays, $n!',0),
(33255,'enUS','Now, to destroy these orcs once and for all.',0),
(33256,'enUS','We did it, $n. Without your heroic efforts, the Temple of Karabor would have been lost to the Iron Horde.$B$BProphet Velen would be proud of us.',0),
(33263,'enUS','Thank the Light. <Cough> I didn\'t think I would get out of here alive.',0),
(33269,'enUS','Every world is better off without those demon-loving scum.',0),
(33271,'enUS','<Something is moving under all of these roots.>',0),
(33332,'enUS','Ah, you have it! Excellent!$B$BA cursory glance indicates that my presumptions were not far-fetched. Though the pages are worn and waterlogged, most of the entries are still legible. It appears that our friend, explorer Harrington, was quite verbose in cataloguing the creatures and treasures he found on his journey through the island.$B$BWell, are you simply going to stand there? This tome is a veritable trove of mysteries, and we have barely scratched the surface! Adventure awaits!',0),
(33333,'enUS','I am happy that you have discovered some riches for your efforts, though we are no closer to unraveling this mystery than before. Take solace in the knowledge that many such bounties are surely scattered throughout the island, eagerly awaiting your exploration skills and combat prowess.$B$BOh, one last thing, my young adventurer - do not forget to look to the skies now and again.',0),
(33334,'enUS','An interesting story of combat and bravery, though I fear that we learned little from your endeavors save that you are quite the adventurer. It seems that we find ourselves at an impasse with each twist and turn of this tale. Time is a fickle mistress.$B$BYou may wish to spend some time honing your skills here, before the sun sets.',0),
(33335,'enUS','In my pride, I sought to keep Pandaria a secret, and once again I have found myself learning great lessons from this land. I am glad to be able to share my stories with my people, once again, in that they may learn as I have, and learn from my mistakes. Perhaps you, too, can still learn a thing or two from the lessons of Pandaria.',0),
(33336,'enUS','Epoch stones are quite rare. The crystallized essence of time, they require a rapid passage through the ages to form. Their presence here indicates that the island may not exist in one time at all, but shift rapidly from timeway to timeway.$B$BThat is of little importance at the moment, though. There are important moments in time that require our attention. Give me a moment to grind the stone and add it to the Vision of Time hourglass.',0),
(33337,'enUS','How very intriguing. I will have to make some additional modifications, and perhaps locate a more proper catalyst. Thank you for performing this experiment, I trust that you did not experience any adverse effects? Should you feel up to the task, I may have use of your services again shortly.',0),
(33338,'enUS','Give me a moment to grind the stones and add them to the hourglass, and we shall see what new events unfold.$B$BIt\'s really quite convenient, I\'ve a particular affinity for specific moments, rather than lengthy chains of events.$B$BThe timeways tell me that we will have need of its power many times in the near future.',0),
(33340,'enUS','The island gives in abundance, in nutriment and in answers. You only need look around to find what you seek.',0),
(33341,'enUS','You have experienced the power and wisdom of the Celestials. Let it flow through you now, and remain in your heart for all time.',0),
(33342,'enUS','Your accomplishments are many, and your bravery cannot be questioned. The Ordon have been driven back for the moment, but do not underestimate them. To restore harmony to the isle, we must continue to be vigilant.',0),
(33343,'enUS','The emissaries of Ordos have been silenced, for a time.$B$BKnow that anger, violence, and hatred will never cease. Wherever there is the darkness within one\'s spirit, you will find these Sha awaiting you. They may become manifest in many forms: a warlord hungering for power, a dagger in your back in the night, a young prince following a dark path, and even your own battle against forces not aligned with your own.$B$BLearn from the lessons of these emotions, lest you lose yourself to the darkness.',0),
(33344,'enUS','The ogres appear to be in disarray and many of my people are now free.',0),
(33354,'enUS','At last, that vicious beast has been slain! Thank you.',0),
(33358,'enUS','Excellent work $n! Everyone always loves it when they hear that you\'ll be making noodle soup. People come from all over Pandaria just to try a taste.',0),
(33359,'enUS','Hello again, $n. You\'re just in time.$B$BWe\'ve tracked the Shadow Council to a nearby village. I suspect that Gul\'dan is with them.',0),
(33374,'enUS','Let this be your daily lesson, and let it hone your strength, wisdom, and fortitude.',0),
(33375,'enUS','A tale of true heroism, and a powerful moment in history. But not quite what we are after, I am afraid.$B$BNot much time remains - I shall double my efforts.',0),
(33376,'enUS','Was that... me? How very interesting.$B$BNow we are beginning to see the shadows between worlds. Was this the future of our world, or simply one possibility? Regardless, our newfound ability to see more deeply into the timeways will allow us to push forward towards the answers we seek.$B$BAllow me some time to continue my research. And be vigilant, hero, for the timeways are as infinite as our enemies.',0),
(33377,'enUS','Stormwind... destroyed?$B$BI realize that this vision may come as a shock to you. I know little more than you at this time. I will do my best to search for answers, you have my word.',0),
(33378,'enUS','Ah, it seems that our little prince has a role to play yet. We should not speak further of this, lest we alter the future ourselves.$B$BThe woods have ears, hero. Keep silent, we will find our answers in time.',0),
(33379,'enUS','Soridormi, the prime consort of Nozdormu, dead? And I was there as well?$B$BWe cannot know what this means, or what will come to pass, or even if this vision takes place in our timeway. You must speak of this vision to no one, lest we alter the course of time and cause great danger to us all. All we can do now is complete the Vision of Time - it will show us what the future truly holds.',0),
(33408,'enUS','Many were killed or wounded on their way here.',0),
(33410,'enUS','This room shook when the monster fell. Your deeds shall not go unremembered.',0),
(33412,'enUS','<Igrimar winces as you show her Durotan\'s orders.>$B$BDon\'t look at me like that... ungh... I\'ve survived worse.',0),
(33419,'enUS','My prayers have been answered, hero. I will tell everyone back at the village of your deeds.',0),
(33427,'enUS','Well done, commander. I shall see what forces we can dispatch to the area for further clean-up.',0),
(33444,'enUS','Goren are abominations. They were created to eat the world. Your have done well.',0),
(33450,'enUS','You have done well in this, but do not become proud. This land has dangers far greater than what you have seen here.',0),
(33454,'enUS','You have done the Frostwolf Clan a service, traveler. I shall be sure to tell Durotan of your deeds.',0),
(33461,'enUS','Nice! Thanks so much! I can use these to make a delicious wolf meat, frog leg, mushroom stew.',0),
(33462,'enUS','With a quick tap of a hammer and a snip of the rings, the Thunderlord Grapple is as good as new.',0),
(33467,'enUS','Impressive work.',0),
(33468,'enUS','Durotan\'s trust in you is well-placed, $n. You have mine as well.',0),
(33469,'enUS','Wolf Home is saved, but I sense a stronger enemy just over the horizon.',0),
(33470,'enUS','This Iron Tide threatens to sweep over all of Draenor.$B$BThe pool has shown you a possible future. This vision of the Frostwolf clan\'s destruction must not be allowed to come to pass.$B$BYou must stop it, $n.',0),
(33473,'enUS','Grim news indeed, $n.$B$BFor saving Wolf Home, I would name you wolf-brother.$B$BNow we must defend Frostfire Ridge from the Thunderlord clan and the Iron Horde.',0),
(33483,'enUS','You have my sincere gratitude, $n.',0),
(33484,'enUS','You found Mulverick?$B$BIt shouldn\'t be long before those ogres clear out after you defeated their master.',0),
(33493,'enUS','Lokra has always lacked the patience and control of her older sister. She approaches problems head-first, and relies on her raw talents to succeed.$B$BSeeing the way her and Karg look at each other, I am not surprised she chased him all the way to Grom\'gar. What surprises me is that they made it back.$B$BAs usual, I expect we have you to thank for that. You continue to honor us with your deeds.',0),
(33513,'enUS','You have done well, but this is only half of the battle. With his support structure in disarray it is time to strike at Death Speaker Blackthorn.',0),
(33514,'enUS','A job well done, $n. With Amnennar\'s phylactery now protected by the Red dragonflight we can now rest at ease.',0),
(33526,'enUS','These are no ordinary enemies, yet you did not show any signs of weakness.',0),
(33527,'enUS','We called you outsider, $R, but you have shown the strength and heart of a Frostwolf.',0),
(33530,'enUS','If this Teron\'gor gains control of Auchindoun, the results would be catastrophic!$B$BWe must stop him before his power grows!',0),
(33533,'enUS','Welcome to Gorgrond, Commander. We only just arrived ourselves.',0),
(33543,'enUS','Ha! Curious. What are you?',0),
(33544,'enUS','Ripfist\'s dying wish has been satisfied. Goren corpses litter the ground, and these corpses have not gone unnoticed by the nearby goren.',0),
(33546,'enUS','Gol\'kosh has completed his mission, then.',0),
(33548,'enUS','These are more than fancy facewear. With a mask and some proper incentive, we can make anyone a Laughing Skull.',0),
(33563,'enUS','These puppets of the magnaron will pay for the skulls they claimed today.$B$BFor now, I shall wear this eye across my waist so this fool you have slain may watch as I slowly slaughter his brethren until my dying breath.',0),
(33578,'enUS','You killed him? Oh, oh thank you!$B$BBut what was that he said about an artifact?',0),
(33579,'enUS','I was worried my little act wouldn\'t fool you, but you played your role perfectly.$B$BIn fact, I would like to ask for your help again.',0),
(33580,'enUS','Mark my words, $R: Aruuna and Veil Shadar were only the beginning.',0),
(33581,'enUS','Yes, yes. Excellent work, these are some of my favorites.$B$BKnowledge is power, and now I can leave for the spires feeling well-armed.',0),
(33582,'enUS','Speaking of fortune, count yourself lucky that I was not among the defenders in Aruuna, for you\'d have seen both ends of your guts before you laid eyes on the Fire-Sage.$B$BAh, sometimes I miss those days.$B$BHere is your coin.',0),
(33586,'enUS','I felt that this day would come. The draenei prophet is not wrong to seek me, traveler.$B$BThough we do not speak often, he and I have a deep mutual respect for one another.$B$BI know the trouble that his people are suffering, and I no longer believe the Shadowmoon are following our ancestor\'s path.$B$BFor those reasons, I will help you.',0),
(33593,'enUS','That didn\'t seem to do much, commander, except to give away our position to every creature in Gorgrond.$B$BWait, did you hear something?',0),
(33622,'enUS','Again we meet...',0),
(33633,'enUS','You feed the hungry boar the nopales. He devours them whole and smacks his lips.$B$BRooter jumps up onto you and licks your face with his disgusting tongue.$B$BIt looks like you have made a new friend.',0),
(33657,'enUS','You have accomplished great things. We could not have captured this citadel without you.',0),
(33660,'enUS','So they started storing their herbs in personal stashes instead of their storage dens, good to know.$B$BYou have helped me a great deal $n.',0),
(33661,'enUS','These are good strong hearts! You have done well $C and I will hold my end of the bargain.',0),
(33662,'enUS','Good work, but we need to move quickly before the plants realize the way is open...',0),
(33663,'enUS','Good work, but we need to move quickly before the plants realize the way is open...',0),
(33685,'enUS','So that is why the saberon have barricaded themselves up there. They are good hunting $n, and I want to get in there!$B$BI have an idea about that...',0),
(33689,'enUS','They just keep coming back! I would hate to lose this hunting ground. We shall find a way to clear this growth, I swear it.',0),
(33694,'enUS','Marrow sent you? Our village destroyed? I would have been back already if it wasn\'t for these cursed plant beasts!',0),
(33695,'enUS','You have... you have brought me the bloom. At last my purpose can be fulfilled!',0),
(33706,'enUS','At last it is done. Dionor has left and his spawn shall follow him in due time.$B$BI grow weary of this conflict and the desire to return to the Overgrowth has left me.$B$BPerhaps I will travel beyond these lands and see what other surprises you little beasts have to share...',0),
(33720,'enUS','A prototype Iron Shredder, huh?! I bet we can get this thing working... they didn\'t have ME to fix it!',0),
(33721,'enUS','I always love a good explosion.',0),
(33722,'enUS','We will have fewer enemies to deal with at our backs. Lok\'tar.',0),
(33724,'enUS','Lots of detail... almost as if a goblin wrote it!',0),
(33728,'enUS','Orgrim seems to be up to no good.',0),
(33729,'enUS','-- ENEMIES ELIMINATED --',0),
(33730,'enUS','Gazlowe has been invaluable in securing Talador. Now, it is up to us.',0),
(33731,'enUS','I cannot believe Orgrim is truly dead. Blackhand has carved a hole in my heart, and I intend to destroy him when the opportunity presents itself.',0),
(33734,'enUS','Thank you.',0),
(33735,'enUS','I believe we can use these at Archenon Siegeyard.',0),
(33736,'enUS','It is a relief to know that their weapons of war cannot be used against us.',0),
(33740,'enUS','Their deaths will not bring back Aruuna, but it does give me comfort to know that some among us can stand against them.',0),
(33754,'enUS','Orgrim leads these orcs? Why has he pledged himself to the Iron Horde?',0),
(33756,'enUS','Good job, and nice time!',0),
(33761,'enUS','My notes! In the chaos, I completely forgot about them!$B$BThis is my life\'s work, $n. I cannot thank you enough.',0),
(33765,'enUS','The forests are clear of Shadowmoon enemies? Good. I knew that you would not fail.',0),
(33784,'enUS','I now understand how you were able to rescue my clan from the clutches of slavery. Such power!',0),
(33785,'enUS','<Karg scoops up a handful of snow and cleans the gore from his axe.>$B$BYou fight well.',0),
(33786,'enUS','Commander! Am I glad to see you.$B$BWe have a situation here.',0),
(33787,'enUS','Bang-up job, $n! The base is just about ready.',0),
(33788,'enUS','Gidwin is looking much better. Thank you, $n.$B$BWe have just enough elixir here to help the others.',0),
(33793,'enUS','I knew I could trust this task to you, $n.',0),
(33794,'enUS','We are taking care of the survivors now. We owe their lives to you. Thank you, $n.',0),
(33795,'enUS','Thank you. My acolytes will study these in great detail. With any luck, we will be able to use this knowledge to defeat the Shadowmoon.',0),
(33807,'enUS','The Frostwolf clan cannot be held like beasts.$B$BYou fight with honor, $n.',0),
(33808,'enUS','Wow, that was fast! Ok, let\'s get to it!',0),
(33813,'enUS','You did it! Squiggy is okay!',0),
(33814,'enUS','Ah, welcome, commander! Just the person I wished to see.',0),
(33815,'enUS','I thank you for returning with my people, and I welcome you as an honored guest.',0),
(33816,'enUS','If you choose to continue to help our clan, the other Shamanstones will sense your closeness to the Frostwolves and might bless you with more gifts.',0),
(33826,'enUS','Nerok and I are the only surviving prisoners, but we cannot leave just yet.',0),
(33828,'enUS','The Iron Horde combines the strengths of every clan. We must continue looking for ways to sever those connections if we hope to defeat them.',0),
(33833,'enUS','The ivory death is slain? Impressive, traveler.$B$BThanks to you, we are all safer with Kuu\'rat gone. I will share news of this deed with the other villagers.',0),
(33834,'enUS','By the elders of Karabor... that thing is huge!$B$BOur trade routes will be safe once again. Well... as safe as you can be running through the northern forests.$B$BWell done, $C!',0),
(33836,'enUS','Thank you, adventurer! We can rest more easily knowing that this beast has been put to its end.',0),
(33837,'enUS','Prophet Velen is gone, and yet there is no time to mourn.$B$BWe will honor Velen\'s passing once the Iron Horde have fled from these hills.$B$BNow, champion, is the time to fight!',0),
(33838,'enUS','Perfect timing. The steel of the blade is still malleable. A few more strikes and my work shall be complete.',0),
(33868,'enUS','<The shaman grins at the harsh, windblown shore.>$B$BWelcome to the home of my people, $n.',0),
(33871,'enUS','I am Seer Malune, the great keeper of memories. It is an honor to finally meet you.',0),
(33872,'enUS','Thank you, $n. With this dust and Aruunem berries I will craft the draught of the dead.',0),
(33873,'enUS','I\'m glad you did not eat any berries. I\'m not sure what I would do if you were to die.',0),
(33874,'enUS','Some memories are better left forgotten. Thank you, $n.$B$BI will return you to our world.',0),
(33882,'enUS','Oh thank you! Now these little peachicks can be moved to safety.',0),
(33884,'enUS','You\'re so brave! I could never have taken Sher\'khaan out on my own!$B$BNow I only have to worry about the scary orcs, giant birds, hippos, big bird men, spiders, everything being on fire...$B$BYa\'know maybe I shouldn\'t be out here all by myself...',0),
(33898,'enUS','You got the fire in you alright.',0),
(33905,'enUS','Wonderful. That should slow down the attack.$B$BOur forces should be able to retake the forest quickly.',0),
(33915,'enUS','Thank you, $n. I\'m sure Orac will think twice before he strays from the pack again.',0),
(33917,'enUS','We can take it from here. Light\'s blessings to you, $C.',0),
(33918,'enUS','Very good. We don\'t be needin\' a gronn bearin\' down on us before we get our defenses all established.',0),
(33919,'enUS','Gutsmash is dead? I\'ll drink to that. You\'re alright, $n.',0),
(33920,'enUS','<Soulbinder Nyami\'s lips curl into a smile.>$B$BWell done. Only two pieces remain. I\'ve already dispatched my soulbinders to track them down.',0),
(33928,'enUS','<Incineratus examines the core as you explain the circumstances behind its acquisition>$B$BIndeed, slag elementals should not exist upon the plateau. The plateau has grown unstable, causing the elemental spirits there to devolve and mutate.$B$BSo long as an earthen fury is absent from the throne, the imbalance in the elements will worsen.$B$BGordawg must return to the Throne of Elements if balance is to be maintained.',0),
(33929,'enUS','Shivertail snuggles up to his mother. He is clearly happy to be reunited with most of his pack.',0),
(33931,'enUS','Haha!',0),
(33944,'enUS','Oh thank you, mister! I can\'t believe Sher\'khaan got Ricky!$B$BYou\'re my hero!',0),
(33955,'enUS','You startle the small pup.',0),
(33958,'enUS','Just as I suspected. Thank you, $n. With Sha\'tari back in our possession there is only one piece of the Heart left to retrieve.',0),
(33967,'enUS','Bless you, $n. There have been enough innocent lives taken today.',0),
(33969,'enUS','We were wise to not underestimate the threat of a land turned against us.',0),
(33970,'enUS','Just as I suspected. Thank you, $n. With Sha\'tari back in our possession there is only one piece of the Heart left to retrieve.',0),
(33971,'enUS','Bless you, $n. There have been enough innocent lives taken today.',0),
(33972,'enUS','<Mehlar smiles.>$B$BIt would seem that the tide of this war is shifting in our favor.',0),
(33973,'enUS','Thank you. Now that I know it is out of the hands of the Iron Horde, I can die peacefully.',0),
(33976,'enUS','Well done! I will take Auch\'naaru to Auchindoun. The Shadow Council has no place in our lands.',0),
(34012,'enUS','<Prowler Sasha nods and assembles two necklaces.>',0),
(34013,'enUS','With these, we can account for our fallen and rebuild. We will persevere.',0),
(34019,'enUS','Your aid in retaking Teluuna Observatory has not gone unnoticed, hero. I grow increasingly impressed at your prowess in battle.$B$BPerhaps you could share some of your knowledge with my disciples. They could learn much from a seasoned adventurer such as yourself.$B$BI have something for you, as a thanks for what you\'ve done even in the short time you\'ve been here. Perhaps it will help you get this garrison of yours on its feet.',0),
(34026,'enUS','Ach! Sir $n, ye\'ve arrived just in time!',0),
(34027,'enUS','I KNEW somethin\' was wrong! IN YER FACE, Alexston!$B$BAh, excuse me.$B$BNow, where have I seen machines like this before?$B$BOh yeah! The Dark Iron!',0),
(34028,'enUS','Mmf! Mm- mff!!$B$B<You remove his gag.>$B$BTHEY GOT THAELIN!!',0),
(34029,'enUS','Close enough!',0),
(34030,'enUS','$n! Oh, yer a sight for sore eyes!$B$BThe prototype mole machine was able to track me here all the way from the shop? I even impress myself sometimes.$B$BNow that I know Hansel is safe, I can enact the brilliant escape plan I\'ve been working on. Glad to have ye here for this!',0),
(34031,'enUS','For the record, the mines don\'t have any voice commands.$B$BI learned that lesson awhile back...',0),
(34032,'enUS','Aye, there she is.$B$BThank you, $n. Let\'s get out of here, shall we?',0),
(34033,'enUS','So I guess it\'s safe to say my old workshop is compromised. We\'ll have to find a new place to set up shop...',0),
(34034,'enUS','<Gazlowe\'s face brightens as you hand over the bulging bag of coins.>$B$BHeyyy! Now we\'re talking!$B$BI usually prefer not to get my hands dirty, but for that kind of cash you could get me to field-strip a kor\'kron outhouse.$B$BGlad to have some muscle here to back me up - and since I\'m such a nice guy, here\'s a little somethin\' for your troubles.',0),
(34035,'enUS','Ya know... this thing is actually pretty impressive.$B$BThe drive system seems... familiar...',0),
(34039,'enUS','<Gazlowe fishes around in his pouch before producing a single gold piece.>$B$BErr... looks like I\'m a little short. Personal bodyguard fees really add up!$B$BI\'ll give you a proper cut when we get back to your garrison. Come on, you know I\'m good for it!',0),
(34040,'enUS','That\'s Darkanvil\'s signature! I knew I\'d seen that work somewhere before.$B$BThaelin Darkanvil is a Dark Iron dwarf who came to Draenor with the Alliance forces, and a damn brilliant engineer. We have what you might call a friendly rivalry.$B$BBut why\'s Thaelin making weapons for the Iron Horde?',0),
(34041,'enUS','Not a bad haul. Here\'s yer cut!',0),
(34042,'enUS','Don\'t worry, Thaelin can handle himself. That was my good deed for the year - don\'t tell nobody!$B$BHey... you think I can write off that fuel as a business expense?',0),
(34043,'enUS','Good, you\'ve arrived. Rulkan\'s message said that you would not be long.',0),
(34048,'enUS','There, my beauties are safely out of the hands of the Iron Horde. No more orcs poppin\' out of the ground!$B$BThere\'s just one more thing I need to do before I can leave with a clear conscience.',0),
(34054,'enUS','We saved everyone we could, $n. We were too late for the others... including my sister.$B$BProphet Velen is right. When it is asked of us, we ALL must fight. I promise this: I will never again let my loved ones suffer.$B$BNer\'zhul is close to calling down the Dark Star. We are the only ones who can stop him.',0),
(34066,'enUS','You have done well, $C.$B$BNow before we can continue our assault we need to look for any supplies in the area that could help our fight.',0),
(34067,'enUS','Rope? Do you expect me to tie a noose and ask the Thunderlords to go hang themselves?$B$BWait... that gives me an idea. Yea, I think I can make this work with the right materials.$B$BGood Job.',0),
(34069,'enUS','Hrm, yes these spears look pretty good.$B$BNot bad! I know just what to use these for!',0),
(34070,'enUS','Well done $n! The removal of the Sky Riders takes the heat off us for a bit. Keep your weapon in hand though, we\'re not done with them yet.',0),
(34072,'enUS','Ugh, those smell awful! No, I don\'t need to see them. I\'ll take you at your word that you have them all.$B$BLet\'s get a move on before another Thunderlord patrol stumbles upon me.',0),
(34073,'enUS','Good job $n, I was able to use the commotion from your work to sneak into the camp.$B$BNow we have only one thing left to do.',0),
(34075,'enUS','Thank you,$n.$B$BI wish we could bring him back just to kill him again but I guess this will suffice.$B$BI hope the spirit of my little one will now know peace.',0),
(34078,'enUS','Told you I was good for it!',0),
(34087,'enUS','Orgrim leads the Iron Horde in Talador... Now we know the face of our enemy.',0),
(34088,'enUS','The Iron Horde has no consideration for the wonders of the forest. In death, they will know respect.',0),
(34089,'enUS','I believe we can use these explosives against the Iron Horde.',0),
(34090,'enUS','Nothing like a good explosion to warm the heart.',0),
(34091,'enUS','A prototype Iron Shredder, huh?! I bet we can get this thing working... they didn\'t have Thaelin Darkanvil to fix it!',0),
(34092,'enUS','You radiate the power of the Ango\'rosh!$B$B<Restalaan smiles.>$B$BIt is time to take this battle to Teron\'gor\'s doorstep.',0),
(34093,'enUS','Hrm, yes these spears look pretty good. Outstanding $n! I know just what to use these for!',0),
(34094,'enUS','I wondered why the manual was so big... they write with really big letters!',0),
(34095,'enUS','They will be unable to use those weapons against us when we attack Tuurem.',0),
(34096,'enUS','That\'s a lot of orcs, eh? Glad I\'m here tinkerin\' away instead of in the thick of it.',0),
(34097,'enUS','-- ENEMIES ELIMINATED --',0),
(34098,'enUS','The screams of our enemies washed over me. The people of Tuurem are avenged.',0),
(34099,'enUS','Maraad is dead... but we must carry on. I will not let his sacrifice be for nothing.',0),
(34102,'enUS','Good work,$n!$B$BSeeing Frostwolf banners standing proudly over our crushed foes fills me with pride!$B$BLet them forever fear the wrath of the Frostwolves!',0),
(34103,'enUS','I have no idea how you managed to track down the creature so close to the Horde base, but well done sir.',0),
(34104,'enUS','Thank you, commander! The peasants will be singing songs about your generosity tomorrow.',0),
(34105,'enUS','All hail your glory, commander.',0),
(34106,'enUS','I knew you\'d kill her. No Iron Horde is safe from your wrath.',0),
(34107,'enUS','Is that what I think it is? You are too kind, commander!',0),
(34108,'enUS','Praise to $n! For the Horde!',0),
(34122,'enUS','<Liadrin smiles.>$B$BI knew they\'d see it our way.',0),
(34123,'enUS','I am glad to see you. Our clan has faced many challenges, but the sheer size of the army coming toward us is beyond anything we have attempted to face.$B$BWe need your experience.',0),
(34124,'enUS','This was a costly victory, and a very painful lesson. We chose to refuse the Iron Horde and live as we always have, but I see now they will never respect such neutrality.$B$BI am not about to wait for the Iron Horde to martial their forces. We will fight with you, and bring the Iron Horde to its knees.$B$BCommander, the Frostwolves stand ready!',0),
(34144,'enUS','Already I can feel the Light triumphing over darkness. We\'ve done it!',0),
(34154,'enUS','Teron\'gor and Gul\'dan... they slaughtered everyone...$B$B...and then they just... disappeared... into the shadows...$B$BHow did they know where to go?',0),
(34157,'enUS','You have to hurry... Teron\'gor just left!',0),
(34164,'enUS','Thank you... kill a couple more for me on your way out, if you can...',0),
(34192,'enUS','Nice job, $n! Let\'s get this mining operation started!',0),
(34193,'enUS','Great work, $n! We will get started planting the garden right away.',0),
(34194,'enUS','Time to see what you can do.',0),
(34209,'enUS','Thank you for coming, $n. The archmage and I are in need of your assistance.',0),
(34216,'enUS','Wolf-brother, already word has traveled to us of your actions at Wor\'gol. You have the eternal respect of the Frostwolf.$B$BNow, who are these strangers that you have brought to us and what is this urgent matter?',0),
(34227,'enUS','Unfortunate that there are those that would pervert such noble creatures.$B$BYou have honored their family once more, $n. They will not forget.$B$BNow it is time to take the fight directly to the Shadow Council.',0),
(34228,'enUS','We haven\'t seen these creatures here in a generation.$B$BTheir sudden appearance and the shaking of the ground are most definitely connected.',0),
(34229,'enUS','I\'ve heard of these strange Pale orcs you saw. They sound like the Warsingers of Nagrand. But no, that cannot be....$B$BAs for the ogre, his name is Cho\'gall. You should kill him if you get the chance. He brings nothing but destruction in his wake.',0),
(34230,'enUS','Yes, this will do nicely. Let\'s use the Shadow Council\'s magic against them.',0),
(34234,'enUS','Excellent. The shards are at last together!',0),
(34240,'enUS','It\'s not safe here. The Shadow Council has already taken the city!',0),
(34242,'enUS','It\'s not safe here. The Shadow Council has already taken the city!',0),
(34264,'enUS','Rope? Do you expect me to tie a noose and ask the Thunderlords to go hang themselves?$B$BWait... that gives me an idea. Yea, I think I can make this work with the right materials.$B$BGood Job.',0),
(34271,'enUS','Gordawg was a mighty ally. The elements will mourn the loss of the fury, but death was the only answer. Gordawg would not have wished to stay a slave to evil.$B$BThough Gordawg is no more, the heart of a fury is eternal and unbreakable. In time, this brightly glowing heart will take shape into a new earthen fury.$B$BSuch is the cycle of life upon the Elemental Plateau.',0),
(34277,'enUS','We should have killed them all at the Dark Portal in the beginning and damn the consequences.',0),
(34278,'enUS','For what they\'ve done, it is not enough.$B$B$n, when you find their base, you salt the earth.',0),
(34279,'enUS','Blook never beat before.$B$BBlook follow tiny person now, so Blook learn how to beat more people.',0),
(34280,'enUS','Gul\'dan is there! We must move quickly to capture him.',0),
(34281,'enUS','With that ball o\' stone gone I be feelin\' better already!',0),
(34284,'enUS','Well I be a son of a gnome! Am I glad to see you! I was hoping fer a rescue but didn\'t expect da boss tae be here himself!',0),
(34285,'enUS','Thank ye, looks like everything\'s still in good shape. Just give me a moment to put this on.',0),
(34286,'enUS','Secluded cave across the lava, check.$B$BCreepy piles o\' bones, check.$B$BOkay, this looks like the place. We\'re gonna have to watch ourselves, I\'ll bet Borgal isn\'t here alone.',0),
(34287,'enUS','Thank you, I am glad that the spirits have been released from their torment.',0),
(34288,'enUS','Very good, I can feel that the magic in these is strong.',0),
(34289,'enUS','That was one hell of a battle! Bloody fine job there la... um commander. $B$BOrlana really helped us out there. I\'ll ask around, maybe a priest can think of something we can do for her. $B$BAt any rate, we still have this artifact to deal with. I think you better hold onto it for safe keeping before any power crazed lunatics comes looking for it.',0),
(34291,'enUS','A heart? How touching.$B$BQuickly. We must use it to destroy the fel crystals and get to Gul\'dan.',0),
(34292,'enUS','Necessary business. We don\'t dare risk letting them grow more powerful.',0),
(34293,'enUS','Necessary business. We don\'t dare risk letting them grow more powerful.',0),
(34294,'enUS','The barrier is down. Now it\'s time to capture Gul\'dan.',0),
(34295,'enUS','Unfortunate, but not surprising. At least we were able to defeat one of the inner council members.$B$BAll is not lost, $n. We know what the Shadow Council is up to and where they\'re heading.$B$BWe\'ll regroup in Talador. Together, we\'ll put an end to Teron\'gor and his plans for Auchindoun.$B$BDid you hear that?...',0),
(34309,'enUS','Oi dere mon! Glad to see a friendly face but I not expect da commander ta come out here for me himself!',0),
(34314,'enUS','Ah now, dat be feeling much better!',0),
(34315,'enUS','Ah dat be me stuff! Give me a moment ta put me stuff on mon. Then, I gonna take me an ogre ear for every bone I had ta pop back in place.',0),
(34316,'enUS','This be da place. We gonna need ta be careful, Borgal an\' da artifact be in there.',0),
(34318,'enUS','Very good, I can feel that the magic in these is strong.',0),
(34319,'enUS','Dat was a battle for da ages mon! Bwu\'ja be glad ye are here commanda, else I\'d likely be back in da spirit world permanently.$B$BDat Soulgrinda be a nasty piece o\' mojo. Ye be the best one to hold onto it.$B$BDat spirit, she helped us out a lot mon. I hope she find da peace she be seeking now.',0),
(34321,'enUS','Thank you flesh creature. In the lava the ashes will mix and the cycle shall continue as it has ever since the beginning.',0),
(34325,'enUS','The lava already burns bright with the return of my people\'s freedom!$B$BWe will have our revenge upon the ogres for everything they have done to us, this I assure you. But for now, we shall rest.',0),
(34326,'enUS','Our enemy has been pushed back and Auchindoun\'s defenses restored thanks to your help, but we are not yet done here.',0),
(34335,'enUS','Greetings, $C. You\'re the commander that Choluna mentioned?$B$B$B$BGood.',0),
(34336,'enUS','I knew you were the right person for this job, $n. I just love results.',0),
(34337,'enUS','So this is it, huh? Let\'s see what\'s hiding in these depths.',0),
(34338,'enUS','That was close, $n. Good work.',0),
(34339,'enUS','Oh my, what an interesting variety! It appears that the goren will eat... anything!',0),
(34340,'enUS','Oh, my! Amazing! This caldera is hotter than hot! Thank you, $n.',0),
(34341,'enUS','Good. We will keep the artifact safe here, in your garrison.',0),
(34344,'enUS','Dem centipedes creep you out boss-mon? Touchin\' ya with their teeny tiny legs? I ain\'t thought of a thing that makes me skin crawl more, except maybe mah sister\'s voice. Hee hee.',0),
(34345,'enUS','Haha! Ya brought \'em! I hope ya not offended I asked such a lowly task of ya. We needed the leaves, and I needed to settle a bet.',0),
(34346,'enUS','Ah, now these be some fine trap making props. Ya know how to make a shadow huntah proud.',0),
(34347,'enUS','These orders come straight from the leader of the Burning Blade!$B$BI\'ve heard of her... the fierce orc with the blade that thirsts for death.$B$BYou\'ve done well to bring this to me, $n.',0),
(34348,'enUS','Now dat be a mighty fine haul. We gonna be keepin\' all the folks at the garrison warm.$B$BIt seemed like a simple task but ya tackled it like a boss-mon. If ya need a shadow hunter in your ranks, I be willin\' to serve.',0),
(34351,'enUS','Light bless you, hero! We need to hold out as long as we can so Nyami can track down the remaining power shards. This pylon will help take the load off of our soulpriests.',0),
(34353,'enUS','You are proving to be a great hunter, $n. But our work on this island is not yet complete.',0),
(34354,'enUS','You have done a good thing here today. Don\'t let the blood on your axe blind you.$B$BYou have given these rylaks the peace they deserve.',0),
(34355,'enUS','With fewer machines these weaklings will quickly lose their foothold on this island.$B$BExcellent work, $n.',0),
(34362,'enUS','Blast it, he\'s given us the slip!$B$BTa make things worse the portal looks like it\'s closed from this side. We\'re gonna have to find a way to track Borgal down or we might be stuck in wherever this is.',0),
(34364,'enUS','I\'m under orders to obey your orders, commander.',0),
(34365,'enUS','Excellent work, $n. You are proving to be a great ally.',0),
(34375,'enUS','That should be plenty of wood for now.',0),
(34378,'enUS','Right! I think we\'ve got this well in hand now. And hardly an explosion to be found!',0),
(34379,'enUS','I hope you are finding your land agreeable.',0),
(34380,'enUS','The clan is prepared. It is time for us to advance on Bladespire Citadel!',0),
(34381,'enUS','Dat ogre, he done give us de slip!$B$B<Bwu\'ja looks around.>$B$BDis place, it be da spirit world! First time I ever walk here in da flesh.$B$BLooks like our path back be blocked and our prey be gone. We gonna have ta go find dat ogre ta get outta dis place.',0),
(34392,'enUS','The portal is weakened, but it remains open.$B$BOnly one option remains, $n.',0),
(34393,'enUS','Gul\'dan... free. This was not the victory I\'d planned for.$B$BGul\'dan may be loose due to our actions, but I gladly bargain his freedom against the lives of the innocents on the other side of this portal. You made a wise decision, $n.',0),
(34397,'enUS','With their leaders dead this operation will surely fall apart.',0),
(34398,'enUS','Looks to me like we ended up in the right place.',0),
(34399,'enUS','The Vindicators welcome you, $n.',0),
(34400,'enUS','Thank you, $n. These moths are typically peaceful creatures and are deserving of mercy.',0),
(34401,'enUS','This will do nicely, $n. All we need now is a suitable crystal...',0),
(34402,'enUS','This land should serve our needs well. I leave it to you to decide how to best use it, commander.',0),
(34403,'enUS','Excellent work, $n. The arcane essence you\'ve collected will do nicely. All we need now is a suitable crystal to attune...',0),
(34404,'enUS','The crystals in this mine are most certainly unique. Thorough study of the samples you have provided should reveal why this is the case.',0),
(34406,'enUS','Thank you for getting the workers our of the mine safely, $n.',0),
(34407,'enUS','I only hope we are enough.',0),
(34409,'enUS','Greetings, $C. You\'re the commander from the garrison?$B$B$B$BGood.',0),
(34410,'enUS','Never in my years have I seen anything like this, $n. You have done well today.',0),
(34414,'enUS','Excellent. Give me a moment and I will prepare the focusing crystal.',0),
(34415,'enUS','It is sad to see such a mighty creature fall, but An\'dure was a danger to all within the mine. The heart of the crystal giant will aid us in restoring peace to the Jorune Mine.',0),
(34418,'enUS','Your valor will give our men reprieve as they work to contain the threat completely. Well done.',0),
(34420,'enUS','With the Dark Portal disabled, we have a new mission: stay alive.$B$BWe must keep pressing on, even if only to honor those who stayed behind to secure our retreat.',0),
(34421,'enUS','Well done, $n.$B$BGiven, they are injured, half-starved, and poorly-equipped... but there is no blade so sharp as a vengeful spirit, no armor so thick as a righteous cause.',0),
(34422,'enUS','Out of the frying pan, into the woods.$B$BTake a breath, then get ready, $n. There\'s not much time to rest.',0),
(34423,'enUS','<Khadgar looks concerned.>$B$BNo - we cannot wait for Ariok. He knew what he was getting into.$B$BHis sacrifice cannot go to waste. We must keep moving.',0),
(34425,'enUS','We will hold this position for now. We must allow these freed prisoners a moment to breathe.$B$BIt is not an ideal position. We will be moving again shortly.',0),
(34427,'enUS','I owe my life to you, stranger. I offer you and your company my support. Together, we may make it out of this jungle alive.',0),
(34429,'enUS','You\'re still alive? Good.$B$BThat cave-in will only hold them for so long. We have to keep moving.',0),
(34431,'enUS','Well done.$B$BBe ready to move. We may have had the element of surprise within this cave, but our advantage is fleeting.',0),
(34432,'enUS','You fight exceptionally well, $n... better than I could ever hope to.$B$BWith those orcs out of the way, Khadgar and Maraad should now be able to safely guide the rest of our group through the cave.',0),
(34434,'enUS','Up there - that is Keli\'dan the Breaker. No doubt he\'s been alerted to our presence, and he\'s attempting to tell his warlord about our little jailbreak.$B$BWe have to take him out, $n.',0),
(34436,'enUS','Fine job in the cave, but this is no time to rest.$B$BWe have momentum. We must stay in motion.',0),
(34437,'enUS','You have my thanks, $n. Durotan, our chieftain, will be happy to hear that Ga\'nar lives.',0),
(34439,'enUS','It\'s a good thing you got to high ground.$B$BLook at the dam!',0),
(34442,'enUS','<The orc\'s lips and wrists quiver with restrained fury.>$B$BWho are you?$B$BWait, what\'s that you say? Drek\'Thar is here?',0),
(34445,'enUS','Takin\' away Gul\'dan was one thing, but blowin\' up the whole damned portal? That\'s my kind of solution.$B$BNow, I think we\'d better get out of here before that army gets to us.',0),
(34446,'enUS','Against all odds, here we stand. Still alive, an entire army on our heels.$B$BOur ship is waiting. Shall we depart?',0),
(34447,'enUS','A wise elder of my order once told me, \"True power is the strength to act and the wisdom to know when not to act.\" May those words and the memory of Kaelynara stay with you on your journey, $n.',0),
(34448,'enUS','A wise elder of my order once told me, \"True power is the strength to act and the wisdom to know when not to act.\" May those words and the memory of Kaelynara stay with you on your journey, $n.',0),
(34450,'enUS','We have accomplished great things on this island today, $n. I look forward to the day we hunt again.',0),
(34451,'enUS','There is still much to be done before we can leave Auchindoun with peace of mind, champion.',0),
(34452,'enUS','We have our work cut out for us, champion. The Legion\'s stench fills the air.',0),
(34458,'enUS','You look like you can fight. We need to get out of here!',0),
(34461,'enUS','This will be a mighty fine barracks, I think. I am sure Warmaster Zog will complain about how it needs to be bigger, and with more spikes. He likes spikes...',0),
(34462,'enUS','Well done commander. Olin spoke to me of your bravery and has already offered to serve under your command.$B$BIf I may advise you in this matter, I would suggest accepting his service. We could make use of a tauren with his skill sets in a land like this.',0),
(34463,'enUS','Ah. Now what do you have there? This ring is going to require some extra research.$B$BIt seems like someone was trying to travel through time but in a very backward fashion.',0),
(34464,'enUS','These boots are fantastic! You did the right thing bringing these to me.$B$BThey are actually trying to replace the space they occupy with a different timeline.$B$BThis will definitely require more study.',0),
(34465,'enUS','Now THAT is a hat. See how it flickers in and out of time as if someone were temporally jiggling it?$B$BI\'d try putting it on if I weren\'t afraid it would wipe me from the timeline.',0),
(34466,'enUS','Hmm. This staff looks familiar. I wonder...$B$BYou did the right thing bringing it to me. I will investigate further!',0),
(34469,'enUS','Thank you, I am glad that the spirits have been released from their torment.',0),
(34472,'enUS','$n? Is that you? Fantastic! And they said it couldn\'t be done.$B$BThey said traversing the worlds in this way was the domain of the bronze dragonflight. Well, guess who\'s temporally laughing now!',0),
(34478,'enUS','I owe my life to you, stranger. I offer you and your company my support. Together, we may make it out of this jungle alive.',0),
(34508,'enUS','There is no time for pleasantries. The raid\'s leader is just ahead.',0),
(34512,'enUS','<Pyxni examines the saberon claws.>$B$BWe\'re gonna make a killing selling these as good luck charms to all the wannabe gladiators here at the arena!$B$BFrom now on, the saberon will think twice about messing with the Steamwheedle Cartel!',0),
(34513,'enUS','You fought your way into Sabermaw, killed Razorpaw...and lived?$B$BThat\'s incredible news!$B$BThe roads will be much safer now that he\'s dead! That means more money for me!$B$BAs promised, here\'s your reward!',0),
(34514,'enUS','You recovered the merchandise? Fantastic!$B$B<Pyxni rummages through the bags.>$B$BIt\'s all here too! I knew I could count on you! Here, take this reward.$B$BYou\'ve earned it!',0),
(34515,'enUS','You got all of the captured traders out of Sabermaw? Fantastic!$B$BNow they owe me and I ain\'t one to let a debt go uncollected! As for you, take this reward for your trouble!',0),
(34516,'enUS','You did a great job, $n. I couldn\'t have asked for a better sidekick!$B$BAnyway, now that I\'ve got my treasure back...$B$BI\'ve got to do...$B$B...things and...stuff.$B$BBye!',0),
(34558,'enUS','Excellent. This will do nicely.',0),
(34563,'enUS','You are the commander of this fort, yes?$B$BMy master wanted to join your fight to reclaim our home but he grew ill and... I\'m sorry, he was a great draenei and I will carry on his memory.$B$BYour new building would give me the means to see out my master\'s vision and honor his passing.$B$BIf you would allow me to do this then I would serve you.',0),
(34564,'enUS','Teron\'gor and Gul\'dan... they slaughtered everyone...$B$B...and then they just... disappeared... into the shadows...$B$BHow did they know where to go?',0),
(34566,'enUS','Your will be done.$B$BFor the Horde!',0),
(34569,'enUS','You\'re the one in charge around here, right? I\'ve heard the guards talk about your exploits and if I wasn\'t looking at you now I\'d swear they were lying.$B$BI\'ve only ever wanted to make the finest blades and put them in the hands of the strongest of fighters. I can tell already that you\'re exactly the type I want to carry my weapons.$B$BIf you can give me a chance I swear you will not be disappointed.',0),
(34571,'enUS','These look pretty good. Ared would have loved to get his hands on these.$B$B<Miall wipes away a tear.>$B$B I\'m sorry, this is making me too emotional, these will do just fine.',0),
(34572,'enUS','Perfect, they will have to concentrate more on base defense now. Hopefully things will get back to normal out there.',0),
(34573,'enUS','This won\'t be as good as some of the stuff we had back at the forge in Shattrath, but it will do.',0),
(34575,'enUS','<The prophet welcomes you with a curious look, then a warm nod.>$B$BSo it begins.',0),
(34576,'enUS','This won\'t be as good as some of the mixes we had back in the Blackrock foundries, but it will do.',0),
(34577,'enUS','Good size chunks and without a lot of the matrix material on them.$B$BThese will do just fine.',0),
(34578,'enUS','I crafted a few things before we left that we may need: some smoke grenades, a grappling hook, even was able to get Thaelin to throw together a rocket pack.$B$BI\'m sure we\'ll find a use for everything.',0),
(34579,'enUS','Thank you boss, this is just what I needed.$B$BBy the way, Goren gas is rather difficult to come by. We should probably hold off on clearing those guys out till we can stockpile enough.$B$BJust a thought.',0),
(34582,'enUS','This will have to do.',0),
(34583,'enUS','So this is Draenor? A bit darker than expected. Still, after building Stormwind, this project should be a walk in the park.$B$BWell then, are you ready to begin, commander?',0),
(34584,'enUS','Perfect.$B$BNot only will this lumber do the job, it will look fantastic!',0),
(34585,'enUS','The base is significantly more secure with that giant dead.$B$BYou have made quite an impression on the peacekeepers.',0),
(34586,'enUS','The garrison is really starting to take shape.',0),
(34587,'enUS','How is the construction of the barracks coming along?',0),
(34592,'enUS','Nasty beasts they got here on Draenor.',0),
(34593,'enUS','Glad you are here. I almost got killed up there at the top. Oh what are these papers? This is much worse than I imagined!',0),
(34596,'enUS','That Felbreaker sounded tough! Good thing there\'s only a small number of them.$B$BNice job stopping Reglakk, but I\'m sure he\'s safely back in Highmaul. The ogre capital will have to be dealt with sooner rather than later.',0),
(34597,'enUS','Excellent job thinking on your feet. The less research these ogres do, the better!',0),
(34598,'enUS','<Greezlex lifts his head to look up at you from the ground.>$B$B...No! Don\'t take me... I... wait...$B$BYou aren\'t a saberon... did Pyxni send you?',0),
(34609,'enUS','This isn\'t quite what they taught me in Dalaran, but it\'ll have to do!',0),
(34612,'enUS','Yes, these will work great! I can freeze the pulp into a fine parchment.',0),
(34616,'enUS','This place is just full of surprises... terrifying surprises.',0),
(34619,'enUS','Perfect! We should have plenty of energy now.',0),
(34624,'enUS','Thank you, this is just what I needed.$B$BGoren gas is rather difficult to come by but thankfully we can make this supply go a long way.',0),
(34631,'enUS','Ah, so you\'ve built an Arcane Sanctum! Splendid!$B$BTroubles connecting to the ley line network, I take it?',0),
(34632,'enUS','Ah, so you\'ve built an Arcane Sanctum! Splendid!$B$BTroubles connecting to the ley line network, I take it?',0),
(34634,'enUS','These pustules are sizzling with energy. They\'ll do nicely.',0),
(34635,'enUS','Such clean breaks on each piece! Fantastic.',0),
(34636,'enUS','Excellent. This ought to be just what we need.',0),
(34646,'enUS','Luuka is a little shaken up, but he is safe, and that\'s all that really matters.$B$BLook... commander, I owe you my life. All of us do honestly.$B$BI would be honored to serve as your agent here in Draenor. If you have need of me, you need only say the word.',0),
(34653,'enUS','<The arakkoa merchant looks you up and down.>$B$BWell-equipped, aren\'t we? Azik is betting you are someone of importance to your people.$B$BCome closer, friend. Speak with me for just a moment.',0),
(34655,'enUS','Azik must have seen something in you. I will trust his judgment, for n-$B$B<Reshad is interrupted as a warm gust of wind surges through the hut.>$B$BOh dear... they\'ve arrived.',0),
(34656,'enUS','Who would expect to find these treasures draped over straw dolls, left to bake in the sun? Sometimes the best place to hide precious things is in plain sight.',0),
(34657,'enUS','Azik was right to guide you to me. If you were coming to help Skettis, we needed to meet.$B$BAnd if you were coming to attack us, well, I\'d be dead either way, wouldn\'t I?$B$B<Reshad lets out a cawing laugh and stuffs another scroll into his robes.>$B$BThere, that\'s nearly everything.',0),
(34658,'enUS','Ah yes, there\'s my name at the top of the list. And a few Talonpriests from the Shadowglade as well.$B$BThey fear the return of Terokk, as they should.',0),
(34659,'enUS','I will point you in the right direction, but I cannot guarantee you\'ll survive the trip.$B$BKah-hah haha!',0),
(34662,'enUS','Whoa! I couldn\'t tell if that was Porkchop squealing in there or if you had Crushmaul crying like a little baby!$B$BYou\'ve got talent, kid!$B$BHere\'s your cut of the profit, but why stop there? Together we can make a mountain of gold!',0),
(34663,'enUS','You did it, $n! Raketalon has actually been defeated!$B$BI\'d never have believed it if I hadn\'t seen it with my very own two eyes. You\'ve got a fire in your belly and dollar signs in your eyes, kid!$B$BHere\'s your cut of the profit, but don\'t stop now! You\'re on a roll!',0),
(34664,'enUS','Watching you fight in the arena is like witnessing an artist create a masterpiece!$B$BWell, a masterpiece of blood and shattered bones... but hey, everyone\'s got to be good at something right?$B$BHere\'s your cut of the profit! That fight was so good I actually thought about giving you a bonus!',0),
(34665,'enUS','I ain\'t ever seen anybody dismantle a shredder quite like that before!$B$BYou\'ve made me a lot of money, $n! Only the best gladiators survive this long in the arena; and yet, even with that in mind, there\'s still something different about you...$B$BIt\'s your eyes...they look as if they\'ve stared death in the face a thousand times and never even blinked.$B$BTake your cut of the profit and rest up, the biggest fight is still ahead!',0),
(34666,'enUS','Long live the champ! I knew you could do it!$B$BCould you hear the roar of the crowd in there? It shook the arena like thunder!$B$BThis is only the beginning! The Highmaul Coliseum awaits, and as the champion of the Ring of Trials you\'ll be expected to make an appearance!',0),
(34672,'enUS','That was incredible, $n! The Old Gods will think twice before trying to crawl out of their pit again.',0),
(34673,'enUS','Dat was amazin\', $n! De Old Gods be thinkin\' twice before tryin\' to take anudder bite outta you, mon.',0),
(34674,'enUS','They came at us... from... nowhere.$B$B<The lieutenant nearly passes out.>',0),
(34675,'enUS','Commander $n. It\'s good to see you. We have much to discuss.$B$BThe situation in Nagrand is rapidly deteriorating. We\'ve lost Telaar.$B$BTo make matters worse, Grommash has named Garrosh Hellscream the new warlord of the Warsong clan.',0),
(34676,'enUS','I won\'t waste any of your time, sir. Let us discuss strategy.',0),
(34678,'enUS','For me? Really you shouldn\'t have.$B$BOkay, this should do it.$B$BI hope.',0),
(34681,'enUS','Your will be done. I require your advisement, commander.',0),
(34682,'enUS','We\'ve been expecting you, commander.$B$BThe situation is grim, but doable with your help.',0),
(34683,'enUS','Ah, $n. I recognized your scent, friend. We have been waiting for your arrival to begin our task.',0),
(34685,'enUS','Kalaam sent you? By the Light, I knew I could count on him!',0),
(34692,'enUS','This is a good start, but we will need more champions to deal with the trials that lay ahead.',0),
(34696,'enUS','We\'ll have to catch up later. We have bigger problems!',0),
(34697,'enUS','The Laughing Skull sent you? If they were any other clan I would find that ironic.$B$BI am Kash\'drakor, hero of the Frostwolf clan, and champion of the slave pits of Stonemaul.$B$BAnd yet, despite all these titles, I need your help.',0),
(34698,'enUS','You have shown more honor in this one act than I have seen in many years.$B$BWhen this is over, I will swear my axe to your forces and pass my knowledge on to your troops.',0),
(34699,'enUS','Thank you, strange one. Now we are free to split that chieftain Kor\'gall wide open!',0),
(34700,'enUS','This deed will never be forgotten as long as I or my son live. You have my gratitude, hero, and my loyalty.',0),
(34701,'enUS','I will not allow a single demon to step foot inside Auchindoun. You will help me ensure that does not happen.',0),
(34702,'enUS','Me watch you from afar. Me like your fighting skills, show much promise.',0),
(34703,'enUS','This blade has caused enough pain and suffering for one lifetime. We shall see to it that it is properly disposed of.',0),
(34704,'enUS','You do not have the look of a Stonemaul bounty hunter.$B$BWe escaped the clutches of their vile arena but at a heavy cost. We were forced to leave too many allies behind and too many ogres breathing.$B$BWe could use a fresh face, one that is unknown to the ogres.',0),
(34706,'enUS','Lady Liadrin was indeed wise in choosing you. I will let Vol\'jin know of your victory immediately.',0),
(34707,'enUS','I will gather any remaining survivors so we can rebuild what we have lost.$B$BThank you.',0),
(34709,'enUS','Aeun sent you? Help has arrived!',0),
(34710,'enUS','Aeun sent you? Help has arrived!',0),
(34711,'enUS','We can finally connect your tower to the ley line network with this crystal.$B$BI also edited your blueprint so you can actually read the thing. Should make building another one much easier.',0),
(34712,'enUS','With this crystal, we can connect your tower to the ley line network at last!$B$BI also made some modifications to your blueprint that should make it much easier to build another tower in your garrison.',0),
(34716,'enUS','Please forgive me. I\'m in no condition to stand, commander.',0),
(34717,'enUS','That bit of justice is sure to have lifted the spirits of my rangari.$B$BLosing Telaar and many of our friends has taken a heavy toll.$B$BThank you, commander.',0),
(34718,'enUS','Khan! No!... he just received his promotion. His whole life ahead of him and now, nothing.$B$BThank you for getting the others out. Light be... nevermind.',0),
(34719,'enUS','Thank you for this kindness, $n. Perhaps I can still salvage some scrap of honor.',0),
(34720,'enUS','That bit of justice is sure to have lifted the spirits of my rangari.$B$BLosing Telaar and many of our friends has taken a heavy toll.$B$BThank you, commander.',0),
(34721,'enUS','I am Seer Malune, the great keeper of memories. It is an honor to finally meet you.',0),
(34722,'enUS','You did well against a coordinated Thunderlord attack, $n.',0),
(34729,'enUS','You have done me a great service. This blade is as much yours as it is mine.$B$BI offer you this blood oath: I shall serve your cause and lend my knowledge of blades and mining to your forces.$B$BWill you accept it?',0),
(34730,'enUS','Commander $n, Your mastery over the battlefield is astounding. If my people are to survive the coming conflict we will need more of our own people skilled in such warfare.$B$BIf you will have me, I would like to join your forces for a time. I wish to learn from you so that I might teach others in my clan.$B$BWill you accept my axe?',0),
(34731,'enUS','My sista have other duties, but I have leave of ol\' Vol\'jin to extend my services to you.$B$BYa proved your worth, and did a task that needed doing.$B$BI be followin\' ya, boss-mon, if ya be willing.',0),
(34732,'enUS','Well, hero, I owe you both my life and my honor. I ask that you allow me to repay this debt by serving under your command.$B$BYou will find that I am a fearsome hunter. I have also mastered the art of riding the rylaks, which few among the Frostwolves can claim.$B$BWill you accept my service?',0),
(34733,'enUS','Gonna have to ask demself, \"Did Dagg get catched or did Dagg catched dem?\"$B$BBig hero been blowin\' Dagg\'s cover! But you special, Dagg tinks. Dagg is master of dis guys and want to join you.$B$BDagg is unanimous in dis.',0),
(34736,'enUS','Eh dere, boss-mon! Watch ya step. Da ground be cracklin\' and breakin\' everywhere.',0),
(34737,'enUS','Well done.$B$BBe ready to move. We may have had the element of surprise within this cave, but our advantage is fleeting.',0),
(34739,'enUS','You fight exceptionally well, $n... better than I could ever hope to.$B$BWith those orcs out of the way, Khadgar and Maraad should now be able to safely guide the rest of our group through the cave.',0),
(34740,'enUS','Up there - that is Keli\'dan the Breaker. No doubt he\'s been alerted to our presence, and he\'s attempting to tell his warlord about our little jailbreak.$B$BWe have to take him out, $n.',0),
(34741,'enUS','Fine job in the cave, but this is no time to rest.$B$BWe have momentum. We must stay in motion.',0),
(34746,'enUS','Perfect! You retrieved the blueprints.$B$BThere\'s only one thing left to do.',0),
(34747,'enUS','I am without a clan. The Burning Blade are dead to me. Perhaps someday I will create a clan of my own.$B$BIn the meantime, it would be an honor to fight at your side. You freed me and fought well.$B$BThere is much we could learn from each other. What do you say?',0),
(34751,'enUS','Yeah, that\'s the stuff! You\'re a good business partner, considering you\'re a $C and all.$B$BNow let\'s just mash these into this port...',0),
(34756,'enUS','How very noble of you to act as bait on my behalf. I will not forget this.',0),
(34758,'enUS','Time to see what you can do.',0),
(34761,'enUS','Those look perfect! By all that is mechanical, this had better work.$B$BNow let\'s just insert these here...',0),
(34765,'enUS','Little known fact, old gronn grottos make for great farming soil.',0),
(34766,'enUS','I never doubted you for a moment. You are truly a commander of the people.$B$BLok\'tar ogar!',0),
(34769,'enUS','This is a momentous occasion, commander. I\'ll have Thaelin and his people get to work right away.$B$BYou\'ll see; this decision is going to be critical in our efforts against the Warsong.',0),
(34770,'enUS','I am without a clan. The Burning Blade are dead to me. Perhaps someday I will create a clan of my own.$B$BIn the meantime, it would be an honor to fight at your side. You freed me and fought well.$B$BThere is much we could learn from each other. What do you say?',0),
(34773,'enUS','Oh thank goodness, I knew ye would come through!$B$BAt your service, as always.',0),
(34774,'enUS','You will accept this gift, and you will like it. To do otherwise will automatically engage my organic incineration weapons. Thank you.',0),
(34775,'enUS','As additional missions come to my attention I will make them available here.',0),
(34776,'enUS','Thank you, $n. I am truly in your debt.$B$BWhen I fulfill my duties to Lady Liadrin I will come find you.',0),
(34777,'enUS','You have my eternal gratitude, hero. I will find a way to repay you someday.',0),
(34778,'enUS','You made it!$B$BBut... one of our wagons didn\'t. Have you seen Maraad? He\'s still out there somewhere.',0),
(34779,'enUS','I am keeping the sickles. They remind me of a lesson so many of us draenei forget - that the Light lives in every farmer as much as in any priest.$B$BYou fight well, and I am pleased to call you friend. Your laborers will be safe here in Elodor. If you are not convinced, speak to Exarch Hataaru here. His devices secure all the draenei strongholds.',0),
(34780,'enUS','The console thrums with energy and lights up as you draw near, as though sensing your presence. Simply touching the main panel brings the defense crystal to life outside.$B$BIf this is the kind of technology Hataaru was able to cobble together from spare parts, you can only imagine the splendor of the world he came from.',0),
(34781,'enUS','You saved the town! The controls shut down as you approach, but many of the indicators are still blinking frantically. Something seems wrong.$B$BHataaru yells out to get your attention outside...',0),
(34782,'enUS','<Exarch Othaar is a towering, intimidating figure. His eyes bore into you, determining if you are friend or foe.>$B$BSo, you are $n, esteemed $C of this \"Alliance\" that has appeared on our shores. On behalf of the Exarch Council, I welcome you to Elodor.',0),
(34783,'enUS','$n! You have only just arrived but already your name is the talk of Elodor.$B$BI will gladly support your cause for the Exarch Council - it has always been my opinion that the draenei need to get out and be proactive in our world instead of hiding behind our walls.$B$BBut first, I need your help with something...',0),
(34784,'enUS','Careful with those... hand them here. Wonderful!$B$BI will have my rangari bury these around the perimeter of Elodor. If the Shadowmoon orcs dare attack us again, they are in for a nasty surprise!$B$BDraenor is a hostile world, but if we take the time to learn and understand it, we can turn it to our advantage.$B$BI will finish up here and meet with the Exarch Council shortly. I will be sure to back your proposal.',0),
(34785,'enUS','Ah, $n! I suspected I would see you again soon.$B$BI am willing to speak on your behalf at the Exarch Council, but an emergency situation has come up...',0),
(34786,'enUS','<The artificer withdraws a loop and peers intently at the scales you\'ve brought him.>$B$BUnreal. The crystalline matrix is flawless, as if produced from one of our forges on Argus.$B$BI wish we could hook up these creatures to our machinery... but I suspect the Exarch would take issue with that.$B$BThank you for your help!',0),
(34787,'enUS','$n, my Alliance friend from Tanaan! I have not forgotten my debt to you.$B$BI will do everything in my power to convince the council to support you in every way possible. However...$B$B$B$BI have grave concerns about our safety here.',0),
(34788,'enUS','An excellent choice! We\'ll send your pick directly to your garrison to help with any missions you encounter.$B$BNow, about those supplies you requested...',0),
(34789,'enUS','One of the five Exarchs is dead. Another is a traitor. Dark times.$B$BWe will end this here and now. Can I count on you for one final task?',0),
(34790,'enUS','Would you look at that - the entire tentacle is barbed. Uggh. No wonder the wounds they inflict tend to get infected. We could learn something from this. I wonder if rangari explorers should start equipping themselves with whips?$B$BThank you, $n. This Alliance that you come from must be quite the collection of heroes!',0),
(34791,'enUS','Dead! Exarch Hataaru is dead! His body was discovered moments ago, stabbed in the back. The weapon that killed him was fel in origin. Tell me everything you know.$B$B<Maladaar nods as you describe what you found.>$B$BYes. The traitors wanted to capture Hataaru\'s soul. Someone wants something he knows, dead or alive... We must act at once.',0),
(34792,'enUS','<The Exarch listens to your tale, his face contorting into concern, grief, and finally anger.>$B$BSo Othaar has lost his way. \"Socrethar\" he calls himself now. At last we have our answer. I fear my capture at the hands of the Iron Horde was his doing. There may be other traitors amongst us - I must hurry back to Auchindoun and make sure we are safe.$B$BIn the meantime, I believe the Exarchs owe you a decision...',0),
(34794,'enUS','They came at us... from... nowhere.$B$B<The stoneguard nearly passes out.>',0),
(34795,'enUS','Commander $n. It\'s good to see you. We have much to discuss.$B$BThe situation in Nagrand is rapidly deteriorating. The Warsong clan is on the move.$B$BTo make matters worse, Grommash has named Garrosh their new warlord.',0),
(34801,'enUS','Thank you, stranger.',0),
(34802,'enUS','Thank you, a thousand times thank you.',0),
(34803,'enUS','For $n! For the Horde!',0),
(34804,'enUS','Victory! For the Alliance!',0),
(34805,'enUS','Blasted things. Nothing more than flying rats if you ask me!',0),
(34808,'enUS','I knew it was a mistake to bring these guys with me from the Valley of Trials.',0),
(34809,'enUS','<The Gold-O-Matic 9000 crunches and grinds through the elemental remains.>$B$Bchakk-chackk-chak-chak, chak-a-chak-akk-chk-chk-chk.',0),
(34810,'enUS','It\'s good to see that there\'s still an interest out there in real archaeology!$B$BThere\'s a lot of misconceptions out there about how archaeology is really done, but have no fear! The great and famous Gazmolf Futzwangler is here to educate you.',0),
(34811,'enUS','Great work, $n!$B$BThat bunch of good-for-nothing\'s came crying when they found out someone else was making their money! I don\'t think Thazwix, or his cronies, will be much trouble from here on out.$B$BAs promised, here\'s the pay I owe you for a job well done!',0),
(34814,'enUS','I am Magister Krelas. Pyromaniac.$B$BPleasure.',0),
(34815,'enUS','Nice to meet you.$B$BI am Magister Serena. Frost mage extraordinaire!',0),
(34818,'enUS','Who are you?$B$BDon\'t you know death by sight, $C?',0),
(34819,'enUS','You got them all? I just know this is going to work.',0),
(34820,'enUS','This is one of the pack mules Shelly and her crew took to Gloomshade Grove.',0),
(34822,'enUS','Hey... now that is some nice salvage. Say what you will about the Iron Horde, but they got some serious raw materials to work with.',0),
(34823,'enUS','Well done, boss-mon. The Bladespire ogres been pullin\' back their raiding parties. But ya can bet dey be comin\' back, and in larger numbers. The threat from their citadel must be dealt with soon.',0),
(34824,'enUS','Yeah, that\'s the stuff. Lumber, stone, peons, more peons. It\'s like we are building you a stronghold or something.',0),
(34826,'enUS','A great victory over the Burning Blade!$B$BThis new Warlord Azuka Bladefury sounds formidable. We will have to keep an eye on her and her blademasters.',0),
(34827,'enUS','Hm, not what I was expecting when I heard that Iskar was sending help.$B$BNo matter. You\'ll have to do.',0),
(34828,'enUS','Hmm... something\'s not right. She\'s been tampered with.$B$BSomeone else has used my orb to enter the realm of shadows.',0),
(34829,'enUS','Blood for blood, as it should be.',0),
(34830,'enUS','Well, you are not stabbing me yet.$B$BThat is a good sign.',0),
(34836,'enUS','Lunarblossoms! You are too kind! I can\'t wait to give these to Kat\'la.',0),
(34837,'enUS','I crafted a few things before we left that we may need: some bombs, a grappling hook, even was able to get one of the goblins to get a spare rocket pack.$B$BI\'m sure we\'ll find a use for everything.',0),
(34838,'enUS','<The hatchling springs immediately to flight, then looks at you expectantly and cheeps.>',0),
(34840,'enUS','Now that we\'re inside we have much to do.',0),
(34847,'enUS','Aka\'Magosh, $C. I knew that void witch was no good.',0),
(34849,'enUS','If you can defeat Luhk, then perhaps there\'s some hope for you after all.',0),
(34850,'enUS','I don\'t expect you to understand the importance of what you\'ve done.$B$BPerhaps one day you will.',0),
(34855,'enUS','Now with the viziers gone the whole Gordunni enchantment trade with the Iron Horde will come crashing down!$B$BWe can now turn our attention to dealing with Morkurk.',0),
(34858,'enUS','Thank you, commander. With this another stain on my honor has been removed.',0),
(34860,'enUS','Alright, that should be the last one we need. $B$BNothing feels as good as knowing you are stronger than your enemy!',0),
(34861,'enUS','Commander, it is an honor to serve you.',0),
(34866,'enUS','You made it. Good.$B$BGetting in here was nothing compared to what\'s to come.',0),
(34867,'enUS','Gorgrond is no place for armies, commander. We are now stepping into the domain of legends.',0),
(34868,'enUS','The garrison blueprints. Outstanding.$B$BThere\'s only one thing left to do.',0),
(34869,'enUS','It sure doesn\'t smell like chicken!$B$BOkay, okay, hand it over. I\'ll feed them and then everyone will be happy and I can turn a tidy - er, um... they\'ll feel better.$B$BYeah.',0),
(34870,'enUS','Fine work commander! Your combat skills are clearly second to none. I am honored to be your armorer!$B$BLet\'s get back to the outpost so we can take stock of our new inventory. I saved a few flares to call us in a ride back.',0),
(34874,'enUS','Your forces burn with passion for your cause.$B$BNot easy against such towering foes. Well done.',0),
(34875,'enUS','Now we can tackle getting that artificial nexus for your tower.',0),
(34876,'enUS','Hmm... I\'m sure one of these toads is my husband.',0),
(34877,'enUS','Excellent. I doubt they will rebuild it after we\'ve completed all of our objectives here.$B$BThis place will return to being a failing outpost for the Gorian Empire.',0),
(34878,'enUS','My apologies for teleporting away. It\'s cheating, I know.$B$BI merely wanted to put a fire under your feet to get here quickly!',0),
(34879,'enUS','Before we take on Morkurk we have some business to attend to in the fortress proper.',0),
(34881,'enUS','You have done well.$B$BAlthough the Elemental Plateau is no longer stable, the cycle of rebirth will soon take place and the elements will be born anew.',0),
(34882,'enUS','He was a big boy, wasn\'t he? The fiends will make quite a feast of him.',0),
(34883,'enUS','Good. With this much dust we can delve deep enough to reach the Talon King\'s refuge.',0),
(34884,'enUS','I see. Well, at least the gavel is safe.$B$BAs you may have guessed, it is another of the Talon King\'s relics.',0),
(34885,'enUS','Shame about Skizzik\'s aviary. That\'s where Percy came from. Skizzik wasn\'t interested in the \"runts\" after he started breeding the big ones full-time.$B$BTo be honest, I never liked those monstrous things.',0),
(34886,'enUS','<You hold the handful of grubs out, steel yourself, and prepare to chew them up as a mama bird would.$B$BThankfully, Ikky snatches them from your hand before you can proceed.$B$BApparently kaliri don\'t do that.>',0),
(34887,'enUS','Yes, these will definitely be useful! Trust me.',0),
(34888,'enUS','Now that they\'re out of the way, Morkurk is exposed.',0),
(34889,'enUS','There\'s nothing Morkurk can do to stop us now.$B$BWell done indeed!',0),
(34890,'enUS','That\'s what we were after.$B$BLet\'s get out of here!',0),
(34891,'enUS','You have done well, $n.$B$BBy linking with each of the four elemental pillars you have attuned your life energy with each of the elements on Draenor.$B$BYou are now ready to undertake the Ritual of Binding.$B$BSpeak to me when your work upon the Elemental Plateau is finished, and we shall begin.',0),
(34893,'enUS','Each of the guardians you put to rest were once mighty and noble elemental spirits.$B$BIn time each shall be reborn anew through the cycle of rebirth, but Gordawg must be found and balance restored lest the plateau become unstable yet again.',0),
(34894,'enUS','This is a fine Ember Blossom that you have brought to me. I know the danger you faced to retrieve it and I thank you.',0),
(34897,'enUS','Thank you for the report, $n. We must keep a close eye on these southern wilds.',0),
(34898,'enUS','<Ikky cheeps at you excitedly.$B$BIt seems you\'ve made a new friend.>',0),
(34899,'enUS','This is a momentous occasion, commander. Thazz\'ril and his peons will get to work right away.$B$BYou\'ll see; this decision is going to be critical in our efforts against the Warsong.',0),
(34900,'enUS','You did it, $n! Mama, papa, and family. It brings a tear to my eye.$B$BHere, take this runty one. Now that I have the whole herd, this one\'s just an extra mouth to feed and won\'t fetch anything at market.',0),
(34908,'enUS','Let\'s not waste any time. Gordal Fortress awaits just up this hill.',0),
(34909,'enUS','They\'re not amazing, but I do think these have some worth to us.',0),
(34910,'enUS','Now that they\'re out of the way, Morkurk is exposed.',0),
(34911,'enUS','Destroying those wards was key to our success. Well done indeed!',0),
(34912,'enUS','Looks like Morkurk was no match for the two of us, huh?',0),
(34913,'enUS','We have the scroll of mass teleportation ready, but we can\'t use it just yet. We must take proper precautions to ensure our success.',0),
(34914,'enUS','Glad dat Aggra send ya, Commanda.$B$BDey situation is grim, an\' it\'s \'bout ta get grimma.',0),
(34915,'enUS','Oh, dat was fun. We workin\' nicely togetha, you an\' me, $n.',0),
(34916,'enUS','Dey movin\' onta a betta place. Samedi be sendin\' dem on all dey missions now.$B$BDank ya, $n.',0),
(34917,'enUS','Soon de shield gonna cover all of Telaar. Den we all be trapped inside togetha.$B$BDen we go kill de packleader.',0),
(34918,'enUS','I\'m sorry to hear about Kajassa\'s shadow hunters, but we couldn\'t afford to let the Warsong have Telaar.$B$BWith the death of Kargora and her pack, we\'re one step closer to the invasion of the Warsong\'s home, Grommashar.$B$BOne step close to justice.',0),
(34921,'enUS','Ah, you come to learn the truth of things.$B$BWe will need to test your dedication first, yes!',0),
(34922,'enUS','Ah! The copies of the ritual!$B$BPraise the Raven Mother!$B$BHand them to me but only one at a time. We must not risk summoning the light.',0),
(34923,'enUS','Your strength has given us time to rest and continue our rituals.$B$BMay the Raven Mother ever keep you in her shadow.',0),
(34924,'enUS','These poor ravens have avoided a horrible future in the Bloodclaw lands.$B$BWe will take far better care of them.$B$BThank you!',0),
(34925,'enUS','<Ga\'nar works his neck out of the shackle.>$B$BMuch better.',0),
(34932,'enUS','Challe, that iniquitous wretch!$B$BIf only I had proof of her treachery long ago, I would have ripped the villainous heart from her chest and crushed it beneath my foot!$B$BYou have brought me the truth as I asked, for that you have my thanks.',0),
(34938,'enUS','Let it be known that on this day the stranger has returned victorious from slaying the feared foe of the Flock!$B$BPraise the Raven Mother!',0),
(34939,'enUS','Yes, these will do nicely as an offering to the Raven Mother! May she feast upon our enemies!',0),
(34941,'enUS','Gar\'rok was a loyal keeper and a true friend. He will be missed, but so is the cycle of life on this world.$B$BIn time we will call a new keeper of the elements, and he will serve us as Gar\'rok did before him.',0),
(34942,'enUS','Excellent work. Ishaal and Zellek have already begun the rites.',0),
(34943,'enUS','Kalandrios sent you to me? I am honored.$B$BThe furies are wise, they know the burdens of my heart.$B$BYou may not know, but you have been sent to grant a last request to a dying shaman.$B$BFor this, I am grateful.',0),
(34947,'enUS','These orders appear to have come from Orgrim Doomhammer.',0),
(34948,'enUS','These orders appear to have come from Orgrim Doomhammer.',0),
(34949,'enUS','We\'ve had quite the journey in getting your tower burning bright. If it\'s agreeable to you, I\'d like to join your campaign.',0),
(34950,'enUS','An infernal machine.',0),
(34951,'enUS','Who are you?$B$BDon\'t you know death by sight, $C?',0),
(34952,'enUS','You done us a solid with them Burning Blade, lad, and we\'re not the forgettin\' kind.$B$BLet\'s celebrate o\'er a pint in an hour. Drinks are on me.',0),
(34953,'enUS','You done us a solid with them Burning Blade, lad, and we\'re not the forgettin\' kind.$B$BLet\'s celebrate o\'er a pint in an hour. Drinks are on me.',0),
(34954,'enUS','If you can defeat Luhk, then perhaps there\'s some hope for you after all.',0),
(34955,'enUS','I don\'t expect you to understand the importance of what you\'ve done.$B$BPerhaps one day you will.',0),
(34956,'enUS','You made it. Good.$B$BGetting in here was nothing compared to what\'s to come.',0),
(34957,'enUS','A great victory over the Burning Blade!$B$BThis new Warlord Azuka Bladefury sounds formidable. We\'ll have to keep an eye on her and her blademasters.',0),
(34958,'enUS','Mmm... yes... simple enough.$B$B<The dwarf flips through the pages and no longer seems to notice your presence.>',0),
(34959,'enUS','They will not use that machine to kill any more draenei. Thank you, $n.',0),
(34960,'enUS','Now this is some handy stuff. This weather has been cutting through our supplies of rope so quick we need something we can use to provide an alternative. Looks like you scored the jackpot.',0),
(34962,'enUS','You have done great work with Durotan, Draka, and Gazlowe.',0),
(34963,'enUS','You have done great work with Maraad, Yrel, and Thaelin.',0),
(34964,'enUS','Throm-Ka, $n. All is not right in Nagrand, it is good that you are here.',0),
(34965,'enUS','I fear that this disturbance is more dire than I had anticipated.$B$BWhatever it is...it threatens to unravel the elemental bonds that hold this world together.',0),
(34971,'enUS','The outpost is now fully up and running and we have enough material to outfit an army - your army!',0),
(34972,'enUS','It took a lot of hard work but we have made a beautiful arsenal here.$B$BSir, I\'ve been able to outfit your soldiers here with new equipment but I\'d like to do more.$B$BI\'d be deeply honored if you would let me work for you in your main garrison.',0),
(34976,'enUS','Now that we\'re inside we have much to do.',0),
(34977,'enUS','Alright, that should be the last one we need. $B$BIt isn\'t the same as retaking Shattrath, but knowing the Iron Horde won\'t be getting these supplies gives me a bit of satisfaction.',0),
(34978,'enUS','Thank you, commander. With this a great dishonor on the legacy of Shattrath has been removed.',0),
(34979,'enUS','Now with the viziers gone the whole Gordunni enchantment trade with the Iron Horde will come crashing down!$B$BWe can now turn our attention to dealing with Morkurk.',0),
(34980,'enUS','Fine work commander! Your combat skills are clearly second to none. I am honored to be your armorer!$B$BLet\'s get back to the outpost so we can take stock of our new inventory. I saved a few flares to call us in a ride back.',0),
(34981,'enUS','The outpost is now fully up and running and we have enough material to outfit an army - your army!',0),
(34982,'enUS','It took a lot of hard work but we have made a beautiful artillery tower here.$B$BSir, I\'ve been able to outfit your soldiers here with new equipment but I\'d like to do more.$B$BI\'d be deeply honored if you would let me work for you in your main garrison.',0),
(34987,'enUS','Woo hoo hoo haaaaa!',0),
(34991,'enUS','Tillik! Dear friend I\'m so glad you have returned! All of the acolytes missed your witty banter after the evening chants.$B$B<Iktis looks back towards you.>$B$BYes, now your great test is done. You have fulfilled the requirements of The Parchment of Dust!',0),
(34993,'enUS','We\'ve had quite the journey in getting your tower up to speed. If it\'s agreeable to you, I\'d like to join your campaign here.',0),
(34994,'enUS','Hmm... How am I going to package this?$B$BI have an idea!$B$B<Beezil writes Youngroot on a label and slaps it onto a bottle of adder oil.>$B$B< He throws the Youngroot in the bushes behind him.>$B$BPerfect!',0),
(34995,'enUS','That\'s what I\'m talking about! Great work out there, $n.',0),
(34996,'enUS','This new is disturbing to say the least. I\'m shocked the infestation has spread so quickly.',0),
(34998,'enUS','<Kurekk gazes at the orb.>$B$BIs that... what I think it is?$B$BWe must get this to the Talon Altar.',0),
(34999,'enUS','Excellent, excellent. Go ahead and drop those directly into the cauldron.',0),
(35000,'enUS','They have suffered a fate worse than death, but at least they are free.',0),
(35001,'enUS','<As the orb meets the altar, the nearby candles flare up.>',0),
(35002,'enUS','<Heaping the wings into the bowl, you hear a faint rustling of feathers from somewhere overhead.>',0),
(35003,'enUS','Ah... I feel their grasp slipping.$B$BThank you, mortal.',0),
(35004,'enUS','Weapons and zealotry do not make one strong.$B$BThey turned to Sethe because they were too weak to face death.',0),
(35005,'enUS','Great work, $n.$B$BDon\'t put away your weapon yet - now\'s when the REAL work begins.',0),
(35006,'enUS','I can never repay you for all you have done here today, $n.$B$BI am truly in your debt.',0),
(35007,'enUS','At last, our prayers to the Raven Mother have been answered!',0),
(35009,'enUS','You have done much to help my little nest of forgotten ones. The poor creatures are not quite sane but with their own kin hunting them I pity their plight.$B$BTheir flying kin, the Adherents you call them, would see the forgotten ones destroyed and my children made into slaves.$B$BThis I must not allow!',0),
(35010,'enUS','In the whispers of the Raven Mother, blessed she be, it was foretold in the Scroll of Order that upon calling for a sign that we would receive one within thirty minutes or less.$B$BThis is most fortunate, for we have already begun our preparations for her arrival and we have need of your assistance.',0),
(35011,'enUS','A bracelet? Interesting... rather plain looking...',0),
(35012,'enUS','Sethe has died twice, but his curse lives on. It seems we will never be rid of it.',0),
(35013,'enUS','That bracelet... I made it for father long ago.$B$BBefore the fall...',0),
(35014,'enUS','Good, you made it. I need your help.',0),
(35015,'enUS','That was close.$B$BIf that genesaur would have grown any larger we would have needed an army to destroy it.$B$BThank you for all your help.',0),
(35016,'enUS','This red slime covers everything, even the skulls of my hunters! I\'ll make a Skulltaker of you yet though, great work!',0),
(35017,'enUS','Hah! If he was that strong he\'d still be alive. Still it is good you did him honor. Did you take his skull by any chance?',0),
(35019,'enUS','Great work, $n.$B$BDon\'t put away your weapon yet - now\'s when the REAL work begins.',0),
(35021,'enUS','What\'s this? Let me check if it has a skull...',0),
(35022,'enUS','Now that the flame of the spirit torch is upon the pyres, the spirits of my ancestors have been insulated from the call of the void within Oshu\'gun.$B$BHowever, more must still be done if the spirits here are to rest peacefully.',0),
(35023,'enUS','Do not mourn the twisted echoes of the dead, they are merely the distorted reflections of once noble spirits.$B$BInstead, mourn the loss of those souls consumed by the dark void that grows within Oshu\'gun.',0),
(35024,'enUS','Golmash was a mighty warrior in life.$B$BFew orcs have been as honored by their clans and feared by their enemies as the great Giantslayer... the father of the Hellscream name. With the mighty spirit of Golmash Hellscream finally put to rest, the ancestral grounds may once again be a place of peace and reverence.$B$BYou have our thanks, $n.',0),
(35025,'enUS','Thank you, friend. I am in your debt.$B$BThis arrogant Iron Horde has made a dangerous enemy today.',0),
(35026,'enUS','<Nisha laps up the water.>',0),
(35027,'enUS','You take too long. Something calls to us deeper in there. Whatever it is, I will have its skull or die trying.',0),
(35029,'enUS','Yes, they smell... wonderful. These will help me find the power of this marsh and take it for my own.',0),
(35030,'enUS','These will aid me greatly. I must consume them and take their power. We are close to the end $n, I can feel it.',0),
(35031,'enUS','We are so close I can almost touch it! We will have to go deeper, much deeper!',0),
(35032,'enUS','<You hear Prophet Velen\'s voice in your mind.>$B$BGood work, $n! The barriers are down. We are on our way.',0),
(35033,'enUS','You have chosen a very unfortunate time to visit our camp, my friend.',0),
(35035,'enUS','Watch them burn!',0),
(35036,'enUS','That half-orc burned my toes!',0),
(35037,'enUS','They are enslaving gronn? This is an even bigger problem than it might seem.',0),
(35038,'enUS','Yes... we don\'t need their bones, but we do need their crystals.',0),
(35040,'enUS','Grulkor was crazy to think he could harness the power of those mushrooms, but then, most Laughing Skull are crazy.$B$BStill, not a complete waste of time.',0),
(35041,'enUS','It is good that you still have your wits about you. You do... have your wits about you?',0),
(35045,'enUS','This is a beautiful and well equipped structure. Thank you for allowing me to work here.$B$BI am positive with this place I can carry on my master\'s legacy. You will not regret this!',0),
(35050,'enUS','The rangari are stout survivalists. I knew they would not go down without a fight.$B$BThank you, $n, for your help in this. You have done us a great honor.',0),
(35055,'enUS','Well, that\'s one down, and about a dozen others to go. We best get a base goin\'. Sounds like we might be here a while.',0),
(35058,'enUS','Ah. I see you have found a creation of Draenor alchemy.',0),
(35059,'enUS','It\'s good to see you, commander. When I\'d heard about your garrison caravan being destroyed....$B$BWell, let\'s just say that I feared the worst.$B$BWhat word from Telaari Station?',0),
(35060,'enUS','Commander $n.$B$B$B$BTerms of surrender? Hmm... let me think.',0),
(35061,'enUS','Unfortunate, but I\'m glad you made it out of that trap alive.',0),
(35062,'enUS','If you hadn\'t gone to Lok-rath, our forces would have been decimated.$B$BI\'m sorry to hear they laid a trap for you. I guess you have a reputation now.',0),
(35063,'enUS','Well, that is one thing ta pick. Tell you what, you get this building up and running at full steam and I\'ll see if I can\'t adapt these blueprints to work for the space in your garrison.',0),
(35065,'enUS','I dread to think what the botani had intended to do with the corpses of our fallen.',0),
(35066,'enUS','These will do nicely, $n! Thank you!',0),
(35067,'enUS','Thank you, commander. I thought we were done for sure.',0),
(35068,'enUS','Regrettable, but I understand the pride of the Warsong. I would never surrender.',0),
(35069,'enUS','That\'s the beast\'s collar? I heard its howls all the way over here!',0),
(35070,'enUS','Excellent. I will send in some peacekeepers to quell any remaining problems.$B$BExarch Naielle may be right - perhaps I am too aggressive in adapting our technology to this world. Still, I will never quit. Our civilization must move forward!',0),
(35071,'enUS','These will do nicely, $n! Thank you!',0),
(35072,'enUS','These will do nicely, $n! Thank you!',0),
(35073,'enUS','These will do nicely, $n! Thank you!',0),
(35074,'enUS','These will do nicely, $n! Thank you!',0),
(35075,'enUS','These will do nicely, $n! Thank you!',0),
(35077,'enUS','Hey good job out there! I couldn\'t have done it any better myself.',0),
(35079,'enUS','Hey you got the dispensers going again.$B$BNice job pal!',0),
(35080,'enUS','Oh my gosh, this is way worse than I thought it was gonna be. I\'m really going to need a hand with getting these survivors out of here.$B$BGood thing I have you on the payroll.',0),
(35081,'enUS','That\'s how ye do it! As soon as my crew gets here we can start work.$B$BHere\'s your pay. Thanks for doing the job.',0),
(35082,'enUS','Good work, $n.$B$BOnce Gazwitz gets his team up here we can get the crewmen back to the Gearworks.',0),
(35083,'enUS','Dark shamanism is a dangerous practice, $n.$B$BIt is true that the void can be a source of terrible power, but it is the kind of power that comes at a price.$B$BThese woods are safer now that you have put an end to the rituals.',0),
(35084,'enUS','The gift of shamanism is not one to be taken lightly. When the gift is abused, the elements will rise up in indignation and smite the shaman.',0),
(35085,'enUS','The Shamanstone appears to be working, even from within the Twisting Nether.$B$BThere is much that needs to be done, $n. The monsters of the void are gathering upon Oshu\'gun and must be stopped, else they invade our realm.',0),
(35086,'enUS','The void lord must be stopped. Thanks to your effort, the tide of void creatures has waned... but if we are to defeat Invalidus we must act swiftly.',0),
(35087,'enUS','If those portals were to fully expand and open, the path would have been clear for the horrors of the Twisting Nether to march upon Nagrand.$B$BThe Warsong have been careless in their mad pursuit of power and glory.',0),
(35088,'enUS','With Invalidus destroyed and the Warsong rituals halted, the threat of the Twisting Nether has subsided.',0),
(35089,'enUS','Yea that\'s the stuff!$B$BNow I just need to connect the spark plugs and patch up a few holes and it\'ll be nearly in working order!',0),
(35090,'enUS','Great work $n!$B$BGive me some time and I\'ll have this thing ready to roll out!',0),
(35091,'enUS','Thank you, $n.$B$BThe less of those spore beasts around the safer we all are.',0),
(35093,'enUS','We saved everyone we could, $n. We were too late for the others... including my sister.$B$BProphet Velen is right. When it is asked of us, we ALL must fight. I promise this: I will never again let my loved ones suffer.$B$BNer\'zhul is close to calling down the Dark Star. We are the only ones who can stop him.',0),
(35095,'enUS','It\'s good to see you, commander. When I\'d heard about your garrison caravan being destroyed....$B$BWell, let\'s just say that I feared the worst.$B$BWhat word from Wor\'var?',0),
(35096,'enUS','Commander $n.$B$B$B$BTerms of surrender? Hmm... let me think.',0),
(35097,'enUS','Unfortunate, but you made it out of the trap alive and Lok-rath is dealt with.',0),
(35098,'enUS','If you hadn\'t gone to Lok-rath, our forces would have been decimated.$B$BI\'m sorry to hear they laid a trap you. You have a reputation now.',0),
(35099,'enUS','Thank you, commander. I thought we were done for sure.',0),
(35100,'enUS','Regrettable, but I understand the pride of the Warsong. I would never surrender.',0),
(35101,'enUS','That\'s the beast\'s collar? I heard its howls all the way over here!',0),
(35102,'enUS','We have a lot of basic arms here but I\'ll get them improved in no time.$B$BThanks for giving me this chance.',0),
(35103,'enUS','My apprentice... Inside... (She dies in your arms.)',0),
(35104,'enUS','What... happened? Where is my master?',0),
(35106,'enUS','My heart is furious with you for stealing my kill, but my mind knows that I did not have the strength to avenge my master myself. I will forgive you, if you allow me to pay my debt of honor.',0),
(35128,'enUS','Most people cannot handle ogron in single combat.',0),
(35129,'enUS','We have the notes. Let us see what they reveal about our enemy\'s strategy.',0),
(35136,'enUS','Good work, $n. We can use this artifact against the Iron Horde when the time is right.',0),
(35137,'enUS','Now that we have the trainers, we can start training your forces to do something other than chop lumber. Heh heh.',0),
(35139,'enUS','Good. We know where we must go to acquire the artifact.',0),
(35140,'enUS','Outstanding.$B$B<Vindicator Yrel beckons you closer so that the two of you can conspire.>',0),
(35141,'enUS','Wait a minute, $n... let\'s be reasonable. I can hear what\'s in that carrier.$B$BIt was just a harmless prank.$B$BDon\'t do it, please!$B$BStop!$B$BDon\'t open that carrier!',0),
(35142,'enUS','The peons will clean this mess, Commander. Rubble and holes everywhere. The rest of us will look for hiding goren so that we may apologize to them for butchering their warleader.',0),
(35143,'enUS','A great victory over the Burning Blade!$B$BThis Flamebender Ka\'graz sounds formidable. We shall have to keep an eye on her and her blademasters.',0),
(35144,'enUS','The pale have been taught by Cho\'gall to enslave the elemental spirits of this land. When an elemental is enthralled in this manner, it cannot be reversed even by a Farseer such as myself.',0),
(35145,'enUS','I have encountered evil in many places, $n. Even deep within my own soul, I have seen dark shadows of what could be.$B$BHowever, the evil within the hearts of the Pale defies explanation. It is dark, loathing, and miserable in a way I have never encountered.',0),
(35146,'enUS','Your timely arrival to rescue me from the podlings was most appreciated!$B$BThis research station has seen better days... my equipment and belongings were damaged in the ambush.$B$BHowever, with your aid, I\'m sure we\'ll be up and running again in no time!',0),
(35147,'enUS','<Sallee Silverclamp examines the fragments you\'ve retrieved>$B$BThese will do nicely! Great work, kiddo!',0),
(35148,'enUS','I\'m afraid we have some trouble.',0),
(35150,'enUS','I\'m honored you\'re here to help, wolf-brother. Things here are worse than we thought.',0),
(35151,'enUS','A fine choice. It will need more work before such a structure could be built in your garrison, but this is a start.',0),
(35152,'enUS','Kash\'drakor is coming here?! Ha! I once saw him cut through a dozen Laughing Skulls because they had his son.$B$BHe is the purist expression of destruction.',0),
(35154,'enUS','Nice job, $n! Let\'s get this mining operation started!',0),
(35155,'enUS','Great! They are pretty scared now. Its hard to do research when you are afraid of being stabbed in the back at any time!',0),
(35156,'enUS','Burning magical paper smells pretty bad! Good thinking $n, keeping these ogres dumb is a solid plan!',0),
(35157,'enUS','Finally some help! I barely got out alive!$B$BYou have some ogre orders? Let me see...$B$BWell that\'s not good news.',0),
(35158,'enUS','We stopped him for the time being, but I think we\'ll have to come up with a more permanent solution. No doubt he\'s back in Highmaul plotting new versions of Breakers.$B$BI think a visit to ogre capital is far overdue.',0),
(35159,'enUS','Good, hopefully they will give up on making a portal here.',0),
(35166,'enUS','Wow... with all these supplies, we should be back on track.$B$BWe are blessed to have you protecting us, commander.',0),
(35167,'enUS','Skytooth! My mama and papa....$B$B<The little girl continues to cry over the corpses of her family.>',0),
(35168,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(35169,'enUS','It\'s over. The Warsong are broken. Garrosh Hellscream is finally dead.$B$BSomehow, I sense it\'s only a matter of time before Grommash seeks vengeance.',0),
(35170,'enUS','Thank you, commander. You really are the greatest $C like everyone says!',0),
(35171,'enUS','It\'s over. The Warsong are broken. Garrosh Hellscream is finally dead.$B$BIt\'s just a matter of time before Grommash seeks vengeance.',0),
(35172,'enUS','We look forward to serving you again.',0),
(35174,'enUS','This is unnerving to say the least.$B$BThose things must have come from underground.$B$BHopefully we have seen the last of them.',0),
(35176,'enUS','You did what? You are a life saver, commander.$B$BWith those tasks out of the way my job will be much easier.',0),
(35185,'enUS','Greetings, $C. Khadgar told me to expect you.',0),
(35186,'enUS','Greetings, $C. Khadgar told me to expect you.',0),
(35187,'enUS','Welcome, my friend. I have managed to earn a bit of favor with the Sargerei, but they still guard their secrets closely.$B$BOnly the strongest will be accepted in the ranks of the Sargerei.$B$BSoulpriest Zamaya is the leader of our operations here. To secure our objectives, you must first win her trust.',0),
(35188,'enUS','I expect no less from an initiate.',0),
(35189,'enUS','I see... Socrethar is purely mad, but his reasoning is logical. No wonder so many draenei are turning to his cause.',0),
(35190,'enUS','Not bad.',0),
(35191,'enUS','Very good. Our mission continues, undetected.',0),
(35194,'enUS','<Mysteriously, Anchorite Laanda is gone. Did something happen here?>',0),
(35195,'enUS','<Anchorite Laanda looks pale. He is not going to make it.>$B$B$n... thank you for all that you have done.',0),
(35196,'enUS','I see... Socrethar\'s ambitions begin with Shattrath and Auchindoun, but they do not end there.$B$BThank you for bringing this information to me, $n.$B$BI will relay it to Archmage Khadgar immediately.',0),
(35197,'enUS','I see... Socrethar\'s ambitions begin with Shattrath and Auchindoun, but they do not end there.$B$BThank you for bringing this information to me, $n.$B$BI will relay it to Archmage Khadgar immediately.',0),
(35202,'enUS','Ahh, yes. Xuk is one step closer to performing a miracle.',0),
(35204,'enUS','Keep this up and we\'ll make a survivalist out of you yet.',0),
(35205,'enUS','Normally I\'m not a violent dwarf, but I ain\'t about to sit by and get turned into a bush. And I ain\'t about to let others do the same.',0),
(35206,'enUS','Well done, commander. At every turn you seem to demonstrate an efficiency with war that even our most seasoned exarchs might fight to be challenging.',0),
(35207,'enUS','Me mother always told me to eat me vegetables. I dunna think this is what she had in mind.',0),
(35208,'enUS','Ah! It was terrible! They made me eat an\' eat an\' eat.$B$BDon\' get me wrong, I enjoy a good meal but these plant people had me eatin\' nuthin\' but fruit.$B$BI canno\' take it anymore.',0),
(35209,'enUS','You are carrying something of great power on you. I could feel it as you approached.',0),
(35210,'enUS','Those goren tunnels have proven useful.',0),
(35211,'enUS','Good work!$B$BOk I need to just finish setting up the ignition mechanism and we\'ll be all set.',0),
(35212,'enUS','Ah good! Ya made it.$B$BThe lasses here insisted on comin\' with, though they don\'t seem to like each other much.',0),
(35213,'enUS','The plant people fattened up my friends with fruit an\' honey an\' mead. Seems they were fattenin\' them up for sure.',0),
(35214,'enUS','I thank you for doing what I could not.$B$BWhile it is the right thing to do, it is hard to loose the arrow when your target was once a friend.',0),
(35215,'enUS','They mulched my friends? Those pointy branch wavers with their wee beady eyes! Thank ya for avenging ma friends.$B$BWe best be findin\' the others before they get turned into plant food.',0),
(35216,'enUS','I may not know much about farmin\' but I do know a power source when I see it. These seeds are packin\' quite a punch.$B$BWay to think on yer feet and grab \'em, Commander.',0),
(35217,'enUS','Excellent! I admit I love the taste of those pears as well, but it is a small price to pay to destroy our enemy.',0),
(35218,'enUS','These orders are written with terrible handwriting.',0),
(35225,'enUS','Co... Commander? Well ain\'t you a sight for sore eyes?$B$BI didn\'t think anyone friendly was comin\' for me.$B$BWe found an artifact that seemed pretty handy against the locals in the area but then those acid-mouthed roly polies showed up and started eatin\' everything.$B$BHelp me up an\' we can git to it.',0),
(35226,'enUS','Orgrim will not stop this foolishness, so we must stop him.',0),
(35227,'enUS','Another successful negotiation.',0),
(35229,'enUS','You give me blackrock orcs, troggs, er evil leper gnomes an\' we\'d be fine. But these acid munchin\' beasts are the end of us.',0),
(35231,'enUS','The situation here is dire, $n, but I sensed that we would meet again.$B$BI do not hear the call of the void as loudly as the others, for I am not long dead and my body rests far from this place.$B$BWith time though, that will change.$B$BIf you are here to help, listen closely for time is short.',0),
(35232,'enUS','It has been many years since I have set foot within these woods.$B$BI was last here for the Kosh\'harg many years ago when this place was shared amongst all clans. Those days have past and now only the Warsong banner flies here.',0),
(35233,'enUS','While I hope we don\' need to fire the big gun, I kinda hope we can fire the big gun.',0),
(35234,'enUS','That artifact was useful until it ran out of juice. Hopefully you got some seeds and water for it.',0),
(35235,'enUS','That was a challenge.',0),
(35240,'enUS','Well done, $n.$B$BGiven, they are injured, half-starved, and poorly-equipped... but there is no blade so sharp as a vengeful spirit, no armor so thick as a righteous cause.',0),
(35241,'enUS','I admire your sense of duty, $n. Even when your own survival hangs in the balance, you still find time to bring closure to a grieving widow. Well done.',0),
(35242,'enUS','I admire your sense of righteousness, $n. Even when your own survival hangs in the balance, you still find time to avenge a grieving widow. Well done.',0),
(35243,'enUS','I was bidden to find my way to you, and to swear my service. Whatever you need of me, I will offer. I take a particular pleasure in turning things to ashes.$B$BThe dark lady sends her regards.',0),
(35245,'enUS','Lithic actually spoke to you? Or, some shade of her at least... $B$BFascinating!',0),
(35247,'enUS','The spirits of my ancestors have betrayed me! Their skulls are surely laughing.',0),
(35248,'enUS','I like killing things. And bones.',0),
(35249,'enUS','You look like you can fight. We need to get out of here!',0),
(35251,'enUS','This camp of yours could be fruitful, but it rests upon the footstep of Grom\'gar. The Thunderlords are not likely to be welcome neighbors.',0),
(35254,'enUS','Already I can feel the Light triumphing over darkness. We\'ve done it!',0),
(35255,'enUS','Well done, Commander. Many of the orcs have tried to master the power of the genesaur but I have never heard of any of them reaching this level of success.$B$BThis should provide us a substantial advantage in the days ahead.',0),
(35257,'enUS','Ah yes, you\'ve arrived just in time.',0),
(35258,'enUS','Excellent. With these we can begin to understand.',0),
(35259,'enUS','<The core of this slumbering construct begins to hum softly.>',0),
(35260,'enUS','Deception is the ultimate power. Remember this, $n.',0),
(35261,'enUS','<The Apexis interface slides into place with a satisfying click. Seems this is the seat for taking full command of the turret.$B$BRifling through the cushions, you find a few spare coins, which you pocket.>',0),
(35262,'enUS','Commander, your skills at survival are to be commended but they have many blind spots.$B$BYou need a rangari like myself to help your forces or Draenor is going to eat you up like a goren with a rock.$B$BWill you accept my offer?',0),
(35264,'enUS','That must of taken great effort to get back to us. You deserve this reward, friend.',0),
(35265,'enUS','<Farseer Drek\'Thar listens closely as you speak of your vision.>$B$BI see... these are truly dark days. Cho\'gall has invaded the heart of Oshu\'gun, draining the naaru of its life. He seeks to destroy the naaru, birthing a dark, void god in its place.$B$BCho\'gall must be stopped. Come, we must travel to the sacred mountain before it is too late.',0),
(35271,'enUS','<Blood Guard Ehanes looks over the attack plans.>$B$BHmm... I see. You have done well to retrieve these attack plans. With the plans in our hands, we will be more than prepared to counter the assault when it comes.',0),
(35272,'enUS','Thank da spirits you showed up. Dey hear my prayers.',0),
(35273,'enUS','Ahh, well done. Even with my condition, I could sense the carnage from here.$B$BIt must have been quite a show, kah-hah-haww.',0),
(35274,'enUS','Now, uh... could we maybe forget this little incident happened, commander?$B$BBodrick and the other agents would never let me live this down.',0),
(35275,'enUS','Our lives for your will, commander.',0),
(35276,'enUS','I hope everything is to your liking. It\'s been one hell of a job.',0),
(35277,'enUS','Your will be done.$B$BFor the Horde!',0),
(35285,'enUS','I have good news and bad news.$B$BThe good news is my uncle\'s alive! The bad news is his leg is injured and we\'re surrounded by infected! With my hotrod wrecked we can\'t get him out of here.',0),
(35286,'enUS','Praise the Light you\'re here. I thought we were going to have to wait until a courier could reach you for a decision on this.',0),
(35293,'enUS','What in the king\'s name happened here?',0),
(35295,'enUS','Everyone be dead, mon. What did dis?',0),
(35298,'enUS','$n, you did fantastic work.$B$BEveryone here at the Gearworks owes you big time for what you\'ve done for us.$B$BHere, I want to give you little something. Think of it as a personal token of my gratitude.',0),
(35317,'enUS','You have done well, $n.$B$BBy defeating the void god Decimatus, the destruction of this great valley has been avoided. The threat of the pale has subsided for now as well.$B$BThe loss of Gordawg will be felt throughout Nagrand, but someday a new earthen fury will take seat upon the Throne of Elements and balance will be restored.',0),
(35322,'enUS','Thank you, friend.',0),
(35329,'enUS','Thank you, friend.',0),
(35330,'enUS','<Vindicator Nobundo listens closely as you speak of your vision.>$B$BThese are grave images of which you speak, $n! If Cho\'gall continues bleeding the naaru of its Light, K\'ure will die and in the naaru\'s place a void god will emerge. Void gods are terrible creatures that live only to destroy!$B$BWe must travel to Oshu\'gun immediately and put a stop to the threat of Cho\'gall!',0),
(35331,'enUS','I am not sure what to make of this.$B$BThe elements are no longer in balance? The great fury Gordawg is missing and must be found?$B$BThe furies appear noble, and deep within my soul their words ring true.$B$BI believe we aid should them in their cause.',0),
(35332,'enUS','I am glad to see that you have arrived safely.$B$BCome, there is much work to be done here.',0),
(35333,'enUS','I see a fire within your eyes and a wind upon your step, $n.$B$BIf what Kalandrios speaks is true, you have attuned your life energy with each of the elemental forces on Draenor.$B$BThe voice says that you are now ready to undertake the Ritual of Binding.$B$BReturn to me when your work upon the plateau is finished and we will speak further.',0),
(35337,'enUS','Twelve pairs, huh? That\'s pretty good, commander.$B$BUm, no, I think that\'s about how many I managed to bag. Yeah... about a dozen pairs of ears. Yep....',0),
(35338,'enUS','Twenty-four, huh? That\'s fine work.$B$BI brought back fifty.$B$BI\'ll send someone out for the meat. Waste not, want not.',0),
(35339,'enUS','We\'re... dead?',0),
(35341,'enUS','You have proven yourself more powerful than my previous leaders. My service is yours.',0),
(35342,'enUS','Ah. I see you have found a creation of Draenor alchemy.',0),
(35343,'enUS','Please. Help me. I need to find my father.',0),
(35344,'enUS','Thank you, stranger. I don\'t think the razorfangs were happy that I was hunting the same prey.',0),
(35345,'enUS','You did this for my family? After you saved our father? Thank you, $n.$B$BYou wished to know about Draenor alchemy? I will do my best to share my knowledge with you.',0),
(35350,'enUS','Magnificent kill, commander. You\'ve done us all proud.',0),
(35353,'enUS','I will convince the others of our fate. There\'s no denying it anymore.',0),
(35356,'enUS','That\'s MY arrow! Where\'d you get it?',0),
(35357,'enUS','Well done, $n. You succeeded where I did not.$B$BPerhaps you outsiders aren\'t such bad hunters after all.',0),
(35372,'enUS','These woods are sacred to the orcs and to my people as well.$B$BBeneath the great mountain of Oshu\'gun lies the heart of Nagrand, the Genedar. This great dimensional vessel rescued my people from annihilation and brought us to this world.',0),
(35374,'enUS','Twelve pairs, huh? That\'s pretty good, commander.$B$BUm, no, I think that\'s about how many I managed to bag. Yeah... about a dozen pairs of ears. Yep....',0),
(35375,'enUS','Magnificent kill, commander. You\'ve done us all proud.',0),
(35376,'enUS','Twenty-four, huh? That\'s fine work.$B$BI brought back fifty.$B$BI\'ll send someone out for the meat. Waste not, want not.',0),
(35377,'enUS','That\'s MY axe! Where\'d you get it?',0),
(35378,'enUS','Well done, $n. You succeeded where I did not.$B$BPerhaps you outsiders aren\'t such bad hunters after all.',0),
(35380,'enUS','If today was any other day I\'d have you court-martialed for being out of uniform.',0),
(35386,'enUS','<Captain Washburn examines the attack plans, squinting at the lettering and holding the pages upside down.>$B$BHmm... I see... yes... indeed!$B$BThese are obviously attack plans, as you yourself have stated, but they are most likely written by kobold pyromancers.$B$BStrange though, I haven\'t seen any kobold pyromancers since my days in Azeroth. No matter! I assure you that the outpost is well armed and mostly fireproof!$B$BIf we are attacked, the outpost shan\'t fall. You have my word, commander!',0),
(35393,'enUS','The situation here is dire, $n, but I sensed that we would meet again.$B$BI do not hear the call of the void as loudly as the others, for I am not long dead and my body rests far from this place.$B$BWith time though, that will change.$B$BIf you are here to help, listen closely for time is short.',0),
(35395,'enUS','Gordawg was a mighty ally. The elements will mourn the loss of the fury, but death was the only answer. Gordawg would not have wished to stay a slave to evil.$B$BThough Gordawg is no more, the heart of a fury is eternal and unbreakable. In time, this brightly glowing heart will take shape into a new earthen fury.$B$BSuch is the cycle of life upon the Elemental Plateau.',0),
(35396,'enUS','The fate of K\'ure could not have been prevented.$B$BCho\'gall accelerated the naaru\'s transition into a void god in hopes of bringing destruction upon Draenor. Cho\'gall must be dealt with, but for now let us honor the memory of the great naaru K\'ure.$B$BK\'ure was truly the savior of my people, a friend to the virtuous, and a teacher of prophets.$B$BMay the great naaru ever live within our hearts.',0),
(35397,'enUS','The Pale are wretched creatures that hate the Light and plot against the innocent. Without Greyseer to lead them, they will be disorganized and in chaos for a time.$B$BShould a new leader arise from within their ranks, we shall smite them down once more.',0),
(35398,'enUS','You have done well to free the elemental spirits from their bonds. If Cho\'gall and the pale seek an army of elemental slaves, they must not be allowed to succeed.',0),
(35399,'enUS','Dead? All dead? Dead and mulched and forgotten. No Chag with his missing nose or Meka with her love for chewing faces.$B$BAnd Torg, my beloved Torg. A son we had together. A son that is still missing.$B$BThe botani will pay for this. They will burn for this.',0),
(35400,'enUS','These creatures... were not what I expected to see. I always knew Gorgrond to be a dangerous place, but I never could have guessed at how vile.$B$BThank you, commander, for your compassion in this.',0),
(35402,'enUS','It isn\'t enough to kill the botani. They will always have greater numbers.$B$BYou must cut them deep and hard, where it hurts them the most.$B$BLike slaying their most sacred leader.',0),
(35406,'enUS','Seeds. So simple to look at but in each the potential for untold amounts of destruction. Much like my son.$B$BYou were wise to take these.',0),
(35407,'enUS','Well fought. For the Alliance!',0),
(35408,'enUS','Good job, soldier.',0),
(35416,'enUS','Well done, Commander. Many of the orcs have tried to master the power of the genesaur but I have never heard of any succeeding.$B$BYou have won us a powerful weapon for the next time we face the Iron Horde.',0),
(35429,'enUS','Ah... yes, yes, yes. Fresh pollen. With a dash of a few secret ingredients you can feed an army with the food you could grow from this, if you know the secret ways.',0),
(35430,'enUS','The botani took my dad. They took my friends. And now they are making me eat fruit!$B$BWhy are they so mean?!$B$BDid you kill them all?$B$BI think you should kill them.',0),
(35432,'enUS','I had thought the Laughing Skull were planning something. Now I think I am beginning to understand.$B$BThey match savagery with savagery.',0),
(35433,'enUS','They are lucky you are the one that killed them. I would have tried to carve pictures in their dead wood bodies.',0),
(35434,'enUS','The Waters of Utrophis. I have never held or smelled or tasted it before. But I have heard many stories, many legends.$B$BI was expecting something more grand.',0),
(35444,'enUS','Thank you for coming to our aid.',0),
(35450,'enUS','Ah, Prelate Luari sent you, did she? Such a sweet woman, always looking out for others.',0),
(35459,'enUS','Thank you for coming to assist us.',0),
(35460,'enUS','Good form, champion. I\'m sure your presence on the field was inspiring for our troops.',0),
(35462,'enUS','It will take the Iron Horde quite a while to get those demolishers operational again. Excellent work, $n.',0),
(35463,'enUS','You killed how many scouts? No wonder we have been unable to execute our plans...',0),
(35464,'enUS','The prisoners are shaken up, but they are free. Their families are in your debt, $n.',0),
(35482,'enUS','From one commander to another... thank you.$B$BWe\'ve been through a lot together, haven\'t we, $n? Vashj\'ir... the Jade Forest... Lion\'s Landing...$B$BI am truly honored that I could end my journey by your side.',0),
(35486,'enUS','Let\'s take a look at these battleplans.',0),
(35487,'enUS','That was stinky.',0),
(35488,'enUS','It\'s important that our enemies understand what happens when you attack the Alliance. I\'m glad you could be there to show them.',0),
(35492,'enUS','The Iron Horde will learn to fear us, as they should.',0),
(35494,'enUS','Thank you, $n. These mementos will forever remind us of the day we lost so many of our loved ones.',0),
(35495,'enUS','Toothsmash is dead? Good, I\'m sure it will take the Iron Horde a while to find another ogre smart enough to help them with their efforts.',0),
(35496,'enUS','I wish I could be there to watch their faces as they suffer. I hope they all die a slow horrible death.',0),
(35500,'enUS','It was an honor fighting alongside of you, $n.',0),
(35501,'enUS','The rounds of doomshot fit into the weapon loader with ease.',0),
(35505,'enUS','Frenna didn\'t make it out of Tangleheart.',0),
(35506,'enUS','You got it! You should be able to use this mole machine one way back to your outpost.',0),
(35507,'enUS','Goren, goren, gone!',0),
(35508,'enUS','Hey, nice job commander!',0),
(35509,'enUS','The genesaur is coming!',0),
(35510,'enUS','It was an honor to fight by your side today, commander.',0),
(35511,'enUS','Commander, you go where you will and kill any who would stand in your way.$B$BI find this fun.$B$BI wish to join your... \"followers\"... as the lady wolf keeps calling them.$B$BMy home is crushed, my family mulched, and this place has lost its charm.$B$BLet me join you.',0),
(35524,'enUS','You saw \'em burn off their own leaves? That\'d be like me cutting off my cute-as-a-button pigtails!',0),
(35527,'enUS','Big baddy botani busted? Works for me!',0),
(35536,'enUS','You found my Cutter! I shall gladly cut a thousand throats in your honor.',0),
(35537,'enUS','Welcome back, boss-mon.$B$BI know you\'ll probably be wantin\' to get things settled here first, but there\'s been some word of an uprisin\' in Spires of Arak. There might be some allies to be made if we get involved.$B$BThought ya might want to know.',0),
(35549,'enUS','We will never forget Admiral Taylor\'s sacrifices for the greater good.',0),
(35550,'enUS','Ukambe gave me the report, commander. You truly are the champion of the Horde.',0),
(35552,'enUS','A flesh-bound book lies on an unholy altar. Your skin crawls. Maladaar was right!',0),
(35554,'enUS','Welcome back, commander.$B$BI know you\'ll probably want to get things settled here first, but there\'s been some word of an uprising in Spires of Arak. If we act fast, we might be able to make some new allies against the Iron Horde.$B$BI\'ll have the scouts keep an ear out for any more news. That\'s it for now, sir.',0),
(35556,'enUS','Welcome to Gorgrond, Commander. We only just arrived ourselves.',0),
(35557,'enUS','Gorgrond is no place for armies, Commander. We are now stepping into the domain of legends.',0),
(35596,'enUS','<Goldmane stretches happily after being cooped up in that tiny cage. He looks around and then at you expectantly. He motions at you gratefully, indicating he will follow you... for a while at least...>',0),
(35611,'enUS','Thank you for returning to us, $n. I must admit we are sorely in need of your help.',0),
(35614,'enUS','I have heard of you, traveler. Your people have come to defeat the Iron Horde.$B$BFrom what I have just seen, your combat skills are as impressive as they say.$B$BI, too, wish to see the Iron Horde gone from this land. I will lend you the strength of my hammer, and you may also find my knowledge of crystalworking to be useful.$B$BWhat do you say?',0),
(35617,'enUS','I have spoken with the rest of my caravan, and we\'ve agreed to rest our wagon for a while while I pledge my service to your garrison.$B$BI think I could be of great use to you. What do you say?',0),
(35619,'enUS','Hey, you\'re from that Alliance base right?$B$BGlad you made the trip because we really could use your help!',0),
(35620,'enUS','Hey, you\'re from that Horde base right?$B$BGlad you made the trip because we really could use your help!',0),
(35625,'enUS','Draenor... even the sound of this place makes me sick.$B$BMy husband is gone. I cannot go home while his memory lingers.$B$BPlease, let me join you and fight for you. Send me to the frontlines, wherever killing is needed.$B$BWith every enemy that I face, perhaps the pain will lessen.',0),
(35631,'enUS','Prophet Velen spoke highly of you, and I can see that your weapons are keen and your intent is just.$B$BI sense great potential within you. If you will allow it, I would warm my hands by your fire for a while.$B$BI would like to follow you and learn from your people. In return, I shall fight for you.$B$BWhat do you say, traveler?',0),
(35632,'enUS','Great work back there! That\'s how real archaeology is done!$B$BIt\'s a good thing you came to me to learn the trade, kid. You\'ve got talent and I\'d hate to see it wasted on a putz like Harrison Jones!',0),
(35633,'enUS','Thank you for doing this $n. Hopefully they can be cleaned of these foul spores that coat everything here.',0),
(35634,'enUS','It will take some time, but this may be the key to our victory.',0),
(35636,'enUS','<Reshad presses the feather into the tome before sliding it into his robes.>$B$BWe have one more stop before the wayshrine...',0),
(35638,'enUS','Every little bit helps.',0),
(35639,'enUS','Great work, $C! I will let Vindicator Maraad know of your bravery.',0),
(35640,'enUS','Thank you for avenging my fallen friends. We will get to the bottom of this I swear!',0),
(35642,'enUS','I\'ve seen these around on corpses and the beasts, but not as big. Let me see it...',0),
(35644,'enUS','Perhaps we shouldn\'t have wasted time on them, this place... drains me. Still it was a good deed you have done.',0),
(35645,'enUS','Sadly, I\'m growing used to the smell of these spores. In fact, they smell quite pleasant now. Perhaps if I eat these it will speed up our work here...',0),
(35647,'enUS','I... I must consume these like the mushrooms. It will help me locate the source, I swear!',0),
(35650,'enUS','Those ancients are crazy! Hard to believe they\'d burn off their own leaves.',0),
(35651,'enUS','Ya took out the big nasty did ya? Yer sure to be causin\' some real trouble out there!',0),
(35652,'enUS','Sap? Who called me a sap?! Oh...',0),
(35654,'enUS','Couldn\'t say what those spores were for, but I feel better knowin\' they\'re gone.',0),
(35656,'enUS','This is unfortunate... I had hoped... Still we are closer now, we are on the right track to finishing this.$B$BNone too soon either, the screaming beasts are really getting to me...',0),
(35659,'enUS','That is terrible news. I will warn off all scouts from venturing to the Crimson Fen from now on. Thank you and I am glad you were not affected by the spores...',0),
(35663,'enUS','You did a great job, kid!$B$BI hope you learned something about teamwork today. Here\'s your cut, minus my teaching fee... the Steamwheedle Preservation Society service charge... and gratuity of course!',0),
(35664,'enUS','The ancients should not be a problem for your outpost for some time.',0),
(35665,'enUS','Thank you, friend. I am in your debt.$B$BThis arrogant Iron Horde has made a dangerous enemy today.',0),
(35666,'enUS','D\'kaan sent you? He\'s not likely to enjoy the report I have to give him.',0),
(35667,'enUS','Marrow sent you, eh? Well we leave when I\'m done here.',0),
(35668,'enUS','<Reshad gazes into the inky orb.>$B$BAmazing. To think Terokk used this very orb to commune with Anzu. One could become quite the darkweaver with an implement such as this.$B$BCome, let\'s get it safely to the Veil.',0),
(35669,'enUS','The peons will sing songs of your glory, commander. Lok\'tar ogar!',0),
(35670,'enUS','I am glad we can count on you, commander.',0),
(35671,'enUS','We owe you a great debt for delivering Reshad safely to us, $n.$B$BHowever, our struggle has only just begun.',0),
(35672,'enUS','A thousand thanks to you, commander. I will call for more supply runs immediately.',0),
(35674,'enUS','Well done, commander. For the Alliance!',0),
(35675,'enUS','I didn\'t think anyone could actually kill the beast. Thank you, commander!',0),
(35676,'enUS','By Muradin\'sh beard... you actually killed the beasht. Praishe be to ye, commander ...hic!',0),
(35679,'enUS','I am glad to see you, $n. Your aid will be invaluable in this critical hour.',0),
(35680,'enUS','I am glad to see you, $n. Your aid will be invaluable in this critical hour.',0),
(35683,'enUS','Excellent. These insignias will surely bring Socrethar out of hiding.',0),
(35684,'enUS','Excellent. These insignias will surely bring Socrethar out of hiding.',0),
(35685,'enUS','Finally, it is done. Othaar... my old friend... be at peace now.',0),
(35686,'enUS','These creatures are relentless in their assault against one another.',0),
(35687,'enUS','Finally, it is done. This creature of darkness shall torment us no longer. Shattrath is free of his taint.',0),
(35689,'enUS','Every little bit helps.',0),
(35690,'enUS','That must of taken great effort to get back to us. You deserve this reward, friend.',0),
(35691,'enUS','Great work, $C! I will let Vindicator Maraad know of your bravery.',0),
(35693,'enUS','You have a true talent for combat.',0),
(35697,'enUS','I believe we can come to an arrangement, savior of Skettis. But first...',0),
(35699,'enUS','I believe we can come to an arrangement, savior of Skettis. But first...',0),
(35702,'enUS','Yes... Think of the orcs that will fall before us with this power...',0),
(35704,'enUS','Percy and I want to give you something as a token of our thanks. It\'s not much but please, take your reward.',0),
(35705,'enUS','I don\'t know what you\'re doin\' all the way out here, but mind helpin\' a gal out since you\'re stopping by?',0),
(35706,'enUS','You\'re a real doll. Let\'s get out of here.',0),
(35707,'enUS','Hey! Looky what I found here.',0),
(35708,'enUS','Cheers! I found a goblin skulkin\' about here. Think I\'ll keep \'er around. Says she knows things about lumberjackin\'.',0),
(35713,'enUS','You\'re armed to the teeth! Say, would you be interested in helping a weary gnome out?',0),
(35716,'enUS','You\'re a lifesaver! Let\'s get these to the excavation site.',0),
(35718,'enUS','Oh, Mixxy sent you? What a relief. I\'m not even armed!',0),
(35719,'enUS','Oh, thank goodness. I don\'t even have any weapons!',0),
(35730,'enUS','Thank you. Her wounds have closed.',0),
(35733,'enUS','<As you place the gavel at the base of the effigy, Reshad speaks over your shoulder.>',0),
(35734,'enUS','That was but one of many such tales.$B$BNo arakkoa living or dead has ever compared to the Talon King.',0),
(35736,'enUS','Excellent work. Your service is always appreciated, $n.',0),
(35737,'enUS','Excellent work. Your service is always appreciated, $n.',0),
(35738,'enUS','That ought to do it! Nice work.',0),
(35739,'enUS','That\'s... quite a bit of charcoal. Nicely done!',0),
(35744,'enUS','Da prisoners be shaken up, but they are free. We be in your debt, $n.',0),
(35745,'enUS','Aka\'Magosh, champion. I\'m sure your presence on the field was inspiring for the troops.',0),
(35746,'enUS','It will take the Iron Horde quite a while to get those demolishers operational again. Throm-Ka, $n.',0),
(35747,'enUS','This... I can work with this.',0),
(35748,'enUS','You killed how many scouts? No wonder we have been unable to execute our plans...',0),
(35750,'enUS','Let\'s take a look at these battleplans.',0),
(35751,'enUS','The Iron Horde will learn to fear us, as they should.',0),
(35760,'enUS','Toothsmash is dead? Good, I\'m sure it will take the Iron Horde a while to find another ogre smart enough to help them with their efforts.',0),
(35761,'enUS','Throm-Ka, $n. These mementos will forever remind us of our champions.',0),
(35762,'enUS','It\'s important that our enemies understand what happens when you attack the true Horde. I\'m glad you could be there to show them.',0),
(35763,'enUS','It was an honor fighting alongside of you, $n.',0),
(35764,'enUS','I wish I could be there to watch their faces as they suffer. I hope they all die a slow horrible death.',0),
(35766,'enUS','Well, I\'ll be. Ghosts. Who knew?',0),
(35782,'enUS','You\'re kidding! What a world.',0),
(35786,'enUS','With every victory, or claim here grows more strong.',0),
(35787,'enUS','Without each battle, or sovereignty here grows, Commander.',0),
(35788,'enUS','Our foes cringe, Commander. Hah! They\'ll lick their wounds for days before even dreaming of another fight.',0),
(35797,'enUS','Perfection. Let\'s get it hooked up!',0),
(35807,'enUS','One minute you are skirting the cauldrons avoiding the Gronn, the next a blast a steam followed by burning hot claws. Erosian\'s death should make our scouts lives a lot easier!',0),
(35808,'enUS','One minute you are skirting the cauldrons avoiding the Gronn, the next a blast a steam followed by burning hot claws. Erosian\'s death should make our scouts lives a lot easier!',0),
(35809,'enUS','You have defeated yet another deadly beast in Gorgrond.$B$BDessicus cared little on who he preyed upon, they all went into his salt pools forever. You have saved many lives $n!',0),
(35810,'enUS','You have defeated yet another deadly beast in Gorgrond.$B$BDessicus cared little on who he preyed upon, they all went into his salt pools forever. You have saved many lives $n!',0),
(35811,'enUS','I thought I felt less quakes in the earth. His fury caused untold damage to this world, it is good that he has fallen to you.',0),
(35812,'enUS','I thought I felt less quakes in the earth. His fury caused untold damage to this world, it is good that he has fallen to you.',0),
(35813,'enUS','I\'ve heard tales of the Crimson Fen from the rangari; no one has yet returned from there. If this was the reason then we can all breathe safer now.',0),
(35814,'enUS','I\'ve heard tales of the Crimson Fen from the Laughing Skull and how no one ever returns from there. If this is part of the reason, then we can all breathe safer now.',0),
(35815,'enUS','Our purpose here was hard enough without a giant beast like Charl harassing our scouts and aggravating the Gronn.$B$BGlory to you $n!',0),
(35816,'enUS','Our purpose here was hard enough without a giant beast like Charl harassing our scouts and aggravating the Gronn.$B$BYou have saved the rangari a great deal of punishment with this kill $n!',0),
(35817,'enUS','The calls of that giant bird could never be ignored.$B$BYou could never be sure if it was far away or if there would be a sudden shadow followed by your immediate death. Well done!',0),
(35818,'enUS','The calls of that giant bird could never be ignored.$B$BYou could never be sure if it was far away or if there would be a sudden shadow followed by your immediate death. Well done!',0),
(35819,'enUS','The Laughing Skull have always steered clear of that area because Khargax was very quick for such a huge beast. They will be pleased to know their eaten dead have been avenged.',0),
(35820,'enUS','You have done us all a great favor $n.$B$BThe existence of that slippery hydra wasn\'t even truly known despite our losses in the area.',0),
(35828,'enUS','Ah perfect. I\'ll get this up an\' runnin\' in no time.',0),
(35834,'enUS','A good start. The growth from a genesaur is pure chaos and must be culled whenever possible.',0),
(35835,'enUS','Alright, let\'s put this thing to use!',0),
(35837,'enUS','<Judging by the marks on her body, the agent put up an impressive fight.>',0),
(35838,'enUS','I\'m glad I found you, $n. I\'ve been hiding out since the Warsong orcs ambushed our camp at the Hidden Camp.$B$BYou should have seen the fight that Jeanine put up. Even after they began torturing her, she never gave up that there were two of us.$B$BShe had a will of steel, that one.',0),
(35839,'enUS','This is remarkable, $n. We now have direct proof of Grommash\'s intentions.$B$BPerhaps now, we can stay a step ahead of the Iron Horde. Great work!',0),
(35840,'enUS','Excellent work, $n.',0),
(35841,'enUS','I have heard many reports about Vor\'gash. It is a relief to know he will trouble us no more.',0),
(35842,'enUS','I know about dis Vor\'gash. It be a relief ta know he won\'t trouble us no more.',0),
(35843,'enUS','<Judging by the marks on his body, the shadow hunter put up an impressive fight.>',0),
(35844,'enUS','I ben lookin\' for ya, commanda. I knew you was comin\', but dat nasty orc lady got ta ya afore I could give warnin\'.$B$BAt least I could save ya. Poor Zasta. He never saw it comin\'.',0),
(35845,'enUS','Now we have proof a Hellscream\'s intentions.$B$BMebbe now, we ken stay a step ahead a da Iron Horde. Gud work.',0),
(35846,'enUS','Dis is gud, $n. Dis be real gud.',0),
(35861,'enUS','These savages have no honor, it is time we deal with the Iron Horde presence on this island.',0),
(35867,'enUS','Every little bit helps.',0),
(35868,'enUS','That must of taken great effort to get back to us. You deserve this reward, friend.',0),
(35869,'enUS','Great work, $C! I will let Vindicator Maraad know of your bravery.',0),
(35870,'enUS','<Nisha downs the meat in one gulp.>',0),
(35871,'enUS','Every little bit helps.',0),
(35872,'enUS','That must of taken great effort to get back to us. You deserve this reward, friend.',0),
(35873,'enUS','Great work, $C! I will let Grand Marshal Tremblade know of your bravery.',0),
(35876,'enUS','These savages have no honor, it is time we deal with the Iron Horde presence on this island.',0),
(35878,'enUS','Fantastic! This is some good old-fashioned adventuring if I\'ve ever seen it.',0),
(35879,'enUS','Now that\'s what I\'m talking about. You\'re tough as nails.',0),
(35880,'enUS','I can see the future of my enemies in the bones. They\'re gonna die!',0),
(35882,'enUS','Now THAT is how you break out of a gladiator pit!$B$BYou are fun. Your weapons are covered in a rainbow of blood types.$B$BI am going to follow you now.',0),
(35883,'enUS','For years the ogres would make me fight, kill, and salute. My soul bled with each salute.$B$BBut because of you, I will never again have to salute an ogre.$B$BYou have helped me win my freedom, so I choose to use that freedom to serve your banner.$B$BToday, I salute you, commander.',0),
(35884,'enUS','Against all odds, here we stand. Still alive, an entire army on our heels.$B$BOur ship is waiting. Shall we depart?',0),
(35895,'enUS','Since that day, the sages have remained in power in Skyreach, now calling themselves the Adherents of Rukhmar and claiming to be the heralds of Her will.',0),
(35896,'enUS','The Shattered Hand is in shambles and the Avatar of Terokk now walks among us.$B$BWhen I promised you power back in Skettis, did you expect that it would come without any strings attached? Ha!',0),
(35897,'enUS','<You carefully hang the bangle upon the effigy\'s arm.>',0),
(35905,'enUS','Commander! Zipfizzle arrived with your laborers in tow just moments ago. We\'ve got a huge surplus of food, now, and promises of more where that came from.$B$BApparently the draenei threw in some other resources as well. Very good work, sir. What should we build next?',0),
(35907,'enUS','These corpses are fresh. Their killers must still be nearby.',0),
(35915,'enUS','Aye, these corpses are definitely fresh. They can\'t have gone far.',0),
(35921,'enUS','Hey there, bub. Lucy sent you? Good kid.$B$BYeah... you look like you\'ll do nicely.',0),
(35922,'enUS','Hey there, bub. Lucy sent you? Good kid.$B$BYeah... you look like you\'ll do nicely.',0),
(35924,'enUS','What is it you found? Let me see that.',0),
(35925,'enUS','This is grim news, $n.',0),
(35926,'enUS','What\'s that? Let me have a look.',0),
(35927,'enUS','Well done, $n. Transporting a brain is no easy task. I mean, they\'re just so darn slippery.',0),
(35928,'enUS','That\'s a good start. I\'ll throw these in the pot.$B$BBring me more.',0),
(35934,'enUS','Thank you, $n. Nisha is nearly returned to health.',0),
(35935,'enUS','The Iron Horde is a menace. Let\'s stamp out the rest of them. For the Horde!',0),
(35937,'enUS','Bah, no ear rings or anything. Better luck next time, $C.',0),
(35938,'enUS','Ha, yea, just some nose trivia for you there. This pointy trophy proves you slayed a Goblin out there. Good job, here\'s a lil\' something for your hard work.',0),
(35939,'enUS','Of course you haven\'t! I mean, look at these things...you can\'t sneak into anything with these things clacking around.',0),
(35940,'enUS','Jeez... somebody didn\'t brush, eh? Hah, here take this reward $n.',0),
(35941,'enUS','Oh man, <coughs> ... get that thing sealed into my bucket quick.',0),
(35942,'enUS','I\'m kidding! I\'m kidding! We all know you\'re a model $C of Stormshield, $n. Here, take this as a reward.',0),
(35944,'enUS','We are impressed with your ability to slay the goren. They are relentless and voracious and can overwhelm those are not prepared.',0),
(35945,'enUS','Ouch... my leg is still asleep, that smarts... Greblin Fastfizzle\'s my name, archeology\'s my game.$B$BHow can I help?',0),
(35947,'enUS','This Gardul Venomshiv is as good as dead.',0),
(35948,'enUS','We are impressed with your ability to slay the goren. They are relentless and voracious and can overwhelm those are not prepared.',0),
(35959,'enUS','Gardul Venomshiv, eh? He\'s good as dead.',0),
(35970,'enUS','Nice! What did you get?$B$BA necklace, not bad.. another necklace, good. A giant rock in the shape of an ogre head?$B$B<Greblin seems puzzled, he glances up at you.>$B$BSeriously? This is a rock in the shape of an idiot. Whatever, the necklaces look good.$B$BNot a bad find overall.',0),
(35972,'enUS','Oh, that\'s way better.$B$BMaybe next time they\'ll think twice before they throw a rock at someone. Err... I mean if they weren\'t so dead and everything.',0),
(35973,'enUS','You got the ring? Nice! The Steamwheedle Preservation Society is going to make some serious moolah on this stuff.$B$BNixxie will be pleased.',0),
(35985,'enUS','You\'re looking for what now? I mean, yeah sure... whatever. Just get me down alright?',0),
(35988,'enUS','<The Archmage looks damp and uncomfortable.>$B$BI apologize for the conditions here, $n. I had no choice. I summoned this tower at the optimal confluence of arcane energies. My hope is to finish my work here before all my books get musty.$B$BSo then! Let\'s get to it.',0),
(35989,'enUS','Your ring is finished. This is but the first step - with more time together we\'ll be able to create a ring of legendary power. But first things first!$B$BGul\'dan could be hiding anywhere, but if we can locate any of his lieutenants I think I know a way to flush him out. Let\'s begin by gathering the magical reagents I\'ll need.',0),
(35990,'enUS','<Khadgar rolls the fiery orb back and forth between his hands.>$B$BDo you know how to use this, $n?$B$BMe neither. Sometimes you just have to improvise as you go.',0),
(35991,'enUS','Oh very good. I\'ve been waiting to get a close look at one of these - let\'s open it up here.$B$BHmmmmm...$B$BWell, those goblins aren\'t very creative but their methods have a certain brute-force charm to them. It\'s amazing this thing doesn\'t explode. Or maybe it does. At least I\'m beginning to understand what they use a \"samophlange\" for.$B$BThis will work. Well done, $n!',0),
(35992,'enUS','Oh - it\'s still alive! Can you feel that?$B$BI must return this to the soil of Draenor when we are done with it. Perhaps in the care of the Cenarion Circle, who can ensure that it doesn\'t grow into another corrupted threat.$B$BWell done, $n. This was no easy feat.',0),
(35993,'enUS','We\'ve done a great thing today, $n. We\'ve deprived Gul\'dan of one of his top lieutenants and we\'re one step closer to finding the fiend himself.',0),
(35994,'enUS','Gul\'dan is countering my magic, $n! He\'s hiding!$B$BHe\'s a crafty one, but we\'re craftier. I think I know a way to increase the power and range of my spell...',0),
(35995,'enUS','<The archmage is out of breath.>$B$BGive me - give me a moment. Pshew.$B$B$n, that was incredible! You are possibly the greatest $C I\'ve ever had the honor to fight alongside.',0),
(35997,'enUS','The felbreaker\'s tome is blank? Let me see that. Did you get the Sorcerer King\'s sigil? Of course - see here, as you run the sigil over the page, runic lettering appears. Oh... this is really advanced.$B$BIt may take some time to fully comprehend what you\'ve discovered, $n, but these initial pages appear to be dedicated to the nature of fel. Exactly what I need! Great work!',0),
(35998,'enUS','<Khadgar holds some of the stones up to the light, allowing narrow filaments of arcane energy to spiral from stone to stone.>$B$BI don\'t think I\'ll ever underestimate ogres again, $n. One or two intelligent ones can mold the others into a formidable army.',0),
(36000,'enUS','$n, Chromie here has offered to help track down our bronze fugitive.$B$BShe may look diminutive, but I assure you she is as old as a hundred of your lifetimes.',0),
(36004,'enUS','How are you feeling? Can I get you a drink?$B$BI wish I could say that things will get easier from here, but we\'re just getting started. I must ask you to storm the very heart of the ogre empire... Are you ready?',0),
(36005,'enUS','Stabbed! He\'s been stabbed!$B$BWhy wasn\'t he more careful? We could\'ve set up wards, we could\'ve -$B$BIt doesn\'t matter now. We have to act fast.',0),
(36006,'enUS','The Kirin-Tor responded quickly. Jaina was here in minutes. But if you hadn\'t located Garona, the Archmage would\'ve died for certain. Thank you, $n!',0),
(36007,'enUS','How are you feeling?$B$BThat ring of yours is now one of the most powerful artifacts on this world. Which is good. Because we\'re about to strike right at the heart of the enemy...',0),
(36009,'enUS','Careful, careful! Set it down gently. I\'ll take it from here.$B$BThe heart of a fury is nothing to toy with.',0),
(36010,'enUS','Let me see what we have here... very interesting! This runic language here seems similar to the ignan kalimag dialect spoken by Azeroth\'s fire elementals. A full translation may take years.$B$BBut these parts written in orcish - yes, these I can probably decipher. Not just to bend steel, but to bend elemental power itself to our will.$B$BGul\'dan may be powerful, but if we continue to unlock the mysteries of Draenor, we will be able to counter his every move...',0),
(36012,'enUS','You found it! I have heard stories of these orbs of power. How I craved to study them during my long exile in Outland. And now, at last, I have one. Show me...$B$B<Reverently, Khadgar opens your pack and looks inside. His face remains motionless for a long time. Finally, he speaks:>$B$B...I don\'t know what I expected.',0),
(36013,'enUS','You\'ve got the tablets. Good, good! It must\'ve been very time-consuming to assemble these - not to mention dangerous. I am lucky to have you.$B$BI see no reason to delay. Show me your ring. Yes... I can do this. Let\'s put these tablets to use and enhance your power.',0),
(36014,'enUS','What do we have here? The legends ARE true. Blackhand sacrificed his own arm to the elements. Now that he\'s dead, it\'s indistinguishable from stone. Or is it?$B$B<Khadgar utters a few incantations from the Flamebinder\'s Tome. The severed hand slowly clenches into a fist.>$B$BHmmmm. Yes. $n, I\'ll be perfectly honest with you: This thing is extremely creepy.',0),
(36016,'enUS','<Khadgar is deeply distressed.>$B$BI am very sorry, commander. For a moment I thought we had lost you forever.$B$BThis ring will serve you well - I have never seen an artifact so powerful and pure of form. It may be possible to enhance it further but... I do not know at what cost.$B$BUse your ring wisely!',0),
(36017,'enUS','Gul\'dan\'s magic is embedded deep within Garona\'s mind. The more time I spend with her, the more it becomes clear that we MUST free her from his control.$B$BI am not giving up on this, $n.',0),
(36018,'enUS','My studies have gone well. I believe we are ready for the next step. You may not like it...',0),
(36022,'enUS','Excellent work.',0),
(36023,'enUS','They got what\'s comin\' to \'em.',0),
(36024,'enUS','Good work, $C. We won\'t let you down.',0),
(36025,'enUS','Good work, $C. We won\'t let you down.',0),
(36026,'enUS','That must of taken great effort to get back to us. You deserve this reward, friend.',0),
(36027,'enUS','Ah, $n. It is wonderful to \"see\" you. As you are no doubt aware the state of Outland in our own timeline is constantly degrading.$B$BI wish to extend my remote services to your cause so that I might better investigate Draenor in the time before it was ripped asunder.$B$BThis projection may seem translucent, but I can assure you it acts as a perfect conduit for my own powers.$B$BWill you accept my service?',0),
(36028,'enUS','We won\'t let him get away.',0),
(36029,'enUS','We won\'t let him get away.',0),
(36030,'enUS','Every little bit helps.',0),
(36031,'enUS','Good work, $C. We won\'t let you down.<table class=\"iconlist\"><tr><th><ul><li><var></var></li></ul></th><td>Collect: <a href=\"/currency=944\">Artifact Fragment</a>(2500)</td></tr></table>',0),
(36032,'enUS','Good work, $C. We won\'t let you down.',0),
(36033,'enUS','IT\'S SO PRETTTTY. WILL FIT NICE ON MY SPIKE OUTSIDE MY HUT. HAHAHA. HERE, TAKE THIS REWARD AND GET BACK OUT THERE.',0),
(36034,'enUS','OOOOH! THIS IS A LONG ONE. HE HE HAHAAH. HERE, TAKE THIS AS A REWARD.',0),
(36037,'enUS','This jungle will kill me and I will not return to cower at the mercy of Mar\'gok!$B$BI am a veteran of several wars and campaigned on two continents now. If you have a war worth joining, I will serve for a time.$B$BAt least until I can kill the Sorcerer-King!',0),
(36038,'enUS','WHATEVER, WHO LIKES PANDAS ANYHOW! <Laughs> TAKE THIS REWARD AND GET BACK OUT THERE!',0),
(36040,'enUS','WAIT, YOU JUST BROUGHT ME THEIR HAIR? UGH. I SAID I WANTED THEIR HEAD! UGHHH! <Stomps Feet> BUT I GUESS THIS IS ENOUGH TO PROVE YOU FOUGHT ONE IN BATTLE, SO TAKE YOUR REWARD. AND NEXT TIME, THEIR HEAD!',0),
(36041,'enUS','A TAIL! WELL, YOU SHOULDN\'T HAVE! I\'LL CHERISH IT FOREVER!',0),
(36042,'enUS','GOOD WORK, BRING ME BACK MORE AND I\'LL COOK YOU UP A CUP OF MY FAMOUS HUMAN BONE BROTH! HAHAH!',0),
(36047,'enUS','Excellent. I have a ride back to your outpost ready.',0),
(36048,'enUS','Perfect work. I called in a ride for ye back to the outpost when yer ready.',0),
(36054,'enUS','A simple exchange with complex results. That\'s the art of doing business.',0),
(36055,'enUS','Of course you agree.',0),
(36056,'enUS','Feeling safe, stranger?',0),
(36057,'enUS','A bloody price to pay just to play with luck. Let\'s hope it was worth it.',0),
(36059,'enUS','You fight well.',0),
(36062,'enUS','Ya know, I\'ve been thinking.$B$BWith uncle Krixel back that now frees me up to take some time off from running the Gearworks for a bit.$B$BIf you have the room in your garrison I\'d be glad to come join you, I could even teach you some tricks I\'ve learned to keep your accounts in order and the books cooked!',0),
(36063,'enUS','Every little bit helps.<table class=\"iconlist\"><tr><th><ul><li><var></var></li></ul></th><td>Collect: <a href=\"/currency=944\">Artifact Fragment</a>(500)</td></tr></table>',0),
(36064,'enUS','That must of taken great effort to get back to us. Once we\'ve collected enough artifacts we\'ll summon the Mage portals back to Warspear within Ashran.',0),
(36065,'enUS','That must of taken great effort to get back to us. Once we\'ve collected enough artifacts we\'ll summon the Mage portals back to Warspear within Ashran.',0),
(36066,'enUS','Every little bit helps.',0),
(36067,'enUS','Good work, $C. We won\'t let you down.',0),
(36068,'enUS','Good work, $C. We won\'t let you down.',0),
(36075,'enUS','It is hard to admit that there is a creature more brutal than an ogre, but the ogron definitely fit that description. Facing a captured ogron in the arena is no mean feat. Facing one in their own lair is something even more dangerous. Hail to thee champion!',0),
(36076,'enUS','We are impressed with your ability to slay the goren. They are relentless and voracious and can overwhelm those are not prepared.',0),
(36078,'enUS','A gladiator saw you tear this off the back of a gronnling, which I am sure did not part with it easily. It is more like a stone than a true scale though as these brutes are part stone it seems. Not an easy trophy to collect!',0),
(36080,'enUS','A gladiator saw you tear this off the back of a gronnling, which I am sure did not part with it easily. It is more like a stone than a true scale though as these brutes are part stone it seems. Not an easy trophy to collect!',0),
(36081,'enUS','A gronn\'s eye is not something they part with alive. Your gladiator described a fight hard won and this trophy is a testament to your abilities. Well done!',0),
(36083,'enUS','A gronn\'s eye is not something they part with alive. Your gladiator described a fight hard won and this trophy is a testament to your abilities. Well done!',0),
(36084,'enUS','The botani are nothing to be trifled with. They are incredibly cunning and their powers are strong on their home land. Taking one of their blooms is an true example of your fighting skill!',0),
(36085,'enUS','Good work!$B$BNow, it is time for the next phase of our plan.',0),
(36086,'enUS','The botani are nothing to be trifled with. They are incredibly cunning and their powers are strong on their home land. Taking one of their blooms is an true example of your fighting skill!',0),
(36090,'enUS','The infested appear to be mere husks animated by plant life. They are slow but very strong. Slaying even one is a strong demonstration of your own skill!',0),
(36091,'enUS','Sometimes we don\'t get turned into mulch for the jungle. Sometimes we get back up, filled with plants. The Infested are hard to kill. Slaying even one is a strong demonstration of your own skill!',0),
(36092,'enUS','Ancients here tend to be guardians and tenders, but that does not make them any less dangerous. An enraged ancient is something to be behold. Taking a branch from one is a worthy deed!',0),
(36094,'enUS','Ancients here tend to be guardians and tenders, but that does not make them any less dangerous. An enraged ancient is something to be behold. Taking a branch from one is a worthy deed!',0),
(36095,'enUS','I\'m sorry to hear Springslip didn\'t make it. He was a good agent.$B$BThis news of Azuka gaining even more power is troubling to say the least.',0),
(36096,'enUS','Even the insects of Gorgrond are larger and meaner than other parts of the world I have been to! Killing them, which you have obviously done, takes a great deal of strength and skill.',0),
(36097,'enUS','Even the insects of Gorgrond are larger and meaner than other parts of the world I have been to! Killing them, which you have obviously done, takes a great deal of strength and skill.',0),
(36098,'enUS','As you can see, the venom Gorgrond wasps have is extremely powerful. To face one is to possibly face your own death. I would refrain from harvesting more of these, one enough to prove your strength here!',0),
(36100,'enUS','Congratulations!',0),
(36101,'enUS','As you can see, the venom Gorgrond wasps have is extremely powerful. To face one is to possibly face your own death. I would refrain from harvesting more of these, one enough to prove your strength here!',0),
(36103,'enUS','A gruesome trophy from a gruesome beast. To be frozen and eaten slowly is not a death I would choose. The world is better with less of these basilisks in it!',0),
(36104,'enUS','A gruesome trophy from a gruesome beast. To be frozen and eaten slowly is not a death I would choose. The world is better with less of these basilisks in it!',0),
(36105,'enUS','I have seen no elementals elsewhere in Draenor that compare in ferocity to those in Gorgrond. I wonder what caused them to be so angry. That crystal was hard-won I am sure!',0),
(36106,'enUS','I have seen no elementals elsewhere in Draenor that compare in ferocity to those in Gorgrond. I wonder what caused them to be so angry. That crystal was hard-won I am sure!',0),
(36107,'enUS','I believe I speak for all of us when I say you are among the fiercest predators in Gorgrond! You have faced and slain Gorgrond\'s most dangerous creatures on their home ground and lived to bring something of them back here.$B$BThe gladiators have come together found something that will show the world your might! Bask in the glory champion!',0),
(36108,'enUS','I believe I speak for all of us when I say you are among the fiercest predators in Gorgrond! You have faced and slain Gorgrond\'s most dangerous creatures on their home ground and lived to bring something of them back here.$B$BThe gladiators have come together found something that will show the world your might! Bask in the glory champion!',0),
(36117,'enUS','You\'re looking for what now? I mean, yeah sure... whatever. Just get me down alright?',0),
(36119,'enUS','You\'ve just now showed up? Well, better late than never.',0),
(36123,'enUS','Fantastic. You can always bring me back tokens you find on Horde corpses for a bonus reward.',0),
(36125,'enUS','Nice work, $n. You\'re a natural.',0),
(36127,'enUS','I can see you have the spirit of a true adventurer, $n. Come visit me anytime and you can see Ashran through my eyes, even from Stormshield.',0),
(36130,'enUS','Yes yes, it\'s the real Harrison Jones. Why is he such a celebrity all of a sudden?',0),
(36131,'enUS','I see you are both a fisherman and a warrior. I will do what I can to help you.',0),
(36132,'enUS','Look at all the bait ideas in this thing! Great job $n!',0),
(36133,'enUS','Good work. If you happen to find anymore Artifact Fragments, bring them to me or the others in need of them to contribute to the war effort.',0),
(36134,'enUS','I\'ve never seen a magnaron of that size before. This is bad, $n.',0),
(36136,'enUS','I\'ve never seen a magnaron of that size before. This is bad, $n.',0),
(36137,'enUS','You\'re going to make a fine overseer, sir! Keep those peons in line!$B$BNow you know the basics of logging and finding timber. Time to put them to good use for the good of your garrison.',0),
(36138,'enUS','That\'s how it\'s done, commander!$B$BWe\'re now fully operational. Any time you have enough timber to place a work order, come on back to me and we\'ll get started.$B$BThis garrison ain\'t gonna build itself!',0),
(36141,'enUS','Not bad traveler, not bad at all.',0),
(36142,'enUS','You didn\'t believe me about those timber lords, did you? Well now you know.$B$BIt looks like this group will serve you well, sir. Medium sized trees across Draenor are now at your mercy. That means more timber per tree!',0),
(36157,'enUS','The ring! You\'ve got it. Feel how it\'s still warm to the touch? The power of Draenor\'s sun is locked into the metal. This is perfect, $n. It is exactly the base material we need to fashion into something amazing.$B$BWhile I prepare your treasure, let\'s talk about our next steps...',0),
(36158,'enUS','Marvelous, marvelous! I will use these to upgrade your ring once we finish up a couple more tasks...',0),
(36160,'enUS','Commander! The Burning Blade attacked just a few moments ago, they are looking for the Heart of Gorgorek. $B$BThankfully, Lieutenant Thorn was here to protect us.$B$BWhat? You found a rose? Shh, hand it to me quickly. I\'ll hold onto this until the time to confess my love is right.',0),
(36161,'enUS','The assassin appeared out of nowhere.$B$BBaros took the blade that was meant for my heart. I ripped out the throat of our attacker... but I was too late.$B$BBaros gave me this flower before he passed.$B$B<Thorn holds up the rose. A tear rolls down her cheek.>',0),
(36162,'enUS','Today was not a good day.',0),
(36163,'enUS','Thank you for coming, $n.',0),
(36164,'enUS','I see that you and Yrel have stared into the eyes of the most primal of the elementals, and not waivered from your path.$B$BIt pleases me to say that your courage is not lacking.$B$BWell done.',0),
(36165,'enUS','By Muradin\'s beard... what a headache...',0),
(36166,'enUS','By da spirits... me head be hurtin\'...',0),
(36167,'enUS','News of your deeds precedes you. Rangari Saardar already sent word of your excellent work.$B$BThanks to the both of you, $n.',0),
(36168,'enUS','It seems you have been successful in your journey.$B$BHow do I know this? If you had not passed the challenge of the ancestors, you would not have returned at all.',0),
(36169,'enUS','Well done, champion. Well done.',0),
(36171,'enUS','We beat back nature, Commander. May I be excused? I\'d like to get all this sap out of my armor.',0),
(36176,'enUS','Another competitor for the competition? How wonderful! Garaal will be pleased!',0),
(36177,'enUS','Congratulations, $n! You did it!$B$BThe other competitors are nowhere to be found!$B$BGaraal will be most pleased. With such an abundance of supplies to work with he and the other craftsmen will have no trouble staying busy.$B$BI\'ll start tanning these immediately. They\'ll be ready for delivery in just a moment.',0),
(36179,'enUS','Lemmy\'s gun broke down again I take it?$B$BGood job covering for \'em out there. I could use more workers like you!',0),
(36182,'enUS','This is fantastic! This sample indicates massive timber reserves in the large timber found across Draenor. And now with the Tree Murderer 9000 at your disposal you\'ll be able to chop those towering monstrosities down with ease.',0),
(36183,'enUS','From one commander to another... thank you.$B$BWe\'ve faced off on the field of battle so many times. Vashj\'ir... the Jade Forest... Lion\'s Landing...$B$BI am glad I could end my journey with such a worthy adversary.',0),
(36185,'enUS','Greetings, $n.$B$BFanara mentioned the competition was fierce this year.$B$BMy, my. These goods should keep me busy for an entire season!$B$BAs the victor of the competition one usually becomes my apprentice, however, your skills are surely in need of no apprenticeship.$B$BPerhaps a trade is in order.$B$BI\'ll keep your delivery and share the goods with our local craftsmen and in return, I\'ll share some of our knowledge with you.',0),
(36189,'enUS','You\'re going to make a fine overseer, sir! Keep those lumberjacks in line!$B$BNow you know the basics of logging and finding timber. Time to put them to good use for the good of your garrison.',0),
(36192,'enUS','That\'s how it\'s done, commander!$B$BWe\'re now fully operational. Any time you have enough timber to place a work order, come on back to me and we\'ll get started.$B$BThis garrison ain\'t gonna build itself!',0),
(36193,'enUS','Thank the Light! All of the rangari who were missing have returned accounted for. Thank you, hero.',0),
(36194,'enUS','We haven\'t even scratched the surface when it comes to overkill.$B$BIt looks like this group will serve you well, sir. Medium sized trees across Draenor are now at your mercy. That means more timber per tree!',0),
(36195,'enUS','This is fantastic! This sample indicates massive timber reserves in the large timber found across Draenor. And now with the Wood Annihilator XXI the Third, Jr. at your disposal you\'ll be able to chop those towering monstrosities down with ease.$B$BGet off my back, I didn\'t name it.',0),
(36196,'enUS','You\'ve just now showed up? Well, better late than never.',0),
(36197,'enUS','Yea, that Zurge really is angry isn\'t he?',0),
(36198,'enUS','Good work. If you happen to find anymore Artifact Fragments, bring them to me or the others in need of them to contribute to the war effort.',0),
(36199,'enUS','Not bad traveler, not bad at all.',0),
(36201,'enUS','I see you are both a fisherman and a warrior. I will do what I can to help you.',0),
(36202,'enUS','Look at all the bait ideas in this thing! Great job $n!',0),
(36205,'enUS','My father\'s hammer, where did you find this!?',0),
(36206,'enUS','That solves one riddle. The moment they arrived in Draenor, Garrosh killed his savior.$B$BHe left the job unfinished; The dragon\'s spirit is still restless.$B$BI hope you\'re ready for a fight.',0),
(36207,'enUS','Where did you find this hammer!?',0),
(36208,'enUS','Goren crystals are used by some as weapons. The acid left behind can be deadly though, even to the wielder.',0),
(36209,'enUS','Your search brought rewards?',0),
(36210,'enUS','Ah, yes, these shells will work perfectly.',0),
(36219,'enUS','I won\'t waste your time, champ. I\'ve got a once in a lifetime opportunity for you.',0),
(36220,'enUS','If you kill Lug\'dol, you definitely belong in da proving grounds.$B$BI don\'t even care that you tiny not ogre!',0),
(36221,'enUS','You? Fightin\' ta be da Blood Champion? Hmm.',0),
(36222,'enUS','You did it, mon! I never thought I\'d be seein\' such a fight!',0),
(36223,'enUS','We have the notes. Let us see what they reveal about our enemy\'s strategy.',0),
(36226,'enUS','You have the spirit of a true explorer, $n.',0),
(36227,'enUS','ONLY FIVE? UGH. TAKE THIS REWARD AND GET BACK OUT THERE.',0),
(36228,'enUS','YES... YES! <Takes a deep whiff of the armor scrap> MMMM, ITS FRESH!',0),
(36230,'enUS','$n, thank you for avenging my death.',0),
(36236,'enUS','It seems that you have found a very special tailoring book.$B$BIt belongs to Ameeka, a tailor of great renown from Embaari Village.',0),
(36238,'enUS','This entire time... I have been so consumed with my own grief.$B$BI never once stopped to consider how much my father was suffering at the hands of our enemies.$B$BThank you so much, $C, for helping him to return to me. Please, allow me to repair his hammer.$B$BIn exchange for everything you have done for us, I will teach you whatever you wish to know.',0),
(36239,'enUS','Oh, my. One of my satchels! Where did you find this? I lost it weeks ago.$B$BI\'ve been so busy training I forgot to collect herbs for Master Ardule. I need your help $n, if you are willing, but I must warn you - the herbs can be quite dangerous!$B$BHand me the satchel and I\'ll restore the protective inscription to guard you from harmful toxins.',0),
(36240,'enUS','That was fast, $n! And such a generous delivery!$B$BI\'ve secured the ink in a vial for you, but please be careful.',0),
(36241,'enUS','My, $n. Your delivery...$B$BI don\'t know how to thank you enough.$B$BThis is a substantial amount of ink. You\'ve helped ensure our history for generations to come.$B$BPerhaps I can repay you with a taste of the very knowledge you\'ve helped preserve?',0),
(36242,'enUS','I knew it was only a matter of time before Azuka would make her move.',0),
(36248,'enUS','Azuka\'s reign of terror continues... we need a new plan.',0),
(36255,'enUS','Interesting, an Arakkoa recently visited the garrison looking for an armor piece with a powerful enchantment like this. His name was Delath.$B$BThe enchantment on this bracer is beyond my skill, but perhaps this Delath can give you the necessary insight to replicate it.',0),
(36256,'enUS','Do I also detect that you have in your possession an artifact of our land? $B$BCan I see it?$B$BOne of Oru\'kai\'s bracers... Thank you!',0),
(36257,'enUS','Thank you. I thought I was going to be stuck here forever.',0),
(36260,'enUS','Yes... This is it, after so many years. Soon, I will have all of the Armaments of Oru\'kai.$B$BReturn my ring as well and I will fulfill the promise I made to that squeamish orc. $B$BTake this book. If you have any skill, you can use it to decipher and learn Draenor\'s enchantments. $B$BOf course, you will need a proper workplace as well. Here are plans; hopefully you can follow them.$B$BNow, be gone, and steer clear of the other armaments, for they are mine.',0),
(36262,'enUS','Is that my tailoring tome? It is! I\'m so glad it is safe! How can I ever repay you?',0),
(36266,'enUS','Again, you show me great kindness.$B$BNow, let us begin.',0),
(36269,'enUS','This is perfect! The cloth and magic are perfectly balanced and stable.$B$BI am happy to say that you have learned the basics of my tailoring methods. I respect your skill and your eagerness to learn new techniques.$B$BLet me give you some other patterns and materials that I hope you find useful during your journey.',0),
(36271,'enUS','Great job, commander! We\'ll have your leather or fur ready in no time.$B$BNow that you know how to use the trap, it will be available for your use at any time. We can only handle so many beasts in the barn at one time, though, so make sure you\'ve got room before you start trapping!',0),
(36272,'enUS','Great work, commander! We\'ll get to grillin\' up those steaks right away. I can already smell them!',0),
(36273,'enUS','Great work, $n.$B$BI\'m surprised we made it out of Spiteleaf Thicket alive! I can still hear the sound of their maniacal laughter as they swarmed us....',0),
(36274,'enUS','That must have been quite a fight, commander!$B$BThe materials we obtain from beasts of this magnitude will last us for quite a while.',0),
(36275,'enUS','Ah! I see you have my research with you... and what\'s this? You also have my supply bag and the anti-fungal boots!$B$BSpectacular! I now have the tools I need to continue my research into the Zangar fungal strain....',0),
(36280,'enUS','I won\'t waste your time, champ. I\'ve got a once in a lifetime opportunity for you.',0),
(36281,'enUS','I won\'t waste your time, champ. I\'ve got a once in a lifetime opportunity for you.',0),
(36282,'enUS','I won\'t waste your time, champ. I\'ve got a once in a lifetime opportunity for you.',0),
(36284,'enUS','You have the spore samples for my research! Excellent!$B$BThe Zangar Shore is a dangerous place... what with the risk of fungal mutation and all.$B$BOh... I didn\'t mention that part before? I was sure I did!$B$BNo matter! You look hardy enough, I\'m sure your genes are impervious to foreign fungal strains that your body has never before encountered!',0),
(36285,'enUS','I see you\'ve retrieved Dirgemire\'s fungal brain!$B$BNot only is the fungal structure perfectly intact, as a specimen it is exquisite! I will need only a moment to begin the examination...',0),
(36286,'enUS','Oh my! What do we have here, commander?$B$B<Inspecting the transponder.>$B$BA little damaged, slightly bent and burnt to a crisp, but this is my lucky day!$B$BWe\'ve been testing a new device and this transponder carries invaluable information! I\'ll have Bixx extract the coordinates for mapping.$B$BJust a few more parts and I should be able to teleport anything across this entire valley! And I do mean anything!$B$BThat\'ll surely help our reinforcements stand against the Iron Horde!',0),
(36287,'enUS','Those supplies were just what I needed! I think I\'m finally figuring out how to work with all these Draenor parts. I\'d be happy to show you, commander. I should be able to fix it in a jiffy.$B$BOh... and remember, deep breaths!',0),
(36289,'enUS','We\'ll need to keep an eye on this Azuka Bladefury character. Sounds dangerous.',0),
(36290,'enUS','We best be keepin\' an eye on dis Azuka Bladefury. She be bad news.',0),
(36292,'enUS','Glad you made it, $n. It\'s time to start pushing back on this Iron Horde invasion.',0),
(36296,'enUS','For tens of thousands of years we Botani have clashed against the mightiest forces of this world, but none have had your unbridled ferocity and resilience.$B$BI... I concede to your battle prowess. I will aid you in your campaign for dominance of my world.$B$BIf you will accept me.',0),
(36301,'enUS','I was chased by ogres and had to leave my bag behind. It looks like almost everything is here, except for... oh, no!',0),
(36307,'enUS','Glad you made it, $n. It\'s time to start pushing back on this Iron Horde invasion.',0),
(36308,'enUS','Interesting, an Arakkoa recently visited the garrison looking for an armor piece with a powerful enchantment like this. His name was Delath.$B$BThe enchantment on this bracer is beyond my skill, but perhaps this Delath can give you the necessary insight to replicate it.',0),
(36309,'enUS','This... this is my satchel... but how?$B$BDid you see a boy - a young boy near this? You must tell me where you found it!$B$BI tried to fight them, but the looters... they were too strong! They almost killed me!$B$BPlease, please....$B$BI\'d give anything to have my only son back! I cannot fail him....',0),
(36310,'enUS','Do I also detect that you have in your possession an artifact of our land? $B$BCan I see it?$B$BOne of Oru\'kai\'s bracers... Thank you!',0),
(36311,'enUS','My boy!$B$B<A tear falls down his cheek, clearing a path down to the skin where soot once rested.>$B$BYou... no words can explain how grateful I am.$B$BI can only repay what I have to offer, which isn\'t much in terms of valued goods. Most of my work goes straight to our soldiers. I do, however, carry the wisdom of my people and my craft.$B$BIt would be an honor if you allowed me to share some of this wisdom with you.$B$BMay the light guide you, $n.',0),
(36313,'enUS','Thank you. I thought I was going to be stuck here forever.',0),
(36314,'enUS','Please, allow me to take a closer look.',0),
(36315,'enUS','Yes... This is it, after so many years. Soon, I will have all of the Armaments of Oru\'kai.$B$BReturn my ring as well and I will fulfill the promise I made to that squeamish draenei. $B$BTake this book. If you have any skill, you can use it to decipher and learn Draenor\'s enchantments. $B$BOf course, you will need a proper workplace as well. Here are plans; hopefully you can follow them.$B$BNow, be gone, and steer clear of the other armaments, for they are mine.',0),
(36316,'enUS','Perhaps there is now hope for a brighter future. I can only hope some of those in Skyreach have been awakened.',0),
(36341,'enUS','Your feats seem to know no limits, $n. Today, our garrison forces have struck a terrible blow to Warchief Hellscream and the Iron Horde.$B$BHowever, he is not defeated so easily. If anything, his hunger for vengeance will grow.$B$BWe must destroy the root of his operations in Tanaan Jungle, but first, there is much preparation to be done.$B$BUntil then, bask in the glow of our momentous victory.',0),
(36342,'enUS','Your feats seem to know no limits, $n. Today, you and your garrison forces have struck a terrible blow to Warchief Hellscream and the Iron Horde.$B$BHowever, he is not defeated so easily. If anything, his hunger for vengeance will grow.$B$BWe must destroy the root of his operations in Tanaan Jungle, but first, there is much preparation to be done.$B$BUntil then, bask in the glow of our momentous victory.',0),
(36344,'enUS','Ah, so the trap held! I can smell the meat already. This will make a great feast for our warriors!',0),
(36345,'enUS','Very good. We will have your leather or fur ready soon.$B$BNow that you know how to use the trap, it will be available for your use at any time. We can only handle so many beasts in the barn at one time, though. I would not advise taking more from the land than necessary.',0),
(36346,'enUS','Blood and thunder, that must have been quite a battle!$B$BThe materials we obtain from beasts of this magnitude will last us for quite a while.',0),
(36352,'enUS','$R, how can I repay you for returning this pendant to me?',0),
(36353,'enUS','$n, we\'ve been through hell and back together more times than I can count. You\'re the Alliance\'s best chance at defeating the Iron Horde, and you know it.$B$BHow do you feel about me joining your garrison? We can bring the fight to orcish scum together, just like old times.',0),
(36368,'enUS','Frenna didn\'t make it out of Tangleheart.',0),
(36376,'enUS','We sent them packing, Commander!',0),
(36378,'enUS','This diamond is marvelous! I shiver at the mere thought of the massive creature this must have come from...',0),
(36379,'enUS','Poor Pazerp... this news is unsettling to say the least. The Iron Horde seems to have an unending supply of troops.',0),
(36380,'enUS','Thank you for your help $n, please take this pendant along with a copy of my research.$B$BI hope these will prove useful in helping you to better understand the secrets of Draenic gems.$B$BUntil we meet again, friend.',0),
(36382,'enUS','Dis not good. Them Iron Horde be causin\' a lot of da trouble round here. We need ta find a way ta deal wit dim.',0),
(36384,'enUS','The serum did what!??!$B$BI must have used too much growth hormone. Possibly... the mixture just needs to be shaken prior to dosage?',0),
(36385,'enUS','So what you\'re saying is that this here book is actually a container to hold the remains of targets on a hit list? And the assassination was being perpetrated by another... tree?$B$BThis world is crazy.$B$BNow let\'s see what happens when we put all the pieces into place.',0),
(36404,'enUS','Great work, $n! We will get started planting the garden right away.',0),
(36408,'enUS','What have you got here...$B$BOnly a keen eye would be able to spot the potential of this drained crystal. You may not be familiar with draenei crystals yet, but your familiarity with gems certainly shows.$B$BTell you what... if you would assist me in the troubles we\'re having with our local defense crystals I\'d gladly share some of my own expertise in jewelcrafting with you.',0),
(36409,'enUS','You\'ve found it! This crystal is overflowing with energy. This is definitely what we were looking for.$B$BI fear even thinking about what kind of ritual this orc was planning to undergo with the power from this crystal.$B$BYou\'ve done a great thing for us, $C. As promised, I would like to show you my appreciation by teaching you how to work with some of our native gems and crystals. I trust you will put the knowledge to good use.',0),
(36412,'enUS','You were a blaze amongst our foes, Commander. It looks like we\'ll see another dawn in Draenor.',0),
(36414,'enUS','Nothing like a little righteous bloodshed, to shake the chill from these old bones.',0),
(36417,'enUS','This looks to be all of the cloth, but it appears that they tried to rip and pull the magic out by physical force. I think I see teeth marks...',0),
(36419,'enUS','There, you\'re on the path to becoming a true Hexweave tailor.$B$BDo not share the secrets I\'ve shown you here with anyone.',0),
(36423,'enUS','Thank you, $n. Let\'s see if your pets like their new space!',0),
(36427,'enUS','\"The brothers united once more,\" he said.$B$B\"A world full of untold riches to plunder,\" he said.$B$B\"Wealth beyond imaging,\" he said!$B$BAnd then he proceeded to drop a log on top of me.$B$B\"There can only be one CEO of Barov Industries,\" he said.$B$BAt least we can agree on that...',0),
(36428,'enUS','Yea! Great work, $n!$B$BI\'ve already heard from the survivors and they\'re glad for this second chance at life.$B$BYou made a real difference today!',0),
(36429,'enUS','\"The brothers united once more,\" he said.$B$B\"A world full of untold riches to plunder,\" he said.$B$B\"Wealth beyond imaging,\" he said!$B$BAnd then he proceeded to drop a log on top of me.$B$B\"There can only be one CEO of Barov Industries,\" he said.$B$BAt least we can agree on that...',0),
(36432,'enUS','D\'kaan worried about me? He is more worried I will be chased back to the camp with one of those giant beasts in tow. Still I could use your help here...',0),
(36434,'enUS','Ahh, there y\'are!$B$BPenny Clobberbottom reportin\' for duty, commander.',0),
(36435,'enUS','We have been studying these orcish texts feverishly since our arrival here. Allow me a moment to translate this for you.$B$BHmmm... The notes appear to contain a list of names.',0),
(36436,'enUS','I have slain quite a few as well but they continue to spring up here.$B$BWe will need another solution...',0),
(36437,'enUS','So the normal ebb and flow of battle has been disrupted by the saberon. I do not think it wise to leave things as such.$B$BWe should see about infiltrating the saberon and setting things right.',0),
(36438,'enUS','You have strong friends $n. We must make haste before the plants realize the way is open.',0),
(36439,'enUS','Your machine is brutish but effective, well done $n. We must make haste before the plants realize the way is open.',0),
(36440,'enUS','Many are finding bolt-holes to weather your storm, friend. That should keep them out of our way.',0),
(36441,'enUS','A good catch discovering those herbs $n. We cannot allow them to continue using these. Who knows what it might set off.',0),
(36442,'enUS','You have... you have brought me the bloom. At last my purpose can be fulfilled!',0),
(36443,'enUS','At last it is done. Dionor has left and his spawn shall follow him in due time.$B$BI grow weary of this conflict and the desire to return to the Overgrowth has left me.$B$BPerhaps I will travel beyond these lands and see what other surprises you little beasts have to share...',0),
(36448,'enUS','<Weldon holds Alexi\'s head up to his face and begins speaking.>$B$BYou no-good, backstabbing son-of-a-goat! Your greed is only surpassed by my own!$B$BAs for you my peasant friend, you have served me well. Here are your just rewards!',0),
(36449,'enUS','<Alexi holds Weldon\'s head up to his face and begins speaking.>$B$BYou no-good, backstabbing son-of-a-goat! Your greed is only surpassed by my own!$B$BAs for you my peasant friend, you have served me well. Here are your just rewards!',0),
(36457,'enUS','You know the trick to fooling a bunch of Orcs? Every once in a while you\'ve got to be holding all the cards!',0),
(36460,'enUS','Perhaps this little creature will earn her keep after all.',0),
(36469,'enUS','Nice job, brudda. I hope your pets be likin\' dere new home.',0),
(36471,'enUS','Next time I won\'t go so easy on you!',0),
(36474,'enUS','My husband sent you, didn\'t he?$B$BNormally I would laugh at that, but seeing these horrors, Kaz and I could use all the help we can get.',0),
(36475,'enUS','$n, this is it, THIS IS IT! Just give me a moment while I look through these.$B$BHmm... I think there are a few things here that you may find very useful. Here, take these plans with you.$B$BDon\'t worry about me, commander. I\'m just gonna take another look around before I sneak out of here.',0),
(36477,'enUS','Ah, I see that you\'ve found my lovelies. Beautiful, aren\'t they? It\'s a shame that the process drives them so... insane.$B$BThe ring is yours to keep, of course. Can you hear them whisper? Marvelous.',0),
(36481,'enUS','Wow, great flying out there, ace! Here\'s your prize!',0),
(36482,'enUS','Yay! Burn the bad guy! Burn him a lot!',0),
(36483,'enUS','I knew you could do it, kid.',0),
(36488,'enUS','Wow. Those... \"dwarves\"... sure do know how to make both botani AND goren mad.',0),
(36494,'enUS','Welcome back, mon.',0),
(36495,'enUS','Welcome back, $n.',0),
(36498,'enUS','The situation here is dire, $n. We have much to discuss.',0),
(36499,'enUS','The situation here is dire, $n. We have much to discuss.',0),
(36502,'enUS','I\'ve seen plant life mimic the vicious hydra before, but to improve on the design? Only in Gorgrond... excellent work $n.',0),
(36503,'enUS','In this land even the plants turn into vicious monsters. Biolante was one of the worst, still as a plant until you were too close.$B$BA fitting end to such a beast...',0),
(36505,'enUS','This is a fine cloak! Sadly, we no longer have the resources to make them like this.',0),
(36508,'enUS','Thank you for vouching for me, commander.',0),
(36510,'enUS','These will do nicely, $n! Thank you!',0),
(36511,'enUS','These will do nicely, $n! Thank you!',0),
(36512,'enUS','Auchindoun would have fallen to the demons if it weren\'t for you. Even the blood elves would not have been enough. I don\'t know how I could possibly ever repay you.$B$B<Tuulani\'s face lights up.>$B$BThat\'s it! We\'re kindred spirits, $n. I can feel it! How about I stick around with you?$B$BI\'ll still have to attend to my duties at Auchindoun, but I can handle it. What do you say, $n? It\'ll be great!',0),
(36513,'enUS','These will do nicely, $n! Thank you!',0),
(36514,'enUS','These will do nicely, $n! Thank you!',0),
(36515,'enUS','These will do nicely, $n! Thank you!',0),
(36516,'enUS','You are covered in soot from head to toe, $n!$B$BAs promised, I will help you repair your cloak. I have a few other items here which you might find useful as well.$B$BCome back and see me any time!',0),
(36517,'enUS','These will do nicely, $n! Thank you!',0),
(36518,'enUS','Wow... I\'ve never seen anyone fight like that. That was... impressive.$B$BI\'m in no shape to join Lady Liadrin and the others at Auchindoun now. You have an entire fortress on this world, though. Could I go there and rest awhile? Maybe repair my armor?$B$BI\'ll stick around and join your forces as a token of my gratitude. Liadrin won\'t mind... we\'re all on the same team, right?',0),
(36519,'enUS','I have never seen anyone fight like that, $B.$B$BI am regrettably in no condition now to join the Auchenai in defending Auchindoun. I have heard stories of your fortress in Shadowmoon Valley. Could I go there and repair my armor?$B$BPerhaps... I could stay there a while longer than that? I feel there is much you could teach me.',0),
(36522,'enUS','I may have fallen, but I will not be forgotten.$B$BI implore you to allow me to stay here and serve in your army. Bralok took my life, but my spirit stands strong before you.$B$BI need to stop the Iron Horde, $n, and I know you are the only one that can help me do that.',0),
(36523,'enUS','Is it still twitchin\'? I think I saw it still twitchin\'.',0),
(36567,'enUS','Now THAT\'S what I\'m talkin\' about! Look at this place!$B$BWe\'ve even got a pool out back. Little cold, sure, but ya can\'t always have a tropical paradise.',0),
(36573,'enUS','$n, we have dealt a great blow to the forces of the Iron Horde.',0),
(36574,'enUS','$n, we have dealt a great blow to the forces of the Iron Horde.',0),
(36575,'enUS','We have dealt a great blow to the Iron Horde, commander. We will defeat them yet.',0),
(36576,'enUS','We have dealt a great blow to the Iron Horde, commander. We will defeat them yet.',0),
(36589,'enUS','I think we could get into some serious trouble with this beauty!',0),
(36592,'enUS','MUCH better! A lot less bumping into walls to be sure.$B$BThere should be room to get in another building or two now. We can get the additional construction going whenever you\'re ready - just point me at anything you\'re interested in on the table here.',0),
(36594,'enUS','What did you think of my rapid disassembly tech? Pretty effective, yeah?',0),
(36595,'enUS','Ah perfect. I\'ll get this up an\' runnin\' in no time.',0),
(36601,'enUS','Commander. Good to have you back.$B$BWe\'ve got some movement in Nagrand. Let me fill you in on the details.',0),
(36602,'enUS','Boss-mon. Good to have ya back.$B $BWe been seein\' some movement in Nagrand. Let me give ya the details.',0),
(36606,'enUS','Commander. Good to have you back.$B$BWe\'ve got some movement in Nagrand. Let me fill you in on the details.',0),
(36607,'enUS','Boss-mon. Good to have ya back.$B $BWe been seein\' some movement in Nagrand. Let me give ya the details.',0),
(36608,'enUS','You came from Draenor? How does that even work?!',0),
(36609,'enUS','We should really catch some big one\'s when Nat\'s gets here!',0),
(36611,'enUS','These fish are exquisite, $n. Great job!',0),
(36612,'enUS','This will do nicely... A fish like this would be hard for anyone to deny, especially Nat!',0),
(36614,'enUS','I think I could just fall over and die happy right now. It\'s a dream come true!$B$BI already ordered some even larger draft paper, boss. Don\'t you worry...',0),
(36615,'enUS','I... I think I like it. A little more blue paint, maybe some taller towers, but you can really call it home, you know?$B$BI already ordered some even larger draft paper, sir. Don\'t you worry...',0),
(36616,'enUS','You truly are a master fisherman!$B$BI would be delighted to join you here on Draenor and help you catch as many lunkers as you can. But first, let\'s grab a drink.',0),
(36617,'enUS','A small tag on this present reads:$B$BHappy holidays, $n!',0),
(36623,'enUS','It\'s good sport, fighting foes larger than yourself. You\'re happy with your grunts\' conduct, Commander?',0),
(36624,'enUS','Just a second, pal. Can\'t you see I\'m busy here?$B$BCommander! I didn\'t think you were actually going to show... I mean... welcome, commander.',0),
(36626,'enUS','Commander $n, I\'m so glad you could make it. It\'s a true honor, sir.',0),
(36627,'enUS','Hmmm... sounds like it still needs a bit more punch. Let me get back to work on it, boss, I\'ll see what I can do!$B$BGood news is, we know a lot more about the Iron Horde tech now. I made a copy of my notes for ya.',0),
(36629,'enUS','Thank you again for taking the time to visit, commander. You have no idea how much it means to us.',0),
(36630,'enUS','Look, I don\'t have time for any... Oh, it\'s you!',0),
(36632,'enUS','Welcome to Gorgrond, Commander. We only just arrived ourselves.',0),
(36633,'enUS','Well it\'s about time ye showed up. I\'m done slumming around with these new recruits.$B$BMe blade is sharp, me armor is spit shined and I combed me beard this mornin\'.$B$BI\'ve been ready for battle since me grandpa Gygax first put an axe in me wee lil hand.$B$BSo whad\'ya say, commander?',0),
(36641,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(36642,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(36643,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(36644,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(36645,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(36646,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(36647,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(36648,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(36649,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(36650,'enUS','Nothing teaches a bully better than a bloody nose! Good fight, Commander. It\'s an honor to stand with you.',0),
(36653,'enUS','Is this what a peon feels like? Chopping down trees and pruning unruly hedges all day? And I thought their job was a bore. Hah!',0),
(36655,'enUS','I don\'t know what\'s worse, the brutality of this Iron Horde or the tempered menace of our old foes. It doesn\'t matter. Neither measures against our strength, Commander.',0),
(36662,'enUS','You showed \'em, boss!',0),
(36667,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(36669,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(36671,'enUS','Incredible! You\'ve got real moxy, kid.',0),
(36674,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(36675,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(36676,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
