(36682,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(36683,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(36684,'enUS','Word of your glory in battle has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(36685,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(36686,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(36687,'enUS','I hear you were a sight to see in the ring. I\'m proud to serve by your side, commander.',0),
(36688,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(36689,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(36690,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(36691,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(36692,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(36693,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(36694,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(36695,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(36696,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(36697,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(36698,'enUS','News about da fightin\' beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils too.$B$BDem Alliance must a been none too happy to see ya on the field.',0),
(36699,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(36700,'enUS','I been hearin\' ya were a sight ya see in the ring.$B$BWe made some bets on ya. Easy money.',0),
(36701,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(36702,'enUS','MEATBALL FEELING BETTER NOW!$B$BMEATBALL FIGHT FOR AKIHIKÓ NOW!$B$BMEATBALL FOLLOW AKIHIKÓ WHEREVER AKIHIKÓ GO!!!',0),
(36705,'enUS','You did it. You really did it! You\'re the new lord of the ring!',0),
(36706,'enUS','Commander! I am humbled to be able to serve you. The Lieutenant requests your presence.',0),
(36707,'enUS','Throm-Ka, commander. I am pleased to finally meet you in person.',0),
(36708,'enUS','Thank you again for taking the time to visit, commander. You have no idea how much it means to us.',0),
(36709,'enUS','So, you are the commander? Sylvanas sent me to find you.',0),
(36711,'enUS','Ya brought my gear! Well it be lookin\' like my luck might be turnin\' around after all!$B$BAbu\'gar will be returnin\' the favor, just ya wait and see!$B$BRight after I hook myself a lunker, of course...',0),
(36741,'enUS','And here\'s your potion, $n! If you don\'t have any use for it, maybe gift it to a friend who does?',0),
(36742,'enUS','It is made. If you don\'t have any use for it, give it to one of our melee.',0),
(36790,'enUS','The lives of all the flock are precious.$BI\'m glad to know that his murderers have been brought to justice.$B$BThank you, $n, you have done us a great honor.',0),
(36791,'enUS','Here she is! Careful with her, these potions have a reputation for mysteriously disappearing.',0),
(36800,'enUS','I will take any lunkers you like find like this off your hands. Come back and see me anytime you catch one and I will pay you top dollar!',0),
(36801,'enUS','Ah, Commander $n. Good to see you. Now our party is complete.',0),
(36802,'enUS','I will take any lunkers you like find like this off your hands. Come back and see me anytime you catch one and I will pay you top dollar!',0),
(36803,'enUS','I will take any lunkers you like find like this off your hands. Come back and see me anytime you catch one and I will pay you top dollar!',0),
(36804,'enUS','I will take any lunkers you like find like this off your hands. Come back and see me anytime you catch one and I will pay you top dollar!',0),
(36805,'enUS','I will take any lunkers you like find like this off your hands. Come back and see me anytime you catch one and I will pay you top dollar!',0),
(36806,'enUS','I will take any lunkers you like find like this off your hands. Come back and see me anytime you catch one and I will pay you top dollar!',0),
(36812,'enUS','You\'re good people, commander.',0),
(36813,'enUS','Within this pouch I have placed three Everbloom seeds. You merely have to crush the seed to release the spores within. Inhale deeply and let the subversive infestation take hold.$B$BOnce empowered you will become an unstoppable force of nature; though be warned, I have modified these seeds to cause you minimal harm, thus their potency is somewhat reduced.$B$BYou must not undergo the transformation too frequently.$B$BShould you require more seeds I will offer them to you - for a small price.',0),
(36828,'enUS','Kick \'em while they\'re down!',0),
(36830,'enUS','They\'re defeated! I\'m glad we came here, Commander. To Draenor. Fighting against demons reminds me why we fight for the Alliance.',0),
(36831,'enUS','Waugh! We beat back the demons, Commander. My blood\'s still boiling from it. My eyes aren\'t turning red, are they?',0),
(36832,'enUS','If my spirits aren\'t with Xuk, Xuk isn\'t with them. You though, Xuk likes you.',0),
(36833,'enUS','You have impressed me greatly, $n. If you will have me, I would like to join you at your garrison.',0),
(36843,'enUS','Akhan is alive? Light bless us - some good news!',0),
(36848,'enUS','Your efforts will be well rewarded, $n. The ancient waygates now serve you.',0),
(36861,'enUS','Hey, you\'re from that Alliance base right?$B$BGlad you made the trip because we really could use your help!',0),
(36862,'enUS','Hey, you\'re from that Horde base right?$B$BGlad you made the trip because we really could use your help!',0),
(36864,'enUS','I can honestly say I never thought I\'d see the premier Horde commander walking through an Alliance garrison.$B$BThen again, I never thought I\'d be caught while performing reconnaissance for the Dark Lady and stuffed in a hole in the ground left for dead.$B$BI\'m clearly not going anywhere without your help. If you help me out of this hellhole, I\'ll serve under your banner. My solo run has been decidedly less than pleasant.',0),
(36870,'enUS','This will do nicely... A fish like this would be hard for anyone to deny, especially Nat!',0),
(36874,'enUS','We may kill from sky break to sky fall and still our work will never be done. Yet at the end of days when we are measured for our accomplishments, only the bloody wake that we have left behind us will show our true strength. For this reason you must never stop the slaughter of those that would seek to harm us and our loved ones.$B$BPromise me, $n.$B$BNever. Stop.',0),
(36876,'enUS','It is a start, to be certain, but there is much work to be done if Draenor is to be saved. Show no mercy, for they will show none to you.$B$BThe only warlords left upon Draenor will be you and I.',0),
(36881,'enUS','Looks to me like we ended up in the right place.',0),
(36882,'enUS','We should really catch some big one\'s when Nat\'s gets here!',0),
(36884,'enUS','OOH IT\'S SO RUBBERY. AND STILL WARM. GOOD WORK!<table class=\"iconlist\"><tr><th align=\"right\" id=\"iconlist-icon1\"></th><td><span class=\"q3\"><a href=\"/item=112119\">Worgen Snout</a></span></td></tr></table><script type=\"text/javascript\">//<![CDATA[WH.ge(\'iconlist-icon1\').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(112119, 0, 1, null, null));//]]></script>',0),
(36889,'enUS','A last warning: once you have accepted this choice you cannot reverse it or make a new choice until you complete your mission$B$BIf your choice is certain, your aim will be true.$B$BStrike fear in the hearts and minds of the enemy! For the Horde. For Draenor.',0),
(36897,'enUS','With this heart you will see and hear things as only the great spirits can. Your enemy will be unable to hide from your unrelenting assaults.',0),
(36911,'enUS','That talbuk\'s already settled down for the night. It will need some rest and grooming before it\'s ready for the next stage in its training.',0),
(36912,'enUS','I have bedded the clefthoof down for the night, it will need rest before it is ready for training.',0),
(36913,'enUS','That boar has taken to the hay. We\'ll let it rest up a bit before more training.',0),
(36914,'enUS','It almost bit me, but I\'ve got it bedded down and happy. A wolf, in my stables! Who\'d have thought?',0),
(36915,'enUS','Quite a big one, but it fits! It\'s resting, we\'ll talk about training it tomorrow.',0),
(36916,'enUS','Was it cold up there? This guy seems to appreciate the warmth, he\'s already snoozin\'!',0),
(36917,'enUS','The talbuk appears to be doing well. Allow it to rest before you continue the beast\'s training.',0),
(36918,'enUS','I\'ve gone and dried it off already. We\'ll see about training this thing tomorrow.',0),
(36920,'enUS','A friend it would seem.$B$BKayn did not think we could handle this? He might have been right this time.',0),
(36921,'enUS','The truth of your deeds is in your eyes. Your hunger for the enemy sated with cries for mercy and rivers of blood.$B$BTake now your place as manslayer.',0),
(36923,'enUS','With this heart you will see and hear things as only the great spirits can. Your enemy will be unable to hide from your unrelenting assaults.',0),
(36924,'enUS','The truth of your deeds is in your eyes. Your hunger for the enemy sated with cries for mercy and rivers of blood.$B$BTake now your place as dwarfstalker.',0),
(36925,'enUS','With this heart you will see and hear things as only the great spirits can. Your enemy will be unable to hide from your unrelenting assaults.',0),
(36926,'enUS','The truth of your deeds is in your eyes. Your hunger for the enemy sated with cries for mercy and rivers of blood.$B$BTake now your place as gnomebane.',0),
(36927,'enUS','With this heart you will see and hear things as only the great spirits can. Your enemy will be unable to hide from your unrelenting assaults.',0),
(36928,'enUS','The truth of your deeds is in your eyes. Your hunger for the enemy sated with cries for mercy and rivers of blood.$B$BTake now your place as worgen hunter.',0),
(36929,'enUS','With this heart you will see and hear things as only the great spirits can. Your enemy will be unable to hide from your unrelenting assaults.',0),
(36930,'enUS','The truth of your deeds is in your eyes. Your hunger for the enemy sated with cries for mercy and rivers of blood.$B$BTake now your place as draenei destroyer.',0),
(36931,'enUS','With this heart you will see and hear things as only the great spirits can. Your enemy will be unable to hide from your unrelenting assaults.',0),
(36932,'enUS','The truth of your deeds is in your eyes. Your hunger for the enemy sated with cries for mercy and rivers of blood.$B$BTake now your place as scourge of the Kaldorei.',0),
(36933,'enUS','With this heart you will see and hear things as only the great spirits can. Your enemy will be unable to hide from your unrelenting assaults.',0),
(36934,'enUS','The truth of your deeds is in your eyes. Your hunger for the enemy sated with cries for mercy and rivers of blood.$B$BTake now your place as terror of the Tushui.',0),
(36935,'enUS','Here she is! Careful with her, these potions have a reputation for mysteriously disappearing.',0),
(36940,'enUS','This is more trouble than I first tink. Da Iron Horde be strong, but we are da true Horde, and we be stronger.$B$BI fear this is da start of much bloodshed, before we go ta war, we be needin\' a plan.',0),
(36941,'enUS','This is worse than I imagined.$B$BThe Iron Horde is proving to be a massive threat to our people... I don\'t want anymore bloodshed, but I fear we are out of options.$B$BWe need a plan before we strike.',0),
(36944,'enUS','The boar has taken to the stables quite quickly. They appear to be nearly domesticated already. It will need some time to rest.',0),
(36945,'enUS','Quite a sight, I must say. Big and powerful, yet full of so much air. It will be ready for training tomorrow.',0),
(36946,'enUS','A powerful creature, it nearly took down the wooden posts of the stable. We will begin training it as soon as it wakes.',0),
(36947,'enUS','I have been training hard since I joined your forces, commander.$B$BLet me prove my new strength to you so that I am worthy to fight by your side. All will tremble at the sight of us on the battlefield!',0),
(36948,'enUS','You can hear the power building inside the unit...',0),
(36950,'enUS','Quite the catch, commander. It will need to rest for some time, but will surely be hungry for combat soon.',0),
(36951,'enUS','<The arakkoa merchant looks you up and down.>$B$BWell-equipped, aren\'t we? Azik is betting you are someone of importance to your people.$B$BCome closer, friend. Speak with me for just a moment.',0),
(36952,'enUS','They came at us... from... nowhere.$B$B<The stoneguard nearly passes out.>',0),
(36953,'enUS','Your will be done. I require your advisement, commander.',0),
(36955,'enUS','A last warning: once you have accepted this choice you cannot reverse it or make a new choice until you complete your mission.$B$BIf your choice is certain, your aim will be true.$B$BStrike fear in the hearts and minds of the enemy! Glory to the Alliance! For Draenor!',0),
(36957,'enUS','With this heart you will see and hear things as only the great spirits can. Your enemy will be unable to hide from your unrelenting assaults.',0),
(36958,'enUS','The truth of your deeds is in your eyes. Your hunger for the enemy sated with cries for mercy and rivers of blood.$B$BTake now your place as slayer of Sin\'dorei.',0),
(36959,'enUS','With this heart you will see and hear things as only the great spirits can. Your enemy will be unable to hide from your unrelenting assaults.',0),
(36960,'enUS','The truth of your deeds is in your eyes. Your hunger for the enemy sated with cries for mercy and rivers of blood.$B$BTake now your place as death stalker.',0),
(36961,'enUS','With this heart you will see and hear things as only the great spirits can. Your enemy will be unable to hide from your unrelenting assaults.',0),
(36962,'enUS','The truth of your deeds is in your eyes. Your hunger for the enemy sated with cries for mercy and rivers of blood.$B$BTake now your place as the butcher.',0),
(36963,'enUS','With this heart you will see and hear things as only the great spirits can. Your enemy will be unable to hide from your unrelenting assaults.',0),
(36964,'enUS','The truth of your deeds is in your eyes. Your hunger for the enemy sated with cries for mercy and rivers of blood.$B$BTake now your place as orcslayer.',0),
(36965,'enUS','With this heart you will see and hear things as only the great spirits can. Your enemy will be unable to hide from your unrelenting assaults.',0),
(36966,'enUS','The truth of your deeds is in your eyes. Your hunger for the enemy sated with cries for mercy and rivers of blood.$B$BTake now your place as troll hunter.',0),
(36967,'enUS','With this heart you will see and hear things as only the great spirits can. Your enemy will be unable to hide from your unrelenting assaults.',0),
(36968,'enUS','The truth of your deeds is in your eyes. Your hunger for the enemy sated with cries for mercy and rivers of blood.$B$BTake now your place as Huojin\'s fall.',0),
(36969,'enUS','With this heart you will see and hear things as only the great spirits can. Your enemy will be unable to hide from your unrelenting assaults.',0),
(36970,'enUS','The truth of your deeds is in your eyes. Your hunger for the enemy sated with cries for mercy and rivers of blood.$B$BTake now your place as killer of Kezan.',0),
(36971,'enUS','That should do it a world of good. We\'ll let \'er rest for tonight, and take on some bigger targets tomorrow.',0),
(36972,'enUS','Oi! That talbuk\'s performin\' admirably. Let\'s let \'er rest.',0),
(36973,'enUS','Those were some mighty big claws to tangle with. Your talbuk will need a nap after that one.',0),
(36974,'enUS','Ye did it! I\'m sure your talbuk\'s enjoyin\' this sort of one-on-one attention. We\'ll let it rest up a bit.',0),
(36975,'enUS','I\'ll bet that was quite a fight! Great job, let\'s let it rest for tonight.',0),
(36976,'enUS','Those poor beasts! I\'m glad you two put that ogre out of commission. Check back in tomorrow and we can continue the training.',0),
(36977,'enUS','From now on, I\'m sure your mount will always remember to keep one eye on the skies. Great job!',0),
(36978,'enUS','Glad to see you two make it back. It\'ll need a bit of time to brush that dust off.',0),
(36979,'enUS','Well, it\'s a bit wet, but seems to be in good spirits. I\'ll get \'er dried off and into bed.',0),
(36980,'enUS','The sand worm\'s bit the dust? Well done, I\'ll get this beast bedded down for the night.',0),
(36981,'enUS','Hunted the hunter, eh? Your beast doesn\'t seem any worse for wear, either! I\'ll brush it down.',0),
(36982,'enUS','Your talbuk has grown from a wee silverpelt into a fine specimen of war beast, and it\'s all due to your diligence.$B$BI\'m happy to hand over the reins of this fully-trained mount to you, commander. Ride it with pride!',0),
