(37032,'enUS','A mighty kill. Your beast will need to rest now.',0),
(37033,'enUS','A savage beast, but you have triumphed. Fine work, I will get your mount some water.',0),
(37034,'enUS','You have returned victorious. I will bed your mount down for the night.',0),
(37035,'enUS','Those beasts will recover, in time. Let us rest for tonight, you have done well.',0),
(37036,'enUS','From now on, your mount will always remember to keep one eye on the skies.',0),
(37037,'enUS','Glad to see you back. I will need some time to brush that dust off of your mount.',0),
(37038,'enUS','Your mount is bit wet, but seems to be in good spirits. I will dry it off and put it to rest.',0),
(37039,'enUS','You stand strong, though the ground crumbles. Admirable.$B$BAllow your mount to rest for the night.',0),
(37040,'enUS','Ah, you have hunted the hunter. Many beasts will be pleased tonight.',0),
(37041,'enUS','The garn is defeated, and your boar is now ready to see combat. Here are the reins, may you never part company.',0),
(37043,'enUS','Those scraps will do.',0),
(37044,'enUS','Pretty cool invention you have there.',0),
(37045,'enUS','That\'s all? Well. don\'t feel too bad. Some days we find nothing and the next we hit the jackpot!$B$BHere, I have a fresh supply of items from our latest outing. Check them out.$B$BGood luck!',0),
(37046,'enUS','I\'m glad ya be findin\' a good hire!$B$BMake sure to check back every week and I\'ll bring ya me latest recruits.',0),
(37047,'enUS','The Light has blessed me with newfound power, commander.$B$BNow none can stand against our conviction!',0),
(37048,'enUS','Your clefthoof appears worn, but happy. You have done well, let it rest for a while.',0),
(37049,'enUS','The clefthoof is in good shape, you are a fine trainer for the beast. It will require some rest.',0),
(37050,'enUS','A mighty kill. Your beast will need to rest now.',0),
(37051,'enUS','A savage beast, but you have triumphed. Fine work, I will get your mount some water.',0),
(37052,'enUS','You have returned victorious. I will bed your mount down for the night.',0),
(37053,'enUS','Those beasts will recover, in time. Let us rest for tonight, you have done well.',0),
(37054,'enUS','From now on, your mount will always remember to keep one eye on the skies.',0),
(37055,'enUS','Glad to see you back. I will need some time to brush that dust off of your mount.',0),
(37056,'enUS','Your mount is bit wet, but seems to be in good spirits. I will dry it off and put it to rest.',0),
(37057,'enUS','You stand strong, though the ground crumbles. Admirable.$B$BAllow your mount to rest for the night.',0),
(37058,'enUS','Ah, you have hunted the hunter. Many beasts will be pleased tonight.',0),
(37059,'enUS','The clefthoof is now fully-trained and prepared to be your mount. Take care of the beast, I hope to see the two of you again shortly.',0),
(37060,'enUS','Thank you, according to the ledger that appears to be everything we\'re missing.$BThose peons are going to be cleaning the latrines tonight for this!',0),
(37062,'enUS','You have learned one of my tricks of the trade, $n.',0),
(37063,'enUS','Those beasts will recover, in time. Let us rest for tonight, you have done well.',0),
(37064,'enUS','From now on, your mount will always remember to keep one eye on the skies.',0),
(37065,'enUS','Glad to see you back. I will need some time to brush that dust off of your mount.',0),
(37066,'enUS','Your mount is bit wet, but seems to be in good spirits. I will dry it off and put it to rest.',0),
(37067,'enUS','You stand strong, though the ground crumbles. Admirable.$B$BAllow your mount to rest for the night.',0),
(37068,'enUS','Ah, you have hunted the hunter. Many beasts will be pleased tonight.',0),
(37069,'enUS','A fine beast, sure to be your companion in many battles to come. Here are the reins, be strong but fair in your care of this great beast.',0),
(37070,'enUS','Fighting alongside you has strengthened my connection to the nether like never before, commander.$B$BI will use my new power to rain death down upon your enemies. They will learn to fear you.',0),
(37071,'enUS','A savage beast, but you have triumphed. Fine work, I will get your mount some water.',0),
(37072,'enUS','You have returned victorious. I will bed your mount down for the night.',0),
(37073,'enUS','Those beasts will recover, in time. Let us rest for tonight, you have done well.',0),
(37074,'enUS','From now on, your mount will always remember to keep one eye on the skies.',0),
(37075,'enUS','Glad to see you back. I will need some time to brush that dust off of your mount.',0),
(37076,'enUS','Your mount is bit wet, but seems to be in good spirits. I will dry it off and put it to rest.',0),
(37077,'enUS','You stand strong, though the ground crumbles. Admirable.$B$BAllow your mount to rest for the night.',0),
(37078,'enUS','Ah, you have hunted the hunter. Many beasts will be pleased tonight.',0),
(37079,'enUS','I had never seen such a beast before coming here, but you have trained it. No small feat, to be certain. Take the reins, you have earned them.',0),
(37080,'enUS','The blood o\' our fallen foes has not yet sated my thirst, commander.$B$BI have a trick up me sleeve that ought ta help change that.',0),
(37081,'enUS','We have shown far too much mercy to your enemies, commander.$B$BIf you would allow me, I have a spell I\'ve been perfecting that will show them what happens when you stand in our way.',0),
(37082,'enUS','A bold decision, gladiator. For most, death is the only thing they find at the Coliseum. Surviving here is more than a test of skill, it is a test of wills. Do you have the fortitude to become a champion?',0),
(37083,'enUS','Remarkable! You have proven yourself a true gladiator. And to a true gladiator goes more than honor and glory!',0),
(37084,'enUS','The shadows... they have taught me how to slip into the minds of our enemies.$B$BYes... turn them against their own. Our victory will be swift. Rawk!',0),
(37085,'enUS','Our clan strong. Strongest.$B$BI feed our lust, make us stronger. We win!',0),
(37086,'enUS','That\'s all? Well. don\'t feel too bad. Some days we find nothing and the next we hit the jackpot!$B$BHere, I have a fresh supply of items from our latest outing. Check them out.$B$BGood luck!',0),
(37087,'enUS','According to the ledger this appears to be everything we\'re missing. Those porters will be cleaning the latrines tonight for this!',0),
(37088,'enUS','You have learned one of my tricks of the trade, $n.',0),
(37091,'enUS','Nice invention!',0),
(37092,'enUS','Those scraps will do.',0),
(37093,'enUS','That was a fine battle to test your talbuk against. It will need to rest before we can continue the training.',0),
(37094,'enUS','Your talbuk is growing quickly, let us let it rest.',0),
(37095,'enUS','A mighty kill. Your beast will need to rest now.',0),
(37096,'enUS','A savage beast, but you have triumphed. Fine work, I will get your mount some water.',0),
(37097,'enUS','You have returned victorious. I will bed your mount down for the night.',0),
(37098,'enUS','Those beasts will recover, in time. Let us rest for tonight, you have done well.',0),
(37099,'enUS','From now on, your mount will always remember to keep one eye on the skies.',0),
(37100,'enUS','Glad to see you back. I will need some time to brush that dust off of your mount.',0),
(37101,'enUS','Your mount is bit wet, but seems to be in good spirits. I will dry it off and put it to rest.',0),
(37102,'enUS','You stand strong, though the ground crumbles. Admirable.$B$BAllow your mount to rest for the night.',0),
(37103,'enUS','Ah, you have hunted the hunter. Many beasts will be pleased tonight.',0),
(37104,'enUS','A powerful and swift companion, and now unafraid of the creatures you may run into. You have done well in your training of the beast, and I am pleased to present you with the reins.',0),
(37105,'enUS','Those beasts will recover, in time. Let us rest for tonight, you have done well.',0),
(37106,'enUS','From now on, your mount will always remember to keep one eye on the skies.',0),
(37107,'enUS','Glad to see you back. I will need some time to brush that dust off of your mount.',0),
(37108,'enUS','Your mount is bit wet, but seems to be in good spirits. I will dry it off and put it to rest.',0),
(37109,'enUS','You stand strong, though the ground crumbles. Admirable.$B$BAllow your mount to rest for the night.',0),
(37110,'enUS','Ah, you have hunted the hunter. Many beasts will be pleased tonight.',0),
(37111,'enUS','A savage beast, yet you have tamed it. I should learn to never underestimate you. It awaits your command patiently, almost like it knows you wait for it. Here are the reins, may your companion be ever at your side.',0),
(37112,'enUS','Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold -- that\'s our motto! Please, take a seat by the fire and rest your weary bones.$B$BWould you like to try a sampling of some of our fine food and drink?',0),
(37112,'frFR','Le repos et la détente pour ceux qui sont fatigués et qui ont froid – c\'est notre devise ! Je vous en prie, prenez place près du feu et reposez-vous.$B$BVoudriez-vous goûter quelques-uns de nos plus excellents mets et boissons ?',0),
(37119,'enUS','Ahh, I\'m glad you were able to find a good hire!$B$BI\'ll get back to looking for more candidates for you. Check back in every week to see my latest selections.',0),
(37121,'enUS','Like I said, the claw has a strange effect on the mounts we\'ve got here. If ye have it with ye when training a mount-in-training, your mount will be MUCH more vulnerable.$B$BShould ye find the training not rough enough, ye might want to challenge yourself.$B$BI\'d have a pretty hefty prize for anyone that could manage that!',0),
(37122,'enUS','I\'ve not seen the beasts go so wild in all of my years, as the day we brought this thing back to the stables.$B$BShould ye find the training still not hard enough, take it along with ye. Your mounts-in-training will be even MORE vulnerable.$B$BBe careful! I\'d give a prize to anyone that could best every beast with such an artifact, but I don\'t want to see you wind up dead!',0),
(37123,'enUS','This claw has a strange effect on the mounts we have. If you have it with you when training a mount-in-training, your mount will be MUCH more vulnerable.$B$BShould you find the training not rough enough, you might want to challenge yourself further by carrying it with you.$B$BI think besting the beasts of Draenor with it would certainly be worthy of a reward.',0),
(37124,'enUS','I have not seen the beasts go so mad in all of my years as a sage, as the day we brought this necklace back to the stables.$B$BShould you find the training still not hard enough, take it along with you. Your mounts-in-training will be even MORE vulnerable.$B$BBe careful! I would gladly reward anyone that could best every beast with such an artifact, but I do not want to see you wind up dead!',0),
(37125,'enUS','Nice find! This relic is going to be a welcome addition to someone\'s private collection!',0),
(37126,'enUS','Yes... this is it.$B$BCommander, I will cleave your foes like never before now that I have my sword.',0),
(37127,'enUS','It\'s so beautiful...$B$BOh, commander, thank you. A million times thank you!',0),
(37128,'enUS','It is done. The Legion have suffered a mighty blow.',0),
(37129,'enUS','I\'ll be takin\' a close look at this... thing. We can\'t have a repeat o\' Northrend.',0),
(37131,'enUS','Thank you, commander. The Dark Lady will appreciate this greatly.',0),
(37137,'enUS','Yes... yes... this will do nicely. We can use this to do great things.$B$BThank you, commander.',0),
(37140,'enUS','Thank you, master! Elements speak to Leorajh again.',0),
(37141,'enUS','My purpose as a Talonpriest has been fulfilled, though Iskar and Zellek must think me a fool for altering the sacred rites.$B$BI care not for their approval, and I am done hiding in the shadows.$B$BLet me fight for you. I should like to improve this world before I fade away from it.',0),
(37142,'enUS','Lunk know you kill many ogre for this, and Lunk very upset about this, but Lunk also still grateful.$B$BWait, dis not Lunk family club...',0),
(37144,'enUS','You have done much for us. What can I offer, but my blade?$B$BTalon King, let me fight for you.',0),
(37145,'enUS','Oh... this is... well that\'s very shiny isn\'t it? I think... I\'ll just sit here for a while.$B$B<Budd smiles contentedly.>',0),
(37146,'enUS','I see you have completed this menial task admirably, almost as if you were intended to experience such a thing. Ah fate, what do you have in store for me next?',0),
(37147,'enUS','I will take this to the Shado-pan right away. Fortune be with you, we will have need of your help again when the winds run quiet.',0),
(37148,'enUS','Good thinkin\'. Winky always loved these flameflies. If we gather enough of them, maybe we can convince hiim to come back!$B$BMaybe, er, you should hold onto this for a while, eh?',0),
(37149,'enUS','Perfect, here\'s a prize for your efforts.$B$BI\'ve got to head out and save everyone now. Again.',0),
(37150,'enUS','<Mylune gently lifts the tiny little bird to her face, nuzzling it. It crawls onto her shoulder and disappears into her nest of green hair. A moment later, a beautiful fan of brightly-colored tailfeathers emerges from the top of her head.>$B$B<Mylune\'s bright blue eyes grow moist with tears and her mouth goes slack with adoration. You\'ve made the dryad VERY happy.>',0),
(37151,'enUS','Yeah, this will do nicely. I\'m going to run out of ammo, but at least I\'ve got something to live for, for a while.$B$BHere, kid, you\'re gonna need this more than I am.',0),
(37152,'enUS','Revenge has the sweetest taste. Like an apple.$B$BTake this, friend. May all of your fruit be CRUSHED INTO PULP LIKE YOUR ENEMIES.',0),
(37153,'enUS','Oi, it\'s a fair sight dirtier, but that\'s her! Here, this is for you. You have my thanks.',0),
(37154,'enUS','This... may help me. I will need to return to Light\'s Hope shortly, you have my thanks.$B$BI will not need these supplies any longer, they are yours.',0),
(37155,'enUS','This might just be what we were looking for. Here\'s your booty.',0),
(37156,'enUS','Excellent, most excellent.$B$BI will wear it down quickly, and it cannot be repaired due to its unique nature. Expect to hear from me again.',0),
(37157,'enUS','One is eternally in your debt for what is, one is certain, an entirely selfless act on the part of the commander.$B$BThough more barrels were likely available, one will staunchly make do with the single barrel provided, comforted in the knowledge that the commander must deal with the great pressing issues of this land, and does not have time to clean up the mud that that so dutifully follows the commander\'s heroic allies.',0),
(37158,'enUS','The sun, I can see it. It is so bright.$B$BI... wish to be alone. Take this, and my thanks.',0),
(37159,'enUS','My thanks, $n. Aviana will be pleased, and we may yet be able to aid you.$B$BAviana has sought fit to bless you with this, use it well.',0),
(37160,'enUS','I like this blade. It will see me through much removing of limbs. Here, for you, something to remember me by.',0),
(37161,'enUS','You found it! It\'s safe! I was so worried! Take this, take it!',0),
(37162,'enUS','This is dire evidence indeed! I shall head there presently, to slay no less than twenty of the great beasts.$B$BFor Doloria!',0),
(37163,'enUS','You have my thanks. I will bring this back to the Ebon Hold immediately.$B$BTake this, I... acquired it... from one of the Shadowmoon.',0),
(37164,'enUS','This is... it can\'t be.$B$BI must be off, here is your reward. I do not part with it lightly...',0),
(37165,'enUS','Dis... is no good. Dey want to consume da whole planet. How did dey get so angry? What happened to dem? I\'m gonna bring dis back to da Circle, we probably gonna need your help again soon.$B$BOne of dem fronds be a bit magical, you hold onto it for a bit.',0),
(37166,'enUS','This is precisely what I was hoping for! I shall begin to study it immediately.$B$BWhile you were away, I collected these pretty flowers for you!',0),
(37167,'enUS','Yes, these will do nicely. My thanks, and here is your reward.$B$BTry not to die, I may need you again.',0),
(37168,'enUS','<The strangely gentle saberon brings a massive paw to his chest.>$B$BMe Leorajh. Not like others. Was small... weak. Banished from clan. Not Bloodmane anymore...$B$BLeorajh find cave. Find stone of sunlight. Learn much from stone. Want learn more. Want new clan.$B$BYou strong. Have clan?$B$BLeorajh join?',0),
(37177,'enUS','Thank you for coming.',0),
(37179,'enUS','You know, you\'re quite handy, and awfully powerful. Why don\'t I just follow you for a while?$B$BLook out Draenor, DOOOOOOOOM is coming!',0),
(37180,'enUS','Yes... this is it.$B$BCommander, I will cleave your foes like never before now that I have my sword.',0),
(37181,'enUS','Thank you, master! Elements speak to Leorajh again.',0),
(37182,'enUS','Yes... yes... this will do nicely. We can use this to do great things.$B$BThank you, commander.',0),
(37183,'enUS','I won\'t waste any of your time, sir. Let us discuss strategy.',0),
(37184,'enUS','They came at us... from... nowhere.$B$B<The lieutenant nearly passes out.>',0),
(37191,'enUS','<Lieutenant Thorn handles the weapon, her keen eyes taking note of every line, edge, and scratch. After several moments, she speaks.>$B$BMagnificent.$B$BThis blade was honed by a master craftsman, and imbued with ancient magic.$B$BJust imagine if such a powerful weapon were placed in the hands of a skilled warrior...',0),
(37192,'enUS','<Warmaster Zog lifts the blade into the air, admiring its balance and heft.>$B$BNever have I seen a weapon such as this. It was clearly made by a master, imbued with ancient magic, and tested in many a battle.$B$BCommander, I will leave the choice to you, but it would be an honor to see this blade placed in service of this garrison.',0),
(37201,'enUS','Thanks for helping me test out these artifacts.',0),
(37203,'enUS','That was fun.',0),
(37204,'enUS','The flames, they burn within me!',0),
(37205,'enUS','You have helped my pups train, and for that I give thanks.',0),
(37206,'enUS','You lucky this time.',0),
(37207,'enUS','The feathers have fallen and shown us much.',0),
(37208,'enUS','We have learned from each other. Thank you.',0),
(37209,'enUS','Ah, that\'s the stuff. I\'m going to run out of ammo, but at least I\'ve got something to live for, for a while.',0),
(37210,'enUS','Great work, $n! You\'ve made the swamp a safer place for archaeology and earned us a profit at the same time!',0),
(37211,'enUS','Wow! I knew Begruu\'s horn would be big, but I never imagined it would be this massive!$B$BWe\'re going to have to charge the buyer extra for delivery!',0),
(37221,'enUS','What a find! Great work, $n!$B$BDekorhan\'s tusk will be the centerpiece of someone\'s collection!',0),
(37222,'enUS','I\'m not going to lie to you, $n... I\'ll be sleeping more soundly at night knowing that Direhoof isn\'t out there somewhere roaming the wild.$B$BI\'ll also be sleeping more soundly on the pile of money I\'m going to make selling this hide to some rich collector!$B$BCha-ching!',0),
(37223,'enUS','I can\'t believe my eyes... you actually took down Gagrog the Brutal? You\'re tougher than I thought!$B$BGreat work, $n!',0),
(37224,'enUS','Wow! Look at the size of that thing... that\'s got to be the biggest hippo I\'ve ever seen!$B$BMu\'gra was one of the angriest hippos I\'ve ever seen, but she\'s all smiles now!$B$BGet it? Hippo teeth... smiles... eh, eh?',0),
(37225,'enUS','What\'s that you got there?$B$B<Gazmolf examines the talon>$B$BHey! That definitely looks like it belonged to Thek\'talon, and even if it\'s not who\'s to say otherwise? Great work, here\'s your cut!',0),
(37226,'enUS','Whoa! Careful where you point that stinger!$B$B<Gazmolf examines Xelganak\'s stinger>$B$BExtraordinary... I\'ve never seen anything like this before. As an archaeologist of the highest caliber, it is an honor to artificially fossilize this item and sell it to the highest bidder.$B$BWell done!',0),
(37227,'enUS','Oh, thank you $n! You\'ve made a lot of wee baby birds very happy.$B$B$B$B$B$BYou\'re my favorite $R!',0),
(37228,'enUS','We are one step closer to crushing the fruit vendor\'s grapes into muddy wine.',0),
(37229,'enUS','By the light, that\'s her! You\'ve done it again, an\' I can\'t thank you enough! We\'ll try to be more careful next time.',0),
(37230,'enUS','Again, though more barrels were likely available, one will staunchly make do with the single barrel provided, comforted in the knowledge that the commander must deal with the great pressing issues of this land, and does not have time to clean up the mud that that so dutifully follows the commander\'s heroic allies.',0),
(37231,'enUS','Let\'s hope this is the real thing, every time I go through that portal I feel my fur stand on end.',0),
(37232,'enUS','Yes, yes this is perfect. It is time, little souls, to return to the twisting darkness.$B$B<Lilian cackles madly.>',0),
(37233,'enUS','Once again, though I will need to return to Light\'s Hope shortly, you have my most sincere thanks.',0),
(37234,'enUS','The warmth comforts me. I thank you.',0),
(37235,'enUS','We will continue to attempt to parlay with the arakkoa.$B$BAviana\'s blessing upon you.',0),
(37236,'enUS','You\'ve saved it! A little nicked, but that can be fixed. Thanks!',0),
(37237,'enUS','By the light, they breed like great fiery rabbits! I shall head there presently, to slay no less than THIRTY of the great beasts.$B$BFor Doloria!',0),
(37238,'enUS','We are greatful for your aid. I shall retire shortly.',0),
(37239,'enUS','Another one? How curious.$B$BI may not be much closer to finding her, but these arrows bring some comfort to me, at least.',0),
(37240,'enUS','Thanks, mon. I\'m gonna bring this back to the Circle, just as soon as I can figure out how ta fly in da savage winds of dis place.',0),
(37241,'enUS','Another excellent find from our most illustrious hero! I will immediately begin transcribing your heroic deeds!',0),
(37242,'enUS','Once again, you have proven yourself invaluable. Perhaps you would like a teaching job?',0),
(37243,'enUS','A mighty blade, but I will wear it out quickly. Orc heads are harder than they look.',0),
(37244,'enUS','Oi, that\'s a bright fly! Thank ye, we\'ll just keep on tryin\' until that two-timing ol\' Winky comes on home.',0),
(37245,'enUS','Perfect, here\'s a prize for your efforts.$B$BI\'ve got to head out and save everyone now. Again.',0),
(37256,'enUS','<Idri stares at the ugly head.>$B$BYes, that\'s him.',0),
(37257,'enUS','Our bones are all we have left of an existence we left behind a long time ago.$B$B<The prince stares intently into your eyes.>$B$BStay with me, $C. I will help you find your Tidestone.',0),
(37259,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. May the souls of Auchindoun remain at peace with the threat of Teron\'gor eliminated.',0),
(37260,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. The families of the rescued miners will never be able to thank you enough for eliminating Gug\'rokk and his slavers.',0),
(37261,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. Eliminating Skylord Tovra\'s rylak escorts and disrupting the Grimrail will save an innumerable amount of lives.',0),
(37262,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. Taking down one of Draenor\'s great giants is regrettable, but letting Skullok, Son of Gruul, remain a tool of the Iron Horde would have led to great distruction.',0),
(37263,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. Putting an end to Ner\'zhul and his deathly rituals will allow many to sleep better at night.',0),
(37264,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. If not for you, all of Draenor may have withered under High Sage Viryx\'s rule.',0),
(37265,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. Your efforts to stop Yalnu may not only have saved our outpost but all of Azeroth as well.',0),
(37266,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. Defeating the Ironmarch Vanguard at Upper Blackrockspire is a major blow to the Iron Horde and Azeroth can rest a bit more knowing Warlord Zaela\'s bid for revenge has been permanently dealt with.',0),
(37268,'enUS','Nothing like a little righteous bloodshed, to shake the chill from these old bones.',0),
(37269,'enUS','You were a blaze amongst our foes, Commander. It looks like we\'ll see another dawn in Draenor.',0),
(37270,'enUS','I\'ve been experimenting again today, and I\'ve come up with some potion formulations that might suit you, commander. Would you like to try one?',0),
(37271,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. May the souls of Auchindoun remain at peace with the threat of Teron\'gor eliminated.',0),
(37272,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. The families of the rescued miners will never be able to thank you enough for eliminating Gug\'rokk and his slavers.',0),
(37273,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. Eliminating Skylord Tovra\'s rylak escorts and disrupting the Grimrail will save an innumerable amount of lives.',0),
(37274,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. Taking down one of Draenor\'s great giants is regrettable, but letting Skullok, Son of Gruul, remain a tool of the Iron Horde would have led to great distruction.',0),
(37275,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. Putting an end to Ner\'zhul and his deathly rituals will allow many to sleep better at night.',0),
(37276,'enUS','The Shattered Hand and their allies are dangerous, commander. No offense, but I don\'t trust your standing forces to keep a future assassin from slipping in unnoticed.$B$BI would like to volunteer myself to join your forces so I can keep a close watch on enemy movements. We cannot risk your untimely death - too much rests on your shoulders.',0),
(37277,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. If not for you, all of Draenor may have withered under High Sage Viryx\'s rule.',0),
(37278,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. Your efforts to stop Yalnu may not only have saved our outpost but all of Azeroth as well.',0),
(37279,'enUS','$n, you\'ve done a great service. Defeating the Ironmarch Vanguard at Upper Blackrockspire is a major blow to the Iron Horde and Azeroth can rest a bit more knowing Warlord Zaela\'s bid for revenge has been permanently dealt with.',0),
(37281,'enUS','I mean nae offense, commander, but I don\'t trust yer forces tae keep ya safe from a Shattered Hand assassination attempt on yer life.$B$BIf it\'s agreeable to ye, I\'d like tae join yer garrison and keep a watch on the scoundrels.',0),
(37284,'enUS','Oh, ya got dem for me? Excellent. Here\'s ya money.',0),
(37285,'enUS','Here ya go! Instant gratification\'s da best gratification!',0),
(37286,'enUS','To the victor go the spoils! All hail $n!',0),
(37287,'enUS','I think ye did the right thing, commander.',0),
(37288,'enUS','Oh you have some blueprint texts for me? That\'s great!$B$BLet\'s do some business!',0),
(37289,'enUS','I don\'t think they were ready for that. The Shadowmoon will think twice before attacking us again.',0),
(37290,'enUS','Oh YEAH buddy! We can work something out. I got plenty of stuff for you to buy!',0),
(37291,'enUS','Well fought, commander. Now to strike back before the Thunderlord can recover.',0),
(37292,'enUS','You be makin\' the right call, commander. There be no room for her kind in your ranks.',0),
(37293,'enUS','Yes! Dat be da heart! You did it...',0),
(37296,'enUS','Perhaps my rituals will be undisturbed for a few nights at least. Your offer is intriguing and I think we can come to an agreement.',0),
(37305,'enUS','With every victory, or claim here grows more strong.',0),
(37306,'enUS','The was a good fight, Commander. It might give me time to clean my sword.$B$BAnd honor our fallen.',0),
(37307,'enUS','A complete victory! Draenor denizens will mewl for weeks as they lick their wounds, in whatever dark places they live.',0),
(37318,'enUS','<The boiling cauldron gasps and spurts boiling liquid with each skull that is plunged into the pot.>$B$B<As the last of the skulls is submerged within the bubbling cauldron, you feel the sharp nip of a ghostly breeze upon your skin.>',0),
(37319,'enUS','These are beautiful. The bride and groom will be well pleased.',0),
(37320,'enUS','Wonderful. The client was just talking about how she couldn\'t wait to put it around her rival\'s neck. I\'m sure they won\'t be in conflict anymore after this gift.',0),
(37321,'enUS','This is beautiful.',0),
(37322,'enUS','The shrine has dozens of niches where the Prophet\'s followers have placed their own memory crystals, mourning the great leader\'s sacrifice. You slide the crystal into an empty socket and the memorial comes to life...',0),
(37323,'enUS','These are perfect. I almost feel like my settings aren\'t worthy of such gems.',0),
(37324,'enUS','Thank you.',0),
(37325,'enUS','We are back in business!',0),
(37326,'enUS','Ah, so you are the one your people spoke of so highly. We may discuss an alliance, but first...',0),
(37327,'enUS','Ah, so you are the one your people spoke of so highly. We may discuss an alliance, but first...',0),
(37328,'enUS','Excellent. We have more immediate concerns to deal with until he visits.$B$BDark Ranger Velonara requires your immediate attention, sir.',0),
(37329,'enUS','Excellent. We have more immediate concerns to deal with until he visits.$B$BHulda Shadowblade requires your immediate attention, sir.',0),
(37330,'enUS','Well done, commander.',0),
(37331,'enUS','Well done, sir.',0),
(37332,'enUS','Oh - you were attacked by an Umbraspore Giant? They\'re very dangerous - you were brave to face one down!$B$BThis growth you found doesn\'t seem to be part of the giant. It\'s almost like another organism living in symbiosis. We\'ll have to study this more closely and see what benefit it conveys to the host.$B$BThank you, $n. Outstanding work!',0),
(37418,'enUS','Can\'t wait to get this thing up and running for you, commander!$B$BCheck back in tomorrow, and be sure to wear your blast goggles!',0),
(37420,'enUS','Can\'t wait to get this thing up and running for you, commander!$B$BCheck back in tomorrow, and be sure to wear your blast goggles!',0),
(37433,'enUS','Congratulations, commander. You have survived Rotun\'s trial and proven yourself powerful indeed. $B$BHere, take this weapon, that you may further dominate your foes in battle!',0),
(37434,'enUS','Congratulations, commander. You have survived the trial of Trial Master Rotun and proven yourself powerful indeed. $B$BHere, take this weapon that you may futher dominate your foes in battle!',0),
(37439,'enUS','You\'ve done well today, $n. Your willingness to learn shows that you may very well rise above the unyielding cravings you must endure as a $R.$B$BRest not on your laurels, young one, but instead seek to master what you have learned. Only through diligence will we as a race survive.$B$BTake this - it may be of some use to you. Go now, and bring glory once more to our people.',0),
(37439,'ruRU','Сегодня ты славно $gпотрудился:потрудилась;, $n. Твоя тяга к учебе показывает мне, что ты одолеешь неутолимую жажду, которую приходится терпеть всем эльфам крови.$B$BОднако не зазнавайся. Стремись к новым знаниям и неустанно применяй их. Только усердие спасет нашу расу.$B$BВозьми этот подарок – он тебе пригодится. Теперь ступай и верни былую славу нашему народу!',25549),
(37440,'enUS','Splendid - these will do nicely. I\'ve been doing quite a bit of thinking on the current malaise Sunstrider Isle suffers under. One possible course of action I had pondered was to collect these arcane slivers from the beasts on the isle. In doing so, they could be experimented on; this would provide a potential source of culpability.$B$BAnyway, I will tend to the research. Allow me to place this incantation on you. I believe you\'ll make good use of it!',0),
(37440,'ruRU','Замечательно! Как раз то, что нужно. Я много размышлял о проклятии, поразившем Остров Солнечного Скитальца. Одно из возможных решений проблемы – собирать магические осколки и проводить эксперименты над ними. Не лучший путь, но другого я пока не вижу.$B$BКак бы то ни было, я продолжу свои исследования. Сейчас я наложу на тебя заклятие. Уверен, оно тебе поможет!',25549),
(37442,'enUS','Ah, $n - thank you for sharing your experience at the Shrine of Dath\'Remar. First off, you should be commended for your sense of duty and respect - it will serve you well not only here, but in all of Azeroth as well.$B$BAs for the odd sensation, it is no doubt a contributing part of the taint that has befallen Sunstrider Isle. We shall keep an eye on it; thank you for alerting us to it!',0),
(37442,'ruRU','Ах, $n, благодарю тебя за то, что ты $gпосетил:посетила; святилище Дат\'Ремара. Прежде всего следует похвалить тебя за чувство долга и почтительность – они послужат тебе не только здесь, но и повсюду в Азероте.$B$BЧто до странных ощущений – несомненно, это от порчи, поразившей Остров Солнечного Скитальца. Мы обратим на это внимание; спасибо за предупреждение!',25549),
(37443,'enUS','Well done - I knew you\'d be perfect for the task. Once it\'s safe to make use of our outdoor facilities on the isle, I\'ll be putting these things to good use.$B$BLike I mentioned, please feel free to keep the satchel. Also, you may find this piece of armor to be useful. Consider it ample compensation for a simple task performed dutifully!',0),
(37443,'ruRU','Отлично! Я знал, что ты прекрасно справишься. Как только мы почувствуем себя в безопасности на этом острове, я сумею найти этим вещам хорошее применение.$B$BКак я и обещал, сумка теперь твоя. Думаю, это справедливая награда!',25549),
(37444,'enUS','With many of the owlkin now inoculated, we can focus on getting out of here and not have to worry about wiping out the owlkin population in the area.$B$BHere, choose from these. You\'ve done good work, and you deserve to be rewarded!',0),
(37445,'enUS','Let me take a look at those.$B$BYes, I think that these will do nicely; good job, $n. The emitter is rather complex so it may take some time to finish the repairs. I\'ll let you know when it\'s ready.$B$BIn the meantime, you might see if Vindicator Aldar has anything he could use you for.',0),
(37446,'enUS','Good, good. Maybe they\'ll think twice before slacking next time! Thanks for the help!',0),
(37447,'enUS','If this is not enough demon blood, no amount will be. Now, let us see if we can make contact with Illidan\'s spirit in the Twisting Nether.',0),
(37448,'enUS','Then, it\'s decided. We either expose Detheroc or it\'s war between the Alliance and Horde, and we lose the world to the Burning Legion.',0),
(37449,'enUS','Grim news indeed. We cannot afford the loss of even one demon hunter, but you and Kor\'vas were right to put an end to Nightglaive.$B$BMore importantly, you have made a good friend in Stellagosa. The remnant of the Blue Dragonflight could prove to be a powerful ally.',0),
(37450,'enUS','Beautiful creatures... pure, one with the world. I didn\'t think that I could hate the Legion more.$B$BThank you, $n.',0),
(37452,'enUS','Of course you agree.',0),
(37453,'enUS','Of course you agree.',0),
(37454,'enUS','A simple exchange with complex results. That\'s the art of doing business.',0),
(37455,'enUS','A simple exchange with complex results. That\'s the art of doing business.',0),
(37456,'enUS','Feeling safe, stranger?',0),
(37457,'enUS','Feeling safe, stranger?',0),
(37458,'enUS','A bloody price to pay just to play with luck. Let\'s hope it was worth it.',0),
(37459,'enUS','A bloody price to pay just to play with luck. Let\'s hope it was worth it.',0),
(37467,'enUS','<The prince appears emotionally drained.>$B$BThis is the end of the road for me, $n. I can\'t bear to look at them. Moreover, my mere presence puts you in danger.$B$BBeyond this point, you must walk alone.',0),
(37468,'enUS','New student?',0),
(37469,'enUS','<You notice the reflection of something sinister upon the core\'s surface...>',0),
(37470,'enUS','You killed Athissa, $n.$B$BThat is to say, you and... and my people...$B$BMy people... they fought for us...$B$BBut, Warlord Parjesh has escaped through the portal with the Tidestone. You must pursue him and retrieve the Pillar of Creation.',0),
(37486,'enUS','She spoke of the Tidestone? That sea witch must not realize how close she truly is to finding it.$B$BWe should move quickly. We are close to your prize, and the naga are circling in.',0),
(37492,'enUS','I can\'t tell you how relieved I am that Elder Aldryth has returned.$B$BHonestly, life here in the palace hasn\'t been the same without him. Everything seemed to have... lost its color. Perhaps now we can get back to our normal lives.',0),
(37494,'enUS','We made it. Now all we have to do is get up there, sneak through my city -- which, mind you, is being watched by everyone -- then reveal and kill a dreadlord inside the headquarters of SI:7, Azeroth\'s most elite spy organization.$B$BPiece of cake. Ready to save the world, $n?',0),
(37496,'enUS','Did you get my bottle? Are you here to help us escape?',0),
(37497,'enUS','Perhaps this was a mistake.',0),
(37507,'enUS','That could have gone better. Sounds like you\'ve already made an enemy.$B$BStill, that\'ll work to our advantage. You versus Boss Whalebelly. The fight of the century... or at least, the day.$B$BNow to set everything up.',0),
(37510,'enUS','Hello, what can I do for you, little $R?$B$BAhahaha... it\'s you! I like how you came in and immediately confronted Whalebelly. That little tuskarr\'s got it coming.$B$BI can tell you\'re going to win big for me in the arena.',0),
(37511,'enUS','Shh... keep it down. The last thing I want is to get punched in the face by an ogre.',0),
(37516,'enUS','It sounds like the excavation of Broken Precipice is going to be fully operational in no time.$B$BI can\'t wait to line my pockets with some of that sweet moolah.',0),
(37517,'enUS','It sounds like the excavation of Broken Precipice is going to be fully operational in no time.$B$BI can\'t wait to line my pockets with some of that sweet moolah.',0),
(37518,'enUS','Yes, the headmistress is in her study, but I can\'t have you bothering her right now. Classes are about to start.',0),
(37520,'enUS','Nice work, $n!$B$BIt\'s times like these that make me proud to be your mentor. You\'ll make a fine archaeologist someday!$B$BHere\'s your cut!',0),
(37528,'enUS','I couldn\'t have snuck past him better. Now, to get these weapons into the right hands.',0),
(37530,'enUS','What happened, Farondis?',0),
(37536,'enUS','Yes, this\'ll do nicely... oh no! The last of my pit fighters have been defeated.$B$BIt\'s just you and me now, little $R.',0),
(37538,'enUS','<This is where you expected to find Okuna. Instead, you only found the pack with the weapons.>',0),
(37540,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments and go in the Light.',0),
(37541,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments and go in the Light.',0),
(37542,'enUS','You made quick work of that monkey. Now there\'s an empty position on Sternfathom\'s team that you can fill.$B$BBut first, let\'s get me set up for what comes after your big match.',0),
(37543,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments and go in the Light.',0),
(37547,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments and go in the Light.',0),
(37548,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments and go in the Light.',0),
(37549,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments and go in the Light.',0),
(37550,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments and go in the Light.',0),
(37551,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments and go in the Light.',0),
(37552,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments and go in the Light.',0),
(37553,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments, and may the Light protect you on your journey.',0),
(37554,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments, and may the Light protect you on your journey.',0),
(37555,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments, and may the Light protect you on your journey.',0),
(37557,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments, and may the Light protect you on your journey.',0),
(37558,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments, and may the Light protect you on your journey.',0),
(37559,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments, and may the Light protect you on your journey.',0),
(37560,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments, and may the Light protect you on your journey.',0),
(37561,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments, and may the Light protect you on your journey.',0),
(37562,'enUS','$n, your courage and dedication has made Draenor a safer place. Take these armaments, and may the Light protect you on your journey.',0),
(37563,'enUS','Excellent choice. I will be sad to see them leave, but I know they will help strengthen our combined packs in the coming conflicts.$B$BI will see that they make their way to your garrison as soon as they have said farewell to their loved ones.$B$BThey should be ready the next time you need to send followers on a mission.',0),
(37565,'enUS','Now the captives are free. Thank you, $n.$B$BReady for the prince?',0),
(37566,'enUS','With Oceanus dead, the skrogs will start fighting amongst themselves. They\'ll certainly be too busy to provide any further assistance to the naga.$B$BI\'d say this was a job well done, despite my being captured. Good thing you came along.$B$BI\'ll see you around, $n.',0),
(37568,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(37569,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(37570,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(37571,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(37572,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(37573,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(37574,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(37575,'enUS','Let me unpack that for you.$B$BI should let you know - while we managed to expedite this one, future work orders will take longer.',0),
(37644,'enUS','You\'ve earned this!',0),
(37645,'enUS','You\'ve earned this!',0),
(37653,'enUS','Yes. Already, I can tell their souls are weaker than their flesh.',0),
(37654,'enUS','Do you know what ship this is? It\'s the Queen\'s Reprisal. Queen... as in the Banshee Queen, Sylvanas Windrunner.$B$BIf the farmstead weren\'t sunk under the waves, I\'d be heading home to Gilneas right about now.',0),
(37656,'enUS','I\'ve always had my doubts about Cyana. Something was never quite right there. Looks like she cracked and joined the Legion.$B$BStill, we are not going to let her, or this Cordana Felsong, get away with it.',0),
(37657,'enUS','What? A jailer demon you say? Oublion? What a ghastly name.$B$BNo wonder we couldn\'t become trade partners with them. Oh, if only I\'d known, there wouldn\'t have been any need for such slaughter!$B$BAh well. Live and learn.',0),
(37658,'enUS','Thank you, $n. That will give us the breathing room we need to launch our counter-offensive.',0),
(37659,'enUS','<Amongst the moldering remains of the chest, you find the captain\'s log. Its pages are partially intact and it contains interesting information about the possible whereabouts of Queen Sylvanas Windrunner, the new warchief of the Horde.>',0),
(37660,'enUS','I wouldn\'t take what Arev\'naal said to heart. The inquisitor demons are masters of misinformation. You don\'t suspect betrayal within the ranks, do you?$B$B<The Souleater looks thoughtful and grim.>$B$BI fear we won\'t have all of our answers about Lord Illidan for a while.',0),
(37666,'enUS','You have my eternal gratitude, $n. Let it never be said that I have underestimated the reach and prowess of the Uncrowned.$B$BThe easy part\'s done. Now it\'s time to do the impossible.',0),
(37669,'enUS','Congratulations!',0),
(37678,'enUS','Don\'t worry about the scattered pages and spines - I will have my aides clean up.$B$BThank you. You may return to your studies.',0),
(37687,'enUS','So the Shadow Council is involved? Interesting...',0),
(37688,'enUS','So the Shadow Council is involved? Interesting...',0),
(37689,'enUS','You did it! Mathias Shaw is back in charge of SI:7 and you prevented an all-out war between the Alliance and Horde.$B$BThe rest of us agree, you\'ve proven yourself an invaluable member of the Council of Shadows and the Uncrowned.$B$BCongratulations, Shadowblade $n!',0),
(37690,'enUS','Who goes there?$B$BAre you an emissary from that bizarre floating city?',0),
(37727,'enUS','Capital! A prodigious start.$B$BI implore you to create this marvelous mixture for yourself. I want to share the delight of alchemical spirits with the world!$B$BYou\'ll need to get more eggs for yourself, though.',0),
(37728,'enUS','I was going to present this to one of the ladies of the court. Doing so might increase my standing in certain social circles.$B$BBut, I just can\'t bring myself to do it. Who better to drink my latest masterpiece than, well... me?',0),
(37729,'enUS','Exemplary work, young $n. With runes like these, you\'ll be graduating in no time.',0),
(37730,'enUS','She... she gave you her key? My word!',0),
(37733,'enUS','That\'s him, behind me.',0),
(37736,'enUS','Your hat and robes don\'t match, but you still look better. I hardly recognize you.',0),
(37756,'enUS','Very good, Commander! Brackenspore\'s infestation will not be spreadin\' to da rest of Draenor.',0),
(37757,'enUS','Ko\'ragh be defeated. You be as strong as dey say, commander. I be proud to be at your side.',0),
(37758,'enUS','A brilliant victory, commander! Imperator Mar\'gok be defeated. You indeed be a champion of da Horde!',0),
(37762,'enUS','Well done, commander. With da Heart of da Mountain defeated, you have crippled the ability of da Blackrock clan to use their most powerful furnace.',0),
(37763,'enUS','Well done, commander! Not since Garrosh Hellscream commanded our forces in Northrend have I seen such decisive action.',0),
(37764,'enUS','Brilliant work, commander. Without da mind of Admiral Gar\'an behind it, da Iron Horde\'s naval fleet be greatly diminished.',0),
(37765,'enUS','One of da most ruthless orcs to walk any land be defeated. You be havin\' my congratulations, and my thanks.',0),
(37766,'enUS','Excellent! Brackenspore\'s infestation will not spread to the rest of Draenor. Thank you, commander.',0),
(37767,'enUS','Great work! Ko\'ragh is defeated. You truly are as powerful as they say.',0),
(37768,'enUS','Well done! A great blow has been dealt this day.',0),
(37769,'enUS','Well done, commander! With the Heart of the Mountain defeated, the Blackrock will have nothing to wield but sticks and stones.',0),
(37770,'enUS','With Kromog defeated, we won\'t seeing as many Iron Horde machines rolling out to the front lines. You\'ve saved a lot of lives today, commander.',0),
(37771,'enUS','Great work, commander! We\'ll wrest control of the seas yet!',0),
(37772,'enUS','So it\'s done, then? The foundry is in shambles. We\'ve delivered a mighty blow today, commander. Great work!',0),
(37773,'enUS','Excellent, this must be the crystal Eksos keeps talking about. We\'ll get top men studying this right away.',0),
(37774,'enUS','Perfect, sir. I\'m glad we won\'t have to worry about saberon spirits on top of everything else that\'s trying to murder us.',0),
(37775,'enUS','Word is already spreading of your epic fight, commander. This may improve relations with the ogres in the future.',0),
(37776,'enUS','Thank you, commander. We hope the intel we gather from the Tanaan Channel will prove very useful in the coming months.',0),
(37777,'enUS','Excellent. This meat ought to keep those pesky saberon busy.',0),
(37778,'enUS','Thank you, commander. We will get to work on this right away!',0),
(37780,'enUS','Another agent of Gul\'dan be fallin\' before your might, commander. Gul\'dan will surely be tremblin\' at the heels of our victory dis day.',0),
(37781,'enUS','Da Bloodmaul be finished, and with dem Imperator Mar\'gok\'s chances of acquirin\' da relic within da slag mines.$B$BDs be a good day, mon.',0),
(37782,'enUS','Derailing da Grimrail be a mighty blow to da Iron Horde. It will take dem a great deal of time to amass more troops thanks to you.',0),
(37783,'enUS','Without Skulloc and their precious docks, da Iron Horde be a wolf pack trapped within their own cave... unable to hunt.',0),
(37784,'enUS','I already be feelin\' da relief of da ancestral spirits of Draenor with Ner\'zhul\'s fall. You have deprived Grommash of a powerful weapon, commander.',0),
(37785,'enUS','Perhaps now da Adherents of Rukhmar will respect we \'lesser races\'.',0),
(37786,'enUS','Dese wizards\' deaths be punishment enough for their lack of foresight. We should be thankful dat we were able to stop da overgrowth before it reached our world.',0),
(37787,'enUS','With Warlord Zaela\'s fall we can be focusin\' our efforts on Draenor and da heart of da Iron Horde. They have nowhere to hide now.',0),
(37789,'enUS','With Warlord Zaela out of the picture we can focus our efforts on Draenor and the heart of the Iron Horde. They have nowhere to hide now.',0),
(37790,'enUS','I wish we could have saved the mages\' lives, but sadly it was not to be. We should be thankful that we were able to stop the overgrowth before it reached our world.',0),
(37791,'enUS','Perhaps now the Adherents of Rukhmar will respect we \'lesser races\'.',0),
(37792,'enUS','I\'m no shaman, far from it, but even I can feel the relief of the ancestral spirits of Draenor with Ner\'zhul\'s fall. You have deprived Grommash of a powerful weapon, commander.',0),
(37793,'enUS','Without Skulloc and their precious docks, the Iron Horde won\'t be launching any attacks for a good long time!',0),
(37794,'enUS','Derailing the Grimrail is a mighty blow to the Iron Horde. It will take them a great deal of time to amass more troops thanks to you.',0),
(37795,'enUS','The Bloodmaul are finished, and with them Imperator Mar\'gok\'s chances of acquiring the relic within the slag mines.$B$BThis is as fine a day as I\'ve seen in some time.',0),
(37796,'enUS','Well done, commander. Gul\'dan will surely tremble at the heels of our victory this day.',0),
(37811,'enUS','This matches the description of what Dr. Jones was looking for. I\'ll make sure it makes it to him. $B$BHere is your reward, $C.',0),
(37813,'enUS','You always be savin\' da day, commander. Thank you.',0),
(37814,'enUS','Da spirits smile upon ya, commander. Thank you for all you do.',0),
(37815,'enUS','Word already be spreadin\' about your exploits. If da ogres did not fear your strength yet, dey should now.',0),
(37816,'enUS','A thousand thank yous, commander. Dis spyin\' should prove valuable in da comin\' months.',0),
(37817,'enUS','Dis be exactly what we need, commander. I\'ll send it to da chefs right away.',0),
(37818,'enUS','Excellent. Dis be exactly what we lookin\' for!',0),
(37819,'enUS','You made it! This is just a practice race so your time doesn\'t matter... other than bragging rights.$B$BTime to try the real race!',0),
(37834,'enUS','Hand it here - gently now - ah, do you feel it? Makes my skin crawl. It\'s watching us, $n.$B$BI have invited the Shadow Council into my house. Let\'s get this over with before this thing can cause any mischief.',0),
(37835,'enUS','Well done, $n! I find it troubling that the Shadow Council is so entrenched in these hidden regions of Draenor. Gul\'dan has kept himself busy.',0),
(37836,'enUS','Garona remains shaken, but she is with us now. She is eager to plot revenge against her former master!$B$BI shall consider forgiving her for stabbing me.',0),
(37837,'enUS','Well done, both of you!$B$BGul\'dan is even more slippery than I imagined. He\'s been building up his power base behind the scenes, and now that we\'ve weakened his foes, he\'s moved in to take control of what remains of the Iron Horde.$B$BWe need to plan our next move.',0),
(37838,'enUS','$C, I know that I have done little to earn your trust. Until you freed me, my life was not my own.$B$BYour tenacity, and the wisdom of your Archmage, have finally set me free. You had faith in me even when I had no faith in myself. You have given me back my life, and now I freely pledge it to you. I will serve you here on Draenor until my dying day.$B$BPoint me at your enemies, and I will deliver unto them a swift and silent end... Commander.',0),
(37839,'enUS','You have earned this, $C. You\'ve traveled the length and breadth of my world. You\'ve surmounted unimaginable odds and stood toe-to-toe against ancient beasts, dark magics, and terrifying machines. Time and again you\'ve inspired my people with your patience and bravery.$B$BThank you, $n.',0),
(37840,'enUS','You have earned this, $C. You\'ve traveled the length and breadth of this savage world. You\'ve surmounted unimaginable odds and stood toe-to-toe against ancient beasts, dark magics, and terrifying machines. Time and again you\'ve surprised me with your patience and bravery.$B$BThank you, $n. I am proud to call you my friend.',0),
(37841,'enUS','We meet again.$B$BNow that you have a shipyard, let\'s talk about next steps...',0),
(37852,'enUS','I\'m glad to see this out of the claws of the Adherents of Rukhmar. $B$BI\'ll get this to Dr. Jones right away.',0),
(37853,'enUS','Thank you. Your efforts dull his pain.$B$B<She sighs.>',0),
(37855,'enUS','Don\'t you worry, small one. I am still back in Azurewing Repose, resting in my pool.$B$BIt doesn\'t take much energy to throw a projection of myself here and there. I may be old and dying, but I AM still a blue dragon.',0),
(37856,'enUS','Twelve withered slain? Very good.$B$BThat should be enough to keep them away for a few months.',0),
(37857,'enUS','They\'re tapping into the ley lines?',0),
(37858,'enUS','...so many of them...',0),
(37859,'enUS','I owe you a great debt, $n.$B$BHelping a weakened old dragon like me is valorous enough. Saving my whelplings, and securing the future of our bloodline?$B$BI am now firmly committed to your cause.',0),
(37861,'enUS','He may not be slain, but at least he is gone.$B$BWithout their leader, the mindless withered should soon scatter and die.',0),
(37862,'enUS','No... we\'re too late!',0),
(37868,'enUS','Good job, and nice time!',0),
(37885,'enUS','I\'ll make sure this gets to Dr. Jones. $B$BTo be honest, I\'m eager to get it off my hands.',0),
(37889,'enUS','The landing was easier than I expected, but there is trouble ahead.',0),
(37890,'enUS','It be good ta hear da road is safer, but here be another problem.',0),
(37891,'enUS','Welcome back, commander. Our scouts just returned with word of your success.$B$BWell done!',0),
(37910,'enUS','Good job, and nice time!',0),
(37911,'enUS','Good job, and nice time!',0),
(37919,'enUS','Who would\'ve thought that such a normal looking spear would be able to take down a full-sized Gronn? $B$BI\'m sure Dr. Jones will appreciate this in his collection.',0),
(37934,'enUS','We be movin\' supplies through here now. We finda good place to build!',0),
(37935,'enUS','The easy part is done, now comes the hard part.',0),
(37940,'enUS','Word of your success has already been passed on by our scouts. $B$BLok\'tar!',0),
(37945,'enUS','This definitely looks like no Laughing Skull mask I\'ve seen before. I\'ll take it to Jones and see what he makes of it. $B$BHe left me with this payment for you.',0),
(37948,'enUS','Word is already spreading of your epic fight, commander. This may improve relations with the ogres in the future.',0),
(37949,'enUS','Word already be spreadin\' about your exploits. If da ogres did not fear your strength yet, dey should now.',0),
(37957,'enUS','Keep your distance from that one, $n.$B$BThose fallen elves are all the same. As two-faced as they come.',0),
(37959,'enUS','<Runas feverishly crushes the jewels and gets to work rubbing magical dust on his face, arms, and back.>$B$B<He is, for the moment, in bliss.>',0),
(37960,'enUS','I do feel a bit stronger.$B$BThose siphons nearly did me in, $n.',0),
(37961,'enUS','What great shape this stuff is in. Yeah, honest! I think I can work with this junk. Give me just a minute here...',0),
(37964,'enUS','This place is absolutely crawling with guards. I don\'t know how Garona can be so confident.$B$BAh well, let me brief you on the plan, such as it is...',0),
(37968,'enUS','Welcome back, commander. Our scouts just returned with word of your success.$B$BWell done!',0),
(37979,'enUS','This is incredible! I would never be able to tell that this crystal was once broken! $B$BI\'m sure Dr. Jones will be pleased to see this, as well as the draenei if the stories behind it are true.',0),
(37981,'enUS','You did it. You really did it! Here\'s your winnings, champ.$B$BMan, the Highmaul ogres are not going to like this...',0),
(37991,'enUS','Hail, $C. We could use your aid.',0),
(37992,'enUS','Excellent, mon! I be takin dis to Jones right away. $B$BHere be your reward.',0),
(37993,'enUS','It\'s good we got dis and not da arakkoa.$B$BJones will be wantin dis, I\'m sure.',0),
(37994,'enUS','Dis book be a bad ting, mon. I\'m glad we got it before it came into da wrong hands. $B$BI\'ll get it ta Jones for ya.',0),
(37995,'enUS','Jones will be happy when he sees dis. $B$BHere\'s da payment he promised.',0),
(37996,'enUS','Dis be an odd mask for a Laughing Skull, to be sure. $B$BJones left dis reward for ya.',0),
(37997,'enUS','Astoundin, mon! I\'d a never been able ta tell dis was eva broken. $B$BHere\'s da reward dat Jones left, I\'ll get dis to im.',0),
(38001,'enUS','We have quite a war on our hands. At least we do not lack for targets to strike!',0),
(38014,'enUS','That will have to do for now.',0),
(38015,'enUS','Well done. I saw the other drakes take to the skies.$B$BAnd look! You found Emmigosa!$B$BIt seems she\'s taken a shine to you, $n. I trust you\'ll keep her safe for now.',0),
(38035,'enUS','Thank you for your cooperation.',0),
(38036,'enUS','Just in time! I was about to start bandaging wounds with leaves.',0),
(38044,'enUS','I already have reports of Bleeding Hollow hunters falling back to Zeth\'Gol. This will give us a good edge in the battles to come.',0),
(38045,'enUS','Well done, commander! The Bleeding Hollow are sending their best warriors back to Zeth\'Gol to defend it.$B$BThis should give us an advantage, albeit temporarily.',0),
(38046,'enUS','I\'m already hearing reports from The Iron Front that the tide of the battle has turned.$B$BSoon, The Iron Horde will have nowhere to run!',0),
(38047,'enUS','Thanks to your aid, we have gained a foothold at The Iron Front. Soon, Gul\'dan and the Iron Horde will have nowhere else to run.',0),
(38052,'enUS','Don\'t worry about the ship - it\'s just wood and metal.$B$BThe Skyfire lives on as long as we keep fighting.',0),
(38053,'enUS','NUTS and BOLTS!$B$BPardon my language.$B$BThis thing is almost as dead as the guy you took it from. We need juice, and lots of it. I have an idea...',0),
(38057,'enUS','<Though his eyes are open, the soldier does not respond to your presence. An electrical field buzzes around him.>',0),
(38060,'enUS','The distress signal got through. We\'ll be evacuated to Greywatch immediately.$B$BI\'m afraid that, for now, you will have to continue on your mission without us. Once we are settled, I will send out recon patrols to see if we can glean the location of the Aegis.$B$BYou must secure the Aegis of Aggramar if we are to drive back the Legion threat!',0),
(38142,'enUS','The forest already whispers of Malfurion\'s return. There are few among us who have not heard of his deeds.$B$BThe trees said he also travels with a companion, one named $n. Are you he?',0),
(38143,'enUS','<The Archdruid\'s deep, shallow breaths rumble across the chamber.>',0),
(38144,'enUS','Excellent. The chambers are clear. Very impressive, $C.',0),
(38145,'enUS','Well done, hero. With my brethren at my side, we will be ready to aid Malfurion.',0),
(38146,'enUS','Graw was the first to succumb to the madness, and the rest of the clan followed.$B$BWith these, I will take the reins as our clan\'s new chieftain.$B$BThank you, traveler. I will do my best to rebuild my clan.',0),
(38147,'enUS','In my dreams, I saw the satyr\'s leader. His face was familiar, though I could not see it clearly.$B$BI pray to Elune that it is not too late. I will go to Malfurion at once.',0),
(38148,'enUS','Wonderful. The Archdruids have already assembled.',0),
(38175,'enUS','Here ya are, commander. We\'ve got to let the forges cool for a while, but we should be ready to process more scraps tomorrow.',0),
(38176,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(38177,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(38178,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(38179,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(38180,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(38181,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(38182,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(38183,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(38184,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(38185,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(38186,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(38187,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(38188,'enUS','Very good, commander. This should prove useful to your troops.',0),
(38189,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(38190,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(38191,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(38192,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(38193,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(38195,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(38196,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(38197,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(38198,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(38199,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(38200,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(38201,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(38203,'enUS','Thank you, outsider! Thank you very much.$B$BYou have done more for me than my own people ever have.$B$BLady Challiane would never take the word of a lowly cellarman over her vintners.$B$BNow I can use this recipe to earn her favor, and then the favor of our beloved queen Azshara...',0),
(38206,'enUS','Are you with us?',0),
(38210,'enUS','I\'m sure your head is filled with questions. Answers will come, in time.$B$BI am Havi, and my words are those of the Valarjar - the glorious keepers of the Halls of Valor. $B$BYou will need my help if it is the Aegis you seek. Oh yes, I know your goals outsider. As I know many things...',0),
(38213,'enUS','This tome looks like the one Iskar used to carry. What could have caused him to leave it?',0),
(38223,'enUS','Thank you, $n.$B$BThis was no easy task and I am grateful once again for your assistance. Iskar\'s madness must be stopped.$B$BI trust that when the time comes you will be ready.',0),
(38225,'enUS','May peace again fill our sacred grove.',0),
(38232,'enUS','Mmmm. Olives. I love these things. They are the only reason worth to come to this filthy world.',0),
(38235,'enUS','Your arrival was a blessing, friend.$B$BAnde\'thoras-ethil.',0),
(38237,'enUS','Great deal right? You got to kill a demon, your fancy weapon got more fancy, and I get to be the master now. Everybody wins!',0),
(38241,'enUS','So it\'s as I imagined, a battle-stone!$B$BI\'ve been able to collect similar stones here in Draenor, but never one this large! A rare find indeed.',0),
(38242,'enUS','Ah sure, I be findin\' stones like this everywhere in Draenor, but never one dis big!',0),
(38243,'enUS','It\'s been a pleasure trading with you.',0),
(38246,'enUS','Thank you, $n! My nephew is returned to me.$B$BHe explains that the source of the madness comes from a powerful totem, deep in our village. $B$BIt makes sense, but who - or WHAT - gave us such a thing?$B$BI will share this knowledge with the druids at once.',0),
(38250,'enUS','Welcome back, commander. Our scouts just returned with word of your success.$B$BWell done!',0),
(38252,'enUS','Welcome back, General. Our scouts just returned with word of your success.$B$BWell done!',0),
(38253,'enUS','<The King is studying maps of Tanaan Jungle and the surrounding area.>$B$B$n! The Alliance owes you a great debt for establishing this garrison. Thanks to your bravery and commanding leadership, we\'ve fought this war here on Draenor, instead of amongst our own homes and farmsteads.$B$BIt\'s time now to finish this. Are you ready for the final campaign?',0),
(38254,'enUS','Roark is definitely in this prisoner train but it\'s locked tight. We\'ll have to - oh - you brought explosives? Naielle thinks of everything! Let\'s crack this car open and see if we can convince that engineer to defect...',0),
(38255,'enUS','Lower your weapon, stranger. Blackhand is dead and our new \"Warchief\" just signed my death sentence. It looks like I\'m going mercenary.$B$BYou want to build a shipyard? Then you want me.',0),
(38256,'enUS','<Solog Roark takes in the view of his harbor one final time.>$B$BWe built it all for nothing, $C. Gul\'dan will claim whatever your troops do not destroy.$B$BNext time, I will build something that will last.',0),
(38257,'enUS','Commander! I was told to expect you. The situation here is chaos.$B$BMy Rangari have had this place under surveillance since your original assault. It\'s come back to life in recent weeks as the remnants of the Iron Horde flee to Tanaan under Gul\'dan\'s orders.$B$BMy scouts have learned something that might interest you...',0),
(38258,'enUS','You found us a shipwright then? Good! Some of your followers are eager to take to the open seas.',0),
(38259,'enUS','<Roark scans the horizon.>$B$BYes, here. A good natural bay. The remains of that old warship can be gutted and turned into your first transport.$B$BI see you\'ve gathered all the materials we need. Are you ready?',0),
(38267,'enUS','Ah, $n. You\'re just in time.$B$BAktar says the Shadow Council are teaching the Sethekk their vile ways. There are even a group of High Arakkoa that have joined the Shadow Council\'s banner!$B$BI wonder how does Iskar factor into this?',0),
(38269,'enUS','Ah, $n. You\'re just in time.$B$BAktar says the Shadow Council are teaching the Sethekk their vile ways. There are even a group of High Arakkoa that have joined the Shadow Council\'s banner!$B$BI wonder how does Iskar factor into this?',0),
(38270,'enUS','You... remember me? I came through the portal with you. I was called... Ariok. Before I became this.',0),
(38271,'enUS','Old earth... old blood. I smell Kilrogg. He has been here.',0),
(38272,'enUS','You step on hallowed ground, invader. Here the chieftains of the Bleeding Hollow have performed rituals to see the future.$B$BYou should die but there is much at stake...',0),
(38274,'enUS','Bah. Kilrogg not here. Only omens and warnings. That is your path $n, mine is to destroy Kilrogg...',0),
(38286,'enUS','<The Tidestone of Golganneth stands whole and unprotected.>',0),
(38287,'enUS','It\'s been a pleasure trading with you.',0),
(38290,'enUS','It\'s been a pleasure trading with you.',0),
(38293,'enUS','It\'s been a pleasure trading with you.',0),
(38296,'enUS','It\'s been a pleasure trading with you.',0),
(38299,'enUS','Not bad. Not bad at all. Stop by the next time I\'m in the neighborhood, and I might have some new pets to check out.',0),
(38300,'enUS','Not bad. Not bad at all. Stop by the next time I\'m in the neighborhood, and I might have some new pets to check out.',0),
(38306,'enUS','<Estelle pages through the damaged tome and sighs wistfully.>$B$BOh dear, another paramour dead! Draenor has a terrible habit of eating my lovers alive.',0),
(38307,'enUS','Satisfied?',0),
(38312,'enUS','That looks like it\'ll do the job nicely. $B$BLet\'s get in there before we\'re spotted.',0),
(38317,'enUS','Finally, I can get back to the action!',0),
(38318,'enUS','You should\'ve seen the look on those vrykuls\' faces when you came sailing over their wall! $B$BI could see that launcher coming in handy in a lot of places. You\'d best hold on to it.',0),
(38322,'enUS','Wonderful. The Archdruids have already assembled.',0),
(38323,'enUS','Thaon will be dearly missed. We may not have always seen eye to eye, but he was a great druid and a true protector of the vale.$B$BXavius will pay for his death...',0),
(38324,'enUS','Ah yes, these will do. $B$BNow lets see what we can make to fool old Guarm, eh?',0),
(38331,'enUS','Hah, you throw like a shieldmaiden!$B$BWhat? That\'s a good thing! $B$BTry the stew, young champion, and savor the taste of a task well done.',0),
(38332,'enUS','<Nathanos narrows his eyes at the wreckage of Sylvanas\' ship.>$B$BShe\'s out there... she has to be.',0),
(38337,'enUS','Good thinking gathering up these scales. $B$BIt should be simple enough to make a solid piece of armor from them.',0),
(38339,'enUS','Wait... ye killed how many kvaldir? Yer braver than I thought, outsider!$B$BI\'m sure Helya will see that neither ye nor I belong here once we get past that dog of hers.',0),
(38342,'enUS','Well, there\'s no stopping you, is there?',0),
(38344,'enUS','Oh now, this brings back some memories. Y\'didn\'t look at the scores did you?$B$BThis belonged to ol\' Nolan, may he rest in peace. Not a very good explorer, but a helluva drinker.',0),
(38345,'enUS','These are in great condition. Nolan would be green with envy.',0),
(38346,'enUS','Excellent work. I knew you\'d be useful, sugarplum.$B$BThere\'s something very unusual about these coins...',0),
(38347,'enUS','That was a truly revolting, outsider. Even in death I\'ve never witnessed such a disgusting smell.',0),
(38351,'enUS','I see you found Varsha. Now, keep him supplied with waystones and we will be well on our way to defeating the iron horde.',0),
(38354,'enUS','I see you found Apprentice Var\'nath. Now, keep him supplied with waystones and we will be well on our way to defeating the iron horde.',0),
(38356,'enUS','This is the best Draenor has to offer? Lucky for you I went to engineering school. One Tune-O-Tron 5000 coming up!',0),
(38357,'enUS','The R.A.S. is nothing if not humane.',0),
(38358,'enUS','Wonderful, just put that down anywhere. Careful not to spill it!$B$B<The apothecary snickers.>',0),
(38360,'enUS','So, she escaped after all...',0),
(38361,'enUS','They have only begun to pay for their insolence.',0),
(38362,'enUS','Look carefully at this head, $n. This is what comes to those who stand against the Forsaken.$B$BFor now, we should begin our search for the Aegis of Agrammar. I will send some scouts out to discern its location. You should start your search as well. $B$BWhat are you waiting for?',0),
(38376,'enUS','I owe you my life, $n. We all do.',0),
(38377,'enUS','Behold, Ysera, the Emerald Queen.',0),
(38381,'enUS','Welcome, traveler.',0),
(38382,'enUS','Cenarius will have my aid once my grove has been made safe.',0),
(38384,'enUS','Cenarius is in need? Lord of the Forest, we shall not fail you...',0),
(38394,'enUS','Y\'know, I think we might be on to somethin\' big here.',0),
(38395,'enUS','That wasn\'t so hard now was it, peaches?$B$B<Estelle holds the coins you brought up the the light and practically purrs.>$B$BYes yes, these are so very strange...',0),
(38396,'enUS','Good, good! I\'ve got some awful suspicious suspicions about these here suspicious coins.',0),
(38397,'enUS','Honeybiscuit, when this is all over, you and I may be remembered as stumbling on a great paranormal discovery. Or I will at least.',0),
(38399,'enUS','Ah yes, an eternium rose. I heard vendors suddenly stopped buying them... something about the resell value being too low.$B$BYou\'re in luck though, because I know a collector who still wants them. In fact, I can take this one off your hands, but you\'ll have to come back tomorrow if you have another one to sell.',0),
(38402,'enUS','Aye, I\'ve been talkin\' to the priests in the Mystic Ward and they confirmed my sucpicions. These \'misprinted\' coins are all demonic in origin.$B$BYeh done a good deed takin\' these out of circulation. Well done, $n!',0),
(38404,'enUS','I am most gracious for your services. So many coins! Such a foul energy within them - do you feel it? Somebody was trying to corrupt the draenei from within.$B$BWell, don\'t you worry your pretty head any. My colleagues and I will take VERY good care of these. Thank you, lovely!',0),
(38405,'enUS','Excellent. These should do well to protect you from the storm.',0),
(38406,'enUS','This big fella must have been growing for years. To be honest, it\'s so cute I\'ll probably just let it go. Maybe you can catch it again one day!',0),
(38407,'enUS','You say you found this message in a bottle? How quaint.$B$BYes, I can point you in the right direction, but are you sure you want to take on the sea giant prince and his skrogs? Just to free a bunch of unwashed sailors?',0),
(38410,'enUS','Hah! I bet they never saw that coming!$B$BSeems like we\'ve got no shortage of obstacles left, though.',0),
(38412,'enUS','You are here for the trial? I\'m afraid you might be too late.$B$BThis battle with these Felskorn has taken its toll. I am too weak to grant you the power you seek...$B$BBut perhaps you may be able to help...',0),
(38413,'enUS','I am truly indebted to you for this act. My siblings were not able to defend themselves against the Felskorn, and would have ended up their slaves. $B$BYou are a true friend of the Thorignir.',0),
(38414,'enUS','I am relieved to hear that our mother is safe. $B$BI am sure she will wish to thank you herself.',0),
(38415,'enUS','I know the battle for Tanaan presses sorely on your forces commander. I am glad you came. The Sargerei and Gul\'dan have the same masters, so this new attack likely affects you as well.',0),
(38416,'enUS','This is unfortunate. We cannot allow Gorefiend to aid Gul\'dan\'s machinations. He must be slain once and for all.',0),
(38421,'enUS','I am glad you came at once. Something terrible is brewing beneath this holy place.',0),
(38428,'enUS','<Tentatively, the pup licks your hand. After receiving a good scratch behind the ears, the pup barks and wags its tail.>',0),
(38435,'enUS','The landing was easier than I expected but there is trouble ahead.',0),
(38436,'enUS','Our forces can finish driving off the remaining lurkers. But there\'s another problem up ahead.',0),
(38440,'enUS','Welcome back, commander. Our scouts just returned with word of your success.$B$BWell done!',0),
(38441,'enUS','Word of your success has already been passed on by our scouts. $B$BLok\'tar!',0),
(38443,'enUS','He is... he\'s dying! Senegos is possibly the oldest dragon alive. We cannot simply let him slip away.$B$BThere is something not quite right with the magic energy here, I can feel it.',0),
(38444,'enUS','Don\'t worry, I have a taskforce coming in a bit to clean the rest up. We should move before their runners get back to Gul\'dan.',0),
(38445,'enUS','The easy part is done, now comes the hard part.',0),
(38446,'enUS','This will be a difficult campaign to be sure.',0),
(38449,'enUS','Welcome back, General. Our scouts just returned with word of your success.$B$BWell done!',0),
(38455,'enUS','The conflict against the furbolgs is abated, for now.',0),
(38458,'enUS','I was too late to give you the message. I am truly sorry. These poor shaman... if only I had known sooner!$B$BGul\'dan has prepared everything for his ritual. He will use the cipher and his own fel magic to corrupt an elemental lord and use it to sunder the elemental link to the land. This will cause a massive upheaval across Draenor!',0),
(38459,'enUS','I\'m sure your head is filled with questions. Answers will come, in time.$B$BI am Havi, and my words are those of the Valarjar - the glorious keepers of the Halls of Valor. $B$BYou will need my help if it is the Aegis you seek. Oh yes, I know your goals outsider. As I know many things...',0),
(38460,'enUS','At last! A minion of my very own!',0),
(38462,'enUS','Not a moment too soon. He has summoned something, I fear the ritual is close to complete.',0),
(38463,'enUS','You have saved us all. The Cipher has become fragmented with Cyrukh\'s death. This means its guardians can hide the shards all over Draenor so the chances of piecing it together will be impossible.$B$BThis victory will echo through the halls of your warriors and spur them to greater deeds. Gul\'dan can continue plotting... he will fail...',0),
(38473,'enUS','It\'s good to see you, $n. Greymane sent me away to scout this village for more information on the Aegis. $B$BI haven\'t gleaned much so far, other than that the locals here don\'t seem so friendly. Of course, when are they ever?$B$BI hope your search fares better.',0),
(38499,'enUS','Fascinating...',0),
(38500,'enUS','Excellent work! This new flux may do wonders for other craftable materials as well.',0),
(38501,'enUS','Of course! They\'ve found their way around the welding problem by simply crafting their armor out of one solid piece of metal.$B$BThe shoulderpads I should have figured out on my own, but their work on the breastplate really is remarkable.$B$BHere, let me jot down a few patterns so you can make these yourself.',0),
(38502,'enUS','If my guess is correct, the answer to our welding problem lies within this core.',0),
(38505,'enUS','Oh, a memory core? One moment.',0),
(38506,'enUS','...is what I would say if we weren\'t floating directly above the ancestral home of the Highborne. You need this translated or something?',0),
(38507,'enUS','I hadn\'t even thought far enough ahead to realize you\'d need this to be translated, too. Good thinking.$B$BSee, this is why I keep adventurers like you around the shop.',0),
(38513,'enUS','You, outsider, think yourself worthy of our wisdom?',0),
(38514,'enUS','The craftsmanship is good, but the quality is feeble at best.$B$B<Barm snaps the gauntlets in half and throws them to floor>$B$BYou have proven yourself worthy of my tutelage however.',0),
(38515,'enUS','Excellent work. Let\'s get these turned into flux right away.',0),
(38518,'enUS','I see, the strength of their work comes from the technique of their hammer strikes. Very interesting...',0),
(38519,'enUS','Thank you, $n.$B$BThank you.',0),
(38522,'enUS','Let me take those bars, make a few adjustments and...$B$BTa da! Hoofplates for your mount!',0),
(38523,'enUS','Now that Mei\'s fit the plates to your mount, you should be able to put them on easily yourself.$B$BOh, and before I forget, here\'s the pattern. Enjoy!',0),
(38524,'enUS','You here to lend us a hand?',0),
(38525,'enUS','That\'ll do.',0),
(38526,'enUS','Not bad, $C. You know how to swing a hammer.',0),
(38527,'enUS','Good. Now let\'s get to work.',0),
(38528,'enUS','Solid work.$B$BLeystone is a fickle metal. Its armguards benefit from the addition of brimstone, but to improve the production of shoulderpads? Enchanting dust. Helms benefit from uncarved gemstones. And so on.',0),
(38530,'enUS','You have returned, $n. Have you come for more training?$B$BWhat? The Firmament Stone?$B$B$B$BThat\'s another matter entirely.',0),
(38531,'enUS','<The tauren carefully looks over your handiwork, brows furrowed.>$B$BYou\'ve learned some things, I see.$B$BVery well. You have succeeded.',0),
(38532,'enUS','<Barm examines the hammer, turning it slowly in his hands.>$B$BNow THIS is a hammer!',0),
(38533,'enUS','I wouldn\'t expect the tauren to part with their recipes easily. We are not quite as... bull-headed as they are, but even our recipes will come at a price.$B$BStill, you have earned access to the Firmament Stone, and proven the path to another great anvil, should Urael and I need it.$B$BYou have earned this recipe, as a token of our thanks.',0),
(38534,'enUS','The armguards you\'ve made are impressive, but you can provide the same level of protection without wasting so much raw material.$B$BHere, let me show you.',0),
(38536,'enUS','Excellent smithing.$B$BNow, allow me to show you a trick I use to conserve resources.',0),
(38537,'enUS','Your anvilwork is to be commended, but the recipe you\'re using is unnecessarily wasteful.$B$BTry this instead.',0),
(38538,'enUS','We don\'t tend to smith many boots up here, but even I can tell that you\'re using too much metal for the sole.$B$BHere\'s a way to cut back on your resource costs.',0),
(38539,'enUS','The Illidari certainly do like to waste ore, don\'t they?$B$BYou should craft them this way instead. You\'ll thank me later.',0),
(38540,'enUS','Don\'t tell Thala and Barm, but I do keep a few helm patterns around, mainly for amusement and decoration.$B$BTake a look at this one. You\'ll get similar results with much less need for raw material.',0),
(38541,'enUS','Now that you\'ve done it the easy way, try this.$B$BIt\'s more difficult, but it will save you loads of materials.',0),
(38542,'enUS','The amount of ore you\'re wasting on that pattern is simply unacceptable. We should conserve wherever possible: it\'s better for the land and easier on the pocket.$B$BPlease, use this plan instead.',0),
(38558,'enUS','<Overspark examines the crystal carefully.>$B$BYep, still shiny.',0),
(38559,'enUS','A new face? It\'s been years...$B$BThis is the Firmament Stone. Memorize her curves. Learn her intricacies. If you truly wish to push your smithing skill to the next level, I predict that you will be spending a lot of time at her side.',0),
(38561,'enUS','I was too late to give you the message. I am truly sorry. These poor shamans... if only I had known sooner!$B$BGul\'dan has prepared everything for his ritual. He will use the cipher and his own fel magic to corrupt an elemental lord and use it to sunder the elemental link to the land. This will cause a massive upheaval across Draenor!',0),
(38562,'enUS','More of my ancestors\' souls plundered by Gorefiend! This must end once and for all. Gorefiend must be put down!',0),
(38563,'enUS','Now that that\'s all taken care of, we can move on to improving our recipes.',0),
(38564,'enUS','Well done, $n. Now let\'s put her to the test!',0),
(38566,'enUS','We\'ve done it, Highlord $n.$B$BThe Order of the Silver Hand is reborn!',0),
(38567,'enUS','<The Warchief studies a map of Tanaan Jungle and its surroundings, his brow creased with worry.>$B$BAh, Commander $n! Voice of da Horde in Draenor. Ya done well here, bringin\' da fight ta our enemies. Thrall tells me ya exceed his every expectation.$B$BIt be time ta finish dis. Are ya ready?',0),
(38568,'enUS','Commander! I was hoping some backup would arrive. This place is going crazy. The Iron Horde retreated from the Foundry and now, under Gul\'dan\'s orders, they\'re using these docks to flee to Tanaan.$B$BBut my people found something that might interest you, if you act fast...',0),
(38570,'enUS','We confirmed that Solog Roark is aboard this prison train, but it\'s locked up tight. Oh - you brought explosives? Hmph. Those goblin friends of yours are always prepared.$B$BLet\'s bust this box open and convince that shipwright to join our cause...',0),
(38571,'enUS','Lower your weapon, stranger. Blackhand is dead and our new \"Warchief\" just signed my death sentence. It looks like I\'m going mercenary.$B$BYou want to build a shipyard? Then you want me.',0),
(38572,'enUS','<Solog Roark takes in the view of his harbor one final time.>$B$BWe built it all for nothing, $C. Gul\'dan will claim whatever your troops do not destroy.$B$BNext time, I will build something that will last.',0),
(38573,'enUS','Ah, ya found us a shipwright? Good! Ya followers be eager ta take on da open seas.',0),
(38574,'enUS','<Solog Roark scans the horizon.>$B$BThis will do. It\'s a good deepwater harbor. We can gut that old warship down there to make your first transport. Moving supplies up and down these cliffs will be a chore, but they\'ll give us additional security in case we\'re attacked.$B$BWe\'ll make it work. Are you ready to get building?',0),
(38576,'enUS','It is fitting that you are here.$B$BTime and again, you have fought to save our world. Now, I fear I must ask you to undertake an even greater act of service.',0),
(38577,'enUS','Now you see what we face here. We will keep as much pressure here as we can so your base can remain free to attack all over the jungle.',0),
(38578,'enUS','We will speak more of this later, but thank you.',0),
(38581,'enUS','Now you see what we face here. We will keep as much pressure here as we can so your base can remain free to attack all over the jungle.',0),
(38582,'enUS','Know this, $n. You did the only thing you could.$B$BWhen a mortal has become corrupted by the nightmare, there is no return. Only death will set them free.',0),
(38585,'enUS','Welcome back, commander. Our scouts just returned with word of your success.$B$BWell done!',0),
(38586,'enUS','Word of your success has already been passed on by our scouts. $B$BLok\'tar!',0),
(38595,'enUS','Oh, $n...$B$BWhat is becoming of this precious land?',0),
(38599,'enUS','Hey welcome back! The signal\'s coming in loud and clear and the ship\'s good to go!$B$BWhen you\'re ready to head back up just take the rocket for the fastest ride on Draenor! We set it up over near Gargash.',0),
(38603,'enUS','Welcome back!$B$BWe\'re getting a strong feed from those sensors! The crew locked the navigation system on to the signal and everything should be good to go!$B$BWe set the machine up next to Skyguard Thann.',0),
(38611,'enUS','These vrykul are so boring! Why does Nathanos send me on missions like this? Does he really think the Aegis is here?$B$BI hope you\'ve come to stir up some trouble.',0),
(38612,'enUS','Yes, that should do quite nicely.',0),
(38613,'enUS','Those vrykul were so distracted seeing someone flying through their village, they never noticed me slip by. $B$BI hope that didn\'t get you too much unwanted attention.',0),
(38614,'enUS','Well, the sizing might be a bit big, but I think you can make them work. $B$BThat path doesn\'t look pleasant, so it\'ll help to be prepared.',0),
(38615,'enUS','We won\'t have to worry about those scrap heaps anymore! $B$BIt looks like we\'ve got a hitch in our plan though. That bridge was the only way up.',0),
(38616,'enUS','Good thinking. If the vrykul can use the drake scales for their armor, why not us? $B$BIt shouldn\'t be too tough to work this into something serviceable.',0),
(38617,'enUS','What a fight! $B$BAnd here I thought this place would be boring.',0),
(38618,'enUS','You are here for the trial? I\'m afraid you might be too late.$B$BThis battle with these Felskorn has taken its toll. I am too weak to grant you the power you seek...$B$BBut perhaps you may be able to help...',0),
(38624,'enUS','<The raven squawks, and Havi\'s voice fills your head>$B$BYou are indeed mighty, as the trial shows. $B$BBut valor is a different animal - one you think to tame?',0),
(38641,'enUS','You - you bear the mark of The Dreamer. Elune be praised!$B$BYou\'ve arrived just in time, visitor. Shaladrassil\'s roots are at our doorstep...',0),
(38643,'enUS','We don\'t need any help, and we don\'t like strangers wanderin\' around on our land.',0),
(38644,'enUS','I\'m sorry for my suspicion earlier. We\'re all on edge with the recent attacks.$B$BI couldn\'t be more grateful to you and your friend.$B$BThanks to you, our situation is under control now. We\'ve got a lot of rebuilding to do, but we\'ll survive.',0),
(38645,'enUS','Good. These innocent villagers have done nothing to deserve these attacks. You have done well to help them.',0),
(38646,'enUS','Well love, we sure did take care of them! Thank you, $C. Glad ta see I \'aven\'t lost my touch.',0),
(38647,'enUS','All right, I\'ll get those barrels loaded up and delivered to the village in no time.$B$BThank you, $n. There\'ll be a lot of full bellies because of you.',0),
(38649,'enUS','Something is amiss. I can feel it in my bones.',0),
(38655,'enUS','It is as I feared, $R. This corruption is... irreversible.$B$BOur only course of action is to somehow find a way to fight it at its source.',0),
(38656,'enUS','I am impressed that you were able to defeat such a powerful demon. We are fortunate that you have lent us your aid.',0),
(38662,'enUS','Xavius has stolen our sacred artifact?$B$BElune, forgive me. I have failed you.',0),
(38663,'enUS','This is dire news indeed, $n.$B$BDraw upon your courage now, friend, for Azeroth needs her heroes more than ever before.',0),
(38669,'enUS','Good. You spent many years in stasis, but I see that your senses have not dulled.\r\n\r\n<Maiev eyes your weapons warily.>\r\n\r\nRaise your hand against me, demon hunter, and you will find out why I was your master\'s jailor.',0),
(38671,'enUS','It is not much, but it is better than I could have hoped for. You have our gratitude.',0),
(38672,'enUS','<Pull the lever.>',0),
(38672,'esES','<Mueve la palanca.>',22522),
(38675,'enUS','No one is safe from this corruption.',0),
(38684,'enUS','The waking world is slipping further and further from my mind. But on the vestiges of this corruption consuming my mind, I sense Malfurion!',0),
(38687,'enUS','This cannot be!',0),
(38689,'enUS','The color has returned to your face, $n.',0),
(38689,'esES','Te ha vuelto el color a la cara, $n.',22522),
(38690,'enUS','We always knew the Illidari would be called upon to defend this world. It is why we sacrificed everything to become who... WHAT... we are.',0),
(38690,'esES','Siempre supimos que se recurriría a los Illidari para salvar este mundo. Por eso sacrificamos todo, para convertirnos en lo que somos...',22522),
(38691,'enUS','What does the Legion want with Ravencrest? He was dead and buried ten millennia ago.',0),
(38692,'enUS','It had to be done.',0),
(38694,'enUS','Oculeth has anticipated our arrival. Good, one less thing to worry on.',0),
(38695,'enUS','Someone must have informed the Grand Magistrix of Vanthir\'s involvement in the rebellion. Such violence is...$B$BElisande... How could you?',0),
(38710,'enUS','Thank you for helping us gather together, $n. We must stand united.',0),
(38711,'enUS','<Jarod gazes at the ring for a long minute before closing his hands around it. He puts the ring in a pocket.>$B$BThis is Maiev\'s ring. She would never part with it.$B$BShe must be at Black Rook Hold!',0),
(38714,'enUS','Good work, $n. There is no doubt that they have already moved Maiev into the prison cells beneath the tower.',0),
(38715,'enUS','Thank you, $n. May their spirits be at peace.',0),
(38717,'enUS','Good, these keys should open any of the cells within the prison.',0),
(38718,'enUS','The attacking spirits spoke of their lord and master. I fear the Legion has raised Lord Ravencrest to do their bidding. What price was paid for such a sinister revival, I do not know.',0),
(38719,'enUS','The other Illidari did not make it, but I owe you my life. There is one thing I learned during my time in the prisons: the demons within Black Rook Hold must die.',0),
(38720,'enUS','I see you managed to find some survivors. Good, that is a weight off my mind.',0),
(38721,'enUS','Lord Stareye came from a noble house, but in war, he never came close to Ravencrest or my brother.$B$BNow that he is defeated, we can turn our attention to his commander.$B$BHowever, that will be no easy task. We must gather our strength before facing Lord Ravencrest himself.',0),
(38723,'enUS','Excellent. You have absorbed the powers of these brutes. Look how strong you have grown!',0),
(38723,'esES','Excelente. Has absorvido los poderes de estos brutos. ¡Mira qué fuerte te has hecho!',22522),
(38724,'enUS','<Maiev\'s face is bruised, her lips cracked, and her body covered in scars. She looks thin and ragged, but she moves with purpose.>$B$BFor weeks they tried to break me. Amateurs!$B$BI kept my silence. I counted the minutes, measured their steps, and listened to the voices beyond my cell.$B$BI have been waiting for my chance to escape, and to strike back at my captors.$B$BNow, you bring my armor AND my blade. My salvation will be followed by bloodshed.$B$B<Maiev smiles.>',0),
(38725,'enUS','$n. I\'ve found her.',0),
(38725,'esES','$n, la he encontrado.',22522),
(38727,'enUS','True leadership is hard to come by. Leading from the front is an even rarer trait.$B$BWe are just about ready to assail Brood Queen Tyranna\'s command center.',0),
(38727,'esES','Es dificil encontrar a un líder de verdad, pero más aún a alguien está dispuesto a liderar desde el frente.$B$BYa casi estamos preparados para atacar el centro de mando de la reina de la progenie Tyranna',22522),
(38728,'enUS','Now that we have the keystone in our possession, there is just one last thing left to do...',0),
(38728,'esES','Ahora que la piedra angular está en nuestro poder, solo nos queda una cosa por hacer...',22522),
(38729,'enUS','<As you invoke the power of the Sargerite Keystone, the fel portal is suffused with an otherworldly energy.$B$BIt is time to return triumphant to the Black Temple and aid Lord Illidan in repelling the invading forces from Azeroth and Shattrath City.>',0),
(38729,'esES','<Al invocar el poder de la piedra angular sargerita, el portal vil se cubre de energía de otro mundo.$B$BHa llegado el momento de regresar triunfante al Templo Oscuro y ayudar a lord Illidan a expulsar a las tropas invasoras de Azeroth y de la Ciudad de Shattrath.>',22522),
(38743,'enUS','This shall be remembered as one of the darkest days in the history of our world. But hope remains. Elune\'s light has strengthened our resolve.',0),
(38753,'enUS','My husband, Malfurion, what has become of him?!$B$BAnswer me!',0),
(38759,'enUS','Their souls were being sucked dry by a jailer demon?$B$BThe Burning Legion in this place is far more powerful and brutal than we have ever seen before.',0),
(38759,'esES','¿Un Demonio Carcelero se ha estado alimentando de sus almas?$B$BEn este lugar, la Legión Ardiente es más poderosa y brutal que nunca.',22522),
(38765,'enUS','Grim. But demon hunters are no strangers to sacrifice. We have given everything to become what we are.$B$BThe Legion will fall. We await your orders, $n.',0),
(38765,'esES','Es duro, pero los cazadores de Demonios estamos acostumbrados al sacrificio. Al fin y al cabo, lo hemos entregado todo para convertirnos en lo que somos.$B$BLa legión caerá, $n, esperamos tus ordenes.',22522),
(38766,'enUS','Already, the flow of demons from below has slowed to a trickle.$B$BI can sense the doom guard\'s energy. You have become more powerful.',0),
(38766,'esES','El número de demonios que provienen de abajo ya se ha reducido en un goteo.$B$BPuedo sentir la energía del guardia apocalíptico. Te has vuelto más poderoso.',22522),
(38777,'enUS','It\'s so light. So pretty, too! Reminds me of elementium, a bit.$B$BIf you see any more ore like this, try and strike it with the grain. You\'ll waste much less of it.',0),
(38778,'enUS','So it was your footsteps I felt upon my woods as the runestones released their grip? $B$BYou have my thanks, outsider.',0),
(38784,'enUS','Look at that! She\'s a lovely one, isn\'t she?$B$BTreat this type of ore with care, lad. No fat-muscle shoulder swings necessary - just a gentle tap on the right spot and you\'ll extract much more ore than a beginner.',0),
(38785,'enUS','Now isn\'t that somethin\'? You got this offa one of those rocky creatures down there?$B$BLooks like ye only brought me a bit o\' the torso, though. Next time, make sure to get the arms and head too. Lots o\' good meat in there.',0),
(38786,'enUS','You\'ve learned much, $n.$B$BStay a while. I have a story for you.',0),
(38787,'enUS','Echoes of Rethu\'s time in this land still remain, $n. Be on the lookout for his influence when you are out in the field.',0),
(38789,'enUS','This... this cannot be! A piece of Rethu\'s own mining log!$B$BLook here, miner... it details a leystone mining technique he was working on...',0),
(38790,'enUS','Rethu\'s own mining pick...$B$BWell, one of them, anyhow. Stories say he went through them almost weekly.$B$BStill, I\'ve never seen one with my own eyes. Look at the wear on the blade, miner. The angles he used... the strength with which he struck: we could learn much from studying this artifact.',0),
(38791,'enUS','This... this could not be...$B$BThis is from a member my tribe, $n. Where did you find this?$B$BOne of the first stories we ever learn about Rethu involves the day he lost his horn in battle. There is no way of knowing if this belonged to him but... but...',0),
(38792,'enUS','You saw a spirit while out mining in the wilds?$B$BNo, I do not believe you. One mustn\'t spend too long out mining, it fatigues the mind. You must be seeing things.$B$BStill, something seems... different about you. You\'ve learned something. Perhaps there\'s some truth to your tale after all...',0),
(38793,'enUS','<The tauren listens as you describe your encounter with the spirit of Rethu Ironhorn.>$B$BI would not normally believe you, but... I can sense truth in your tale. You are a lucky miner.$B$BI am pleased to know that our ancestors look upon us with pride. We have chosen an admirable path.$B$BThank you, $n.',0),
(38794,'enUS','The spirit of Rethu Ironhorn? Tell me everything he said.$B$BHe said he... dug too deep? I see. The Earthmother took him.$B$BThank you for coming to me, miner. This is a tale that the rest of the tribe must hear. We are all the wiser for it.',0),
(38795,'enUS','This is no natural stone, miner. It stinks of demon\'s blood. Where\'d you find this?$B$BReminds me a bit of old fel iron. Come \'ere, lemme teach you a trick or two on how to properly gather this stuff.',0),
(38796,'enUS','This came out of a cliffside seam? Remember, ye can\'t mine seams like ye mine deposits. Totally different thing. I\'ll show ye my trick.',0),
(38797,'enUS','This came from a blasted infernal? Look out, we\'ve got mister COMBAT miner, here!$B$BSome o\' this ore seems to \'ave lost its shine on the trip back, however. Next time, make sure to cut out the sword and spell wounds before ye mine it.',0),
(38798,'enUS','It is done.$B$BStretch it out a bit.$B$BYou may experience some stray urges to burn worlds and sow chaos for the next week or so. Do your best to resist them.',0),
(38799,'enUS','Yes, this is my sister\'s ring.$B$BThe fact that you found it on a demon\'s corpse suggests that she has either fallen in battle or, like my other sisters, thrown in her hat with the demons themselves.$B$BThank you for bringing this to me. We don\'t have many spare materials here on the front lines... but I can do without these.',0),
(38800,'enUS','It is. This eye once belonged to my sister, Rin\'thissa.$B$BPoor fool, she cut out her own eye and replaced it with a hunk of ore. That was the tipping point... she\'s completely fel-maddened now.$B$BLearn from her mistake, $n.',0),
(38801,'enUS','This was my sister\'s. Lyrelle\'s.$B$BHer fate is clear now. She no longer needed that signet ring... the girl must have traded in her own mining arm for one carved out of felslate itself.$B$BAren\'t you glad we only used three small shards?$B$BTake this to heart, $n: you can lose everything to greed if you don\'t exercise restraint. Poor Lyrelle paid that price for all of us.',0),
(38802,'enUS','My sister Ondri was the first among us to mine, and the first among us to fall. Some Nathrezim dreadlord convinced her to replace her own heart - her heart! - with a chunk of felslate.$B$BI slew the dreadlord myself, but couldn\'t find the heart. This must be it.$B$BBig sister... I am sorry. Your loss will not be forgotten. We will learn from your missteps.',0),
(38803,'enUS','My sister\'s soul rests now. I have you to thank for that.$B$BRin\'thissa was always a charmer. You did well to avoid her invitations, and even better to slay her and end her demonic possession. You\'ve learned much since we first met, $n.',0),
(38804,'enUS','Poor Lyrelle.$B$BI do not blame you for putting her down, $n. I thank you. I hope that you would do the same to me, if I were to slip and fall down that same path.$B$BJust... try to learn something from your ordeal. Reflect on your experience. I would hate to see her sacrifice be for nothing.',0),
(38805,'enUS','My sister\'s villainy is finally at an end.$B$BShe was always the wisest among us. Sad that she had to go out the way she did. I\'m certain there was much she could have taught us.',0),
(38806,'enUS','This odiferous morsel ye\'ve brought me... it\'s infernal brimstone, isn\'t it?$B$BAmazing.$B$BI\'ve heard tales, but I\'ve never actually SEEN the stuff before.$B$BI\'ve got to study this. In the meantime, here\'s all I know about this rare, rare ore.',0),
(38807,'enUS','Fascinating...',0),
(38808,'enUS','These hearts are fat and bloody. $B$BThe slumbering rulers will not refuse an offering of Bjornharta.',0),
(38810,'enUS','Yes, these Soulcaps should be adequate for your ritual. $B$BSpeak with me once you are ready to proceed and I will guide you further.',0),
(38811,'enUS','Ashildir\'s grave has been disturbed, outsider. $B$BDo you know something of this?',0),
(38813,'enUS','Our forces have engaged the Legion.$B$BSoon we will stand together victorious with Lord Illidan at the Black Temple.',0),
(38813,'esES','Nuestras fuerzas han comprometido a la Legión.$B$BPronto nos alzaremos victoriosos junto a lord Illidan en el Templo Oscuro.',22522),
(38815,'enUS','Where... where am I now? $B$BI... know you...',0),
(38816,'enUS','Your glorious battle honors the Valkyra queen.',0),
(38817,'enUS','The treachery of the Bonespeakers knows no limit. $B$BTheir rituals seek to sunder the very essence of our queen, but we will use their own magic to return her to us!',0),
(38818,'enUS','I cannot believe this fate... $B$BI am sorry, outsider, for I had underestimated Faljar\'s power.$B$BThat he could banish us here... is unthinkable.',0),
(38819,'enUS','I am in complete agreement. From where I\'m standing, you utterly decimated their forces.$B$BWhat do you think? Are we ready to fly up to that command center and take the Sargerite Keystone?',0),
(38819,'esES','Estoy completamente de acuerdo. Desde aquí parece que has diezmado completamente sus fuerzas.$B$B¿Qué opinas? ¿Crees que estamos listos para subir al centro de mando y hacernos con la piedra angular sargerita?',22522),
(38823,'enUS','These mystics have gone to great lengths to weaken Ashildir. $B$BWe must hope that her spirit is strong enough for the wakening.',0),
(38833,'enUS','There you have it... demonsteel.$B$BWelcome to the next level of smithing, $n.',0),
(38834,'enUS','The two of you are a welcome sight. We pushed the demons out of these ruins, but they are stronger than any we have encountered before.$B$BYour help is appreciated. If we do not crush this Legion invasion now, they will overrun Azsuna and then the rest of the Broken Isles.',0),
(38857,'enUS','Excellent, my good sir. I cannot thank you enough for the freedom of my people. Rosh is especially appreciative.$B$B<Gentle Rosh grunts.>$B$BPerhaps you and I can do some more business together.',0),
(38862,'enUS','Until I can discover what is vexing the Thistleleaf, I\'ll have to look after the Lunarwing eggs. At least I know they will be safe.',0),
(38872,'enUS','Finally someone competent arrives at this sorry excuse for an outpost. $B$BOur efforts to complete Sylvanas\'s mission are at a standstill, but now we have even more pressing matters on our hands.',0),
(38873,'enUS','Hah! Greymane will find his cannons aren\'t so useful when the blight takes his crew!',0),
(38878,'enUS','I would hope that you bring me some good news, $C. $B$BFor both of our sake.',0),
(38882,'enUS','It looks like we underestimated Greymane\'s tenacity - a mistake that cost the Forsaken dearly. $B$BThis Eyir cannot hide for long, however. If I must I will hunt her through the Halls of Valor! $B$BGo now, $C. I will call upon you when you are needed.',0),
(38888,'enUS','You are indeed a miner. You have the look of it. There is ore in your blood.',0),
(38889,'enUS','You kneel down and hold out a hand. The baby bear sniffs at your fingers, looking up at you trustingly.$B$BThis bear cub is too little to fend for itself. Will you take it with you on your travels?',0),
(38901,'enUS','You want to mine felslate?$B$BDo you really think you have what it takes?$B$BAre you willing to make sacrifices?$B$BGood.',0),
(38904,'enUS','Welcome to Skyhold, hero. Normally one must die to gain entrance, but times have changed.',0),
(38907,'enUS','I know you seek the Pillar of Creation but I am sad to say it was one of many things we lost today.',0),
(38909,'enUS','Riverbend was... destroyed? That disgusting beast Dargrul! I will not stop until I see him dead.$B$BBut we cannot do that with the army we have.$B$BWe need help from the other tribes.',0),
(38910,'enUS','Your bravery has returned to us some of our fine feathered friends. Well done.$B$BNow how do you feel about a frontal assault?',0),
(38911,'enUS','Mayla was still able to send help? I could hug that child.$B$BWelcome, outsider. I am Jale Rivermane, Chieftain of the Rivermane tribe. And we could really use your help.',0),
(38912,'enUS','Outsider, you are one of few from beyond Highmountain who has made it into these woods alive. With me vouching for you, the Bloodtotem have been given a no-kill order by Torok.',0),
(38913,'enUS','Ha ha! And what are you, tiny creature? Have you come to battle us or join us in battle?',0),
(38915,'enUS','That... is a lot of drogbar.',0),
(38916,'enUS','Ah, thank you for coming. Mayla is as stubborn as her father if not more so.',0),
(38922,'enUS','Uncle?',0),
(38923,'enUS','NICE WORK. TOO BAD THE ALLIANCE IS STILL BEATING DOWN OUR GATES! GET BACK OUT THERE!',0),
(38924,'enUS','NICE WORK. TOO BAD THE ALLIANCE IS STILL BEATING DOWN OUR GATES! GET BACK OUT THERE!',0),
(38925,'enUS','Well done. That will give the Horde something to think about next time they decide to test us here in Ashran.',0),
(38926,'enUS','Well done. That will give the Horde something to think about next time they decide to test us here in Ashran.',0),
(38932,'enUS','This is a blueprint for some high tech naval equipment. I should be able to reverse engineer the plans and have this equipment available for you shortly!',0),
(38933,'enUS','Now is the time to strike back against the Legion.',0),
(38935,'enUS','Ha ha! You were sent by Bolo? The \"Keg Mender,\" right? From the Drunken Hozen?$B$BHow is his eye healing? Is his friend still hung over?$B$BAhh... that was an enjoyable evening.',0),
(38936,'enUS','Oh, you are a friend of Cho\'s? Welcome! Welcome!$B$BI would serve you a banquet, but as you can see, we are in dire straights at the moment.$B$BSay, would you be willing to lend us a hand?',0),
(38944,'enUS','Now this... this I can work with!$B$BReminds me of some old night elven festival cloth I\'ve seen.',0),
(38945,'enUS','That\'s a shame. Without the ability to do any stitching, we can hardly do anything with this fabric.$B$B<Tanithria pouts.>$B$BStill, there ARE patterns we know that don\'t require stitching. Shoulderpads are easy, and belts should be a cinch.',0),
(38946,'enUS','My my, look at you! Such an attractive young $C, and all bedecked in magical finery and weaponry. To what do I owe the pleasure?$B$BAha! Tailoring! It\'s your lucky day, er...$B$BI\'m sorry, what was your name? $n?$B$BIt\'s your lucky day, $n! I happen to be one of the best tailors in Suramar...',0),
(38947,'enUS','Perfect. Marvelous!',0),
(38948,'enUS','You, $n, are a person of great skill. I send you out for patterns, and you do so without question. Remarkable!',0),
(38949,'enUS','There you have it!$B$BNo, no, don\'t thank me. I\'m just happy to have been of service.',0),
(38950,'enUS','Your friend certainly has an... interesting appearance.$B$BHe taught you to sew this silk? Hmm. Maybe we should keep him around for a while.',0),
(38951,'enUS','Hmm... he may have a point.$B$BThese needles ARE quite strong, and they have a nice bounce to them. Still, I do take issue with their shape and feel. I have an idea.',0),
(38952,'enUS','Look at these! Strong, light, flexible, sharp, with a refined curve and a smooth edge. You\'ve certainly put your Dalaran touch on it. It\'s the best of both worlds!$B$BEnough fussing over our tools, now. Shall we sew?',0),
(38953,'enUS','Now isn\'t that just lovely. Go on, try it out yourself!',0),
(38954,'enUS','Sorry about that, $n. You caught me snooping around. I suppose my curiosity got the better of me.$B$BAllow me to make it up to you.',0),
(38955,'enUS','There you have it. Not the best bag in the world, but it\'s better than most.$B$BI want to apologize again for running off, $n. My hunger... err, curiosity... occasionally gets the better of me. I promise it will not happen again.',0),
(38956,'enUS','My most sincere apologies, $n. Not only did I make a spectacle of myself, I fear I may have also put the good name of your tailoring shop at risk.$B$BYou have every right to be upset with me.',0),
(38957,'enUS','Aha! This will be much simpler than I\'d first thought.$B$B<Lyndras takes a moment to jot some instructions down on a scrap of vellum.>$B$BHere, $n. You should have it.',0),
(38958,'enUS','Marvelous!',0),
(38959,'enUS','Excellent! It\'s always nice to have familiar things.$B$BThis will make instructing you much easier for me.',0),
(38960,'enUS','This will be plenty.',0),
(38961,'enUS','Lyndras ran off again before you could return, $n. He left a note and a pattern for you.$B$BThe note reads,$B$B\"I\'m sorry, $n, but I\'m afraid I may become a threat to the fellow tailors of this shop. I\'m off to find somewhere to try and control my urges, or fall into depravity. It has been an honor training you.$B$BSincerely,$B$BLyndras\"$B$BHow sad...',0),
(38962,'enUS','Now that you can move safely around the city, it\'s time to find some new masters.',0),
(38963,'enUS','Well done, $n. Before long you may be the one teaching me a thing or two.',0),
(38965,'enUS','<Tanithria listens to your account of Lyndras\' fate.>$B$BI... I see. That\'s a shame.$B$BI had grown to enjoy his company, you know. If you\'ll excuse me, I need a moment to think about him.',0),
(38966,'enUS','The good news is that we can now craft more efficient patterns out of silkweave.$B$BThe bad news is that we\'ve expended the remainder of Lyndras\' knowledge. Where should we turn next?',0),
(38967,'enUS','Ah, a fellow tailor. Pleasure to make your acquaintance, uh... $n, was it?$B$BI trust you\'d like to come into the fold of our guild? Where did you receive your prior training?',0),
(38968,'enUS','Hmm.$B$BVery well. We may continue.',0),
(38969,'enUS','Your stitching is still a little rough, but you\'ve already mastered all of the basics.$B$BWell done.$B$BI don\'t say that very often. Savor it.',0),
(38970,'enUS','Don\'t look at us that way, $n. Selling our services to the demons may have been morally dubious, but our skills have grown exponentially since Azayna made the deal.$B$BContinue your training with us, or don\'t. If you want to leave now, nobody\'s stopping you. If you want to learn more... we are the only game in town.',0),
(38971,'enUS','Excellent work. I will get to studying this fabric right away. As promised, I will teach you what I know. Are you acquainted with our patterns for gloves?',0),
(38974,'enUS','<Tellumi takes the loincloth from you and gives you a sly smile.>$B$BI trust you now see looking at a situation from a functional angle than a reactionary one will earn you far more knowledge.',0),
(38975,'enUS','Not quite what I\'d expected, but it was an interesting history lesson, at least. You can keep the robes, I\'ve learned all I need just by watching you work.$B$BNow, as promised, I shall show you what I know.',0),
(38989,'enUS','Lok\'tar General. Your forces await your orders.',0),
(38990,'enUS','The Lich King made a wise choice in giving you those blades, $n. You\'ve more then proven yourself worthy of them.$B$BI have to admit though, I\'m glad it wasn\'t me, I\'m through with having magical weapons dictate my fate.',0),
(38996,'enUS','Greetings General. Your forces await your orders on the Planning Table.',0),
(39000,'enUS','<Khadgar gingerly looks over the spine of each book as you hand it to him, growing more and more visibly disgusted.>$B$BWill you look at these? This is like a set of encyclopedias for psychopaths.',0),
(39003,'enUS','<Khadgar\'s face falls as you describe your encounter at the tower.>$B$BCordana...? Oh no no no...She\'s been very distant lately. I just... I thought it was part of her stone-cold warden routine. I didn\'t realize...$B$BAh, $n! You see? This is exactly what Gul\'dan does. He finds our weakness and turns it against us. Be careful who you trust. Ah, Cordana!$B$B$B$BCordana.',0),
(39004,'enUS','<Khadgar\'s face is ashen.>$B$BDraenor is saved, $n. But the Legion is more powerful than even I had imagined. And Gul\'dan, that snake - he\'s still alive. Somewhere.$B$BStay here and celebrate with the others, $n. You\'ve earned it. But I will soon return to Azeroth to deal with this, and I hope you will join me there when the time comes.',0),
(39015,'enUS','<The puppy wags its tail furiously as soon as he spots you. He seems extremely grateful.>',0),
(39018,'enUS','<The Archmage looks damp and uncomfortable.>$B$BI apologize for the conditions here, $n. I had no choice. I summoned this tower at the optimal confluence of arcane energies. My hope is to finish my work here before all my books get musty.$B$BSo then! Let\'s get to it.',0),
(39019,'enUS','Welcome back, my friend. We have much work to do.',0),
(39020,'enUS','Ah, $n, you have returned. An otherworldly air hangs heavy about you.',0),
(39021,'enUS','Ah, $n, you have returned. An otherworldly air hangs heavy about you.',0),
(39022,'enUS','Welcome back, my friend. We have much work to do.',0),
(39025,'enUS','It has been an age or more since the drogbar last walked the surface in such numbers.$B$BThey became the dark stories we tell children.',0),
(39026,'enUS','Your battle skills are impressive.',0),
(39027,'enUS','Oro and the others? Did they make it out as well?$B$BSuch destruction. So many good warbraves have fallen today.$B$BIt is clear now, we will need the full might of the Highmountain tribes if we are to recover the hammer.',0),
(39033,'enUS','Well done, $n. Fortunately, a skilled diviner can use Apexis crystals to reveal oil deposits beneath the earth. I cannot teach you this art, but you may nevertheless reap its benefit.',0),
(39034,'enUS','Your new allies left this here, as a tribute for your efforts on their behalf.',0),
(39040,'enUS','I trust your battles went well?',0),
(39041,'enUS','The wind whispers your name, $n, and tales of your conquest.',0),
(39043,'enUS','Thank you for clearing us a path. We should have a straight shot at Dargrul now.',0),
(39047,'enUS','We need to move quickly. With every moment we sit here, the Legion\'s hold strengthens.',0),
(39049,'enUS','An inquisitor\'s essence... perfect. Allari was right.$B$BNow to complete my ritual and spy on the Legion\'s leadership.',0),
(39049,'esES','La esencia de un Inquisidor... Perfecto. Allari tenía razón.$B$BY ahora a completar mi ritual y a espiar a los líderes de la Legión.',22522),
(39050,'enUS','That\'s new. She looks like some kind of spider demon. As if the Legion needed spiders...',0),
(39050,'esES','Eso es nuevo. Ella parece una especie de demonio Araña. Como si a la Legión le hicieran falta arañas...',22522),
(39051,'enUS','Suramar is not far from here.',0),
(39054,'enUS','Hah, we\'ll make you a sea-dog yet. Let\'s get started on our first ship!',0),
(39055,'enUS','We have our first ship! Great work $n. I will get to work preparing her for travel to Tanaan right away.',0),
(39056,'enUS','Great work Commander! You are going to make a great captain one day.',0),
(39057,'enUS','Well done, $n. These docks are buzzing with activity.$B$B$B$BLet\'s do some damage.',0),
(39059,'enUS','It is good you arrived when you did, $n.',0),
(39060,'enUS','The deed is done. $B$BYou have done a great service to the worgen of Greywatch, $n.',0),
(39061,'enUS','Excellent. The puzzle is finally coming together. $B$BWe may not know why Sylvanas\' forces are here, but I think we know where they are.',0),
(39062,'enUS','So the cavalry has arrived? $B$BGood, we must make haste if we wish to uncover Sylvanas\' plot before it comes to bear.',0),
(39063,'enUS','Val\'kyr, you say? This is worse that I had imagined. If Sylvanas is able to create more Val\'kyr, there will be no limit to her armies!$B$BIt seems the vault is her goal. We must stop her!',0),
(39067,'enUS','Great work! We will get to work right away on the upgrade.',0),
(39068,'enUS','Controlling the seas of Draenor is in our grasp!',0),
(39082,'enUS','I love the smell of fresh-cut wood and tar! Are you ready to start construction?',0),
(39090,'enUS','NICE WORK. TOO BAD THE ALLIANCE IS STILL BEATING DOWN OUR GATES! GET BACK OUT THERE!',0),
(39092,'enUS','It is good to see you, $n. $B$BThe assault on Dreadwake\'s Landing fared poorly, and I had thought our cause lost until Crowley informed me of your success.$B$BNow, let\'s finish this!',0),
(39096,'enUS','Well done Commander! But there are still a lot of Horde out there wreaking havoc.',0),
(39107,'enUS','Eh, ya got dem all! Dat\'s wonderful for the both of us. I can give ya dis much...',0),
(39117,'enUS','Thank you. Grisly, eh? I think I\'ll mount it over the door.$B$BI want you to have this, too. Fresh-caught mossgill was Papa\'s favorite.',0),
(39122,'enUS','You\'re awake! We nearly lost you there... $B$BIt\'s a good thing we managed to get you and Greymane out of there in time, otherwise we wouldn\'t have been able to reverse Sylvanas\'s poison. It\'s a shame she got away, but her plans in Skold-Ashil failed and we have you to thank for it. $B$BI\'m sure Greymane will order a commendation for you once he is fully recovered. You did a great thing here, $n. $B$BGilneas is in your debt.',0),
(39123,'enUS','Not a scratch on ya that I can see. I bet those lions never saw ya comin\'!',0),
(39124,'enUS','You\'ve hunted the Highmountain Elderhorn and lived to tell about it. That\'s not a feat that most can say they\'ve accomplished. Color me impressed.',0),
(39127,'enUS','Welcome to Townlong Steppes. If you insist on wandering in to the darkest places of Pandaria then far be it from me to not put you to good use.',0),
(39133,'enUS','It has been a long time since the earth itself has moved against us like this.',0),
(39134,'enUS','I suspect this is not the last of Dargrul\'s assaults. He is still learning the powers of the Hammer like a child with a new toy.',0),
(39142,'enUS','The subject died during the testing process? Well that was unexpected.$B$BNonetheless, you\'ve held up your end of the bargain. I suppose it\'s time for me to fulfill mine.',0),
(39149,'enUS','We don\'t need any help, and we don\'t like strangers wanderin\' around on our land.',0),
(39153,'enUS','It looks like the ravens will feast on worgen flesh today, $C.$B$BWell done.',0),
(39154,'enUS','You seem surprised to find me here? I was surprised as well, to find that my forces were unable to even breach the city of these cursed vrykul! $B$BThe time has come to employ some different tactics, and your arrival couldn\'t have been more fortuitous.',0),
(39155,'enUS','The hero returns, and with the barrier disabled. I will see that you are commended for this. $B$BBut first, we must claim this vault!',0),
(39175,'enUS','Yes?',0),
(39176,'enUS','<The construct lies amidst rubble, in disrepair.>$B$B<Judging by the tools on its manipulator arms, this construct does appear to be designed for gemwork.>',0),
(39177,'enUS','Are you responsible for the return of this construct, $n? It came barrelling through our camp like it was on a mission. It took three of the warders to tackle and subdue it, but for the time being, it appears content to stay here.',0),
(39178,'enUS','These antlers are going to look quite impressive hanging from the walls of the hunters\' lodge.',0),
(39179,'enUS','You\'re quite resourceful. I can see why Ritssyn likes to send you on errands.',0),
(39180,'enUS','Welcome to Cenarion Refuge, $n. I hope you\'ve come to aid us in our mission. We\'ve much work ahead of us.',0),
(39181,'enUS','Welcome to Cenarion Refuge, $n. I hope you\'ve come to aid us in our mission. We\'ve much work ahead of us.',0),
(39182,'enUS','I\'m glad that Stonebreaker Hold sent you. The druids of the thicket have been slain! Only myself and one other have survived, and he\'s insane.$B$BI don\'t know what happened, but I intend to get to the bottom of it. Whatever it was, it happened quickly and feels unnatural.$B$BWill you help me?',0),
(39188,'enUS','I\'m glad that Stonebreaker Hold sent you. The druids of the thicket have been slain! Only myself and one other have survived, and he\'s insane.$B$BI don\'t know what happened, but I intend to get to the bottom of it. Whatever it was, it happened quickly and feels unnatural.$B$BWill you help me?',0),
(39191,'enUS','A great deed was done today. I have gained a mighty $C, and you a powerful artifact.',0),
(39192,'enUS','Your weapon has untold potential! You will need to get more acquainted with it first and we can work on it some more.',0),
(39195,'enUS','Yes?',0),
(39196,'enUS','<Even though he endeavors to hide it, a look of relief spreads over Kroghan\'s face.>$B$BIt\'s about time you got here! Granted, you\'re not an army, but any able-bodied $R than can wield a weapon or chant a spell is welcome here. The people of Garadar are kin to all the Horde and we are proud to shed our blood in their defense.',0),
(39197,'enUS','Your people have done a great service for my good friend, Ikuti. For this, you are welcome here in Telaar.',0),
(39198,'enUS','Denjai seeks help? I\'d send him reinforcements, but we\'re spread thin here as it is. We\'ve got trouble of our own with the ogres up here.$B$BWhen I can, I\'ll give him what information we have on the local ogre tribes and their tactics. Perhaps if he can survive long enough, we\'ll be able to launch a two-pronged assault on the vile scum.',0),
(39199,'enUS','Ah, good. We could use more able bodies.',0),
(39201,'enUS','Hey there. Looking for work? Perfect!',0),
(39202,'enUS','Hey there. Looking for work? Perfect!',0),
(39203,'enUS','What took you so long? Time waits only for Aspects, $R.$B$BWe have much work to do, you and I.',0),
(39204,'enUS','I\'ve been expecting you, $C. We have much work to do, you and I.',0),
(39206,'enUS','Who are you?$B$BTell me why I shouldn\'t split you in two where you stand!',0),
(39207,'enUS','You were almost shot down, eh? Savage monsters - those Horde.$B$BPayback will come for what they\'ve done. You can count on at least that much, $C.$B$BNow, it\'s time to put you to work.',0),
(39208,'enUS','<Stefan reads the missive, then crumples it up and tosses it into the fire.>$B$BOld news. The Argent Crusade is - once again - late to the party. We\'ve been tracking Drakuru since Grizzly Hills. He is slated for eradication.',0),
(39209,'enUS','Aye, Hemet\'s here. He\'s at the camp, just go northwest toward the river and you\'ll soon see it. And for the love of the Light, lad, have him send someone to cut me down!',0),
(39210,'enUS','Welcome to Dalaran.',0),
(39212,'enUS','Aye, Hemet\'s here. He\'s at the camp, just go northwest toward the river and you\'ll soon see it. And for the love of the Light, lad, have him send someone to cut me down!',0),
(39214,'enUS','It has been a while since I\'ve talked to the living. I hope you don\'t mind if I assist you. Being slain in combat has given me a calmer outlook in this emergency than other warriors.',0),
(39217,'enUS','Good work $n! It\'s not a pretty situation down there.',0),
(39221,'enUS','I wonder if dat magnaron fel into da pool. Get it, mon?',0),
(39225,'enUS','I wouldn\'t know dat monster started off as an orc if Saurfang hadn\'t told me.',0),
(39228,'enUS','Anotha follower of da darkness falls before ya.',0),
(39231,'enUS','Dat bag of bones be gone again.',0),
(39232,'enUS','Ya saved Draenor from one of da strongest demons in all creation, Commander. Dey will sing songs of your victory.',0),
(39233,'enUS','Good work $n! You see the mess the Alliance has made I\'m sure.',0),
(39236,'enUS','I love the smell of fresh-cut wood and tar! Are you ready to start construction?',0),
(39241,'enUS','Hah, we\'ll make you a sea-dog yet. Let\'s get started on our first ship!',0),
(39242,'enUS','It is done. Quite the beauty! You provide the army, she\'ll get \'em where they need to go.$B$BI will prepare her for the trip to Tanaan.',0),
(39243,'enUS','Great work Commander! You are going to make a great captain one day.',0),
(39245,'enUS','Great work! We will get to work right away on the upgrade.',0),
(39246,'enUS','Controlling the seas of Draenor is in our grasp!',0),
(39247,'enUS','What of the others? Did they...?$B$BI see. They gave their lives for a worthy cause - the Twinblades will change the tide of this war, mark my words.',0),
(39250,'enUS','We can\'t handle too many more of those fel-corrupted beasts.',0),
(39253,'enUS','That was some kind of monster, wasn\'t it?',0),
(39256,'enUS','How does a vindicator fall so far from the light?',0),
(39259,'enUS','Let\'s hope Mannoroth stays down longer this time.',0),
(39260,'enUS','You have saved Draenor from one of the strongest demons in all creation, Commander. They will sing songs of your victory.',0),
(39261,'enUS','We have much to do, and precious little time to do it.',0),
(39262,'enUS','I KNEW that I\'d sensed something foul!',0),
(39262,'esES','¡Sabía que había percibido algo inmundo!',22522),
(39272,'enUS','Thank you, $R. Some of the crops still live. I believe with hard work and some of Jale\'s magical waters, we will not lose the entire harvest.',0),
(39276,'enUS','Interested in shipbuilding I see? I will do everything I can to help out commander.',0),
(39277,'enUS','That worked quite well. I will hold on to this Bug Sprayer; it might be useful in the battles to come.',0),
(39278,'enUS','Dis... is important! Where you find dis? We been lookin for dis stuff a while.$B$BYou got a dock now? Dat is VERY interesting. Maybe it time we became good friends? Da big fort you have is hard to sneak a spy-- er, forget I said dat.$B$BI gots an idea.',0),
(39283,'enUS','Wow, look at this thing.$B$BI think maybe I\'ll... actually, I\'m not sure what to do with this. Is it really a fish?',0),
(39299,'enUS','I am pleased to make your acquaintance, commander. If you ever wish to see the latest wonders that Madame Goya offers, please do not hesitate to speak with me. She sends this as a token of appreciation for your work in retrieving the manifest.$B$BRemember, Madame Goya only accepts bids in person. You must travel to meet her, if you wish to acquire any of her wares.',0),
(39305,'enUS','Thanks to you, the great eagles of Highmountain will live on.$B$BOne of the eggs I thought was too damaged to salvage appears to be hatching...',0),
(39313,'enUS','Great! I\'m always here if ye\' ever want to change your mind!',0),
(39315,'enUS','A whole slew of artillery options at your hands! Living the dream.$B$BRemember, you can return to me at any time if you change your mind!',0),
(39316,'enUS','They have returned relatively unharmed. Thank you, $n.',0),
(39318,'enUS','Julan is dead? He was a good shaman and full of life. Not as morbid as some of these spiritwalkers.$B$BI will miss his laughter tonight.',0),
(39321,'enUS','Well done. Now to cut the head off the snake, as it were.',0),
(39322,'enUS','You have our respect and honor, $n. I name you Skyfriend, and grant you free passage through our lands at your discretion.',0),
(39323,'enUS','<Moozy squeals in delight at your presence.>',0),
(39325,'enUS','I trust you were successful in making the potions? This will be the first step in building trust between us.',0),
(39326,'enUS','You found them! I had the utmost faith, of course. What\'s a few demons or naga to one so dedicated to advancing our craft?',0),
(39327,'enUS','It seems that twerp of a scribe has his uses after all! Let\'s see what he came up with...',0),
(39328,'enUS','My poor table!$B$BAll the implements we needed to mix the new potions were on that table. Without them, the new recipes are useless!$B$BFinding replacements will be no small task, but I\'m confident you\'re up to it. If you need guidance, I can suggest places to look for the items we need.$B$BNow, off with you!',0),
(39329,'enUS','Ah, this burner is exactly what we need for the alchemy table!$B$BWait just a moment... No, no, this will never do!',0),
(39330,'enUS','You imbued the burner with ley energy, eh? Let\'s have a look.$B$B<Deucus examines the leyflame burner.>$B$BYes, this will do nicely! A crucial step in rebuilding the alchemy table.',0),
(39331,'enUS','What\'s this? The spoils from another of your adventures, eh? Let\'s have a look.',0),
(39332,'enUS','These potions have the corks we need for the alchemy table. Another successful endeavor!',0),
(39333,'enUS','Oh yes, these are fine. Fine indeed. Unfortunately they need to be calibrated in order to for us to get any accurate readings off of them.',0),
(39334,'enUS','Barm did his work, then? I hoped that tauren would come through!$B$BThis is a very useful addition to my alchemy table.',0),
(39335,'enUS','You... you found some? I\'m impressed, and that doesn\'t happen easily I\'ll have you know.$B$BNow let\'s see what exactly it was that you found...',0),
(39336,'enUS','The ghost of Svena appeared again? Seems she doesn\'t take kindly to our attempts to learn these vrykul recipes...$B$BThankfully, the satchel you recovered has all the precipitating powder we require for the alchemy table. Another victory for us!',0),
(39337,'enUS','This Shaldorei Silk appears to be torn into strips. The elves have apparently been using it as bandages for their fallen warriors.',0),
(39338,'enUS','This Shaldorei Silk will make an excellent filter for the alchemy table. Nice work getting that nightborne to help us, $n!',0),
(39339,'enUS','You\'ve found something quite intriguing here! Others have brought me fragments of such implements, but never so complete a sample.$B$BThis is going to require a lot of work...',0),
(39340,'enUS','It looks like you acquired everything we need. Give me a few moments to apply them to the interior.$B$B<Deucus works on the crucible, restoring its lining.>$B$BPerfect! The crucible is almost ready for use.$B$BJust one more tiny detail...',0),
(39341,'enUS','You did it! I must say, I was a bit concerned for your well-being, but once again you\'ve proven resourceful.$B$BNow that the crucible\'s lining is restored and it has been bathed in demon\'s bile, it\'s ready for use on the alchemy table.$B$BWell done!',0),
(39342,'enUS','You got the hair?!$B$B<Ms. Xiulan laughs audibly.>$B$BOh, I wish I could have been there to see the look on his face. Nevertheless, a deal\'s a deal.',0),
(39343,'enUS','What\'s this you have for me, $n? Say, these are some wondrous tubes! I bet I know a way to make them even better.$B$BI\'ll need you to temper these glass tubes in the fire of a dragon\'s breath under the light of a full moon on the equinox, then travel into the Emerald Dream and--$B$BOh, hold on. These tubes are perfect just as they are. Nevermind!$B$BSometimes I get a bit caught up in this whole adventuring business...',0),
(39344,'enUS','Well, now that we understand one another let\'s see what sort of arrangement we can come to.',0),
(39345,'enUS','Yes, I\'d say these burettes look well-calibrated.$B$BI knew those three would be meticulous. Never underestimate the value of someone who obsesses over tiny details, $n!',0),
(39346,'enUS','That\'s quite an armload of potions you made! I think it\'s safe to say that these burettes are working as intended.$B$BI\'ll add them to the alchemy table.',0),
(39347,'enUS','What\'s this then?$B$B<Alard takes the list and looks it over. His eyes widen as he reaches the bottom>$B$BI take it you don\'t fully grasp what it is that you need, do you? If this is truly what\'s required then we better get started.',0),
(39348,'enUS','Well done, $n. Once we have everything together, I\'ll get started right away.',0),
(39349,'enUS','<Alard takes the bag from you and peers inside.>$B$BSo this is the stuff? It\'s definitely true what I\'ve heard. It is quite heavy.',0),
(39350,'enUS','It was there? You found some?$B$B<Alard takes the crate and opens it. He reels back from the smell.>$B$BYep, that\'s the stuff alright. By the light, does that reek.',0),
(39351,'enUS','<You hand the heart over to Alard. He places it within his forge and it begins to burn white hot.>$B$BPerhaps I should refer to you as Dragonslayer $n from now on.$B$BJoking aside, I\'ll begin my forging.',0),
(39354,'enUS','Oh thank you traveler! You have truly helped the forest today.',0),
(39355,'enUS','This is a blueprint for some high tech naval equipment. I should be able to reverse engineer the plans and have this equipment available for you shortly!',0),
(39356,'enUS','This is a blueprint for some high tech naval equipment. I should be able to reverse engineer the plans and have this equipment available for you shortly!',0),
(39358,'enUS','This is a blueprint for some high tech naval equipment. I should be able to reverse engineer the plans and have this equipment available for you shortly!',0),
(39359,'enUS','This is a blueprint for some high tech naval equipment. I should be able to reverse engineer the plans and have this equipment available for you shortly!',0),
(39360,'enUS','This is a blueprint for some high tech naval equipment. I should be able to reverse engineer the plans and have this equipment available for you shortly!',0),
(39363,'enUS','This is a blueprint for some high tech naval equipment. I should be able to reverse engineer the plans and have this equipment available for you shortly!',0),
(39364,'enUS','This is a blueprint for some high tech naval equipment. I should be able to reverse engineer the plans and have this equipment available for you shortly!',0),
(39365,'enUS','This is a blueprint for some high tech naval equipment. I should be able to reverse engineer the plans and have this equipment available for you shortly!',0),
(39366,'enUS','This is a blueprint for some high tech naval equipment. I should be able to reverse engineer the plans and have this equipment available for you shortly!',0),
(39368,'enUS','This is a blueprint for some high tech naval equipment. I should be able to reverse engineer the plans and have this equipment available for you shortly!',0),
(39372,'enUS','The Bloodtotem don\'t often allow outsiders into their midst. Even asking them to give you an audience is a danger.',0),
(39373,'enUS','I could hear them screeching from here. With this victory and the defeat of the Witch of the Wood, Torok will surely be willing to see you.',0),
(39374,'enUS','Strange that he would be in the cavern at this time... perhaps this is a good sign?',0),
(39381,'enUS','You have little reason to trust me, but we have a common enemy in the Bloodtotem and I could use your help.',0),
(39383,'enUS','Xandris has finally paid for his crimes, but his blood will not bring back the innocents he has slain.',0),
(39384,'enUS','You have my thanks, $C.$B$BIf not for your arrival I would have surely perished here.',0),
(39385,'enUS','By the Dark Lady\'s favor, you did it! I witnessed the explosion from here - there\'s no way that Greymane could have survived such destruction! $B$BYou have done a great deed today for the Forsaken. Rest assured, it will be remembered.',0),
(39386,'enUS','A gnome hunter, huh? Is that a joke?$B$BFine, fine. What the boss wants, the boss gets. I\'ll start working on a prototype as soon as I finish up my latest project.',0),
(39387,'enUS','The Skyhorn are with us? This day just got much better.',0),
(39389,'enUS','The Bloodstone looks sated. Well done! Now it\'s time for a test...',0),
(39390,'enUS','Well now, this is intriguing! This book is... well, you see, it\'s obviously... uh...',0),
(39391,'enUS','Frag has fallen? The youngest of my pets was perhaps my most dear... curse the Bloodtotem and their cruelty!',0),
(39392,'enUS','These pelts are even sharper than I imagined. Well done, $n.',0),
(39394,'enUS','You have saved us all. The Cipher has become fragmented with Cyrukh\'s death. This means its guardians can hide the shards all over Draenor so the chances of piecing it together will be impossible.$B$BThis great victory will give us more time to stop Gul\'dan but I shudder to think of what his next plan may be...',0),
(39395,'enUS','I am glad you trusted me, $n. I feel like a great weight has been lifted from me.$B$BI still owe Draenor a great debt for the part I played in Gul\'dan\'s plot. My sons will aid the shamans in rebuilding and hiding the shards. Also, if you will allow it, I want to help you remove Gul\'dan from this world.$B$BI will serve you... Commander.',0),
(39401,'enUS','They lured us right into their trap, Commander. I want revenge!',0),
(39404,'enUS','They lured us into a trap, commander. I want revenge!',0),
(39405,'enUS','The verses of the poem unfold the tale of Ashildir founding the shieldmaidens and bringing them to Skold-Ashil.$B$BIf these shieldmaidens revere the Valkyra queen as this would suggest, your dealings with her in Helheim may prove advantageous.',0),
(39417,'enUS','It\'s good to hear that Razik is makin\' some progress on his gadgets.$B$BMaybe if he could design a gun that aims itself, these amateurs infesting the basin would hit their targets for once.',0),
(39419,'enUS','You have done the Skyhorn a great service, $n.',0),
(39422,'enUS','We have been waiting for you, Commander.',0),
(39423,'enUS','We have been waiting for you, Commander.',0),
(39425,'enUS','This will help me repair my broken body.',0),
(39426,'enUS','You have earned my trust. The Stonedark are not yet safe from our brothers led by Dargrul the Underking. We would willingly join Mayla Highmountain and her tauren against them.',0),
(39427,'enUS','We saved the Eagle Spirit and received her blessing. I feel even more confident we will get Talonclaw now!',0),
(39429,'enUS','Haha! You are covered in the feathers of your enemies.',0),
(39430,'enUS','Your gift is a noble gesture, $R. Smithing can be a surprisingly perilous profession.$B$BNow let\'s see that flask.$B$B$B$BEh, that\'s not so bad. Give me a moment to fix it.',0),
(39431,'enUS','You dare request such a menial task from me? Surely you must be joking.',0),
(39432,'enUS','As your archmage told me, the power that has warped these crystals comes from far beyond this world. I will need more help in discovering how to turn back the darkness inside my people.',0),
(39433,'enUS','I will continue to need your help until this world is free of whatever terrible presence Gul\'dan has invited to destroy us.',0),
(39437,'enUS','I could hear their murlurulurls echoing in the cavern. Maybe they\'ll think twice before taking our stuff next time.',0),
(39438,'enUS','That ought to send some of the murlocs packing.',0),
(39439,'enUS','You found them! Not sure how you carried them all at one time...',0),
(39440,'enUS','Stronger than you look, little one.',0),
(39455,'enUS','They said an outsider would wield the Hammer of Khaz\'goroth. I doubt you could even lift it.',0),
(39456,'enUS','Torok is dead? By... your hand? He must have truly given in to his thirst for blood if that came to pass.$B$BThe Stonedark on our side, though... That is an advantage I had not expected. Navarrogg has always been much more agreeable than Dargrul and his brood. Thank you for striking this rare alliance, $n.',0),
(39472,'enUS','To think that the Forsaken were brash enough to brew their blight in our own backyard. With the loss of their apothecary, their invasion force is left without teeth. $B$BYou have done well, $n.',0),
(39487,'enUS','I have never seen a drogbar transform like that. The Hammer of Khaz\'goroth is indeed powerful.',0),
(39488,'enUS','With the magic now spreading back into the cave, the balance of elements will be restored and the drogbar will not last long here.',0),
(39489,'enUS','The cave is nearly restored...',0),
(39490,'enUS','With fewer of those insects out there, I can tend to some of the crops.',0),
(39491,'enUS','Now we have what they used to spray our fields. I wonder what use we could put this to...',0),
(39495,'enUS','Excellent. You\'ve absorbed that fel lord\'s power and become more powerful in-turn.$B$BNow, we can fully concentrate on destroying the Legion and their Brood Queen.',0),
(39495,'esES','Excelente. Has absorbido el poder del señor vil y te has vuelto más $gpoderoso:poderosa;.$B$BAhora podrenos concentrarnos en destruir a la Legión y a su Reina de la progenie.',22522),
(39496,'enUS','I\'m glad you arrived when you did. The drogbar are increasing their aggression as we speak.',0),
(39498,'enUS','It would seem we beat the Underking here.',0),
(39499,'enUS','A-ha! Soul Remnants!$B$B<Khadgar cradles the Remnants briefly and focuses intently upon them.>$B$BThere, now you and your companions may access the upper level of the Citadel directly.',0),
(39500,'enUS','A-ha! Soul Remnants!$B$B<Khadgar cradles the Remnants briefly and focuses intently upon them.>$B$BThere, now you and your companions may access the upper level of the Citadel directly.',0),
(39501,'enUS','A-ha! Soul Remnants!$B$B<Khadgar cradles the Remnants briefly and focuses intently upon them.>$B$BThere, now you and your companions may access the upper level of the Citadel directly.',0),
(39502,'enUS','You did it!$B$BStrange, these Fel Essences bear the unique signature of the pit lord Mannoroth.... How in the world did you manage to... It\'s almost like you\'ve been here before!$B$B<Khadgar peers at you curiously.>$B$BNo matter! With this power, I can send you and your companions straight to the top of the Citadel!',0),
(39504,'enUS','You did it!$B$BStrange, these Fel Essences bear the unique signature of the pit lord Mannoroth.... How in the world did you manage to... It\'s almost like you\'ve been here before!$B$B<Khadgar peers at you curiously.>$B$BNo matter! With this power, I can send you and your companions straight to the top of the Citadel!',0),
(39505,'enUS','You did it!$B$BStrange, these Fel Essences bear the unique signature of the pit lord Mannoroth.... How in the world did you manage to... It\'s almost like you\'ve been here before!$B$B<Khadgar peers at you curiously.>$B$BNo matter! With this power, I can send you and your companions straight to the top of the Citadel!',0),
(39509,'enUS','<Denjai runs one of the blades along his thumb. A sinister smile spreads across his elongated face.>$B$BThese will do, commander. These\'ll do nice.',0),
(39510,'enUS','Yes, yes, this be the good stuff commander.$B$BI\'ll send a messenger with these to your shipyard. Don\'t you worry none, me hunters slip through this jungle like they was invisible.',0),
(39511,'enUS','I get these to Lady Liadrin then.$B$BYou really think there be a way back for these monsters, commander? You got a brighter outlook then me, mon.',0),
(39512,'enUS','This be just what we need! I get my people at work on these right away, commander.',0),
(39513,'enUS','They don\'t look like much, do they?$B$BI put these in safekeeping, commander. The blood elves might know what to do with \'em.',0),
(39514,'enUS','You lugged that thing all the way back here? You must got a bit of gronn-blood yourself, commander!$B$BWe send this to the goblins at Orgrimmar to take a look at.',0),
(39515,'enUS','I blame myself, $n. Mannethrel was already struggling. It is a never-ending battle we all must endure... to control the fel energies that we have taken in.$B$BMaybe it would be best if you held off teaching the others for now. We can not afford to lose anyone else.',0),
(39515,'esES','La culpa es mía, $n. Mannethrel ya se debatía internamente. Todos debemos librar una batalla sin fin por controlar las energías viles que hemos absorbido.$B$BTal vez sería mejor que no compartieras tus enseñanzas con los demás de momento. No podemos permitirnos perder a nadie más.',22522),
(39516,'enUS','I blame myself, $n. Mannethrel was already struggling. It is a never-ending battle we all must endure... to control the fel energies that we have taken in.$B$BMaybe it would be best if you held off teaching the others for now. We can not afford to lose anyone else.',0),
(39516,'esES','La culpa es mía, $n. Mannethrel ya se debatía internamente. Todos debemos librar una batalla sin fin por controlar las energías viles que hemos absorbido.$B$BTal vez sería mejor que no compartieras tus enseñanzas con los demás de momento. No podemos permitirnos perder a nadie más.',22522),
(39519,'enUS','How does it feel, $n? To look the Burning Legion directly in the eye and to tell them... \"Not today.\"',0),
(39526,'enUS','You done it, commander! Day by day, we be conquerin\' this whole Jungle.',0),
(39529,'enUS','Oh, this is quite the collection. How many of these sunk into your flesh? Exhilarating, isn\'t it?',0),
(39530,'enUS','That artifact is amazing, I can already see the potential we can unlock.',0),
(39532,'enUS','You gave them the glorious death they craved, $n. Soon Gul\'dan will have no one left to do his dirty work.',0),
(39565,'enUS','Ya done good, mon. We gotta keep up da pressure.',0),
(39566,'enUS','A sodden, aged tome lies partially buried in the muck.',0),
(39567,'enUS','What terrible instruments these are! We will learn what we can from these and then destroy them.',0),
(39568,'enUS','Wonderful, wonderful. I\'ll send a messenger to your shipyard with the information we learned. Thank you, commander.',0),
(39569,'enUS','Thank you, commander. Our scholars will study these samples at once!$B$BWe mustn\'t give up hope. Our eredar brothers are seemingly lost forever, but orcs from the world of Azeroth managed to break free from the Burning Legion....',0),
(39570,'enUS','Yes, yes, so many papers... Ah, some of this is in code. It\'s all very crude, though. Our scholars will learn much from this. Well done commander!',0),
(39571,'enUS','Very good, $n. Our scholars will be able to use these crystals to protect and empower our people.',0),
(39572,'enUS','Moozy! Thank the spirits you are okay! Oh thank you for returning him to me. Thank you!',0),
(39573,'enUS','My word, that device is enormous. Thank you for carrying it all the way back here.$B$BThere is so much my people can still learn about this world!',0),
(39574,'enUS','This is wonderful news, commander. We will soon have Gul\'dan\'s ghoulish citadel completely surrounded!',0),
(39575,'enUS','Quite a drop. Mind yourself in here, this is not a safe place.',0),
(39577,'enUS','That day, the hammer freed me of the corruption of the Black Dragonflight.$B$BIn gratitude, I have faithfully served the Highmountain family since Huln rescued me from this pit.$B$BIt has been my honor and my pleasure to watch each of his descendants earn the title of High Chieftain.',0),
(39578,'enUS','And so Huln cast out Deathwing into the land of Deepholm and claimed the Hammer of Khaz\'goroth as his charge.$B$BBut there was one last bit of business for him to attend to...',0),
(39579,'enUS','I always thought it odd that Ebonhorn never seemed to age. Or at least, he always looked old, but he never got older.',0),
(39580,'enUS','Even without the hammer, I know what to do next. When our forces are rallied, we can take the fight to the Underking.',0),
(39581,'enUS','Nice! You\'re quite the slayer, $n. Gimmie a low-five!',0),
(39582,'enUS','<Parvink is covered in bleeding scratches and shredded leaves.>$B$BHey, not bad! We\'ll call it a tie. This jungle don\'t scare me for nothin\'.$B$BMaybe we can hunt some more tomorrow?',0),
(39586,'enUS','<You and Parvink compare stories of your battles throughout the jungle. Finally, she hollers:>$B$BGLORY TO THE ALLIANCE!!$B$B<...Loud enough to frighten birds from the trees.>',0),
(39588,'enUS','Their numbers are fewer, but still they threaten our safety.',0),
(39590,'enUS','It is a shame to see the first worthy challenger for the Aegis treating the trials with such disrespect. Such hubris cannot win the Aegis, for the gods will surely strike him down for his arrogance.$B$BYou, however, seem different. You have shown that you are a worthy challenger. $B$BI will allow you to begin the trials.',0),
(39591,'enUS','You have learned of the obstacles you must face. $B$BDo you still wish to continue?',0),
(39592,'enUS','The knowledge you\'ve gained is a powerful tool to use against your foes. $B$BDo not forget this.',0),
(39593,'enUS','Wonderful! $B$BIt is good to be whole again!',0),
(39594,'enUS','The trial is done, and you emerge victorious! $B$BIt is a great feat you have done here, but you are not through yet. Many great challenges await you on your path to the Aegis.',0),
(39595,'enUS','I appreciate your gifts, outsider. You show great respect to the trials. $B$BYou do well to honor our ways.',0),
(39597,'enUS','The trial is done and you yet live. This land is full of wonders, yes?$B$BBut it looks like the God-King intends to give you trials on top of trials. Still you must hurry, for even now, the next awaits!',0),
(39601,'enUS','I look forward to seeing your impressive fleet of battleships, commander.',0),
(39604,'enUS','I look forward to seeing your impressive fleet of battleships, commander.',0),
(39605,'enUS','The trail ended at Linzy\'s ley flame burner, lying in pieces upon the ground.$B$BThere are too many guards around for this to have gone unnoticed. Perhaps they have some information about Lyndras.',0),
(39614,'enUS','Thank you. You saved enough fish that they can breed a new population.',0),
(39645,'enUS','Yes, I\'d say these burettes look well-calibrated.$B$BI knew those three would be meticulous. Never underestimate the value of someone who obsesses over tiny details, $n!',0),
(39648,'enUS','Thank you for all the help! Their families will be so happy to see them.',0),
(39649,'enUS','Well that was fast! Grumpus is gonna have a hard time continuing his work without his minions.$B$BTake these. I had them specially crafted for ya.$B$BYou never know what you\'ll run into out here in Draenor!',0),
(39651,'enUS','Thanks, $n. I couldn\'t have done it without you.$B$BTake these as a token of my appreciation.$B$BHappy holidays!',0),
(39652,'enUS','You are truly a hero to my brood. $B$BYou have gained a powerful ally today, outsider. The God-King has reason to fear you.',0),
(39654,'enUS','Now all here know who you are. It is time for armaments befitting my champion.',0),
(39655,'enUS','That was an amazing turn around commander! Great work.',0),
(39656,'enUS','You made it back without any scratches. It looks like the backfire issue from the last prototype worked itself out.$B$BA few more tweaks and I\'d say this hand cannon is ready for mass production. Thanks for the help, $n.',0),
(39657,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(39658,'enUS','This present looks like it has been shaken a few times. The tag on it reads:$B$BTo a very special $R $C.',0),
(39659,'enUS','A small tag on this present reads:$B$BHappy holidays, $n!',0),
(39661,'enUS','Are you ready? We are about to enter a cave... and the drogbar are at home in such dark places.',0),
(39663,'enUS','Can you sense her power? It will take all of you combined.$B$BEven so... I better go secure our way out of here.',0),
(39663,'esES','¿Percibes su poder? Es superior al de todos vosotros juntos.$B$BAún así... será mejor que busque una forma de salir de aquí.',22522),
(39665,'enUS','Equipment can really make a difference out there!',0),
(39666,'enUS','Equipment can really make a difference out there, let\'s see what I can do to help ya out.',0),
(39667,'enUS','You looking for that crazed elf? Sorry to say he\'s been locked up.$B$BWe found him hunched in the corner making all sorts of noise and when we approached him, he attacked one of our guards.$B$BWe also found him with an item that was reported stolen. We had no choice but to lock him up in Violet Hold.',0),
(39668,'enUS','Wow. Those were some nasty presents. You might want to, uh... wash up. Who knows what was inside some of those packages.',0),
(39670,'enUS','Hrm, these rabbits are a bit bigger than I thought, but we should still be able to stuff a few of them into the hand cannon.',0),
(39674,'enUS','That was an amazing turn around commander! Great work.',0),
(39675,'enUS','Equipment can really make a difference out there, let\'s see what I can do to help ya out.',0),
(39676,'enUS','Equipment can really make a difference out there!',0),
(39680,'enUS','Thank you, $n. Words cannot express what this means to me.$B$BAnd as promised, here is a gift of knowledge to you.',0),
(39681,'enUS','Are you alright? Most of my stock seems to be unharmed by the flames. It\'s a good thing this wasn\'t the tailoring shop.$B$BThe explosion seemed to happen when I applied the flux.$B$BNo flux means no welding. That\'s a shame. Without the ability to weld, we\'re limited to crafting belts and bracers.',0),
(39682,'enUS','Kayn and Altruis said you would be coming. Just in time, $n.',0),
(39682,'esES','Kayn y Altruis dijeron que vendrías. Justo a tiempo, $n.',22522),
(39683,'enUS','Yes... just look you... surging with new power and knowledge!',0),
(39683,'esES','Sí... Mírate... ¡Rebosante de nuevo poder y conocimientos!',22522),
(39684,'enUS','I had no doubt you would know what to do.',0),
(39684,'esES','No tenía ninguna duda de que sabrías que hacer.',22522),
(39685,'enUS','I knew you could do it, $n. We could not let that creature escape.',0),
(39685,'esES','Sabía que podías hacerlo, $n. No podíamos dejar que esa criatura escapara.',22522),
(39686,'enUS','This is serious. Their core ideals are in direct conflict.$B$BI fear they will take this duel to the death.',0),
(39686,'esES','Esto es grave. Sus ideales más básicos están en conflicto directo.$B$BTemo que este duelo acabe en muerte.',22522),
(39688,'enUS','We escaped the Vault, but our work is far from over.$B$BThe Legion\'s assault on this world is just beginning.$B$BIf Azeroth is to survive, we may have to work with this... Archmage Khadgar.',0),
(39688,'esES','Hemos huido de la Cámara, pero nos queda mucho por hacer.$B$BEl asalto de la Legión a este mundo no ha hecho más que empezar.$B$BSi queremos que Azeroth sobreviva, es probable que debamos colaborar con ese tal... archimago Khadgar.',22522),
(39689,'enUS','If you are ready, I will take you to our destination.$B$BAre you prepared to leave?',0),
(39689,'esES','Si estás preparado, te llevaré a tu destino.$B$B¿Estás listo para partir?',22522),
(39690,'enUS','If you are ready, I will take you to our destination.$B$BAre you prepared to leave?',0),
(39690,'esES','Si estás preparado, te llevaré a tu destino.$B$B¿Estás listo para partir?',22522),
(39691,'enUS','Dark times have fallen upon Stormwind, $n.$B$BWith King Varian Wrynn slain on the Broken Shore, uncertainty and tension grip the Alliance leaders.$B$BThe timing of this tragedy is no accident. The Burning Legion seeks to sow disorder amongst its enemies, weakening its prey from within.$B$BWe must act.',0),
(39691,'esES','Son tiempos oscuros para Ventormenta, $n.$B$BEl rey Varian Wrynn ha muerto en la Costa Abrupta, y la incertidumbre y la tensión se instalan entre los líderes de la Alianza.$B$BEsta tragedia no ha ocurrido ahora por casualidad. La Legión Ardiente busca sembrar el caos entre sus enemigos y debilita a su presa desde dentro.$B$BDebemos actuar.',22522),
(39694,'enUS','We escaped the Vault, but our work is far from over.$B$BThe Legion\'s assault on this world is just beginning.$B$BIf Azeroth is to survive, we may have to work with this... Archmage Khadgar.',0),
(39696,'enUS','Highlord, so long as the Order of the Silver Hand stands, we will do everything in our power to destroy the Legion\'s foothold on Azeroth.$B$BTo succeed, we will need to enlist the best of our order.$B$BLet me be the first to serve, $n. I will act as your eyes and blade where you are not; I will carry out your will until my dying breath.',0),
(39697,'enUS','Yes yes, this is it. This map is invaluable. By triangulating these oceanic junction points we can graph out Draenor\'s key ley lines. Hmmm... there\'s where I built my tower, of course. Energy also seems to converge near Karabor. And here, by the throne of elements.$B$BOh very good, we\'ll be able to put this to use very soon.',0),
(39698,'enUS','Do you understand the gravity of our task? If we do not fight for our future, we will not have one.',0),
(39699,'enUS','Your hammerwork is solid, outsider. You have separated yourself from the chaff.',0),
(39702,'enUS','Thank you again for freeing me, stranger. I see you wish to discuss the art of blacksmithing.',0),
(39716,'enUS','I bet it felt great to smash those things! Smash, squish, squash!',0),
(39718,'enUS','Perfect. Up for a little trip down to Azsuna?',0),
(39719,'enUS','Finally, he\'s returned to the briny deep. I\'m sure we\'ll see him again, but for now let\'s celebrate!',0),
(39720,'enUS','Thinking what goes into normal fertilizer, I don\'t even want to know what was in THAT stuff.',0),
(39721,'enUS','We\'re lucky you were around to take care of those bony brutes!',0),
(39722,'enUS','I will continue beseeching the Light to bolster the power of your weapon.$B$BFor now, its newfound strength should be more than enough.',0),
(39726,'enUS','These pieces will do fine as examples. Now, let me explain how I crafted them...',0),
(39729,'enUS','This is... this is amazing! There are techniques in here I\'d never imagined trying. Good work, $n!',0),
(39731,'enUS','<Archmage Khadgar smiles.>$B$BI rarely get to say this, but I have good news for you, $n.',0),
(39733,'enUS','Greetings champion. I am Warbrave Oro of the Highmountain tauren. I come on the winds of war to find you.',0),
(39735,'enUS','It\'s an honor, $n.',0),
(39741,'enUS','Up until now, the Illidari have been a fairly exclusive club. Demon hunters only. But, as you have so clearly demonstrated, my dear, if we are to move forward trusting one-another, then bringing Akama in is an important step.$B$BIt gives one hope.$B$BAnd, of course, making Kor\'vas one of your champions is the obvious choice. No one fights as well as she does.$B$BWhat\'s that?',0),
(39746,'enUS','Thank you, $n. You saved me. You saved us all.$B$BI was... outmatched. My relationship with the elements has changed since the events on Draenor. I have some soul-searching to do. $n, you must carry the Earthen Ring forward without me. You are the leader they need.',0),
(39756,'enUS','Good luck out there! We\'re all in this together.',0),
(39757,'enUS','Ah this weapon is amazing! Do you see the souls of the damned dancing along its edge? Oh how they scream for release!$B$BYes... in their forms I can see how the blade must be shaped.',0),
(39761,'enUS','Oh yes... that will do nicely!$B$BReturn after you\'ve fed your blade another feast of souls and we will make it the most powerful weapon that\'s ever existed!',0),
(39763,'enUS','<Matthew lets out a gleeful howl>$B$BImpressive.',0),
(39764,'enUS','Is this all you could find?$B$BWhile I\'m grateful to have these gems in my possession once again, it seems that there are still a few missing. I fear they\'ve been broken, which means the demons within have escaped.',0),
(39765,'enUS','This will work perfectly, I believe.',0),
(39768,'enUS','Some of them seem to be digging less enthusiastically, at the very least.',0),
(39769,'enUS','What you want, stinky?',0),
(39771,'enUS','You really are the chosen one, $n. I will gladly lay down my life for you.$B$BWherever you take the Earthen Ring, I will follow!',0),
(39772,'enUS','Thank the spirits! These kobolds do not honor their ancestors in the way we do. I can rest peacefully now.',0),
(39773,'enUS','Uriah would not want me to waste time with tears. My mourning can wait until the escaped demons are trapped once again.',0),
(39774,'enUS','Thank you for you help, $n. I will honor Uriah\'s memory by completing our journey to Azsuna and delivering the demon prisoners to Allari as planned.',0),
(39775,'enUS','This looks like one of the grapple launchers the local vrykul use to scale the steep ridges in Stormheim.$B$BThis could come in handy.',0),
(39776,'enUS','That should slow these invaders down.',0),
(39777,'enUS','Excellent. Thank you, Champion.$B$BWe have managed to get the children and the wounded to safety thanks to your efforts.',0),
(39780,'enUS','Dargrul is just postponing the inevitable.',0),
(39781,'enUS','It was a hard fight, but necessary. $n, on behalf of the Rivermane, the Skyhorn, the Stonedark, I thank you for your efforts.$B$BBut where one battle ends, another begins. When you stand against the coming of the Burning Legion, know that the tribes of Highmountain stand with you.',0),
(39786,'enUS','Well, well. I half expected to find your statue on the riverbank. You\'re gonna get a nice payout once those tauren get back...$B$BYou haven\'t seen them around, have you?',0),
(39787,'enUS','So you took him out, eh? Those tauren are gonna be so jealous when they get back! $B$BNaturally, you\'ll have to wait till the tauren get back and pay their wager before I can give you your cut. But in the meantime, I\'ve got another target for you.',0),
(39788,'enUS','The Runewood will know peace once more with these Bonespeakers removed from the land. $B$BIt is a good beginning.',0),
(39789,'enUS','Oh, hey! You must be lookin for them tauren was camped here. They just stepped out for a bit, but Snaggle here and I - we can take care of ya!$B$BYou say they were gonna pay you for killin\' some worgs, huh? No prob, bub!$B$BI ain\'t got a lot of gold, but these goods are pretty valuable. Take your pick!',0),
(39790,'enUS','<Sniff sniff> I smell something...fel.',0),
(39791,'enUS','I see you carry a branch of the Runewood. Then it was you who laid the spirits to rest? $B$BThough I do not know your purpose, outsider, I appreciate what you have done for our people.',0),
(39792,'enUS','Oh hey, it\'s... you again! Of course you didn\'t have any trouble with those musken. You\'re a big, tough hero after all!$B$BThe tauren still aren\'t back, though. I\'m a bit worried that they may have gone off and hunted a bit more that they can chew.$B$BOh, I\'ll take those ribs, though. What do you want for em?',0),
(39793,'enUS','You\'re back? $B$BI mean... hey, you\'re back!$B$BWell, the tauren haven\'t come back yet, but no worries, I\'ll take that stuff off your hands! Let me show you some of my prime trade goods.',0),
(39796,'enUS','Bound... twisted... $B$BThe Bonespeakers...',0),
(39799,'enUS','A fine choice, Deathlord.',0),
(39800,'enUS','It seems you were spared the brunt of the explosion. If only Greymane were so lucky...$B$BOn your feet! We had better get a move on before the Forsaken are on top of us!',0),
(39801,'enUS','Hey, you\'re alive! I guess Withers isn\'t as crazy as I thought.$B$BIt\'s a miracle you escaped the Skyfire alive! The pieces of that thing must be scattered all over these mountains after that explosion!',0),
(39803,'enUS','Ah, the hero of the hour! We must waste no time! $B$BOur business at hand is most important if you wish to succeed in your trials!',0),
(39804,'enUS','A fine cut, I must say. $B$BYes, you will do well against the Bonespeakers, I think.',0),
(39816,'enUS','You and I have been through much together, $n. Now, you stand before me as Deathlord and leader of our order. I could not be more proud!$B$BThe battle against the Burning Legion will be hard fought and filled with peril. You should not embark on this alone, my friend.$B$BI will go wherever you command and I will kill whoever you wish me to kill.',0),
(39817,'enUS','I see. Well that\'s at least a little helpful.$B$BWith that information in mind, I believe we can move forward with our investigation into this resource.',0),
(39818,'enUS','These foolish class trainers speak to me as if I have never held an axe before!$B$BThey have nothing to teach that I do not already know. The dark power of undeath flows through my veins and it seeks blood and battle!$B$BLet\'s waste no more time in this dusty necropolis! Send me to the front so that I may spill the blood of our enemies!',0),
(39830,'enUS','You actually found something?!$B$B<Mama Diggs thumbs through the codex, a stern look on her face as she reads each page.>$B$BAye, here it is. All the answers are within these pages...',0),
(39832,'enUS','Deathlord, I\'ve prepared a brief report on all we\'ve discovered about this new land.$B$BYou should find it quite interesting.',0),
(39837,'enUS','Free at last! $B$BThe kvaldir caught me while I was tryin\' to put together a plan to sneak past that foul dog, Guarm, and have had me locked up ever since! $B$BI thought surely my fate was sealed.',0),
(39838,'enUS','That was... unexpected. Fel flames? I\'d say this warrants further investigation.',0),
(39840,'enUS','I like the way you think, $R. I\'ve long tried to convince the council that winning this war against the Legion means occasionally stooping to their level.$B$BThe Kirin Tor could use more mavericks like you.',0),
(39841,'enUS','The archmage sent you? Hmph.$B$BWas he afraid to come down and visit me personally? Or is he worried that the sewer water might touch the hem of his robe?',0),
(39842,'enUS','I hope these weren\'t too much trouble to obtain.',0),
(39843,'enUS','Let\'s not make a big deal out of this. You wanted a forge... I\'m making one for you. The ends will justify the means.',0),
(39845,'enUS','Look at the horns on that thing. And glowing eyes?$B$BThose demon hunters sure do have a flair for the dramatic, don\'t they?',0),
(39847,'enUS','Hey, look at that, you know how to spell your name correctly.$B$BGood job, now we can begin!',0),
(39848,'enUS','<Helya\'s voice fills the air as you stand>$B$BNobody leaves Helheim without my approval! Entertain me, and I may let you pass.',0),
(39849,'enUS','This appears to be what we need. $B$BNow, we can prepare for the battle ahead.',0),
(39850,'enUS','Yes, I can feel your power returned. $B$BHelya will regret the day she challenged one such as you.',0),
(39851,'enUS','It is good to have my shieldmaidens returned to my side. $B$BYou have gained allies today, but know you have also gained my gratitude.',0),
(39853,'enUS','The day is won. Now, we must collect our reward. $B$BLet us hope that Helya keeps her side of the bargain.',0),
(39855,'enUS','So the dead return from Helheim and back? An impressive feat. $B$BYour worth has been judged and the trial passed. $B$BNow, to your destiny. To the Halls of Valor!',0),
(39857,'enUS','You do not look good. $B$BI take it Helya did not prove lenient?',0),
(39859,'enUS','I\'ve been eager to get my hands on this manuscript! I was startin\' to think the gnome had writer\'s block.',0),
(39860,'enUS','Thank you for saving me. I hope now we can trust each other. We must if we are to defeat these Feltotem.',0),
(39861,'enUS','Elune-Adore, $n.',0),
(39862,'enUS','\"Siegebrul.\" Bah!$B$BBefore this war we had no need for such titles.$B$BOlgrul was always just a brute who takes pleasure in the pain of others.',0),
(39863,'enUS','You have the bracers? Very good, now stand back...',0),
(39864,'enUS','<Nathanos glances over at you, pausing for a moment before acknowledging your presence.>$B$BYes?',0),
(39867,'enUS','So I was right! The lion with the amber eyes did exist.$B$BHere\'s the gold as promised. This is worth every copper. You can\'t put a price on proving that you\'re right!$B$BI\'ll keep this eye, but I wouldn\'t want the rest of our prize to go to waste. Let\'s eat!',0),
(39873,'enUS','<The cage is empty. Navarrogg is gone.>',0),
(39874,'enUS','I\'m relieved you\'ve come, $n. We could certainly use another enchanter in the shop at a time like this.',0),
(39875,'enUS','<You hand Ildine the vellums.>$B$BAnd that\'s the last of \'em. Thanks, $n!',0),
(39876,'enUS','<Jace takes the crate from you and peers inside.>$B$BThe vellums! They\'re finally here.',0),
(39877,'enUS','That will certainly help us keep these demons at bay for much longer. We\'re in your debt, $n.',0),
(39878,'enUS','The spirits told me of your coming, outlander. Let us see if you are indeed the hero this land needs.$B$B<The tauren clears his throat.>$B$BPardon me. I know I come off as a bit dramatic. It\'s just... well, these things have meaning for me.',0),
(39879,'enUS','These will do perfectly for my explanation.$B$B<Guron begins to describe the process of speaking to the spirits and how they interact with the crystal.>$B$BI believe you may have come across another type of crystal: the \"leylight shard\". That crystal works similarly, but resonates with different spirits.',0),
(39880,'enUS','You honor our tribe with your deeds. I will see that this dust goes to good use.',0),
(39881,'enUS','What is it you want, $R?$B$B$B$BOh, I see now. You\'re an enchanter.$B$BI warn you though, if you take my enchantments like those foul elves of Black Rook and use them for evil, you shall feel my wrath one way or another.',0),
(39882,'enUS','You found it? I trust Glaidalis fell in the process?$B$BWhile I feel relieved such a powerful foe has been defeated, I can\'t help but feel sad for what could have been...$B$BRegardless, you\'ve proven yourself an ally. As a reward, I will teach you one of my enchantments.',0),
(39883,'enUS','I see you brought back a gift from Highmountain.$B$B<Nalthanis thumbs through the pages.>$B$BThis is fascinating! Look here, $n, some formulas for cloak enchantments. I believe these would come in handy for us at this point in time.',0),
(39884,'enUS','<Nalamya takes the dust from you.>$B$BWell done, $R.',0),
(39891,'enUS','Ah, a fellow enchanter. Come to earn the marks of my subordinates, have you?$B$BIf that\'s the case, then you may speak with my sentinel and druid. Earn their trust and they\'ll grant you their marks.$B$BI, however, have a different task for you...',0),
(39903,'enUS','So, $R, you have discovered my home... all that is left of me.$B$BNot even enough to sustain my beloved enchantments...',0),
(39904,'enUS','You have brought back to me my most prized possession. For this I will grant you a bit of my knowledge.$B$BShould you wish to learn more, you only need bring me a few, small components.',0),
(39905,'enUS','$n, you\'re back. Excellent work down in Azsuna. Jace gave you high praises for your help with his troops and against the Legion.$B$BBefore you go, I wanted to share with you the other new formulas we have for ring enchantments. It would do our side good in this war if you were to share these with your fellow adventurers.',0),
(39906,'enUS','<Alynblaze takes the vellums from you and applies them to his gear.>$B$BYes! I feel like I can take on the entire Legion now!$B$BWell, that may be a bit of an exaggeration, but I certainly feel up for some battle.',0),
(39907,'enUS','<You tell Nalthanis of your time with the cursed elves and the enchantments you learned.>$B$BThat\'s fascinating! You managed, through enchantments, to create a bond with those elves and now they may come to your aid?$B$BThose are some truly powerful enchantments you were gifted, $n. Don\'t let them go to waste.',0),
(39910,'enUS','<Merrus takes the idols from you and clutches them closely to his chest.>$B$BYou\'ve no idea how long it\'s been since I\'ve held these. Thank you, $n.$B$BYou have earned my respect and as promised, you shall have my marks.',0),
(39914,'enUS','You fought bravely, $n. I see that you truly are worthy of my marks and I hereby grant them to you.$B$BPerhaps one day we shall stand again side by side in battle.',0),
(39916,'enUS','After watching these demons helplessly for so long, you have given me a chance to strike back at them!$B$BNow the real work begins.',0),
(39918,'enUS','You have returned my love to me and for that I am forever grateful.$B$BAs she is with me now, she shall be at your beck and call should you need her. I grant to you her marks.',0),
(39920,'enUS','I sense the power of enchantments about you, $n. Yes, I think I will enjoy working with you!',0),
(39921,'enUS','Oh yes, that seems to be everything.$B$B<Kharmeera takes the components from you and assembles the rod.>$B$BNow, let\'s see what I can share with you.',0),
(39923,'enUS','I\'m truly amazed at what you\'re able to accomplish for such a young creature.$B$BShall we get to work then on learning from these cores?',0),
(39931,'enUS','Yes, these pigments look like they will do the trick. Well done, student.$B$BIn fact... I\'ve been researching a new glyph that these pigments would work splendidly with. Why don\'t you give it a shot?',0),
(39932,'enUS','Holy mackerel! This stuff really puts the \"ink\" in \"stink\", doesn\'t it?',0),
(39933,'enUS','And there we have it. Just as good as those witless Darkmoon cretins.$B$BWhile we owe this success almost exclusively to my genius, I feel you ought to be rewarded for doing the legwork. Here\'s the recipe for my newest masterpiece.',0),
(39934,'enUS','Are you here to reinforce us, $C? We could always use your strength.',0),
(39935,'enUS','Some may condemn our methods. We simply do what we must to destroy the Burning Legion.',0),
(39936,'enUS','Allari sent you? I am about to start a ritual. I could use you, stranger.$B$BYou seem more ally than enemy. In this time, allies are more important than ever.',0),
(39937,'enUS','If you can believe it, that was the easy part. The next part will be a bit more challenging$B$B...at least, for me it will.',0),
(39938,'enUS','It is done. I fear that if I had waited any longer to improve my wards, the demon in me may have taken over.$B$BThank you again, $n.',0),
(39939,'enUS','Allari has sent you to learn from me? In that case, I have much to tell.',0),
(39940,'enUS','As I\'m sure you sensed, these runes hold quite a bit of energy.$B$BGreater knowledge of the Legion is your best weapon against it.',0),
(39941,'enUS','I commend you, scribe. You would make an excellent demon hunter.$B$BTake this ink as payment for your efforts. I have no need of it.',0),
(39942,'enUS','A crystal... inside the flower? That gives me an idea.$B$BI dabbled in jewelcrafting in my younger years. Take a look at this technique...',0),
(39943,'enUS','<Professor Pallin looks over the demon hunter glyphs you\'ve designed.>$B$BHuh! Apparently I don\'t have to hold your hand as much as I thought.$B$BLook at this glyph you\'ve made right here. If you flip this symbol around, and adjust the stroke width here...',0),
(39944,'enUS','Seriously? Pallin wants me to do what now?!$B$BThat old bag of wind thinks he\'s so great, but he\'s always making me do all his work. It\'s a surprise I\'m not running that shop.$B$BBut fine, I\'ll help you. As long as you help me too.',0),
(39945,'enUS','I believe these have enough information for us to finish the codex. Excellent work, $n.$B$BIf you don\'t mind me saying, it\'s nice to finally not be the one running errands.',0),
(39946,'enUS','Wow. It\'s much... bigger than I had expected.$B$BThen again, vrykul are very large and I\'m... well, I am not.$B$BStill though, I believe I can work with this.',0),
(39947,'enUS','It was a good thing you were here to help me with that.$B$BI surely would have been killed by those spirits!',0),
(39948,'enUS','These all seem to be in order.$B$BIf you have a moment, scribe, I have a proposition for you that you may be interested in...',0),
(39949,'enUS','You, $n, are a godsend. I thought I\'d never be rid of that nuisance.$B$BAs promised, here is the bounty for the contract.',0),
(39950,'enUS','I... I know this work. My old apprentice, what\'s-his-name, was trying to prove he could create something as great as I could.$B$BImpressively, he seemed to have succeeded in this one case.$B$BWe should learn from what he created and make our own, less putrid version.',0),
(39951,'enUS','How did you get an extract so pure? Show me exactly what you did, step by step.$B$BFascinating. Do you mind if I write this down, so I can show my other students?',0),
(39952,'enUS','We\'ve ventured into undiscovered territory, $n. There isn\'t anyone out there in ANY academic circles I\'m aware of that is milling felwort this effectively.$B$BWell done, student. Or, should I say... well done, junior deputy assistant scribe?$B$BNah... I still prefer \"student\".',0),
(39953,'enUS','My stars... these are very nice indeed! In fact, this gives me an idea...',0),
(39954,'enUS','That\'s it! Hmm... let\'s see...$B$B<Pallin looks quickly through the pages of the old book.>$B$BNot much in here that will help you with our Broken Isles herbs.$B$BWait, hold that thought. Look at this here...',0),
(39955,'enUS','Hello! Ye must be one of me many fans here for an autograph.$B$BOh, yer here about the romance novels, are ye? I see ye\'ve discovered my little secret.$B$BYe know, I\'ve grown tired of writing those. I\'ve moved on, ye see. Wrote me last one yesterday.$B$BBut perhaps ye\'d like to carry on the tradition...?',0),
(39956,'enUS','Hmm... yes, ye seem to have gotten the hang of it. I particularly like that line: \"Oh, Lord Gravesbane!\" That would make a nice catchphrase...$B$BHere, take this list o\' story prompts. I certainly don\'t need them anymore.',0),
(39957,'enUS','This is more than enough. Excellent work!$B$B<Professor Pallin produces a small quill, dips it in the ink and begins scribbling on a small card.>$B$BJust as I thought, easy enough to make.$B$BAs is usually the case with tarot cards, you\'ll have to make a complete set in order for them to yield their full potential.',0),
(39958,'enUS','These materials have my mind racing. I can\'t wait to see what we can make with them!$B$BI\'m just going to keep some to study. You can have the rest back.',0),
(39959,'enUS','Come for an autograph, have you? Very well, you may present your chest to me.$B$BOh, you\'re here about the romance novels? I see you\'ve discovered my little secret.$B$BYou know, I\'ve grown tired of writing those. I\'ve moved on, you see. Wrote the last one yesterday.$B$BBut perhaps you\'d like to carry on the tradition...?',0),
(39960,'enUS','Hmm... yes, you seem to have gotten the hang of it. I particularly like that line: \"Oh, Lord Gravesbane!\" That would make a nice catchphrase...$B$BHere, take this list of story prompts. I certainly don\'t need them anymore.',0),
(39961,'enUS','Get your hands off of... err, I mean... that\'s not my...$B$BWhere did you...$B$B<The professor makes a sputtering sound.>$B$BSomeone must be playing a trick on me!',0),
(39983,'enUS','[In broken Common] Feathered one said you come. Unng Ak not hope for you come. Tauren have thanks.',0),
(39984,'enUS','The mists of this bay rot not only the wood of the ships, but the very souls of its inhabitants.$B$BBut it seems you have already discovered this.',0),
(39985,'enUS','Thank you for coming, $n.',0),
(39986,'enUS','A magical message in a bottle, slipped right beneath the Legion\'s nose... Clever.',0),
(39987,'enUS','An outlander...$B$BYou received my message?',0),
(39988,'enUS','You bring with you Eche\'ro, and... what is this? The blessing of Cenarius?!',0),
(39990,'enUS','The ritual is complete. Reinforcements will be able to push through the portal and assist against the demonic horde.',0),
(39992,'enUS','You see now, that Huln was mighty? He united the tribes and defeated terribly powerful foes.',0),
(40000,'enUS','Now that\'s how a real hunter does it.',0),
(40001,'enUS','What is this... I see? $B$BA friendly face... in a sea of foes?',0),
(40002,'enUS','You still manage to surprise me, outsider. Your trials are complete, and yet you still have challenges to face. $B$BThe God-King\'s forces are many, but in your weapon you possess the powers of Stormheim herself! Approach the gates, and these powers will lay low the enemies of this land!$B$BNow, let us take the fight to the God-King, and cleanse the Gates of Valor of his fel taint!',0),
(40003,'enUS','I do not understand, the portals are closed and yet Skovald\'s demonic forces still assault the gates! $B$BWe must find where they are coming from!',0),
(40004,'enUS','With their fel leaders slain, the God-King\'s forces will scatter. $B$BStill, we are not finished here. So long as the demons continue to assault the gates, Stormheim will not be safe.',0),
(40005,'enUS','It\'s unfortunate that the God-King escaped, but his defeat has stemmed the flow of the Legion into Stormheim.$B$BNow, the Halls of Valor await you.',0),
(40008,'enUS','You fight well.$B$BPerhaps it is time for a proper introduction.',0),
(40009,'enUS','<Thalyssra takes the crystals with a trembling hand.>',0),
(40010,'enUS','And just who might you be?',0),
(40011,'enUS','You may deliver me to Thalyssra once my work here is complete.',0),
(40012,'enUS','<Somebody has been living here recently. This scroll bears strange lettering that glows warmly, beckoning your hand.>',0),
(40013,'enUS','From the look of it, I would expect such an herb to be fragile and delicate, but... it\'s quite sturdy.$B$BOooh, look at these!',0),
(40014,'enUS','<Your trainer looks over the pistil and stamen, clearly impressed.>$B$BThe Earthmother must have been feeling generous when she created the aethril.$B$BContinue to focus on this part of the flower, $n.',0),
(40015,'enUS','You found withered implements near an aethril bloom?$B$BHmm... you\'re the third one today.',0),
(40016,'enUS','<Your trainer examines the stems, fingering the individual bite marks.>$B$BIf you\'ll pardon my language, they really gnawed the crap out of these things.$B$BLook more closely, though. You can see that they focused on extracting the energy from the stem\'s central filament...',0),
(40017,'enUS','<Kuhuine listens to your story about the aethril.>$B$BWhat you\'re saying rings true, $n. I have heard tales of herbalists that could coax flowers into quickly reproducing, but I was never able to master the technique myself.$B$BWell done, herbalist. I feel great pride.',0),
(40018,'enUS','I know this herb. I\'ve seen it once before, in the Pandaria\'s Valley of the Four Winds.$B$BThis is dreamleaf.',0),
(40019,'enUS','It is just as I suspected. The infested herb is dying... but this may be turned to our advantage.$B$BLook, herbalist. The dying dreamleaf has swollen with herbaceous extract. While harvesting the healthy dreamleaf is trivial, you can harvest enormous amounts of product from the infested ones.',0),
(40020,'enUS','Another plant, fallen...$B$B<The druid attempts to blink back tears, and fails.>$B$BDAMN YOU, NIGHTMARE! DAMN YOUUUUU!!!',0),
(40021,'enUS','I feel the blight subsiding. Good.$B$BOur respite will not last forever, but look... even now, the dreamleaf has succumbed more of its bounty.',0),
(40022,'enUS','<Osme looks at the herb.>$B$B<He is silent for a moment.>$B$BNOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO!!!!!!',0),
(40023,'enUS','I thank you for your bravery, $n.$B$BThe next time you approach a sprig of dreamleaf, you may just find that the land thanks you, too.',0),
(40024,'enUS','I like this herb you\'ve brought me, $n. In a way, it reminds me a bit of the Gorgrond Flytrap: both of them have a habit of attacking your nose.$B$BLook. If you collect the herb this way, your yield should be a bit higher...',0),
(40025,'enUS','You\'re right, $n. Something has been chewing on this herb.',0),
(40026,'enUS','Foxes.$B$BHuh.$B$BThat... that makes sense. I suppose I should have guessed that.$B$BWell, now that I feel sufficiently stupid, let\'s look at these bits of flower, to see if there\'s anything we can learn...',0),
(40028,'enUS','<Kuhuine sniffs the small gland.>$B$BThat\'s certainly a scent gland, alright. It seems to be mostly inert from an alchemical point of view... but I\'d guess that this is what is attracting those foxes.$B$BExpress this gland when you can, and you may find yourself attracting a friend or two.',0),
(40029,'enUS','What a fantastic find, $n. This must be the celebrated vrykul herb, fjarnskaggl. I\'ve only read about it in books!$B$BHere, I\'ll share what I remember with you...',0),
(40030,'enUS','You found this near a snarl of fjarnskaggl?',0),
(40031,'enUS','This book: \"Herblore of the Ancients\", seems promising, but several pages are ripped out. Shame.$B$BStill, there is much to learn in the others.$B$B<Kuhuine turns to a random page, flips a few pages back and...>$B$BSee, look at this technique here!',0),
(40032,'enUS','What good fortune! This page matches perfectly with the book you retrieved for me. We just need to piece them together, and...',0),
(40034,'enUS','This herb just disintegrated in your hand?$B$BFascinating...',0),
(40035,'enUS','Any success? None?$B$BEven if you haven\'t found success, your skills are improving. Don\'t give up, herbalist.',0),
(40036,'enUS','You say you found this near a starlight rose?$B$BYou adventurers, always finding such interesting things out there in the wilds...',0),
(40037,'enUS','The blade is enchanted - of course it would be. I\'m certain that we can replicate this enchantment here in Dalaran.$B$BShame that that herbalist wasn\'t more agreeable. There may have been more that we could have learned from him. At least he\'s still alive out there, somewhere...',0),
(40038,'enUS','My word. This person really hates you.$B$BSay - do you think this is written by that nightborne herbalist you... encountered?',0),
(40039,'enUS','Fantastic work, $n! With this knowledge, we may never have to suffer a handful of starlight rosedust again!',0),
(40040,'enUS','Oh. I don\'t like this herb at all. I\'m fascinated, but I don\'t like it.$B$B<Kuhuine peers into the center of the plant.>$B$BLook at the size of these seeds, $n. We can use these. Make sure you harvest them carefully next time.',0),
(40041,'enUS','Much of this is very technical and mundane, but Ryno\'s analysis can be applied right away.$B$BLook at this, here...',0),
(40042,'enUS','<Kuhuine carefully takes the seed from you and listens to your tale of Cenarius\' cleansing.>$B$BFascinating! If what you\'re saying is true then that means we can harvest Felwort in a similar manner. Now listen...',0),
(40043,'enUS','Curse Helya, she\'s corrupted the blades! Still, her champion defeated, her helarjar skulking back to Helheim, and my weapons in the hands of my chosen champion! She even made them more powerful than before. Wield them well, $n, smite the enemies of this world!',0),
(40044,'enUS','Their toil is ended, and fewer kvaldir walk the lands of Stormheim.$B$BBoth are blessings, I would say.',0),
(40045,'enUS','Murky\'s gained quite the following, hasn\'t he? Perhaps they can help him out.',0),
(40046,'enUS','The Naglfar...$B$BSo Helya\'s kvaldir can navigate the mists?',0),
(40047,'enUS','The pufferfish will be a perfect resource for Murky! I\'ll just whip up a spell to make them grow more quickly.$B$BAll he\'ll have to do is throw, then boom!',0),
(40048,'enUS','Yes, this is it.$B$B<Jace turns the rune over in his hands, studying the intricate markings.>$B$BExcellent work, $n. I\'ll make sure Nalthanis is made aware of your contribution.',0),
(40049,'enUS','Murky seems to have gotten a very strong slime ability due to this slimeweed. Fantastic!',0),
(40051,'enUS','Surprising. I agree. Well chosen, $n.$B$BNow, you must teach the rest of us.',0),
(40051,'esES','Sorprendente. Me parece una buena elección, $n.$B$BAhora deberías enseñarnos a los demás.',22522),
(40052,'enUS','So, Nicholo was able to complete the codex? And the tablets are deciphered!$B$BHmm... that\'s interesting. These tablets have some interesting spells that we could use to our benefit... although I find working with stone to be a bit archaic. I\'ll just put these down on parchment and let you test for any side effects.',0),
(40056,'enUS','$n, good to see you again. We could certainly use your strength.',0),
(40057,'enUS','I wish I had more like you, $n. You fight with a great passion.$B$BAnd I see you also learned a bit more about how to augment our abilities. I\'m sure your master in Dalaran will be pleased.',0),
(40058,'enUS','You\'ve come to help me with my ritual? I thank you, $n.$B$BIn this time, allies are more important than ever.',0),
(40059,'enUS','If you can believe it, that was the easy part.$B$BThe next part will be a bit more challenging, at least for me it will.',0),
(40060,'enUS','It is done. I fear that I had waited any longer to improve my wards, the demon in me may have taken over.$B$BThank you again, $n.',0),
(40061,'enUS','Good to see you again, $n. Kayn has sent you to see what I have learned?$B$BIn that case, I have much to tell.',0),
(40062,'enUS','Pods like this contain tremendous amounts of energy. Milling one incorrectly can be catastrophic to the front of one\'s robes.$B$BLearn to mill them correctly, though, and you can dramatically increase your milling speed. Watch and learn, student!',0),
(40063,'enUS','I commend you, scribe. You are an excellent hunter.$B$BTake this ink as payment for your efforts. I have no need of it.',0),
(40064,'enUS','This came from a foxflower? Fascinating.$B$BYou know, we can use these woody cores to our advantage. If you mill a woody flower along with several softer flowers, you can speed up your process dramatically! Watch this...',0),
(40065,'enUS','<The Professor dips his finger into the fluid and tastes it.>$B$BOh! I know what this is. The herbalists were talking about this. It\'s called fjarnsk.$B$BYou know, stranglekelp often contains pockets of fluid not unlike this. Let\'s see if we can carry an old milling technique forward...',0),
(40069,'enUS','Those worm guts will be perfect for a special sort of rope.',0),
(40070,'enUS','These eggs are in poor condition, $n. Some are cracked and spoiled, while others are cold to the touch.$B$BYet there is still hope. I believe a few of the eggs you recovered can be saved.',0),
(40071,'enUS','Korgrul deserved his fate. Thank you, $n.',0),
(40072,'enUS','With the God-King\'s defeat, the Aegis of Aggramar is yours to claim.',0),
(40077,'enUS','That ought to get their attention.$B$BNow, onto the business of summoning in the rest of our forces.',0),
(40077,'esES','Eso debería llamar su atención.$B$BAhora vamos a invocar al resto de nuestras tropas.',22522),
(40078,'enUS','It is clear that your cooking prowess is only matched by your might in combat. $B$BNow, on full bellies, we ride to Valhallas!',0),
(40102,'enUS','This cave will make a great base for the young tadpoles!',0),
(40112,'enUS','<Eche\'ro looks up briefly, then lowers its head before you. This creature is thankful for your aid.>',0),
(40120,'enUS','It is good to know that our warriors remains have been honored.$B$BMay they now celebrate their victories in the halls of Valhallas.',0),
(40122,'enUS','This corruption - I\'ve never seen it before.$B$BAnd yet, it seems somehow familiar...',0),
(40123,'enUS','We must find a way to reclaim Suramar City.',0),
(40125,'enUS','I never imagined I would spend my time in exile studying withered. Through them, I have learned a great deal about my own people, and the nature of our relationship with the Nightwell.',0),
(40130,'enUS','The demon I was is no more. I believe I am ready to return.',0),
(40131,'enUS','Greetings, $n. What have you brought for me today?',0),
(40132,'enUS','Mm. This is better.$B$BKeep my advice in mind the next time you take out your skinning knife.',0),
(40133,'enUS','Ye found me extra set o\'pants!',0),
(40134,'enUS','Y\'got these fer me, laddie? I... I don\'t know what ta say!$B$BHere, take this. It\'s the least I can do.$B$B<Hemet buries his nose deep into the bear hide.>',0),
(40135,'enUS','These are marvelous, $n. Well done.$B$BI can show ye how t\'get better results from yer skinnin\'. Take a look at this wolf hide, here...',0),
(40136,'enUS','$n, you return. What can I do for you today?',0),
(40137,'enUS','Ey dere. You be a skinna\'?',0),
(40138,'enUS','Ya gone and outdid y\'self. Look at dese hides, bruddah!',0),
(40139,'enUS','I seen wolf hides before, but dis be sometin\' else.',0),
(40140,'enUS','You\'ve returned, and with Ske\'rit\'s book, I see.$B$BLet\'s look through this together, $n...',0),
(40141,'enUS','Yes, skinner?',0),
(40142,'enUS','Very good, $n. Greater understanding of the stormscale leads to more efficient skinning, which in turn leads to fewer unnecessary animal deaths.',0),
(40143,'enUS','<Kondal looks over the paper, brows furrowed.>$B$BI know of only two people who may have written this, $n. I can tell you where they both are located, if you so desire.',0),
(40144,'enUS','What? No, that scroll isn\'t mine. I don\'t do much writing these days.',0),
(40145,'enUS','Looks like you\'ve got the hang of it. Well done.',0),
(40146,'enUS','Yes, yes, that\'s my manuscript, but there\'s no time for that.$B$BLook what they\'ve done to my MOTHER!',0),
(40147,'enUS','This is it - look, you can still see some of me on it.',0),
(40148,'enUS','Thank you. I don\'t know why, but your murder spree helps me feel a little bit better.',0),
(40149,'enUS','<Seymour places the scale lovingly upon his mother\'s chest. Even in death, she seems to disapprove.>$B$BThank you, $n. Here, you take her skinning knife. It\'s not much, but she won\'t be needing it anymore.',0),
(40151,'enUS','What do we have here, $n?',0),
(40152,'enUS','What do we got here?',0),
(40153,'enUS','Dese\'ll do, skinnah.$B$BDese\'ll do.',0),
(40154,'enUS','Very nice. You got a good knife hand, $n.',0),
(40155,'enUS','You\'ve been working together with Ske\'rit? I should\'ve known. You two are cut from the same hide.$B$BLet\'s see what he has written here.',0),
(40156,'enUS','I know very little about demonic hides, $n. I prefer to stay away from them.$B$BThat said, I will share with you what I do know...',0),
(40157,'enUS','What\'cha be needin\' from me, mon?',0),
(40158,'enUS','<Ske\'rit takes the hide from you and looks it over.>$B$BYou definitely got da hang of it, bruddah.',0),
(40159,'enUS','You have done it, $n. You\'ve earned the last of my knowledge.$B$BNow get out there, and get skinning!',0),
(40167,'enUS','You have seen only a taste of what Huln Highmountain accomplished during his lifetime. Let us delve deeper into the past...',0),
(40168,'enUS','Oh, interesting! $B$B<Cupri quickly grabs the vial and studies it intensely.> $B$BPerhaps Zeph was right to keep investigating here. This vial certainly didn\'t originate from any currently known timeline. Most curious! Thank you for bringing it to me. Or did you already bring it once before?',0),
(40169,'enUS','<The satyr takes the journal you offer and sobs.>$B$BYou bore the book of someone lost long ago, stranger. Better that you leave me in my misery than linger in this fel-cursed place.',0),
(40170,'enUS','Ya seem to have a gift when it comes to dealin\' with amateurs. Maybe ya can help my ghostwriter, Addie?$B$BI\'ve promised to teach her how to hunt, but I don\'t have time to show her the basics.',0),
(40173,'enUS','Let me see that. $B$B<Auzin ponders the prism for a while, before turning back to you.>$B$BHmm... Cupri could run tests on this for an eternity. This certainly qualifies as further evidence of meddling by a third party... or is it a sixth party...$B$BDo you mind if I keep it?',0),
(40176,'enUS','I\'m still amazed at how easily this leather takes shape. It\'s so flexible, yet keeps its strength.$B$BI think from here you can take my pattern and make it your own.',0),
(40177,'enUS','You\'re the one Namha\'s been talking to. Pleased to meet you.$B$BHopefully we can expand our pattern list beyond the helm you\'ve made.',0),
(40178,'enUS','<Diane examines the chest piece thoroughly.>$B$BThis has some very interesting design. I think we can easily copy what they\'ve achieved with this piece.$B$BHere, try this pattern out.',0),
(40179,'enUS','Well now, this is a good variety of equipment you\'ve brought me. Let\'s see what we have here...$B$B<Diane studies the armor pieces very carefully for a while.>$B$BLook here, $n. See how they\'ve strengthened the leather by over-stitching the seams...',0),
(40180,'enUS','Pleasure to meet ye! Now, I\'ll be needing ye to do one very important thing fer me.$B$BIgnore anything me brother tells ye. He\'s been out of practice fer years, but still thinks he\'s better than me.$B$BIt\'s a lie, lad.',0),
(40181,'enUS','I knew ye had it in ye! Good work, lad.$B$B<Thanid looks the pieces over with a careful eye.>$B$BVery clever. The elves certainly know their trade.$B$BWe should be able to copy this method with little to no problem.',0),
(40182,'enUS','Oh, this is a beauty. Just look at that craftsmanship.$B$B<Thanid looks the piece over very carefully.>$B$BAnd looking at how it\'s pieced together, this should be a snap to replicate.$B$BHere, lad, give this pattern a try and see how that works for ye.',0),
(40183,'enUS','Well done, $n. Here\'s a copy of that pattern to add to your collection.$B$BI personally specialize in softer leather armor. If you want to make a MAIL helm, talk to Ranid... although I\'m sure he\'ll charge you a pretty penny for it.',0),
(40184,'enUS','I can smell the leather on you, stranger.$B$BIt\'s in your skin, your bones, your spirit. It\'s also clear to these eyes that you wish to know about the leather of these lands.$B$BIf that\'s the case... then I must test your grain.',0),
(40185,'enUS','Thank you, $n. As promised, let me teach you one of our crafts.',0),
(40186,'enUS','If you can take down the drogbar, then perhaps you are worthy of my knowledge.$B$BI\'ll start you with a couple simple patterns to start.',0),
(40187,'enUS','Yes, $C? You seek to know the techniques of crafting elven mail?$B$BI see. Perhaps a bargain can be struck to benefit us both.',0),
(40188,'enUS','You are a man of your word, $n. I thank you for your service to us.$B$BAnd as we agreed, I shall pass on some of my wisdom to you.',0),
(40189,'enUS','These are good pieces. Look here...$B$B<Celea begins to explain the armor\'s construction to you.>$B$B...and with that, I trust you can create something of equal quality.',0),
(40190,'enUS','Come for more lessons, $n?$B$BVery well. Let us begin.',0),
(40191,'enUS','I see hope in your eyes, $n. I take it our lessons of the past will aid you with your future?',0),
(40192,'enUS','You\'ve gathered enough here to last me for many moons.$B$B<Hrul begins to work with the claws. It\'s clear that he\'s using very little of each, but still able to make an excellent armor piece.>$B$BI hope you were able to learn something from this, $n.',0),
(40193,'enUS','Back so soon, $n?$B$BAhh... you wish to master your existing patterns. That\'s the characteristic of a true leatherworker.$B$BYes, I can help you.',0),
(40194,'enUS','They\'re a bit rusty, but at least they\'re intact. Let me explain how these were made...$B$B<Celea begins to describe the method in which the armor was constructed.>$B$BTedious, yet efficient.',0),
(40195,'enUS','Wait, Celea sent you? I thought she had been lost ages ago.',0),
(40196,'enUS','I see.$B$BThat shouldn\'t be too difficult to make.',0),
(40197,'enUS','I\'ve got the plans. You have the leather?',0),
(40198,'enUS','Nice work stitching these back together. Too bad you couldn\'t get all the rat saliva off of them.$B$BLet\'s read them together, shall we?',0),
(40199,'enUS','Well wouldn\'t ye know it, $n. While ye were out, I found me crowbar! Isn\'t that great news?$B$BOh, ye were able to acquire one too? Ha ha!$B$BWell why don\'t ye hold onto that fer yerself and have a look at these armor pieces with me.',0),
(40200,'enUS','Oh, those are good ideas! Let\'s get started.',0),
(40201,'enUS','Awww, my pets are going to look so cute sitting on this. Well, most of them will. Probably not all of them.',0),
(40202,'enUS','This will be the last of what I have to teach.$B$BAre you ready for the trials that await you?',0),
(40203,'enUS','You never cease to disappoint me, $n.$B$BAnd now I impart to you sacred knowledge which was once passed unto me.',0),
(40204,'enUS','See this, $n? What was once a soft, simple scale...$B$B$B$B...has evolved into a jagged weapon that can kill!$B$B<He then indicates to the spined scales at the base of the creature\'s neck.$B$BI trust you now understand the purpose of change.',0),
(40205,'enUS','You look wiser, $n. The ancestors clearly deemed you worthy of their lessons...$B$B...as do I.',0),
(40206,'enUS','Thank you for coming, $n. I wish to impart to you the remainder of my wisdom.',0),
(40207,'enUS','Yes, these are perfect, $n. As is fair, I will return this grand favor and impart more of my leatherworking knowledge to you.',0),
(40208,'enUS','You\'ve taken down a mighty adversary, $n. The naga no doubt will be on the hunt for you.$B$BBefore they get to you though, allow me to show you a few things...',0),
(40209,'enUS','The basilisk scale is thick. Even a thinned version of this is enough to repel any sword or spear attack.$B$BThat strength is what makes these scales so valuable to our craft.',0),
(40210,'enUS','<Namha listens to your tales with wide eyes and an eager ear>$B$BThat\'s it, $n. You\'ve inspired me. I\'ve been stuck in this floating city for far too long. It\'s time to get out there and see the world again.',0),
(40211,'enUS','I says to him, I go, \"The world is on the cutting edge of the knife, and we, we\'re just the shavings!\"$B$BAnd he says to me, he says, \"But then who\'ll feed the sabers?!\"$B$BWait... who are you? Leatherworking? Oh... right. I, I was once a great leatherworker...',0),
(40212,'enUS','Green is good. Green is good. Green is good? No way!$B$BOh, it\'s you $n. Right, you needed something?$B$BWait, they\'re dead? And you slew them? Fantastic!',0),
(40213,'enUS','Hey $n! Come here and listen. You hear it don\'t you? Come on, I know you hear it!$B$BWhat are those infernal things you\'re dragging behind you? Fel hounds? For me?$B$BYou have a strange taste in gifts for your friends, $n.',0),
(40214,'enUS','Yes, you\'ve done it, $n. Good work.$B$BNow go, before I do or say something I\'d regret, but probably won\'t remember.',0),
(40215,'enUS','Now that\'s a beast worth riding. Here\'s the pattern for that harness, if you want one for yourself.',0),
(40216,'enUS','You haven\'t got any holes in ya, I guess that means Addie\'s aim isn\'t as bad as I thought!',0),
(40217,'enUS','We gave up usin\' that kind of ammo long ago! Don\'t worry though, we won\'t let the gift go to waste. I\'m sure we can use the arrows for kindling.',0),
(40218,'enUS','It appears Kira travels faster than your word. She arrived moments ago, though her eyes purposely avoided mine.$B$BIn gaining her trust, you accomplished something I could not. With her help, we should be able to summon the gateway.',0),
(40219,'enUS','And so it was that Huln Highmountain came to this mountain, freeing the drogbar slaves of Deathwing, and came into possession of the Hammer of Khaz\'goroth.',0),
(40220,'enUS','That should set those vexing Thorndancers on their way.',0),
(40221,'enUS','On behalf of the Lunarwings, thank you.',0),
(40222,'enUS','Can you feel the power emanating from the book? I cannot wait to learn its secrets.',0),
(40222,'esES','¿Sientes el poder que emana del libro? Estoy deseando aprender sus secretos.',22522),
(40224,'enUS','The orcs had a prophecy about the Doomhammer. It was said that a stranger will raise the hammer high, and with it, justice shall reign. Maybe... maybe YOU were meant to be that stranger all along.$B$BCome, $n. The Earthen Ring needs you. And Azeroth needs us.',0),
(40225,'enUS','The Earthen Ring rises once more to defend Azeroth. You will be our Farseer, $n, and we will be your instruments. Only by working together can we preserve our world.$B$BWe are yours to command, Farseer.',0),
(40227,'enUS','Honeyed words from a stranger. While comforting, they do not shake my resolve. Come, at this rate I will wither before we are through.',0),
(40228,'enUS','That was a kill I won\'t soon forget!$B$BAddie will write the tale of our adventures here today, but not many will believe that a gnome hunter took down a beast ten times her size.',0),
(40229,'enUS','Welcome to our humble home. You are free to move about here from now on.',0),
(40230,'enUS','You did it! Murky will make a great leader for the next generation of the murlocs here.$B$BI can\'t help but feel sad over losing my little buddy, but you\'ve got to let them go sometime.',0),
(40235,'enUS','Finally! Today is da day I can get out of here!$B$BIf not I\'ll need more of dem to try again.',0),
(40236,'enUS','Congratulations, Grand Master $n!',0),
(40237,'enUS','I\'d say thanks, but I\'m pretty sure that us shutting down the Foundry helps you out more than it helps us. So you\'re welcome.',0),
(40238,'enUS','Good work. They will return in time, but we can use this advantage.',0),
(40241,'enUS','Oh, those are good ideas! Let\'s get started.',0),
(40244,'enUS','Hello, adventurer! Here to help me and Murky out?',0),
(40247,'enUS','It\'s good to see you again. If there\'s anything I can do to help you take the fight to the Legion, just let me know.',0),
(40249,'enUS','What of the others? Did they...?$B$BI see. They gave their lives for a worthy cause - the Warblades will change the tide of this war, mark my words.',0),
(40253,'enUS','Excellent. You have absorbed the powers of these brutes. Look how strong you have grown!',0),
(40253,'esES','Excelente. Has absorvido los poderes de estos brutos. ¡Mira qué fuerte te has hecho!',22522),
(40254,'enUS','Yes... just look you... surging with new power and knowledge!',0),
(40255,'enUS','We escaped the Vault, but our work is far from over.$B$BThe Legion\'s assault on this world is just beginning.$B$BIf Azeroth is to survive, we may have to work with this... Archmage Khadgar.',0),
(40256,'enUS','We escaped the Vault, but our work is far from over.$B$BThe Legion\'s assault on this world is just beginning.$B$BIf Azeroth is to survive, we may have to work with this... Archmage Khadgar.',0),
(40265,'enUS','It pleases me that you have brought life to my beloved enchantments.$B$BOnce I could accomplish much more than mere parlor tricks... until the source of my power was stolen from me.',0),
(40266,'enUS','<Thaedris stirs from his thoughts as you approach.>$B$BThese will be sufficient, $R.$B$B Cliffthorn is a deadly poison, and will be perfect for my needs.',0),
(40267,'enUS','$n, I\'m glad you came.$B$BI\'ve found information on just the thing we need to turn this war in our favor.',0),
(40270,'enUS','Our next journey will be to Icecrown, $n.$B$BThere, in the heart of the Scourge, we will find Felo\'melorn.',0),
(40276,'enUS','I sense that your work here has only begun. As you get more familiar with your artifact, you will be able to continue augmenting its power.$B$BThe others are watching you carefully. You have become a symbol of hope in our struggle against the Legion!',0),
(40297,'enUS','My name is Lyana. What is yours, $C?$B$BYou have my gratitude for releasing me.$B$BI do not know how long I have been held captive... but I sense an overwhelming number of demons nearby.$B$BWe have much to do here, you and I.',0),
(40300,'enUS','Truly a testament to our preservation techniques. I had lost hope that anything would have survived looting and the sands of time.$B$BThe ancestors will be pleased with this.',0),
(40306,'enUS','Hmph. I suppose if you\'re assisting me with my task, I should learn your name.$B$B<Thaedris reaches into the book and pulls out an unfamiliar, dried plant.>$B$BThank you for fetching me another one of the ingredients. Your assistance is... welcome, $n.',0),
(40307,'enUS','Thank you. Now that my warglaives are returned, I will bring ruin upon Felsoul Hold.$B$BMy wrath is unending and my vengeance swift.',0),
(40308,'enUS','These relics are tokens and mementos of the former lives of those interred here. They like to be remembered and these offerings keep them in their eternal peace.$B$BThe spirits of the fallen will be at rest now. You have my gratitude.',0),
(40310,'enUS','I\'ll get better. I have all eternity to train!',0),
(40315,'enUS','Your arguments are not without merit, $n. But I remain steadfast.',0),
(40319,'enUS','You saw Latara? What happened?$B$B... I see. I am so sorry I failed you, my love.',0),
(40320,'enUS','My kin are safe. Let us see to these serpents!',0),
(40321,'enUS','Thank you, $n. You have given me clarity of purpose and a reason to live again. Together we will save Suramar and atone for the sins of my people.',0),
(40324,'enUS','Good. Let us see what we can learn.',0),
(40325,'enUS','The withered... Not only do they suffer a burning thirst for the Nightwell, but their own memories torture them as well.$B$BTruly a fate worse than death...',0);
INSERT INTO `quest_offer_reward_locale` VALUES
(40326,'enUS','<A bag containing countless pages of technical notes. Flipping through them, you find Kel\'danath\'s last journal entry.>',0),
(40327,'enUS','He made it out safely? Praise Elune, and you, $n.$B$BYour heroics continue to earn my trust and my tutelage, $n. Here are some more efficient ways of crafting your armor.',0),
(40328,'enUS','The destruction of the soul is a fate far worse than death. You have done a great service to those you saved.',0),
(40329,'enUS','Your dominance of the pet battlers of Draenor are unmatched. You are now better prepared to challenge other heroes like yourself.',0),
(40331,'enUS','I will wear this in honor of Throndyr!',0),
(40332,'enUS','Hail Jarl Throndyr. May your soul find its place in Valhalas.',0),
(40334,'enUS','<Brandolf mixes the concoction together.>$B$BWell, I never said that it would taste good. Bottom\'s up.',0),
(40336,'enUS','You have done it, $n. You have slain the Tidemistress and saved Jandvik from the Sashj\'tar.',0),
(40339,'enUS','What you doing back so soon?',0),
(40341,'enUS','So the legends of the Scepter of Tides were true, $n!$B$BIt lifts our spirits to have such a powerful artifact in the hands of the Earthen Ring.',0),
(40345,'enUS','What that?! You have Candleking\'s Special Candle!',0),
(40348,'enUS','Now that we have cleared out the corruption the fresh water elementals will be able to flourish.',0),
(40364,'enUS','There is no glory or honor in being digested.',0),
(40368,'enUS','These will do nicely.',0),
(40370,'enUS','It is done. Already I can feel the corrupting presence washing away.$B$BThank you, $n. You have done this place a great service.',0),
(40373,'enUS','I see. I support you no matter your choice. With this new beginning, we shall rebuild the Illidari.',0),
(40373,'esES','Muy bien, independientemente de tu decisión, yo seguiré apoyandote. Con este nuevo comienzo, traeremos de vuelta a los Illidari.',22522),
(40378,'enUS','I saw them run by. Not the most impressive of our troops, but the Ashtongue have proven effective in the past.',0),
(40378,'esES','Los he visto pasar corriendo por aquí.$B$BContamos con tropas más impresionantes, pero los Lengua de Ceniza ya han resultado útiles en el pasado.',22522),
(40379,'enUS','Grim business, but we\'ve all sacrificed just about everything to get to where we are.$B$BWe will do ANYTHING it takes to defeat the Burning Legion. Anything.',0),
(40379,'esES','Es una tragedia, pero todos hemos sacrificado lo indecible para llegar hasta aquí.$B$BHaríamos cualquier cosa con tal de derrotar a la Legión Ardiente. Cualquier cosa.',22522),
(40384,'enUS','Your reputation precedes you, $n.$B$BIt is important that we speak.',0),
(40385,'enUS','So the Bane of the Highmountain is dead and Talonclaw is recovered! Well done, $n!$B$BI mourn the loss of Apata and Wuho. They will be greatly missed in the conflict to come.',0),
(40388,'enUS','I am happy to see you, great ally.',0),
(40391,'enUS','Hello again, champion. I see we are all here now.',0),
(40392,'enUS','The Farstriders have been interrogating captured demons.$B$BOne of the vile creatures claims to know the whereabouts of someone... crucial to our cause.',0),
(40400,'enUS','The time to make our move is now.',0),
(40401,'enUS','I hope for both of our sakes that you were not followed. We must work quickly, considering how close I am.',0),
(40402,'enUS','The time to make our move is now.',0),
(40403,'enUS','The time to make our move is now.',0),
(40408,'enUS','Excellent choice! There\'s no time to waste.',0),
(40412,'enUS','With Azoran slain, the Legion has been dealt a crippling blow that they will not soon recover from.$B$BYou have my respect, $n.',0),
(40415,'enUS','To think that leatherworking has been that ingrained in the highmountain tauren heritage for that long is absolutely amazing.$B$BI suddenly wish I knew more about my own people\'s past as well as they do.',0),
(40417,'enUS','<The Warchief studies a map of Tanaan Jungle and its surroundings, his brow creased with worry.>$B$BAh, Commander $n! Voice of da Horde in Draenor. Ya done well here, bringin\' da fight ta our enemies. Thrall tells me ya exceed his every expectation.$B$BIt be time ta finish dis. Are ya ready?',0),
(40418,'enUS','<The King is studying maps of Tanaan Jungle and the surrounding area.>$B$B$n! The Alliance owes you a great debt for establishing this garrison. Thanks to your bravery and commanding leadership, we\'ve fought this war here on Draenor, instead of amongst our own homes and farmsteads.$B$BIt\'s time now to finish this. Are you ready for the final campaign?',0),
(40419,'enUS','We didn\'t recover Alleria, but at least we have proof she was there. She will be found... I know it!$B$BThas\'dorah has long been symbolic of the Windrunner family, but until Alleria\'s return, it belongs in your hands.$B$BUse it to rally the greatest hunters of Azeroth and drive the Burning Legion back to the abyss!',0),
(40424,'enUS','Excellent. Your part here is done.$B$BRest assured knowing that you have done me a great service.$B$BHere, take this payment. It is a small token for your service.',0),
(40469,'enUS','Is that mana wine? For me?$B$B<Iadreth hungrily gulps down the bottle.>$B$BYou and this Astoril have my thanks. I would surely have perished out here.',0),
(40470,'enUS','This is a most troubling tale. $B$BYou have done a good thing, $n. Now he will no longer torment our people.',0),
(40495,'enUS','I am left with little choice. I cannot face another Dark Rider ambush alone, and you are obviously formidable.$B$BI will help you find the weapon you seek, but only if you will allow me to return the others in their possession to their rightful place.$B$BDo we have a deal, $C?',0),
(40515,'enUS','You made Mayla smile. That is the first time I have seen her smile in... ever?',0),
(40517,'enUS','<Anduin sighs and reads the letter from his father. Tears well in his eyes. He is silent for several moments.>$B$BThank you for bringing this to me, $n, it means... more than I can say. I wish Greymane felt he could present it himself, but his mind is fixed on revenge.$B$BI cannot blame him... or Jaina, for that matter, but we must find a better way.$B$BEnough of such talk. It is good you are here. We will need heroes like you in the many battles to come.',0),
(40518,'enUS','Glad to see you back on your feet, $n. Many good soldiers who sailed for the Broken Shore were not so fortunate.',0),
(40519,'enUS','Hail, $n. I\'ve got your ship assignment right here.$B$BBut first, a bit of readiness is in order!',0),
(40520,'enUS','Ah, these will be perfect for what is in store.',0),
(40522,'enUS','You have served the Horde well in the past, $n.$B$BMore will be asked of you... much more.',0),
(40523,'enUS','As for myself, I\'m the proprietor of this establishment. If you have any questions concerning our shop, please direct them to me.$B$BNow, onto business.',0),
(40524,'enUS','So the ring was stolen by murlocs? Sounds like another opportunity for you and I to work together!$B$BPartners in crime, for the rest of time!',0),
(40525,'enUS','You got all the pieces!$B$B<Timothy looks over each piece and nods his head.>$B$BYeah, I can fix this. No prob, bob.',0),
(40526,'enUS','Oh yes! That is a choice-lookin\' skystone.$B$B<Timothy pops the stone into the fixed ring.>$B$BLike a painter or poet, I\'m a master\'n you know it!$B$BTell ya what, since you did all the legwork, I\'ll share the design for this ring with you.',0),
(40527,'enUS','Oh yes! That is a choice-lookin\' deep amber.$B$B<Timothy pops the stone into the fixed ring.>$B$BLike a painter or poet, I\'m a master\'n you know it!$B$BTell ya what, since you did all the legwork, I\'ll share the design for this ring with you.',0),
(40528,'enUS','Oh yes! That is a choice-lookin\' azsunite.$B$B<Timothy pops the stone into the fixed ring.>$B$BLike a painter or poet, I\'m a master\'n you know it!$B$BTell ya what, since you did all the legwork, I\'ll share the design for this ring with you.',0),
(40529,'enUS','<Tiffany looks over the gem chips.>$B$BYes, I suppose these will do.$B$BQuite different from the ones I\'m used to working with, but then again, we\'re not exactly in Northrend anymore.$B$BHere\'s a design for one of the newer jewels with which I\'ve been working. I call it a Versatile Skystone.',0),
(40530,'enUS','What\'s this?$B$B<Tiffany opens the bag and pulls out a jewel. She examines it and then drops it on the floor, where it shatters.>$B$BThese jewels were delivered by...$B$BWINSTON!!! That thief! How dare he switch them out for these... pathetic imitations!',0),
(40531,'enUS','<Tiffany takes the bag from you and pulls out the jewels. She carefully looks over each one.>$B$BGood, they\'re all here. And from the looks of it, they\'re all the original jewels.$B$BHow did you deal with... actually, nevermind. I really don\'t care.',0),
(40532,'enUS','<Tiffany examines your work.>$B$BI see. I would have ground this facet\'s angle differently... but your work is passable.$B$BWhy don\'t I write down my design for you. That way, you can try to be more like me.',0),
(40533,'enUS','<Tiffany examines your work.>$B$BI see. I would have ground this facet\'s angle differently... but your work is passable.$B$BWhy don\'t I write down my design for you. That way, you can try to be more like me.',0),
(40534,'enUS','<Tiffany examines your work.>$B$BI see. I would have ground this facet\'s angle differently... but your work is passable.$B$BWhy don\'t I write down my design for you. That way, you can try to be more like me.',0),
(40535,'enUS','Jabrul thanks you, $n.',0),
(40536,'enUS','It feels good to be out of there. As promised, Jabrul will share with you some of his knowledge.$B$BWhat is it you\'re most interested in learning about?',0),
(40538,'enUS','<Tiffany looks over the gem and nods her head.>$B$BVery good work, $n. It seems your skills have improved since the last time you cut something for me.$B$BEnjoy that design, it\'s one of my finest.',0),
(40539,'enUS','<Clive looks over the lock picks.>$B$BNot bad, not bad.$B$BListen, me friend, you\'ve done me a great service today. I trust now that you have the design, should I ever need another set, I\'ll know who to contact.$B$B<Clive gives you a sly wink of his eye.>',0),
(40540,'enUS','Good to see you again, $n. Jabrul wanted to know if you would like to learn some more designs.',0),
(40541,'enUS','Jabrul has never seen something so radiant in all his life.',0),
(40542,'enUS','I hope these weren\'t too heavy for a small brul such as yourself to carry.$B$BBut these will be more than enough to show you a suitable design.$B$B<Jabrul begins to carve one of the jewels into a design, instructing you how it\'s done as he works.>',0),
(40543,'enUS','I hope these weren\'t too heavy for a small brul such as yourself to carry.$B$BBut these will be more than enough to show you a suitable design.$B$B<Jabrul begins to carve one of the jewels into a design, instructing you how it\'s done as he works.>',0),
(40544,'enUS','I hope these weren\'t too heavy for a small brul such as yourself to carry.$B$BBut these will be more than enough to show you a suitable design.$B$B<Jabrul begins to carve one of the jewels into a design, instructing you how it\'s done as he works.>',0),
(40545,'enUS','Now that\'s quite the haul of guns! I suppose these fell off the back of a gryphon, right?$B$B<Filgo gives you a sly wink.>',0),
(40546,'enUS','An excellent piece. Now watch carefully...$B$B<Jabrul begins to carve the glass into a rather interesting shape, describing how the shape of the gem dictates its behavior.>',0),
(40547,'enUS','That was a much rougher trip than Jabrul thought it would be. But nonetheless, Jabrul is here.$B$BJabrul can\'t wait to start working with the masters here!',0),
(40556,'enUS','$n, good to you see you again! Now listen...',0),
(40558,'enUS','<Tiffany holds up the box and explains how she fixed it.>$B$BNow if you ever need to make one for yourself, you should have no problem.',0),
(40559,'enUS','<Timothy thumbs through the pages.>$B$BWhat a rare find, $n. Excellent work on finding this.$B$BAs promised, here\'s a new design I\'ve been holding on to.',0),
(40560,'enUS','You found it?! And you made it back!$B$B$n, I came up with a line just for this occasion and just for you.$B$BHe laughs at death, he shrugs off the pain, but $n comes back again and again!',0),
(40561,'enUS','Now that\'s a ring! How amazing would it be to sit alongside the jewelcrafters of the heavens.$B$BA find as grand as this deserves an equally grand reward. Here\'s one of my latest ring designs, I hope it servers you well, $n.',0),
(40562,'enUS','The elves always make the best quality items. I\'ll hang onto these gems, if you don\'t mind.$B$BThis jewelry design, on the other hand... it\'d be perfect for a jewelcrafting $C like you!',0),
(40567,'enUS','Praise Elune and all that her light touches... Malfurion is alive.$B$BI thought I would spend the rest of my days alone, dreaming of the choices I did not make.$B$BThank you. Thank you for returning my love to me.',0),
(40568,'enUS','The Felskorn have witnessed true strength today. $B$BThey will think twice before raising their blades to you again.',0),
(40569,'enUS','Do you think that the story is true? I bet you could control the power of those blades!',0),
(40570,'enUS','That was a fantastic trip, $n! We really should do this kind of thing more often!$B$BNow that you have those blades I bet there\'s going to be a bunch of adventures ahead!$B$BMaybe I should just stick around here a while.',0),
(40573,'enUS','Thaon Moonclaw was a great druid and a true protector of this land.$B$BHow can we hope to defeat the Nightmare Lord without him fighting beside us?',0),
(40578,'enUS','It pains me to see them suffering. In time they will return, but for now they will be at peace.',0),
(40579,'enUS','I knew you would pick that one. Let us be about it.',0),
(40585,'enUS','An excellent choice, $n. As more opportunities arise, I will bring them to your attention. Good luck in battle!',0),
(40588,'enUS','It\'s strange that the Dark Riders haven\'t followed us here, but I will take whatever boon I can get.$B$BI believe the key to finding the Dark Riders is here somewhere. Let us begin our search.',0),
(40593,'enUS','This attack... even the battle on the Broken Shore... it\'s only the beginning of the Legion\'s campaign.$B$BIf we don\'t find a way to stop them, we\'re going to lose everything my father and the other leaders built.$B$BWe need the strength of the Illidari behind us.',0),
(40594,'enUS','Well done. We will make a Skyhorn out of you yet.',0),
(40603,'enUS','Speak not. I know what you seek.$B$BDo you believe yourself ready to face the trials ahead?',0),
(40604,'enUS','Otherwise an ordinary looking journal, this book hums with dark energy as you approach it.$B$BA quick scan of the writing reveals this as the journal of Ariden, and chronicles his time in Deadwind Pass. Toward the end of the journal, the writing begins to change, and the tone becomes noticeably darker. It constantly refers to \"the curse\" and of the endless desire to possess things of great power.$B$BOne such entry catches your eye as you glance through.',0),
(40605,'enUS','Ah, so you\'re the vaunted $C I\'ve heard about. Good.$B$BWe shall see if your reputation holds true.',0),
(40606,'enUS','There is definitely something wrong with this compass. $B$BIt seems to be trying to point in all directions at once.',0),
(40607,'enUS','It would seem the demon hunters\' concerns were well-founded. To think the demons would dare worm their way into our city during this period of mourning!$B$BThis does not bode well for the rest of my kingdom.',0),
(40608,'enUS','<Ashildir nods knowingly.>$B$BYou are ready for the next step.',0),
(40611,'enUS','It looks like it worked, and the compass is pointing toward the river. $B$BCould it be..?',0),
(40613,'enUS','There is one last task before you journey to the Halls, $n.',0),
(40614,'enUS','My guards will prepare the feast. We must discuss your journey to the Halls.',0),
(40615,'enUS','I can feel Odyn\'s power from here - the Legion\'s magic will no longer stop you.',0),
(40617,'enUS','Thank you, $R. I will tend to Nighteyes\' wounds. Tell me what happened!',0),
(40618,'enUS','Now you must begin your pursuit of the artifact. It will not be easy to obtain, but a weapon this powerful seldom is.$B$BAfter you succeed, return here to me and we shall speak at greater length. There is much for us to do!',0),
(40623,'enUS','Today was a great blow against the Dark Riders, and a victory for the people of Duskwood. $B$BThey are in your debt, as am I.',0),
(40625,'enUS','This was all you could find? I suppose it will have to do, although it is a primitive instrument.',0),
(40632,'enUS','Hello again, champion. I see we are all here now.',0),
(40633,'enUS','Hey there, $n. What took you so long?$B$BWhile you were traveling the long way I\'ve been doing some research of my own. King Phaoris offered to help us as long as we can take care of a problem for him.$B$BI\'m sure you\'ll be able to handle whatever it is.',0),
(40634,'enUS','So, you found this stone upon his body?$B$BInteresting... Let me take a closer look.',0),
(40636,'enUS','As you wish, Grand Master.',0),
(40642,'enUS','<Kyrtos greedily consumes the essence.>$B$BAhh, much better. My senses are focused and ready for research!',0),
(40643,'enUS','$n, I\'m pleased you came on such short notice.$B$BWe have a great undertaking here in the Moonglade that is about to begin, one in which you will play a key role.',0),
(40644,'enUS','Well done, $n!$B$BNow that the path is open we can begin our journey to Val\'sharah.',0),
(40645,'enUS','You did well to navigate through the Emerald Dream to get to this place. Still, there are times when you might wish to return here a bit more quickly. This spell will guide you.$B$BTraveling the Dreamway is no small feat in itself, but it pales to the tasks ahead.',0),
(40646,'enUS','Excellent choice, $n!$B$BWith the power of that weapon in your hands we will be able to bring balance back to Azeroth.',0),
(40647,'enUS','I owe you my life, $n. If it wasn\'t for your actions I\'d be dead or worse.$B$BThat traitor, Xavius, may have taken Ursoc but at least we were able to recover the claws. Hope is not lost to us yet.',0),
(40649,'enUS','<Mylune\'s eyes are watery with dew, her usual smile an unsightly frown.>$B$BY-yes?',0),
(40650,'enUS','I ben tinkin\' for a while, $n. I set aside my walking staff a long time ago for a life of peace, seekin\' to teach da druidic arts in my twilight years.$B$BBut now, war has come to tear my home to shreds, and I can\'t watch that happen.$B$BMy staff and I are ready for another journey with you, $n.',0),
(40651,'enUS','Excellent!$B$BAs your weapon grows in power you can return here and unleash its true potential.',0),
(40652,'enUS','Greetings, Archdruid.$B$BThe threats we face are numerous. We must act quickly.',0),
(40653,'enUS','Yes, I agree. That is a good place to focus our initial efforts.$B$BAs new threats arise, I will bring them to your attention. Elune guide your path, Archdruid.',0),
(40654,'enUS','Excellent. Soon enough, the Druids of the Claw will bolster our ranks.',0),
(40657,'enUS','Excellent. By studying these materials I can better understand how they imbue magic into their machinery and architecture.',0),
(40661,'enUS','You\'ve done it! You\'ve broken an invasion!$B$BIf only that had ended our campaign. But the Legion will never relent until they are destroyed... or have destroyed us.$B$BDon\'t let up! Fight off more of these wretched invasions, $n. The wyrmtongue we\'re holding captive here will reward your efforts.',0),
(40668,'enUS','The Heart will require a great deal of work to properly hone the destructive energies within its depths, but I have faith that you will prevail.',0),
(40672,'enUS','These will make a worthy vessel indeed.',0),
(40673,'enUS','<Thalrenus reads over the scroll carefully.>',0),
(40675,'enUS','Well done. The Eon Winder will help us control the delicate magics at play within the Heart.',0),
(40678,'enUS','Now, let\'s see what happens if we use the Heart to drain the power from them.',0),
(40683,'enUS','Fel magic is... strange. Almost slippery like an oil, and it burns long and hot. Maybe there\'s a connection...',0),
(40684,'enUS','Yes, friend chose very wisely!',0),
(40694,'enUS','Yes...$B$BThis power is... different. Brutal, blunt, powerful.$B$BI can control it. I can master it!',0),
(40698,'enUS','This weapon is truly amazing, yet much of its potential remains untapped.$B$BIf we are to end the threat of the Burning Legion once and for all we will need to fully unlock its power.',0),
(40704,'enUS','You know, I\'ve been thinking about all the fun we\'ve had together. You\'re great to hang around and I\'m sure Uncle Chen wouldn\'t mind if I stuck around since you\'re a Grandmaster and all.$B$BWhat I\'m trying to say is, I\'d be happy to be your explorer, scout, or resident adventurer. So, what do you say?',0),
(40705,'enUS','Can I take that as a yes?$B$BIf you are ready, I\'d like to get started immediately.$B$BI know you are immensely capable, but let\'s not leave anything to chance!',0),
(40706,'enUS','A wise choice. My brethren and I stand ready to assist you on your next move, $n.',0),
(40710,'enUS','You have demonstrated no small amount of skill in these sorts of tasks.$B$BThat is good, for we will require even more of you if we are to survive this conflict.',0),
(40712,'enUS','Friend has the weapon? $B$BYes, Calydus can feel its power!',0),
(40713,'enUS','Yes... Within these pages lies the secret to true mastery of this power.',0),
(40714,'enUS','I\'m sure you have many questions, but they\'re just going to have to wait. We\'re at war now!$B$BWe have to move quickly, but I\'ll try to explain what I can.',0),
(40715,'enUS','Excellent choice.',0),
(40716,'enUS','You have made the right decision.$B$BLet us hope you live up to your reputation.',0),
(40727,'enUS','Deline was able to deliver the goods safely, thanks to you.',0),
(40729,'enUS','Calydus sorry we not save your friends, but maybe they survive if we hurry.$B$BJagganoth torture them, yes, but he likes to keep victims alive... mostly.',0),
(40730,'enUS','I will see that this gets back to our friend safely. Good work.',0),
(40731,'enUS','The cruel Jagganoth is defeated!$B$BFriend is the new Overlord of the Dreadscar! $B$BThis place will be friend\'s new home. With the Dreadscar under your control, you can come and go as you please!',0),
(40740,'enUS','That axe makes me feel uneasy, $n. Its power is undeniable, but its very essence embodies the eternal hunger.$B$BWe will use it because we must do whatever it takes to win this war. Still, I\'d be careful with that weapon if I were you.',0),
(40744,'enUS','That should be plenty. Talondust loses its potency fairly quickly, so we must make haste.',0),
(40745,'enUS','I-I thought... they were gonna... *sniff*',0),
(40746,'enUS','Glad you could make it. Your help is sorely needed here.',0),
(40747,'enUS','These are in rough shape, but they will suffice.',0),
(40748,'enUS','Did we... make it?',0),
(40753,'enUS','While I am programmed for gift distribution, my observations indicate that you are programmed for gift reception.$B$BShall we engage in a mutually-favorable transaction?',0),
(40755,'enUS','Not long after you left, the first wave of demons struck. We\'re holding them at bay... for now.$B$BI\'ll keep this tome safe until we have a chance to study it.$B$BGood work in there. I should like to delve into the libraries of Karazhan myself one day. At least... I think I would.',0),
(40760,'enUS','<Allari furrows her brow as she speaks.>$B$BYou didn\'t think the leadership of the Horde could gather in one location and go unnoticed by the Burning Legion, did you?',0),
(40761,'enUS','Something is very wrong here.',0),
(40762,'enUS','I was wondering why she had suddenly gone silent. It is a small comfort to my heart, but a great blow to the remaining forces of the Nightborne. Well done, $n.',0),
(40783,'enUS','Well met, champion. $B$BAre you ready for the burden you must bear?',0),
(40784,'enUS','Valorn...$B$BThat was.. a Dark Rider!$B$BBut how did they reach us here, under the protection of the grove?',0),
(40785,'enUS','So I was correct, and the Scythe is your quarry. Know that in order to retrieve it, we must do what no denizen of Duskwood has ever attempted.$B$BWe must hunt the Dark Riders.$B$BI have been tracking them for some time since my encounter with them while hunting down the Wolf Cult. They are a blight upon these lands, and they hold no right to the artifacts they hoard.$B$BIf we wish to recover this artifact, we will need to find their lair. Fortunately, I may just have the clue we need.',0),
(40786,'enUS','Yes, another one of these pesky artifacts. The meddling in the timestreams has grown worse of late... or is it that it will grow worse?$B$B<She sighs heavily.>',0),
(40787,'enUS','Yes, another one of these pesky artifacts. The meddling in the timestreams has grown worse of late... or is it that it will grow worse?$B$B<She sighs heavily.>',0),
(40792,'enUS','Ah, $n, you have returned. An otherworldly air hangs heavy about you.',0),
(40793,'enUS','Grandmaster, I\'ve prepared a brief report on all that I\'ve heard about the Broken Isles.$B$BYou may find it quite interesting.',0),
(40794,'enUS','<The officer looks down at what you\'re offering him and his eyes light up.>$B$BDo you know what you have here? You might have just delivered some of the most significant intel of the campaign.$B$BI will see to it personally that this gets into Lord Greymane\'s hands.',0),
(40795,'enUS','An excellent choice, Grandmaster.',0),
(40796,'enUS','<Absolon immediately consumes the Ancient Mana and seems incapable of speech for a short while.>',0),
(40798,'enUS','Absolon... is alive?',0),
(40814,'enUS','Well chosen. There isn\'t a moment to spare.',0),
(40815,'enUS','Oh, $n, it\'s you. Good, we\'ve got a little problem here .$B$BAltruis didn\'t think that Cyana and I could handle this on our own? He might have been right this time.',0),
(40816,'enUS','You must move quickly - our time is short.',0),
(40819,'enUS','I hold little love for these mages and their ilk, but they are necessary allies.',0),
(40821,'enUS','Yes, your weapon grows stronger! $B$BFriend cannot rest, though, for a new danger lies around the corner!',0),
(40823,'enUS','I can hardly believe my eyes. For one $C to control an entire army of demons is beyond what I thought the council was capable of. $B$BI only hope such power is enough to turn the tide of this war.',0),
(40824,'enUS','The plan is set, and the wheels are in motion.',0),
(40830,'enUS','Thank you for recovering Oculeth. He will be an invaluable asset to our cause.',0),
(40832,'enUS','Your reputation precedes you, $n.$B$BApologies for the secrecy. We simply could not risk the wrong person finding us here.',0),
(40834,'enUS','It\'s strange that the Dark Riders haven\'t followed us here, but I will take whatever boon I can get.$B$BI believe the key to finding the Dark Riders is here somewhere. Let us begin our search.',0),
(40835,'enUS','Dark energy hums from the journal, which appears to be the writings of Ariden, and chronicles his time in Deadwind Pass. One entry in particular stands out:$B$B\"The Nightbane have become restless of late, and whispers are abound of the Scythe of Elune having left Darnassus. It must be coming nearer, for the worgen are constantly drawn to it. They will lead me to it.$B$BThose cursed night elves think the weapon is safe in their care. They will soon find how wrong they are\"',0),
(40837,'enUS','The worgen appear to be drawn to the catacombs beneath Karazhan.$B$BCould it be...',0),
(40838,'enUS','Today was a great blow against the Dark Riders, and a victory for the people of Duskwood. $B$BThey are in your debt, as am I.',0),
(40839,'enUS','Welcome to the Uncrowned, Shadow $n.',0),
(40840,'enUS','Well chosen.',0),
(40847,'enUS','Aha! I knew you\'d come!',0),
(40849,'enUS','You did fine work today, lad.',0),
(40854,'enUS','How did you get your hands on this?!$B$B<Didi begins inspecting the husk.>$B$BDo you realize what we could do with something like this? Our own personal fel reaver?!$B$BWe could lay waste to our enemies!$B$BWe could advance our knowledge of science and technology!$B$BWe could make it serve us drinks!',0),
(40855,'enUS','Shush-it, $C! This \'ere place is crawlin\' with demony things.$B$BAye, Didi sent ye, did she? How is tha wee lass?$B$BIf yer lookin\' for demon parts, I can certainly help yeh with that!',0),
(40856,'enUS','Just wat are ye and Didi puttin\' together exactly?$B$BIs it big? Dangerous? Rer-diculous?$B$BI want in!',0),
(40857,'enUS','Oh good, another pair of hands. I\'m on ta somethin\', $n. I jes\' know it!',0),
(40858,'enUS','<You give Didi a slap on the back.>$B$BUgh! I take it Flintlocke says hello?$B$BLet\'s see what you brought me! Oh good, these will work perfectly.$B$BI\'ll get started on the repairs using a new invention of mine, the Auto-Hammer.$B$BHere\'s a copy of the blueprints for it if you\'re interested in making one for yourself.',0),
(40859,'enUS','What\'d I tell ya? Now THAT\'s usin\' yer HEAD!$B$BYeh see what I did there?$B$BSeeing as \'ow yeh tested them out fer me, I\'ll let yeh \'ave a copy of the blueprint fer \'em.',0),
(40860,'enUS','Oh aye! This is exactly what we needed! I wuz about ta start flingin\' wee animals.',0),
(40861,'enUS','Ohhh me poor innocent bullet dispensers! Look what they\'ve done ta yeh.$B$BWell at least they went down shootin\', tha\'s how I\'d like ta go.$B$BEre\'s tha schematic fer \'em. Deploy \'em near somethun\' yeh don\'t like!',0),
(40862,'enUS','Quite tha weed killer, eh? Haha!$B$BI figure ye\'ll be wantin\' more of them charges so I went ahead an\' wrote down tha schematic fer ye.$B$BI figure it\'s always good ta keep them plants an\' trees in line when they get all uppity.',0),
(40863,'enUS','We did it! That\'s one fully functional, killer-lookin\' fel reaver.$B$BShould it ever run out of power, here\'s the schematic for that battery I came up with.$B$BJust pop a new one in it and you should be good to go.$B$BBy the way, whatcha think we should name it? I was thinking somethin\' deadly, like \"Reaves.\"',0),
(40864,'enUS','Everything appears to be running as expected. Although to be honest, I half expected an explosion to go along with it.$B$BHere\'s the other schematic I made for Reaves. It\'s based off the auto-hammer design I gave you earlier.',0),
(40865,'enUS','$n, what\'re ya doin \'ere? Hobart sent ye, didn\'e?$B$BListen, I dunnae need yer help, but seein\' as how yeh made yer way down \'ere, maybe we can stir up some trouble ta\'gether.',0),
(40866,'enUS','Oh, yer finished! I swear I was jes\' about ta join yeh, too.$B$BWell, what\'s done is done. I s\'pose I can share me design with yeh since yeh got all the shells fer me.',0),
(40867,'enUS','Well lookie there! You managed to talk \'em outta their trinkets! Ye\'ll have to teach me their language someday.',0),
(40868,'enUS','The pieces! Well it\'s about time.$B$B<Hobart moves over to a machine and begins inserting the items you gave him.>$B$BI take it Flintlocke made you deliver these? Well since you did the legwork, you can have a copy of my design.$B$BIt\'s a new type of wormhole generator. Specifically designed for getting around Dalaran in the blink of an eye!',0),
(40869,'enUS','Good job on calibrating the power. Shame about those first few though...$B$BI\'ve adjusted the numbers on the schematic to the new specifications so you should be able to make the safe version.',0),
(40870,'enUS','<Didi takes the fireworks from you and continues to work at her bench.>$B$BThere we go. All done!$B$BApply this to your bot, and you should be able to launch fireworks wherever you want! ALL explosions are beautiful in their own way... but fireworks really are something else.',0),
(40871,'enUS','Oh aye, there yeh are lad. I was kinda hopin\' ta see yeh again.',0),
(40872,'enUS','Ah terrific! Nice work gettin\' them parts back. I thought I was gonna have ta drain the bay by blowin\' up Warden\'s Isle over there.$B$BThem boots seemed ta suit yeh - here\'s the schematic fer \'em if yeh need another pair.',0),
(40873,'enUS','Oh aye, tha\'s plenty, lad. I made sum adjustments ta tha design fer tha gunpack.$B$BYou should probably hold on to \'em, seein as \'ow these inventions of Hobart keep explodin\' on me.',0),
(40874,'enUS','Oh I wish I coulda been there ta see tha look on their fishy faces!$B$BEh, come ta think of it, fish always look kinda ser-prised.',0),
(40875,'enUS','Oh aye, yeh get me schematic! Here, keep a copy fer yerself, in case yer lookin\' for somethin\' to tattoo somewheres.$B$BIt\'s a damn shame about Lowping. Yeh know, come ta think of it, maybe we shoulda rescued him. Ah! Multi-tasking were never my thing.',0),
(40876,'enUS','So the gunshoes and pack were a success? I guess all these guns I made weren\'t such a waste after all.$B$BWhich reminds me, I saw the plans for those goggles Flintlocke made and I\'ve got to say, they were rather crude in their design. \"Dwarven Engineering\" is a bit of an oxymoron.$B$BI\'ve updated the schematic to not require so many materials.',0),
(40877,'enUS','Keep your fingers crossed, $n, and let\'s hope this works.$B$B$B$BYes! YES! It\'s alive, ALIVE!$B$BNow I can mass-market these gun parts as toys for children!',0),
(40878,'enUS','<Didi takes the pylons and begins tinkering with them and starts writing some notes.>$B$BYea, that should do the trick!$B$BOne new and improved Reaves module schematic for you, $n.',0),
(40879,'enUS','It\'s time I showed you my ultimate plans for Reaves! Allow me to present... piloted combat mode! Sure, the ingredients are ridiculously hard to find, and nobody even knows if it works, but hey - that\'s engineering for you!$B$BEnjoy the schematics!',0),
(40880,'enUS','An old schematic, still intact, is floating amongst the papers.$B$BAs you examine the schematic you realize that it\'s the circuit design for Blingtron!',0),
(40881,'enUS','That circuit design was exactly what I needed to finish the Blingtron module for Reaves.$B$BNow to reap the rewards, $n!',0),
(40882,'enUS','<Hobart takes the mechanism from you and begins tinkering with his design.>$B$BYes, I believe that\'s it. Good work, $n.$B$BAs per usual I\'ll let you have a copy of my schematic for your personal gain.',0),
(40883,'enUS','I thought the Moon Guard could endure anything...',0),
(40890,'enUS','<Archmage Khadgar has set aside a space here for the Tears of Elune, as well as the rest of the Pillars of Creation.>',0),
(40898,'enUS','I see that you have returned with the freshly carved remains of the fel basilisks.$B$BListen closely, and I will explain the purpose behind retrieving them...',0),
(40900,'enUS','The Scythe of Elune!$B$BI never thought I would see that weapon used without turning its wielder into a savage beast, but you\'ve brought balance to its primal nature.$B$BElune has certainly guided your hand, $n. You\'ve accomplished what no $C has done before!',0),
(40901,'enUS','Grimwing was a formidable demon... I must say I am impressed with your skill, $n.$B$BThere are many more demons here to kill. It is good to have someone capable at my side.',0),
(40904,'enUS','Where... where did you find this?',0),
(40907,'enUS','With my adversaries gone, I can claim leadership of Jandvik unopposed.',0),
(40908,'enUS','<Throndyr mutters through shallow breaths.>$B$BPoison... runs through... my body.',0),
(40919,'enUS','I can no longer hear their shrieking. Finally, peace and quiet!',0),
(40927,'enUS','I do not know who you are, but I must thank you.',0),
(40929,'enUS','I see you have returned with the emblems. Excellent.$B$BLet\'s see how this wyrmtongue reacts when we show him what we\'ve made of his comrades.',0),
(40930,'enUS','I am left with little choice. I cannot face another Dark Rider ambush alone, and you are obviously formidable.$B$BI will help you find your artifact, but only if you will allow me to return the others in their possession to their rightful place.$B$BDo we have a deal, $C?',0),
(40931,'enUS','As much as your company pains me, you are proving to be a powerful ally. $B$BI believe the key to finding the Dark Riders is here somewhere. It is strange that the riders haven\'t followed us here, but we should make haste lest they change their mind.',0),
(40932,'enUS','Dark energy hums from the journal, which appears to be the writings of Ariden, and chronicles his time in Deadwind Pass. One entry in particular stands out:$B$B\"I hear the whispers. They call me from the wet soil of shallow graves, hearkening me to my legacy. $B$B\"But what legacy? The merchant I once was had no special bloodline...$B$B\"Nevertheless, I am drawn to it. The dread blade... the world-ender... Apocalypse.\"',0),
(40933,'enUS','The chill down my spine tells me that you must have met with success.$B$BWhat did you find?',0),
(40934,'enUS','Today was a great blow against the Dark Riders, and a victory for the people of Duskwood. $B$BThey are in your debt, as am I.',0),
(40935,'enUS','The champion of the Lich King returns, and with a mighty weapon to bear against our demon foes!$B$BMay the Burning Legion tremble at the sight of our forces!',0),
(40938,'enUS','Welcome back, Cardinal. I think you\'ll find we\'ve done quite a job getting this place prepared for you. We should get started immediately.',0),
(40941,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(40942,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(40943,'enUS','News about da assault beat ya back, boss-mon. And some spoils of the fightin\'.$B$BYa be a force to be reckonin\' with.',0),
(40944,'enUS','Word of the assault has already made it back, as have some spoils from the fight.$B$BWell done sir, if you don\'t mind me saying.',0),
(40947,'enUS','Fine work. I will read these over.',0),
(40949,'enUS','Thank you. I feel better knowing they will not continue to sacrifice themselves for us.',0),
(40950,'enUS','It seems you struck a nerve.',0),
(40952,'enUS','There is much to do, noble $C. But first, I suppose you\'ll want to learn a little more about who I am and why I have sought you out.',0),
(40953,'enUS','I\'ve observed your skills for some time, $n. Watched you from a distance.$B$B$B$BWait, that sounds a little creepy. Sorry, my social skills are a tad rusty. Let me start again.$B$BOur order has been on the lookout for hunters who could lead the Unseen Path into a new era. No one is more qualified for that role than you.',0),
(40954,'enUS','The Legion has returned, and the Unseen Path needs new blood... new leadership.$B$BThe weapon you hold is proof there is no one better suited to this task.$B$BWill you take up the mantle? Will you fulfill the oath my order took so long ago?',0),
(40955,'enUS','Ohn\'ahra has not appeared to us since the order\'s founding!$B$BThis is surely a sign that with you guiding us, the Unseen Path will triumph over the Legion!',0),
(40956,'enUS','<This seems like a good location for the teleporter.>',0),
(40957,'enUS','Even with the support of your fellow hunters, the crusade against the Legion will consume much of your time and attention. It is a war you cannot fight alone.$B$BI first served our order\'s founder, Namuria Gladesong, acting as her eyes and ears when she was needed elsewhere. It would be my honor to do the same for you, $n.',0),
(40958,'enUS','Hail, Pathfinder! It will be my honor to aid you in the fight against the Legion.',0),
(40959,'enUS','Excellent choice. The campaign against the Legion has begun!',0),
(40960,'enUS','A pearl, you say? Well now, let me have a good look at that...',0),
(40961,'enUS','She\'s a BEAUTY! I\'ve never seen the like!$B$BYeah yeah, sure, throw \'er in that fountain. Light knows people throw all sorts of other junk in there.$B$B<The pearl glows brighter now, and moves to a spot above the water.>',0),
(40962,'enUS','Malfurion departed in a great hurry, but he bade me give you this before you left. Thank you for all you have done for Azeroth, and for all that you will do in time to come.',0),
(40963,'enUS','I heard screams, and I was gratified that they belonged to the Nightborne. Well done.',0),
(40964,'enUS','Serena sent you? Good... she still lives.',0),
(40965,'enUS','A lesson we all must one day learn. Never assume your enemy dead until you see their corpse. <Lothrius grins.>',0),
(40967,'enUS','Thank the Mother Moon... They survived!',0),
(40969,'enUS','Lothrius and Thalrenus live, then. There may be some hope yet. Thank you for braving the bridge, stranger.',0),
(40970,'enUS','They had no right to this power. Thank you.',0),
(40971,'enUS','We were able to make it here safely, thanks to you.',0),
(40972,'enUS','I called them here. I will see that they are taken care of after the horrors my people put them through.',0),
(40976,'enUS','Vol\'jin\'s death was part of a larger plan. The Legion thrives on weakening its enemies from within. The demons will strike when their enemy is at its most vulnerable.$B$BWhatever grief the Horde\'s people are feelilng, they can no longer afford to ignore us.$B$BOur time is now, Illidari!',0),
(40982,'enUS','Of course the Legion would try to infiltrate this funeral. With the leaders of the Horde gathered in one place at one time, it was too tasty of a target for the demons to resist.',0),
(40983,'enUS','Your warning just saved us from what might have been a catastrophic loss. Now we can unleash our vengeance upon this Legion filth.$B$BYou now have my attention, $C... and perhaps a bit of appreciation as well.',0),
(40986,'enUS','Though I\'ll admit I may not have been able to do this alone, I will not forget the transgressions that happened today.$B$BYou have what you came for, $C. I think it is time you were on your way.',0),
(40987,'enUS','The champion of the Lich King returns, and with a mighty weapon to bear against our demon foes!$B$BMay the Burning Legion tremble at the sight of our forces!',0),
(40988,'enUS','$C! I was hoping you\'d come back.$B$BHere, take a sample of some of the recipes and dishes I\'ve been working on.',0),
(40989,'enUS','Master $n!! I knew you\'d come.$B$BHere, take a sample of some of the recipes and dishes I\'ve been working on.',0),
(40990,'enUS','You are truly amazing, Master $n.$B$BNow, let\'s get to work, shall we?',0),
(40991,'enUS','We\'ve done it! With this technique, we should be able to prepare dried mackerel strips much more efficiently.$B$BI am certain that there is much more we can learn. Keep bringing me ingredients, and I will keep the oven on!',0),
(40994,'enUS','So, what can I do for you today, Master $n?',0),
(40995,'enUS','Hey, don\'t even mention it, pal. I\'m here for ya any time you need anything!$B$BSeriously though, don\'t mention it. There are some folks that would do anything to get their hands on this stuff.',0),
(40996,'enUS','I don\'t know nothin\' about nobody.$B$BOh, who I am I kiddin\'? I know everything about everybody! How\'s it goin\', Shadow $n?',0),
(40997,'enUS','Great choice! We have tons of intel on that place.',0),
(41001,'enUS','We may have finally overcome this naga threat.',0),
(41002,'enUS','You have proven our worth to the new Warchief. Excellent work.$B$BTo vanquish the Legion, we will need the Horde\'s strength at our backs.',0),
(41003,'enUS','Incredible. The very staff the Emperor used to cloak Pandaria in mists all those ages ago!$B$BTreat that staff well, $n. It will save your life. And probably the lives of all your friends, as well...',0),
(41009,'enUS','There is much to do, noble $C. But first, I suppose you\'ll want to learn a little more about who I am and why I have sought you out.',0),
(41010,'enUS','What in the world have you brought me?! Nat told you to ask me to turn THIS into a pole?$B$B<Marcia takes the severed lure from you. As she holds it close to the pearl, it begins to resonate with it.>$B$BThat\'s interesting. There seems to be a connection between this and the pearl. Maybe turning this into a fishing rod can yield some interesting results...',0),
(41015,'enUS','Ach, there ye are. Let me see that priceless weapon ye\'re swingin\' \'round like a stick ye bought at the gift shop!',0),
(41017,'enUS','Well ain\'t that nice an\' shiny!$B$BYou\'ll need ta get used to usin\' that thing. Then we can mess with it rather than, ye know, puttin\' it in a museum and respectin\' it for the piece o\' history that it is.$B$B You should head back to Alonsus, he\'s giving us the eye.',0),
(41019,'enUS','An excellent choice! We will do our best to support your efforts on the Broken Isles.',0),
(41028,'enUS','I must admit I am impressed. You may actually be of some use to us.',0),
(41030,'enUS','You were wise to keep these out of our enemies\' hands, $C. I believe you can be trusted.',0),
(41032,'enUS','Yes! I can feel their spells receding. Soon I will be able to rejoin Thalrenus!',0),
(41033,'enUS','This place is built for war - it\'s exactly what we need to level the playing field.',0),
(41034,'enUS','There are sea giants in the bay!?$B$BYou must tell Toryl about this grave news right away.',0),
(41035,'enUS','I was a fool. I thought that I could banish Kathra\'natir once and for all, but instead the dreadlord broke free.$B$BIn the years he spent trapped within my body, he must have been privy to my secrets... such as those of the Council of Tirisfal.$B$BThe damage he could do with this knowledge is unthinkable. He must be stopped.',0),
(41036,'enUS','In times past, the Council of Tirisfal called upon the Tirisgarde, the protectors of Dalaran, to do battle in the Guardian\'s absence.$B$BIt is clear now that the hall of the Tirisgarde must be rebuilt to face this new threat.$B$BI need your help to accomplish this. First of all, you\'ll need to know how to get to this hall. I will show you.',0),
(41037,'enUS','The Fel Hammer is fully operational.',0),
(41038,'enUS','My master was loved by many, and she passed her knowledge to me.$B$BHowever, the recipe for Storm Brew, her most fiercely guarded secret, was stolen before she could teach it to me.',0),
(41039,'enUS','The last time I saw these notes, I was still a young child.$B$BI understand much of what is written here now.$B$BIt won\'t be easy to acquire everything here, but I believe we can do it, $n.',0),
(41040,'enUS','Hello, champion.$B$BI have been watching you from afar.',0),
(41047,'enUS','Wondrous! The growing power of your artifact will strike fear into the hearts of the demon army!',0),
(41052,'enUS','Very well, let us see what awaits us on that ill-fated shore.$B$BAt the very least, a lot of dead demons! Hah!',0),
(41053,'enUS','Greetings, $n. It will be my honor to assist you with your artifact.',0),
(41054,'enUS','Pray my husband makes it through this alive, $R.',0),
(41056,'enUS','I pray it is not too late, friend.',0),
(41059,'enUS','Tell me, were the Halls of Valor as amazing as the stories say? Regardless, you got the cauldron. Now we can begin brewing.',0),
(41060,'enUS','The Fel Hammer is ours at last.$B$BNicely done.',0),
(41062,'enUS','It is my honor to serve, $n.',0),
(41064,'enUS','Such power! The Legion\'s armies will fall before you in droves.',0),
(41066,'enUS','We must not underestimate the Legion - I fear they are even more powerful than we realize.',0),
(41067,'enUS','<Kayn sighs.>$B$BI know that look. I, too, gazed into the crucible and saw the horrors of the tomb.$B$BWe must act quickly.',0),
(41069,'enUS','Agreed. You are as skilled a tactician as myself.',0),
(41070,'enUS','It is my honor to serve, $n.',0),
(41085,'enUS','This is a wise choice. $B$BIt should serve you well in our hunt for Kathra\'natir.',0),
(41086,'enUS','Astounding, Grandmaster! Reports are flying in about your success. Without your help, many of our outposts around the Broken Isles would have fallen.',0),
(41087,'enUS','I don\'t know about you, Grandmaster, but I think we should take a well-earned rest after all of this.',0),
(41096,'enUS','<Altruis nods knowingly.>$B$BI saw it too.$B$BWe must consider our next move carefully.',0),
(41097,'enUS','<The Shard of Vorgos locks into position next to the portal. Swirling fel energy collects around the shard, filling the room with an ominous, dark presence.>',0),
(41098,'enUS','<The Shard of Kozak locks into position next to the portal. You can feel the dark writhing of fel energy surround you as it collects near the portal.>',0),
(41099,'enUS','Well-chosen. The Legion will soon fear the very sight of the Illidari on the battlefield.',0),
(41105,'enUS','A mighty blade! Forged by the son of vrykul, enchanted by elven sorcery, and quenched in the blood of a C\'thraxxi. It will serve you well, $n. With it, you will put an end to our enemies!',0),
(41106,'enUS','Good, soon the ritual will be ready to begin.',0),
(41107,'enUS','Excellent. This will be enough for my purposes.',0),
(41112,'enUS','You could say you\'ve got my attention, pal!$B$BSo you\'re looking to hire me on full-time, eh? Well if the future payoffs are anything like this, I\'d say you\'ve got yourself a deal.',0),
(41113,'enUS','I understand he may be unconventional, but I think this goblin is exactly what we\'ll need to quickly get this new Tirisgarde up to snuff for the task at hand.$B$BI\'ve already sent word to many talented mages who can help. They await transportation to the Hall, where they can begin their new purpose.$B$BShall we?',0),
(41114,'enUS','You learn quickly, $n. $B$BI think Kathra\'natir will rue the day he made you his enemy.',0),
(41115,'enUS','I am honored to have fought by your side at the Peak of Serenity, $n. Your leadership will help us greatly in the fight against the Legion.$B$BI would like to fight for you, if you would have me as a champion. I believe my skills as a brewer may also be of service to the order.',0),
(41119,'enUS','What of the others? Did they...?$B$BI see. They gave their lives for a worthy cause - the Twinblades will change the tide of this war, mark my words.',0),
(41120,'enUS','Let\'s get this done with. These bureaucrats already test my patience.',0),
(41121,'enUS','Suramar? That is only a short flight from here.',0),
(41123,'enUS','Oh, thank the Magistrix! I was worried it was lost forever.$B$BI see that this ring has seen some... use. I do hope it doesn\'t belong to anyone important. Or... vocal.',0),
(41124,'enUS','So you\'re a Conjuror now, huh? Fan-cy!$B$BWe\'ve got a good start with this Tirisgarde thing here, but I think we should keep up the recruiting if we actually plan on invading demon-town.$B$BFortunately for you, nobody negotiates contracts like a goblin!',0),
(41125,'enUS','Your artifact is well on its way to reaching its true potential, but even with this power you will not be able to fight the Legion alone.$B$BWe will need to begin recruiting other mages to our cause. Unfortunately, the protective wards surrounding the hall may be prohibitive to this. $B$BAfter all, I cannot personally teleport every one of them here.$B$BHowever, a solution to this particular problem might be right under our noses.',0),
(41138,'enUS','I will call upon you again, I am sure.',0),
(41139,'enUS','Ye found the key! Quickly, see if it fits...$B$BAye, that\'s the one! Ye did it!',0),
(41140,'enUS','It\'s good to finally be free from this dreadful cage. As thanks, I will keep my word to you and your grotesquely hairy friend.',0),
(41141,'enUS','Alright, then! I can get started recruiting, and you can get to taking the fight to the demons!$B$BYeah, I know I\'m letting you take the easy job, but hey, what are friends for?',0),
(41143,'enUS','Mlrgmlr rmlgml! Mrlmgrlg gmlrmlrg, grmlgmlr lmrglgr mlgmrlr. Mlgrmlgr grmlmgl, Mrgrlilgrl...',0),
(41146,'enUS','Lespin shall pay for his crimes!',0),
(41148,'enUS','Your eyes are opening to our reality. I can see it in your expression. Good.',0),
(41149,'enUS','<The ward snaps to life, giving you a slight pinch. Kel\'danath must have put great care into developing a spell that would scare the withered away without harming them.>',0),
(41155,'enUS','Though I\'ll admit I may not have been able to do this alone, I will not forget the transgressions that happened today.$B$BYou have what you came for, $C. I think it is time you were on your way.',0),
(41156,'enUS','Friend has the weapon? $B$BYes, Calydus can feel its power!',0),
(41157,'enUS','<Brann takes the fragments and begins reassembling them.>$B$BWell, ye definitely found more o\' the Titan Disc, but ye found something else too.$B$BHere, take a look at that!',0),
(41158,'enUS','I\'m gettin\' closer to finding another piece of the titan relic, an\' I need yer keen eyes.',0),
(41159,'enUS','Did ye run into any imps while ye were out diggen? Those blasted demons kept poppin\' up on me!$B$BAlright, if ye dinnae find the disc at any o\' those places, then there\'s but one place left ta look.',0),
(41160,'enUS','It would appear the earth trembled at YOUR power instead. Well done, champion.$B$BAs we agreed, here are your prizes in exchange for the cores.',0),
(41161,'enUS','I\'m close, $n. I can feel it in me bones!',0),
(41162,'enUS','Aye, that\'s all of \'em, lad. I\'ll just fix this up and we\'ll see what happens...',0),
(41163,'enUS','Well that was a bit... eh... underwhelming. But hey, at least we got a piece o\' tha titan disc!',0),
(41164,'enUS','There\'s demon stink all over this place. But there\'s also a lot of clues as to where a piece of the titan disc is!',0),
(41165,'enUS','I\'m startin\' ta think you may be as good an archaeologist as I am. But don\'t let that go ta yer head, lad.$B$B<Brann lets out a chuckle and begins to study the artifacts you brought him.>$B$BAye, that\'s it! I know where the chamber is. And once I\'ve reassembled tha key, we\'re in business.',0),
(41166,'enUS','A piece of the titan disc and a jar of blood. Well it\'s no wonder the elves locked this place up nice\'n tight.$B$BI\'ll take me disc piece and you can do whatever ye want with that blood.',0),
(41167,'enUS','Me equipment? Thanks, $n!$B$BYe know, it\'s a good thing ye\'re here. This place gives me tha willies!',0),
(41168,'enUS','<Brann skims over the book you\'ve compiled.>$B$BSo where\'s the last chapter?',0),
(41169,'enUS','Oh ho! Ye found the missing chapter AND a piece of me titan disc?!$B$BThis truly is a day of celebration. I\'ll let ye have the book, and ye can tell me what \'appened at tha end of it.',0),
(41170,'enUS','After all that time, and we\'re still missing one piece!$B$BI swear the gods are workin\' against me on me quest, $n.$B$BOh well, back ta work! And here\'s a little somethin\' for all the hard work ye\'ve done fer me.',0),
(41171,'enUS','I ask for an archaeologist and they send an adventurer. Or perhaps you are both.$B$BEither way, let\'s get to work.',0),
(41172,'enUS','<Tae\'thelan listens to your recount of what you learned.>$B$BVery interesting. If what you\'ve said is true, then I believe I know where the location of the artifact is.',0),
(41173,'enUS','Let\'s see what you\'ve found.$B$B<Tae\'thelan studies the artifact for some time and lets out a sigh.>$B$BUseless. It\'s nothing more than a star field generator. Probably from some academy before the war.$B$BYou can have it back, $n. I have no use for it.',0),
(41174,'enUS','$n, good to see you.$B$BI was hoping that the elves here would be a bit more... willing to let us inspect their artifacts, but such is not the case.$B$BAnd that\'s where you come in.',0),
(41175,'enUS','You found it?$B$B<Tae\'thelan listens as you explain about the missing jewels.>$B$BI see. So the crown was just a vessel and the jewels are the true source of power.',0),
(41176,'enUS','<Tae\'thelan takes the jewels from you and looks them over closely.>$B$BThere may have been power in them once, but it\'s been all but drained. These are just pretty jewels now.$B$BHere, take them. Consider them payment for your services here.',0),
(41177,'enUS','$n, you\'re just in time to test out a new method I\'ve been working on.',0),
(41178,'enUS','It was successful? That\'s excellent news!$B$BThis will speed up our process ten fold!',0),
(41179,'enUS','<In the small chest, you find a chest with a raven\'s head etched into the lid.>',0),
(41180,'enUS','This is an exciting time, $n. And you\'re going to get a front row seat to the show.',0),
(41181,'enUS','You\'ve found the location? Then we must make haste.$B$BLet\'s go, $n.',0),
(41182,'enUS','NO! How did we fail? We were so close.$B$BThe explosives were too powerful. Those damned goblins ruined everything!$B$BNow only a handful of shards of what was once an object of unimaginable power remain.$B$BTake whichever one you want, $n. I\'d like to keep the rest to study.',0),
(41183,'enUS','Hello, $n. I\'m glad you came.$B$BI\'ve found something that may serve both of our interests.',0),
(41184,'enUS','Yes, I believe that\'s all of them.$B$B<Tae\'thelan carefully reconstructs the mold.>$B$BAnd now we just need to forge a new set of keys.',0),
(41185,'enUS','This is not a true key, but rather a device to provide access to the Nar\'thalas Academy.$B$BThe academy was once a great location of knowledge for night elves to learn the arcane magics, but has long since long been destroyed.$B$BThe key is useless junk. You can keep it.',0),
(41186,'enUS','Good to see you, $n. I hope you\'re as interested about the tauren here as I am.',0),
(41187,'enUS','Thank you for your help, $n. Now perhaps you can help me with my research.',0),
(41188,'enUS','This is... not a weapon of Huln\'s. From the looks of it, I believe this to be the Spear of Rethu, an ancient tauren miner.$B$BI have no interest in this artifact, $n. You may have it.',0),
(41189,'enUS','There\'s more to this land than I ever realized, $n. Now listen...',0),
(41190,'enUS','<Lessah listens to your recounting of the stories you discovered.>$B$BIf what you\'ve said is true then that means that the piece I\'m looking for is the necklace that Huln once wore.',0),
(41191,'enUS','<Lessah examines the necklace.>$B$BHow can this be?! All my research suggested that this belonged to Huln.$B$BI\'m sorry, $n, but this necklace is a creation of the drogbar. I\'ll give it back to you to do with it what you want.',0),
(41192,'enUS','$n, I\'ve found an actual piece of something very close to Huln$B$BI believe that this is the very bone of Eche\'ro, Huln Highmountain\'s animal companion!',0),
(41193,'enUS','What an honor, $n. To think that Eche\'ro\'s spirit will come to your aid should you need it... that is a great reward indeed.$B$BAnd for me, to witness the majesty of Huln himself! I shall continue to study him, and the glorious legacy he left behind.',0),
(41197,'enUS','They look so happy to be home. Excellent work.',0),
(41206,'enUS','Many thanks, miner. This leystone shall not be wasted.',0),
(41207,'enUS','Many thanks, $C. This leystone shall not be wasted.',0),
(41214,'enUS','<Angus wipes away a tear as he speaks.>$B$BBrambley, lad... I promise ye\'ll have tha\' best burial money can buy! An\' all the ale ye can drink...',0),
(41215,'enUS','Excellent work. They do not respect the hunt, so they must be reminded of their place.',0),
(41216,'enUS','I could hear their cries and see the carnage from here! That will teach the Nightborne to enslave creatures. Have they fallen so far during all those years under the shield?',0),
(41217,'enUS','For a $R who has spent so much time inside Gnomeregan, you look positively fit and healthy, $n. That\'s good. Before we can complete what Operation: Gnomeregan began, we\'re going to need more hunters like you.',0),
(41218,'enUS','It\'s good to meet you, $n. You\'ve probably heard others speaking of Operation: Gnomeregan. Let me tell you a bit about what happened and why we left the dwarven city of Ironforge.',0),
(41220,'enUS','As I suspected, the Illidari are holding the line against the Burning Legion, but just barely.$B$BWe must come to their aid, $n.',0),
(41221,'enUS','This citadel was one of the Legion\'s most valuable assets - it will serve us well.',0),
(41222,'enUS','It canna\' be true!$B$BBrambley... my dear ol\' friend! Why did ye have to go an\' die?',0),
(41223,'enUS','Many thanks, herbalist. This foxflower shall not be wasted.',0),
(41224,'enUS','Many thanks, $C. This foxflower shall not be wasted.',0),
(41230,'enUS','These devices are peculiar. They are like the traps our hunters use, but can magically attract and trap nearby beasts.',0),
(41231,'enUS','I saw everything from out here. That was... messy.',0),
(41235,'enUS','Many thanks, skinner. This leather shall not be wasted.',0),
(41237,'enUS','Many thanks, $C. This leather shall not be wasted.',0),
(41240,'enUS','Many thanks, fisherman. This salmon shall not be wasted.',0),
(41255,'enUS','Excellent. There\'s no time to waste.',0),
(41256,'enUS','Manatrout was completely fished out of our harbors. Since the shield was raised all we have had of the liquor is memories on our palates.',0),
(41258,'enUS','Victory tastes sweeter than any dish, even one of mine.',0),
(41267,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, fisherman. We needed this queenfish badly.',0),
(41272,'enUS','Hail, fisherman. I can take these perch off of your hands. Your gift will be put to good use.',0),
(41277,'enUS','Well met, $R fisherman. The Valarjar thank you for bringing these stormrays.',0),
(41282,'enUS','You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time, fisherman. Our people were running short on supplies.',0),
(41287,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, herbalist. We needed this aethril badly.',0),
(41288,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, $C. We needed this aethril badly.',0),
(41292,'enUS','Hail, herbalist. I can take this dreamleaf off of your hands. Your gift will be put to good use.',0),
(41293,'enUS','Hail, $C. I can take this dreamleaf off of your hands. Your gift will be put to good use.',0),
(41297,'enUS','Well met, $R herbalist. The Valarjar thank you for bringing this fjarnskaggl.',0),
(41298,'enUS','Well met, $R $C. The Valarjar thank you for bringing this fjarnskaggl.',0),
(41302,'enUS','You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time, herbalist. Our people were running short on supplies.',0),
(41303,'enUS','You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time, $C. Our people were running short on supplies.',0),
(41307,'enUS','Excellent. I shall have these melted down and turned into ingots for my next batch of commissions.',0),
(41309,'enUS','It\'s good to see a friendly face, I don\'t know how much longer I could have held out on my own!',0),
(41311,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, miner. We needed this leystone badly.',0),
(41312,'enUS','Hail, miner. I can take this leystone off of your hands. Your gift will be put to good use.',0),
(41313,'enUS','Well met, $R miner. The Valarjar thank you for bringing this leystone.',0),
(41314,'enUS','You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time, miner. Our people were running short on supplies.',0),
(41315,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, $C. We needed this leystone badly.',0),
(41316,'enUS','Hail, $C. I can take this leystone off of your hands. Your gift will be put to good use.',0),
(41317,'enUS','Well met, $R $C. The Valarjar thank you for bringing this leystone.',0),
(41318,'enUS','You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time, $C. Our people were running short on supplies.',0),
(41320,'enUS','Those wretched creatures are a scourge on our beautiful lands. At least they had good taste in their accessories.$B$BOr maybe they just like shiny things.',0),
(41326,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, skinner. We needed these stormscales badly.',0),
(41327,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, $C. We needed these stormscales badly.',0),
(41332,'enUS','Congratulations, Archdruid $n.$B$BWe will be counting on you in the days ahead.',0),
(41335,'enUS','A good choice. There is no time to lose - let us begin!',0),
(41338,'enUS','Hail, skinner. I can take this leather off of your hands. Your gift will be put to good use.',0),
(41339,'enUS','Hail, $C. I can take this leather off of your hands. Your gift will be put to good use.',0),
(41344,'enUS','Well met, $R skinner. The Valarjar thank you for bringing these stormscales.',0),
(41345,'enUS','Well met, $R $C. The Valarjar thank you for bringing these stormscales.',0),
(41350,'enUS','You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time, skinner. Our people were running short on supplies.',0),
(41351,'enUS','You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time, $C. Our people were running short on supplies.',0),
(41367,'enUS','You\'d best carry a reason of a higher caliber than that to dare interrupt my time with these buxom beauties.',0),
(41368,'enUS','Ah, a bank note. Mr. Stonebrow\'s payment.$B$BJust in the nick of time it would seem.',0),
(41394,'enUS','<Johnny raises his arm exaggeratedly, glancing at his naked wrist.>$B$BMy, my, quite the LETHARGIC adventurer, aren\'t you? That just might cover my repair bills from the many dungeons I\'ve plundered.',0),
(41397,'enUS','Is the deed done?',0),
(41409,'enUS','Fjolrik died in honor of Jandvik. We will remember his bravery.',0),
(41410,'enUS','<Fjolrik looks at you weakly.>$B$BYou made it back in time...',0),
(41411,'enUS','Ah, a bank note. Mr. Stonebrow\'s payment.$B$BJust in the nick of time it would seem.',0),
(41413,'enUS','Zen\'kiki be excited ta\' be learning from da Archdruid!$B$BI be keepin\' dis place real nice for ya in return for ye help.',0),
(41415,'enUS','Any of the three weapons you learned of would be a huge boon in the war against the Legion.$B$BBut your crusade must start with one of them, so you must choose.',0),
(41422,'enUS','<Mylune\'s face brightens.>$B$BThen there is still hope!',0),
(41425,'enUS','The Sashj\'tar forces are far greater than I imagined.',0),
(41426,'enUS','I must express gratitude for the vrykul you have saved this day.',0),
(41436,'enUS','Delving into the Dream with such darkness encroaching is no simple task, one few druids dare attempt, but I\'m afraid your journey is far from over.',0),
(41449,'enUS','My preparations are complete. Are you prepared to enter the Dream?',0),
(41452,'enUS','All is in its proper place. We are that much closer to being settled.',0),
(41453,'enUS','Well this is an interesting turn of events.',0),
(41462,'enUS','Ahhhh... Well done, I am sure our furry friends here are very thankful for your efforts.',0),
(41463,'enUS','How good of Mayruna to send help. I had nearly lost hope.',0),
(41464,'enUS','I am relieved, though there remains more we must do.',0),
(41465,'enUS','Ahh, see! I told you it would not tarnish. Now there\'s nothing linking me to that fool...$B$BWhat\'s that? A plot to weaken his position? Regardless, the damage has been done. Better safe than sorry.',0),
(41466,'enUS','By the Magistrix, I had forgotten how ugly that thing is. Impeccable workmanship, obviously. Just... ugh. I should melt the whole thing down.',0),
(41467,'enUS','What a disturbing tale!',0),
(41468,'enUS','The Claws of Ursoc?$B$BI thought I\'d go the rest of my days without hearing of them again. Is our situation truly so dire? They were sealed away for good reason!',0),
(41469,'enUS','Welcome back. I see we are ready to begin.',0),
(41473,'enUS','This fine gentleman was just telling me how dearly he loves his forest. Let us assist him!',0),
(41474,'enUS','They are looking better fed already!',0),
(41475,'enUS','In the end, they will all thrive- for with more Sablehorn, the wolves will eat better in the years to come.',0),
(41478,'enUS','Welcome, $R.',0),
(41479,'enUS','Well done, $R.',0),
(41480,'enUS','Such a gluttonous creature.',0),
(41485,'enUS','I am much relieved, $n.',0),
(41494,'enUS','Your assistance made this all possible. Thank you.',0),
(41499,'enUS','The naga will not be taking any more of my kin!',0),
(41510,'enUS','A sound decision, Farseer. Behind me I have opened up an astral portal to Dalaran to help our people move quickly between our base of operations and the Broken Isles. Step through to return to Dalaran. You may always use the portal to travel back here whenever you need to augment your artifact or command your followers.$B$BMay the elements guide you, Farseer.',0),
(41540,'enUS','I don\'t know the full details, but a demon prisoner has given us the first solid lead on Alleria Windrunner\'s whereabouts in a very long time.$B$BThe ranger-general has joined with members of the Farstriders on the Broken Shore. She\'s putting a team together, and your presence is crucial to its success.',0),
(41541,'enUS','There you are! I knew you\'d be bitin\' to find Titanstrike.$B$BDon\'t mind ol\' Huey here. The city of mages is no place for a gryphon.',0),
(41542,'enUS','My brother Wuho and I will be honored to have you on this quest, $n. Talonclaw is a sacred artifact to my people, and I know with your help we will recover it.$B$BWe just have to do one thing before we head out, speak with the Eagle Spirit.',0),
(41574,'enUS','You might feel a bit dizzy after going through that teleporter. The Broken Isles isn\'t exactly next door, after all.',0),
(41575,'enUS','<The beacon glows as you infuse it with Ancient Mana.>',0),
(41606,'enUS','I do not know who you are, but you are not a sea giant, and that is enough for me.',0),
(41607,'enUS','They are alive? That is good news. Their knowledge of the defenses will be invaluable.',0),
(41618,'enUS','I only wish that I had the chance to get to him first.$B$BBah! His body can rot in these waters for all I care.',0),
(41625,'enUS','So you seek Light\'s Wrath? A dangerous weapon, to be sure.$B$BLong ago the Kirin Tor entrusted its safekeeping to the blue dragonflight. It was locked away in the only place that could contain its rampant power - the Nexus Vault.$B$BI have not been there in some time, however. After the blue dragonflight was dissolved, the Nexus was abandoned. There is no knowing whether the Nexus Vault is still intact - or what may be waiting in the Nexus itself.',0),
(41626,'enUS','This appears to be a communication device commonly utilized by the ethereals.$B$BPerhaps it could be the key to finding out who is behind the happenings at the Dragonshrine.',0),
(41631,'enUS','You have my gratitude for saving Azuregos, $n. I can rest easy knowing that the Nexus is under his care.$B$BAs for you, I can see you\'re full of surprises. Never in my time have I seen a $C who can control the chaotic energies of Light\'s Wrath. $B$BYou are truly the hero we need to face the Legion.',0),
(41632,'enUS','So the dragons proved helpful? This is good, we may need their assistance in the war to come.',0),
(41633,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, blacksmith. We needed these greaves badly.',0),
(41634,'enUS','Hail, blacksmith. I can take these armguards off of your hands. Your gift will be put to good use.',0),
(41635,'enUS','Many thanks, blacksmith. These boots shall not be wasted.',0),
(41636,'enUS','Well met, $R blacksmith. The Valarjar thank you for bringing this breastplate.',0),
(41637,'enUS','You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time, blacksmith. Our people were running short on supplies.',0),
(41638,'enUS','The Kirin Tor thank you.',0),
(41639,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, leatherworker. We needed these spaulders badly.',0),
(41640,'enUS','Hail, leatherworker. I can take this mask off of your hands. Your gift will be put to good use.',0),
(41641,'enUS','Many thanks, leatherworker. These armbands shall not be wasted.',0),
(41642,'enUS','Well met, $R leatherworker. The Valarjar thank you for bringing these boots.',0),
(41643,'enUS','You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time, leatherworker. Our people were running short on supplies.',0),
(41644,'enUS','The Kirin Tor thank you.',0),
(41645,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, tailor. We needed these epaulets badly.',0),
(41646,'enUS','Hail, tailor. I can take these gloves off of your hands. Your gift will be put to good use.',0),
(41647,'enUS','Many thanks, tailor. This robe shall not be wasted.',0),
(41648,'enUS','Well met, $R tailor. The Valarjar thank you for bringing these bracers.',0),
(41649,'enUS','You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time, tailor. Our people were running short on supplies.',0),
(41650,'enUS','The Kirin Tor thank you.',0),
(41651,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, jewelcrafter. We needed this necklace badly.',0),
(41652,'enUS','Hail, jewelcrafter. I can take this jewelry off of your hands. Your gift will be put to good use.',0),
(41653,'enUS','Many thanks, jewelcrafter. This jewelry shall not be wasted.',0),
(41654,'enUS','Well met, $R jewelcrafter. The Valarjar thank you for bringing this ring.',0),
(41655,'enUS','You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time, jewelcrafter. Our people were running short on supplies.',0),
(41656,'enUS','The Kirin Tor thank you.',0),
(41657,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, alchemist. We needed these potions badly.',0),
(41658,'enUS','Hail, alchemist. I can take these elixirs off of your hands. Your gift will be put to good use.',0),
(41659,'enUS','Many thanks, alchemist. These elixirs shall not be wasted.',0),
(41660,'enUS','Well met, $R alchemist. The Valarjar thank you for bringing these potions.',0),
(41661,'enUS','You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time, alchemist. Our people were running short on supplies.',0),
(41662,'enUS','The Kirin Tor thank you.',0),
(41663,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, scribe. We needed these supplies badly.',0),
(41664,'enUS','Hail, scribe. I can take these supplies off of your hands. Your gift will be put to good use.',0),
(41665,'enUS','Many thanks, scribe. These supplies shall not be wasted.',0),
(41666,'enUS','Well met, $R scribe. The Valarjar thank you for bringing these supplies.',0),
(41667,'enUS','You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time, scribe. Our people were running short on supplies.',0),
(41668,'enUS','The Kirin Tor thank you.',0),
(41669,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, enchanter. We needed this enchantment badly.',0),
(41670,'enUS','Hail, enchanter. I can take this enchantment off of your hands. Your gift will be put to good use.',0),
(41671,'enUS','Many thanks, enchanter. This enchantment shall not be wasted.',0),
(41672,'enUS','Well met, $R enchanter. The Valarjar thank you for bringing this enchantment.',0),
(41673,'enUS','You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time, enchanter. Our people were running short on supplies.',0),
(41674,'enUS','The Kirin Tor thank you.',0),
(41675,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, engineer. We needed this device badly.',0),
(41676,'enUS','Hail, engineer. I can take this device off of your hands. Your gift will be put to good use.',0),
(41677,'enUS','Many thanks, engineer. This auto-hammer shall not be wasted.',0),
(41678,'enUS','Well met, $R engineer. The Valarjar thank you for bringing this gunpack.',0),
(41679,'enUS','You couldn\'t have arrived at a better time, engineer. Our people were running short on supplies.',0),
(41680,'enUS','The Kirin Tor thank you.',0),
(41689,'enUS','We all owe you a great deal for your heroism, $n. I owe you a great deal.$B$BI suspect this war is far from over.',0),
(41690,'enUS','I don\'t know how much longer I would have lasted had you not arrived - thank you.',0),
(41702,'enUS','<A small tag hanging from his sleeve reads \"16 - Theryn.\">',0),
(41704,'enUS','So, Kel\'danath turned in the end...$B$BHe deserved better. Thank you for giving him peace.',0),
(41707,'enUS','Such violence should not be necessary. Thank you, regardless.',0),
(41708,'enUS','He is still alive, but the rest remains to be seen.',0),
(41709,'enUS','You have all the parts that you will need... two in some cases.',0),
(41724,'enUS','No one is safe from this corruption.',0),
(41728,'enUS','I did not expect the Grandmaster himself! Your strength will help us turn the tide. We cannot let these demons succeed!',0),
(41729,'enUS','You did well, little wicket. Stay strong together, that\'s the ticket! The enemies have tried to spread their taint, but we stopped them with a little restraint!',0),
(41730,'enUS','Good wicket, strong wicket, thanks for helping! You\'ve sent the demons off, groaning and yelping!',0),
(41731,'enUS','The grounds are safe, thanks to you... too bad we couldn\'t save any of that brew!$B$B<The Monkey King heaves a great sigh.>',0),
(41732,'enUS','Tian Monastery is safe again, thanks to you.',0),
(41733,'enUS','Our order\'s teachings will continue, thanks to you, Grandmaster.',0),
(41734,'enUS','Grandmaster, the stories they tell about you are true. I witnessed your fortitude first hand at Tian Monastery.$B$BMy life and heart are pledged to the $C order, and we have many battles ahead of us.$B$BLet me be one of your swords. I would be honored to fight for you.',0),
(41735,'enUS','Clever $R, we fought as one, to defend the temple of the rising sun.$B$BA natural leader, you laid enemies low, I\'d much rather be your friend than foe!$B$BInto the ring, my hat I toss! Let me fight with you, new boss!',0),
(41736,'enUS','It was an honor to see ye in action, Grandmaster $n. I\'m more determined than ever to put an end to Lady Keletress and the Legion forces.$B$BI think we could take the vrykul\'s Storm Brew and make our own recipe, and use their own weapon against them.$B$BWill ye let me fight by your side?',0),
(41737,'enUS','Ahhh, it feels good to be back out of harm\'s way.$B$BNow dat I\'ve got a couple brews in me, I feel much better.$B$BI owe you my life, Grandmaster. You have my undying loyalty. Just say da word, and I will do whatever you ask of me.',0),
(41738,'enUS','<Sylara gazes out the door at the sky beyond. She seems deep in thought, as if thinking about some other, unfinished task. She heaves a small, barely audible sigh.>$B$B<Then, her steely eyes shift and lock on to you.>$B$BMy place is here.$B$BI fight for you.',0),
(41739,'enUS','We have been through quite a lot together, $n.$B$BWithout your help, I could not have avenged my master, nor found the courage to make her legendary brew.$B$BThanks to you, we should have plenty of Storm Brew to supply the entire temple.$B$BSpeaking of which, I feel there are many similarities between your fighting style and mine.$B$BWould you accept me as the newest member of your order?',0),
(41740,'enUS','Excellent choice, Farseer. $C from all over the world have much to learn from one another.',0),
(41741,'enUS','The scouting mission was more successful than we could have imagined, $n. Your troops were able to rescue Journeyman Goldmine, a... most unusual little $C.$B$BIn thanks, he has agreed to lend his skill to our cause.',0),
(41742,'enUS','The Windlord has commanded that I shall assist the Earthen Ring in your campaign against the Burning Legion.$B$BLord Thunderaan sees great potential in you, Farseer. As thanks for your help in securing his return as Windlord, he has granted you my services here in the mortal realm.$B$BWhen the time for battle approaches, the armies of Skywall will be at your back.',0),
(41743,'enUS','Your leadership during this time of crisis has been inspiring, Farseer $n. It was truly an honor to journey with you through Skywall.$B$BAlthough there are many matters here that require my attention, it would be an honor to fight at your side once again.$B$BShould you have need of my aid once again, I will be yours to command.',0),
(41744,'enUS','I have always respected you for your courage in battle, Farseer.$B$BHowever, the way you have championed the Earthen Ring and united the Elemental Lords... it has been an honor to behold. You truly are a great leader. The leader our order needs!$B$BThough the elements are united against the Burning Legion, our work is not yet done. If you should have need of my abilities, you need only ask.$B$BI live to serve the Earthen Ring!',0),
(41745,'enUS','The Firelord has commanded me to aid the mortals in their battle against the Burning Legion.$B$BMy master has decreed that demon invaders have no place upon this world. I live to destroy the enemies of my master.$B$BI will obey your commands as though they are the Firelord\'s himself. Who shall I destroy first?',0),
(41746,'enUS','It was an honor to fight at your side in Deepholm, Farseer. The way you lead our order with courage and determination inspires us all with hope.$B$BYet, I fear that the worst is still ahead of us. You should not bear this burden alone.$B$BGive me the honor of fighting alongside you once more, and I will not let you down.',0),
(41747,'enUS','<The deep, thundering words of Avalanchion rumble out slowly as he speaks>$B$BStonemother... send me to help Farseer...$B$BSay crush demons... protect $C.$B$B$B$BAvalanchion go with Farseer... make demons cry.',0),
(41748,'enUS','Rebuilding the council is our key to defeating the Legion, but it\'s a task that cannot be completed alone.$B$BYou could use someone at your side, someone who\'s familiar with the burden of leadership.$B$BI would be honored to serve as Second. Through your power and guidance, we can rebuild.',0),
(41749,'enUS','My sight fades, but I am glad that he rests.',0),
(41750,'enUS','Calydus no longer suffers under the cruel hand of Jagganoth, thanks to friend.$B$BCalydus has a choice who to follow, and he pledges loyalty to the new Overlord!$B$BThat is, if friend is willing to let Calydus help?',0),
(41751,'enUS','Your commitment to rebuilding the council is commendable. You could have left Shinfel to die and found a replacement, but you look out for your own.$B$BI followed blindly once before, trusting my mentor to look out for my best interests. Instead, he left me to lead a council that admonished my way of doing things.$B$BFor this, I will never be a follower. Instead, I choose to stand beside you. My power is yours to use as you see fit, if you wish to use it.',0),
(41752,'enUS','<Zinnin\'s gaze meets yours while standing in quiet contemplation. His stare remains steady as he places a fisted hand over his chest, making an unspoken oath.>',0),
(41753,'enUS','We have to stop meeting like this, $n. You\'ve saved me more times than I care to admit.$B$BIf you in turn ever need saving, I\'ll be there to return the favor.',0),
(41754,'enUS','So Ritssyn appointed you First of our council, did he?$B$BIt seems much has changed in the short time I\'ve been gone.$B$BThe Legion threat is greater than ever. I have witnessed their power firsthand, and know that we cannot defeat them as we are now.$B$BYou will unite us, $n, and together we will strip the Legion of their power!',0),
(41755,'enUS','I don\'t have to hide away in shame anymore, and I have you to thank for that.$B$BIt\'s a debt I doubt I\'ll ever be able to repay, but I\'d like to try.',0),
(41756,'enUS','We live to serve you, $n.$B$BIt would please us to do your bidding.',0),
(41759,'enUS','Ritssyn sent you, did he? I see my old mentor still refuses to do his own dirty work.$B$BBut of course, someone in his position can\'t be seen consorting with a purported member of the Argus Wake! What would the others think?$B$BAs much as I relish the idea of Ritssyn needing my help, I don\'t barter in kindness and favors, $n.$B$BMy currency is power and knowledge. If you have either, then it\'s possible we can come to an arrangement.',0),
(41760,'enUS','Fascinating.$B$BLet us hope the spell holds.',0),
(41762,'enUS','We should be safe to speak here for a moment.',0),
(41763,'enUS','This cannot be!',0),
(41764,'enUS','I am pleased you were able to place the first ward. We are one step closer to saving Ebonhorn.$B$BBut this mention of the Darkness is unsettling. It is a monster spoken of in our myths and folklore, tales told around campfires to spook the young.$B$BCould these stories be based in truth?',0),
(41767,'enUS','Shinfel cannot be broken at the hands of Mephistroth. Armed with her power and knowledge, the dreadlord would be able to mount a devastating attack against Dreadscar Rift.$B$BA ritual of summoning should be able to summon Shinfel to our side, but we\'ll need to create a powerful anchor.',0),
(41768,'enUS','We may have Shinfel in our possession, but her mind remains in the hands of her demon captors.$B$BWhat kind of ancient magic have they cursed her with? I\'ve never seen anything like it.',0),
(41769,'enUS','That\'s a name I thought I\'d never hear again.$B$BWe may have worked together in the past, but Ritssyn needs to know I\'m not the man I was before.$B$BMy priorities are Marl and this farm.',0),
(41770,'enUS','Farseer Nobundo has told me of your plan to save Azeroth. I fear I may be the only zephyr to share your desire.',0),
(41771,'enUS','At long last, the Windseeker shall return to to his rightful place as heir to the Throne of Four Winds. This is a glorious day for Skywall!',0),
(41772,'enUS','At last you have arrived, Farseer $n.$B$BIt seems our presence in the Firelands has not gone unnoticed.',0),
(41773,'enUS','The son of Rhyolith slain by mere mortals? What an ignominious death!$B$BYou have done well, $C. This pleases me greatly.',0),
(41775,'enUS','The Earthen Ring has come to offer help? This is unexpected... but welcome, nonetheless.',0),
(41776,'enUS','At long last, I have returned to Skywall thanks to the help of mortal hands. I owe you a great debt, Farseer.',0),
(41777,'enUS','The Twilight\'s Hammer will not soon recover from the damage we\'ve dealt to their numbers this day. It is an honor to battle at your side, Farseer $n.',0),
(41778,'enUS','Success! While their interior decoration sensibilities may differ significantly from those of Dalaran\'s architects, the demon hunters do make an efficient forge.$B$BYou keep the obliterum, $n. I have a feeling you\'ll be needing it eventually.',0),
(41780,'enUS','This looks like everything I need. Just give me a moment to mix it all together.',0),
(41781,'enUS','I can see all my goats have been accounted for.$B$BNow, let\'s see if we can do something about that curse.',0),
(41782,'enUS','Excellent! We will need this water to enter the Emerald Dream, but first we need to address the magical wards that protect the claws.',0),
(41783,'enUS','Yes, this should work!$B$BI hate rummaging through the pockets of the dead but we need them more than they do.$B$BNow, let\'s begin.',0),
(41784,'enUS','Killing a demon isn\'t always the answer. Sometimes, the solution is to control one, or two as the case may be.$B$BIf we can summon the sisters and bend their will to ours, it will deliver a devastating blow to Mephistroth\'s forces and rid Shinfel of her curse.',0),
(41785,'enUS','You\'re the council\'s new leader, aren\'t you? I could tell by your weapon. I bet you have an amazing story to tell about how you got it.$B$BMy name\'s Lulubelle, or Lulu for short. But, uh... I\'d appreciate if you didn\'t mention to anyone that you saw me, ok?',0),
(41787,'enUS','Thank you, $n.$B$BYour willingness to help an outcast will not be forgotten.',0),
(41788,'enUS','This writing is a bit difficult to decipher, but I think all the pertinent information is included.$B$BArmed with this confession, I should be able to prove my innocence and focus on more pressing matters.',0),
(41790,'enUS','You are powerful indeed, but strength alone will not impress me.',0),
(41791,'enUS','Well done, $n. You handled yourself with honor!$B$BYou\'ve done well so far, yet a single trial remains before I will give you my blessing.',0),
(41792,'enUS','You have passed every trial I\'ve placed before you and emerged victorious. You are worthy indeed of my brother\'s legacy, and have earned my blessing!$B$BGo, seek out the claws and claim them as your own.',0),
(41793,'enUS','With Lulubelle\'s assistance, we should be able to complete the summoning.',0),
(41795,'enUS','You did it, $n. The demon twins are under your control.$B$BI have not witnessed such power since the fall of Ragnaros.',0),
(41796,'enUS','And so the choice is made.',0),
(41797,'enUS','Excellent. These troops will be invaluable in our defense of the Broken Isles. Deploy them on missions, just as you would with our champions.',0),
(41798,'enUS','I\'m here to help build you an army, $n.',0),
(41799,'enUS','These shadows of the spirit realm grow stronger. I fear they may soon pierce the veil into our reality.$B$BI pray restoring the wards will set things right.',0),
(41800,'enUS','Huln battled the Necrodark?$B$BThere are so many tall tales attributed to Huln that I assumed those drogbar to be just another story. But it is clear they served the Darkness.$B$BA troubling discovery... but there is no time to dwell on it now.',0),
(41802,'enUS','Alright, let\'s see what ye brought me.$B$B<Brann examines the disc pieces.>$B$BWell look at this? There\'s a piece o\' somethin\' fel here. I betcha that\'s what was causin\' all those imps ta show up \'round here.$B$BI\'ll give it to ya to dispose of, or do whatever it is ye do with things like that.',0),
(41803,'enUS','It\'s good to see you again. If there\'s anything I can do to help you take the fight to the Legion, just let me know.',0),
(41804,'enUS','No need to thank me, just promise you won\'t accidentally blow anything up in the city; our repair bills are already astronomical.',0),
(41806,'enUS','Did the Archmage have anything of use?',0),
(41807,'enUS','Not good... not good at all.',0),
(41815,'enUS','Mayla charged ahead with Ebonhorn. Now they\'re cut off from the rest of us.$B$BThis is bad, $n.',0),
(41834,'enUS','That mask suits you.$B$BIn Suramar, it can be quite advantageous to be someone else for a time...',0),
(41840,'enUS','Perfect timing, $n. These shards will prove very useful in what I\'m about to do.',0),
(41841,'enUS','We failed! The ward is shattered.$B$BI sense the Darkness rising...',0),
(41849,'enUS','They made you Grandmaster, eh? Well, I was busy anyway!$B$BAnyway, I managed to escape from those fel-drinking dirt-kickers across the road, but our own are still in trouble.$B$BThose Legion worms are goin\' ta sacrifice the prisoners for their souls.$B$BWe\'ve got ta help them!',0),
(41850,'enUS','Good, ye did it. Sylara is worth ten well-trained monks.',0),
(41851,'enUS','<Sylara bows deeply.>$B$BWell fought.',0),
(41852,'enUS','Good work, Grandmaster!$B$BThat should be all of them.',0),
(41853,'enUS','Ahhh, tanks be to ya for freein\' me. I thot I was demon-food for sure.',0),
(41854,'enUS','This is fantastic news, $n!$B$BNot only have you disrupted the Legion\'s plans, but you\'ve saved the lives of numerous people.$B$BIn addition, you rescued three of the greatest monks we\'ve trained in recent history.$B$BThe order is indebted to you once again.',0),
(41863,'enUS','What of the others? Did they...?$B$BI see. They gave their lives for a worthy cause - the Warblades will change the tide of this war, mark my words.',0),
(41877,'enUS','I hope you have prepared yourself to enter the City. It is time.',0),
(41878,'enUS','Let\'s get started, shall we?',0),
(41882,'enUS','Well done, $n. If left unchecked, the whispers can turn even the best of friends against one another.',0),
(41884,'enUS','The spirits hold many truths, $n.$B$BWalking in their footsteps may reveal the locations of Ebonhorn\'s wards.',0),
(41888,'enUS','I did not think that I would live to see the day when the four great Elemental Lords would unite with the mortal races of Azeroth.$B$BYou have done what no other Farseer has done in the history of the Earthen Ring.$B$BThis is truly a day that will be remembered for generations!',0),
(41889,'enUS','Is there anything we can\'t do? I\'m starting to think not!$B$BI\'ll make sure this barding gets to Mei. You hold on to the pattern and maybe you can make some profit with it.',0),
(41890,'enUS','He is still alive, but the rest remains to be seen. For your sake, let us pray that he is unharmed.',0),
(41893,'enUS','My sight fades, but I am glad that he rests.',0),
(41897,'enUS','If The Master is not stopped, the Twilight\'s Hammer will have all the power they need to conquer Deepholm and enslave the elements!$B$BWe must not allow that to happen.',0),
(41898,'enUS','The servants of Therazane are free and the dark rituals of subjugation have been halted... for now.',0),
(41899,'enUS','The captives have been set free, but there is still much more to be done if we are to dismantle the Twilight\'s Hammer cult...',0),
(41900,'enUS','It is good to see you safely back, Farseer. With Therazane\'s allegiance, we now have three of the Elemental Lords united to our cause.$B$BHowever, one still remains...',0),
(41901,'enUS','The Windlord has pledged to aid The Earthen Ring in the war against the Burning Legion?$B$BThis is fortuitous news indeed!$B$BStill, there is little time for celebration, much remains to be accomplished.',0),
(41905,'enUS','Your champion moved swiftly, $n! This report clearly indicates that Tian Monastery is under attack!',0),
(41907,'enUS','Ah, yes yes yes! High Elder Cloudfall was right to send you to me.',0),
(41909,'enUS','Excellent. It will be extremely dangerous to infiltrate the Gates, but with this information, we will know exactly the enemy\'s location and numbers.',0),
(41910,'enUS','This water is filtered from only the freshest fallen snow every winter, and is a vital ingredient to our brew!',0),
(41911,'enUS','Mmmm, just smell those hops! This will be a good batch, I just know it.',0),
(41915,'enUS','Well well, looks like that old fool finally met his match?$B$BIt looks like the Promenade is in need of a new jeweler, and I think I have learned all I could from my former master.$B$BHere is something for your efforts.',0),
(41916,'enUS','Our strength grows and our enemies wane. We will win this fight, $n!',0),
(41918,'enUS','So, Xavius is behind this. A thousand deaths isn\'t enough of a punishment for that defiler!$B$BBut, you have returned with the claws, that is not an accomplishment that even I could have performed.$B$BYou are truly the hero we need to face the Legion.',0),
(41919,'enUS','<Valeera glances in your direction.>$B$BAny luck?',0),
(41920,'enUS','Val\'zuun actually kept his end of the bargain... I\'m impressed.',0),
(41921,'enUS','It was a ruse?!',0),
(41922,'enUS','He\'s lying again, I know it... but he might be our only option.',0),
(41924,'enUS','I knew you\'d succeed, $n. I\'m glad you\'re on our side.',0),
(41934,'enUS','I see that you have successfully awakened Emberscar, and that it has been well-fed.$B$BPerhaps you are stronger than I first thought...',0),
(41945,'enUS','Most excellent, Grandmaster! The mission was a success. Our new teacher, Recruiter Tianji, is getting situated as we speak.',0),
(41946,'enUS','Excellent. These troops will be invaluable in our defense of the Broken Isles. Deploy them on missions, just as you would with our champions.',0),
(41957,'enUS','Thank you for arriving in such haste, Brother.',0),
(41966,'enUS','I... I owe you my life, brother, but that look on your face tells me you\'re here for something else.$B$B<You tell Barrem about his mentioning of T\'uure in his sleep.>$B$BI must have been dreaming of Alora, she was my cell mate in that accursed world the demons took me to. She told me she saw the crystal but never said much else.$B$BI just hope she is still alive.',0),
(41967,'enUS','I felt my soul being ripped from my body. If you hadn\'t come when you did... I don\'t even want to think about it!$B$BIs there anything I can do to repay you? I owe you my life after all.$B$B<You mention to her Barrem\'s story.>$B$BBarrem still lives too? Oh thank the light! Yes, I\'ll gladly tell you everything I know.',0),
(41989,'enUS','Thank you. Now our work can begin.',0),
(41993,'enUS','You seek a demon with a staff of crystal? The Eredar that calls itself Lady Calindris has one that matches your description perfectly.$B$BShe\'s MY prey though! I\'ve been chasing her minion all over the isles and I\'m not about to let this opportunity pass.$B$BI could use someone to watch my back though. If you help me out I\'d be willing to let you take this staff you seek. I don\'t care about her equipment, it\'s her soul that I\'m after.$B$BWell, what do you say?',0),
(42000,'enUS','I\'m glad yer coming. I\'ve been wanting to pursue this for some time now. With help from the Seers, I think it can be done!',0),
(42001,'enUS','So you seek Aluneth? A dangerous weapon, to be sure.$B$BLong ago the Kirin Tor entrusted the blue dragonflight with its safekeeping. It was locked away in the only place that could contain its rampant power - the Nexus Vault.$B$BI have not been there in some time, however. After the blue dragonflight was dissolved, the Nexus was all but abandoned. There is no knowing whether the Nexus Vault is still intact - or what may be waiting in the Nexus itself.',0),
(42002,'enUS','I trust the journey wasn\'t too long or hard.$B$BLet\'s go find our dead adventurer, eh?',0),
(42005,'enUS','I think I already have a lead on that island. Word around the tavern was a great warrior had broken into a vrykul king\'s tomb on an island in Stormheim.$B$BThat\'s got to be the one we\'re looking for!',0),
(42006,'enUS','This appears to be a communication device commonly utilized by the ethereals.$B$BPerhaps it could be the key to finding out who is behind the happenings at the Dragonshrine.',0),
(42011,'enUS','You have my gratitude for saving Azuregos, $n. I can rest easy knowing that the Nexus is under his care.$B$BAs for you, I can see you\'re full of surprises. Never in my time have I seen a $C who can control the chaotic energies of Aluneth. $B$BThank you for what you have done for me and my kind today. You are truly the hero we need to face the Legion.',0),
(42017,'enUS','I am heartened that your quest was a success, $n. We have been awaiting your return.',0),
(42031,'enUS','You were just with Naralex? What were the results of the sampling?',0),
(42032,'enUS','Our champions returned from Shaladrassil just moments ago, Archdruid. The journey was a great success!',0),
(42033,'enUS','I\'m glad you are here, $n, but if only we had arrived earlier! This place was in chaos when I arrived.$B$BThe survivors claim they were attacked by satyr, but how can this be? No satyrs have roamed these woods since ancient times.',0),
(42034,'enUS','The satyr have never been this bold, or powerful. They took us completely by surprise, and our magic could not withstand their attacks. Without you, I would not have survived.$B$BI have only one purpose now - to recover that idol.',0),
(42035,'enUS','Look what we dragged in.',0),
(42036,'enUS','The Idol... so relieved am I to see it in your hands, $n.$B$BWe will keep it here at the Dreamgrove for safekeeping.',0),
(42037,'enUS','Good, the druids have gathered. Even now, they should be flocking to Nordrassil to prepare for the ritual.',0),
(42038,'enUS','I have seen enough of the Nightmare to know that it is not an idle threat. Within its grasp, even the strongest become their own worst enemies.$B$BYou, however, have displayed courage and fortitude even in the face of this great danger. I feel faith that you will lead us to victory against our enemy.$B$B$n, I wish to pledge my loyalty in service of you and the druidic order',0),
(42039,'enUS','$n, I owe you my life. Your actions gave me a second chance, and it is a chance I have no intention of squandering.$B$BWith your help, we were able to recover the Idol of the Wild. Such a sacred relic would have been a devastating loss had it fallen into the wrong hands.$B$BNow, I will see this journey through to its end.$B$BLet me fight for you. If there is anyone who can defeat the Nightmare, I believe it is you.',0),
(42040,'enUS','Something isn\'t right here, $n. This isn\'t the Dream. Could Xavius\' creatures have invaded our sanctuary? How did they get past our protective wards?',0),
(42041,'enUS','Good, I already feel the Nightmare\'s power waning.',0),
(42042,'enUS','Yay, they\'re saved! Thank you!',0),
(42043,'enUS','Excellent work, $n. I knew that Elune\'s power could purify the nightmare\'s taint. Her blessing is strong here.',0),
(42044,'enUS','Today I grieve for a fallen ally, one who has wandered these forests for eons.$B$BHe can now be at peace, knowing he gave his life to protect this sacred place.',0),
(42045,'enUS','My grandfather, Malorne, the ancient god of the wilds himself... long have I wished for this day, only to find that he is in great peril.$B$BIf he is trapped in the Nightmare, then what hope remains for the rest of us?',0),
(42046,'enUS','Thank you for all of your heroic efforts, great $C. Without your help, we could not have recovered the Idol and spoken to Malorne himself.$B$BNow that we know he is trapped in the Nightmare, we can devise a plan.',0),
(42047,'enUS','I have served the wilds for as long as I can remember, mentoring young druids and watching them grow in knowledge and experience.$B$BThere are few who have ascended to the rank of archdruid, but I believe you can become one of our best.$B$BI would be honored to follow your leadership of the grove.',0),
(42048,'enUS','Oh, hi $n! My woodland friends just couldn\'t stop talking about you after you left, and it was they who convinced me to come find you here!$B$BA noble $C with your courage and kindness just doesn\'t come along every day.$B$BThis is going to be SO much fun, don\'t you think?',0),
(42049,'enUS','Excellent. These shards are positively surging with negative energy. Be careful when touching them, $n.',0),
(42050,'enUS','Well chosen. The others will aid me in defending here. We must hurry.',0),
(42051,'enUS','Do not be deceived, $n. What appears to be the mountains of Hyjal, is in fact an illusion created by our enemy.$B$BThis is a re-creation of the darkest nightmare in Malorne\'s mind. This is the War of the Ancients, a battle that occurred thousands of years ago.$B$BIt was during this war that Azeroth was first threatened by the Burning Legion, and the War in which Malorne and the Wild Gods fell.',0),
(42053,'enUS','You lead us to triumph today, $n.',0),
(42054,'enUS','<Malorne gazes directly at you. Radiant, soothing energy exudes outward from his body. Suddenly, you feel a serene sense of peace and gratitude envelop your entire being.>',0),
(42055,'enUS','$n, we elders of the Dreamgrove have spoken and all agree. We would like to see you take leadership of the Dreamgrove.$B$BToday, we grant you the title of Arch $C of the Dreamgrove, a nomination of the highest honor in our order.$B$BWith it, you now carry the responsibility of our order: to protect the wilds! Lead well, $n.',0),
(42056,'enUS','We have come a long way together, $n. At every step, your choices have led the Dreamgrove to victory.$B$BI would give my life to defend Azeroth, and I know you would do the same.$B$BGreat danger still faces us. $n, take my pledge. We must serve and protect the wilds!',0),
(42065,'enUS','So, the Mistress of Twilight was actually a dragon... I thought the brood of Sintharia had all been defeated.$B$BI wonder if Zeryxia was not the last of her kind...',0),
(42068,'enUS','It is good that you have arrived, Farseer $n. The Twilight\'s Hammer has built a formidable stronghold here in Deepholm.',0),
(42074,'enUS','It is T\'uure! I had thought it was lost to us forever!$B$BWhen I last saw this staff we were escaping from a small world called Niskara. The Legion came upon us unawares, we were only able to escape thanks to a few brave Vindicators who remained behind with T\'uure to stall their attack.$B$BI did not think it could be done, but you were able to recover T\'uure. You truly walk in the light, $n. You have my respect, and my thanks.',0),
(42079,'enUS','My little brother is about to turn over a new leaf, whether he likes it or not.',0),
(42081,'enUS','You\'re finished? Let\'s see it!$B$B<Deucus takes the conduit from you and places it against the wall.>$B$BNow that is a good looking decoction conduit. I\'m glad I upgraded its strength from that old hunk of junk I had before.$B$BYou might even say Svena did me a favor by destroying that old one.',0),
(42088,'enUS','And not a moment too soon. Our scouts report the Underking himself has come.',0),
(42096,'enUS','I\'ve watched you rise up the ranks for a long time, $n. With you leading our order, I know we are in good hands.$B$BCount me as one of your champions, Archdruid.',0),
(42097,'enUS','Our search of the archives recovered a tome that details the process of creating a demonic gateway. It has the power to access any demon world, assuming we know where to direct it.$B$BWe could use such a gateway to locate and retrieve the remaining council members.',0),
(42098,'enUS','You never disappoint, $n.$B$BThis otherwise forgotten soul will now serve a greater purpose.',0),
(42100,'enUS','Your troops have done well. Our soul shard supply is sufficient enough to create the anchor.',0),
(42102,'enUS','Our scouting efforts have hopefully paid off. I have a lead on a $C who might possess the skills we need to perform the summoning ritual.$B$BWe should follow up as soon as possible.',0),
(42103,'enUS','This should be more than enough blood to satiate the Bloodstone.',0),
(42104,'enUS','The Underking is coming. Best keep that weapon of yours handy in case this does not go well.',0),
(42107,'enUS','Glory is ours, indeed! The great worm cannot hide from us!',0),
(42110,'enUS','You\'re after the great worm? You must be very foolish or very brave$B$BI know these mountains inside and out. Help me avenge my village and I will help you find the foul beast.',0),
(42114,'enUS','I have seen you before, Farseer.$B$B<Lord Neptulon judges you silently for a moment before continuing.>$B$BI sense the potential for great power within you. We shall see if this prophecy holds true...',0),
(42120,'enUS','I am heartened at your successful quest. We have been waiting for you to return.',0),
(42125,'enUS','Friend was able to get the skull?$B$BYes, Calydus senses it! Keep its gaze turned away from Calydus, friend. I gladly work for you without compulsion.',0),
(42126,'enUS','Your champion did well! Archmage Omniara agreed to join us and is getting situated as we speak.',0),
(42127,'enUS','Well done. These troops will be invaluable in our fight against the Burning Legion. Deploy them on missions, just as you would with our champions.',0),
(42128,'enUS','Very good! Now, we\'re ready to begin.',0),
(42129,'enUS','Yes, this is it... the pendant of the keepers! Hooray! Vengeance is so fun!',0),
(42131,'enUS','The two of them are puppets of Kil\'jaeden and a bane on our existence. I am glad that you have their warglaives.$B$BThey will be that much easier to kill when we invade their world.$B$BI wonder, do you have a moment to discuss a rather urgent issue?',0),
(42132,'enUS','There is just one thing left to do.',0),
(42133,'enUS','These weapons will work well against Hakkar and his minions. I\'ll ensure that they are distributed to our allies.',0),
(42134,'enUS','It\'s my honor to be of service to the Unseen Path. I\'ll help in any way I can.',0),
(42137,'enUS','Your willingness to help is admirable, and it gives me insight into what kind of leader you will be.$B$BI know you mean to gather priests from all factions and lead them in a battle against the Burning Legion. It\'s an extraordinary task, but one that you will not have to embark on alone.',0),
(42138,'enUS','I have a good feelin\' about ya, $n. Dis terrible day really started to turn around when ya showed up.$B$BSome might call it luck, but I think it\'s fate. We were meant to cross paths.$B$BDis could be da beginnin\' a somethin\' great.',0),
(42139,'enUS','So, I guess I\'ll be hangin\' out with Vanessa here a lot? Don\'t you worry \'bout nothin\'.$B$BShe and I are gonna be besties.$B$BSay, you gotta moment?',0),
(42140,'enUS','Gold! The rogues, thieves, and cutthroats are gonna start rollin\' in.$B$B<Nikki looks over at Vanessa and says in a whisper.>$B$BMaybe we\'ll even get some unemployed Defias to sign up. Too soon?',0),
(42141,'enUS','Good, Mylra was successful in her mission! Our recruiting efforts have paid off.',0),
(42142,'enUS','Excellent. These troops will be invaluable in our defense of the Broken Isles. Deploy them on missions, just as you would with our champions.',0),
(42147,'enUS','The Lunastre family is well-connected. They will be of great help to us when the time comes.',0),
(42149,'enUS','You\'d better take those back to the Hall of the Guardian for safekeeping, $n.',0),
(42158,'enUS','The Temple of Storms is close by, so you should get there before that thieving vrykul.',0),
(42166,'enUS','They\'re using fel magic. I knew there was something off about them, but I never suspected this!',0),
(42168,'enUS','Yes, Felsoul Hold! Calydus knows where that is!$B$BCalydus can make a path that connects to one of the portals there!',0),
(42170,'enUS','The Dreamweavers thank you.',0),
(42171,'enUS','Thank you for uncovering the truth about the Empyrean Society, $n!',0),
(42175,'enUS','Good to see you here, $n. There is much to be done!',0),
(42184,'enUS','The Earthen Ring champions sent to Skywall have successfully returned to the class hall.$B$BThe plane of air is currently in a state of turmoil, however our champions identified a powerful elemental who may be willing to aid our cause.',0),
(42185,'enUS','Brann will hardly believe his ears when I tell him what happened. What an adventure!',0),
(42186,'enUS','Thank you for coming, Grandmaster.',0),
(42187,'enUS','Chen and Li Li are two of the greatest monks in recent history.$B$BAs long as they stay out of trouble, they will be great representatives of our order.',0),
(42188,'enUS','I hear you have been making good progress down among the Broken Isles. Good. We, too, have been busy here at the Maelstrom.$B$BThere are important matters that await us...',0),
(42191,'enUS','Excellent work, $n! I can see that the Order of the Broken Temple is in good hands.',0),
(42193,'enUS','What is it you seek? Are you here to pilfer heirlooms like the others?',0),
(42194,'enUS','Odyn truly guides your hand, $n.',0),
(42197,'enUS','Lord Neptulon has sent me to aid the Earthen Ring in the defense of Azeroth.$B$BI have been commanded to serve the Farseer of the Earthen Ring with the same loyalty I give to the Lord of Tides. I will fulfill this duty until the Burning Legion is driven from this world and the future of Azeroth is secured.$B$BI am yours to command, Farseer.',0),
(42198,'enUS','Uniting the elements won\'t be easy, Farseer $n. You\'ll be needin\' all the help you can get!$B$BAye, These are dark times indeed... but we\'ll face \'em t\'gether, don\'t you worry.$B$BOl\' Mylra has yer back, Farseer.$B$BNow, let\'s get a move on then! There ain\'t no time to waste!',0),
(42200,'enUS','The mission to Deepholm was a success. The champions of the Earthen Ring made contact with Therazane, but the situation there is worse than we feared...',0),
(42202,'enUS','You have my thanks, $n.',0),
(42204,'enUS','It is done! The armies of Ulduar are bound by oath to join us now that we\'re in possession of the Gjallerhorn!',0),
(42206,'enUS','I like you, $n. You don\'t hesitate to take action when necessary!',0),
(42208,'enUS','It seems that our mission to the Firelands was a success, Farseer. We have much to discuss.',0),
(42210,'enUS','It was very lucky that we were able to retrieve those scrolls. Number Nine Jia\'s help will be invaluable to our order.',0),
(42213,'enUS','<Archmage Khadgar has set aside a space here for the Tidestone of Golganneth, as well as the rest of the Pillars of Creation.>',0),
(42214,'enUS','Oh yes! There are some fine looking jewels here. Let\'s just scratch the goop off, and...',0),
(42222,'enUS','Ravandwyr speaks very highly of how you dealt with the Empyrean Society, $n.',0),
(42223,'enUS','You could not have arrived at a better time, $R.',0),
(42224,'enUS','<You recognize the relic from Thalyssra\'s vision.>',0),
(42225,'enUS','<As the magical barrier begins to fade, you hear the rustling of leaves and the clattering of mandibles just outside.>',0),
(42226,'enUS','Do you have any idea what you have done?!',0),
(42227,'enUS','We must move swiftly.',0),
(42228,'enUS','<Energy pulses around the ancient seed.>',0),
(42229,'enUS','Such a temporary home will serve us well.',0),
(42230,'enUS','<The seed sits perfectly atop the stand and sinks in with a satisfying click.>',0),
(42231,'enUS','My order guards a powerful secret. We are the keepers of the final resting place of the mighty Tyr!$B$BRecent intrusions have proven his tomb\'s location to be a secret no longer. We must protect the sacred relic stored there... the Silver Hand!',0),
(42233,'enUS','The Highmountain tribes thank you.',0),
(42234,'enUS','The valarjar thank you.',0),
(42238,'enUS','Yeah yeah, the new master sent you. I get it. I have to deal with my former master first.',0),
(42244,'enUS','<The advisor looks down at what you\'re offering her and then looks around nervously, straining to give you a rictus grin. She continues in hushed tones.>$B$BDo you know what you have here? You have kept the Alliance from getting their grubby little hands on some rather delicate information.$B$BI will see to it personally that this is safely filed away.',0),
(42271,'enUS','Of course they would attack now.$B$BThose withered devils couldn\'t have chosen a more effective time to strike. My brood already suffers.',0),
(42365,'enUS','Excellent, Archdruid. These will do nicely.',0),
(42366,'enUS','Kyrtos, you old fool! You should have known the risks...',0),
(42367,'enUS','With Arkethrax and his minions dealt with it should help prevent them from flanking Illidari Stand. Well done.',0),
(42368,'enUS','That should stall these demons for a time. We may need to return in the future to ensure they have not regrouped.',0),
(42369,'enUS','If you think the explosion was big on our side of the portal, you should see what the other side looks like. Ha!',0),
(42370,'enUS','And... it looks like we\'re out of time for today\'s wand practice. Go on, then. Off to your next class!',0),
(42371,'enUS','My hand is beginning to tire from taking so many notes. I think it\'s time we took a break.',0),
(42372,'enUS','Keep your voice down unless you feel like being felbat food.',0),
(42375,'enUS','Why? Why would demons, of all things, be this bad at summoning their own kind?',0),
(42377,'enUS','A terrible loss. You have the Spark he held, though, and I have another.$B$BWe must press on. I will mourn Galford another day.',0),
(42383,'enUS','Excellent. Stormcaller Mylra and Duke Hydraxis are worthy champions. We can trust them to carry out any task we ask of them.',0),
(42384,'enUS','I\'ve received word from our scouts, and just in time it seems. There are plenty of people out there who could use our help.',0),
(42385,'enUS','I don\'t know who sent you, but I sure hope you\'re here to help.',0),
(42386,'enUS','Whatever you did out there, it worked. The hounds\' attacks have slowed.$B$BLet\'s hope that the villagers can get some rest, and live to fight another day.',0),
(42387,'enUS','Thank you, $n. I think the children will be able to sleep better tonight knowing that those assassins aren\'t lurking just outside their door.',0),
(42388,'enUS','I\'m so glad we\'re able to help people once again. Your work in Bradensbrook just proves how much the Unseen Path is needed.$B$BSince you\'ve been away, we\'ve had reports pouring in from all over Azeroth. With our ranks a little low, I\'m not sure we\'ll be able to keep up.',0),
(42389,'enUS','It\'s been quite some time since I\'ve come across another from our order.$B$BIf you\'ve come to collect me, I\'m afraid that\'s not going to happen.',0),
(42390,'enUS','You\'re from the lodge on the hill, am I right? I\'ve heard of your order, a respectable group no doubt, but a bit dull for my tastes.',0),
(42391,'enUS','Thank you for securing Cora\'s release. She\'s still a bit skittish, but I think she\'ll recover in time.',0),
(42392,'enUS','Well, you\'ve got my attention, $n. Not many hunters have what it takes to survive a night in these unforgiving mountains.',0),
(42393,'enUS','It is so good to have Hilaire back at the lodge. Her dedication and skill will be useful in the times to come.',0),
(42394,'enUS','Whether they know it or not, the people of Azeroth have the Unseen Path to thank for their safety.',0),
(42395,'enUS','I fear that the Burning Legion is planning to invade Dalaran.$B$BI\'ve dispatched members of the Kirin Tor to spy on various demon strongholds, with hopes that they can uncover any plots involving the city.$B$BIn the meantime, Dalaran could benefit from the protection of the Unseen Path. I know its citizens will be safe with the Unseen Path watching over them.',0),
(42396,'enUS','<Phin grabs your shoulders and hops happily.>$B$BMlrglr! Grlrlrglrmg.',0),
(42397,'enUS','You traveled all this way to see Baron? It\'s been a long time since we\'ve had visitors.',0),
(42398,'enUS','I don\'t know what kind of bones you and Baron found in these fields, but he hasn\'t had this much energy since he was a pup!',0),
(42399,'enUS','Good work recruiting Huntsman Blake. His hound could be the key to tracking down Khadgar\'s mages.',0),
(42400,'enUS','Thank you for meeting me, $n.',0),
(42401,'enUS','The Houndmaster is an ancient and powerful demon who has attacked our world once before.$B$BHis return could have dire consequences for mages throughout Azeroth.',0),
(42402,'enUS','Our allies have all gathered here at the lodge and are waiting to be updated on the situation.',0),
(42403,'enUS','You\'re from the lodge up on the hill, aren\'t ya?',0),
(42404,'enUS','If we can help, we should help. Hakkar isn\'t welcome in our world, and he won\'t be allowed to stay.',0),
(42405,'enUS','With the faction leader\'s help and your leadership, Hakkar doesn\'t stand a chance.',0),
(42406,'enUS','The Houndmaster has done some interesting things with this breed of felhound.',0),
(42407,'enUS','This is unsettling news. If our weapons won\'t work against Hakkar\'s minions, how are we going to defeat him?$B$BWe should call in our allies and see what they can do to help.',0),
(42408,'enUS','This should do.',0),
(42409,'enUS','I\'ve been expecting you, $n. Ohn\'ahra\'s presence told me that change would be coming.$B$BThe Highmountain tribes have long been allies of the Unseen Path.$B$BMy ancestors welcomed Namuria and her hunters to our land, and together, they helped build the lodge you stand in today.$B$BI am honored to serve at your side.',0),
(42410,'enUS','An old threat has resurfaced, stronger than ever. Azeroth needs hunters like you who are willing to survive at all costs.$B$BAs the leader of the Unseen Path, many will look to you for guidance. Show them that they can survive.$B$BI will stand beside you, and together we will send a message that we can endure, even in the face of an enemy as great as the Burning Legion.',0),
(42411,'enUS','I knew it was only a matter of time before us scouts would be called home.$B$BMy post has been a quiet one over the years, without much to act on. Yet in recent times, I\'ve seen the clans abandon their traditions in favor of following a king who chose to side with the Legion.$B$BThe people I sought to protect, allied with my enemy. I will not let others find a similar fate.',0),
(42412,'enUS','You brought a tear to this old man\'s eye by bringing Baron back to life. I never thought I\'d miss his ear-piercing howls, but I did. It\'s a wonderful thing to see him working again.$B$BWe\'re happy to help wherever we\'re needed.',0),
(42413,'enUS','Ya did a fine job takin\' down that bird.$B$BMaybe I was wrong about you hunters up in that lodge. Clearly ya know what you\'re doin\'.$B$BI\'d be happy to hunt by your side again, as long as you\'re huntin\' big game!',0),
(42414,'enUS','I don\'t think Hemet himself could have taught me better, but I have to believe there\'s more to hunting than taking down big game.$B$BSticking with you, I think I\'ll be able to learn exactly what it means to be a true $C.$B$BHere\'s to you, and the many grand adventures that await us!',0),
(42415,'enUS','You faced Hakkar with more strength and courage than I have seen in quite some time.$B$BAs Emmarel said, our battle with the Legion has only just begun. You can count on the Farstriders to be there when you need us.',0),
(42416,'enUS','If it is true that Archmage Vargoth is exploring fel magic, I will be shocked! Still, we owe you our thanks in bringing this matter to our attention.',0),
(42418,'enUS','Have we met before? Your face seems a bit familiar.',0),
(42420,'enUS','The Court of Farondis thanks you.',0),
(42421,'enUS','The nightfallen thank you.',0),
(42422,'enUS','The wardens thank you.',0),
(42423,'enUS','Hmm. This appears to be Archmage Vargoth\'s notes on the Nightborne Soulstone. Supposedly the energy of captured souls stored within it can be channeled directly from the stone! If that\'s true, it is very powerful, indeed!',0),
(42424,'enUS','Good news! Your champion found Archmage Vargoth entering the Arcway Vaults in Suramar.',0),
(42425,'enUS','I can\'t believe it! I hoped it would work, but I couldn\'t be sure.$B$BYou recovered heirlooms passed down by my family for many generations.$B$BI thought them lost forever.',0),
(42428,'enUS','Rensar sent you? As much as I\'d like to help, whatever you need is going to have to wait. As you can see, we have bigger problems.$B$BActually, we could really use your help. If you could lend us your aid then I\'ll do all that I can to help you with whatever it is you\'re here for.$B$BWould this be acceptable?',0),
(42429,'enUS','Ah, your eyes gleam with newfound knowledge, $n.$B$BThat staff of yours has seen the passing of many mortal lifetimes. It can teach you a great many things, if you\'re willing to listen.$B$BAs for its memories... they may be unreliable. You may find a different reflection haunts the streets of Dalaran each day. I leave it to you to find them all.',0),
(42430,'enUS','I\'ve heard from Delandros about how you rescued the Ashen and protected the shrine.$B$BWe all owe you a great deal for your heroism, $n. And it seems that you were able to recover the Fangs as well!$B$BI suspect this war is far from over.',0),
(42432,'enUS','Finally, we are triumphant, $n! With Xavius\'s defeat, the Nightmare\'s presence will slowly recede from the Emerald Dream.$B$BThe tranquil realm of the sleepers is safe once again. Our druids will work on its restoration and recovery.$B$BThank you, Archdruid $n. Azeroth will see many more serene days and tranquil nights because of you.',0),
(42433,'enUS','Your champion has discovered some very powerful artifacts, $n!',0),
(42434,'enUS','Good; you found me, $n.',0),
(42435,'enUS','Good. Now we should be able to enter the Empyrean Society enclave and have a look around.',0),
(42436,'enUS','Our alliance with the Skyhorn is stronger than ever, thanks to your efforts.',0),
(42438,'enUS','Thank you, $n.$B$BMy heart weeps for those who we\'ve lost this day. The Legion will pay for this, I swear it!',0),
(42439,'enUS','<Delandros nods.>$B$BThank you, hero. Now that my people are safe we might be able to turn the tide of this battle.',0),
(42440,'enUS','What? Verstok fled with the Fangs? That fool, he\'s going to get himself killed!',0),
(42444,'enUS','Caw?$B$B<The ravenbear chieftain seems preoccupied with the gathering of reagents for some sort of ritual. Perhaps you could help him?>',0),
(42445,'enUS','Caw! Caw! $B$B<The ravenbear chieftain flaps his wings excitedly when he sees the reagents you\'ve brought.>',0),
(42446,'enUS','The Blackfeather chieftain bows respectfully to you. $B$BYou have helped ensure the survival of his tribe.',0),
(42447,'enUS','It seems that Nithogg wasn\'t interested in the ravenbears\' tribute.$B$BIt\'s probably a good idea to get out of here before he comes back...',0),
(42449,'enUS','The world of the living will forever revile us for the dark task that we begin this day...',0),
(42451,'enUS','Good to see you again, $n.',0),
(42452,'enUS','From the texts you found, it is clear that Ebonchill is in the hands of Balaadur. There is no way he would not claim such a powerful staff.$B$BThat is a problem, but not an impossible one. All we need to do is get access to Balaadur.',0),
(42454,'enUS','<Archmage Khadgar has set aside a space here for the Hammer of Khaz\'goroth, as well as the rest of the Pillars of Creation.>',0),
(42455,'enUS','Excellent! Honestly, I\'m surprised you mages no longer use Mana Gems. I found them terribly useful.$B$BAt any rate, these will make up for the lack of additional mages.',0),
(42476,'enUS','This is better than I hoped. A working ward prototype and the ritual notes as well!$B$BI\'m beginning to believe this is possible!',0),
(42477,'enUS','Our order suffered a great loss that day. It is a shame we chose to hide it instead of study it.$B$BYou have another critical element to the ritual, and we are one step closer.',0),
(42479,'enUS','Your ability continues to astound me! Balaadur lies dead in his own realm, and you now wield Ebonchill. I look forward to seeing what you will do next.',0),
(42483,'enUS','<A note from the goblins is left behind, along with an old magnifying glass>$B$BI wish I coulda been there to see the look on your face, but Raz and I got bigger fish to fry!$B$BThanks for the trophies and meat. I\'m sure they\'ll fetch a nice sum on the black market, along with all the goodies we got from those stupid tauren! I\'m sure they won\'t be needing them any more!$B$BSo long sucker!',0),
(42484,'enUS','Well done, Deathlord. One of the Horde\'s greatest generals in life now serves you in undeath as your first horseman!',0),
(42486,'enUS','Oh my sweet little Korine! Thank you, thank you!',0),
(42487,'enUS','Vanthir is a very pleasant fellow.',0),
(42488,'enUS','How lucky we are that it could be recovered... thank you.',0),
(42489,'enUS','This is a comfort beyond words.',0),
(42490,'enUS','Thank you. It is one thing I no longer need to think about.',0),
(42491,'enUS','Excellent! I will study this immediately.',0),
(42493,'enUS','It is true, then. Archmage Vargoth has been corrupted by the legion.',0),
(42494,'enUS','Good job, $n.',0),
(42504,'enUS','Every second I held those blades was torture. They\'re all yours.',0),
(42508,'enUS','I\'ll keep them busy outside while you head in.',0),
(42510,'enUS','We must prepare. There is much to do.',0),
(42512,'enUS','The village. It... it is just... gone. They told me what happened to Riverbend but I figured that was an exaggeration.',0),
(42516,'enUS','Good. I see you have grown in power.',0),
(42517,'enUS','So I take it things went well then?$B$BA ritual of that magnitude requires a bit of recovery time. You cannot expect to perform it more than once a day.',0),
(42519,'enUS','Excellent. Emmarel Shadewarden and Loren Stormhoof are worthy champions. We can trust them to carry out any task we ask of them.',0),
(42520,'enUS','The loss of Archmage Vargoth from our order is terrible to hear, $n. These are indeed dark times.',0),
(42521,'enUS','I hope you are able to put Millhouse\'s determination to good use!',0),
(42522,'enUS','Ready, $n?',0),
(42523,'enUS','Good, your champions were successful with their mission! We may be seeing some new faces around here soon.',0),
(42524,'enUS','Excellent. These troops will be invaluable in our defense of the Broken Isles. Deploy them on missions, just as you would with our champions.',0),
(42525,'enUS','The scouting mission was more successful than we could have imagined, $n. Your troops were able to rescue Survivalist Bahn, a cunning strategist.$B$BIn thanks, he has agreed to lend his skill to our cause.',0),
(42526,'enUS','Excellent choice, $n. Survivalist Bahn has made the lodge his home, so just speak to him when you want to make upgrades.',0),
(42533,'enUS','For what purpose do you intrude upon my kingdom, $C? Speak quickly, for I have little patience...',0),
(42534,'enUS','Soon the heads of my enemies shall line the walls of my kingdom! These shall be the first of many.$B$BNot even Sylvanas will dare to step foot upon the free kingdom of Stromgarde!',0),
(42535,'enUS','You have done my kingdom a service, $C. Stromgarde will not forget the service you have done us this day.',0),
(42536,'enUS','We have tarried here long enough, Deathlord. The time has come to open the tomb and raise our champion.',0),
(42537,'enUS','Today, a great king has risen from the dead to once more take up the sword in the name of liberty.$B$BIt will be an honor to fight at his side against the legions of terror.',0),
(42567,'enUS','$n? Is that you, my friend?',0),
(42568,'enUS','If you\'re with me, drench your blades with poison now. This is going to get bloody.',0),
(42583,'enUS','Good. I know Zen\'tabra and Naralex, and they will serve the Dreamgrove bravely.',0),
(42584,'enUS','Excellent, $n. Zen\'tabra has done well.',0),
(42585,'enUS','Well done. I knew that Sister Lilith would come through for us.',0),
(42586,'enUS','Not only was the mission a success, but our champions recovered an inscribed leaf of ancient knowledge. These may be of great interest to Leafbeard the Storied, the Ancient of Lore who resides to the north.',0),
(42588,'enUS','Well done! I see that Leafbeard\'s advice has already been useful.',0),
(42590,'enUS','Your kindness will not be forgotten. You are a friend to my family, $n.',0),
(42593,'enUS','The matron mother?$B$B<The archmage\'s face goes red as he chokes out a cough and looks around surreptitiously.>$B$BYes, of course. Anything for Malevolence.',0),
(42594,'enUS','I\'ll make sure to give the grimoire to Malevolence so that she can unravel its mysteries.$B$BMeanwhile, we have some Black Temple scouting to conduct.',0),
(42596,'enUS','Thank you, friend to Highmountain.',0),
(42597,'enUS','It is as I predicted. You continue to grow in power and prove your worth.$B$BThe time has come for you to take command of my armies, $n.',0),
(42598,'enUS','You are ready to command your forces. Let us begin!',0),
(42601,'enUS','Excellent choice, $n. Archivist Melinda will remain within Dreadscar Rift, so just speak to her when you want to upgrade more of the class hall.',0),
(42602,'enUS','The scouting mission was more successful than we could have imagined, $n. Your troops were able to rescue Archivist Melinda, a brilliant strategist.$B$BIn thanks, she has agreed to lend her skill to our cause.',0),
(42603,'enUS','Ritssyn and Calydus were successful in getting information, though we don\'t know how reliable it is, considering how it was obtained.',0),
(42605,'enUS','Odyn\'s putting you in charge, eh? Count me in. I find it generally unwise to question the gods.',0),
(42606,'enUS','I will gladly follow you, $n. I\'ve seen what you\'re capable of and you have no fear of death.',0),
(42607,'enUS','Excellent. Hjalmar will have the valarjar whipped into shape in no time.',0),
(42608,'enUS','It says a lot that Ritssyn would give up his position and look to you for leadership. He must believe that you are the key to rebuilding the council.',0),
(42609,'enUS','We are well underway. Before long you will command an army to be reckoned with.',0),
(42610,'enUS','Excellent! With the runecaster\'s powers your armies will be even stronger!',0),
(42611,'enUS','A wise choice, $n.',0),
(42614,'enUS','I spent enough time in the afterlife. Point me at the enemy and I will end them!',0),
(42616,'enUS','I was sworn to protect Ulduar and if it wasn\'t for yer aid, I would\'ve failed that promise.$B$BYe can count on me!',0),
(42618,'enUS','You showed bravery in Ulduar, $n. I will fulfill my oath and answer the call of the Gjallarhorn.',0),
(42619,'enUS','I thank you for aiding me, $n. I will gladly fight along your side in Odyn\'s army.',0),
(42622,'enUS','Nice! Got \'em! Feel free to play the drums, but leave them down here, will you? You\'re alright by me, $n.',0),
(42627,'enUS','Every second I held those blades again was torture. They\'re all yours.',0),
(42630,'enUS','That was some nice work you did there, $n. Thanks for the assist.',0),
(42634,'enUS','Who would have thought he would be working with us?$B$BWe are now one step closer to taking the fight directly to the Burning Legion on their own worlds.',0),
(42635,'enUS','Excellent! Luckily I brought a copy of the vrykul cipher that the League procured from Northrend.$B$BI\'ll get to work on this straightforth! Let us hope the dialects are not too dissimilar.',0),
(42639,'enUS','You have the amulet! Most excellent!$B$BOf course, that probably won\'t help you with the pirates that are already mad as hatters, but small victories, eh chap?',0),
(42640,'enUS','Well that was most noble of you to save these ancient relics from a water-logged fate.$B$BI will be sure that the Explorer\'s League puts these to good use!',0),
(42641,'enUS','Oh, the stake didn\'t work you say? My apologies, I must\'ve had my immortal evil undead mixed up.$B$BYou\'re all in one piece though, and the evil has seen its end. Hopefully, at least.$B$BVampyr can die, can\'t they?',0),
(42645,'enUS','Good riddance to bad rubbish, I say. $B$BThose louts were ne\'er-do-wells before they went crazy. Just imagine what they would do if we let them run rampant!$B$BCheers to your bravery, sir.',0),
(42650,'enUS','I can feel it. My soul is my own again!',0),
(42651,'enUS','Jorhuttam! We must track the great worm at once. It will surely be a great battle.',0),
(42653,'enUS','I am encouraged that we have come to an understanding. I admired Altruis when he opposed the direction Illidan was taking all those years ago. While the annihilation of the Burning Legion is of paramount importance, in the process, we must not become that which we hope to destroy.$B$BIf you would have me as a champion, I will bring all of my knowledge to bear on the task at hand. With time, I believe that we might even come to trust each other.',0),
(42654,'enUS','A little bit of oak can go a long way when making ammo.',0),
(42655,'enUS','This looks like more than enough ore to craft weapons and ammo for our allies.',0),
(42656,'enUS','Halduron\'s blacksmith does fine work, but these weapons still need to be enchanted before they will work against Hakkar\'s hounds.',0),
(42657,'enUS','The Sentinels told me you would be coming.$B$BI apologize for the state of my home. I\'ve been having some trouble with unwanted guests, recently.',0),
(42658,'enUS','I\'d get a lot more work done if I could convince you to stay, but I know you have pressing matters elsewhere.',0),
(42659,'enUS','You have no idea how relieved I am to see you!',0),
(42660,'enUS','Once this heart is devoured, the Bloodstone will be strong enough to control the eredar sisters.',0),
(42662,'enUS','The blue dragonflight has always represented magic on Azeroth, and it is fitting that we work together against the Burning Legion now more than ever. I would be honored to fight for you as your champion in these dark times.',0),
(42663,'enUS','Archmage Kalec and Archmage Modera are two of the greatest mages in Azeroth\'s present and past. They will be exemplary representatives of our order.',0),
(42664,'enUS','I have always admired Illidan\'s singular vision. After all, the annihilation of the Burning Legion is of paramount importance. Nothing else matters. Nothing else can be allowed to stand in our way.$B$BYou will take me as your champion. In return, I will bring all of my knowledge and power to bear on the task at hand. In time, we will destroy all of our enemies... perhaps even Akama as well?',0),
(42665,'enUS','Up until now, the Illidari have been a fairly exclusive club. Demon hunters only. But, as you have so clearly demonstrated, my dear, if we are to move forward trusting one-another, then bringing Akama in is an important step.$B$BIt gives one hope.$B$BAnd, of course, making Kor\'vas one of your champions is the obvious choice. No one fights as well as she does.$B$BWhat\'s that?',0),
(42666,'enUS','Commander. I am glad to see that Asha was able to find you so quickly.$B$BThere is something important that you must attend to as soon as possible.',0),
(42669,'enUS','And now we know that Caria and Varedis are hiding away on the demon world known as Niskara.$B$BTime to finish this.',0),
(42670,'enUS','You have selected your first two champions. There are great things ahead of us, $n.',0),
(42671,'enUS','You have selected your first two champions. There are great things ahead of us, $n.',0),
(42673,'enUS','It\'s about time, you big lummox. For a while there, when you chose Asha Ravensong first, I started to doubt your sanity.$B$BNot that there\'s anything wrong with Asha. But, we both know who the better fighter is.$B$BRight?$B$BAnyway, of course, I\'d be honored to be your champion. I accept!',0),
(42677,'enUS','Well, at least we\'re going to have some fresh faces around here. If a broken\'s face can ever be called fresh, that is.$B$B<Kor\'vas smirks.>',0),
(42678,'enUS','We have it. Finally, we will be able to crack SI:7\'s coded letter.',0),
(42679,'enUS','Outstanding. These new Ashtongue will give you the flexibility you need to position troops wherever you see fit.',0),
(42680,'enUS','I must admit, I was not expecting that. Mathias Shaw taken prisoner by the Legion.$B$BThat, at least, explains all of the strange actions SI:7 has been taking lately. They have a dreadlord in charge of them.',0),
(42681,'enUS','They\'ve returned with him. It\'s Loramus, alright. But, he\'s trapped within the body of the dreadlord, Razelikh the Defiler!$B$BUntil we can make sure he doesn\'t pose a danger, I\'ve ordered him kept in one of our demon traps, below.',0),
(42682,'enUS','Do we really need all of these ingredients to contact the Master\'s soul?',0),
(42683,'enUS','That sounds like good news. He is already contributing to the cause and we are that much stronger for his help.$B$BStill, he is not fully in control of Razelikh. I think it best that we leave him in that trap until we can find him a new body. Don\'t you?$B$BAnd, if he proves to be too much of a problem, we can take \'other\' measures.',0),
(42684,'enUS','Surprisingly nice bit of work there. What I am hearing from our scouts is that the diversions are working perfectly.$B$BAs an added bonus, some of my suspicions about a particular item, which will prove useful in deciphering the SI:7 letter, have come to light in Stormheim.',0),
(42685,'enUS','It is good to see the Tirisgarde rise again, $n. While not everyone on the Council of Six agrees with me, I believe it is imperative for us to work together and defeat the Burning Legion once and for all!',0),
(42687,'enUS','It was very lucky that we found Chronicler Elrianne among the survivors. A well-respected archivist from the Kirin Tor, she also spent several months studying with the pandaren in their library in Tian Monastery.$B$BHer knowledge of ancient magic will be invaluable to our order.',0),
(42688,'enUS','Mlrgmlr! Rgmrlmg, grmlmglr lmrglmrg mrlgmlglr! Mlrgmlrg grmlgrl.',0),
(42689,'enUS','Faronaar is crawling with demons, some familiar, and some peculiar.',0),
(42690,'enUS','You honor me, $n. Of course I will serve as your champion and right-hand man. How could I refuse?$B$BWe have only just begun to change the way in which the Illidari operate, but already, you have made great strides. If we are to defeat the Burning Legion, it must be done in concert with everyone working together. Not just the Illidari standing alone.$B$BAnd not standing upon the smoking husk of a world that we have carelessly destroyed while trying to save it.',0),
(42691,'enUS','These entrails are rich with magic. They\'ll make excellent bait.',0),
(42692,'enUS','This Prince Farondis opposed Queen Azshara, so she got mad and blew everything up? That\'s awesome!$B$BHey Olothil, listen to this!',0),
(42693,'enUS','Perfect. Let\'s get this ritual started, shall we?',0),
(42694,'enUS','After over ten thousand years... to see mother and father again...$B$B<The elven mage is at a loss for words.>$B$BThank you, $n. Thank you.',0),
(42695,'enUS','An honor, $n. Of course I will serve as your champion and second-in-command. Could it have been any other way?$B$BWe have only just begun to move forward with the master\'s plan, but already, you have made great strides. If we are to defeat the Burning Legion, we must remain vigilant. Any other goal pales in comparison. The fate of everything hangs in the balance.$B$BAt the end of the day, we will stand victorious... no matter the cost!',0),
(42696,'enUS','Excellent work, $n! I can see that the Hall of the Guardian is in good hands.',0),
(42697,'enUS','You want me to be one of your champions?$B$B<Asha thoughtfully ponders your request a moment.>$B$BI accept, but on one condition. I want you to put me into field duty. While I am of use here on the Fel Hammer, my talents will be put to better use back on Azeroth.$B$BBeyond that, I trust that the plan is still to bring the Burning Legion to its knees?',0),
(42701,'enUS','What a rare honor. To be one of the Illidari, instead of a servant. I must admit, I was worried you wouldn\'t choose me as one of your champions.$B$BBut now you have, and I could just kiss you!$B$BIt never made any sense to me that all worlds should be purged in flame when there are so many delicious playthings to have fun with. Sargeras can be such a bore. Together, we will bring the Burning Legion to its knees and make them grovel in the dirt.',0),
(42702,'enUS','Your Hall here isn\'t too shabby, $n. I\'m sure there are lots of nifty secrets I can uncover here. I think I\'ll stay! Er, if you don\'t mind, of course.',0),
(42703,'enUS','Greetings, $n. The fires of Azeroth give us the power to see beyond ourselves.',0),
(42704,'enUS','<The Arcane Destroyer makes a high pitched, quizzical chirp and looks at you expectantly.>',0),
(42705,'enUS','I have been Archmage Vargoth\'s apprentice for far too long. Perhaps it is time for me to serve a new master. I would be honored if you would accept me as your champion, $n.',0),
(42706,'enUS','You and I have proven to be quite successful together. I\'d be happy to lend you my swords and spells against the Burning Legion anytime, $n.',0),
(42707,'enUS','Good -- you\'re back just in time! This will sustain Meryl while we search for his attacker.',0),
(42708,'enUS','Sylvanas will not be pleased with our actions, but we have more to worry about than offending the Dark Lady.',0),
(42719,'enUS','Oh! Clean water, so pure and magical! Thank you, hero!',0),
(42722,'enUS','You let them go? I\'m glad. I didn\'t like being in a cage either...',0),
(42728,'enUS','Mrrgml... mlrgmlrg. Mlrmglrg gmrlr!',0),
(42730,'enUS','No hard feelings, right? Business is business, baby, and business is good. I saw an opportunity and I took it, just like you.$B$BTo show my continued allegiance with your little organization, and as a gesture of goodwill, here\'s a little sample of the product. It\'s magic. Bottoms up!',0),
(42731,'enUS','Well, we did everything that she asked, but that wasn\'t enough for Sira Moonwarden.$B$BShe\'s asking for one more thing and she wants you to deal with it personally.',0),
(42732,'enUS','That stuff\'s hard to get and expensive. Impressive! I can\'t wait to see the results.$B$BReady for the next big task? No rest for the wicked.',0),
(42733,'enUS','Of course. Like all Legion constructs, the Fel Hammer is powered by souls. You have collected some of the most powerful souls around.$B$BThey should be enough to take us anywhere you want to go.',0),
(42734,'enUS','You have done the unimaginable, $n.We are all in your debt. I am proud to henceforth name you Archmage $n!',0),
(42735,'enUS','$n, is that you? This is a rather odd turn of events, don\'t you think?$B$BYou\'re free and now I am the prisoner.',0),
(42736,'enUS','I guess I underestimated you. Good. I like to learn and grow.$B$BUp to helping me out with one more little thing?',0),
(42737,'enUS','<The runestone begins to vibrate as you approach, rune in hand.>',0),
(42738,'enUS','<Ragnar\'s rune grows warm as you approach the runestone.>',0),
(42739,'enUS','<The rune and the runestone begin to glow and thrum with increased power.>',0),
(42740,'enUS','Ah, $n, you\'re up! I\'m relieved you made it out of that bloodbath alive. We lost so many good women and men down there...$B$B$B$BDamn the Horde for serving us up to the Legion!',0),
(42747,'enUS','I wish it did not have to come to this, truly.',0),
(42748,'enUS','The owlbeasts are... melting the dryads down and using their bones to create minions?! How... how could this even be?',0),
(42750,'enUS','I knew Leirana... she was one of Remulos\' favored, and kindhearted soul. If he has been captured as she believes, we have no time to mourn her passing.',0),
(42751,'enUS','My wounds are great, and my magic has been severely drained. I must recover from this enervation and return to the Dreamgrove.$B$BThe owlkin here are beyond saving by mortal hands, but perhaps Elune will one day shine her light upon them again.$B$BThank you, $n. May your path be blessed.',0),
(42752,'enUS','Finally, revenge against Cordana Felsong for all of the demon hunters whom she tempted into becoming Felsworn. Cyana, Tirathon, Glayvianna, Cailyn, Illysanna, and more.$B$BHer death has been a long time coming.$B$BThe Sargerite Keystone is once more in our possession. Now, to look to the future.',0),
(42753,'enUS','Finally, revenge against Cordana Felsong for all of the demon hunters whom she tempted into becoming Felsworn. Cyana, Tirathon, Glayvianna, Cailyn, Illysanna, and more.$B$BHer death has been a long time coming.$B$BThe Sargerite Keystone is once more in our possession. Now, to look to the future.',0),
(42754,'enUS','These will do nicely. We couldn\'t have asked for better.$B$BTell me, were the demons angry when you stole their precious parts?',0),
(42756,'enUS','Hah! Ha ha ha haaaa!$B$BI haven\'t felt this alive in YEARS!$B$BWhat you\'ve done, $n - not only to replenish my mana pools, but also to save my brood - will not be forgotten. The blues of Azsuna are ever in your debt.',0),
(42758,'enUS','Blimey! This one still has blood on it! Looks like he got a good bite on ye good, lad!',0),
(42762,'enUS','You seek my staff? You make me laugh!$BYou say you want my help and time?$BOkay then, wikket, hear this rhyme:$B$BThree new riddles will I ask,$BThree true answers are your task.$BProve you\'re smart, show you\'re worth it.$BAnswer the King and we\'ll unearth it!',0),
(42765,'enUS','I knew you\'d succeed, $n. I\'m honored to be at your service.',0),
(42766,'enUS','Them greenies were really curious about this smelly brew. It\'s powerful and smelly, I wonder if it\'s delicious too?',0),
(42767,'enUS','For this grain, the wikkets work real hard. They toil and struggle so they do not starve.$B$BWith these bags safe from the greenies, we should do the right thing and give them back.$B$BOkay, maybe we take a bit for ourselves, probably just one sack.',0),
(42768,'enUS','This splashie spirit core holds far more water than you might think. Enough to fill a big bowl or a small sink!$B$BI bet we can find some good use for it, like squeezing it out to make ookin\' excellent slerp!',0),
(42770,'enUS','These brave watchers require our aid. The Light may well ignore our prayers if we choose not to help our brethren.',0),
(42771,'enUS','Those poor souls are finally at peace. Thank you.',0),
(42772,'enUS','Good. Given time, the last few lingering souls will make their way home.',0),
(42773,'enUS','Tirion... could it be?',0),
(42774,'enUS','We\'re ready to depart when you are.',0),
(42775,'enUS','With the Sargerite Keystone in our hands, all that we have to do is prepare our forces and formulate an invasion plan.',0),
(42776,'enUS','You now have six champions, all of the Illidari and its forces, as well as a growing army of troops, all willing to make the ultimate sacrifice to bring down the Burning Legion.$B$BTime to prepare for the endgame.',0),
(42777,'enUS','You are choosing me as one of your champions?$B$B<Belath looks both surprised and pleased.>$B$BThis is a great distinction. I pledge myself to you again, $n. I will see to it that the enemies of the Illidari are dealt with in your name.',0),
(42782,'enUS','It\'s good to see you\'ve prepared yourself. You never know what you\'ll be facing out there.$B$BWe\'ve commissioned these rings for high-ranking members of the Alliance. May this one protect you in the battle to come.',0),
(42786,'enUS','These remains... this is horrible! They are turning dryads into mindless piles of ooze!',0),
(42787,'enUS','The Wardens should have cooperated with us much sooner than this. Still, we now know that we need to go find the Warden, Malace Shade, in Stormheim. She was the one entrusted with safeguarding the Sargerite Keystone.$B$BThat information, combined with some scouting I did on my own, will point you in the right direction.$B$BWe\'ll have the Keystone before you know it, $n.',0),
(42792,'enUS','They will not so easily dismiss the Dusk Lily now. Well done.',0),
(42800,'enUS','Of course I will serve as your champion. In for a copper in for a gold as they say.$B$BWe work well together. I bring out the best in you.',0),
(42801,'enUS','Belath is such a dear. Very thoughtful of him to arrange for some scouting.$B$BI do hope that not too many of the broken died to get us this information.$B$BIn any case, I now have the means and the perfect location within the Black Temple to make our grand entrance.',0),
(42802,'enUS','Ariana Fireheart?! I thought she died the first time we were here. How horrible that she\'s been down there all this time. But, what an amazing survivor!$B$BI remember her being an excellent trainer of demon hunters. We should put her talents to good use immediately.',0),
(42808,'enUS','Glad to hear that Ariana has recovered and is ready to train up our first new demon hunters.$B$BIt\'s been awhile since we had some fresh blood in our ranks.',0),
(42809,'enUS','We\'ve won the day! Caria and Varedis are no more, and we\'ve sent a clear message to the Burning Legion that they are vulnerable, even on their own worlds.$B$BIt\'s about time that we celebrated, but first...',0),
(42810,'enUS','Kil\'jaeden?! If that\'s not the gauntlet being thrown down, I don\'t know what is.$B$BCan we survive this, $n?',0),
(42811,'enUS','It is fitting that you are here.$B$BTime and again, you have fought to save our world. Now, I fear I must ask you to undertake an even greater act of service.',0),
(42812,'enUS','It is fitting that you are here.$B$BTime and again, you have fought to save our world. Now, I fear I must ask you to undertake an even greater act of service.',0),
(42814,'enUS','I am relieved you survived the Broken Shore when so many brave heroes were lost.$B$B<Danath hangs his head in a moment of silence.>$B$BI have been recalled from Honor Hold to aid the Alliance in its darkest hour. It is crucial that we learn from our mistakes.$B$BDo you have time to speak?',0),
(42815,'enUS','Welcome to the Halls of Valor, hero. Normally one must die to gain entrance, but times have changed.',0),
(42818,'enUS','It is good that you are here, Deathlord $n. The battle has already begun.',0),
(42821,'enUS','Soon, the Scarlet Crusade shall be overrun, Deathlord $n. This battle is nearly finished...',0),
(42823,'enUS','Our path is clear now, Deathlord. The time has come for us to offer Sally Whitemane the opportunity for redemption.',0),
(42824,'enUS','I have heard that the battle at Scarlet Monastery was a success, thanks to you.$B$BInitiate Whitemane has already begun her training as a $C. She shows much promise, and I have no doubt she will make a formidable horseman.',0),
(42828,'enUS','Hmm, yes. It is as I suspected.',0),
(42829,'enUS','Let me show you around, then.',0),
(42832,'enUS','You may want to cleanse your palate - we craft some strong flavors here!',0),
(42833,'enUS','Welcome, enjoying your tour?',0),
(42834,'enUS','Simple, no?',0),
(42835,'enUS','I will be certain to have a bottle of your arcwine prepared for you before you leave.',0),
(42836,'enUS','Much better. You have my thanks.',0),
(42837,'enUS','I will have these... ah... souvenirs... boxed for you.',0),
(42838,'enUS','Margaux... no!',0),
(42839,'enUS','Steel yourself, $n.$B$BMargaux\'s loss is regrettable, but not likely to be the last in this effort. Far from it, I fear.',0),
(42840,'enUS','Glad to know you understand the value of my services, partner.',0),
(42841,'enUS','Pleasure doing business with you.',0),
(42844,'enUS','Thank you for coming so quickly, Highlord.',0),
(42846,'enUS','Excellent. Both Lord Tyrosus and Lady Liadrin will serve proudly.',0),
(42847,'enUS','Maxwell Tyrosus has returned with important news. First, he did recover some survivors. They are recovering in the chapel now. Among them was Commander Ansela, a veteran $C and trainer.$B$BAs for the second, I will let Sir Tyrosus tell you himself.',0),
(42848,'enUS','Good. These squires will fight well.',0),
(42849,'enUS','Our mission was a success! Not only did we defeat the enemy, but we recruited Alamande Graythorn, a noted scholar from the Hearthglen archives.',0),
(42850,'enUS','Excellent. I knew Sir Graythorn would come through.',0),
(42851,'enUS','Highlord, I cannot thank you enough for both saving my life, and opening my eyes.$B$BIt is true I harbor great hatred against the Burning Legion, but you have reminded me that my choices define the path I take.$B$BI choose to live a path of righteousness, and I will follow your leadership and guidance, Highlord.',0),
(42852,'enUS','For years I have heard of your deeds, Highlord. Now that I have fought at your side, I can say the stories were true.$B$BAllow me to represent the Order of the Silver Hand as a champion of the light, $n. I will fight justly and bravely, and carry out your orders to the end.',0),
(42857,'enUS','Ah yes, this is the grell food supply. Perhaps I can use this to lure them away. Thank you.',0),
(42865,'enUS','I don\'t know if grell have mothers, but I hope that one never kissed his mother with his mouth.',0),
(42866,'enUS','I see that you have an urgent message for me. What is it?',0),
(42867,'enUS','Thank you for gathering everyone together.',0),
(42868,'enUS','This brew be excellent! Its taste be the best!$B$BYou\'ve proved yourself well, now I\'ll tell you where my staff rests.',0),
(42869,'enUS','I have exciting news to share with you, $n.',0),
(42872,'enUS','I look forward to joining the rest of our forces.',0),
(42881,'enUS','Good tidings, $n. I am told that you seek to stop the demon\'s reign of terror. Is this true?$B$BThe Legion has hunted our people across countless worlds... taken countless lives. With each of our paladins that falls the Light reels in pain.$B$BI have had enough - I will fight by your side.',0),
(42882,'enUS','The Scarlet Crusade will pay for their crimes. Soon the monastery shall fall, and with it so too does the Scarlet Crusade\'s last hope for survival.',0),
(42883,'enUS','Thank you, $n. You are welcome in our village anytime.',0),
(42884,'enUS','The grell trapped our young within the huts. They are no longer at risk, thanks to your generous efforts.',0),
(42885,'enUS','Good. This intel will prove vital to our operations.',0),
(42886,'enUS','Excellent, Highlord. You\'ve arrived.',0),
(42887,'enUS','Glorious.',0),
(42888,'enUS','No... we underestimated the enemy.',0),
(42889,'enUS','When you suddenly vanished from our awareness we thought the worst.$B$BI do not know what to make of your adventures... I will need time to process this tragedy.$B$BRegardless, I am glad you are back safe and sound.',0),
(42890,'enUS','Our mission to Faronaar was successful, no thanks to me.$B$BI let my anger get out of control, and I would have paid for it dearly were it not for you.$B$BThank you, Highlord.',0),
(42911,'enUS','That\'s it! This will do nicely. Please bring me as many of these as you can!',0),
(42914,'enUS','I have been fighting the Burning Legion for an eternity, $n. I would be honored to impart my wisdom to you as you lead the fight against them once again. I believe I have picked up a few tricks they will not expect!',0),
(42917,'enUS','You have saved my reputation, not to mention my life! Without your persistence, I would still be hanging above the Nexus yet, $n. I hope you will accept my everlasting gratitude.',0),
(42918,'enUS','Excellent! The Legion will rue the day they set their sights on Azeroth!',0),
(42919,'enUS','Our mission is clear, but what are our next steps?',0),
(42920,'enUS','We have won the day! Caria and Varedis are no more, and we have sent a clear message to the Burning Legion that they are vulnerable, even on their own worlds.$B$BIt is about time that we celebrated, but first...',0),
(42921,'enUS','Who would have thought he would be working with us?$B$BWe are now one step closer to taking the fight directly to the Burning Legion on their own worlds.',0),
(42928,'enUS','Thank you, $n.$B$BThese bandages will help heal our injured allies.',0),
(42929,'enUS','Thank you, $n.$B$BThese salmon will help nourish our tribe.',0),
(42930,'enUS','Thank you, $n.$B$BThis meat will help strengthen our troops.',0),
(42931,'enUS','The Doomhammer could be anywhere here. And that demon is still alive.',0),
(42932,'enUS','You there! What is this nonsense falling into my domain? Green fire raining from the Maelstrom! Are you surface dwellers behind this?$B$B<You explain everything to the Stonemother.>$B$BA missing artifact, hm? I have not seen it, but I know where to start. You help the Stonemother, yes, and she will help you.',0),
(42933,'enUS','Troggs. So tiresome. Pebbles for brains. Easily swayed by any cult, demon, or dragon that tries to interfere with my rule. Thank you for giving them a solid whomping.',0),
(42935,'enUS','Very very good, $C. The cavern is once more filled with their delightful wails.',0),
(42936,'enUS','How delightful! Aeosera is very pleased with you, $C. As am I.$B$BNow then, it\'s time to find that artifact of yours. Thanks to your efforts, the stone drakes will help us.',0),
(42937,'enUS','Oh ho ho ho! I heard the cavern shake from here, $n! It\'s good to rattle some stones and remind everyone who\'s the boss down here, I must say.$B$BNow about that hammer of yours. Your companions have come up empty, but I think you know where to go next, hm?',0),
(42940,'enUS','Your champions have done well. I think I should be able to get you into the Oculus now.',0),
(42954,'enUS','Books on magical illnesses? I might know where such a thing exists...',0),
(42955,'enUS','Power in its purest form. It is a lovely color, is it not? A fitting gift for a book of healing. Will you come out old one, now that you are no longer lost and forgotten?',0),
(42956,'enUS','Ari found just the book I needed! And she included a ring for you as well.',0),
(42957,'enUS','Ah, there the wikket is. Now, we see how well you can brew!',0),
(42959,'enUS','These are wonderful! I couldn\'t keep them for myself, of course. But... Can you hear the bees humming in the honey brew? They sing so sweetly... Oh! What a lovely idea! Thank you, little friends.',0),
(42966,'enUS','Excellent work.',0),
(42967,'enUS','Well done. That should halt the Legion attacks for a while.',0),
(42968,'enUS','Excellent. Our paladins will be well equipped for battle.',0),
(42970,'enUS','Magni\'s information was crucial to our efforts against the Legion. And it was good to see him again.$B$BNow to find that tome about the Pillars of Creation...',0),
(42971,'enUS','Now the other elements will truly fear you.',0),
(42974,'enUS','I thank you, $n. Without your help, one of Azeroth\'s mightiest guardians would have fallen into the hands of the Legion.$B$BYou have proven you are capable of leading my armies and defeating the Legion in their own territory.',0),
(42977,'enUS','What does the Earthen Ring want with an old servant of the Windseeker?',0),
(42978,'enUS','It\'s an honor, $n.',0),
(42982,'enUS','Well-earned, $n.',0),
(42983,'enUS','Excellent. You have exactly the right amount of Mistral Essence necessary to restore the pillar!',0),
(42984,'enUS','Yes, this is it! With this, I will be able to bind the element of air nicely. And, maybe do some impressive tricks at future festivities.',0),
(42985,'enUS','The pleasure is mine, $n.',0),
(42986,'enUS','Excellent work, Farseer. With events in his realm calmed, Windlord Thunderaan can focus his efforts on the war effort.',0),
(42987,'enUS','You have impressed me, $n. No simple feat.$B$BBe sure you continue to do so.',0),
(42988,'enUS','Impressive, truly impressive, Farseer! Everything I believed about your prowess has been proven true.$B$BYou have helped mend the rift caused by our enemies on the Broken Isles. We can rest easier, knowing what we have accomplished.',0),
(42989,'enUS','<Ma\'haat the Indomitable speaks with a low, rumbling voice>$B$BWhat... do you ask... of the earth?',0),
(42990,'enUS','Yes, this is exactly what we need! I can get to work at once!',0),
(42995,'enUS','<Ma\'haat the Indomitable guzzles the Blood of Sargeras down his throat as he speaks.>$B$BYesh... thish ish... just what I wanted. The egg ish... yoursh!',0),
(42996,'enUS','It is good to see you, Farseer. We have much to discuss!',0),
(42997,'enUS','Ah, good timing Farseer! I was hoping you would come by.',0),
(43002,'enUS','This blade could indeed be the key to resurrecting the Windseeker. However, it has been damaged and the elemental soul within has diminished in power.$B$BTime may very well be running out...',0),
(43003,'enUS','It\'s true! The Egg of Gaiath does exist... right before my very eyes!',0),
(43007,'enUS','It is good that Valeera was able to find you so quickly.$B$BThere is something important that you must immediately attend to.',0),
(43013,'enUS','I saw. Not the healthiest-lookin\' bunch, but I\'m sure they\'ll do in a pinch.$B$BRegardless, they\'ll be out with Vanessa and Garona, so what could go wrong?',0),
(43014,'enUS','Phew!$B$B<Nikki wipes her brow with a sense of relief.>$B$BWhatever we offered him, I\'m glad he was agreeable. I can tell you if he wasn\'t happy, I\'d be on the first flight off this rock for sure.',0),
(43015,'enUS','Things are already looking up. But, of course, in my experience, there is always some amount of bad to temper the good.',0),
(43054,'enUS','Wonderful, yes yes! These supplies will fill our storehouse for weeks to come. Thank you so much, Grandmaster.',0),
(43055,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(43056,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(43057,'enUS','Candy buckets like this are located in inns throughout the realms. Go ahead... take some!',0),
(43058,'enUS','Yes, these will do nicely. I\'ll get them salted and cured right away!',0),
(43060,'enUS','What a beautiful catch! I\'ve never seen fish this size! Thank you, Grand Master.',0),
(43061,'enUS','These bandages will help save many lives. Thank you.',0),
(43062,'enUS','Very impressive indeed, $n. I had no doubt that your form is still top notch.',0),
(43090,'enUS','I thank you, $n. That Hodir is gone is unfortunate, but things could have gone much worse and thanks to you Ulduar did not fall to the Legion today.',0),
(43100,'enUS','Gul\'dan says any of power may join. What if friend joined? Then when close take the Scepter and run!$B$BYes! Could work but must work hard to earn trust. Gul\'dan still needs Eye. Friend should help with that, earn more respect.',0),
(43106,'enUS','<As you offer the mana crystals, they blink out of your hand one by one.>',0),
(43151,'enUS','Thank you, $C. I\'ll make good use of this.',0),
(43153,'enUS','Yes, yes! Found the Eye! Helped Shadow Council! Now you go to ritual. Scepter will be there.$B$BTricky it will be friend, but Calydus have great faith in you!',0),
(43162,'enUS','My dear sister laid to rest,$BA tortured hero proves their best,$BToday I do lift this curse,$BAnd offer you a token, a small purse,$BMy other sisters are still gone,$BThere comes a day to right their wrong...',0),
(43179,'enUS','The kirin tor thank you.',0),
(43182,'enUS','I am relieved that this weapon of destruction is no longer in the hands of our enemies.',0),
(43184,'enUS','Very astute of you to have saved the best for last.$B$B<Allari smirks playfully.>$B$BIn all seriousness, I am deeply honored that you have chosen me, $n. Something tells me that the worst is yet to come. We must remain vigilant and bring the Burning Legion to an end.',0),
(43185,'enUS','Me? You want me to be one of your champions?$B$BYes, of course. A million times, yes! Just tell me where you want me to go, what you want me to do, and consider it done.',0),
(43186,'enUS','Your leadership has provided us with victory after victory. We gladly serve and will sacrifice everything in your name.$B$BAll hail, Slayer $n!',0),
(43249,'enUS','Now, what do you say you and I go to Val\'sharah and recover the most powerful jewel in existence?',0),
(43250,'enUS','Now that you are finally here, we can begin.$B$BThe elves here have somehow risen from the dead. They are deluded. They think that we are the Burning Legion and have come here to destroy Black Rook Hold.',0),
(43251,'enUS','A ledger? Wait, let me look.$B$B<Valeera reaches out and begins thumbing through the tome\'s pages.>$B$BThis is the key!',0),
(43252,'enUS','Thank you, $n. It means a great deal to me that you have given my ancient ancestors the peace they deserve.',0),
(43253,'enUS','The legend was true! I was right about my suspicions. I had heard about Ravencrest\'s almost perfect espionage team during the War of the Ancients. Now we know how they got their information.$B$BThe others will not believe it when we tell them. Of course, we could keep it to ourselves.$B$B<Valeera considers for a weighty moment.>$B$BNo. That is how the foolish and greedy lose their heads. We will spread the risk around to everyone.',0),
(43254,'enUS','Calydus not believe that worked! Ritual messed up, Shadow Council wiped out, and we not dead!$B$BOh, and you have Scepter! Big win for friend!',0),
(43259,'enUS','So you\'ve come to the crooked tree,$B$BTo name a foe you ask of me,$B$BBut listen first to my tragic tale,$B$BThen you will hear my sister\'s wail...',0),
(43261,'enUS','After all that, you want me as your champion?$B$B<Vanessa gives you a look of disbelief as she takes a moment before replying.>$B$BFine, but I do things my way. Agreed?',0),
(43262,'enUS','<Garona spins one of her razor-sharp blades around her fingers before deftly sheathing it at her waist.>$B$BAs long as there\'s a challenge to the kill, I\'m game for whatever little missions you have in mind.',0),
(43264,'enUS','Well done, Deathlord. Nazgrim and Thassarian are powerful champions. I am sure they will carry out their orders with deadly precision.',0),
(43265,'enUS','It appears that Nazgrim and Thassarian were successful in their mission. We have identified several promising candidates to aid us in the war against the Burning Legion.',0),
(43266,'enUS','Good work, Deathlord.$B$BThese ghouls will be invaluable in the war effort on the Broken Isles. Deploy them on missions just as you would your other champions.',0),
(43267,'enUS','Excellent work, Deathlord. The mission was a complete success.$B$BWith continued success in the field, the Burning Legion will surely be beaten back.',0),
(43268,'enUS','That was an excellent choice, Deathlord. Feel free to speak to Zubashi whenever you require further upgrades.',0),
(43270,'enUS','Excellent. Calia Menethil and High Priestess Ishanah are worthy champions. We can trust them to carry out any task we ask of them.',0),
(43271,'enUS','Well met, $n. It\'s an honor to serve at your side.$B$BI\'m happy to help in any way I can.',0),
(43272,'enUS','Your efforts to restore Saa\'ra have not gone unnoticed. As a humble servant of the Sha\'tar, I thank you.$B$BAs leader of the Aldor, it is my duty to safeguard all that is holy. This temple is a beacon of light that must be protected.$B$BYou can count me among your allies, willing to do whatever is necessary to destroy the Burning Legion.',0),
(43273,'enUS','Calia\'s mission was a success! We may be seeing some new faces around here soon.',0),
(43275,'enUS','Excellent. These troops will be invaluable in our defense of the Broken Isles. Deploy them on missions, just as you would with our champions.',0),
(43276,'enUS','The scouting mission was more successful than we could have imagined, $n.$B$BYour troops were able to rescue Archon Torias, a skilled researcher whose knowledge extends far beyond light and shadow.$B$BIn thanks, he has agreed to lend his expertise to our cause.',0),
(43277,'enUS','Excellent choice, $n. Archon Torias will continue to conduct his research in Netherlight Temple. Speak to him when you want to make additional upgrades.',0),
(43309,'enUS','Ahh, $n.$B$BSo good to see you once again. I trust you are ready to assist me with my campaign.',0),
(43310,'enUS','I love Lady Lunastre like a sister, but I am afraid my hands are tied.',0),
(43311,'enUS','Very well. Let us talk strategy.',0),
(43312,'enUS','He is unharmed! I owe you- and Ly\'leth- a great debt.',0),
(43313,'enUS','The city is buzzing with very interesting gossip, $n. Victory is that much closer.',0),
(43314,'enUS','<Thalyssra clutches the spellstone tightly for a moment.>$B$BHe brought this upon himself.$B$BI cannot linger in the past. Elisande is weaker without him, and we are one step closer to righting the wrongs inflicted upon the shal\'dorei.',0),
(43315,'enUS','It seemed as though you had that well in hand. I did not want to... interrupt.$B$BThat is one less power hoarding noble to worry about. Well done, $n.',0),
(43317,'enUS','This may not end as cleanly as I would have preferred.',0),
(43318,'enUS','We made great strides today. I will not forget this.',0),
(43319,'enUS','I will do my best to teach the way of the tiger, Grandmaster: to observe the enemy, and strike without hesitation. Soon, our initiates will be ready for battle.',0),
(43323,'enUS','A moment to reminisce on how far we have come. A day to look to the future and where we might go. A year of reflection on what it means to grow and a lifetime of memories made by those brave enough to seize it.',0),
(43331,'enUS','With the Sixtrigger brothers ended, you\'re finally able to collect your payment for services rendered.$B$BYou rummage through their most prized possessions and take your pick.',0),
(43334,'enUS','Welcome $C! You seek the weapons of the storm god Ra-den?$B$BMany have traveled here to Pandaria, but none have proven themselves worthy.',0),
(43335,'enUS','You built your campfire with ease, and put a perfect sear on that steak. I\'m impressed... and hungry.',0),
(43338,'enUS','That tiger is serious about this, isn\'t he?$B$BWhile you were here, others came to the Temple of the White Tiger to present their offerings to him. It looks like we\'re going to have some competition.',0),
(43341,'enUS','Excellent work, $n. We still have a long road ahead of us to rid this world of the Legion, but this brings us one step closer.',0),
(43349,'enUS','The Aegis of Aggramar is secure within the well-defended city of Dalaran.$B$BYour quest to drive back the Legion is one step closer to fruition.',0),
(43352,'enUS','You\'re becoming quite the dependable associate.',0),
(43359,'enUS','May the new powers of your weapon aid you in the times ahead.',0),
(43360,'enUS','Thank you. This place will never recover, but their madness need not harm others.',0),
(43361,'enUS','I will study these carefully. If we are fortunate, there will be answers.',0),
(43362,'enUS','I do not know how you obtained this, but I know it was not easy. Much stands against us, but you prevailed. Come. Let us restore the arcan\'dor.',0),
(43363,'enUS','A small tag on this present reads:$B$BHappy holidays, $n!',0),
(43364,'enUS','This present looks like it has been shaken a few times. The tag on it reads:$B$BTo a very special $R $C.',0),
(43365,'enUS','Thank you... it gives Brightwing much peace to know that life continues.',0),
(43368,'enUS','Your heroic efforts within the Emerald Dream were inspiring, $n. The Dream is safe for now, but it remains threatened as long as Xavius lives.$B$BI will lend you my aid. Together, let us keep Azeroth safe from those who would seek its destruction.',0),
(43370,'enUS','Here you go, $n. Take care of Hati and the Titanstrike and be safe in your adventures.',0),
(43371,'enUS','Hopefully our priests have a chance to rest before heading back into battle.',0),
(43372,'enUS','Gilner\'s hearing voices, is he? All that dabbling in the shadows has finally caught up to him.',0),
(43373,'enUS','It\'s a good thing ya showed up when you did.$B$BSo Velen wants to induce a vision? That\'s no easy task, but it\'s nothing Yalia and I can\'t handle.',0),
(43374,'enUS','Your quick thinking got me out of a terrible situation. Thank you, $n.',0),
(43375,'enUS','There\'s no tellin\' how many lives ya saved by recoverin\' these vials.',0),
(43376,'enUS','We\'ve found the ingredients we\'ll need for Velen\'s elixir.',0),
(43377,'enUS','<Saa\'ra\'s soothing voice fills your mind.>$B$BYour gift of Light is a welcome one, $C.',0),
(43378,'enUS','You\'ve returned, and just in time it would seem.$B$BYalia and Zabra have just finished crafting the elixir. This lens will allow you to see what I see when the vision begins.',0),
(43379,'enUS','We will not let this demon determine our fate. You have the power to change our future.$B$BI have seen the path to salvation, and you will lead us there.$B$BI must retire for now. The weight of this vision has taken its toll on my mind and body.',0),
(43380,'enUS','Born of Light, I fight for Light.',0),
(43381,'enUS','I owe you my life, and so much more.$B$BYou saw something in me worth saving, and allowed me to eventually believe that as well.$B$BLet me live my life with purpose, $n. Let me fight by your side.',0),
(43382,'enUS','You pulled my spirit from the Void, which is no easy feat. I cannot deny the part of me that would stay there forever, embraced by the shadows.$B$BThe Void is filled with many whispers, $n. The kind that should have us all worried.$B$BWe cannot afford to be separated by our beliefs. We must come together as priests of both Light and Shadow to face the Burning Legion together.',0),
(43383,'enUS','<The room begins to warm as the Light expands.>',0),
(43384,'enUS','These are in excellent condition! Thank you, $n.',0),
(43385,'enUS','Your efforts have provided us with the information we need to move forward.$B$BIt\'s been discovered that there are a few defectors among the Scarlet Onslaught.',0),
(43386,'enUS','Why are you here? Why bother saving me? I was prepared to die. I should pay for the terrible things I\'ve done...',0),
(43387,'enUS','The Light truly shines upon me, $n. Your presence has proven that.',0),
(43388,'enUS','The mercy you have shown brings tears to my eyes.',0),
(43389,'enUS','Is this the enemy we should welcome as an ally?',0),
(43390,'enUS','Alonsus sent you, did he? He\'s never shown much interest in us before.$B$BOf course, we\'ve never been ones to follow the Light, at least not in the way that most would want us to.$B$BWe embrace the Shadows as well, finding our faith in the balance between both extremes.',0),
(43391,'enUS','This is it! This is the journal that contains the spell to locate Natalie\'s spirit!',0),
(43392,'enUS','The lure of the Void is strong. There were times I thought I would be lost there forever.$B$BThank you for freeing me, $n.',0),
(43393,'enUS','The Forsaken will rejoice at Natalie Seline\'s return, and we will as well, knowing that the prophecy is being fulfilled.',0),
(43394,'enUS','Thank the Light, $C. I didn\'t want to give up hope.',0),
(43395,'enUS','I already heard of your heroism from Delas Moonfang. Thanks to you, many lives were saved.',0),
(43396,'enUS','The intelligence you have gathered is further proof that the prophecy cannot be ignored. The Legion\'s attack is imminent, and we will not survive without the paladins as our allies under the Light.',0),
(43397,'enUS','We will help defend Netherlight Temple and lay a trap for Balnazzar.',0),
(43398,'enUS','I knew from the moment we met in the quiet fields of Tirisfal that you would be the one to unite the priests.$B$BI\'d like to take credit for finding our leader, but I really think the truth of it is, you found us.$B$BOur time together has only just begun, $n.',0),
(43399,'enUS','This should be enough to make the necessary improvements to our defenses.',0),
(43400,'enUS','There\'s enough lumenstone here to craft armor and weapons for an army. Nice work, $n.',0),
(43401,'enUS','You fought well, High $C.',0),
(43402,'enUS','You are a leader worthy of our praise, High $C.',0),
(43403,'enUS','You have represented the Dreamgrove honorably, Archdruid. Your aid has helped many, and your victories will be spoken of for years to come.',0),
(43407,'enUS','May the new powers of your weapon serve you well.',0),
(43409,'enUS','With this new power, the Legion will fall!',0),
(43412,'enUS','May the new powers of your weapons serve you well.',0),
(43414,'enUS','With this new power, nothing shall stop us!',0),
(43415,'enUS','May this power aid you in the times ahead.',0),
(43418,'enUS','May this power aid you in the times ahead.',0),
(43420,'enUS','May the new powers of your weapon serve you well.',0),
(43422,'enUS','May your new weapons serve you well.',0),
(43423,'enUS','May the new powers of your weapon serve you well.',0),
(43424,'enUS','May this blessed power aid you in the times ahead.',0),
(43425,'enUS','May your new weapon serve you well.',0),
(43441,'enUS','It is decided then.',0),
(43461,'enUS','A moment to reminisce on how far we have come. A day to look to the future and where we might go. A year of reflection on what it means to grow and a lifetime of memories made by those brave enough to seize it.',0),
(43462,'enUS','Good riddance.',0),
(43468,'enUS','That ought to do it. I will make sure that The Wolf gets every drop.$B$BThank you, $n.',0),
(43469,'enUS','Well, now we know that our SI:7 friend is being held at Felsoul Hold in Suramar. Not sure why we didn\'t check there first.$B$BI trust that you already have a general plan for how to retrieve him? I know that I do. Perhaps we can put our heads together.',0),
(43470,'enUS','There, now that is much better. I would say that our garden is much more beautiful.',0),
(43471,'enUS','$n, you\'re here. You must have received my letter.',0),
(43472,'enUS','$n, you\'re here. You must have received my letter.',0),
(43473,'enUS','Want to earn a few quick coins? I need subjects to try one of my potions.$B$BThis one gets its unique aroma from frog eyes, frog hearts... wait a minute. Let me check the ingredient list here.$B$BMm-hmm, mm-hmm, OK, yeah.$B$BThis is pretty much just liquid frogs. Bottoms up!',0),
(43474,'enUS','Want to earn a few quick coins? I need subjects to try my newest potion.$B$BUnfortunately, I can\'t taste this one myself because it contains a few ingredients that I\'m allergic to. Drinking this would be incredibly toxic to me. In fact, as far as I\'m concerned, this is just one big bottle of poison.$B$BDrink up!',0),
(43475,'enUS','Want to earn a few quick coins? I need subjects to try this potion.$B$BI spent most of my development time focusing on the potion\'s effects, and not a lot on its... pleasantness. You may have to ignore the taste, smell, mouthfeel, and appearance.$B$BActually, I think I heard a few SOUNDS coming from this particular potion... you should ignore those, too.$B$BCheers!',0),
(43476,'enUS','Want to earn a few quick coins? I need a new subject to try one of my favorite potion recipes.$B$BI have to admit, the last few times I tried to make a potion like this, it didn\'t work out so well for the test subjects. In fact, this is why I have to pay people to drink my potions now.$B$BPlease enjoy.',0),
(43477,'enUS','Want to earn a few quick coins? I need test subjects to try my newest potion.$B$BI\'ve had several requests for vegetarian potions. You\'d be surprised how many potions have meat in them!$B$BTo compensate for the complete lack of carcasses in this potion, I\'ve had to make a few substitutions. I hope you like crushed-up bits of glass and rotten fish guts!$B$BFish aren\'t animals, right?',0),
(43478,'enUS','Want to earn a few quick coins? I need test subjects to drink a potion while I watch them.$B$BI\'ve had a lot of trouble getting this potion to perform its desired effect. Mostly it just seems to make people mad at me for making them drink it.$B$BGo on, then. Drink up.',0),
(43479,'enUS','A wise choice of targets indeed. The Uncrowned are fortunate to count you amongst our ranks, Mister $n.',0),
(43485,'enUS','That was a big distraction!',0),
(43486,'enUS','Aponi sent you? How is she? It is hard to keep in touch with friends in these times.',0),
(43487,'enUS','Yes, I believe this is it! Just look at it, $n. I will put this knowledge to good use.',0),
(43488,'enUS','Yes, this will do nicely.',0),
(43489,'enUS','<The book is written in Aponi\'s hand. What happened here?>',0),
(43490,'enUS','Thank the Light, Highlord. I didn\'t want to give up hope.',0),
(43491,'enUS','I already heard of your heroism from Aponi Brightmane, Highlord. Thanks to you, many lives were saved.',0),
(43492,'enUS','Highlord, I owe you my life and my thanks. You live by the Light, as my Sunwalkers believe.$B$BIt is an honor to fight by your side, and with your permission, I would like to continue fighting for the Order of the Silver Hand.',0),
(43493,'enUS','Incredible, Highlord. With the threat at Black Rook Hold contained, we can focus efforts on other areas.',0),
(43494,'enUS','Wonderful! These knights will serve the order well.',0),
(43496,'enUS','Senegos has generously offered us his assistance in the journey ahead.$B$BA truly kind soul.',0),
(43501,'enUS','Senegos has generously offered us his assistance in the journey ahead.$B$BA truly kind soul.',0),
(43502,'enUS','It would seem our tree is quite thirsty.',0),
(43503,'enUS','Senegos has generously offered us his assistance in the journey ahead.$B$BA truly kind soul.',0),
(43505,'enUS','Senegos has generously offered us his assistance in the journey ahead.$B$BA truly kind soul.',0),
(43506,'enUS','It is done. Let us prepare the Valarjar for glorious battle!',0),
(43508,'enUS','Hurry, $n. We must get him out of here before the demons raise the alarm.',0),
(43509,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Odyn\'s challenge?',0),
(43514,'enUS','Well done. We can use this to disable the magic protecting the Heart.',0),
(43517,'enUS','The ancient is at peace once more.$B$BMay his sacrifice not be in vain.',0),
(43518,'enUS','Fantastic! This will do quite nicely.',0),
(43519,'enUS','Well done! Everything went as planned.',0),
(43520,'enUS','That is... far more than we needed.$B$BThank you, $n.',0),
(43521,'enUS','Your bravery rivals that of my own kind.$B$BWell done.',0),
(43522,'enUS','That is all I can do for you, little one. If you seek more power, you must look elsewhere.',0),
(43523,'enUS','Let us speak with Thalrenus and discuss our plan of action.',0),
(43524,'enUS','That\'s the one! Oh, thank you, $n. Thank you!',0),
(43525,'enUS','Excellent. This will work quite well.',0),
(43526,'enUS','I\'m... so sorry, $n. I was so sure that would work...',0),
(43527,'enUS','It seems we have gained new allies. Let us figure out a plan of action.',0),
(43528,'enUS','We\'ve found a back entrance into the Nighthold that should provide some relief from the armies at the main gate.$B$B\'Some\' being key.',0),
(43530,'enUS','<Thalrenus\' eyes widen at the sight of the Millenia Tome.>$B$BIf Elisande has seen reason... perhaps there is still hope for the Guard after all.',0),
(43531,'enUS','<Kalec sifts through the pile of Nightshards.>$B$BYes, these are perfect! There\'s just one more thing we need.',0),
(43532,'enUS','Let us not waste another moment.',0),
(43533,'enUS','Your artifact\'s new form is even more fantastic than I imagined.$B$BPlease, take what remains of the Heart as a token of my gratitude for such a marvelous adventure - there is still a fair bit of power left inside it.',0),
(43534,'enUS','Yes, this is just what we need to complete our preparations. These must have been difficult to come by. Thank you, Highlord.',0),
(43535,'enUS','Thank you for bringing Delas with you, $n. I knew she could help us.',0),
(43539,'enUS','The Ebon Blade champions sent to the Realm of Shadows have successfully returned to Acherus.$B$BSalanar the Horseman will be arriving shortly to begin preparations for the dread steeds. You should meet with him when he arrives.',0),
(43540,'enUS','The Legion has plans to attack the priests\' center of command? It is critical that you discovered this information in time, Highlord.$B$BIt makes sense that the Legion would target Prophet Velen and his followers. We cannot allow Balnazzar to succeed.',0),
(43541,'enUS','I believe you have chosen well, Highlord. We will help defend Netherlight Temple and lay a trap for Balnazzar.$B$BThe priests of the Conclave are formidable allies. With our combined strength, we may just have a chance against Balnazzar.',0),
(43545,'enUS','Were you able to defeat Lord Ravencrest?',0),
(43546,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Emerald Nightmare?',0),
(43547,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Emerald Nightmare?',0),
(43548,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Emerald Nightmare?',0),
(43549,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Emerald Nightmare?',0),
(43551,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Darkheart Thicket?',0),
(43552,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Eye of Azshara',0),
(43553,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Maw of Souls?',0),
(43554,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Neltharion\'s Lair?',0),
(43556,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Vault of the Wardens?',0),
(43557,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Assault on the Violet Hold?',0),
(43558,'enUS','And so you return with the bindings in hand. The Firelord shall be very displeased to have lost these.',0),
(43560,'enUS','The bindings now belong to me. When the time comes, the Firelord shall be imprisoned as I once was. But that time is not now.$B$BYour reward is this, a small fragment of my power. Unleash it upon your blades, $R, and you shall have what you seek.',0),
(43562,'enUS','We must take drastic measures.',0),
(43563,'enUS','These will do nicely.',0),
(43564,'enUS','If my map of the arcways is accurate, that should be all of the outlets we need to worry about.',0),
(43565,'enUS','Excellent. With this, the chances of me teleporting you all to the bottom of the sea are much lower!',0),
(43567,'enUS','Behold. The redemption of the Nightfallen.',0),
(43568,'enUS','At last... we are free.',0),
(43569,'enUS','I am not hungry any more. I can think- I will live! Oh, Arluin...',0),
(43571,'enUS','Well done, Deathlord. The cords of this braid will be used in the fashioning of reins for our steeds.$B$BI assume Dargrul was more than willing to part with it, yes?$B$B<Salanar flashes an evil grin.>',0),
(43572,'enUS','At long last, the Nightmare Lash! Holding it in my hands, I can feel the truth of the legends.$B$BSuch power... such darkness... such... anguish!$B$BYes, this will do nicely.',0),
(43573,'enUS','The Ebon Blade\'s success on the battlefield has not gone unnoticed by the Burning Legion.$B$BAs we continue the war effort, we must be mindful of increased attention from the forces of Sargeras...',0),
(43574,'enUS','The legendary Maul of the Dead... it resonates with the hatred and despair of countless anguished souls. As a tool of misery, it is the embodiment of perfection.',0),
(43576,'enUS','Already my mind is sharper.',0),
(43577,'enUS','The Valarjar have captured the Legion\'s gateway at Felblaze Ingress.$B$BThe time has come to deliver a decisive blow to the enemy. We shall not wait for them to strike here!',0),
(43581,'enUS','Your next steps will be difficult, young one, and more dangerous than any threat you\'ve faced, but they must be taken.$B$BFor the good of Azeroth.',0),
(43582,'enUS','That was quite the spectacle, $n.$B$BSu\'esh will be a valuable ally in the days to come. I will keep an eye on her for the time being.',0),
(43585,'enUS','You and your armies have accomplished much. Odyn chose his commander well.',0),
(43586,'enUS','A glorious victory! It\'s unfortunate that Helya survived, but she will think twice about moving against us with you leading the armies of Skyhold.',0),
(43587,'enUS','<As you imbue the feed with the mana the structure stirs to life. Your skin tingles as the surrounding air becomes charged with arcane power.>',0),
(43588,'enUS','<As you imbue the feed with the mana the structure stirs to life. Your skin tingles as the surrounding air becomes charged with arcane power.>',0),
(43590,'enUS','<As you place the broken piece onto the pillar and begin infusing it with mana, arcane energy begins to repair the break. It slowly begins to turn as the leyline is activated.>',0),
(43591,'enUS','<As you insert the fragments back into the pillar the arcane energy begins repairing the cracks. You infuse the feed with ancient mana and the structure stirs to life.>',0),
(43592,'enUS','<As you imbue the feed with the mana the structure stirs to life. Your skin tingles as the surrounding air becomes charged with arcane power.>',0),
(43593,'enUS','<As you imbue the feed with the mana the structure stirs to life. Your skin tingles as the surrounding air becomes charged with arcane power.>',0),
(43594,'enUS','<As you imbue the feed with the mana the structure stirs to life. Your skin tingles as the surrounding air becomes charged with arcane power.>',0),
(43595,'enUS','I will see that these blades are returned where they belong.$B$BThe dead smile upon you, outsider.',0),
(43596,'enUS','With the dread ship sundered, the souls of the dead will know their judgement. $B$BOdyn will have his champions, and the Tideskorn will have their honor.',0),
(43604,'enUS','Very well then. Let it be done!',0),
(43643,'enUS','Thank you, Battlelord. The Valarjar will be even better equipped once I\'ve made my adjustments.$B$BIt has also inspired me to think of your weapon. The Blade Breaker. In my mind\'s eye the axe is called that.',0),
(43644,'enUS','Very good!$B$BIf you haven\'t been to this realm before, I have learned a trick or two to give you your \"Sea Legs,\" allowing you to breathe underwater for the duration of our mission here.$B$BNow, let\'s find out missing $C and the scepter she was looking for!',0),
(43645,'enUS','<You report your findings to Erunak, who listens distractedly while flipping through the journal you located.>$B$BSo... the naga have conscripted sea giants to their cause? This is disturbing.$B$BAdelee\'s journal confirms my fears. The naga have infiltrated the Abyssal Maw once again, and this time they have a powerful weapon with them: Sharas\'dal. Our task is clear.',0),
(43686,'enUS','I see now what I did not see before. My destiny was written long ago.$B$BThis burden has always been mine to bear.',0),
(43687,'enUS','It is done. I hope you\'re right about this, Highlord.',0),
(43697,'enUS','Thank you for leading us to victory. All hail, Highlord $n!',0),
(43698,'enUS','There\'s enough lumenstone here to craft armor and weapons for an army. Thank you, Highlord.',0),
(43699,'enUS','Thank you, Highlord. Too many dangers abound in these dark times. With heroes like you out there, we are all a little bit safer.',0),
(43700,'enUS','Victory is ours, Highlord.',0),
(43701,'enUS','I am sure you have many questions, Highlord $n. It was fate that our paths crossed that day on Niskara.$B$BI serve High Exarch Turalyon and Lady Alleria Windrunner. When the Legion turned its armies toward Azeroth, I was sent here to help protect it.$B$BHow I got to Niskara is a tale for another time, but had it not been for you, I would still be Balnazzar\'s prisoner.$B$BNow, I can fulfill my original mission. Let me fight for you. Together, we will drive back the Burning Legion!',0),
(43702,'enUS','This place remains deadly, but we can now press forward.',0),
(43705,'enUS','You have my thanks, and the gratitude of the Broken, hero. Many would have considered us an acceptable loss, yet you have shown us great compassion and kindness. An act that I - we - will not soon forget.$B$BNow we will return to the Vault of Lights and assist Velen as best we can.',0),
(43723,'enUS','I am honored beyond words, $n. I will gladly serve as your champion.$B$BPoint me in the right direction. I can sneak anywhere. Find out anything.',0),
(43724,'enUS','Shall we form an alliance, you and I? Of course, I dare not officially become one of the Uncrowned, let alone the Council of Shadows.$B$BI am the leader of SI:7 after all.$B$BBut, when you need my assistance or guidance, you need but ask. I will be there. We will work together through back channels to ensure that the Burning Legion is destroyed.',0),
(43726,'enUS','Hey, wow! It IS a book!$B$BI\'m always looking for my next good light novel. What\'s this one about? A $C who fights some stuff? Neat!$B$BHere, have some coins.',0),
(43749,'enUS','You are lovely. Just lovely. I\'ll get to work right away.$B$BKeep us in mind with any resources the Tirisgarde can spare. If you can keep the researchers busy, we should unfold everything there is to know about your weapon in no time.',0),
(43750,'enUS','Ah yes, the Gjallarhorn.',0),
(43785,'enUS','Highlord $n, for many years I sought to follow the footsteps of my father, Turalyon.$B$BIn you, I see an exemplary leader, one who can still teach me so much. In you, I see a champion rivaling my father himself.$B$BI would gladly lay down my life and fight for the Order of the Silver Hand.',0),
(43797,'enUS','With the paladins on our side, united under the Light, the prophecy is fulfilled.$B$BWe must now prepare. Balnazzar will attack, and we need to be ready.',0),
(43806,'enUS','Ah, $n, you\'re up! I\'m relieved you made it out of that bloodbath alive. We lost so many good women and men down there...$B$B$B$BDamn the Horde for serving us up to the Legion!',0),
(43808,'enUS','<The beacon glows as you infuse it with Ancient Mana.>',0),
(43809,'enUS','<The beacon glows as you infuse it with Ancient Mana.>',0),
(43810,'enUS','Any regret I had for these people vanished when they went under that shield.',0),
(43811,'enUS','<The beacon glows as you infuse it with Ancient Mana.>',0),
(43812,'enUS','Excellent. We will be able to defend our borders for now.',0),
(43813,'enUS','<The beacon glows as you infuse it with Ancient Mana.>',0),
(43829,'enUS','Why is Mathias Shaw stepping up the number of agents that he has in Horde territory?$B$BWe must keep a close and watchful eye on this situation.',0),
(43832,'enUS','You are as dependable as you are resourceful.',0),
(43841,'enUS','Arrr! Now that be what I like t\' hear.$B$BWhat do you think, Crackers... will a bunch o\' freebooters class up this crow\'s nest or scuttle th\' ship? I say it\'s a fair toss o\' th\' bones.',0),
(43851,'enUS','It is an honor to serve you, High $C.',0),
(43852,'enUS','Now that\'s more like it. Get them some holystone and put them t\' work scrubbin\' th\' deck.$B$BThat and a few black jacks o\' rum will put courage in their sails.',0),
(43877,'enUS','Excellent. I\'ll get back to you with the results as soon as I can.',0),
(43878,'enUS','Excellent. I\'ll get back to you with the results as soon as I can.',0),
(43879,'enUS','Excellent. I\'ll get back to you with the results as soon as I can.',0),
(43880,'enUS','Excellent. I\'ll get back to you with the results as soon as I can.',0),
(43881,'enUS','Excellent. I\'ll get back to you with the results as soon as I can.',0),
(43882,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43883,'enUS','Excellent. I\'ll get back to you with the results as soon as I can.',0),
(43884,'enUS','Excellent. I\'ll get back to you with the results as soon as I can.',0),
(43885,'enUS','On it, boss. Will get back to you soon!',0),
(43886,'enUS','Thank you. I\'ll get back to you with what I\'ve learned soon.',0),
(43887,'enUS','Very good. I\'ll get back to you with the results soon.',0),
(43888,'enUS','I will have results for you soon.',0),
(43889,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43890,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43891,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43892,'enUS','Feeling safe, stranger?',0),
(43893,'enUS','Feeling safe, stranger?',0),
(43894,'enUS','Feeling safe, stranger?',0),
(43895,'enUS','A simple exchange with complex results. That\'s the art of doing business.',0),
(43896,'enUS','A simple exchange with complex results. That\'s the art of doing business.',0),
(43897,'enUS','A simple exchange with complex results. That\'s the art of doing business.',0),
(43898,'enUS','We\'ve found a back entrance into the Nighthold that should provide some relief from the armies at the main gate.$B$B\'Some\' being key.',0),
(43899,'enUS','Excellent work, Deathlord. The missions for the Steeds of the Damned were successful. Salanar the Horseman now has the first set of necessary components for conjuring the steeds.',0),
(43902,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Emerald Nightmare?',0),
(43903,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Emerald Nightmare?',0),
(43904,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Emerald Nightmare?',0),
(43905,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Emerald Nightmare?',0),
(43906,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Emerald Nightmare?',0),
(43907,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Emerald Nightmare?',0),
(43908,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Emerald Nightmare?',0),
(43909,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Emerald Nightmare?',0),
(43910,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43911,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43912,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43913,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43914,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43915,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43916,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43917,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43918,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43919,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43920,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43921,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the The Nighthold?',0),
(43923,'enUS','Good work, $n.$B$BThese supplies are crucial to crafting the elixirs we will need for the upcoming battle.',0),
(43924,'enUS','Good work, $n.$B$BThese supplies are crucial to crafting the elixirs we will need for the upcoming battle.',0),
(43925,'enUS','Good work, $n.$B$BThese supplies are crucial to crafting the elixirs we will need for the upcoming battle.',0),
(43926,'enUS','The ships are leaving from the dock in Bladefist Bay.$B$BBefore you leave, prepare yourself. I have the feeling that this fight won\'t be an easy one.',0),
(43928,'enUS','With the Aggregates of Anguish procured, our work is nearly complete. Soon, the Steeds of the Damned will rise... and the Burning Legion will fall!',0),
(43929,'enUS','Greetings, $n.$B$BIt is my understanding that you have been one of the foremost scribes responsible for equipping our forces with Vantus runes. Do not think that your efforts as an artisan have gone unnoticed.$B$BWe noticed.$B$BI would like to present you with this technique. Now go, and use it to help us win this war.',0),
(43933,'enUS','Highlord, I am proud to begin the first steps of this new journey.$B$BThank you for taking me under your wing. I vow to follow the guiding principles - to act honorably, to uphold what is righteous, to fight against injustice, and to celebrate with my new brothers and sisters of the Silver Hand.$B$BUnder the Light, we stand as one!',0),
(43934,'enUS','Thank you, Highlord.',0),
(43935,'enUS','Excellent. You can begin as soon as you are ready.',0),
(43942,'enUS','Just what I\'ve been looking for! <King Mrgl Mrgl studies the artifact> Ah! Yes. But there must be more of these Timeworn Artifacts still on the shore. Any more you can bring back would be greatly appreciated!',0),
(43945,'enUS','Very well. Your allies have gathered here on the precipice - they will know how best to proceed.$B$BMay the winds be ever in your favor, Farseer.',0),
(43949,'enUS','A powerful weapon for a powerful champion of the Halls. Let us begin.',0),
(43958,'enUS','So it\'s true? An SI:7 agent was assassinated in our own backyard?$B$BIf SI:7 links us to the murder, this will be bad for business. We\'ll need to get to the bottom of this sooner rather than later...',0),
(43962,'enUS','Very well.',0),
(43969,'enUS','I will help you, but first I need you to do something for me.',0),
(43973,'enUS','A wise choice.',0),
(43975,'enUS','I will rally the worthy in Odyn\'s name.',0),
(43980,'enUS','A sound choice.',0),
(43984,'enUS','Yes, very good choice!',0),
(43991,'enUS','Did you sense the protectors of the wilds? Their presence is ever with us.',0),
(43994,'enUS','<She tenderly plucks the crystals from your hand one by one.>',0),
(43995,'enUS','<She hesitates for a moment before accepting the crystals.>',0),
(44004,'enUS','Kil\'jaeden took the child from Velen, let Velen believe that the boy had been killed, then raised the child as an agent of the Burning Legion with the express purpose of murdering his own father? That bastard waited 13,000 years to exact vengeance upon Velen for defying Sargeras and the Legion? The Deceiver indeed...$B$BFor Velen to have to experience such tragedy after what he and his people have already been through is heartbreaking. Such a thing would test anyone\'s faith.',0),
(44006,'enUS','The path ahead is clear. Your allies await you on this ledge. May the spirits walk with you, Farseer!',0),
(44009,'enUS','Most curious indeed! This is no object of the Legion\'s making. Let me have a closer look.',0),
(44034,'enUS','Yes, I think that will do rather nicely as well.$B$BGood choice.',0),
(44040,'enUS','I know of Coryn. We will not underestimate his venom, rest assured.$B$BThank you for helping Aurore. She is a dear friend of mine.',0),
(44041,'enUS','Let me get this straight...$B$BYou are saying that Master Mathias Shaw ordered the death of one of his best agents? This is far more serious than I first thought.$B$BWe\'ll need to continue the search for clues...',0),
(44043,'enUS','A wise path to follow - may it take you far.',0),
(44051,'enUS','I heard rumors that you intend to leave the City... that there is another place for the Nightborne where we are not beholden to Elisande\'s insanity.$B$BI wish to go with you.$B$BI can offer my harp and my hands, as they are not wanted here.$B$BSay the word and I will go with you through the teleporter and share my music with whomever awaits me on the other side.',0),
(44052,'enUS','It is a relief, if a small one. You have done well - rest for now.',0),
(44053,'enUS','She certainly is a worthy companion.',0),
(44055,'enUS','The other demons we will contend with in time. But that pit lord, it was a creature of great evil and beyond our devices to defeat on our own. Your skills were appreciated.',0),
(44057,'enUS','Yes, its all here, the location of the hunt for Volpin. $B$BI\'m sure there are better uses for a wonderful creature such as he than a pelt on some Noble\'s shoulders, don\'t you agree?',0),
(44063,'enUS','Excellent. There\'s no time to waste.',0),
(44074,'enUS','Thank you, Archdruid.',0),
(44075,'enUS','Excellent, Arch $C.',0),
(44076,'enUS','I am sad to hear of Oakheart\'s demise, but his soul will live on.',0),
(44077,'enUS','Wonderful. This is exactly what we need.',0),
(44082,'enUS','Greetings, Deathlord. It is an honor to serve you.$B$BI have been keeping an eye on the casualties of the Alliance and Horde upon the battlefield. Supply is limited, but there are some very promising prospects...',0),
(44083,'enUS','The altar is coated with hundreds of years of dust, but the candles somehow still glow in the distance.$B$BThis must be the site for the ritual.',0),
(44084,'enUS','<Thalyssra is speechless for a moment.>',0),
(44087,'enUS','Commander. I am glad to see that Asha was able to find you so quickly.$B$BThere is something important that you must attend to as soon as possible.',0),
(44089,'enUS','Friend is very wise! You can never have too many weapons!',0),
(44090,'enUS','I see you received my message.',0),
(44092,'enUS','You\'ve done it! You\'ve broken an invasion!$B$BIf only that had ended our campaign. But the Legion will never relent until they are destroyed... or have destroyed us.$B$BDon\'t let up! Fight off more of these wretched invasions, $n. The wyrmtongue we\'re holding captive here will reward your efforts.',0),
(44098,'enUS','Good to see you, $n. My apprentices are learning rapidly and are ready to serve you.',0),
(44099,'enUS','It\'s so good to see friend once again.',0),
(44100,'enUS','I see you received my message.',0),
(44101,'enUS','Very well, I yield - I yield!$B$BCurse you, $C, and that weapon of yours. Without it the Grimtotem would\'ve been victorious.$B$BTake your lousy supplies. But we will be back!',0),
(44106,'enUS','Welcome, $n. News of your heroism spreads from the Dreamgrove.',0),
(44112,'enUS','You\'ve crafted this rather well. I\'m slightly impressed.$B$BNow let me see that silk of yours...',0),
(44116,'enUS','Ye had best keep ye voice below whispers, matey... thar be a band \'o pirates ahead! Fer sure, these be not th\' type ye want to mess around wit\'...',0),
(44117,'enUS','<Fleet Admiral Tethys pops the cork from a bottle and takes a long gulp.>$B$BAye, \'tis be th\' stuff, $n. Ye\'ve done well!',0),
(44120,'enUS','I see by the blood spatters that Jace revealed the demons to you. I trust the young king is safe.$B$BWe have more work ahead of us, $C. Much more.',0),
(44137,'enUS','You are a most welcome sight, $n. And, you brought considerable firepower in the form of Archmage Khadgar.$B$BMalevolence has been portaling us back and forth between here and the Fel Hammer. We pushed the demons out of these ruins, but they are stronger than any we have encountered before.$B$BYour leadership is greatly appreciated. If we do not crush this Legion invasion now, they will overrun Azsuna and then the rest of the Broken Isles.',0),
(44140,'enUS','Oh, $n, it\'s you. Good, we\'ve got a little problem here.$B$BKayn didn\'t think that Cyana and I could handle this on our own? He might have been right this time.',0),
(44152,'enUS','I must find a way...',0),
(44153,'enUS','<A force within Light\'s Heart activates as you lay it down.>$B$B<You feel hopeful.>',0),
(44155,'enUS','Aye, what do ye have thar? \'tis be a letter from Master Mathias Shaw himself! Writ\' to th\' Red Blade no less.$B$BAye, it be just as I thought... these orders be fishier than a bucket \'o chum!',0),
(44156,'enUS','We must find a solution. We are running out of time.',0),
(44159,'enUS','Have at it, $n. Make your choice.',0),
(44161,'enUS','Well, at least we\'re going to have some fresh faces around here. If a broken\'s face can ever be called fresh, that is.$B$B<Kor\'vas smirks.>',0),
(44164,'enUS','Ah, $n, you have returned. An otherworldly air hangs heavy about you.',0),
(44166,'enUS','Ah, $n, you have returned. An otherworldly air hangs heavy about you.',0),
(44167,'enUS','Ah, $n, you have returned. An otherworldly air hangs heavy about you.',0),
(44171,'enUS','Well done, $n. I knew you could do it.',0),
(44172,'enUS','Well done, $n. I knew you would do it.',0),
(44173,'enUS','I trust your battles went well. And that\'s not just a turn of phrase. I know they did. I knew they would.',0),
(44174,'enUS','Well done, $n. With courage, you have faced every challenge along the way, and battled every day to claim your rightful place.',0),
(44175,'enUS','Well done, $n.',0),
(44176,'enUS','The heavy chest offers plenty of room to carry all of your belongings.',0),
(44177,'enUS','SI:7 made a secret deal with The Red Blade to hunt down Amber Kearnen?$B$BIt seems that Master Mathias Shaw was willing to pay any cost to have her dealt with...',0),
(44178,'enUS','Aww, yesss! That\'s the stuff!$B$B<Noggenfogger pops the cork and dabs some of the potion on his finger.>$B$BHave mercy! WOWZA! I\'m going to need some time alone with this stuff!',0),
(44180,'enUS','Look, $n. I\'ll level with ya...$B$BWithout your thieving prowess I\'d be a much poorer goblin than I am today. I think we should keep this gold-en partnership going!$B$BYou scratch my back, I\'ll scratch yours. Together, we\'ll put an end to this Burning Legion invasion and line our pockets with all the wealth in Azeroth!',0),
(44181,'enUS','Aye, matey! We\'ve had some good voyages together! Blood was spilt, rum was drank, n\' our search fer clues was a success!$B$BI\'ll level wit\' ye, $n. I be not havin\' such an adventure in some years now. Sailin\' wit\' ye felt like early mornin\' on th\' poop deck when th\' salty ocean rum splashes ye wide awake!$B$BHow abouts I come aboard n\' join yer crew as first matey?',0),
(44182,'enUS','I shored up Karazhan\'s defenses as best I could, but I have little confidence they\'ll hold. We have other matters to focus on in any case.$B$BGul\'dan has set his demon dogs loose upon Dalaran. He wants this city gone... but we\'re not going to let him have his way.$B$BI believe Dalaran will become the focal point of our campaign against the Legion, neutral ground where the heroes of every kingdom can join together against our mutual foe.$B$BLet\'s get to work, $n.',0),
(44183,'enUS','This is a dangerous mystery we\'ve stumbled upon, $n. It would not be fair for me to stand idly by as you risk your life to uncover this corruption.$B$BAfter all, without honor and brotherhood among thieves, none of us will stand to profit!$B$BFrom this point on, I\'ll pledge my personal services against the threat of the Burning Legion and the dark mystery we are unraveling. My blade is yours, $n...',0),
(44184,'enUS','Ah, $n, it\'s good to see you on your feet! The members of the Council of Six are recuperating from their ordeal.$B$BThe intensity of the teleportation spell can be disorienting. It seems you lost consciousness for a time, but at least you didn\'t awaken to find yourself stuck in a wall!$B$BDalaran has been relocated to the Broken Isles. From here, we will spearhead the effort to acquire the Pillars of Creation and drive the Legion from Azeroth once and for all!',0),
(44195,'enUS','The orders been sent, my people are on the case. Check back soon and you can pickup the shipment right here.',0),
(44202,'enUS','$n, I hope you don\'t mind me dropping by unexpectedly. I was in the area on business.$B$BMy people procured what look to be some rather nice armaments for the cause. I\'m sure that you know best how to distribute them.$B$BDo not doubt that our continued cooperation, even if it is a bit cloak and dagger, is making a huge difference in the war against the Burning Legion.',0),
(44203,'enUS','Shadowblade $n, always a pleasure. I was in the area on Alliance business and decided to drop in. It looks like our operations are faring well.$B$BMy people procured what look to be some rather nice armaments for the cause. I\'m sure that you know best how to distribute them.$B$BThough we must continue to cooperate through back channels and behind closed doors, know that for the duration of the war against the Burning Legion, you can count on my support and that of SI:7.',0),
(44204,'enUS','The order has been sent. Once my people have procured the item, it will be here for you to collect.$B$BGood... luck.',0),
(44205,'enUS','The ritual has begun. This will take some time. Return later.',0),
(44206,'enUS','The ritual has begun, they will Rise. Return here when the ritual is complete.',0),
(44207,'enUS','All those years of study are really paying off...$B$BOnce they\'ve sent the shipment through, it will be waiting here for you.',0),
(44208,'enUS','The spell has begun. Return to me when it is complete. Fate is in the hands of time now.',0),
(44209,'enUS','Well done, though that certainly takes all of our efforts. It will be some time before we can do that again.',0),
(44211,'enUS','The order has been issued. Once the shipment arrives it will be here for you to collect.',0),
(44212,'enUS','Word has been sent. The Seal will arrive soon.',0),
(44213,'enUS','Our glaives are yours, $n.',0),
(44214,'enUS','Excellent. You\'re going to like this.',0),
(44215,'enUS','I think you will appreciate this. I must admit to a certain level of envy.',0),
(44217,'enUS','We is with you, $n!',0),
(44218,'enUS','Aye, sir, the men have their orders. Once the shipment arrives it will be here for you to collect.',0),
(44219,'enUS','Word has been sent. The Seal will arrive soon.',0),
(44220,'enUS','Well done, though that certainly takes all of our efforts.',0),
(44221,'enUS','The order has been placed. Once the shipment arrives it will be here for you to collect.',0),
(44222,'enUS','Well done, though that certainly takes all of our efforts.',0),
(44223,'enUS','The order has been placed. Once the shipment arrives it will be here for you to collect.',0),
(44224,'enUS','Well done, though that certainly takes all of our efforts.',0),
(44226,'enUS','Word has been sent. The Seal will arrive soon.',0),
(44227,'enUS','Well done, though that certainly takes all of our efforts.',0),
(44228,'enUS','Murr will make Lurr smash fast! When he done smashing, we put it in box. Box here for you later.',0),
(44229,'enUS','The order has been placed. Once the shipment arrives it will be here for you to collect.',0),
(44230,'enUS','Word has been sent. The Seal will arrive soon.',0),
(44231,'enUS','The order has been placed. Once the shipment arrives it will be here for you to collect.',0),
(44232,'enUS','We are with you, $n.',0),
(44233,'enUS','Yours is the path we will follow, $n.',0),
(44234,'enUS','Well done, though that certainly takes all of our efforts.',0),
(44235,'enUS','Word has been sent. The Seal will arrive soon.',0),
(44237,'enUS','The sapling ignores you, but seems busy at work. Perhaps you should return later.',0),
(44238,'enUS','Word has been sent. The Seal will arrive soon.',0),
(44239,'enUS','Tianili seems distracted. Perhaps you should return later.',0),
(44240,'enUS','Our hearts and minds are with you, $n.',0),
(44243,'enUS','These Knights of the Ebon Blade are a powerful order, Deathlord.$B$BThat you command such respect amongst their ranks speaks to your strength and leadership.$B$BDuring my life, I always fought to preserve my kingdom and people. But for my failure as a father, their blood now stains my hands.$B$BSo, I will wash the failure from my hands with the blood of demons. The time has come for me to return to the fray. My sword is yours to command.',0),
(44244,'enUS','Words cannot fully express my gratitude for rescuing me, $n. In truth, I always knew that the Ebon Blade would not forsake me.$B$BI do not wish to elaborate on my years in captivity. That time has passed and we are now presented with an imminent danger in the Burning Legion.$B$BMy blade is yours, Deathlord. My life and my allegiance are yours to command.',0),
(44245,'enUS','There is no greater hatred and scorn in this world than that which exists in my heart.$B$BThe Burning Legion will pay for all that they have taken from me.$B$BThe day of my judgment awaits, but theirs is at hand and I will be the executioner\'s blade. I will not rest until every demon lays dead, their corpses paving the very ground I walk!$B$BCommand me to the front, Deathlord and I will rain terror upon the armies of the Burning Legion!',0),
(44246,'enUS','<Rottgut motions in your direction, gurgling and belching the words from its gaping mouth.>$B$BROTTGUT!!$B$BROTT. GUTT. ROTT! ROTTGUT ROTTGUT ROTTGUT!!!$B$BGUT? ROTTGUTT, GUT. ROTT... GUT!$B$BROTTGUT??',0),
(44247,'enUS','Deathlord, I have been your humble tutor in the dark arts for some years now. From your birth at the hands of the Lich King, to your ascension as leader of our order, I have taken pride in watching you grow in power and undeath.$B$BI believe the time has passed in which my services as a teacher are necessary. Perhaps I would be of more use to you on the battlefield?$B$BThe time has come for me to warm these frozen bones of mine in the blood my enemies. Please, allow me to be of service on the battlefield.',0),
(44248,'enUS','The Four Horsemen of the Ebon Blade are gathered together, but our work has only just begun.$B$BThe Burning Legion has come to our world hungering for destruction, but we will feed them their own demise. Apocalypse awaits the demon invaders and we shall bring it to them!$B$BDeathlord, you have triumphed where no others could have succeeded. I shall lead the Four Horsemen like my father before me, and so long as I lead them our loyalty is yours!$B$BThe return of the Four Horsemen is at hand!',0),
(44249,'enUS','In this fight, our spirits are as one, $n.',0),
(44250,'enUS','We stand with you, $n.',0),
(44251,'enUS','We are with you, $n.',0),
(44252,'enUS','Our blades are yours, $n.',0),
(44253,'enUS','We stand with you, $n.',0),
(44254,'enUS','The Council admires your power, $n.',0),
(44255,'enUS','The might of the Valarjar stands with you, $n.',0),
(44257,'enUS','Most curious indeed! This is no object of the Legion\'s making. Let me have a closer look.',0),
(44258,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Violet Hold?',0),
(44259,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Violet Hold?',0),
(44260,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Vault of the Wardens?',0),
(44261,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Vault of the Wardens?',0),
(44263,'enUS','Were you able to overcome The Arcway?',0),
(44264,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Neltharion\'s Lair?',0),
(44265,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Neltharion\'s Lair?',0),
(44266,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Maw of Souls?',0),
(44267,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Maw of Souls',0),
(44268,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Odyn\'s challenge?',0),
(44269,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Odyn\'s challenge?',0),
(44270,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Eye of Azshara',0),
(44271,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Eye of Azshara',0),
(44272,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Darkheart Thicket?',0),
(44273,'enUS','Were you able to overcome Darkheart Thicket?',0),
(44275,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the challenge?',0),
(44276,'enUS','Were you able to defeat Lord Ravencrest?',0),
(44277,'enUS','Were you able to defeat Lord Ravencrest?',0),
(44278,'enUS','We mourn together brother over the loss of Arduen, Cassiel, and Sirius. But, I owe you my life... again.$B$BThere is one thing I learned during my time in the prisons: the demons within Black Rook Hold must die.',0),
(44281,'enUS','You look quite prepared for battle. Do not let the bloodlust overtake you out there.$B$BThe Warchief wishes to present you with this ring before you head to war. May you return with the heads of many demons.',0),
(44282,'enUS','So this is the legendary Frozen Soul Pendant! I sense a great power in this item...$B$BI will begin my study of it at once. You have my gratitude, Deathlord.',0),
(44283,'enUS','Incredible... where did you find these? With these Essences, I will be able to open the way directly to the heart of the Nightmare. Let us make haste!',0),
(44284,'enUS','Incredible... where did you find these? With these Essences, I will be able to open the way directly to the heart of the Nightmare. Let us make haste!',0),
(44285,'enUS','Incredible... where did you find these? With these Essences, I will be able to open the way directly to the heart of the Nightmare. Let us make haste!',0),
(44286,'enUS','Yes, these parts shall do nicely!$B$BNow go on and introduce yourself to Rottgut! I\'m sure the two of you will get along... infamously!',0),
(44306,'enUS','The Blessings are under way, they will be ready for you to receive here shortly.',0),
(44310,'enUS','So it shall be done.',0),
(44337,'enUS','If this works, then perhaps there is still hope for Turalyon and the Army of the Light.',0),
(44338,'enUS','If this works, then perhaps there is still hope for Turalyon and the Army of the Light.',0),
(44366,'enUS','So it shall be.',0),
(44370,'enUS','Agreed. We must seek it out at once.',0),
(44375,'enUS','I couldn\'t agree more.',0),
(44379,'enUS','Good idea. There is no more dependable ally than a worthy blade.',0),
(44383,'enUS','I think that is wise. We need every weapon we can gather to defeat the Legion once and for all.',0),
(44400,'enUS','Whew. That\'s a SECOND invasion dealt with. Well done.$B$BNow, who do I talk to about getting this place shut down?',0),
(44401,'enUS','Very well.',0),
(44406,'enUS','I have been waiting for you, Farseer.',0),
(44407,'enUS','That was probably the easiest decision you\'ve had to make! Let\'s get started.',0),
(44411,'enUS','Such a cacophony! I could hear it before you pulled it from your pack.$B$BWhat you\'ve got there is a highborne memory crystal, somehow still intact. Created by ancient sorcery, they were used to store memories, stories, music, history, and whatnot.$B$BQuite rare! With a little... tinkering... I should be able to create something useful with it.',0),
(44412,'enUS','I appreciate your discretion, $n.$B$BNow, look here! I have imparted all of my substantial worldly wisdom into this globe, in addition to my ruggedly handsome features. No doubt you will find my counsel invaluable in your travels.$B$BI could only get it to say a handful of phrases, however, so be VERY SPECIFIC in your questions.',0),
(44414,'enUS','We\'ve done it! Without you, I fear I would have eventually succumbed to the onslaught.',0),
(44415,'enUS','A wise warrior welcomes all allies. You fight with the strength of an orc.',0),
(44416,'enUS','The spirits honor us with a day of glorious combat! You have my well-earned respect, Illidan Stormrage. I will gladly follow you into any battle.',0),
(44417,'enUS','That will definitely increase your power greatly.',0),
(44421,'enUS','Good work. There are still some stray anomalies floating about, but you\'ve negated enough interference that we should no longer be prevented from relocating the city.$B$BNow we just need to determine our destination.',0),
(44424,'enUS','A wise choice.',0),
(44431,'enUS','A sound choice.',0),
(44443,'enUS','A sound choice.',0),
(44448,'enUS','Dead? The titans are dead?$B$B<Khadgar ponders the news for a minute.>$B$BIt explains so much, yet I cannot help but feel an overwhelming sense of sadness. We have been on our own all along. Our gods killed before we were born.$B$BAs for the Army of the Light and Illidan, I am at a loss. I have never felt so powerless.$B$BIllidan is dead and the Golden Army fights an endless war in our name from across the cosmos.$B$BI need a moment, $n. This is too much bad news for an old man to bear.',0),
(44449,'enUS','Look at that shine!',0),
(44457,'enUS','<Maiev\'s face is bruised, her lips cracked, and her body covered in scars. She looks thin and ragged, but she moves with purpose.>$B$BFor weeks they tried to break me. Amateurs!$B$BI kept my silence. I counted the minutes, measured their steps, and listened to the voices beyond my cell.$B$BI have been waiting for my chance to escape, and to strike back at my captors.$B$BNow, you bring my armor AND my blade. It\'s your turn to set me free, $C. Let us destroy the Legion together.',0),
(44463,'enUS','I must admit, you saved us from what might have been a terrible tragedy. You have my gratitude, $C.',0),
(44463,'esES','Debo admitir que nos has salvado de la que podría haber sido una terrible tragedia. Tienes mi gratitud, $c.',22522),
(44464,'enUS','An auspicious start to a life of tragedy. Perhaps one of the few joyous memories Illidan would have in his life. While the years that followed tested the prophesied child, they would never break him. You must remember that, despite what you may see as our journey continues.$B$BThere is much more to be done, but I am not yet ready. I will call for you when it is time.',0),
(44465,'enUS','Greetings, Farseer $n. I have been waiting for you.$B$BThe Earthcallers are ready and at your command!',0),
(44466,'enUS','Failure. Rejection. From that day, Illidan would be haunted by both. Ever undaunted, he would continue the search for his destiny. Another path would be found.',0),
(44471,'enUS','Of course the Legion would try to infiltrate this funeral. Having all the leaders of the Alliance gathered in one place at one time... it is too tasty a target for the demons to resist!',0),
(44471,'esES','Pues claro que la Legión intentaría infiltrarse en este funeral. Tener a todos los líderes de la Alianza en el mismo lugar y a la misma hora... ¡es demasiado tentador para cualquier demonio que se precie!',22522),
(44473,'enUS','I trust the young king is safe.$B$BWe have more work ahead of us, $C. Much more.',0),
(44473,'esES','Confío en que el joven rey esté a salvo.$B$BNos queda mucho por hacer, $c.',22522),
(44479,'enUS','The line between good and evil is thin, and resides in a place where intention means little.$B$BIllidan wondered how those around him could be so blind to the threat of the Burning Legion. Fate is not without a sense of irony.',0),
(44480,'enUS','Illidan sought out the truth and was blinded by what he saw. He was beginning to understand his destiny, but there was one final sacrifice that he had yet to make.',0),
(44481,'enUS','I wept when I touched your consciousness in the Great Dark, mortal. For I saw his fall, and I saw you, your shadow casting a dark pall over his body. I felt hatred in your heart as it corrupted your mind.$B$BIt was not Light\'s Heart, but you, that needed preparation. Now you know truth. Are you prepared to do what must be done to save your world and all others?$B$BWhen the time is right, I will call upon you to begin the hunt for Illidan\'s soul.$B$BHis rebirth will be the story of your redemption.',0),
(44486,'enUS','Ah, the burns can be reversed with the right alchemic tinctures.$B$BHow interesting. A formal Darnassian writing style with... demonic affectations.$B$BI suspect I know who penned this.',0),
(44487,'enUS','I would recognize that handwriting anywhere. This is our own Khadgar\'s journal!',0),
(44488,'enUS','Foul magic wards these texts.$B$BMuch stronger than anything I\'ve seen before, but nothing that can\'t be undone by our mages!',0),
(44489,'enUS','$n, you are a sight for sore eyes. You have my gratitude for releasing me.$B$BI do not know how long I have been held captive... but I sense an overwhelming number of demons nearby.$B$BI have much to do here. Care to join me?',0),
(44490,'enUS','Grimwing was a formidable demon... I must say I am always impressed with your skill, $n.$B$BThere are many more demons here to kill. It is good to be at your side once more.',0),
(44492,'enUS','Now listen closely.',0),
(44493,'enUS','Do your best to pick this up the first time - I do hate repeating myself.',0),
(44495,'enUS','Perhaps there is hope for outlanders after all.',0),
(44496,'enUS','In the end, the denizens of Azeroth and Outland came to exact their vengeance upon Illidan. Though you did not strike a blow against him, you were complicit in his fall.$B$BI showed you Illidan\'s life so that you would understand why he fought and made the choices that he made. Yours was the vessel that needed preparation.$B$BIf the hatred and doubt in your heart has subsided, take your place at the side of the Light. Soon I will call upon you as we begin the hunt for Illidan\'s soul.',0),
(44497,'enUS','Forgive me, noble soul. I mislead you. Light\'s Heart was not the vessel that required preparation, it was yours.$B$BYou, who sacrificed everything for your world, and served your master dutifully until the end. These memories will serve to strengthen your resolve. Look to them when the dark temptation surrounds you and let them grant you the strength to resist and rise against the corrupters.$B$BWe will save Illidan and once more you will battle at the side of your master for the fate of all worlds.',0),
(44500,'enUS','We may not have the exact location of the Pillars of Creation, but at least we know where to start. We\'ll explore every corner of the Broken Isles until they\'re recovered.$B$BThe Legion\'s attack is intensifying. We must prepare to move Dalaran to the Broken Isles!',0),
(44543,'enUS','Glad to see you back on your feet, $n. Many good soldiers who sailed for the Broken Shore were not so fortunate.',0),
(44544,'enUS','It is good that you are here, Farseer $n. We have much to discuss.',0),
(44550,'enUS','You have arrived at last, Deathlord. We have much to discuss.',0),
(44555,'enUS','Thank you for coming, $n.',0),
(44556,'enUS','We have work to do!',0),
(44557,'enUS','Well done! At least now most of the remaining demons we have to deal with are currently inside the tower.$B$BCouldn\'t be more than a thousand or two, I\'m sure.',0),
(44561,'enUS','In the changing of seasons, the truth will be revealed.',0),
(44562,'enUS','We shall help the shal\'dorei find harmony.',0),
(44563,'enUS','Finally, my long lost brethren can return to this world. Elves belong beneath a starry sky - not a conjured one.$B$BThank you, $n.',0),
(44570,'enUS','Honor the Spires of Arak flame.',0),
(44571,'enUS','Honor the Talador flame.',0),
(44572,'enUS','Honor the Nagrand flame.',0),
(44573,'enUS','Honor the Gorgrond flame.',0),
(44574,'enUS','Honor the Azsuna flame.',0),
(44575,'enUS','Honor the Val\'Sharah flame.',0),
(44576,'enUS','Honor the Highmountain flame.',0),
(44577,'enUS','Honor the Stormheim flame.',0),
(44579,'enUS','Honor the Shadowmoon Valley flame.',0),
(44580,'enUS','Honor the Frostfire Ridge flame.',0),
(44581,'enUS','Hey, $n, it\'s me, Nomi. You know, from Pandaria?$B$BIt\'s fine if you don\'t remember, it\'s been ages since you may have seen me last.$B$BI\'m a full-fledged cook now and have been coming up with some of my own creations.$B$BHere, take a sample of some of the recipes and dishes I\'ve been working on.',0),
(44582,'enUS','Desecrate the Alliance\'s Shadowmoon Valley bonfire!',0),
(44583,'enUS','Desecrate the Horde\'s Frostfire Ridge bonfire!',0),
(44613,'enUS','Honor the Suramar flame.',0),
(44614,'enUS','Honor the Suramar flame.',0),
(44624,'enUS','Desecrate the Alliance\'s Suramar bonfire!',0),
(44627,'enUS','Desecrate the Horde\'s Suramar bonfire!',0),
(44663,'enUS','Ah, $n, it\'s good to see you on your feet! The members of the Council of Six are recuperating from their ordeal.$B$BThe intensity of the teleportation spell can be disorienting. It seems you lost consciousness for a time, but at least you didn\'t awaken to find yourself stuck in a wall!$B$BDalaran has been relocated to the Broken Isles. From here, we will spearhead the effort to acquire the Pillars of Creation and drive the Legion from Azeroth once and for all!',0),
(44667,'enUS','You\'ve done well. Our enemies tremble before you and your armies.',0),
(44672,'enUS','Keep a lookout for those crystal formations all over Suramar. We will need them.',0),
(44680,'enUS','You are an inspiration to us all, $n.',0),
(44682,'enUS','The power within you grows, $n. You will serve the council well.',0),
(44683,'enUS','The Legion\'s hold wanes. Our time to strike grows nearer.',0),
(44684,'enUS','Every bit contains an essence of sorts - one we can study to learn things about the magic wielder and ways to manipulate their magic for... other purposes.',0),
(44685,'enUS','You\'ve bought us precious time.',0),
(44686,'enUS','This information is just what we needed.',0),
(44689,'enUS','Well done, conjuror. With heroes like you at the helm, the Tirisgarde is a force to be reckoned with!',0),
(44690,'enUS','At last, I have enough Blood of Sargeras to fuel my creations! You will see, Deathlord, what my genius is truly capable of creating...$B$BNow, I must ask that you leave me to my work... there is much to do, and we have little time to waste!',0),
(44691,'enUS','Ah, I am feeling much better. Thank you!$B$BNow let us get to work.',0),
(44694,'enUS','It would seem that you have done an excellent job of eliminating a great many threats on the Broken Isles.$B$BYou never fail to impress me, $n.',0),
(44700,'enUS','It\'s an honor, $n.',0),
(44701,'enUS','<Nathanos glances over at you, pausing for a moment before acknowledging your presence.>$B$BYes?',0),
(44719,'enUS','I must commend your knack for overcoming adversity. Take your time gathering your fellow champions, $n, but don\'t take TOO long!',0),
(44720,'enUS','It is good of you to come.',0),
(44721,'enUS','She has forced my hand...',0),
(44722,'enUS','Glad you could make it.',0),
(44723,'enUS','Hopefully more will follow their example.$B$BThank you for showing them another way to serve the Nightborne.',0),
(44724,'enUS','<Silgryn stares grimly at the communicator.>',0),
(44725,'enUS','Thank you for taking this risk. Let us put an end to this now!',0),
(44726,'enUS','Well done. Let us leave before they call in reinforcements.',0),
(44727,'enUS','Thank you. We had no hope of rescue before you came along.',0),
(44729,'enUS','Now a greater task awaits you.',0),
(44733,'enUS','Our worst fears have been proven true, $n. The Legion\'s presence is deeply rooted in the tower.$B$BThe time has come. We must take back Karazhan!',0),
(44734,'enUS','For so long the secrets of the tower have remained hidden... I feel as if I have learned more about my former master.$B$BI am greatful we were able to see this journey through together, $n.',0),
(44735,'enUS','Your efforts today will not be forgotten, $n.$B$BThough the Legion\'s presence has left its mark on the Karazhan we once knew, I am certain the fate of the tower will not disappoint.',0),
(44736,'enUS','Thank you for saving me. It seems we underestimated Elisande\'s power.',0),
(44738,'enUS','The telemancy traps you placed prior to the battle are doing wonders for reducing our losses.',0),
(44739,'enUS','Well, with these plans and a little luck, we might be able to get through this with far less collateral damage than I would have expected.',0),
(44740,'enUS','Well done, hero. With this as our staging ground, our forces have a clear shot at the city gates.$B$BThalyssra has ordered her rebels to secure our location and cover our rear flank.$B$BOnce we have our siege vehicles in place we should be ready to assault the city.',0),
(44741,'enUS','Now, look closely.$B$B<Tytallo goes into a lengthy explanation concerning the thread count, weaving techniques, and other miscellaneous details that, to a tailor, are fascinating.>$B$BYou still seem confused. Here, take the pattern and see for yourself. Perhaps then you\'ll learn a thing or two.',0),
(44742,'enUS','We need to take action immediately!',0),
(44743,'enUS','The Nightfallen insisted on being a part in this conflict. There is more work to be done than people we have.',0),
(44752,'enUS','All that remains is to focus on his essence to isolate his location. Good work.',0),
(44753,'enUS','That was... difficult... but I am glad we succeeded.',0),
(44754,'enUS','<Vanthir\'s hands dart up to snatch the fruit from your grasp.>',0),
(44756,'enUS','I will see that he is made comfortable next chance I get. We made a great stride forward today, $n.$B$BElisande will not soon forget that we do not simply abandon our own.',0),
(44758,'enUS','This gunpowder is the key to my plan. Right good work retrieving it.',0),
(44760,'enUS','Around the isles, the very blood of our enemy attempts to corrupt all things. But as you may already know, this blood can be extracted.$B$BWe demon hunters use this blood for our own rituals, fueling us to fight back the demon invasion.$B$BBring me any Blood of Sargeras you find and I will trade with you what I can.',0),
(44764,'enUS','The samples have proven to be quite helpful along with your... influence.',0),
(44765,'enUS','You\'d better hurry up and hand over the fish if you want to win!',0),
(44766,'enUS','Hmm. An interesting challenge!',0),
(44767,'enUS','Ah, quite the breath of fresh solar winds. Take this, my favorite constellation, may it remind you of the watchers that watch over us all.',0),
(44768,'enUS','That is one less Legion supporter we need to worry about. Oh, and you found a shield generator too? Wonderful!',0),
(44770,'enUS','Few texts written by the ancient shal\'dorei remain. I am sure the Tirisgarde\'s librarians will be thrilled with these!',0),
(44771,'enUS','Delicious, thank you.$B$BBefore we act, we must gather more information onto what Helya is planning.',0),
(44775,'enUS','Finally you\'re here, Deathlord. I\'ve been waiting so long I could\'ve died again.',0),
(44782,'enUS','Don\'t worry, she\'ll be alright.$B$BWhatever demon did this to her didn\'t hang around long enough to finish the job.',0),
(44783,'enUS','I could feel their energy, even in undeath.',0),
(44787,'enUS','That was quite the entrance, Deathlord.',0),
(44789,'enUS','Our victory here is well deserved. With their forces subdued we can press our attacks to the forward camp and the monstrosity on the horizon.',0),
(44790,'enUS','Well done. Sometimes a single victory is enough to bring an army together. With time, these recruits shall train others, and we can grow our army to many times this size.',0),
(44800,'enUS','The Doomstone! I thought it legend, but here it is before me$B$BCan you feel its power radiating? We must only use it in times of utmost need; its power has a heavy price.$B$BYou were right not to give it to Magatha. It could do much harm in her hands.$B$BI trust you to keep it safe while we prepare an appropriate home for it.',0),
(44803,'enUS','Wonderful, you brought dinner! Moroes was worried he would let his master down.',0),
(44814,'enUS','These people owe their lives to your bravery. They will not forget the risks we have taken for them.',0),
(44821,'enUS','So what do you say? Up for a challenge?',0),
(44822,'enUS','We got lucky that time, but trying again could risk all our lives for nothing. We must find another way.',0),
(44827,'enUS','The trainees you helped cannot seem to stop talking about your fighting prowess. Already they are passing along what you taught them.$B$BI appreciate your help in this.',0),
(44829,'enUS','These weapons should prove quite useful in the coming conflict. Well done, hero.',0),
(44830,'enUS','Excellent. The knowledge in these books should prove very useful in the days to come.',0),
(44831,'enUS','It is good to know that they are alive. Their knowledge will be valuable in the coming siege.',0),
(44832,'enUS','It appears Ly\'leth was correct. This is an entrance to the Nightwell - and it is well protected. Nothing is impenetrable though.$B$BLet us have a look at the ley lines powering this shield, shall we?',0),
(44833,'enUS','Valtrois told me everything. She is hard at work on a plan for bringing down that barrier.$B$BI am afraid all we can do for now is wait. Thank you for your help.',0),
(44834,'enUS','Excellent work. The weapon will provide the proper housing, and the magical signatures on the core will let me bypass...',0),
(44842,'enUS','Good. With him out of the way we will be able to establish a stronger foothold once the main force arrives.',0),
(44843,'enUS','Nice work. They will not be opening that portal again any time soon.',0),
(44844,'enUS','A portal that big will not be reopening any time soon. I would say that counts as weakening their defenses.',0),
(44845,'enUS','We almost lost the invasion before we could begin. Good work.',0),
(44849,'enUS','Keep your wits about you, $n. There are many here who will attempt to steal your soul.',0),
(44850,'enUS','Good. These will be invaluable in the coming battles.',0),
(44858,'enUS','Thank you, $n. Hopefully, since our forces saw you performing this task they will come to their senses and stop this harassment.',0),
(44859,'enUS','I can relate to Thalyssra\'s frustration.$B$BI remember when I launched my first offensive. I swear I didn\'t eat or sleep for a week.',0),
(44860,'enUS','Thank you, $n. Hopefully, since our forces saw you performing this task they will come to their senses and stop this harassment.',0),
(44861,'enUS','Every member of the Duskwatch has had centuries to perfect their fighting techniques. We do not have that much time to get these rebels in to fighting shape.',0),
(44862,'enUS','Every member of the Duskwatch has had centuries to perfect their fighting techniques. We do not have that much time to get these rebels in to fighting shape.',0),
(44863,'enUS','I smell the air about you and see that you have returned triumphant.$B$BHere is the knowledge that you seek.',0),
(44865,'enUS','I can\'t believe it\'s finally over.',0),
(44868,'enUS','It is done. Helya\'s reign comes to an end and now we move forward. You have done a great thing today, champion. Consider yourself counted among those in the Halls of Valor.',0),
(44869,'enUS','It took all my willpower not to jump into the fray without backup. Let\'s go!',0),
(44870,'enUS','It is good to see you. I could use a helping hand.',0),
(44873,'enUS','That was a little terrifying. Sometimes I am not entirely sure that Oculeth knows what he is doing.',0),
(44874,'enUS','That was more infuriating than it should have been. At least her natural talents mostly matched my calculations...',0),
(44875,'enUS','It is done. Shal\'Aran will have no want of mana now.',0),
(44876,'enUS','That is quite the adventure you had. Thankfully we now have plenty of mana for the refugees. Thank you, $n.',0),
(44877,'enUS','Ha! Take that, demon scum!',0),
(44886,'enUS','You believe Skovald didn\'t want you to find this crystal, eh? Let me have a look.$B$B<Khadgar peers at the fel crystal fragment, tracing the lines of power that run through it.>$B$BI have seen this sort of crystal before. They are used to convey orders that come from the highest ranks of the Legion.$B$BThis is not good.',0),
(44887,'enUS','Well done! That couldn\'t have been easy.$B$BThis should be enough fragments. Let\'s have a look.',0),
(44888,'enUS','Nature is in dire need, mortal. You must fix it.',0),
(44889,'enUS','Good to see you made it, Battlelord $n!',0),
(44914,'enUS','So someone stole the Focusing Iris and you suspect Xylem might be the culprit? You may be right. $B$BIt is no secret that the archmage has been seeking artifacts of late. However, after the discovery of an ancient grimoire in the Legashi ruins, Xylem has become... unstable. I fear the grimoire may be stealing his mind.$B$BI can help you gain audience with the archmage. With any luck, you can reclaim the Iris peacefully.',0),
(44915,'enUS','Yes, I think that will do.$B$BThe apprentices outside the tower should think you outrank them now, so you should be able to get some information out of them. You\'ll need it to bypass the barrier.',0),
(44917,'enUS','Were you able to defeat the evils within Karazhan?',0),
(44918,'enUS','I do not know what lies in store for us, but we cannot sit idly while Ly\'leth is missing.$B$BWe must act now!',0),
(44919,'enUS','The withered... defeated so easily.$B$BWe must find a way to negate the magic of the felborne. We cannot afford to fight if our own can be turned against us.',0),
(44921,'enUS','If Goldrinn is in the Dream, he\'s defenseless! We\'ve got to help!',0),
(44924,'enUS','It is as I feared, the archmage is beyond reason... and now he is beyond reach.$B$BYou have done a great thing here, freeing his apprentices from his corruption, but this fight is not over yet.',0),
(44925,'enUS','I apologize for my actions, $C. I was a fool to tap into the power of the grimoire, and that folly could have cost Azeroth dearly. $B$BI thank you not only for purging and defeating the shadowy evil that had hold of me, but also for sparing my life.$B$BMyself, as well as all of Azeroth, are in your debt.',0),
(44926,'enUS','Oh aye! I know the make of that chopper.$B$BTha master who made it also created the famous Bleakwood Hew. You may \'ave heard of it.$B$BAn\' it just so happens I know how to make the hew too!',0),
(44927,'enUS','Oh ho! Look at all that STEEL!$B$BI\'ll have this shipment finished by the end o\' the week. Well done, lad! Well done!$B$BAn\' as I promised, here are those plans for the hew.',0),
(44928,'enUS','It is as I feared. Hopefully they will think twice before sending more spies.',0),
(44930,'enUS','Ha ha ha! I hope those rotten thugs rot in whatever pit of misery spawned them.',0),
(44944,'enUS','The time has come, $n.',0),
(44948,'enUS','<The hatchling seems to trust you a bit more now. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44949,'enUS','<The hatchling seems to be more comfortable around the sights and sounds of a human city. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44950,'enUS','<The hatchling seems quite content with its victories, and settles in for a nap. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44952,'enUS','Whoa, now that\'s a RUBY! I\'d only ever seen one other of its kind in the world and now I have one.$B$BI tell ya, this is gonna make me stinkin\' rich!$B$BBut uh, onto your payment. Here are those plans I was mentioning.',0),
(44953,'enUS','<The hatchling trills at the sight of Thunder Totem. That\'s quite an improvement! It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44954,'enUS','<The hatchling rams you softly with its head and trills. It seems to like doing things with you quite a lot! It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44955,'enUS','She looked good. The Arcan\'dor truly is a miracle for our people.$B$BShe is a welcome ally in the fight to come. Silgryn will take good care of her.',0),
(44956,'enUS','<The hatchling looks at you with admiration. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44957,'enUS','<The hatchling looks more confident after besting those beavers, and settles in for a nap. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44958,'enUS','<The hatchling emits a low hiss when you pass a member of the opposite faction. Mission accomplished! It will need to rest after this adventure.>',0),
(44959,'enUS','<You feel a special bond form between you and the hatchling. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44960,'enUS','<The hatchling looks more confident in its abilities. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44961,'enUS','<The hatchling looks like it might have absorbed some of that lesson, at least it enjoyed the trip. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44962,'enUS','<The hatchling looks much more at ease around elementals now. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44964,'enUS','The preparations are nearly complete. Oculeth will be ready to teleport us soon.',0),
(44967,'enUS','<The hatchling positively beams at you in pride for defeating such a frightening foe. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44968,'enUS','<The hatchling looks proud of itself and preens after the victory. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44971,'enUS','<The hatchling seems to be more comfortable around the sights and sounds of an orc city. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44973,'enUS','<The hatchling struts around happily, clearing showing off. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44974,'enUS','<The hatchling seems to be more comfortable around the sights and sounds of a dwarven city. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44975,'enUS','<The hatchling seems to be more comfortable around the sights and sounds of a tauren city. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44976,'enUS','<The hatchling seems quite content with its victories, and claws at your leg until you sit down and create a lap it can sit on. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44977,'enUS','<The hatchling no longer cowers behind you when the storms crackle in Stormheim. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44978,'enUS','<The hatchling nips at your feet excitedly. It seems to like doing things with you quite a lot! It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44979,'enUS','<The hatchling looks at you with interest. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44980,'enUS','<Your direbeak certainly doesn\'t look afraid of ghosts. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44981,'enUS','<The hatchling scratches the ground aggressively when you pass a member of the opposite faction. Mission accomplished! It will need to rest after this adventure.>',0),
(44982,'enUS','<You feel a special bond form between you and the hatchling. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44983,'enUS','<The hatchling builds a small nest of eaglet feathers, and settles in for a nap. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44984,'enUS','<The hatchling has taken a large puff of wolf fur for its nest, and you\'re not entirely sure where it was concealing it. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44985,'enUS','<The hatchling looks much more at ease around machines now. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44986,'enUS','<The hatchling growls at you possessively. It seems... proud? It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44987,'enUS','<The hatchling somehow still has energy, and runs off to play with your other pets. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44989,'enUS','<The hatchling is no longer shaking and clinging to your side. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44990,'enUS','<The hatchling looks strong and confident. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44991,'enUS','<The hatchling seems to be more comfortable around the sights and sounds of a draenei city. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44992,'enUS','<The hatchling seems to be more comfortable around the sights and sounds of a night elf city. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44993,'enUS','<The hatchling seems to be more comfortable around the sights and sounds of a blood elf city. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44994,'enUS','<The hatchling seems to be more comfortable around the sights and sounds of a forsaken city. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44995,'enUS','<The hatchling seems quite content with its victories, and butts you with its head lovingly. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44996,'enUS','<The hatchling seems quite content with its victories, and clucks happily at you. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44997,'enUS','<The hatchling no longer shivers when entering the dense foliage of Val\'sharah. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44998,'enUS','<The hatchling is more curious than afraid of the ghosts in Azsuna now. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(44999,'enUS','<The hatchling emits a loud \"baroo!\" It seems to like doing things with you quite a lot! It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45000,'enUS','<The hatchling beams at you. It seems to like doing things with you quite a lot! It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45001,'enUS','<The hatchling looks more confident in your abilities. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45002,'enUS','<The hatchling caws at you. A compliment, perhaps? It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45003,'enUS','<The hatchling gulps down one of the larva, then momentarily looks like it is going to be sick. You had better keep an eye on it. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45004,'enUS','<Besting another flying pet has really boosted your bloodgazer\'s confidence. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45005,'enUS','<The hatchling runs behind you when you pass a member of the opposite faction. Mission accomplished! It will need to rest after this adventure.>',0),
(45006,'enUS','<The hatchling puffs itself up when you pass a member of the opposite faction. Mission accomplished! It will need to rest after this adventure.>',0),
(45007,'enUS','<You feel a special bond form between you and the hatchling. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45008,'enUS','<You feel a special bond form between you and the hatchling. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45009,'enUS','<The hatchling pulls at a shedding nail, it will be sharp again soon. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45010,'enUS','<The hatchling licks its wounds, hurt but satisfied. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45011,'enUS','<The hatchling looks exhausted, and falls asleep immediately. It appears to be having some kind of nightmare. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45012,'enUS','<The hatchling glows slightly with magical energy, what did it get into? It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45013,'enUS','<The hatchling looks much more at ease around water now. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45014,'enUS','<The hatchling looks much more at ease around insects now. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45015,'enUS','<The hatchling looks at you timidly. It appears to be a little afraid of your power. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45016,'enUS','<The hatchling chews on a fragment of the great scorpion thoughtfully. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45017,'enUS','<The hatchling looks worn out, and spends quite a few minutes drinking after the victory. It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45018,'enUS','<The hatchling looks quite full. What did it eat? It will need some time to recover from this adventure.>',0),
(45021,'enUS','Shinfel should not have told you of my suspicions. This is my burden to bear.$B$BNevertheless, I am glad you are here. It would seem my fears are founded.',0),
(45024,'enUS','Can it be true? Does some sliver of my friend remain within that wretched demon?',0),
(45025,'enUS','Excellent work, as always, Netherlord. This should certainly buy us some time.',0),
(45026,'enUS','Thank you, Netherlord. I will keep these crystals safe until they are needed.$B$BWhen we find Kanrethad, we will be ready.',0),
(45027,'enUS','You\'re here, Netherlord! Quickly, there\'s no time to lose!',0),
(45028,'enUS','I have lived with a heavy heart since the day I fulfilled my promise to banish Kanrethad. I never thought I\'d live to see the day he would be returned to us.$B$BI thank you, Netherlord. You have lifted the burden of guilt from my shoulders, and in doing so, prevented the Legion from gaining control of one of our own.',0),
(45044,'enUS','Ay mon, whatcha got der in your hands?$B$BDat be da Darkspear! Ya found it?!',0),
(45051,'enUS','Dem\'s some mighty fine materials dat was made of. No wonda\' da boss wants it so bad.',0),
(45055,'enUS','Oh mon, I wish I could\'a seen da look on their faces when you pummled dem!$B$BNow dat we have all da materials, we just need to put it together.',0),
(45056,'enUS','I cannot possibly thank you enough. We will be reunited, and I will see we are never separated again.',0),
(45057,'enUS','Dat\'s it, mon! Ya did it!$B$BI tink before I head off back to da Isles, I\'ll be making a few extra copies of dees plans, just in case.$B$BI\'ll make ya a copy too, in case I be needing your help wit\' making another one.',0),
(45062,'enUS','Oculeth will be quite pleased with your findings. As you know, he\'s been working diligently on a new device for the withered.',0),
(45063,'enUS','The withered seem to be adapting quite well.',0),
(45064,'enUS','Our efforts have proven quite successful. I believe we are just about ready to make our stand.',0),
(45065,'enUS','I will begin analyzing this data at once.$B$BFor now, let us turn our attention to more... <Oculeth touches his fingertips together in succession.>$B$B...interesting technological advances.',0),
(45066,'enUS','Wonderful! Now the fun begins. You should speak with Thalyssra, I believe she is ready for more... testing.',0),
(45067,'enUS','Let us begin.',0),
(45073,'enUS','Thank ye, me friend. I feel better knowin\' I have been avenged.',0),
(45079,'enUS','<Annie looks at you, her eyes hollow and empty. Her clothes are stained with blood, though she seems to be mostly unscathed. She stutters, but her words are unintelligible.>',0),
(45083,'enUS','There are feathers everywhere! What a mess.',0),
(45088,'enUS','With these souls returned to the Halls of Valor my forces return to their former strength. As promised, the bounty is yours.',0),
(45103,'enUS','Now we have proven the might of the Ebon Blade to the Legion. The ability to take down so many demons without fear of death... that is the power that we hold. We shall see many more demons fall to our blades, and we shall strike them down for Azeroth.$B$BSuffer well.',0),
(45111,'enUS','Ok, I\'ll let your champions come and prove themselves in the ring. If they manage to win themselves a fight, come talk to me again and we can see about letting them fight harder brawls.',0),
(45118,'enUS','Revenge is sweet. The kvaldir will be forced to obey us, now!',0),
(45123,'enUS','So it seems that Levia has fallen under the spell of a succubus\' seduction. I fear her time alone as an outcast must have left her vulnerable to such tactics. I cannot help but feel some guilt for her turning down this path.$B$BIn any case, Levia is in great danger. She must be found!',0),
(45125,'enUS','I\'m pleasantly surprised, $C. Without your quick thinking, your mage friend would be lost to Agatha.$B$BThe portal is stabilized, and should lead to the mage\'s location.',0),
(45126,'enUS','Disgusting! I can\'t believe I let myself fall under the spell of such a creature! $B$BI was such a fool! She made me think she really cared about me. In the end, it seems nothing I thought I knew about Agatha was true!',0),
(45127,'enUS','So Levia is safe? That is a relief, though I wish we could have reached her sooner. An imp mother is bad enough - I can\'t imagine what Agatha will be capable of with Levia\'s power. And who knows what secrets Levia shared while under her thrall?$B$BI\'m afraid that this battle may not be over yet.$B$BFor now, we should celebrate whatever victories we can get. Thank you for your assistance, $n.',0),
(45128,'enUS','You have done all that I hoped, and more, Battlelord $n.',0),
(45143,'enUS','Your judgment is firm and fair, Highlord.$B$BThese new recruits will learn much under your command.$B$BThough I am beginning to wonder, if my worthiness was tested, would I be found lacking?',0),
(45145,'enUS','I know the name Nerus. He\'s a distant relative of mine, but why would he hold on to fel trinkets?$B$BThe answer to that question might be found within this scroll, but it appears to be blank.',0),
(45146,'enUS','It should only take a moment for the runes to appear once I apply the purified blood.',0),
(45147,'enUS','If you were strong enough to destroy the pendant that bound my spirit to the Burning Legion, then there might be hope for my ancestors.',0),
(45148,'enUS','With Zorak dead, my ancestor\'s spirits can finally be free of their curse.',0),
(45149,'enUS','What you have done for my family will never be forgotten.$B$BThe spirits of the Moonfang family will forever be in your debt.',0),
(45159,'enUS','<Dariness peers at the artifact you hand her.>$B$BA most interesting design! It reminds me of an ancient curio I read about long ago while still in training. I doubt it could be that though. Such a device has never been found.$B$BHmm, I wonder if it still works. Only one way to find out...',0),
(45160,'enUS','I trust you obtained all the ancient mana we need to infuse the cube?',0),
(45162,'enUS','Hey not bad, they beat the Council huh? Sure, they can advance to the next level.',0),
(45163,'enUS','You think you guys are tough, beating up a janitor and all? Well ok, I suppose I\'ll get you into the next fight.',0),
(45172,'enUS','Well done! Battlegrounds are certainly no place for the weak.$B$BWith your success, your champions will now look for more opportunities for you to prove your worth.',0),
(45173,'enUS','Well done!',0),
(45174,'enUS','The naaru heard my call? Interesting...$B$BVery well, let\'s get to work. We\'ve found Illidan\'s soul - finally - and it\'s not where we expected it to be held.',0),
(45175,'enUS','The Soul Prism of the Illidari is ready for use.$B$BIllidan\'s soul was plucked from the Nether - stolen - and taken to the underworld. A place known as Helheim.',0),
(45176,'enUS','<Light\'s Heart illuminates brightly and seemingly consumes the Soul Prism.>',0),
(45177,'enUS','I... I will do my best, Battlelord. You will - of course - have to do the hard work and lead the assault on the Nighthold!$B$BFOR AZEROTH!',0),
(45179,'enUS','Congratulations are in order I hear?',0),
(45180,'enUS','Ashran is no place for the faint of heart. You did well.',0),
(45182,'enUS','You come from the Kirin Tor? So you\'ll help me find my brother?',0),
(45185,'enUS','A letter? From one of the cultists? $B$BThat could be the lead we need!',0),
(45187,'enUS','Well, this definitely says... something.',0),
(45188,'enUS','What\'s this, a cultist\'s manifesto? $B$BSo Raest has really gone down a dark path, hasn\'t he?',0),
(45190,'enUS','My brother is here!',0),
(45192,'enUS','We\'re too late, the rift has closed!$B$BWe\'ll have to find another way to get to him.',0),
(45193,'enUS','So Raest escaped? This is unfortunate. $B$BStill, I will rest easier knowing the Nethersworn cultists will no longer skulk in the streets of Dalaran. I thank you for that.$B$BThe Kirin Tor will set out at once to figure out how we can reach Raest in the Twisting Nether. I will send for you when we find a way to reach him.',0),
(45207,'enUS','I\'ve heard so much about you, Archmage $n. It is a pleasure to finally meet you!',0),
(45209,'enUS','So they did intercept her messages! I hope Ly\'leth is okay...$B$BWe must investigate this breach she spoke of immediately!',0),
(45238,'enUS','You\'ve done it! Was the wyrm truly gargantuan? Oh, nevermind, size is relative...$B$BLet us get this focus into the cube and see what it does!',0),
(45239,'enUS','<Something about the power coursing through the cube urges you to take it into your possession.>',0),
(45240,'enUS','Deathlord! The vrykul have the harness!',0),
(45243,'enUS','Let\'s show the Legion true power.',0),
(45251,'enUS','Let us get to work, shall we?',0),
(45260,'enUS','I will ask this of you again, as more fruit is ready.$B$BFor now, we have some disturbing news to discuss.',0),
(45261,'enUS','Good, now to set our attention to those still suffering within the city.',0),
(45262,'enUS','There. I certainly hope Ly\'leth has good news...',0),
(45263,'enUS','Very well, let us go.',0),
(45265,'enUS','Good. Now let us see to business at the warfront.',0),
(45266,'enUS','The time has come.',0),
(45267,'enUS','Just in time. We are ready to begin.',0),
(45268,'enUS','I am glad we can still cure my people, but... I have troubling news.',0),
(45269,'enUS','Very well. Let us begin.',0),
(45271,'enUS','Welcome hero. Your arrival could not have been better timed.',0),
(45272,'enUS','Welcome hero. Your arrival could not have been better timed.',0),
(45277,'enUS','You are going to want to hear this.',0),
(45278,'enUS','It would seem the elves have returned to Suramar.',0),
(45280,'enUS','This is an unexpected problem, but we have more soldiers than food or weapons.',0),
(45281,'enUS','The time for our attack has come. It is time for us to take back Suramar from Elisande and her demonic allies!',0),
(45282,'enUS','The time for our attack has come. It is time for us to take back Suramar from Elisande and her demonic allies!',0),
(45285,'enUS','Thank you for coming. Your skills will prove to be invaluable for this next part of our plan.',0),
(45287,'enUS','The time for our attack has come. It is time for us to take back Suramar from Elisande and her demonic allies!',0),
(45291,'enUS','You were HOW small? Gracious! That must have complicated things.$B$BIt looks like there are more books on the floor than when we started. It\'s as if the books keep jumping off the shelves or something...$B$BThis is going to be harder than I thought!',0),
(45292,'enUS','The box is empty? Drat!$B$BI may be a mage, but I\'ll never be able to copy Medivh\'s motivator crystal enchantment!',0),
(45293,'enUS','Oh dear. My fault entirely!$B$BI should have ensured the horseshoes were in good shape before having you deliver them.$B$BThe humidity out here is a real killer!',0),
(45294,'enUS','I can\'t believe you found what we needed!$B$BUh, not that I doubt you, it\'s just... well, this is the first time one of my projects has actually worked out.$B$BAnyway, I think delivering these items to the actors will ease tensions for a while.$B$BThis is a momentous day!',0),
(45295,'enUS','You got every single spider, right?$B$BEither way, I\'ll just check that one off the list. No need to check up on your work.$B$B<Darius makes a squinched-up face.>',0),
(45296,'enUS','Nightbane has been defeated! I\'m in awe!$B$BMany years have passed since the blue dragon Arcanagos was slain by the corrupted Medivh. Archmage Alturus sought out the remains of the fallen dragon in an effort to study the Guardian\'s power. $B$BIn retrospect, maybe not the best idea. $B$BYour help has been invaluable.$B$BI still have a lot of work ahead to clean up Karazhan, but for now I dare ask no more of you. Thank you again for your assistance, $n.',0),
(45301,'enUS','Good, you made it.',0),
(45304,'enUS','Between you and me I\'m glad they won, that guy always creeps me out. Ready for the final challenge?',0),
(45312,'enUS','I can\'t believe you beat him! Meatball was so impressed he now insists he wants to work for you. Hope you don\'t regret it!',0),
(45316,'enUS','Thank you, $n. Every day we come closer to freedom for Suramar.',0),
(45317,'enUS','Leadership is a difficult burden, $n.$B$BWe must often split our attention - be sure to keep the big picture in mind.',0),
(45329,'enUS','That was surprisingly easy...',0),
(45330,'enUS','You got most of our scouts out alive. And Lady S\'theno appears somewhat chastened, at least. Well done!',0),
(45331,'enUS','Welcome back, Deathlord. I see you were successful.',0),
(45339,'enUS','That was quite a hit you took...$B$BFrankly, I\'m amazed that the Fel Hammer didn\'t self destruct when we fired her weapons. We are lucky to be alive.',0),
(45342,'enUS','Your allies have you to thank for their lives.',0),
(45343,'enUS','Ah, good. So the Conclave received my request. I didn\'t expect they\'d send their leader!',0),
(45344,'enUS','I hope you handled these samples with care, $n. I wouldn\'t forgive myself if I was responsible for getting the High $C sick.',0),
(45345,'enUS','Thank you, $n. I thought those goats seemed a little strange.',0),
(45346,'enUS','While there is no hope of curing those who have reached stage III, at least they will be able to provide crucial information about how the contagion works.',0),
(45347,'enUS','Brilliant work, $n. For a moment I thought I\'d need to find a new companion.',0),
(45348,'enUS','This cure could not have come at a better time.',0),
(45349,'enUS','You\'re here, High $C! Quickly, there\'s no time to lose!',0),
(45350,'enUS','I believe our combined efforts have effectively eradicated the fel contagion from Azeroth.$B$BWell done, $n.',0),
(45352,'enUS','Marvelous! It is such a joy to work with such magnificent craftsmanship. Please, come see me again should you find another such masterpiece.',0),
(45353,'enUS','I count myself fortunate to be able to work with the heroes who fight for our world\'s survival.',0),
(45354,'enUS','To say you\'ve earned your archmage status would be an understatement. Your success today proves that you were born one.$B$BNow mount your new vessel and ride against the Legion with all the might of your knowledge.',0),
(45372,'enUS','Thank you for being here, $n.$B$BUltimately the Nightborne must shape their own destiny, regardless of the help we have received from Outlanders like yourself.$B$BIt is no easy burden we bear, but Elisande has shown us that we must stand alone, without the Nightwell, to properly rejoin the world.$B$BThank you for all you have done for us.',0),
(45381,'enUS','The power these fragments hold will allow me to call the talisman to us. Well done!',0),
(45382,'enUS','The power these fragments hold will allow me to call the talisman to us. Well done!',0),
(45383,'enUS','The power these fragments hold will allow me to call the talisman to us. Well done!',0),
(45385,'enUS','About time, Sslayer $n. We have work to do.',0),
(45391,'enUS','You have gone above and beyond to honor our pact, Sslayer $n. You know I\'m not one for sappy speechess, but I assure you that I am grateful.$B$BI will take my place by your side if you will have me.',0),
(45392,'enUS','Velonara asked you to deliver this to me personally?$B$B<Moorgoth\'s eyes sparkle as he grins from ear to ear.>$B$BShe DOES care! She DOES care!$B$B<Moorgoth settles down and clears his throat.>$B$BThat was kind of her. Say, it is a nice hood. I bet I could mass-produce this and offer it to my fellow dark ranger aficionados.$B$BWould you like to browse my wares?',0),
(45398,'enUS','During my training, Mograine told me of what we could achieve with this harness. I look forward to the results.',0),
(45399,'enUS','Watching those vrykul shamble off mindlessly made my dead heart go \"pitter patter\".',0),
(45404,'enUS','How could this have happened to us; to me? I never thought I would die so young... and so violently...$B$BWe have tried to Detox our fallen friends, but this poison is too advanced.$B$BI cannot rest while our order\'s very survival is still at stake. I am so sorry I let you down, Grandmaster $n.',0),
(45406,'enUS','Today will not be your end, hero. The Legion threatens the Gates of Valor and without the power you wield they will surely fall.',0),
(45412,'enUS','You - I\'ve seen you out on the isles.$B$BWe need to move quickly!',0),
(45413,'enUS','No... no, no, no, no!$B$BNot good. Not good at all.',0),
(45414,'enUS','Kruul must not be allowed entrance into this world.',0),
(45415,'enUS','We must strike before Kruul reaches his full strength, but we\'re going to need help.',0),
(45416,'enUS','Kruul will never again threaten our world, or any other.$B$BProphet Velen sends his thanks, Archdruid.',0),
(45417,'enUS','A fitting end.',0),
(45420,'enUS','With the Eye of Aman\'Thul in our possession, we are one step closer to sealing the portal.',0),
(45423,'enUS','Yes, I saw the shadowy character as well, he ran right past me. Probably a tauren, but we can\'t be sure. Keep a look out for him, something tells me we\'re just beginning to unravel this mystery.',0),
(45425,'enUS','We have asked a lot of you over the last few months, $n. You not only rose to our expectations, but surpassed them. By killing Katith\'rax, you have stopped the attacks against our ancients.$B$BYou deserve the position of Archdruid of the Dreamgrove. I am honored to be your colleague, and expect us to do much for the world. Together.',0),
(45426,'enUS','What news do you have of the attack on Aviana\'s shrine?',0),
(45437,'enUS','I have been unfairly maligned by many. I am glad the Tirisgarde does not fall prey to petty rumors!',0),
(45440,'enUS','Whew. Celebration brew is..*hic* shtronger than I remembered it to be. *urp*',0),
(45442,'enUS','It makes my heart glad to see our order returning to health.',0),
(45449,'enUS','Thank you. That\'s one less demon working against us.',0),
(45459,'enUS','Good, you made it!',0),
(45482,'enUS','Yes, outsider? What business do you have here?',0),
(45486,'enUS','I thank you for bringing Sigryn to me, outsider. She truly is the future of our people.$B$BThough you have already done so much, I would ask another favor of you. Please accompany Sigryn in her challenges. She has grown to trust you, and will need guidance through the trials she must face.',0),
(45498,'enUS','We did it! We saved Goldrinn!',0),
(45522,'enUS','The Bonespeakers yield. Our clan will not interfere with Sigryn\'s claim to the throne.$B$BBe careful of this one, $C. I can see the darkness that consumed Skovald dwelling in this girl\'s heart. How she has resisted it this far, I do not know.$B$BYou had best hope she can control it.',0),
(45523,'enUS','You have the backing of the Dragon-Riders, but a greater rival to the throne still lives in secret.$B$BThe God-King\'s son yet lives. My riders spotted him among the outcasts of Vrekt. He would be the true heir to Skovald\'s throne. $B$BThe vrykul would never follow you were he to contend your claim!',0),
(45524,'enUS','I cannot believe that I find my brother alive, only to see him fall by my own blade. $B$BHow can fate be so cruel?',0),
(45525,'enUS','Sigryn has taken the path of Skovald before her. Only, I fear she is more powerful than her father ever was. $B$BI fear that Sigryn\'s thirst for revenge may lead to her undoing. Though truly powerful, she would be no match for Odyn.$B$BShe must be stopped before it is too late.',0),
(45526,'enUS','I... thank you for coming for me. I hope you can forgive me for what I\'ve done.$B$B$BI will return to Eyir. I only hope she can grant me her forgiveness as well...',0),
(45527,'enUS','To think, when you met me I had all intentions of living out my days as a farmer. Little did I know that the gods had other plans for me.$B$BThank you, outsider, for showing me my true purpose. I only hope I can live up to Eyir\'s visions and truly unite the Tideskorn once more.$B$BIf that day comes, the Legion will regret ever setting foot in Stormheim.',0),
(45528,'enUS','Now the demons can\'t call reinforcements. That was great!',0),
(45532,'enUS','What did she say about a distraction?! This isn\'t sounding good...',0),
(45534,'enUS','Remarkable! So there really was something to that prophecy after all!$B$BI am glad that Sigryn will lead the vrykul instead of the brutes who challenged her. Let us just hope she can unite the Tideskorn under her banner before the Legion has this place overrun.$B$BWell done, $n!',0),
(45539,'enUS','Wow, that\'s impressive! Here\'s the sack of supplies, you earned it! Sorry about the dampness.',0),
(45540,'enUS','Thank you for coming, I have some interesting news about what\'s been going on in the Wailing Caverns since Naralex has awakened.',0),
(45545,'enUS','Blowing up demons never gets old, does it? Ha!',0),
(45551,'enUS','<Nighthuntress Syrenne\'s pet is too weak to react to your presence.>',0),
(45552,'enUS','<D\'Bynn gently nuzzles your hand.>',0),
(45553,'enUS','I suppose I have you to thank for saving my beloved companion.',0),
(45554,'enUS','I have encountered many outsiders in my time patrolling the city, but never one quite as resourceful as you.',0),
(45555,'enUS','You continue to surprise me, outsider.',0),
(45556,'enUS','Let\'s make this quick. It won\'t be long before more demons come rushing through this pass.',0),
(45557,'enUS','There is no joy when a Nighthuntress falls, but it had to be done. The truth is, she died the moment she aligned herself with the Burning Legion.',0),
(45560,'enUS','Thank you for coming. I am glad you are treating this threat seriously.',0),
(45561,'enUS','Are you ready to begin?',0),
(45562,'enUS','Very good, now we can begin!',0),
(45563,'enUS','Coins are interesting items. They travel far and wide across the lands, yet this one seems to also travel through time.$B$BThe fact that you found this coin where you did is both an omen and a blessing.',0),
(45564,'enUS','There were quite a few guards as I scouted around. I noticed more strange things on the other side.$B$BLet me see those totems.',0),
(45565,'enUS','Very good, Squire- First Class! Now the real journey begins!',0),
(45566,'enUS','Excellent, you found my armor.',0),
(45567,'enUS','Pimento! You found him!',0),
(45568,'enUS','Yes!',0),
(45570,'enUS','At last, the Focusing Iris is returned! I will rest easier knowing it is once again safe in the vaults.$B$BI\'m sorry to hear about Xylem, though I\'m happy he survived the ordeal. He may be eccentric, but his heart is in the right place. $B$BWe can use more allies like him in the wars to come.',0),
(45571,'enUS','Good, you\'re here. Let\'s get to work.',0),
(45572,'enUS','We must remember our allies who have fallen on this day and in their honor, continue our fight.$B$BThe time is upon us, $n. Our riders are ready. Let us show the Burning Legion the true strength of Highmountain.',0),
(45573,'enUS','Easy as pie, Shadowblade. Now is when the plan kicks into action!',0),
(45574,'enUS','Let\'s hope that\'s enough to brew a cure for our dying monks!',0),
(45575,'enUS','Tugar... I thought he was dead. He was a nasty Bloodtotem even before the Legion arrived.$B$BWe have to get to him.',0),
(45576,'enUS','Ah, my blade sings. Time to put this plan into action, Shadowblade.',0),
(45586,'enUS','Good. The Soulstone\'s shields should be sufficiently strengthened now.',0),
(45587,'enUS','That was powerful fel magic. If it is true, if he is raising an army of such beasts... Thunder Totem is in peril!',0),
(45614,'enUS','The Felborne will respect the Tirisgarde now, do you not agree?',0),
(45615,'enUS','Now that\'s what I\'m talking about! You know what they say - where there\'s mages, there\'s dust!',0),
(45627,'enUS','Thunder Totem and countless lives are saved. One more crisis down in this war against the Legion.',0),
(45628,'enUS','That couldn\'t have gone better if I had done it myself. Good work, Shadowblade.',0),
(45629,'enUS','That couldn\'t have gone better if I had done it myself. Good work, Shadowblade.',0),
(45630,'enUS','You make a pretty good business partner, bud! I\'ll see what I can do to get ol\' Khadgar on board with these new servants. $B$BI tell ya I\'m gonna make a fortune!$B$BOh, don\'t think I forgot you. I\'ve got somethin\' special in mind for ya!',0),
(45632,'enUS','The filthy naga ambushed me. I will not fail again.',0),
(45633,'enUS','With their leaders defeated, the Felrage naga will not be preying on our warriors again. Still, we should keep an eye on them in the future.',0),
(45634,'enUS','Well done, $n. The kvaldir will be useful tools in the battles to come.',0),
(45639,'enUS','This will work just fine. De Horde thanks you, bruddah.',0),
(45642,'enUS','Look at that mountain of meat. You done de Horde proud, $n.',0),
(45643,'enUS','You make your Warchief proud. For da Horde!',0),
(45644,'enUS','Blast, I didn\'t think he would find me again so fast.',0),
(45645,'enUS','<Doloria gives you a sly wink from behind her mask>$B$BUh, no, haven\'t seen her for a few days, not sure who you\'re talking about.',0),
(45647,'enUS','Our soliders will be back in action soon, and the Felrage naga will think twice before messing with us again!',0),
(45648,'enUS','Thanks. I was ambushed by a dozen naga and skrog! At least I took quite a few down before they overwhelmed me...',0),
(45649,'enUS','Our soliders will be back in action soon, and the Felrage naga will think twice before messing with us again!',0),
(45650,'enUS','With their leaders defeated, the Felrage naga won\'t be launching any more raids for awhile! Still, we should keep an eye on them in the future.',0),
(45652,'enUS','You\'re in charge here?',0),
(45706,'enUS','Let\'s not keep my tribe waiting.',0),
(45723,'enUS','Fel blood has never been sweeter.',0),
(45724,'enUS','I reclaimed Arikara. Did you find the Doomstone?',0),
(45725,'enUS','The Legion cannot break the Grimtotem.',0),
(45726,'enUS','You\'ve done those souls a great favor. I hope they find peace.$B$BLet\'s cut off these experiments at the source now.',0),
(45727,'enUS','Excellent work, $n. We still have a long road ahead of us to rid this world of the Legion, but this brings us one step closer.',0),
(45729,'enUS','Many thanks, friend.$B$BFor the Alliance!',0),
(45730,'enUS','With your help, the Alliance may win this thing.',0),
(45731,'enUS','This will work just fine. The Alliance thanks you.',0),
(45733,'enUS','Excellent hunting, $C.',0),
(45734,'enUS','Look at that mountain of meat. You have done the Alliance proud, $n.',0),
(45735,'enUS','You make your King proud. For the Alliance!',0),
(45747,'enUS','Well done, $R. For the Horde!',0),
(45748,'enUS','Oh, I see. This is a trophy of battle.$B$BWe will add it to the many treasures you and your fellow adventurers have brought. For the Horde!',0),
(45749,'enUS','Ahh, the trophy of an epic battle. Well fought, $C!',0),
(45750,'enUS','Ah, I see, it is a hard-earned reward from one of your many battles. Well done, $C!',0),
(45751,'enUS','This is an impressive find indeed. The Abyssal High Council do not part with their sigils easily.',0),
(45752,'enUS','To wrest a sigil from one of the Abyssal High Council is a feat worthy of praise. For the Horde!',0),
(45753,'enUS','Ah, a sigil. From the Abyssal High Council, no less!$B$B<Warlord Gorchuk wipes a bead of sweat from his brow.>$B$BI... I had assumed that it was... that you were... oh, never mind.$B$BFor the Horde!',0),
(45754,'enUS','A sigil from the Abyssal High Council? You\'ve outdone yourself today, $R.$B$BFor the Horde!',0),
(45755,'enUS','Well done, $R. For the Alliance!',0),
(45756,'enUS','Oh, I see. This is a trophy of battle.$B$BWe will add it to the many treasures you and your fellow adventurers have brought. For the Alliance!',0),
(45757,'enUS','Ahh, the trophy of an epic battle. Well fought, $C!',0),
(45758,'enUS','Ah, I see, it is a hard-earned reward from one of your many battles. Well done, $C!',0),
(45759,'enUS','This is an impressive find indeed. The Abyssal High Council do not part with their sigils easily.',0),
(45760,'enUS','To wrest a sigil from one of the Abyssal High Council is a feat worthy of praise. For the Alliance!',0),
(45761,'enUS','Ah, a sigil. From the Abyssal High Council, no less!$B$B<Field Marshal Snowfall wipes a bead of sweat from his brow.>$B$BI... I had assumed that it was... that you were... oh, never mind.$B$BFor the Alliance!',0),
(45762,'enUS','A sigil from the Abyssal High Council? You\'ve outdone yourself today, $R.$B$BFor the Alliance!',0),
(45763,'enUS','The Legion is forcing Azeroth to bend to its will. We cannot allow this any longer!',0),
(45764,'enUS','It\'ss a shame the batriderss didn\'t make it. Even more reason to blast the hell out of the Legion as soon as the Fel Hammer\'ss weaponss core iss operational again.',0),
(45765,'enUS','I provided cover as the weaker of your people retreated. They will return to the Maelstrom safely.',0),
(45767,'enUS','It seems the Doomstone is pulsating with energy.',0),
(45769,'enUS','Ah, you\'ve awoken. I have heard tale of what happened.',0),
(45770,'enUS','That was quite the encounter, wouldn\'t you say Highlord $n? Reminds me of my glory days.$B$BNevertheless we\'ll be keeping a more watchful eye on Stratholme from now on. But that\'s not important right now.$B$BWe should move on to the ceremony and have you claim your prize!',0),
(45771,'enUS','Grandmaster $n, these old bones grow weary. Our future depends on you to continue the fight against the Legion.$B$BSo long as you remain a beacon of light in the darkness, hope remains!',0),
(45785,'enUS','And who are you? $n?$B$BAhh... yes, I believe I\'ve heard mention of you before. Welcome to Silithus, $n.$B$BToday, we celebrate our heritage as sons of Kalimdor. Furthermore, we prove that the Horde will always grind those puny Alliance into the ground.$B$BAre you with me?',0),
(45787,'enUS','And who are you? $n?$B$BAhh... yes, I believe I\'ve heard mention of you before. Welcome to Silithus, $n.$B$BToday, we celebrate the fabled war history of Kalimdor. Furthermore, we prove that the Alliance will always show the Horde their inferiority.$B$BAre you with me?',0),
(45788,'enUS','Thank ye for coming so quickly, High $C. King Magni, or I suppose I should say \'The Speaker,\' thinks he\'s found a hidden Titan vault!',0),
(45789,'enUS','Tis our greatest honor ta present ye with this steed, High $C. An\' thank ye for leading us, ye are truly blessed by the Light, an\' so are all of us for havin\' ye.',0),
(45790,'enUS','I will miss Brewmaster Blanche. She taught me to follow my dreams.$B$BAnd I have always wanted to study Mistweaving...$B$BGrandmaster $n. If you will have me, I will defend you and our order from all that wish us harm.',0),
(45794,'enUS','Thank you for bringing me news of Jubeka. It could not have come at a better time.$B$BWe\'ve received information on Kanrethad\'s whereabouts.',0),
(45795,'enUS','Our fight doesn\'t end here, $n.',0),
(45796,'enUS','You have saved Thunder Totem and we owe you yet another debt.$B$BIt\'s a shame that Tugar wasn\'t there. As long as he lives, we are in danger.$B$BI will do everything I can to find him, and then we will finish this... together.',0),
(45798,'enUS','It\'ss about time you shut that demon up. Thanksss...',0),
(45799,'enUS','Ah, $n, you have returned. An otherworldly air hangs heavy about you.',0),
(45812,'enUS','We must continue our fight.',0),
(45813,'enUS','Well, she has been taken, but we shall never rest. Join me as my Follower, lead my troops, perform missions for me! Together we will find her!',0),
(45833,'enUS','Straighten up, Shadowblade. We\'ve got work to do.',0),
(45834,'enUS','With the Valarjar leading the vanguard, our offensives will be glorious!',0),
(45835,'enUS','They ran right past us on their way out.',0),
(45836,'enUS','Welcome back, Shadowblade. I assume you\'ve retrieved the gunpowder?',0),
(45838,'enUS','I\'m afraid our fight has only brought us so far. We must press our attack before the Legion advances beyond their stronghold within the Temple of a Thousand Lights!',0),
(45839,'enUS','Just beyond these cliffs, the forces of the Legion are gathering for their assault. For every moment that passes their number grows.$B$BWe must strike soon before we are overwhelmed!',0),
(45840,'enUS','My apologies, $n. I hope Aviash and I did not offend you. One cannot be too careful during times like these.',0),
(45841,'enUS','I am relieved that you have dealt with immediate threat. We barely have enough resources for the Broken Shore as it is!$B$BStill we have something for you...',0),
(45842,'enUS','We hope the increased power to your weapon will prove useful on the Broken Shore and beyond.',0),
(45843,'enUS','Any luck out there?',0),
(45844,'enUS','Archmage, I\'ve found something you may be interested in. An old journal of the late Archmage Antonidas. In it, he speaks of a project he was working on that I think we may be able to finish.$B$BIt was a sort of flying disc that could attune itself to the rider\'s magical specialization.$B$BBut I need your help tracking down the pieces. From what I could gather, he gave them to trusted friends and allies through the years. Perhaps you could persuade them to give us the pieces.',0),
(45845,'enUS','You\'ve recovered it! And it is as Antonidas wrote, still surging with great fire magic!',0),
(45846,'enUS','Ogres took it? Those beasts will grab anything they can I suppose.$B$BRegardless, it\'s excellent you were able to find it.',0),
(45847,'enUS','To think it was right here in Dalaran the whole time.',0),
(45848,'enUS','Squawk! Tethys is lame! Bad pirate! bad pirate!$B$B$n better pirate, raaaaawk! Go with you now!',0),
(45856,'enUS','You have sacrificed for our lands, brave $C.$B$BYour perseverance has inspired our brothers and sisters to stand against the Burning Legion.',0),
(45861,'enUS','We hope the increased power to your weapon will prove useful on the Broken Shore and beyond.',0),
(45862,'enUS','We hope the increased power to your weapon will prove useful on the Broken Shore and beyond.',0),
(45863,'enUS','We hope the increased power to your weapon will prove useful on the Broken Shore and beyond.',0),
(45864,'enUS','We hope the increased power to your weapon will prove useful on the Broken Shore and beyond.',0),
(45865,'enUS','We hope the increased power to your weapon will prove useful on the Broken Shore and beyond.',0),
(45866,'enUS','We hope the increased power to your weapon will prove useful on the Broken Shore and beyond.',0),
(45873,'enUS','I am not one for emotional speeches, Battlelord $n, so I will keep this short. $B$BI owe you my life. My axes are at your service.',0),
(45876,'enUS','You are an inspiring leader, Battlelord $n. I will follow you to Argus and back if you will have me!',0),
(45883,'enUS','I will not allow such insolence!',0),
(45890,'enUS','What business do you have here? Have you come to scavenge what the harpies left behind?',0),
(45902,'enUS','It is small compensation for the deed you have accomplished, I hope it is enough.',0),
(45904,'enUS','I cannot thank you enough, hero.',0),
(45905,'enUS','Your competence in these matters is greatly appreciated.',0),
(45906,'enUS','Once this is all over, the Council hopes to thank you properly.',0),
(45908,'enUS','Your talent for this sort of thing is astounding!',0),
(45909,'enUS','We hope the increased power to your weapon will prove useful on the Broken Shore and beyond.',0),
(45910,'enUS','Once again you have proven to be a capable agent against the Legion.',0),
(45916,'enUS','The amount of power this Levia channeled into this portal is impressive, if unnecessary. Unfortunately, if we don\'t get it stable, it\'s likely to collapse and take us with it. $B$BSufficed to say, that would end your mission pretty quick.$B$BI have to concentrate to keep this open, so I\'ll need your help...',0),
(45917,'enUS','What... what is going on? $B$BWho are you?',0),
(45971,'enUS','I laughed as their infernals crumbled. They return to Azeroth, as they belong.',0),
(45974,'enUS','Greetings, Highlord. I\'ve just been informed about the wounded soldier who escaped from the Broken Shore.$B$BWhat he must have endured...',0),
(45975,'enUS','Grim tidings indeed.$B$BI suggest we continue sending our champions to scout out the dangers that await.',0),
(45986,'enUS','Greetings, Battlelord. I\'ve just been informed about the wounded soldier who escaped from the Broken Shore.$B$BWhat she must have endured...',0),
(45987,'enUS','Grim tidings indeed.$B$BI suggest we continue sending our champions to scout out the dangers that await.',0),
(45989,'enUS','Greetings, Netherlord. I\'ve just been informed about the wounded soldier who escaped from the Broken Shore.$B$BWhat she must have endured...',0),
(45990,'enUS','Grim tidings indeed.$B$BI suggest we continue sending our champions to scout out the dangers that await.',0),
(45991,'enUS','Greetings, Shadowblade. I\'ve just been informed about the wounded soldier who escaped from the Broken Shore.$B$BWhat she must have endured...',0),
(45992,'enUS','Grim tidings indeed.$B$BI suggest we continue sending our champions to scout out the dangers that await.',0),
(45993,'enUS','Greetings, Slayer. I\'ve just been informed about the wounded soldier who escaped from the Broken Shore.$B$BWhat she must have endured...',0),
(45994,'enUS','Grim tidings indeed.$B$BI suggest we continue sending our champions to scout out the dangers that await.',0),
(45995,'enUS','Greetings, Farseer. I\'ve just been informed about the wounded soldier who escaped from the Broken Shore.$B$BWhat she must have endured...',0),
(45996,'enUS','Grim tidings indeed.$B$BI suggest we continue sending our champions to scout out the dangers that await.',0),
(45997,'enUS','Greetings, Archmage. I\'ve just been informed about the wounded soldier who escaped from the Broken Shore.$B$BWhat she must have endured...',0),
(45998,'enUS','Grim tidings indeed.$B$BI suggest we continue sending our champions to scout out the dangers that await.',0),
(46000,'enUS','Well done, Archmage $n! Dalaran can defend herself once again.$B$BFor all of our sakes, let us hope that the shields keeping Kathra\'natir imprisoned do not fail before we are able to find a safer solution.',0),
(46020,'enUS','The crystals will be safe here, with each of the council members watching over them.$B$BKanrethad is still recovering, but is well enough to speak.',0),
(46022,'enUS','Greetings, Huntmaster. I\'ve just been informed about the wounded soldier who escaped from the Broken Shore.$B$BWhat she must have endured...',0),
(46023,'enUS','Grim tidings indeed.$B$BI suggest we continue sending our champions to scout out the dangers that await.',0),
(46024,'enUS','Greetings, Grandmaster. I\'ve just been informed about the wounded soldier who escaped from the Broken Shore.$B$BWhat she must have endured...',0),
(46025,'enUS','Grim tidings indeed.$B$BI suggest we continue sending our champions to scout out the dangers that await.',0),
(46026,'enUS','Greetings, Archdruid. I\'ve just been informed about the wounded soldier who escaped from the Broken Shore.$B$BWhat he must have endured...',0),
(46027,'enUS','Grim tidings indeed.$B$BI suggest we continue sending our champions to scout out the dangers that await.',0),
(46028,'enUS','Greetings, High $C. I\'ve just been informed about the wounded soldier who escaped from the Broken Shore.$B$BWhat she must have endured...',0),
(46029,'enUS','Grim tidings indeed.$B$BI suggest we continue sending our champions to scout out the dangers that await.',0),
(46030,'enUS','Greetings, Deathlord. I\'ve just been informed about the wounded soldier who escaped from the Broken Shore.$B$BWhat he must have endured...',0),
(46031,'enUS','Grim tidings indeed.$B$BI suggest we continue sending our champions to scout out the dangers that await.',0),
(46034,'enUS','All these priests? They report to you? It\'s astonishing, really.$B$BI have only one Roland, and it seems you have hundreds!$B$BI think we will get along well, $n. Very well, indeed.$B$BAllow me to stay, and in return, I will offer you my services.',0),
(46035,'enUS','Another crisis averted! Your effectiveness is without compare.',0),
(46043,'enUS','Archmage, the events of the past have long weighed heavily upon me. While I do not regret my actions, I do regret what happened. If I could go back and change things...$B$BI hope in time the Kirin Tor - indeed, all of Azeroth - will better understand my loyalties. Thanks to you, crisis has been averted. Please accept my enduring gratitude.',0),
(46044,'enUS','Look, Archdruid, don\'t get me wrong. I love Aviana. She\'s my ancient! But she\'s a little too passive for me to follow around all the time.$B$BYou, on the other hand? You\'re the real deal! I want to be in the fray, ruining some demon\'s day!$B$BSo? Will you take me with you?',0),
(46045,'enUS','I know I have much to answer for.$B$BAlthough you have freed my family from their curse, nothing can take away the pain my mistakes have caused them. $B$BDelas has done well to devote herself to the Silver Hand. Do not let my past reflect poorly on her.$B$BI\'d like to follow her lead, and lend my aid to your order.',0),
(46047,'enUS','Although my recollection of recent events is still a bit hazy, the power you displayed when dispatching Rezara was something I could never forget.$B$BIt seems fitting that the council chose you as its leader in my absence.$B$BRest assured, I have no desire to challenge their decision. I owe you my life.$B$BLet me serve you and the council. There is much we can learn from each other.',0),
(46048,'enUS','Tell me, $n, are all those among your ranks as dedicated as their leader?$B$BI\'ve been reluctant to trust outsiders, but you and I aren\'t so different, are we? We\'re both willing to go to great lengths to protect the things we care about. Our goals seem to align in that regard.$B$BI would like to lend my aid to you and your hunters, if you\'ll allow it.',0),
(46049,'enUS','<Your tadpole has prepared a gift for you. What could be inside?>',0),
(46050,'enUS','Look, I may be dead and my lungs may serve no purpose, but raising Daumyr to undeath was like a breath of fresh air for me. I ask that you continue to take me under your guidance. Bring me to the battlefield again! I will scatter the bones of any demon that so much as looks at me.',0),
(46057,'enUS','You are a foolish child. You think you have great power, but you know nothing. The Doomstone should be used for the greatness it can accomplish! It will waste away sitting in the Maelstrom.$B$BPerhaps it was a mistake coming here. Nobundo requests that the Grimtotem stay. I stay for my own reasons, not because he asked. If you need me or my warriors to earn our keep, we will oblige.$B$BBut remember your place.',0),
(46058,'enUS','You made quick work of those demons, and I hope you do the same to many more. So long as the Legion extends their influence on our world, they will continue to corrupt our people as well.$B$BI would like to continue to work with you to end this madness. My blades are yours, Shadowblade.',0),
(46059,'enUS','You\'ve proven your expertise to me many times over, Shadowblade. While my colleagues have already pledged their service to you, I took a step back. Though all rogues step in the shadows, it is of vital importance that my status remains truly secret.$B$BHowever, the threat is too great. We are so close to taking the Legion down... and I want to take on a greater role in it.',0),
(46060,'enUS','You risked your life freeing those animals from a life worse than death. I commend you, $n.',0),
(46061,'enUS','Glrm. Mrr glrg.',0),
(46062,'enUS','Glrrrrms!',0),
(46064,'enUS','Mrrga mr. Gll-mrrr!',0),
(46065,'enUS','News has reached me of Agatha\'s demise, as well as her plot to infiltrate the Kirin Tor. If it weren\'t for your swift action, I fear the damage her sayaad could\'ve done would be irreparable. $B$BMy mages are working to hunt down any of Agatha\'s remaining allies, but the real victory today belongs to you, $n.$B$BThe Kirin Tor thanks you.',0),
(46069,'enUS','Highlord! I\'d like to speak with you about obtaining a special mount...',0),
(46070,'enUS','<Grayson examines the barding.>$B$BThis is... well, a good start, Highlord. But I think it will have to be strengthened a bit.',0),
(46071,'enUS','Greetings, Highlord. What can I help you with?$B$B<You explain what you need to Alard as he looks over the barding.>$B$BI see. I can certainly help you with your upgrading this, but I\'ll need a few things first.',0),
(46074,'enUS','<Grayson examines the barding.>$B$BThis is perfect. Exactly what I expected from Alard. Now that we have everything together, there is but one task left.',0),
(46078,'enUS','A bit late for the warning, eh? Still, I appreciate that we haven\'t been forgotten.',0),
(46079,'enUS','You\'ve saved many lives this day, $C. Bradensbrook thanks you.',0),
(46080,'enUS','We realize these spirits are misguided, but we have to care about the living more than the dead at this point.$B$BThe attacks should ease off for a while.',0),
(46082,'enUS','I had hoped this town had found peace after what we\'ve all been through. Somehow restless dead have been stirred into a fury. We need to stop it.',0),
(46083,'enUS','You got them! Now to upgrade your barding.$B$BNever say a blacksmith can\'t improve on a leatherworker\'s work, I always say. I mean never. I mean... well you know what I mean.',0),
(46089,'enUS','We have shown the demons why they should truly fear the darkness. Now, Lord Ravenholdt has something for you from his personal collection.',0),
(46103,'enUS','You don\'t really know if an ally is an undead pawn under the control of a dreadlord until you carve into them a bit.',0),
(46106,'enUS','That should disorganize the assault for some time, but we must get to the bottom of this. I sensed a fel taint about those leaders, did you?',0),
(46107,'enUS','The attacks on Bradensbrook should relent for now. We must still deal with Lord Erdris, and soon.',0),
(46108,'enUS','Learning more about your artifact weapon will help hasten our victory over the Legion.$B$BIf you supply me with order resources, I can provide research notes on your weapon. Read them, and learn how to take greater advantage of the power you infuse into your artifact.$B$BDeath to our enemies!',0),
(46110,'enUS','Well done, $n! Well done indeed!$B$BThe Legion will rue the day they set their sights on the land of Stormheim.',0),
(46119,'enUS','$n! Listen. You\'ve been real good to our business. REAL good. Never thought I\'d sell so many guns.$B$BWe like to reward those that patronize our establishment, so... here. Take this.$B$BSlap this puppy on your shoulderpads and go hunting for engineering supplies. You\'d be surprised how many basilisks get sprockets stuck in their gullets!',0),
(46125,'enUS','The order resources you have provided are crucial to further empowering your weapon.$B$BHere, take these notes. Read the research and apply the knowledge you have learned.$B$BOnward to victory!',0),
(46127,'enUS','So Raest has fallen, and in his hubris has taken his brother with him. I mourn for them both, but his brother most of all. $B$BKaram Magespear was truly a beacon of the Light. I only hope that the stories of his sacrifices live throughout the ages. $B$BYou have done well, $n.',0),
(46128,'enUS','I been thinkin\' more about this whole battery thing, and how the whole process is just so... wasteful.$B$BI ain\'t goin\' green or nothin\' like that - I\'m just worried about our bottom line!$B$BYou know, if one were to supercharge one of these batteries with some Blood of Sargeras, maybe cap it off with some concentrated leystone...',0),
(46129,'enUS','Learning more about your artifact weapon will sure speed up our victory over the Legion, boss.$B$BIf you supply me with order resources, I can whip up research notes on your weapon. Read \'em, and in no time you\'ll be taking greater advantage of the power you infuse into your artifact.$B$BLet\'s do this!',0),
(46130,'enUS','Learning more about your artifact weapon will help hasten our victory over the Legion.$B$BIf you supply me with order resources, I can provide research notes on your weapon. Read them, and learn how to take greater advantage of the power you infuse into your artifact.$B$BFor Azeroth!',0),
(46131,'enUS','Knowledge of your artifact is the key to bending the demons to your will.$B$BIf you supply me with order resources, I can provide research notes on your weapon. Read them, Netherlord, and the power you infuse into your artifact will magnify.$B$BYour foes will quake in fear... as it should be!',0),
(46132,'enUS','Learnin\' more about yer artifact weapon\'ll help hasten our victory over tha Legion.$B$BIf ye supply me with order resources, I can provide research notes on yer weapon. Read \'em, and learn how to take greater advantage of the power ye infuse into yer artifact.$B$BFor Azeroth!',0),
(46133,'enUS','Learning more about your artifact weapon will help hasten our victory over the Legion.$B$BIf you supply me with order resources, I can provide research notes on your weapon. Read them, and learn how to take greater advantage of the power you infuse into your artifact.$B$BLet pain and suffering fall upon our enemies!',0),
(46140,'enUS','Learning more about your artifact weapon will hasten our victory over the Legion.$B$BIf you supply me with order resources, I can provide research notes on your weapon. Read them, and learn how to take greater advantage of the power you infuse into your artifact.$B$BWe will send the Legions back to the hell that spawned them!',0),
(46141,'enUS','Learning more about your artifact weapon will help hasten our victory over the Legion.$B$BIf you supply me with order resources, I can provide research notes on your weapon. Read them, and learn how to take greater advantage of the power you infuse into your artifact.$B$BFor Azeroth!',0),
(46142,'enUS','There is power in old tales. Learning the legend of your artifact weapon will hasten our victory over the Legion.$B$BIf you supply me with order resources, I can scribe tales of might and wonder. Read them, and the power you infuse into your artifact will echo through the Halls of Valor.$B$BFor Odyn!',0),
(46143,'enUS','Learning more about your artifact weapon will help hasten our victory over the Legion.$B$BIf you supply me with order resources, I can provide research notes on your weapon. Read them, and learn how to take greater advantage of the power you infuse into your artifact.$B$BFor Azeroth!',0),
(46144,'enUS','Learning more about your artifact weapon will help hasten our victory over the Legion.$B$BIf you supply me with order resources, I can provide research notes on your weapon. Read these tales, for within them you will learn how to take greater advantage of the power you infuse into your artifact.$B$BIn stories, we find strength!',0),
(46145,'enUS','What a charming place this is. Much more hospitable than that demon-infested island.',0),
(46147,'enUS','Learning more about your artifact weapon will help speed us on the path to victory over the Legion.$B$BIf you supply me with order resources, I can provide research notes on your weapon. Read them, and learn how to take greater advantage of the power you infuse into your artifact.$B$BLet the wind guide your way!',0),
(46148,'enUS','These order resources are just the ticket for juicing up your weapon\'s power.$B$BHere, take these notes. I\'m not a big reader myself, but in this case, it\'s worth it. That artifact of yours will really get the job done.$B$BGood luck, boss!',0),
(46149,'enUS','The order resources you have provided are crucial to further empowering your weapon.$B$BHere, take these notes. Read the research and apply the knowledge you have learned.$B$BOnward to victory!',0),
(46150,'enUS','The order resources you have provided are crucial to further empowering your weapon.$B$BHere, take these notes. Read the dark secrets within and apply the knowledge you have learned.$B$BAll enemies will fall before us!',0),
(46151,'enUS','The order resources ye \'ave provided be crucial ta further empowerin\' yer weapon.$B$BTake these notes. Read tha research an\' apply tha knowledge ye \'ave learned.$B$BOnward ta vict\'ry!',0),
(46152,'enUS','The order resources you have provided are crucial to further empowering your weapon.$B$BHere, take these notes. Read the research and apply the knowledge you have learned.$B$BOnward to victory!',0),
(46153,'enUS','The order resources you have provided are crucial to further empowering your weapon.$B$BHere, take these notes. Read the research and apply the knowledge you have learned.$B$BVictory will be ours!',0),
(46154,'enUS','The order resources you have provided are crucial to further empowering your weapon.$B$BHere, take these notes. Read the research and apply the knowledge you have learned.$B$BOnward to victory!',0),
(46155,'enUS','The order resources you have provided are crucial to further empowering your weapon.$B$BHere, take these notes. Read the tales within and apply the knowledge you have learned.$B$BLet the minstrels write songs of your glory!',0),
(46156,'enUS','The order resources you have provided are crucial to further empowering your weapon.$B$BHere, take these notes. Read the research and apply the knowledge you have learned.$B$BOnward to victory!',0),
(46157,'enUS','The order resources you have provided are crucial to further empowering your weapon.$B$BHere, take these notes. Read the research and apply the knowledge you have learned.$B$BEvery good story needs a hero!',0),
(46158,'enUS','The order resources you have provided are crucial to further empowering your weapon.$B$BHere, take these notes. Read the research and apply the knowledge you have learned.$B$BMay the elements guide us to victory!',0),
(46159,'enUS','Lady S\'theno went down to lend a hand, but this sounds like it\'s getting serious!',0),
(46173,'enUS','It is good to see you again, my friend.',0),
(46177,'enUS','So Xylem has been corrupted by shadow magic and has escaped with the Focusing Iris? This is not good.$B$BThe Kirin Tor will pool our efforts with those of his apprentici-- I mean, apprentices. We must track down the archmage before he does something drastic.$B$BWe will be in touch.',0),
(46178,'enUS','We have shown the demons why they should truly fear the darkness. Now, Lord Ravenholdt has something for you from his personal collection.',0),
(46182,'enUS','Our efforts today have prevailed over the Legion\'s presence, though let us not be remiss - our journey has only just begun.',0),
(46199,'enUS','With the fall of their commander the Legion\'s presence in Azsuna will be more manageable for our defenders to make headway. For your efforts, we may see the end of these attacks once and for all.',0),
(46200,'enUS','I am relieved that you have dealt with immediate threat. We barely have enough resources for the Broken Shore as it is!$B$BStill we have something for you...',0),
(46205,'enUS','With the conduit destroyed, now may be our only chance.',0),
(46206,'enUS','This warning is an ill omen indeed, $n. It seems the fate of Azeroth is tied to that of Argus, the homeworld of the Legion.$B$BWe must uncover the Dark Titan\'s plan! I believe the Speaker\'s connection to the world soul will prove crucial to our efforts.$B$BStay vigilant, Archdruid. We must trust in Magni\'s guidance... and Azeroth\'s as well.',0),
(46207,'enUS','That was truly a grand exposition of $C skill. I was truly impressed at how you handled Asrea. She will be missed.$B$BBut now on to a grander event. The prize which you so rightfully deserve.',0),
(46208,'enUS','Battlelord $n, I have an offer you may be interested in...',0),
(46213,'enUS','You brought crystals with you? Thank the Light, that\'s just what we need!',0),
(46235,'enUS','You\'ve done so much so quickly here on the Broken Shore. Impressive, $n.',0),
(46237,'enUS','Our task will not be easy, but when this is over it is we who will be the true masters of Xoroth.',0),
(46238,'enUS','Excellent. This Unbending Potion should shore up the Felslate enough to hold the portal\'s structure, and these Chaotic Spinel crystals should focus the portal\'s magic nicely.$B$BI will set the mo\'arg to work posthaste.',0),
(46239,'enUS','I sense the fel energy emanating from the core the moment you entered Dreadscar Rift. $B$BI think this will suit our needs.',0),
(46240,'enUS','That\'s... quite a bit of blood. I am impressed, $n.$B$BI really should just start stockpiling this stuff. It has so many uses!',0),
(46242,'enUS','Long have I waited to get my hands on one of the dreadlord\'s calling stones. Were it not for our current task, we could outfit an army with dreadsteeds.$B$BHowever, this will serve a greater purpose. With the lure of this stone, Arax\'ath will not be able to restrain the Wrathsteed. So long as we can keep the portal open long enough, it will come.',0),
(46243,'enUS','The Wrathsteed is prepared for your binding, Netherlord. It will not be easy to enslave, its will is strong.$B$BI have to say, I\'m a bit jealous. Never before have I seen such a ferocious beast, our disciples have it barely held in check.',0),
(46244,'enUS','Mephistroth is dead and the Cathedral is secured, but the lower reaches of the Tomb remain in the hands of the Legion.$B$BThis is not the outcome we wanted, but this fight is far from over, $n.$B$BDo not relent. Give the Legion no quarter, no place to hide. When we are ready, we will take the Tomb and drive them from Azeroth!',0),
(46245,'enUS','Good on ya, mate! Not that there\'s a bad choice to be made, of course, but it\'s important to keep a positive attitude when surrounded by an infinite number of demons looking to kill ya.$B$BAs you gather additional supplies, come on back and I\'ll see they get assigned to the fortification of your choice.$B$BPhew! That was a mouthful, right? I\'d say it\'s time for a pint.',0),
(46246,'enUS','I have spent a lifetime hunting the wicked and making them pay for their crimes. When I strike a demon down, I feel a measure of justice has been served.$B$BYou have been an instrument of retribution this day, Huntmaster. Had you walked a different path, you might have made a worthy Warden.',0),
(46247,'enUS','A fine victory, Archdruid.$B$BBut do not grow complacent! Fight back against the Legion wherever they strike.',0),
(46248,'enUS','Step by step, we march closer to victory. We must not relent!$B$BOnly through courage and persistence will we stop the insidious evil that threatens the soul of this world.',0),
(46249,'enUS','Excellent work, Huntmaster! When this war is finally won, I believe I owe you and your order champions a banquet to honor your heroism.$B$BSay, that sounds like something that Odyn fellow would say. Not that I\'ve met him myself, of course...',0),
(46250,'enUS','We must take every opportunity to shatter the will of Kil\'jaeden\'s army.$B$BWhen they see their mightiest champions crumble to dust, they will realize that the vaunted Legion is doomed to fall.',0),
(46251,'enUS','It has been pointed out to me that I can, on occasion, get a bit carried away.$B$BThis... <clears throat> might possibly have been one of those times.$B$BA single Nethershard will suffice for my purposes. I\'m certain you can put the rest to good use.$B$BLet\'s not speak of this again.',0),
(46252,'enUS','Thinning the ranks of demons in locations like Faronaar and Felsoul Hold cuts the legs out from under the Legion.$B$BKil\'jaeden will fall!',0),
(46253,'enUS','The Pillars of Creation are in place. The Tomb of Sargeras is sealed, and Aegwynn\'s echo is at rest.$B$B<Khadgar gestures toward the sky.>$B$BUnfortunately, we do not have that luxury.$B$BThough you won a great victory this day, there is no time for revelry. The final battle awaits us. Make ready.',0),
(46258,'enUS','You have witnessed the destruction the Doomstone can wreak firsthand. You are a trusted warden of Azeroth, but even in your hands the power caused chaos and panic amongst your people. Imagine it in the control of someone with ill intent...$B$BWe cannot let that happen.$B$BWe discussed what to do with this artifact at length while we waited for you to awaken. We considered giving it a new home in one of the elemental planes, but each one provided its own danger.$B$BThere is no safer place for it than here.',0),
(46259,'enUS','You have my thanks, $n. The Moonfang family has certainly seen better days.',0),
(46260,'enUS','We\'ve been discussing your recent success, $n. We walk the shadows, and that often goes taken for granted. But without us, the Armies of Legionfall would have a great many more powerful demons to deal with.$B$BWe do not need the fame. We reap the rewards.',0),
(46266,'enUS','Your quick blades have proven your worth to the Illidari yet again, Slayer $n. We will begin the repairs to the Fel Hammer immediately. $B$BWe cannot allow the Legion to catch us with our pants down again!',0),
(46267,'enUS','Your return is triumphant indeed, Battlelord $n!$B$BUnder your leadership, the warriors of Skyhold are truly a force to be reckoned with!',0),
(46268,'enUS','<As the king examines the compass, his expression turns from recognition to sorrow.>$B$BWhen I went through my father\'s things and didn\'t find this compass, I assumed it was with him on the Broken Shore when Gul\'dan...$B$B<The king\'s voice breaks.>',0),
(46272,'enUS','You\'ve arrived at last, Huntmaster!$B$BYou may have noticed that King Anduin is conspicuous by his absence.$B$BThis is a situation that only you can rectify.',0),
(46274,'enUS','Let me guess... Genn sent you.$B$BI wonder which he\'s more concerned about... my well-being, or keeping up the appearance that everything is normal?',0),
(46275,'enUS','They\'re right. They\'re absolutely right.',0),
(46278,'enUS','You\'re an absolute natural!$B$BSay, do you mind sticking around for awhile? I could sure use a helping hand!',0),
(46282,'enUS','You have helped me more than I can say, $n. For that, you will always have my thanks.',0),
(46286,'enUS','That\'s what I\'m talkin\' about, mate!$B$BOi! Time to get to work.',0),
(46290,'enUS','We must not forget that this is a temporary measure. I cannot overstate the devastation that will ensue if Kathra\'natir escapes... $B$BStill, thanks to you, Dalaran\'s teeth are sharpened once more. Well done, Archmage $n!',0),
(46291,'enUS','Someone took something from Cookies\' cauldron? I\'ll report this to Breanni immediately. It seems the Wailing Caverns was not a singular incident. There is something big going on and I feel you have unknowingly stepped into the middle of it.',0),
(46292,'enUS','Impressive work. Here\'s the supplies I promised you. I believe that shadowy figure left it behind.',0),
(46293,'enUS','I don\'t know nothing about nothing! Better get going before my shiv finds your face! Don\'t test me, cause I ain\'t all that bright!$B$BOh, Breanni? Yeah, sure! She\'s an old friend!',0),
(46297,'enUS','Now for the main weapon.',0),
(46305,'enUS','See? Totally convinced. Let\'s take this torch down to the beacon.',0),
(46314,'enUS','Slayer $n, you\'re a sight for sore eyes.$B$BWe need to move quickly!',0),
(46316,'enUS','I remember you, $n. We met long ago within the Black Temple. How could I forget such power?$B$BIt seems fitting that the council chose you as its leader in my absence.$B$BRest assured, I have no desire to challenge their decision. I owe you my life.$B$BLet me serve you and the council. There is much we can learn from each other.',0),
(46317,'enUS','Archdruid! We don\'t have much time, the shrine burns as we speak!',0),
(46318,'enUS','The Legion will pay for what we\'ve lost today. We escaped with as many of us as we could, but too many died in vain, trying to protect the Shrine and the Idol of Aviana, which was lost anyway, thanks to that demon scum, Shadegrove.',0),
(46319,'enUS','You place the Corrupted Idol of Aviana on the pedestal.',0),
(46320,'enUS','Hmm let me take a look... Yes, I think I can counter these!',0),
(46322,'enUS','Finally... my time to shine. Let\'s do this right.',0),
(46323,'enUS','Yes... the gunpowder. It is the key to my plan!',0),
(46324,'enUS','They left with such purpose... fools.',0),
(46326,'enUS','Welcome back, Shadowblade. I assume you\'ve retrieved the gunpowder?',0),
(46327,'enUS','You are lucky that Modera contacted me for assistance. $B$BAgatha is beyond you, $C. She is beyond any of us.',0),
(46333,'enUS','Slayer $n, I have something I would like to speak with you about when you have a moment.',0),
(46334,'enUS','Never would I have thought an adult fel bat could be tamed, but your efforts seemed to have prove otherwise. This is a promising revelation for us.$B$BBut for now, let all see what you have accomplished.',0),
(46335,'enUS','Now that\'s quite the eclectic collection if I ever saw one!$B$BThese are all powerful in their own way to be sure, but none are useable for our needs. At least not in their current form.$B$BI wonder...',0),
(46336,'enUS','<You gingerly pick up the shimmering letter and open it.>',0),
(46337,'enUS','<An empty saddle sits here, as if it is waiting for your new companion.$B$BYou feel a warm kinship with the beast as you recall your meeting. and you know what you must do to call the Wolfhawk. You put your fingers to your lips...>',0),
(46338,'enUS','So word has gotten out about Ryanna already? Ha!',0),
(46339,'enUS','This appears to be some sort of attunement crystal. Perfect.',0),
(46340,'enUS','So the daughter of Skovald followed in her father\'s footsteps? A pity, but it may have been inevitable. I believe this may be the \"fall\" the scrolls mentioned.$B$BIf this is true, there may still be hope! I will work on a way to get us into the Halls of Valor to pursue this Sigryn. I will be in touch when we find a way.$B$BIn the meantime, you have done a great service to bring her this far. I would not let that go unrewarded.',0),
(46341,'enUS','Thank you for listening, and for paying for this beverage.',0),
(46342,'enUS','A senseless loss of life, and for what?$B$B<Master Bu looks heavily at the portal and shakes his head.>',0),
(46343,'enUS','These old bones just need a little rest. But we appear to be one step further on our journey.$B$BThat grummle over there looks like he could use some assistance. Why don\'t you talk to him while I get some rest?',0),
(46344,'enUS','Smelly has a new idea! Leave his pack on fire!$B$BNothing else bad happen while pack on fire! Pack on fire IS Smelly\'s new luckydo! You keep old one.$B$BOh, you looking for big tiger? Smelly saw big glowy tiger. Went towards monastery. Smelly was helpful?',0),
(46345,'enUS','I think we have stumbled upon their headquarters. Be careful in here!',0),
(46346,'enUS','I\'ve just begun my meditation, Grandmaster. But we may have another lead...',0),
(46347,'enUS','The Shado-pan appear greatful, Grandmaster.$B$BShall we cont... what is that black residue on your foot?',0),
(46348,'enUS','Greetings. It is not every day that a Grandmaster $C comes to visit me. How can I be of service?',0),
(46349,'enUS','Thank you. Allow me to search for answers for you.',0),
(46350,'enUS','It will be my honor to carry you on the ceremonial path from this shrine to the temple, as I have done for the Grandmasters before you.',0),
(46351,'enUS','What is this?$B$BThis is not just any old shield generator - it is almost... a sentient entity...$B$BAnd it is very eager for a job to do. Yes, I think it will be quite content to work with us.',0),
(46353,'enUS','Thank you for coming, Grandmaster.',0),
(46499,'enUS','Oh, look here! You went and got that treasure! Hey... You still got a spider on your shoulder.$B$BLets see what fantastic treasure you brought me... This is it? This is worthless! Here you keep it.$B$BTough break, kid. Keep at it.',0),
(46501,'enUS','You found a key in a chest? Nothing else?$B$BI\'m guessing the last guy took all the goods, then accidentally locked the key in the chest. So, you just found a key to a chest that you\'ve already looted. Fantastic work... And people say I suck at this job.',0),
(46509,'enUS','Did you bother to read the label on this potion? I\'m going to assume, no. You may find some sucker who will pay you for it.$B$BBetter luck next time kid.',0),
(46510,'enUS','It\'s... Wet. This thing is most likely worthless now.$B$BIs there a good piece of treasure on this cursed island? I may not be the brightest tool in the bag, but I\'m starting to think this place doesn\'t really fit my \"chance of death versus treasure\" ratio.',0),
(46511,'enUS','This is it? You sure you didn\'t find anything else? Like a giant pile of gold on top of a statue made of diamonds which was holding a scroll listing the combination to the vault in Ironforge? That would have been pretty sweet.$B$BOh well. I can make this into a paper weight or throw it at a squirrel.$B$BCome back tomorrow, I\'ll have another job for you.',0),
(46666,'enUS','Looks like we hit the motherlode! Now all we need is a key... Huh. Why don\'t you go work on getting some keys for these chests and I\'ll hang out with goofy-nose here.',0),
(46674,'enUS','Look at him squirm. He gave in easily!',0),
(46675,'enUS','Let me take a look at these... I think I\'ve got it!',0),
(46676,'enUS','I feel a lot better knowing we were able to save some of the other druids. We did what we could.',0),
(46677,'enUS','Revenge feels so good.$B$BBut stopping the attacks on the ancients feels even better.',0),
(46678,'enUS','Ah thank you for locating that. Let me see--we\'ll want to target the most stylish of the Nightborne... this seems like the perfect list... oh, she\'s dangerous... so\'s that one... very well. $B$BThere is a lot to do so you should get started!',0),
(46679,'enUS','Excellent, $n! Oh the things you will sew!',0),
(46680,'enUS','Excellent work, my friend! I will find an appropriate use for this as soon as I can.',0),
(46681,'enUS','The soul thread is so beautiful! I am very pleased, $n.',0),
(46682,'enUS','Ah, that is just what we need, young $R!',0),
(46683,'enUS','The cloth you\'ve created is like none I\'ve ever seen. Beautiful! $B$BTake these elements and make something wonderful with them. I will be the first to write of your accomplishments and I truly believe you will become, at last, an icon of heroic style, $n!',0),
(46684,'enUS','Ancient wisps? Beautiful! This is a strong start, $n.',0),
(46685,'enUS','The shroud is perfect, $n. Well done!',0),
(46686,'enUS','These gloves have an air of sadness about them, do they not? Regardless, thank you for restoring them and bringing them here.',0),
(46687,'enUS','The spellsash looks perfect, $n! I couldn\'t have done a better repair myself.',0),
(46688,'enUS','That is, indeed, dreadleather. Should be enough for our needs, $n. My thanks!',0),
(46689,'enUS','The Elderhide leather that you\'ve created is magnificent. Take this, and work your magic to create something of wonder and beauty. $B$BIt is an extraordinary accomplishment and you will look quite dashing--and I should know!',0),
(46690,'enUS','What a magnificent creature! Allow me to attune him to you...there! With his ancient knowledge, we are ready to begin.',0),
(46691,'enUS','The mantle looks brand new! Excellent craftsmanship, $n!',0),
(46692,'enUS','Those legplates are rather large! I\'m surprised you survived that encounter--and you\'ve refinished them beautifully!',0),
(46693,'enUS','These bracers have legends of their own--too bad we need to sacrifice them to build a proper reputation for you but we all must suffer for fashion. $B$BI would also like to personally thank you for killing Viz\'aduum. It just shouldn\'t... exist. I mean... well you know what I mean.',0),
(46694,'enUS','That should be enough Ancient Gravenscale. Well done, $n!',0),
(46695,'enUS','The Wardenscale is incredibly light yet strong--I have never seen its equal. $n, there is nothing else I can do. It is all up to you now. $B$BTake what you have earned and make wonders with it. Stylish, stylish wonders.',0),
(46696,'enUS','Ah, the book! Let\'s see... blah, blah, blah, 3 heroes... blah, blah, blah, forge 3 hammers and create the ultimate hammer... blah, blah, blah, forger will be metaphorically crushed and possibly literally killed under impossible expectations, etc. Looks good! $B$BIt appears I can help you find what remains of the armor and weapons of these heroes and these incredible materials can be used to make amazing things!',0),
(46697,'enUS','What a remarkable metal! I feel like it tingles just to hold it. Incredible!',0),
(46698,'enUS','It is a powerful magic that kept the draconic slag hot so many years later. Is it the will of the Dragonhunter? Was dragon fire even more dangerous in ancient times? Or was it actually the dragon Neltharion, whom you know as Deathwing, whom she fought back then? $B$BI wonder if I shall ever find out. $B$BWell done! The hammer is extraordinary.',0),
(46699,'enUS','The hammer is perfect but rather cold. I do respect your craftsmanship!',0),
(46700,'enUS','That will be enough for our needs. Good work, $n!',0),
(46701,'enUS','The Hammer is possibly the most perfect item you have ever forged. With this, you will create armor of such style and taste that you will become a figure of legends. $B$BI\'m proud of you, $n. I\'m so happy you will finally start to look good.',0),
(46705,'enUS','Revenge is so sweet. Thank you.',0),
(46719,'enUS','Ah, Deathlord, you have returned.$B$BI have inscribed a series of frozen runes above Acherus. Once attuned, you will be able to communicate with the Lich King more... completely.$B$BHe will be able to show you things he could not before.$B$B<Amal\'thazad emits a horrible, rasping noise, that you can only assume is a chuckle.>',0),
(46722,'enUS','This is a catastrophe! Something must be wrong with my rabbit dimension!$B$BOkay, I\'m gonna need your help again.',0),
(46723,'enUS','I can\'t believe a wolf got in my pocket dimension! That\'s the last time I order a crate of rabbits from Moonbrook!$B$BI owe you a solid, bud. Here, take my spare hat. Just don\'t go trying to muscle in on my Dalaran business, got it?',0),
(46724,'enUS','You know, you\'re a useful fella to have around, $n. $B$BTell ya what, I think I\'ll accompany you on your adventures. Seems to be good gold in it, and I think it\'ll be a good way to scout out some new business opportunities around the Broken Isles.$B$BWhat do you say?',0),
(46725,'enUS','I alwayss hated heightss. I\'m glad you\'re the one who has to do the dirty work.',0),
(46730,'enUS','Our forces are assembled. We are ready to begin.',0),
(46732,'enUS','Turalyon yet lives! Perhaps there is still hope after all.',0),
(46734,'enUS','Mephistroth is on the run, and we have a foothold here at Deliverance Point.$B$BA good start, I\'d say, though we still have much to do.',0),
(46743,'enUS','Champion, your help to our people has far exceeded any of our expectations, and has provided us some much needed breathing space.$B$BPlease, take these supplies to aid you in the war against the Legion. With your continued aid, we should be able to gather more and prepare them for you.',0),
(46744,'enUS','Excellent! Your artifact is as powerful as you can make it... for now.$B$BWe are working on a solution for that, but in the meantime you should continue your efforts on the Broken Shore.',0),
(46745,'enUS','Prince Farondis has asked me to thank you for your continued efforts to aid our lands.$B$BPlease take these supplies as a token of our gratitude, and a promise of more to come, should you continue to help us.',0),
(46746,'enUS','Greetings, little hero.$B$BThe mighty Odyn has proclaimed that you should receive these gifts of war. At every turn you continue to prove your valor and your efforts to aid the Valarjar have not gone unnoticed. $B$BFor the Valarjar! For Odyn! For $n!',0),
(46747,'enUS','Hero! $B$BYour dedication to defending Val\'sharah has given us a much needed respite from the vile influence of the Legion. We were able to scavenge some supplies as a result of your efforts. $B$BHere, take them and know that, should you continue to aid us, we will set aside more rewards such as these as we find them.',0),
(46748,'enUS','Outlander, I have some supplies for you. These goods are yours, earned by your continued efforts to our forces here in Suramar.$B$BI shall set aside similar treasures should you choose to aid our people more.$B$BYou have my deepest thanks.',0),
(46749,'enUS','Your dedication to our efforts has yielded results. We have supplies for you.$B$BContinue your dedication and there will be more.',0),
(46765,'enUS','This scroll, fascinating... this confirms our concerns about indirect Legion threats. We must return to Dalaran, $n!',0),
(46769,'enUS','Fine work. It\'s important to keep powerful treasures out of demon hands.$B$BThere are more ways to undermine the Legion\'s agenda than simply killing demons... although there\'s a lot to be said for good old-fashioned violence.',0),
(46772,'enUS','Our grand efforts have resulted in a boon which all can leverage in the coming days.',0),
(46773,'enUS','Our grand efforts have resulted in a boon which all can leverage in the coming days.',0),
(46774,'enUS','Our grand efforts have resulted in a boon which all can leverage in the coming days.',0),
(46777,'enUS','Shadowblade, thanks to your efforts, our forces have been able to secure additional resources from the battlefield.$B$BThe more you continue to dominate the battlefield the more resources our forces can spare.',0),
(46778,'enUS','Our power grows.',0),
(46779,'enUS','Our power grows.',0),
(46780,'enUS','Our power grows.',0),
(46781,'enUS','Our power grows.',0),
(46782,'enUS','Our power grows.',0),
(46783,'enUS','Our power grows.',0),
(46784,'enUS','Our power grows.',0),
(46785,'enUS','Our power grows.',0),
(46786,'enUS','Our power grows.',0),
(46788,'enUS','Our power grows.',0),
(46789,'enUS','Our power grows.',0),
(46791,'enUS','Thank you for coming, Farseer.',0),
(46792,'enUS','Now that the council is reunited, the plane of air shall flow as one again!$B$BI believe Windlord Thunderaan has a reward waiting for you.',0),
(46794,'enUS','Greetings Deathlord $n.$B$BFor some time now you have been a Paragon to our prince and to our people. Our gratitude goes beyond anything mere words can define.$B$BTake these trophies as a token of our gratitude and a share in the spoils of war. The more you aid us, the more we can provide you.',0),
(46796,'enUS','Greetings Huntmaster $n.$B$BFor some time now you have been a Paragon to our people. Our gratitude goes beyond anything mere words can define.$B$BTake these trophies as a token of our gratitude and a share in the spoils of war. The more you aid us, the more we can provide you.',0),
(46797,'enUS','Greetings Highlord $n.$B$BFor some time now you have been a Paragon to Nature and to our people. Our gratitude goes beyond anything mere words can define.$B$BTake these trophies as a token of our gratitude and a share in the spoils of war. The more you aid us, the more we can provide you.',0),
(46798,'enUS','Greetings Highlord $n.$B$BFor some time now you have been a Paragon to Odyn and a hero to the Valarjar. Our gratitude goes beyond anything mere words can define.$B$BTake these trophies as a token of our gratitude and a share in the spoils of war. The more you aid us, the more we can provide you.',0),
(46799,'enUS','Greetings outlander, liberator, Huntmaster, friend.$B$B.Our gratitude goes beyond anything mere words can define.$B$BTake these trophies as a token of our gratitude and a share in the spoils of war. The more you aid us, the more we can provide you.',0),
(46800,'enUS','Greetings Huntmaster.$B$BFor some time now you have been a Paragon in your efforts against the Legion and your aid of the Wardens. Our gratitude goes beyond anything mere words can define.$B$BTake these trophies as a token of our gratitude and a share in the spoils of war. The more you aid us, the more we can provide you.',0),
(46802,'enUS','Greetings, Deathlord.$B$BFor some time now you have been a paragon in your efforts against the Legion, the beacon that unites our armies together. Our gratitude goes beyond anything mere words can define.$B$BTake these trophies as a token of our gratitude and a share in the spoils of war. The more you aid us, the more we can provide you.',0),
(46804,'enUS','Glad I could share the Hammerbeard System of Style and Taste with you. Are you ready to work for your legacy in your chosen profession?',0),
(46805,'enUS','When we faced the Deceiver, millennia of rage flooded my heart. Hatred took hold, blinding me to every thought but revenge.$B$BThankfully the Light helped me see that the future must not be defined by vengeance, but by hope. Your courage showed me that as well, $n.$B$BIn those last moments of Kil\'jaeden\'s life, I had to let go of the past. Not only for my own sake, but for the memory of my son.$B$BMy spirit and mind are clear and focused. Now we take the fight to Sargeras himself. Now we end the Legion.',0),
(46809,'enUS','What have you brought today, Deathlord?$B$B<Illanna examines the ancient tome.>$B$BThis book... it changes everything!',0),
(46810,'enUS','If you find any other unwanted spoils of war, obliterate them at the forge and I can help you find something more desirable.',0),
(46813,'enUS','<A crack in the ice beneath the snow, it\'s very deep. You feel the unholy power surge within you, this would be the ideal location to unleash the energy to raise the dragon.>',0),
(46815,'enUS','It is as if the battle never ceased. How long have they suffered like this?',0),
(46816,'enUS','Lothraxion is an old friend, and a noble warrior. We are fortunate to have him among us.',0),
(46818,'enUS','The tide is turning. We must press forward.',0),
(46827,'enUS','We\'ve been discussing your recent success, $n. We walk the shadows, and that often goes taken for granted. But without us, the Armies of Legionfall would have a great many more powerful demons to deal with.$B$BWe do not need the fame. We reap the rewards.',0),
(46832,'enUS','Chambers sent you? He can down a tankard with the best of \'em, I\'ll give him that. But if he says I owe him anything, he\'s a liar!$B$BDon\'t you worry, my drakes and I will hold the point here. But more of this shore will need to be secured before your campaign can find victory.',0),
(46834,'enUS','I cannot right every wrong that happened here, but this is a comfort nonetheless.$B$BThank you, $n.',0),
(46839,'enUS','So it begins.',0),
(46840,'enUS','Hatuun\'s people will greatly appreciate what you\'ve done for them.',0),
(46841,'enUS','Now that their lords have been reduced to ash, we may strike at the heart of their power.',0),
(46842,'enUS','This victory is only the first link in a long chain, Archdruid.',0),
(46843,'enUS','Our absence has wounded Arator. We knew it would. But we had to know that he was safe while we fought the Legion.$B$BNow that we are reunited, I will not let us be separated again.',0),
(46845,'enUS','The Illidari don\'t waste time on congratulations. There is more to do, and you\'re the one to do it.$B$BGet a move on.',0),
(46904,'enUS','Well done, I can now provide you with a boon that will grant you a benefit while the Command Center is activated.',0),
(46924,'enUS','We must warn the Dreamgrove of what is happening.',0),
(46935,'enUS','The Legion uses these beacons to communicate with their fleet up above. If we were to find more of these...',0),
(46938,'enUS','Welcome to Argus, homeworld of the Burning Legion.',0),
(46941,'enUS','The way forward is clear, and we have the Army of the Light at our side.',0),
(46946,'enUS','If you find any other unwanted spoils of war, obliterate them at the forge and I can help you find something more desirable.',0),
(46997,'enUS','Well done, I can now provide you with a boon that will grant you a benefit while the Command Center is activated.',0),
(46998,'enUS','Well done, I can now provide you with a boon that will grant you a benefit while the Command Center is activated.',0),
(46999,'enUS','Well done, I can now provide you with a boon that will grant you a benefit while the Command Center is activated.',0),
(47000,'enUS','<Khadgar gives you a knowing nod.>$B$BI\'m glad you came, Archdruid.',0),
(47003,'enUS','A bit late for the warning, eh? Still, I appreciate that we haven\'t been forgotten.',0),
(47004,'enUS','A bit late for the warning, eh? Still, I appreciate that we haven\'t been forgotten.',0),
(47005,'enUS','A bit late for the warning, eh? Still, I appreciate that we haven\'t been forgotten.',0),
(47006,'enUS','A bit late for the warning, eh? Still, I appreciate that we haven\'t been forgotten.',0),
(47007,'enUS','Well done, I can now provide you with a boon that will grant you a benefit while the Mage Tower is activated.',0),
(47008,'enUS','Well done, I can now provide you with a boon that will grant you a benefit while the Mage Tower is activated.',0),
(47009,'enUS','Well done, I can now provide you with a boon that will grant you a benefit while the Mage Tower is activated.',0),
(47010,'enUS','Well done, I can now provide you with a boon that will grant you a benefit while the Mage Tower is activated.',0),
(47012,'enUS','Well done, I can now provide you with a boon that will grant you a benefit while the Nether Disruptor is activated.',0),
(47014,'enUS','Well done, I can now provide you with a boon that will grant you a benefit while the Nether Disruptor is activated.',0),
(47015,'enUS','Well done, I can now provide you with a boon that will grant you a benefit while the Nether Disruptor is activated.',0),
(47016,'enUS','Well done, I can now provide you with a boon that will grant you a benefit while the Nether Disruptor is activated.',0),
(47017,'enUS','Our traders on the front lines were able to procure items of incredible rarity. Please use this wisely.',0),
(47018,'enUS','Thank you for coming. I am glad you are treating this threat seriously.',0),
(47019,'enUS','Thank you for coming. I am glad you are treating this threat seriously.',0),
(47020,'enUS','Thank you for coming. I am glad you are treating this threat seriously.',0),
(47022,'enUS','You - I\'ve seen you out on the isles.$B$BWe need to move quickly!',0),
(47023,'enUS','You - I\'ve seen you out on the isles.$B$BWe need to move quickly!',0),
(47024,'enUS','You - I\'ve seen you out on the isles.$B$BWe need to move quickly!',0),
(47025,'enUS','You - I\'ve seen you out on the isles.$B$BWe need to move quickly!',0),
(47027,'enUS','Thank you for coming. I have something I\'d like to show you.',0),
(47030,'enUS','Thank you for coming. I have something I\'d like to show you.',0),
(47031,'enUS','Thank you for coming. I have something I\'d like to show you.',0),
(47032,'enUS','Thank you for coming. I have something I\'d like to show you.',0),
(47033,'enUS','Thank you for coming. I have something I\'d like to show you.',0),
(47034,'enUS','Thank you for coming. I have something I\'d like to show you.',0),
(47035,'enUS','Thank you for coming. I have something I\'d like to show you.',0),
(47037,'enUS','You come from the Kirin Tor? So you\'ll help me find my brother?',0),
(47039,'enUS','You come from the Kirin Tor? So you\'ll help me find my brother?',0),
(47040,'enUS','I have bent this to my will, I have drained its power, and summoned a Seal. Would you like it?',0),
(47041,'enUS','You come from the Kirin Tor? So you\'ll help me find my brother?',0),
(47042,'enUS','You come from the Kirin Tor? So you\'ll help me find my brother?',0),
(47043,'enUS','So someone stole the Focusing Iris and you suspect Xylem might be the culprit? You may be right. $B$BIt is no secret that the archmage has been seeking artifacts of late. However, after the discovery of an ancient grimoire in the Legashi ruins, Xylem has become... unstable. I fear the grimoire may be stealing his mind.$B$BI can help you gain audience with the archmage. With any luck, you can reclaim the Iris peacefully.',0),
(47045,'enUS','The Disruptor continues to bend to my will! I will be unstoppable!',0),
(47046,'enUS','So someone stole the Focusing Iris and you suspect Xylem might be the culprit? You may be right. $B$BIt is no secret that the archmage has been seeking artifacts of late. However, after the discovery of an ancient grimoire in the Legashi ruins, Xylem has become... unstable. I fear the grimoire may be stealing his mind.$B$BI can help you gain audience with the archmage. With any luck, you can reclaim the Iris peacefully.',0),
(47047,'enUS','So someone stole the Focusing Iris and you suspect Xylem might be the culprit? You may be right. $B$BIt is no secret that the archmage has been seeking artifacts of late. However, after the discovery of an ancient grimoire in the Legashi ruins, Xylem has become... unstable. I fear the grimoire may be stealing his mind.$B$BI can help you gain audience with the archmage. With any luck, you can reclaim the Iris peacefully.',0),
(47048,'enUS','So someone stole the Focusing Iris and you suspect Xylem might be the culprit? You may be right. $B$BIt is no secret that the archmage has been seeking artifacts of late. However, after the discovery of an ancient grimoire in the Legashi ruins, Xylem has become... unstable. I fear the grimoire may be stealing his mind.$B$BI can help you gain audience with the archmage. With any luck, you can reclaim the Iris peacefully.',0),
(47049,'enUS','Yes, outsider? What business do you have here?',0),
(47050,'enUS','Yes, outsider? What business do you have here?',0),
(47051,'enUS','Yes, outsider? What business do you have here?',0),
(47052,'enUS','Yes, outsider? What business do you have here?',0),
(47054,'enUS','I am... spent. I fear I have gone too far. Here, take this final Seal.',0),
(47055,'enUS','So it seems that Levia has fallen under the spell of a succubus\' seduction. I fear her time alone as an outcast must have left her vulnerable to such tactics. I cannot help but feel some guilt for her turning down this path.$B$BIn any case, Levia is in great danger. She must be found!',0),
(47056,'enUS','So it seems that Levia has fallen under the spell of a succubus\' seduction. I fear her time alone as an outcast must have left her vulnerable to such tactics. I cannot help but feel some guilt for her turning down this path.$B$BIn any case, Levia is in great danger. She must be found!',0),
(47057,'enUS','So it seems that Levia has fallen under the spell of a succubus\' seduction. I fear her time alone as an outcast must have left her vulnerable to such tactics. I cannot help but feel some guilt for her turning down this path.$B$BIn any case, Levia is in great danger. She must be found!',0),
(47058,'enUS','So it seems that Levia has fallen under the spell of a succubus\' seduction. I fear her time alone as an outcast must have left her vulnerable to such tactics. I cannot help but feel some guilt for her turning down this path.$B$BIn any case, Levia is in great danger. She must be found!',0),
(47059,'enUS','So it seems that Levia has fallen under the spell of a succubus\' seduction. I fear her time alone as an outcast must have left her vulnerable to such tactics. I cannot help but feel some guilt for her turning down this path.$B$BIn any case, Levia is in great danger. She must be found!',0),
(47066,'enUS','<Velen peers at you, troubled.>',0),
(47067,'enUS','This tome is fascinating! It appears to seek out any and all knowledge that it does not already possess.$B$BI\'d wager an experienced researcher could direct it to locate specific knowledge.$B$BHmm, that gives me an idea...',0),
(47069,'enUS','What have you brought today, Grandmaster?$B$B<Cho examines the ancient tome.>$B$BThis book... it changes everything!',0),
(47070,'enUS','What have you brought today, Archmage?$B$B<Edirah examines the ancient tome.>$B$BThis book... it changes everything!',0),
(47071,'enUS','What have you brought today, Highlord?$B$B<Elda examines the ancient tome.>$B$BThis book... it changes everything!',0),
(47072,'enUS','What have you brought today, Battlelord?$B$B<Fjornson examines the ancient tome.>$B$BThis book... it changes everything!',0),
(47073,'enUS','What have you brought today, Huntmaster?$B$B<Holt examines the ancient tome.>$B$BThis book... it changes everything!',0),
(47074,'enUS','What have you brought today, Farseer?$B$B<Gorma examines the ancient tome.>$B$BThis book... it changes everything!',0),
(47075,'enUS','What have you brought today, Archdruid?$B$B<Celadine examines the ancient tome.>$B$BThis book... it changes everything!',0),
(47076,'enUS','What have you brought today, Netherlord?$B$B<Mile examines the ancient tome.>$B$BThis book... it changes everything!',0),
(47077,'enUS','What have you brought today, High $C?$B$B$B$BThis book... it changes everything!',0),
(47078,'enUS','What have you brought today, Slayer?$B$B<Vahu examines the ancient tome.>$B$BThis book... it changes everything!',0),
(47079,'enUS','What have you brought today, Shadowblade?$B$B<Filius examines the ancient tome.>$B$BThis book... it changes everything!',0),
(47097,'enUS','This place is filled with indescribable horrors. To think... I was blind to all of this pain and suffering.',0),
(47100,'enUS','<The broken peers suspiciously at his surroundings, avoiding eye contact with you.>',0),
(47101,'enUS','What is this... a sermon? Fascinating.',0),
(47102,'enUS','You\'ve found one of our scouting reports? It was overdue, and I feared it had been intercepted by the enemy.$B$B<The captain looks over the letter.>$B$BYes, this is what I\'ve been expecting. The Legion is planning something and this is the breakthrough we\'ve been looking for!',0),
(47104,'enUS','High Inquisitor Raalgar? A fearsome creature but he has been held securely in the Arcatraz at Tempest Keep for a very long time. $B$BIf the Legion plans to free him then they must know that he is particularly dangerous to us.',0),
(47112,'enUS','Thank you, $n. A peaceful rest is all we have to offer those who have made the ultimate sacrifice for the Alliance... for Azeroth.',0),
(47114,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47115,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47116,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47117,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47118,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47119,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47120,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47121,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47122,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47123,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47124,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47125,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47126,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47127,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47128,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47129,'enUS','Were you able to overcome the Tomb of Sargeras?',0),
(47134,'enUS','You did your best, $n, but the demons won this round.$B$BIt won\'t take Raalgar long to gather his power to attack us. But I have learned the source of his immortality while you were gone!',0),
(47137,'enUS','Another powerful ally recruited to our cause!$B$BYou have bolstered our strength against the Legion once more, $n.',0),
(47139,'enUS','Even the mightiest demons unleashed by the Sentinax have fallen before you.$B$BGood. The Legion will be driven from our world, no matter what it takes.',0),
(47148,'enUS','Even I didn\'t see that coming.',0),
(47180,'enUS','I can feel the Void\'s influence retreating. Perhaps now we can find out what happened here.',0),
(47182,'enUS','You are a true hero, $n. Even though the demons freed Raalgar and thought him immortal, he was no match for you! Perhaps the Fel Heart will be of use to you. It is now available in the Matrix Core.',0),
(47183,'enUS','I should have seen this coming.',0),
(47184,'enUS','As I said, the Void\'s influence is rarely peaceful. We must press on.',0),
(47202,'enUS','<Velen listens closely to your words as you tell him of King Anduin\'s plan.>$B$BThe Broken Shore is a dangerous place... far too dangerous to travel alone. But perhaps this journey is necessary for Anduin to find peace.$B$BWhen the moment is right, I\'ll inform King Greymane of Anduin\'s departure. Until then, go and see that Anduin is not alone on the Broken Shore. I trust that you will return him safely.',0),
(47203,'enUS','<Alleria seems momentarily speechless.>',0),
(47217,'enUS','We buy time but nothing more.',0),
(47218,'enUS','It is good to know we can share a common goal. Perhaps I will find some use for your kind yet.',0),
(47219,'enUS','<Alleria takes the heart in her hands.>$B$BThis is the next step, $n. Thank you for bringing me to this point.',0),
(47220,'enUS','What is it you bring, $n?$B$B$B$BIntriguing...',0),
(47221,'enUS','I\'m glad you were among those called for the expedition to Argus. There will be plenty of fighting ahead.',0),
(47222,'enUS','May the Light protect us all this day.',0),
(47223,'enUS','Thank the Light you have arrived.',0),
(47224,'enUS','I have waited many years for this day.$B$BBehold the triumph of the draenei, the Vindicaar!',0),
(47238,'enUS','This is grave news indeed. It would be wise to follow Alleria\'s lead from here.',0),
(47251,'enUS','$n, you\'re here. You must have received my letter.',0),
(47252,'enUS','$n, you\'re here. You must have received my letter.',0),
(47253,'enUS','Let us use this moment to reflect upon the past, lest we forget the lessons it teaches us, and doom ourselves to repeat it once more.',0),
(47254,'enUS','Let us use this moment to reflect upon the past, lest we forget the lessons it teaches us, and doom ourselves to repeat it once more.',0),
(47287,'enUS','Light\'s Judgment will now fire on your command when you use the Matrix Uplink. $B$BPerhaps you will find more objects that we can link into the Matrix on your travels. I have routed enough energy to that part of the Core to handle anything that you can link into it. $B$BGo well, my friend.',0),
(47330,'enUS','This warning is an ill omen indeed, $n. It seems the fate of Azeroth is tied to that of Argus, the homeworld of the Legion.$B$BWe must uncover the Dark Titan\'s plan! I believe the Speaker\'s connection to the world soul will prove crucial to our efforts.$B$BStay vigilant, Huntmaster. We must trust in Magni\'s guidance... and Azeroth\'s as well.',0),
(47416,'enUS','I worried for L\'ura, but this is... unthinkable.$B$BHow she must have suffered...',0),
(47430,'enUS','<Makkaw seems very pleased about what you have learned.>',0),
(47431,'enUS','We\'ve secured a foothold. Good.$B$BNow we take the fight to them!',0),
(47473,'enUS','<Turalyon listens in grim silence.>',0),
(47508,'enUS','We may be grounded, but that does not mean they have to rule the skies!',0),
(47523,'enUS','What\'s this, $n?$B$B$B$B$B$BThese are the plans for the raid on Mardum, were we too late?$B$BWhat\'s strange, is the new plan seems better than the original! It\'s unlikely this is the Legion\'s doing, Illidan surely would have detected any fel manipulation. So if not the Legion, who is behind this?',0),
(47526,'enUS','<The panel is now pulsing a soft golden glow. According to Romuul, activating it should teleport the cannon to the Vindicaar.>',0),
(47541,'enUS','You fought well. The Light shines brighter, thanks to your efforts.',0),
(47543,'enUS','That didn\'t go so great, did it? Maybe next time.',0),
(47545,'enUS','I guess we have plenty of leads to follow up on.$B$BWow, whoever wants to kill me really thought this through!',0),
(47550,'enUS','Fifteen minutes isn\'t a whole lot of time. We\'re going to have to move quickly.',0),
(47554,'enUS','Skara and Brae gave their lives to get us this information and the codebook. Their sacrifice will not be forgotten.$B$BNow, let us decipher the orders and see what the Legion is up to.',0),
(47557,'enUS','Yeeeeeowch! It\'s hot! What could it possibly... oh, yeah, that makes sense.',0),
(47558,'enUS','A chronoshard, you say? I know what to do with those.',0),
(47559,'enUS','Hand over that chronoshard, $n. If you don\'t mind.',0),
(47560,'enUS','I hate when they get all chilly like this.',0),
(47589,'enUS','We may yet stand a chance.',0),
(47591,'enUS','See, I told ya it be a great idea!',0),
(47592,'enUS','Ooh, ooh, lemme see!',0),
(47594,'enUS','Dis be da best day. I\'m going ta fleece dat Baron so hard his eyes be covered in more wool than a flock of sheep.',0),
(47595,'enUS','Be you sure ya wanna do dis? I got other wares that be much more interestin\' and next week I be needin\' more of these.',0),
(47603,'enUS','You really don\'t see it? I can sense the magic in their pockets!',0),
(47604,'enUS','Fantastic, simply fantastic. This will be a profitable partnership, my puny associate.',0),
(47605,'enUS','I entrust you with my lamp. May our partnership be fruitful.',0),
(47606,'enUS','Yes, yes, YES! Do you see the power radiating from the lamp? I can sense objects of great power that were concealed even from my mighty eyes.',0),
(47607,'enUS','You\'ve done it! My lamp has never shone brighter. I shall continue to grant you coins, but I shall have to find new uses for the magic you provide.',0),
(47627,'enUS','It seems we underestimated the Legion\'s cunning.',0),
(47641,'enUS','This must be it.',0),
(47642,'enUS','I think this is the spot.',0),
(47643,'enUS','Based on the clues the ancients gave us, this must be the spot. It HAS to be!$B$BLet\'s do this, $n!',0),
(47644,'enUS','I\'m not a big fan of dreadlords, but I think you and I can handle one if we stick together. You ready, $n?',0),
(47645,'enUS','I sense something... bad.',0),
(47652,'enUS','Light be praised! This was a dark day, and many lives were lost. $B$BBut the Army endures. The Light Mother\'s prophecy will be fulfilled.$B$BAll is as it was meant to be.',0),
(47653,'enUS','The Army endures. The Light Mother\'s prophecy will be fulfilled.$B$BAll is as it was meant to be.',0),
(47654,'enUS','It is done. My heart mourns the loss of L\'ura, but at least you brought her peace.$B$BOnce the Crown is in place, the Vindicaar will stand against the Legion\'s vile assault. Antorus will fall!',0),
(47663,'enUS','Oh, is it time?',0),
(47685,'enUS','Oh. You were successful.$B$BSurprising.',0),
(47686,'enUS','This place has its share of secrets. Thankfully, I know enough of them to get us started.',0),
(47687,'enUS','I must admit, I am impressed.',0),
(47688,'enUS','I had not imagined the final product to be so... sticky.$B$B<Y\'mera wipes her hands on her robes.>$B$BIt will do.',0),
(47689,'enUS','You may be worthy of the Conservatory\'s secrets, if you survive that long.',0),
(47690,'enUS','I have never felt power like this before...$B$B<Y\'mera handles the shard cautiously.>$B$BWe should get this to Velen as soon as we can.',0),
(47691,'enUS','You came upon me in a moment of reflection.$B$B<Velen peers at you with a tired expression.>$B$BThere is no time for such sentiment. We must press on.',0),
(47709,'enUS','One small step for $n, one giant leap for gnomekind!',0),
(47725,'enUS','With the remnants of this seal, we can dispel the wards and enter my sanctum.',0),
(47726,'enUS','With the remnants of this seal, we can dispel the wards and enter my sanctum.',0),
(47727,'enUS','With the remnants of this seal, we can dispel the wards and enter my sanctum.',0),
(47743,'enUS','I did not expect this of Xe\'ra. Nor could I have foreseen Illidan\'s reaction.$B$BWe must ensure these events do not crush the spirits of our allies.',0),
(47744,'enUS','The smoke and the meat are for me. The flowers, on the other hand, are for the kids at the orphanage down the street.',0),
(47745,'enUS','These are from Emery, I assume?$B$B<Meliana blushes.>$B$BThat dummy. Gotta admire his persistence, though...',0),
(47746,'enUS','I don\'t know how long we\'ll need to stay holed up in the orphanage, but there\'s no way I\'m letting the kids out while our prince walks the streets like some sort of madman.',0),
(47747,'enUS','This\'ll do, $C.$B$BTake this key. You\'ve earned it.',0),
(47750,'enUS','From the kids, you say?$B$B<Emery struggles to conceal a smile as he pockets the jerky.>',0),
(47754,'enUS','Excellent. The path is clear.',0),
(47771,'enUS','We\'re under too much pressure here. And it\'s so close to us...',0),
(47772,'enUS','You did it! Now hurry along... if I remember this correctly, you don\'t have much time left!',0),
(47773,'enUS','You did it! Now hurry along... if I remember this correctly, you don\'t have much time left!',0),
(47790,'enUS','I\'ve managed to stabilize the mixture without diminishing its potency. No simple task, mind you, and I do hope you will appreciate the hard work it took to get this far.$B$BI feel a great sense of unease regarding what might have been the source of this disruption. One would have expected that releasing Aman\'thul\'s power would bring harmony, not chaos.',0),
(47791,'enUS','Maddening! I am no closer to a breakthrough on this matter. Such a failure is unacceptable!$B$B<Vridiel breathes deeply and composes himself.>$B$BThank you, $n. I must not let this setback deter me from further attempts. Please, take this. You will no doubt find a use for it.',0),
(47793,'enUS','This is worrisome. Gul\'dan\'s defeat may have disrupted forces far more fundamental than anyone realized. $B$BHmm... perhaps we can turn that to our advantage.',0),
(47807,'enUS','It was a dreadlord? That\'s... unusual. I mean, I know we\'re in Northrend and everything, so risen skeletons aren\'t all that rare, but demons?$B$BOh well! Thanks for taking the time to calm my worries.',0),
(47808,'enUS','You have my thanks, $R.$B$BI know that you are here today in service to the Bronze Dragonflight. Perhaps this gift will aid you in your journeys.',0),
(47809,'enUS','Your assistance is appreciated.',0),
(47810,'enUS','With your assistance, the ancients have fallen back into their restful slumber. Thank you, $R.',0),
(47835,'enUS','I knew you would be among those called to fight. It will be an honor to fight by your side.',0),
(47851,'enUS','A simple exchange with complex results. That\'s the art of doing business.',0),
(47853,'enUS','<Velen stares at the shattered statue before him and says nothing.>',0),
(47854,'enUS','If I have learned anything about the Legion, it is that we have no other option but to fight back.$B$BIt was a pleasure to have you at my side.',0),
(47855,'enUS','<Prophet Velen peers solemnly at you.>$B$BThank you.',0),
(47856,'enUS','It is done. This one wrong, of many, is finally set to rights.',0),
(47864,'enUS','A simple exchange with complex results. That\'s the art of doing business.',0),
(47865,'enUS','A simple exchange with complex results. That\'s the art of doing business.',0),
(47867,'enUS','May the Light protect us all this day.',0),
(47882,'enUS','Yes, excellent. The conduits are back online.$B$BThe construct however is proving a little more difficult to awaken than I had hoped.',0),
(47883,'enUS','Prepare yourself, stranger.',0),
(47889,'enUS','Thank ye fer joinin\' me, lad. There\'s somethin\' ye have to see.',0),
(47890,'enUS','I don\'t know how Sargeras managed to raise Aggramar, but it\'s bad news for us, believe you me.',0),
(47891,'enUS','What did Magni have to show you?',0),
(47892,'enUS','If we do not act quickly, the demons stationed here are more than enough to overwhelm us.',0),
(47895,'enUS','I\'m going to have to go back to the drawing board!',0),
(47904,'enUS','We\'ve stopped all four attacks from the dragonshrines - but the timelines are still incorrect. I\'m still being assassinated, elsewhere, at the same time.$B$BLooks like our work isn\'t done yet, $n!',0),
(47906,'enUS','We\'ve done it! The timelines are exactly as they\'re supposed to be again. With me, alive.',0),
(47967,'enUS','With these new steeds our forces stand a chance.',0),
(47986,'enUS','Perfect! Thank you, $n.',0),
(47987,'enUS','Thank you, $n. Your actions deny the Legion power and grant the dead the peace they deserve.',0),
(47988,'enUS','Now that their forces are in disarray, let us proceed.',0),
(47989,'enUS','Impressive. Without the shivarra bolstering their strength we just might stand a chance.',0),
(47990,'enUS','Yes! This is it!',0),
(47991,'enUS','No war is won by a single act, but without the spires protecting them the rest of the hold will fall as well.',0),
(47992,'enUS','Well fought! Now for the commander.',0),
(47993,'enUS','By the Light...',0),
(47994,'enUS','Now that it has been thoroughly tested, I will direct our artificers to energize the warframe once more so that you may call it into battle. If you wish, you may select it at the Matrix Core at your leisure.',0),
(47995,'enUS','Fareeya\'s forces are the best the Army of the Light has to offer. Our mission is that much more likely to succeed with them at our side.',0),
(48002,'enUS','You\'ve found some! These will certainly be enough to get us by for a good while longer.$B$BAs promised, here is a recipe for one of the potions I brew to help in our fight against the Legion.',0),
(48013,'enUS','You\'re an honorable ally, $n. Thank you for helping us.$B$BAs promised, here is the recipe for the potion.',0),
(48016,'enUS','And there you have it! I believe this will be far more useful for you in your fight against the Legion.$B$BAllow me to explain how it\'s done...',0),
(48021,'enUS','Despite her troubles, this has been a welcome reminder that, although our battle with the Legion remains at the forefront of our concerns, the rest of the world does not simply wait for us.',0),
(48027,'enUS','So you were trying to gather astral glory I see. Yes, there is a method to doing it correctly.$B$BThe flower has a power to it, allowing it to protect itself from anything it thinks may seek to destroy it. If it feels truly threatened, it extinguishes itself.$B$BYou mustn\'t try to pick it with intent to harm, but to protect. It\'s an unfortunate irony as we eventually destroy it in the process of making items with it.$B$BHowever, this deception is necessary for it to yield itself to you.',0),
(48028,'enUS','Indeed, the newer blooms are particularly stubborn and would rather give up their life than live in servitude to those who pick them.$B$BTo handle the herb in this form, one must coax the herb into submitting, as it can\'t quite fully read the intentions of those who wish to gather it.',0),
(48029,'enUS','I see the glory has come to trust you fully. It is now exposing its heart to you.$B$BFocus your intentions here and you will gather it in its entirety.',0),
(48034,'enUS','Empyrium requires a precise strike to yield the best results. Aim your pick at the brightest bits of the ore, which also happen to be very small, hence the precision.$B$BThis will break the deposit apart faster and you\'ll be able to harvest ore quicker.',0),
(48035,'enUS','As I mentioned before, precision is key with mining empyrium. You\'ve learned to strike at the correct spots, now you must learn to strike at the correct angle.$B$BTake out your pick and I\'ll show you what I mean...',0),
(48036,'enUS','You\'ve learned where to strike and at what angle to strike, but should you wish to leave the core intact to mine, you must finally learn how hard to strike.$B$BThe fractures you found in this core are the result of striking the ore too hard. As I\'m sure you no doubt know by now, mining empyrium is not just a task, but an art.$B$BCome, let us practice your swing until it\'s just right.',0),
(48037,'enUS','Empyrium is quite a sight to behold once it\'s been mined. And while the deposits of this ore require precision, the seams require exposure.$B$BIf you spend some time picking away the surrounding rock, you\'ll find much more ore to harvest.',0),
(48038,'enUS','Empyrium seams can be tricky in that regard. The ore is very good at interweaving itself into the surrounding elements.$B$BI\'ve found that striking those areas with the shaft of the pick loosens the empyrium\'s grip on it, so that when you pick at it, the rock should just fall away.',0),
(48039,'enUS','Much like the deposit, empyrium requires a balanced extraction. Its core is its most fragile section.$B$BIf you swing too hard, it breaks, too soft and you\'ll be there forever. The same is true for loosening it from its surrounding rock.$B$BHere, let me show you a method which balances both.',0),
(48040,'enUS','If you haven\'t already guessed, the key to skinning these creatures properly is speed. They\'re born of foul energies and those spill out once you begin to cut into the corpse.$B$BI would suggest training your hand to become faster at removing the hide.',0),
(48041,'enUS','So you\'ve become faster, but you\'re still thinking in your old ways.$B$BInstead of cutting away small pieces at a time, try making one large cut and removing as much of the hide in as few cuts as possible. Move away from the corpse and begin cutting the large pieces into smaller, usable pieces.',0),
(48042,'enUS','So it\'s just more teeth and claws you\'re after? This should be simple to explain then.$B$BThe teeth receive the greatest exposure to the creature\'s foul insides, so removing them first will still give you time to dissect the rest of the beast. Next, remove the hide. And lastly the claws, as those take the longest to take on any corruption.',0),
(48053,'enUS','Whaddya got for me?$B$BMore felslate, fantastic! This stuff weighs a ton, and is perfect for anchors.$B$BI see you have the arms of a blacksmith. Perhaps you\'d like ta have a hand at making a few anchors as well, eh?',0),
(48054,'enUS','More felslate, fantastic! This stuff weighs a ton, and is perfect for anchors.$B$BI see you have the arms of a blacksmith. Perhaps you\'d like to have a hand at making a few anchors as well, eh?',0),
(48055,'enUS','This is quality work. It appears you even solved an issue I was having with the spacing between the front and back chest plates.$B$BYou wouldn\'t mind if I kept this, would you? A fair trade for the recipe, yes?',0),
(48056,'enUS','That last jump looked about what I had in mind for how the gravity was gonna be.$B$B<Hobart scribbles some notes on the schematic.>$B$BAnd there ya have it. They\'ll only last ya a few minutes before they\'re spent, so use \'em wisely.',0),
(48065,'enUS','Oh, this is great stuff. That\'s some landscape up there! Let me just get this information written down...$B$B<Didi begins to scribble some notes on some blueprint paper.>$B$BThat should do it. As with all generators, you\'ll need to use local materials for it, so whatever you can find on that planet should work.',0),
(48066,'enUS','Welcome, $n.$B$BMayla speaks of you as a trusted ally. Your presence will surely help convince her of the merits of joining the Horde.',0),
(48067,'enUS','The Old Gods are known for subversion and duplicity. To attack so brazenly...$B$BWhatever they seek, they want it badly.',0),
(48069,'enUS','$n, you came at the perfect time. I just finished creating this Ionized Geographical Recorder.$B$BNow, here\'s how you\'re gonna use it...',0),
(48074,'enUS','You have no idea the time you\'ve just saved me, $n. You have my utmost gratitude.$B$BAnd as promised, here is my most coveted design.',0),
(48075,'enUS','My book! And it doesn\'t appear to be damaged either, thank the Light.$B$BLook here, $n.$B$B$B$BHere are the designs for turning those gems into accessories of power.',0),
(48076,'enUS','Excellent work, $n. Now, onto the different combinations...',0),
(48078,'enUS','An interesting balance, but necessary. You may keep the oil, I have plenty.$B$BOh, and now that you know how to purify the leather, let me show you how to use it. Here are some shoulder patterns my allies ask for regularly.',0),
(48079,'enUS','Ebonhorn has spoken of ancient wards that must be maintained in Highmountain. Wards that hold back a great darkness.$B$BThis may be tied to the evil that grips him now.$B$BWe must hope that Spiritwalker Graysky can tell us more.',0),
(48081,'enUS','<Velen\'s gaze is drawn to the ruins spread out before him.>$B$BI am home.',0),
(48107,'enUS','We are that much closer to restoring the Crown of the Triumvirate to its former glory.',0),
(48185,'enUS','The next ward is nearby. I can sense it.',0),
(48190,'enUS','Do you sense it, $n? Such strength... such courage.$B$BThe echo of Huln Highmountain\'s spirit is all around us.',0),
(48199,'enUS','I never imagined such destruction... such horror.',0),
(48200,'enUS','Good. From here we can quickly access and reinforce each of the encampments.',0),
(48201,'enUS','We have a foothold here... for now.$B$BI am unsure how long it could hold out against a sustained assault.',0),
(48202,'enUS','So many demons. So much work to do.',0),
(48203,'enUS','After so many years... so many sacrifices... victory is finally within our grasp.',0),
(48230,'enUS','<Fareeya examines the crystal fragment.>$B$BThis is old... very old. It is a piece of an elaborate key, the sort my people use to secure our most prized and sacred places.$B$BI wonder...',0),
(48231,'enUS','The Armor of the Triumvirate! I never believed I would see it again. It is a reminder of our proud history, one which the evil of the Legion will never overshadow.$B$BGaal told me of your dedication, $n. It is fitting that you don this armor. May it serve as a beacon of the Light in these dark times.',0),
(48261,'enUS','Ah, yes. Combined, these clusters should provide just enough power for me to fuse the key fragments back together.',0),
(48271,'enUS','Nice work, Huntmaster. Those ethereals stood no chance against you.$B$BNow that we have the fragments, I can prepare them for reforging.',0),
(48272,'enUS','The Pantheon has been dead for thousands of years... I fear this plan has been in the works for a very, very long time.',0),
(48273,'enUS','Thank ye fer joinin\' me, lad. There\'s somethin\' ye have to see.',0),
(48277,'enUS','Ye came just in the nick of time.',0),
(48280,'enUS','Our answer lies in the Legion\'s own portal network in the heart of Antorus.',0),
(48288,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48292,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48293,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48294,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48295,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48296,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48297,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48298,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48299,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48300,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48301,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48302,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48303,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48304,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48305,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48306,'enUS','Did you triumph in Antorus?',0),
(48318,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, alchemist. We needed these potions badly.',0),
(48323,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, alchemist. We needed these potions badly.',0),
(48337,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, herbalist. We needed this astral glory badly.',0),
(48338,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, $C. We needed this astral glory badly.',0),
(48344,'enUS','There is no room for error here, $n.',0),
(48345,'enUS','<Velen does not seem to notice your presence.>',0),
(48349,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, miner. We needed this empyrium badly.',0),
(48358,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, $C. We needed this empyrium badly.',0),
(48359,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, skinner. We needed this fiendish leather badly.',0),
(48360,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, $C. We needed this fiendish leather badly.',0),
(48363,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, jewelcrafter. We needed these florid malachites badly.',0),
(48364,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, jewelcrafter. We needed this hesselian badly.',0),
(48373,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, tailor. We needed this lightweave cloth badly.',0),
(48374,'enUS','Thank you for assisting us, $C. We needed this lightweave cloth badly.',0),
(48375,'enUS','<As Caelen takes the Sargerite, you see him fusing it with the Obliterum near the forge. The power radiating from it is quite impressive.>$B$BHere you are, lad. Say, ya don\'t think this stuff is toxic, right?',0),
(48376,'enUS','<As Caelen takes the stack of Sargerite, you see him fusing it with the stack of Obliterum near the forge. The power radiating from it is quite impressive.>$B$BHere you are, lad. Say, ya don\'t think this stuff is toxic, right?',0),
(48403,'enUS','I cannot put into words how much you have done for us this day, or how grateful I am to have you as an ally.$B$BYou have our thanks, hero. You have MY thanks.$B$BI owe you a great debt for this.',0),
(48433,'enUS','It seems we have secured a new ally. You have done well.$B$BThe Highmountain tauren are famed for their prowess in battle. I look forward to the pummeling they will unleash upon the Alliance.',0),
(48434,'enUS','I am myself again, $n.$B$BYou and Graysky have freed me from the grasp of the Old Gods. Had I remained in that state for much longer, I would have been lost.',0),
(48440,'enUS','We must act quickly!',0),
(48441,'enUS','You have recovered our supplies. As promised, we will aid your forces on Argus.',0),
(48442,'enUS','Soon, the krokul will raid Nath\'raxas Hold. My people are anxious to begin.',0),
(48443,'enUS','We were a great civilization, once. But, now?... Thank you, $n. Our combined forces freed many from Nath\'raxas. With fewer slaves, and the Army of the Light on their doorstep, the Legion\'s influence over this region will be greatly diminished.',0),
(48445,'enUS','Your champions discovered someone living in a cave beneath Oranaar. He is hiding from the Void-Touched, and he appears lucid.',0),
(48446,'enUS','The voidcallers roaming the Shadowguard Incursion must be extinguished. Your people are sufficiently armed for the coming encounter.',0),
(48447,'enUS','With L\'ura defeated, and the voidcallers eliminated, the Shadowguard\'s dominance over the city has been crippled. if our campaign against the Legion is successful, there could be a future for the creatures living here.',0),
(48448,'enUS','Three Legion facilities decimated in a single operation. Extraordinary.',0),
(48453,'enUS','You\'ve been a great asset to my wranglers here. Please take this as a token of our gratitude.',0),
(48455,'enUS','Keeping balance within the forest ensures its longevity.',0),
(48460,'enUS','I fear the forest may be lost.',0),
(48461,'enUS','So many Legion worlds are ripe for the taking...',0),
(48483,'enUS','A cowled figure... and it did not attack you?$B$BMost curious.',0),
(48500,'enUS','Are you ready to continue on our journey?',0),
(48506,'enUS','I\'m glad you were among those called for the expedition to Argus. There will be plenty of fighting ahead.',0),
(48507,'enUS','I knew you would be among those called to fight. It will be an honor to fight by your side.',0),
(48513,'enUS','The Legion\'s defeat is at hand.',0),
(48542,'enUS','You\'ve been a great asset to my wranglers here. Please take this as a token of our gratitude.',0),
(48544,'enUS','The Wranglers are essential for our survival here. Any assistance you have given them must be repaid.',0),
(48559,'enUS','An important first step, $n.$B$BIf we can bring balance to the Netherlight Crucible, I believe it will make your weapon even more powerful.',0),
(48560,'enUS','Ah, yes. Balance is key, just as the Prophet said.',0),
(48600,'enUS','One step closer to defeating the Legion.',0),
(48601,'enUS','There\'s nothing more beautiful than a lightburst charge erupting in a Legion stronghold. Your people afforded themselves well.',0),
(48605,'enUS','Their commanders fall before us!',0),
(48634,'enUS','You must value our aid greatly, to part with such a bounty.',0),
(48635,'enUS','I am humbled by your generosity.',0),
(48636,'enUS','Another lightforged to fight alongside your forces.',0),
(48639,'enUS','The Army of the Light thanks you.',0),
(48641,'enUS','The Armies of Legionfall thank you, mate.',0),
(48642,'enUS','The Argussian Reach thank you.',0),
(48654,'enUS','I told the others; I will not abandon my people. I must remain here, but maybe you can help? I have discovered a way to purge the shadow from the void-addled.',0),
(48668,'enUS','This beacon will be added to the Navigation Console.$B$BA contingent of the Army of the Light will remain to hold this location for future use.',0),
(48799,'enUS','A good start, hero. There is plenty more where that came from.',0),
(48803,'enUS','Success! It is nice to know I haven\'t lost my touch.$B$BHere you go, $n; it is as good as new.',0),
(48864,'enUS','I am glad to hear Fareeya is well.$B$BShe is right... this is a fragment of the armory key I forged her so long ago.',0),
(48910,'enUS','What say you, offworlder?',0),
(48911,'enUS','Another soul freed from the cruelty of the void.',0),
(48912,'enUS','A lightforged soldier can wade through a sea of demons. They will serve you well.',0),
(48929,'enUS','<Turalyon listens in grim silence.>',0),
(48954,'enUS','Champion, you have returned... and not a moment too soon.$B$BThe object you hold in your hands is but one of many mysteries unfolding before us.',0),
(48962,'enUS','Former blood elves willing to pledge to our cause. This is better than I dared hope.',0),
(48973,'enUS','Greetings, $n.$B$BLong have we awaited this day. Argus was all but lost, its true denizens forced to remain hidden lest we perish. Your efforts on our behalf have allowed us to once again live free from fear. Please accept these trophies as a symbol of our gratitude.',0),
(48974,'enUS','Krona ki cristorr, champion!$B$BYour presence among the Army of the Light has been a singular boon to our cause. Gratitude is not all that we may offer. Please accept these trophies as a tribute to your unwavering support.$B$BTogether we will bring about the Legion\'s end.',0),
(48976,'enUS','Highlord, thanks to your efforts, our forces have been able to secure additional resources from the battlefield.$B$BThe more you continue to dominate the battlefield the more resources our forces can spare.',0),
(48977,'enUS','Archenon poros, champion.$B$BThe Army of the Light wishes to thank you for your aid against the Legion\'s forces on Argus.$B$BPlease accept these supplies with our gratitude. Your continued support brings us ever closer to our ultimate goal of eradicating the Legion once and for all.',0),
(49014,'enUS','After so many years... so many sacrifices... victory is finally within our grasp.',0),
(49015,'enUS','It is finished. At long last, the Burning Crusade is over.$B$BI thank you for all you did, $n. With the power of Argus feeding his Dark Pantheon, Sargeras would have been unstoppable.$B$BOn behalf of the draenei, the eredar, the countless worlds destroyed by the Legion...$B$BThank you.',0),
(49032,'enUS','Magnificent work!$B$BOnce these runes are integrated into our shielding matrix, the Vindicaar will be able to bypass the Burning Throne\'s defenses and strike directly at the felworks.',0),
(49075,'enUS','Magnificent work!$B$BOnce these runes are integrated into our shielding matrix, the Vindicaar will be able to bypass the Burning Throne\'s defenses and strike directly at the felworks.',0),
(49076,'enUS','Magnificent work!$B$BOnce these runes are integrated into our shielding matrix, the Vindicaar will be able to bypass the Burning Throne\'s defenses and strike directly at the felworks.',0),
(49133,'enUS','With these sigils, the Vindicaar can bypass the Burning Throne\'s defenses.$B$BThe time has come to press our advantage and end this war.',0),
(49134,'enUS','With these sigils, the Vindicaar can bypass the Burning Throne\'s defenses.$B$BThe time has come to press our advantage and end this war.',0),
(49135,'enUS','With these sigils, the Vindicaar can bypass the Burning Throne\'s defenses.$B$BThe time has come to press our advantage and end this war.',0),
(49143,'enUS','Ah yes, I sense the Light within these fragments. Do not lose hope, $n!',0),
(49224,'enUS','As your weapon increases in strength we will be able to infuse it with even greater power, but its new strength should be more than enough for now.',0),
(49266,'enUS','T\'paartos is... enthusiastic. He means well, and he has a fire within him that few even among the Lightforged possess. Thank you for keeping him safe, $R.',0),
(49293,'enUS','The Legion\'s defeat is at hand.',0),
(49354,'enUS','That was not wholly expected.',0),
(49445,'enUS','As you\'ve no doubt learned, Primal Sargerite is a precious material which yields great power when infused with items. In our fight against the Legion, we need all the power we can get our hands on.$B$BBring me any Primal Sargerite you find and I will trade with you what I can.',0),
(49472,'enUS','The changes this substance has undergone since the Vindicaar departed for Argus are alarming.$B$BWhat will the outcome mean for Azeroth? I fear this to be an ill omen, $n.',0),
(49473,'enUS','Take this. May it aid your efforts to stop the Legion... and to save our world.',0),
(49474,'enUS','The Betrayer lives up to his name once more.',0),
(49532,'enUS','Welcome to the battlefield, grunt!',0),
(49533,'enUS','Ah, $n, you have arrived!$B$BLet\'s get to work.',0),
(49534,'enUS','Death and acts of sacrilege pervert this land.$B$B<Lantinga lets out a drawn-out sigh.>$B$BThankfully, we\'re here to stop it.',0),
(49535,'enUS','I am glad you\'re here, $R. Hemet has not been heard from for quite some time, and I could really use your help finding him.',0),
(49536,'enUS','Yo! Do I have an explosive proposition for you, pal....',0),
(49537,'enUS','The Warsong Offensive is ready to strike at the heart of the Scourge, $C. Are you up to the challenge?',0),
(49538,'enUS','Lok\'tar ogar, $n. You\'ve arrived not a moment too soon....',0),
(49539,'enUS','You seem like someone who needs some excitement in their life. Excitement... and beer!',0),
(49540,'enUS','What the dook is going on here, $R?!$B$BWhy are pandaren so sad?!',0),
(49541,'enUS','Traveling to Kun-Lai? Right this way, wanderer, right this way!',0),
(49542,'enUS','Welcome to Townlong Steppes, outsider.$B$BIf you insist on wandering in to the darkest places of Pandaria then far be it from me to not put you to good use.',0),
(49543,'enUS','A volunteer for Dread Wastes duty? I think you might be the first.$B$BPleased to meet you.',0),
(49545,'enUS','I am glad to see you are well after Tanaan Jungle.$B$BWe have much to do.',0),
(49546,'enUS','Gorgrond is no place for armies. We are now stepping into the domain of legends.',0),
(49547,'enUS','It is good to see you, Commander $n. I require your advisement.',0),
(49548,'enUS','<Azik looks you up and down.>$B$BAzik is betting you are someone of importance to your people.$B$BCome closer, friend. Azik could use your help.',0),
(49549,'enUS','They came at us... from... nowhere.$B$B<The stone guard nearly passes out.>',0),
(49550,'enUS','We\'re gettin\' hammered out here, lad.$B$BI hope you\'re here to help.',0),
(49551,'enUS','What is it?!$B$BCan\'t you see I\'m already busy trying to get this port ready, $R?',0),
(49552,'enUS','Death and acts of sacrilege pervert this land.$B$B<Lantinga lets out a drawn-out sigh.>$B$BThankfully, we\'re here to stop it.',0),
(49553,'enUS','I am glad you\'re here, $R. Hemet has not been heard from for quite some time, and I could really use your help finding him.',0),
(49554,'enUS','Yo! Do I have an explosive proposition for you, pal....',0),
(49555,'enUS','The Valiance Expedition is ready to strike at the heart of the Scourge, $C. Are you up to the challenge?',0),
(49556,'enUS','Our role is of utmost importance, $n.$B$BAdmiral Taylor and his flagship have gone missing.... More importantly, the young Prince was with him, and it is our primary objective to bring him back home safely.',0),
(49557,'enUS','You seem like someone who needs some excitement in their life. Excitement... and beer!',0),
(49558,'enUS','What the dook is going on here, $R?!$B$BWhy are pandaren so sad?!',0),
(49559,'enUS','Traveling to Kun-Lai? Right this way, wanderer, right this way!',0),
(49560,'enUS','Welcome to Townlong Steppes, outsider.$B$BIf you insist on wandering in to the darkest places of Pandaria then far be it from me to not put you to good use.',0),
(49561,'enUS','A volunteer for Dread Wastes duty? I think you might be the first.$B$BPleased to meet you.',0),
(49564,'enUS','Welcome to Gorgrond, commander.$B$BWe have just arrived ourselves.',0),
(49565,'enUS','It is good to see you, Commander $n. I require your advisement.',0),
(49566,'enUS','<Azik looks you up and down.>$B$BAzik is betting you are someone of importance to your people.$B$BCome closer, friend. Azik could use your help.',0),
(49567,'enUS','They came at us... from... nowhere.$B$B<The lieutenant nearly passes out.>',0),
(49613,'enUS','Good, we\'re all here. Our guests should be arriving shortly.',0),
(49614,'enUS','You return with good news, $n.',0),
(49698,'enUS','Welcome, $n. You are about to bear witness to a ritual none but members of the Army of the Light have seen.',0),
(49756,'enUS','A fine kill, $n. My people can clean up from here.',0),
(49772,'enUS','What have we here? One of the famed Lightforged draenei! Welcome, welcome.$B$BThank you for your service against the Legion, $n. Truly an inspiration!',0),
(49773,'enUS','Are you the new one? I\'m supposed to welcome you. Here, take this letter.$B$B<Blackguard lets out an exasperated sigh.>',0),
(49782,'enUS','Duty. Honor. Sacrifice. The Lightforged strive to embody these qualities. You have done so with aplomb.$B$BIt is my pleasure to award you with a symbol of your service, $n.',0),
(49783,'enUS','You have brought great honor to our tribes, $n. It is fitting that we give you a symbol of our thanks.$B$BHighmountain stands... because you have the courage to fight for it.',0),
(49784,'enUS','When we were liberated from the Legion, some among the shal\'dorei believed we should remain isolated. Alone.$B$BYour accomplishments in Azeroth have shown that we made the right decision in reclaiming our place in this world. It pleases me to honor you with this symbol of Suramar\'s gratitude.',0),
(49787,'enUS','Umbric\'s methods are a bit cavalier, but he seems competent. We must get to him before things become too dangerous.',0),
(49788,'enUS','Ah, there you are, $n! We\'ve been inspecting--err--expecting you!',0),
(49812,'enUS','Goddess be praised that you are here, $n. I\'m hoping that you can aid me.',0),
(49851,'enUS','Ah, $n. Thank you for responding to my request.',0),
(49852,'enUS','Lok\'tar, $n.',0),
(49855,'enUS','We knew the Horde would send help and not a moment too soon!',0),
(49865,'enUS','Ah, $n. Thank you for responding to my request.',0),
(49866,'enUS','Greetings, $n.',0),
(49928,'enUS','Though some continue to doubt us, your deeds have proven that the ren\'dorei serve the Alliance with honor.$B$BYour will is strong, $n. Accept this gift as a symbol of the powers you command.',0),
(49929,'enUS','Welcome, $n. I am pleased you answered the call.',0),
(49930,'enUS','Ah, $n. Now we can begin.',0),
(49933,'enUS','Are you the new one? I\'m supposed to welcome you. Here, take this letter.$B$B<Blackguard lets out an exasperated sigh.>',0),
(49973,'enUS','The city of Suramar is beautiful to behold. I hope Silvermoon City is not a disappointment to them.',0),
(49976,'enUS','If this strange substance is as powerful as it appears to be, we cannot allow it to fall into the wrong hands. Your presence will be needed in Silithus.',0),
(49977,'enUS','About time you arrived, $n. The very future of the Horde may depend on what I am about to tell you...',0),
(49981,'enUS','Well met, $n. It\'s good to have someone of your renown here with us in Silithus.',0),
(49982,'enUS','Greetings, $n. I was told you\'d be coming. The mining operation is currently underway.',0),
(50046,'enUS','Great work, $n! With the shredders sabotaged, the Bilgewater Cartel mining operation will grind to a halt!',0),
(50047,'enUS','I\'ve never seen anythin\' like this before... I\'ll get to work examinin\' it at once!',0),
(50048,'enUS','You made it back alive. That\'s good news, indeed! I trust the expedition went well?',0),
(50049,'enUS','Thank you for delivering Khadgar\'s letter ta me. I\'m goin\' ta need some time ta consider his words. If what he says is correct, we may be able ta save Azeroth... but at a great cost.',0),
(50052,'enUS','You did well, $n... Crisis averted! But we better keep an eye out for reinforcements.$B$BIf this stuff is as valuable as Gallywix says it is, the Alliance is going to be all over this place in no time!',0),
(50053,'enUS','Hmmpf! I hope you didn\'t go easy on them. If it were up to me they\'d be getting more than a simple beating!',0),
(50054,'enUS','I\'m pleased to see that you made it back alive. I\'m sure you fought with honor!',0),
(50055,'enUS','Thank you for delivering Khadgar\'s letter ta me. I\'m goin\' ta need some time ta consider his words. If what he says is correct, we may be able ta save Azeroth... but at a great cost.',0),
(50071,'enUS','The stories of the Lightforged echo throughout the streets of Stormwind. An army of elite soldiers dedicated to fighting the Legion... they will be one of our strongest allies.',0),
(50130,'enUS','Thank you for helping the people of Sporeggar, $R. You are always welcomed here.',0),
(50131,'enUS','Thank you, $n! Thank you.',0),
(50226,'enUS','Oh! Look at these big, beautiful brains! I can\'t wait to dig in... thanks for your help, $n! You can stay and watch if you want, but it may get a bit messy!',0),
(50227,'enUS','I see you have the broodlings! These will do nicely. Would you like to stay and watch me carefully dissect and catalog every detail of their anatomy?',0),
(50228,'enUS','I see you have brought the head of Michiel Voidstrider. A gruesome task, but a necessary one. The Alliance thanks you for your service, $n.',0),
(50229,'enUS','Aye! This\'ll do nicely! Just give us a wee minute here...',0),
(50230,'enUS','Holy moly! Look at the size of these big, beautiful brains! Where\'s my scalpel?! Wait... no... bring me the electric hacksaw. It\'s time for the big guns baby!',0),
(50231,'enUS','You\'ve got the larvae! These are gonna make us a boatload o\' money! I can already hear the gold jinglin\' in my pockets!',0),
(50232,'enUS','I see you have brought the head of Michiel Voidstrider. It will look glorious mounted on a spike! The Horde thanks you for your service, $n.',0),
(50239,'enUS','Your wisdom is always appreciated, $n. The choice you make today will strengthen the Alliance.',0),
(50242,'enUS','I have come to value your wisdom, $n. The choice you make today will strengthen the Horde.',0),
(50247,'enUS','Well done! $B$BIs it not fulfilling? To see each letter safely to its destination?$B$BCome by and help any time!',0),
(50303,'enUS','So this is Orgrimmar. The orcs have made some... interesting aesthetic choices. Be careful of the spikes, $n.$B$BAnd the smells. So many smells.',0),
(50305,'enUS','Welcome to Stormwind. Though it is no Silvermoon, the city does have its charms.$B$BIf you came here expecting a warm welcome, I cannot say I have received one myself. But most folk are polite enough.$B$BNo matter. I am off to seek adventure! And perhaps a stiff drink.',0),
(50313,'enUS','Welcome to this beautiful city, $n. I am sure you will feel as welcome by the other members of the Alliance as I do.$B$BI have met a number of the city guards. Good people, though there are a few things they could learn from us.',0),
(50318,'enUS','We\'re behind schedule - let\'s get moving.',0),
(50319,'enUS','So many tauren! I think I\'ve seen more tauren since I got here than in my entire life in Highmountain.$B$BThey all ask to touch my antlers. It\'s weird at first, but now I kind of like it.',0),
(50335,'enUS','The uprising quelled, the elements calmed, and Hogger slain... I cannot thank you enough, $n. My people have been avenged.$B$BThank you.',0),
(50336,'enUS','I\'d love for you to come aboard as a full G-Team Commando, but our bylaws specifically prohibit Horde team members; however, I CAN enroll you in the G-Team Fan Club!$B$BHere\'s something for your trouble.',0),
(50337,'enUS','Took you long enough. Get behind the pillar before you blow our cover!',0),
(50338,'enUS','The mission is far from over!',0),
(50341,'enUS','The Dark Lady has given orders that you are to personally oversee the operation in Silithus.',0),
(50358,'enUS','You\'re here to collect the samples? It\'s about time they sent someone to help me out!',0),
(50360,'enUS','It\'s good to see you, $n. I suspect that my welcome among the Horde is wearing thin...',0),
(50364,'enUS','The blood of Azeroth? Hmph.$B$BI\'ll make sure this news reaches the warchief, but this operation must continue until I\'m ordered to cease!',0),
(50371,'enUS','At last you have arrived, $n. The very future of the Alliance may depend on what I am about to tell you...',0),
(50372,'enUS','You\'re here to collect the samples? Let\'s get started!',0),
(50373,'enUS','It\'s good to see you, $n. I wish that I were here under more pleasant circumstances...',0),
(50374,'enUS','The blood of Azeroth? I\'ll make sure this news reaches Stormwind, but I must continue the operation until I am ordered otherwise.',0),
(50432,'enUS','Spectacular! Marvelous! At last, I understand fully, and the titans themselves speak to me! They have shown me how to use the essences to craft the finest armors the world has ever seen, though I think the results may be... somewhat unpredictable.$B$B<Vridiel beams with pride.>$B$BWell, what are you waiting for? Bring me as many Wakening Essence as you can find!',0);
